b</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-18-2023, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T16:04:03-08:00","id":1500667,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Greater Tupla, and Bound Supernals.<br /> <br /> 1.) How long does a Greater Tupla hang around, it says they can use immediate, signature or long term Nimbus (or the Rapt mage who 'summoned' them) as a resonant conditions, and they don't start losing corpus (for being in the Fallen) until the Nimbus fades. But only one of those Three types of Nimbuses fades.<br /> <br /> So does it mean it can last 1+ weeks like a standard signature nimbus?<br /> <br /> And can you reduce that by cleaning up the Nimbus in question?<br /> <br /> Also if it is using the long term Nimbus as a resonant condition - or effectively as part of the summoning circle - but long term nimbuses spread to all of a character's sympathic connection (the lower the wisdom the further it spreads). For a Rapt mage that means even below a weak sympathic connection. So it is just anything the Rapt mage has even had contact with is part of the summoning circle?<br /> <br /> 2.) For Bound i am presuming the work the same way as Supernals except for where it specifically states otherwise. When they run out of mana they go into hibernation, if they lose all corpus (when the have mana or when they don't?) Do they return to their prison in hibernation? Are they able to absorb mana from a hallow if they are hibernating near one (Like other invisible entities absorbing essence from a resonant condition)? It say they can only take mana destructively, which suggests meditating at a hallow doesn't help them... But they can be given mana, so i am confused.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T16:50:34-08:00","id":1500669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500654#post1500654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Some photos aren't displaying on my phone. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Uh no. It's not displaying except when I'm logged in, except on my tablet where it displays all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500654#post1500654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: nor are the pictures displaying on my tablet. Thaaat... may become a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah...I'm going to try again if you don't mind. For Science if nothing else.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"128\" height=\"150\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-01sc-classical-mechanics-fall-2016/5c0511873bddef77db501d8c84e65623_ropes_and_pulley_intro.svg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-01sc-classical-mechanics-fall-2016/5c0511873bddef77db501d8c84e65623_ropes_and_pulley_intro.svg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-01sc-classical-mechanics-fall-2016/5c0511873bddef77db501d8c84e65623_ropes_and_pulley_intro.svg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"152\" height=\"141\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/courses-images/wp-content/uploads/sites/2952/2018/01/31200740/CNX_UPhysics_15_05_SimplePend.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/courses-images/wp-content/uploads/sites/2952/2018/01/31200740/CNX_UPhysics_15_05_SimplePend.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/courses-images/wp-content/uploads/sites/2952/2018/01/31200740/CNX_UPhysics_15_05_SimplePend.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Url links in case that doesn't work.<br /> <a href=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-01sc-classical-mechanics-fall-2016/pages/week-4-drag-forces-constraints-and-continuous-systems/12-1-pulley-problems-part-i-set-up-the-equations/\" target=\"_blank\">1</a> <a href=\"http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/hpul2.html\" target=\"_blank\">2</a> <a href=\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-osuniversityphysics/chapter/15-4-pendulums/\" target=\"_blank\">3</a><br /> <br /> Edit: ok that really didn't work.<br /> Edit 2: I got one to work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-18-2023, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T18:42:38-08:00","id":1500687,"title":"","content":"Probably a Patterning, considering Ghostwall does an equivalent feat by rendering an object insubstantial. In this case, rendering an object massless or immovable can probably be done with that Practice of Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T22:25:42-08:00","id":1500703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500667#post1500667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) How long does a Greater Tupla hang around, it says they can use immediate, signature or long term Nimbus (or the Rapt mage who 'summoned' them) as a resonant conditions, and they don't start losing corpus (for being in the Fallen) until the Nimbus fades. But only one of those Three types of Nimbuses fades.<br /> <br /> So does it mean it can last 1+ weeks like a standard signature nimbus?<br /> <br /> And can you reduce that by cleaning up the Nimbus in question?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Greater Tulpa can exist without weakening from exposure to the Phenomenal World within the Nimbus of the Enraptured mage that spawned it. This applies as usual for a mage of the same Gnosis, with the only caveat being that the portions of reality affected by their Long-Term Nimbus are even more plot-determined than usual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if it is using the long term Nimbus as a resonant condition - or effectively as part of the summoning circle - but long term nimbuses spread to all of a character's sympathic connection (the lower the wisdom the further it spreads). For a Rapt mage that means even below a weak sympathic connection. So it is just anything the Rapt mage has even had contact with is part of the summoning circle? </div> </div> </div>&quot;An Enraptured mage\u2019s Nimbus is the wound from which her magic spills, a font of uncontrolled Supernal power. Without Wisdom, she can\u2019t contain it or choose when and how to let it out. Her Long-Term Nimbus is more like a magical contagion than an occult confluence, spreading without regard for any meaningful connection between mage and subject.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> &quot;The character\u2019s Long-Term Nimbus spreads regardless of sympathetic ties; instead, the Storyteller dictates its spread to show how the Rapt\u2019s sorcerous influence taints the world, using it as a Mystery and a story hook to draw player characters in.&quot;<br /> <br /> For an ordinary mage the Long-Term Nimbus can show up according to their sympathetic connections and how well they've separated their Shadow Name from their mundane life. That doesn't mean your mentor, apprentice, Sanctum and familiar will all constantly have weird things going on with them appropriate to your Path, and the only difference the Rapt provide in this regard is that the range of possible links between them and the things their Nimbus draws weirdness towards is even more tenuous than casual acquaintance or regular association. See again &quot;even more plot-determined than usual.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) For Bound i am presuming the work the same way as Supernals except for where it specifically states otherwise. When they run out of mana they go into hibernation, if they lose all corpus (when the have mana or when they don't?) Do they return to their prison in hibernation? </div> </div> </div>Explicitly yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they able to absorb mana from a hallow if they are hibernating near one (Like other invisible entities absorbing essence from a resonant condition)? It say they can only take mana destructively, which suggests meditating at a hallow doesn't help them... But they can be given mana, so i am confused. </div> </div> </div>Meditation alone does not remove Mana from a Hallow and an oblation is not a spell devised to give Mana to the Bound. They don't eat tass in their sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T03:15:50-08:00","id":1500713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500703#post1500703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Greater Tulpa can exist without weakening from exposure to the Phenomenal World within the Nimbus of the Enraptured mage that spawned it. This applies as usual for a mage of the same Gnosis, with the only caveat being that the portions of reality affected by their Long-Term Nimbus are even more plot-determined than usual.<br /> <br /> &lt;Snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm with you on everything except the lenght of time they can exist.<br /> <br /> It is explicitly says &quot;The entity doesn\u2019t start losing Corpus until the Nimbus fades.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which could be multiple weeks at Gnosis 6+ (for a very strong signature nimbus) but not indefinitely.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Explicitly yes. </div> </div> </div>Then i must have missed that bit, only saw what happens 'if they run out of mana' not corpus. Can you point me in the right direction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meditation alone does not remove Mana from a Hallow and an oblation is not a spell devised to give Mana to the Bound. They don't eat tass in their sleep. </div> </div> </div>So basically, if you take all their mana, a bound will go into hibernation indefinitely, in their prison.<br /> <br /> Edit: snipped the bits where you confirmed all the things i suspected. Appreciate the detailed answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T16:40:29-08:00","id":1500785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500713#post1500713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm with you on everything except the lenght of time they can exist.<br /> <br /> It is explicitly says &quot;The entity doesn\u2019t start losing Corpus until the Nimbus fades.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which could be multiple weeks at Gnosis 6+ (for a very strong signature nimbus) but not indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not contradict anything I said, which was that an Enraptured Mage's Nimbus only differs from an unEnraptured mage's by the particulars of what their Long-Term Nimbus can affect. The way the Signature Nimbus works is not stated to be different for the Rapt than other mages. If a means of getting rid of the traces of a mage's Nimbus exists, it works on the Nimbuses of the Rapt unless specifically noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then i must have missed that bit, only saw what happens 'if they run out of mana' not corpus. Can you point me in the right direction? </div> </div> </div>Capitalization in the sentence threw off my reading of the question. They explicitly return to their prison in hibernation if they run out of Mana. Given that 1e's mechanics for the Bound had this also happen if they ran out of Health or Willpower and they're still primarily things that lair/are imprisoned in Atlantean complexes; they use the Supernal being mechanics in 2e, and from the particulars of their description (including the word that comprises their common name) it can be safely assumed that they're usually physically manifested and operate on similar rules to the &quot;Avatars in the Fallen&quot; quality of Ochemata described in Signs of Sorcery rather than being poisoned by the world they're stuck in; if one of the Bound loses all its Corpus, it presumably reforms in its prison/the place it fell to Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T17:04:47-08:00","id":1500787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500785#post1500785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does not contradict anything I said, which was that an Enraptured Mage's Nimbus only differs from an unEnraptured mage's by the particulars of what their Long-Term Nimbus can affect.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you said, or what i tjjught you said, was &quot;A Greater Tulpa can exist without weakening from exposure to the Phenomenal World&quot; - which i inferred to mean without time limit.<br /> <br /> Long term Nimbus may not fade, while signature nimbus does. So i am just trying to figure out the intended time limit of an entity which can use any type of Nimbus (of the Rapt mage who 'summoned' them) as a summoning circle<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Capitalization in the sentence threw off my reading of the question. They explicitly return to their prison in hibernation if they run out of Mana. Given that 1e's mechanics for the Bound had this also happen if they ran out of Health or Willpower and they're still primarily things that lair/are imprisoned in Atlantean complexes; they use the Supernal being mechanics in 2e, and from the particulars of their description (including the word that comprises their common name) it can be safely assumed that they're usually physically manifested and operate on similar rules to the &quot;Avatars in the Fallen&quot; quality of Ochemata described in Signs of Sorcery rather than being poisoned by the world they're stuck in; if one of the Bound loses all its Corpus, it presumably reforms in its prison/the place it fell to Earth. </div> </div> </div>Apologies if my capitalizationnwas off putting.<br /> <br /> I guess i would also have assumed those 1e style rules, or something akin to what is written about the other invisible entities (ie they go into hibernation in a location which is 'resonant' - which in the case of the Bound is where-ever they are Bound on the earth, or Underworld or whatever part of the phenomenal they are 'imprisoned' in).<br /> <br /> If we take the general rules for Invisible entities (run out of corpus but not mana/essence then the usual thing happens) then the additional ruling for them running out of mana makes sense, ie it overrules the default Invisible Entities rule that makes you want to take all the essence before destroying their corpus of you want to kill them.<br /> <br /> It just happens that the Supernal Being rules for summoned entities are ignored in this interpretation (especially the whole being dragged into the Abyss).<br /> <br /> EDIT: infact this makes perfect sense now that i think it through the 4th time. All Invisible entites will reform at their 'anchor' point - Summoned Supernals 'anchor' point being on the other side of the Abyss is a problem for them. Not so much for other types of Supernal being or other type of entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-19-2023, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T17:18:57-08:00","id":1500791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500787#post1500787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you said, or what i tjjught you said, was &quot;A Greater Tulpa can exist without weakening from exposure to the Phenomenal World&quot; - which i inferred to mean without time limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rest of that sentence immediately continued &quot;within the Nimbus of the Enraptured mage that spawned it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If a piece of the Nimbus has a time limit, that time limit exists separately from the consequences a Supernal being faces from being outside of a summoning circle or other supporting environment, as stated by the entity not starting to lose Corpus until the Nimbus fades. While the Signature Nimbus has not faded, the Tulpa can use it to stave off the chill of the Abyss, but if it leaves the area covered by the Nimbus it has no such protection until it returns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T17:27:32-08:00","id":1500792,"title":"","content":"Ok, so you are proposing that Immediate Nimbus flares provide very little time (immediate), Signature Nimbuses provides lots of time (1+ weeks depending on gnosis), and Long term Nimbuses offer Long term protection (unspecified).<br /> <br /> Feels a bit odd if the Long Term Nimbus is basically left all over the place, spreading like crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T19:02:37-08:00","id":1500801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1500792#post1500792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feels a bit odd if the Long Term Nimbus is basically left all over the place, spreading like crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The function of the Long-Term Nimbus in general is &quot;weird shit happens around the Awakened&quot; and for the Rapt that expands to &quot;and the Supernal being that supports or enacts the mage's Fault can hang around in the vicinity of that weirdness while it's going on.&quot; This isn't a Promethean's Wasteland, this is the normal consequences of existing as a mage with some of the sensibilities broken off and turned into ventilation points for the Stress of a fractured wizard soul.<br /> <br /> It spreads, to be sure, but the Long-Term Nimbus doesn't have additional staying power for the Rapt except in the sense that if a Lesser Tulpa manifests through the Long-Term Nimbus (i.e. if the mage has a full Stress track but doesn't manage to roll at least three successes on a Stress roll with rote quality) it leaves the mage's Signature Nimbus on an area based on the Advanced Area Scale table after the phenomena created by the Tulpa cease to persist.<br /> <br /> Given that rolls to generate Tulpa happen at the start of every scene the Rapt is present and get more likely to succeed at all (and thus generate Tulpa and reduce Stress), that's a relatively infrequent pace, especially when the section on Lesser Tulpa manifesting through the Long-Term Nimbus highlights the key prerequisite of the Long-Term Nimbus <i>actively influencing people and events at the time</i> \u2014the Long-Term Nimbus is not like the Immediate and Signature Nimbuses, it's &quot;strange, fractal geometry in the universe.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Greater Tulpa being able to sustain itself in the presence of the Long-Term Nimbus means that the occasions where reality warps to steer the Rapt toward feeding their Fault sometimes have a consistent actor attached to them. A Rapt mage fatally obsessed with spirit possession rolls into town and ends up with their Totem appearing at the locus in the park that they haven't learned about yet to open a hole out of the Shadow. An Enraptured Alchemist bent on trying to alloy human souls with precious metals unknowingly sends their Apeiron to cause an armored car transporting gold ingots to lose half its cargo. The Malefactor consumed by the need to burn down inhabited buildings sees their Seraph set fire to an apartment block across town, and decides to visit the site out of morbid curiosity, not yet knowing the event will have draw the attention of agents of the Ruin. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T18:14:39-08:00","id":1501196,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Does requisitioning using Consilium/Order status also cover the new merits (Perfected Item, Mana Battery, etc) in Signs of Sorcery?</b><br /> I assume you need to buy them with Caucus Assets merit, but would like confirmation.</li> <li><b>Can I combine requisition request in a single item (assuming it exists)? </b><br /> I want a Soul Stone of mage with higher Gnosis (2 availability), that is also a Magical tool (1 availability) and if possible a Path tool (+1 availability)</li> <li><b>Does using a Soul Stone overrides the Yantra Bonus if it is also a Magical Tool?</b><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>When used by another mage as a tool Yantra, soul stones<br /> offer a +2 die bonus, or +3 if the creator\u2019s Gnosis is higher<br /> than the user\u2019s. <u>The stone\u2019s form must still be useable for<br /> the spell.</u></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So if Mark the Obrimos has a Soul Stone of a higher Gnosis mage that is also a Gold Coin.<br /> Does he get +1 using the coin as a Yantra, +3 because of being a Soul Stone, or can he use the 2 different Yantras (being a coin and being a Soul Stone) using different Yantra Slots?</li> <li>The Soul Stone requisitioning on <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> seems wrong, it says as the merit (1 o 2 dots), but +1 if the stone is from a mage with higher Gnosis, and that is what the 2 point of the merit does if you pick it... Am I missing something?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-24-2023, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T18:17:38-08:00","id":1501197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501196#post1501196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does requisitioning using Consilium/Order status also cover the new merits (Perfected Item, Mana Battery, etc.) in Sign of Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as your Order / Consilium has reasonable access to those resources, then yes. <br /> <br /> As to the Soulstone bit... I'd say it's because high Gnosis Soulstones are (probably?) rarer than low, so Orders are much less likely to give them out. That makes them less available than just their dot rating would imply when it comes to requisitioning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T18:55:02-08:00","id":1501202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501196#post1501196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Soul Stone requisitioning on <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> seems wrong, it says as the merit (1 o 2 dots), but +1 if the stone is from a mage with higher Gonisis, and that is what the 2 point of the merit does if you pick it... Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would read that as a reminder rather than an additional surcharge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T08:41:33-08:00","id":1501237,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> What about the Soul Stone as Yantra example I put? Any insight on that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<i>When used by another mage as a tool Yantra, soul stones<br /> offer a +2 die bonus, or +3 if the creator\u2019s Gnosis is higher<br /> than the user\u2019s. <u>The stone\u2019s form must still be useable for<br /> the spell.</u></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So if Mark the Obrimos has a Soul Stone of a higher Gnosis mage that is also a Gold Coin.<br /> <br /> Does he get +1 using the coin as a Yantra, OR +3 because of being a Soul Stone, OR can he use the 2 different Yantras (being a coin and being a Soul Stone) using different Yantra Slots?\u200b<br /> <br /> Essentially, does it being a Soul Stone overrides any Magical Tool Yantra value?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  I just realised that you might have just read the message before I edited those questions. 01-24-2023, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T13:27:58-08:00","id":1501262,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb is that the highest bonus applies, assuming all potential Yantra-forms resonate with the spell. The Path of the soulstone might perclude certain spells, like Matter for a Mastigos soulstone, in which case you'd only use the Coin Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T21:21:00-08:00","id":1501297,"title":"","content":"Can you use the Space spell Q<u>uarantine</u> on a Goetia while in the Astral, and if so, what heppens if it's the Mind-conjunctive version? Does the world forget the Goetia, or the thing that the Goetia represents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T21:46:29-08:00","id":1501299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501297#post1501297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the Space spell Q<u>uarantine</u> on a Goetia while in the Astral, and if so, what heppens if it's the Mind-conjunctive version? Does the world forget the Goetia, or the thing that the Goetia represents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space looks physical in the Astral, so it should behave similarly. Using the Mind version of <i>Quarantine</i> makes people forget that specific goetia. All concepts are too broad to be fully embodied by one goetia. You may wipe people's memories of Anubis, but there are also other interpretations of death, such as the grim reaper, Nergal, Death from the Endless, Milu, Death from the Discoworld setting, Mandos from Lord of the Rings and many more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T13:22:17-08:00","id":1501340,"title":"","content":"I think with goetia it can go that in the Oneiros they're more intimately connected to the quality they embody, if not outright being that quality seen through a frame of reference that separates it out from everything else and makes it an entity, but in the Temenos it's more something that emerges out of a collective quality of people.<br /> <br /> Still, while I wouldn't say that using Quarantine on, say, the Teenage Rebel causes all teenage rebellion to cease or be forgotten, the expression of that quality can lose a kind of spark while the goetia is absent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T15:18:03-08:00","id":1501349,"title":"","content":"If you quarentine it will be as if you had destroyed the goetia, but for any significant one it may be replaced by a new one fairly fast...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T16:56:18-08:00","id":1501355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501349#post1501349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you quarentine it will be as if you had destroyed the goetia, but for any significant one it may be replaced by a new one fairly fast...</div> </div> </div> </div>A base Quarantine shouldn't trigger an effect like that - as far as I can tell it would just stop the Goetia from roaming. Which can potentially keep it from interacting meaningfully with other Goetia, but also prevents it from being destroyed of messed with without a good deal of Awakened effort.<br /> <br /> Mind-conjunctive Quatantine... I don't <i>think</i> it would be like killing them. Quarantine doesn't sever the target's existance, just makes them physically inaccessable. Time-conjunctive Quarantine <i>probably </i>replaces them temporarily, but that's not going to result in a long-term two-fer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T17:42:04-08:00","id":1501361,"title":"","content":"So using Goetic Evocation and using the +2 Reach option to incorporate the Goetia into one's Oneiros and letting it stay there is a bad idea...worse still if the Soul Stone's creator was at Falling Wisdom. So do you think it would be even worse if the Soul Soul was created by one of the Raptured? What would happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T18:15:37-08:00","id":1501364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501361#post1501361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So using Goetic Evocation and using the +2 Reach option to incorporate the Goetia into one's Oneiros and letting it stay there is a bad idea...worse still if the Soul Stone's creator was at Falling Wisdom. So do you think it would be even worse if the Soul Soul was created by one of the Raptured? What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the contents of the &quot;Souls of the Rapt&quot; section on page 89 of SoS adequately covers the most likely initial consequences of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T18:40:41-08:00","id":1501366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501361#post1501361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So using Goetic Evocation and using the +2 Reach option to incorporate the Goetia into one's Oneiros and letting it stay there is a bad idea...worse still if the Soul Stone's creator was at Falling Wisdom. So do you think it would be even worse if the Soul Soul was created by one of the Raptured? What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have specific opinions regarding Rapt soul/soulstone shenanagins that I probably shouldn't share with you. If you're ok with spoilers:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Both of these are my opinion, since there aren't any rules on it that I remember. Intergrating a Rapt Goetia automatically gives you Persistent Soul Cracks, as if you had been using the stone as a Yantra or a Desmense. The condition refreshes every [Ritual Interval], which makes it a VERY bad idea to do as a high Gnosis mage. Using <u>Soul Grafting </u>is worse - as long as the graft remains, you gain their Fault, and become a vector for Tulpa.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-25-2023, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T02:27:51-08:00","id":1501388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501361#post1501361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So using Goetic Evocation and using the +2 Reach option to incorporate the Goetia into one's Oneiros and letting it stay there is a bad idea...worse still if the Soul Stone's creator was at Falling Wisdom. So do you think it would be even worse if the Soul Soul was created by one of the Raptured? What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome, especially if you can find multiple soulstones from different Rapt mages, you become more and more deeply connected to the Supernal (while eroding your own personal connection) possibly develop multiple (contradictory?) Faults, your Nimbus becomes a mixture of the Nimbuses of the Rapt mages you have in your Oneiros... Almost certainly an Act of Hubris (as uncontrolled Long Term Nimbus is not Wise).<br /> <br /> Closest thing to a walking verge.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T07:49:33-08:00","id":1501404,"title":"","content":"Multiple order status questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What would it mean for a starting character to have high Order Status? </b><br /> I think someone with low Arcana might be impossible on certain orders, I could envision the Free Council granting high status for a low Arcana mage that spends his time working the order goals, but other orders seem to me to be to very be focused on Arcana and Gnosis potence.</li> <li><b>Do you need to know Rotes to actually advance in the Mysterium? </b><br /> I am envisioning a Mage that is focused on spending his experience on growing in understanding (Gnosis) and capabilities (Arcana), but not much focus on formulaic efforts (Rotes)</li> <li><b>Can you get to the high status levels of Silver Ladder on Personal (not Allies, Contacts, Resources just Gnosis + Arcana) power only?</b></li> <li><b>Do you need to have/be part of Cryptopolies to get to upper levels of status with Silver Ladder?</b></li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members dedicated to the Order financial matters almost exclusively? </b><br /> I am thinking Silver Ladder and Free Council, but how does the Mysterium finance itself? By selling to other orders? How does the Adamantine Arrow get money? Guardians of the Veil?</li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members exclusively dedicated to the members</b><b> security and well-being? </b><br /> A mix of human resources AND security office for the Order members. Could include the financial part: guaranteeing income for all members, that their living quarters are at least safe, and that they can be reached in case of need (whether their own needs or the order needing their skills).</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-26-2023, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T12:33:34-08:00","id":1501422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501404#post1501404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple order status questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What would it mean for a starting character to have high Order Status? </b><br /> I think someone with low Arcana might be impossible on certain orders, I could envision the Free Council granting high status for a low Arcana mage that spends his time working the order goals, but other orders seem to me to be to very be focused on Arcana and Gnosis potence.</li> <li><b>Do you need to know Rotes to actually advance in the Mysterium? </b><br /> I am envisioning a Mage that is focused on spending his experience on growing in understanding (Gnosis) and capabilities (Arcana), but not much focus on formulaic efforts (Rotes)</li> <li><b>Can you get to the high status levels of Silver Ladder on Personal (not Allies, Contacts, Resources just Gnosis + Arcana) power only?</b></li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members dedicated to the Order financial matters almost exclusively? </b><br /> I am thinking Silver Ladder and Free Council, but how does the Mysterium finance itself? By selling to other orders? How does the Adamantine Arrow get money? Guardians of the Veil?</li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members exclusively dedicated to the members</b><b> security and well-being? </b><br /> A mix of human resources AND security office for the Order members. Could include the financial part: guaranteeing income for all members, that their living quarters are at least safe, and that they can be reached in case of need (whether their own needs or the order needing their skills).</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Apprenticed based nepotism, local emergency incited a shuffling of the power structure, the keeping of a lot of logistical upkeep and direction as a sleeper/sleepwalker prior to Awakening, setting up a patsy, possible consequences of a Metamorphic Awakening or a Destiny, so on and so forth.<br /> 2. No, but one has to wonder why you'd be hamstringing yourself. Yes, it's ideal to be able to improvise with mastery, but Rotes are among the most powerful Yantras out there, and their acquisition also tends to bring forth a lot of the other things that would get you lots of kudos in the Mysterium.EDIT: Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools\">this sounds familiar.</a><br /> 3. In theory, yes, and in fact the ideal is such. In practice though, one again has to ask why you'd want to hamstring yourself, particularly since the merits mentioned are among some of the most powerful in the game. It's hard to be a Sage with cults working towards the metaphysical and spiritual liberation of the human race if you don't <i>have</i> cults.<br /> 4. The Seers of the Throne. Though, the real answer is &quot;All of them, the Seers just have an in.&quot; Global mystery religions need them that cash flow.<br /> 5. The Guardians, followed closely by the Arrows. Though, again, the real answer is all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-26-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T13:15:16-08:00","id":1501425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501388#post1501388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds awesome, especially if you can find multiple soulstones from different Rapt mages, you become more and more deeply connected to the Supernal (while eroding your own personal connection) possibly develop multiple (contradictory?) Faults, your Nimbus becomes a mixture of the Nimbuses of the Rapt mages you have in your Oneiros... Almost certainly an Act of Hubris (as uncontrolled Long Term Nimbus is not Wise).<br /> <br /> Closest thing to a walking verge.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What happens if you get goetia from 10 Rapt, each of which produced a soul stone of a different Arcanum ? What would happen to a soul blasted by the unfiltered madness and power of all Arcana at once ? If the mage becomes Rapt while under the strain of all of them, what happens to them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T15:14:26-08:00","id":1501430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501425#post1501425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens if you get goetia from 10 Rapt, each of which produced a soul stone of a different Arcanum ? What would happen to a soul blasted by the unfiltered madness and power of all Arcana at once ? If the mage becomes Rapt while under the strain of all of them, what happens to them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a Mystery. Possibly an epic mystery, might even attract the attention of some powers that be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T15:42:12-08:00","id":1501433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501404#post1501404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple order status questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What would it mean for a starting character to have high Order Status? </b><br /> I think someone with low Arcana might be impossible on certain orders, I could envision the Free Council granting high status for a low Arcana mage that spends his time working the order goals, but other orders seem to me to be to very be focused on Arcana and Gnosis potence.</li> <li><b>Do you need to know Rotes to actually advance in the Mysterium? </b><br /> I am envisioning a Mage that is focused on spending his experience on growing in understanding (Gnosis) and capabilities (Arcana), but not much focus on formulaic efforts (Rotes)</li> <li><b>Can you get to the high status levels of Silver Ladder on Personal (not Allies, Contacts, Resources just Gnosis + Arcana) power only?</b></li> <li><b>Do you need to have/be part of Cryptopolies to get to upper levels of status with Silver Ladder?</b></li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members dedicated to the Order financial matters almost exclusively? </b><br /> I am thinking Silver Ladder and Free Council, but how does the Mysterium finance itself? By selling to other orders? How does the Adamantine Arrow get money? Guardians of the Veil?</li> <li><b>Which Order is most likely to have members exclusively dedicated to the members</b><b> security and well-being? </b><br /> A mix of human resources AND security office for the Order members. Could include the financial part: guaranteeing income for all members, that their living quarters are at least safe, and that they can be reached in case of need (whether their own needs or the order needing their skills).</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>Important note before I go into my opinions - the Orders aren't necessarily homogeneous monoliths. The Ladder in Japan is different from the Ladder in Brazil, for example, and while you can generalize the practices every one is going to be a little different. Further, the size and composition of a given Consilium is going to have a MASSIVE impact on how things are done. The thirty-some Consilium of DC is going to look very different to the five-man Consilium of middle-of-nowhere Alaska. Cooperation is also important - a Consilium whose FC is on the outs with everyone else (London, for example) probably doesn't have access to TELM.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Free Council has a good chance of it happening - as I recall, force of personality and charisma are the deciding factors in electing Chairmen or being recognized as a Syndic. For the rest...<br /> <br /> Silver Ladder might give higher status to a former Cryptopoly/Mystery Cult member. As I recall, 1e's Order book explains how the SL handle low-level initiation for non-Awakened.<br /> <br /> The Arrow decides by strength, so if you challenged someone and won, you could &quot;keep what you kill&quot;, as it were. Better hope you're popular though, because otherwise you're likely to be challenged yourself soon enough.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium is probably pretty Mystery-dependent, in addition to factoring in how much you've contributed to the Athenaeum. <br /> <br /> Guardians are pretty regimented, I imagine their promotion system hinges on how successful you are at your assigned duties.<br /> <br /> and for all of them, having dirty laundry on others might lead to a rapid promotion. Or assassination.<br /> <br /> 2. I doubt it. It's a good resource to have when trying to make yourself appealing as a teacher, but scholarly work is more likely to be an important consideration for them.<br /> <br /> 3. Potentially. The Ladder has a political bent, and showing you can further their aims without resorting to magic is one of the initiatory trials IIRC. You'll get less respect than someone with a higher Gnosis in the same rank would expect, but you'd still have clout.<br /> <br /> 4. No, but like becoming a Factotum, it's a good feather in your cap to make you look good to the bosses. Also provides you with influence in the Fallen World and any new Awakened that come from the Cryptopoly.<br /> <br /> 5. Most Actual Plays I've seen will mention off-handedly one or two uber-rich Mages who fund the rest of the Consilium. From the Broken Diamond it was Shore, and in The Man Comes Around there was a stockbroker for TELM. <br /> <br /> It's also not difficult for a Mage to be wealthy -although it's hard to be a Life doctor unless you get good forged credentials or were already certified, or take the time to go back to school- and honestly quite a few minor concerns can be handled with Magic. Need something build, or maintenance done? Matter Mage gets some practice in. Can't afford enough food this month? Use Mend or Knit to stretch your larders. A Time Mage can play the stock markets like nobody's buisness, and a Mind Mage can skill-monkey their way into just about any profession.<br /> <br /> It's also going to depend on how unified the Consilium is. In one where everyone gets along, the Mysterium can probably just ask the Hierarch and Council for a blank check to build a new Athenaeum. In one where they don't get along, every order probably has their own revenue streams and occasionally Clash over them.<br /> <br /> Also worth remembering that anyone might join any order. You could easily have an AA doctor, or a SL gangster. It's really going to depend on the local landscape.<br /> <br /> 6. Entirely subjective to the location and disposition of the local Mages. The cult-ier Orders are probably more likely to have compounds though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T15:59:47-08:00","id":1501436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> thanks for the answer, the size of Consilium you mentioned got me thinking... Is there an average size per million of citizens in a city?<br /> <br /> Like how many mages (approximately) should have a city with X million people? Some ups and downs related to the city importance (New York City has about 9 million people, but many more commute AND it is an attractive city for foreign citizens so I expect it to have above average Mage population, I just dont know how many is that).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-26-2023, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T16:03:37-08:00","id":1501437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501436#post1501436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> thanks for the answer, the size of Consilium you mentioned got me thinking... Is there an average size per million of citizens in a city? Like how many mages (approximately) should have a city with X million people? Some ups and downs related to the city importance (New York City has about 9 million people, but many more commute AND it is an attractive city for foreign citizens so I expect it to have above average Mage population).</div> </div> </div> </div>There probably is somewhere, but I don't remember it offhand. My rule of thumb otherwise would be that it depends on how many Mysteries are present. A small town in the middle of nowhere might have an Awakened population on-par with a large city, if the Mysteries in the former are interesting enough or the latter boring enough. Worth noting though that it's easier to hide from Seers and counter their plots in a city.<br /> <br /> I think I remember the Neolithic Dark Eras mentioning that the number of mages then is uncomfortably similar to the number of Mages now - that is, it isn't proportional to population. I'd need to re-read that to confirm tho.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dark Eras I, Page 50: In comparison to the size of the population, far more humans are Awakening during the Neolithic than in following eras. The strict number of Wise in the world may not be vast, but were the modern world to produce as many Awakened in proportion to its bloated population, it would be drowning in mages\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-27-2023, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T16:25:57-08:00","id":1501439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501437#post1501437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There probably is somewhere, but I don't remember it offhand. My rule of thumb otherwise would be that it depends on how many Mysteries are present. A small town in the middle of nowhere might have an Awakened population on-par with a large city, if the Mysteries in the former are interesting enough or the latter boring enough. Worth noting though that it's easier to hide from Seers and counter their plots in a city.<br /> <br /> I think I remember the Neolithic Dark Eras mentioning that the number of mages then is uncomfortably similar to the number of Mages now - that is, it isn't proportional to population. I'd need to re-read that to confirm tho.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Tokyo in the Core 2ed has 40 million people, and about 200 mages:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The city boasts a <b>disproportionately high number of<br /> Awakened</b>, including two Mystagogue caucuses and a caucus<br /> of every other Order<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The Awakened Orders exist in Tokyo, as with most cities. The<br /> six stand strong and populous<b> among the metropolitan area\u2019s<br /> nearly 40 million people\u200b</b>.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> This means getting over 100 Awakened to both congregate,<br /> and agree on a single agenda. (This also assumes a unanimous<br /> vote, since<b> over 200 Awakened reside in the metropolitan area</b>.)<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> So, Tokyo has a ~0.0005% Awakened/Sleeper rate, and it is a high numbered city. So, assuming a similar rate for New York City metro area 20 million citizens, gives around ~100 mages.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-15-2025, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T16:47:29-08:00","id":1501440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501404#post1501404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would it mean for a starting character to have high Order Status?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something's up, for which the individual character's situation should probably provide an explanation given that, as you observe peripherally, even mage societies that don't talk about Gold Laws still tend to favor recognizing mages for their mastery of the Arcana. As with putting a disproportionately high starting rating in other Traits, players should be expected to have an answer for where that comes from if it seems to produce weird results in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you need to know Rotes to actually advance in the Mysterium? </div> </div> </div>Not on paper, but transmissible knowledge is certainly a useful currency to spend in the Order that has its own named economy of favors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you get to the high status levels of Silver Ladder on Personal (not Allies, Contacts, Resources just Gnosis + Arcana) power only? </div> </div> </div>If you can get the Caucus to recognize you in that regard, sure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which Order is most likely to have members dedicated to the Order financial matters almost exclusively? </div> </div> </div>One of the many advantages of 2e being more explicit about the Orders being more than their Awakened membership is that this is a non-issue unless someone's pursuing a Mystery related to it. The Orders run cults, make connections, dip their toes into organized crime, and so on \u2014 if they need to secure funds, <i>they have people for that</i>. Sleepers and Sleepwalkers don't have a pressing metaphysical focus on personal mystical R&amp;D to keep them away from the distractions of cooking the books, drumming up funds, and making sure the budget is balanced.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which Order is most likely to have members exclusively dedicated to the members[/B][B] security and well-being? </div> </div> </div>If this a question assuming that the Orders work like open institutions, I would point out that you are talking about global conspiracies that mostly work with fronts and other obfuscatory measures, and that as the most generally knowledgeable groups about the Awakened condition they are going to know better than to put their constituents' day-to-day living situations in frequent contact with active wizards. You were ostensibly trained by a mentor who was likely to be held responsible if things turned out badly for you, and &quot;graduating&quot; to the point of being trusted to handle yourself generally means the local Caucus knows you can handle yourself (or at least keep in touch with your peers enough to get help if something goes wrong).<br /> <br /> Just as the Consilium is a court of adjudication rather than a governing body, belong to a Caucus is not active military service or an extended monastic retreat or an undergraduate program. If you are dealing with work for the Order that entails maintaining a secure site, someone is going to be responsible for that site, and the particulars will vary based on the work, the site, the Order, and all manner of other conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T14:53:29-08:00","id":1501484,"title":"","content":"1. Is it possible to create artificial Synesi? What Arcana and Practice if so? Mind and Making, to ape <u>Create Avernian Gate</u>? <br /> <br /> 2. Are Synesi two-wayed? That is, is it possible for Goetia to exit the Astral through them?<br /> <br /> 3. How do you reach dreams from the Astral, and how difficult is it for Goetia enter them? Goetia generally don't roam far from areas related to them, but a Familiar -or a <u>Psychic <u>Genesi</u>s</u> creation- might have reason to. Plus Core mentions that some Goetia stalk there.<br /> <br /> 4. Does <u>Telepathy</u> work across realms? That is, could a Mage in the Fallen use it to communicate with a Goetic Familiar in the Astral, a Sineater ally in the Underworld, or a Changeling ally in the Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T16:52:55-08:00","id":1501501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501484#post1501484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Is it possible to create artificial Synesi? What Arcana and Practice if so? Mind and Making, to ape <u>Create Avernian Gate</u>?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Synesi two-wayed? That is, is it possible for Goetia to exit the Astral through them?<br /> <br /> 3. How do you reach dreams from the Astral, and how difficult is it for Goetia enter them? Goetia generally don't roam far from areas related to them, but a Familiar -or a <u>Psychic <u>Genesi</u>s</u> creation- might have reason to. Plus Core mentions that some Goetia stalk there.<br /> <br /> 4. Does <u>Telepathy</u> work across realms? That is, could a Mage in the Fallen use it to communicate with a Goetic Familiar in the Astral, a Sineater ally in the Underworld, or a Changeling ally in the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. Mind 5 is sufficient as always, but with Spirit 3 Reaching being able to create a Shadowed Door (an Iris to the Shadow) with +1 Reach, an argument could be made for Patterning. (You are re-defining the fundamental interaction between body and soul in an area)<br /> <br /> 2. Er, I don\u2019t think so? Most Goetia seem out of luck on this matter.<br /> <br /> 3. First we need to reach the individual\u2019s Oneiros at minimum. \u2019Real\u2019 dreams are not the Astral proper, so some sort of threshold-hopping would be needed. Dunno if this should be something only a few Goetia can do, or any can with the right know-how.<br /> <br /> 4. Telepathy being Potency-primary makes me think it\u2019s a one-time broadcast per casting. Which would mean that you need a way to somehow contact said otherworldly ally every casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T17:07:49-08:00","id":1501503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501501#post1501501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Telepathy being Potency-primary makes me think it\u2019s a one-time broadcast per casting. Which would mean that you need a way to somehow contact said otherworldly ally every casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The Reach effects detailing the ability to send and receive makes me think it's like initiating a phone call, with casting the spell being the equivalent of dialing. I assume it's Potency-primary because it's invasive with a goal-driven purpose, much like <u>Psychic Domination, Alter Mental Patterns, Emotional Urging,</u> or <u>Read the Depths.</u><br /> <br /> In any event, it can still be cast at Sympathetic Range, which should be able to cross dimensional boundaries, correct?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T17:08:14-08:00","id":1501504,"title":"","content":"3. was kinda answered by DaveBrookshaw on <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/zvhrqm/where_dreams_happen/\" target=\"_blank\">Reddit</a>. I know Larval Horrors count as Goetia, but I'm uncertain if they can make it to dreams before they transform. \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dreams occur in one's personal Oneiros while the hedge connects to it. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveBrookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they don't. They're the layer before the Oneiros. Because the Vestibule of the Oneiros reflects the current thoughts of the person whose soul it is, you <i>can</i> watch someone's dreams from inside it, but it's like watching something on a TV.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-27-2023, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T17:26:04-08:00","id":1501505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501501#post1501501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. First we need to reach the individual\u2019s Oneiros at minimum. \u2019Real\u2019 dreams are not the Astral proper, so some sort of threshold-hopping would be needed. Dunno if this should be something only a few Goetia can do, or any can with the right know-how.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this note, do Temenonic Geotia invade a person's Oneiros when being exposed to concepts, like during a conversation or while reading a book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T17:31:13-08:00","id":1501506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501504#post1501504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Larval Horrors count as Goetia, but I'm uncertain if they can make it to dreams before they transform. \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, they're Anima Mundi natives originally, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501505#post1501505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On this note, do Temenonic Geotia invade a person's Oneiros when being exposed to concepts, like during a conversation or while reading a book?</div> </div> </div> </div>LA's Goetia problem would imply there might be some element of connection whenever you interact with a Goetia's concept, so it's not implausible<br /> <br /> Unrelated question. You can gain one dot of Status with at most one Order besides your own. The Ally Merit would cover most social interactions, so does that mean the Status qualifies you for that order's Rote Skills and Order Tools? And their Merits? I <i>think</i> a 5-dot Masque can emulate Order-specific traits, but that's a bit of an edge case.<br /> <br /> Similarly, can a Pentacle Mage progress higher than one dot in a Nameless Order Mystery Cult, or is it treated like an Order in that regard? I generally assume the Status limit is political, but given the symbolic nature of the Orders I could see them creating metaphysical limitations on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-27-2023, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T18:01:21-08:00","id":1501508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501506#post1501506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, they're Anima Mundi natives originally, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> According to the player guide, they are Goetia that come from Beast's interpretation of the Anima Mundi, make their way to the Temenos, claim a piece of the transition beween Anima Mundi and Temenos which transforms them into a Horror proper, and then they seek out dreams for food. I guess technically stuff can use the bridges Horrors make to invade dreams alongside them. <br /> <br /> Rereading that section did bring up one detail though, Larval Horrors can access dreams before they change into a Horror proper. It's how the Insatiable are created. This is interesting since hypothetically they still should be normal Anima Mundi Goetia at that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501506#post1501506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LA's Goetia problem would imply there might be some element of connection whenever you interact with a Goetia's concept, so it's not implausible</div> </div> </div> </div> Guess that means that catchy songs and memes really can be called viruses.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T18:05:45-08:00","id":1501509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501505#post1501505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this note, do Temenonic Geotia invade a person's Oneiros when being exposed to concepts, like during a conversation or while reading a book?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding would be that you form Oneiric Goetia relating to the concept once you're exposed to them, and those Oneiric Goetia in turn are the likely actors or raw material by which a Temenotic Goetia would affect changes through your presence in the Temenos.<br /> <br /> The interactions between the Astral layers from their native are currently not very explicitly defined, but just as I wouldn't assume Animal Masters cross the Omphalos to give rise to animal-headed gods in the Temenos, I wouldn't assume those animal-headed gods are crossing the second inversion to do the job of an individual's personal concept of e.g. the ancient Egyptian pantheon.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T19:37:00-08:00","id":1501512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501505#post1501505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this note, do Temenonic Geotia invade a person's Oneiros when being exposed to concepts, like during a conversation or while reading a book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral Threshold (see page 33 of <i>Astral Realms</i>) would impede them. Mages have the ability to navigate to it and bypass it. I think the people create their own goetia, based on their own interpretation of the concept and the personal significance it holds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T20:03:27-08:00","id":1501513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501503#post1501503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? The Reach effects detailing the ability to send and receive makes me think it's like initiating a phone call, with casting the spell being the equivalent of dialing. I assume it's Potency-primary because it's invasive with a goal-driven purpose, much like <u>Psychic Domination, Alter Mental Patterns, Emotional Urging,</u> or <u>Read the Depths.</u><br /> <br /> In any event, it can still be cast at Sympathetic Range, which should be able to cross dimensional boundaries, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, S. Range would work.<br /> <br /> For Potency &amp; Duration; I remember reading a player\u2019s analysis about primary factors, but I can\u2019t recall how to find it\u2026 In any case, Duration is still there to be raised, so this shouldn\u2019t be too much of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T00:38:54-08:00","id":1501521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501503#post1501503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any event, it can still be cast at Sympathetic Range, which should be able to cross dimensional boundaries, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not.<br /> <br /> Teleportation at sympathetic range explicitly calls for conjunctional Death (2) to move in/out of the Underworld. Or Spirit for the Shadow.<br /> <br /> But it is not called out as such anywhere, so i may be house ruling this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T03:21:05-08:00","id":1501524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501521#post1501521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not.<br /> <br /> Teleportation at sympathetic range explicitly calls for conjunctional Death (2) to move in/out of the Underworld. Or Spirit for the Shadow.<br /> <br /> But it is not called out as such anywhere, so i may be house ruling this.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cross-dimensional Sympathetic casting would probably require conjunctive Arcana, you're right. Whether <u>Telepathy</u> once cast can maintain communication across dimensions without having been cast with conjunctive Arcana at the start would probably be firmly in house rule territory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T03:28:14-08:00","id":1501525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501524#post1501524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cross-dimensional Sympathetic casting would probably require conjunctive Arcana, you're right. Whether <u>Telepathy</u> once cast can maintain communication across dimensions without having been cast with conjunctive Arcana at the start would probably be firmly in house rule territory</div> </div> </div> </div>I am less convinced now, the conjunction seems to be called out as necessary for teleportation, but that is written like an exceptional circumstance, rather than the general rule.<br /> <br /> If you were Scrying on someone's past using Temporal sympathy, you wouldn't expect to need conjunctive Death to see what they did in the Underworld (though that might make an interesting story if it was true...). But if you can scry on someone currently in the Underworld you would co-locate at sensory range (+remote viewing) and bypass the stated requirement from teleportation for conjunctional Death.<br /> <br /> *Substitute Spirit or any other Arcana for the Shadow or any other realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T03:40:24-08:00","id":1501526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501524#post1501524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cross-dimensional Sympathetic casting would probably require conjunctive Arcana, you're right. Whether <u>Telepathy</u> once cast can maintain communication across dimensions without having been cast with conjunctive Arcana at the start would probably be firmly in house rule territory</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, I\u2019d rather not require it, for the same reason mind-controlling a ghost does not require Death. A mind is still a mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T04:48:09-08:00","id":1501530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501526#post1501526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm, I\u2019d rather not require it, for the same reason mind-controlling a ghost does not require Death. A mind is still a mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. <u>Co-Location</u> seems like it would need conjunctive for cross-dimensional travel tho, since its functionally similar to <u>Teleport.</u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T05:01:22-08:00","id":1501531,"title":"","content":"Edit - Double posted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T12:34:27-08:00","id":1501559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501501#post1501501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Mind 5 is sufficient as always, but with Spirit 3 Reaching being able to create a Shadowed Door (an Iris to the Shadow) with +1 Reach, an argument could be made for Patterning. (You are re-defining the fundamental interaction between body and soul in an area)</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating an Iris is always Making. The thing about the Shadow is that the Gauntlet is basically an ever-present Iris to the Shadow, so you only ever need Spirit 3 to open the pathway that already exists.<br /> I don't think the same argument can be made for Synesi, unless it's a particularly weird one centered on a person (who already has a pathway of sorts to the Astral) rather than a spatial location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T16:14:33-08:00","id":1501580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501559#post1501559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating an Iris is always Making. The thing about the Shadow is that the Gauntlet is basically an ever-present Iris to the Shadow, so you only ever need Spirit 3 to open the pathway that already exists.<br /> I don't think the same argument can be made for Synesi, unless it's a particularly weird one centered on a person (who already has a pathway of sorts to the Astral) rather than a spatial location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind Patterning could probably allow the target to temporarily have the Astral Adept Merit. That seems about in line with the general equivelants, and makes an acceptable transition up to Making a full Synesi at Mind 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T01:50:43-08:00","id":1501597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501559#post1501559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creating an Iris is always Making. The thing about the Shadow is that the Gauntlet is basically an ever-present Iris to the Shadow, so you only ever need Spirit 3 to open the pathway that already exists.<br /> I don't think the same argument can be made for Synesi, unless it's a particularly weird one centered on a person (who already has a pathway of sorts to the Astral) rather than a spatial location.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like the astral equivalent is a connection to the Anima Mundi, which usually (for mages) is several layers deep (going via the Oneiros and Temenos) but a physical location should be connected directly to the world soul/part of the world soul. And in that case the Iris would only connect to the related part of the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Is there an equivalent for Avernian gates to compare? Like without Making you can open existing gates. With Making are you able to connect any location in the material to any location (which you know about) in the Underworld??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T03:16:56-08:00","id":1501600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501597#post1501597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like the astral equivalent is a connection to the Anima Mundi, which usually (for mages) is several layers deep (going via the Oneiros and Temenos) but a physical location should be connected directly to the world soul/part of the world soul. And in that case the Iris would only connect to the related part of the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Is there an equivalent for Avernian gates to compare? Like without Making you can open existing gates. With Making are you able to connect any location in the material to any location (which you know about) in the Underworld??</div> </div> </div> </div>Synesi connect to specific Astral locations, so you could basically just replace &quot;Avernian Gate&quot; and &quot;Underworld&quot; with &quot;Synesi&quot; and &quot;The Astral&quot; on the <u>Create Avernian Gate</u> spell. That is, it would connect to something appropriate to the location as the base spell (the Onieros of anyone using it? The Tenemos Realm of the Synesi's physical location?) and a Reach will open to a specified place in the Astral as a whole that the caster has been to before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T16:12:00-08:00","id":1501643,"title":"","content":"Did previous versions of the Mage 2e core rulebook have a +2 Reach option for Platonic Form and Eidolon to make the spells Lasting? My version of the core rulebook at least doesn't have those reach options, but the site I sometimes so check spell effects when I don't have access to the books has that reach listed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T01:24:20-08:00","id":1501673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501643#post1501643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did previous versions of the Mage 2e core rulebook have a +2 Reach option for Platonic Form and Eidolon to make the spells Lasting? My version of the core rulebook at least doesn't have those reach options, but the site I sometimes so check spell effects when I don't have access to the books has that reach listed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those reach effects are from the old version of the core. The updated one has indeed removed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T02:46:51-08:00","id":1501679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501673#post1501673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those reach effects are from the old version of the core. The updated one has indeed removed them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it was lasting, Platonic form would dissapear if it ran out of mana, right?<br /> <br /> Should an inert piece of Tass made from mana should be lasting by default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T03:08:37-08:00","id":1501680,"title":"","content":"Related question, should Create Tass be a (lasting) Ruling practice, like platonic form but only allowing an inert object to be created.<br /> <br /> No equipment bonus, additional durability? Or ability to spend mana from the object (requiring channel mana to remove it)<br /> <br /> Possibly with an optional conjunctional Life 2 to make it 'food'.<br /> <br /> Seperately can a mage withdraw mana from a Platonic form without using channel mana?<br /> <br /> And if not, is this different from imbued items and/or mana batteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T03:32:28-08:00","id":1501687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501680#post1501680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question, should Create Tass be a (lasting) Ruling practice, like platonic form but only allowing an inert object to be created.<br /> <br /> No equipment bonus, additional durability? Or ability to spend mana from the object (requiring channel mana to remove it)<br /> <br /> Possibly with an optional conjunctional Life 2 to make it 'food'.<br /> <br /> Seperately can a mage withdraw mana from a Platonic form without using channel mana?<br /> <br /> And if not, is this different from imbued items and/or mana batteries?</div> </div> </div> </div>While not outright stated, the wording of SoS's section on Mana Batteries implies that while a <u>Create Tass</u> spell does exist or is at least RAW-legal, the effects are temporary. Gimme a sec and I'll see about editing in the relevant quote.<br /> <br /> EDIT: SoS, Page 70<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The next logical step is to imbue an item with Mana but no spells. Some crafters are content to channel Mana into a physical form to create tass. This kind of storage is short term, as when all the Mana is used up the physical form crumbles away. Some mages trade created tass, knowing the spell under their control will be used up shortly and, if not, she can always prematurely end her spell to regain her spell control slot </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-30-2023, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T06:11:43-08:00","id":1501694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501687#post1501687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While not outright stated, the wording of SoS's section on Mana Batteries implies that while a <u>Create Tass</u> spell does exist or is at least RAW-legal, the effects are temporary. Gimme a sec and I'll see about editing in the relevant quote.<br /> <br /> EDIT: SoS, Page 70<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> I wonder though if this is refering to Platonic Form, which can be used for tp mana batteries, with one durability and no potency used for anything else.<br /> <br /> But it is weaving. My thought is that Mana naturally coaleses into Tass, so there should be a ruling spell which replicates the effect (or Compelling in the right circumstances, but i think Ruling to force it to happen when it wouldn't otherwise).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T09:22:06-08:00","id":1501719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501679#post1501679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if it was lasting, Platonic form would dissapear if it ran out of mana, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, indefinite, not lasting, but yes it would disappear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should an inert piece of Tass made from mana should be lasting by default? </div> </div> </div>Nope, it still lasts as long as the spell.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501680#post1501680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question, should Create Tass be a (lasting) Ruling practice, like platonic form but only allowing an inert object to be created.<br /> <br /> No equipment bonus, additional durability? Or ability to spend mana from the object (requiring channel mana to remove it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Platonic Form already is the 2e version of Create Tass, as well as Phantasm and Phantasmal Weapon. The spell's wording might be a bit weird, but if you check out the other mentions of tass throughout the book you'll find that it's the same as the one mentioned in the spell description. Accordingly, you still need Channel Mana to access the Mana in the created tass if it cannot be consumed somehow, even if it's just &quot;inert&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly with an optional conjunctional Life 2 to make it 'food'. </div> </div> </div>Depends on your interpretation of whether natural tass that manifests as food is the same as regular food or just looks like it. If it's the same, then the Life component would be unnecessary. Personally, I'd say it's not the same and that you'd need Life/Matter 3 to make the tass food also physically nourishing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seperately can a mage withdraw mana from a Platonic form without using channel mana? </div> </div> </div>No, as clarified in the previous point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if not, is this different from imbued items and/or mana batteries? </div> </div> </div>Mana batteries do not require Channel Mana to absorb their Mana, while tass and imbued items do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T19:57:51-08:00","id":1501843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501719#post1501719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana batteries do not require Channel Mana to absorb their Mana, while tass and imbued items do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important point, that. You don't need <u>Channel Mana</u> to pull Mana <i>out</i>, but you do to put Mana <i>in. </i>\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:02:01-08:00","id":1501977,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily a simple question but here is quite active.<br /> <br /> On the <b>Boston Unveiled</b> book, there is a 3/4 Mysterium cabal (The Company) that is not at all like a Mysterium is depicted in the Order book nor in the second edition core. No research to speak-off, a focus on the commercial side of the fallen world, no treating magic as a valuable thing in itself.<br /> <br /> My questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is this 1st edition early weirdness that should be ignored?</li> <li>If previous question answer is NO, what do cabals like these bring to the Mysterium? Why would you tolerate such members instead of sending them to say, Free Council or simply disavow them?</li> <li>Could you rise to the Egregore (merit high values, 4 or 5) and Status (high values, 4 or 5) while not contributing real academic / occult research? Just being skilled in the Arcana and doing favours for the other Order members?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:20:59-08:00","id":1501981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501977#post1501977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily a simple question but here is quite active.<br /> <br /> On the <b>Boston Unveiled</b> book, there is a 3/4 Mysterium cabal (The Company) that is not at all like a Mysterium is depicted in the Order book nor in the second edition core. No research to speak-off, a focus on the commercial side of the fallen world, no treating magic as a valuable thing in itself.<br /> <br /> My questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is this 1st edition early weirdness that should be ignored?</li> <li>If previous question answer is NO, what do cabals like these bring to the Mysterium? Why would you tolerate such members instead of sending them to say, Free Council or simply disavow them?</li> <li>Could you rise to the Egregore (merit high values, 4 or 5) and Status (high values, 4 or 5) while not contributing real academic / occult research? Just being skilled in the Arcana and doing favours for the other Order members?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Different areas have different behaviors. The Company is unusual -and is more like an Arrow Free Company- but hardly impossible. Nothing wrong with ignoring it if you don't like it, but it's a good way to show how the Orders are far less homogeneous than they like to claim.<br /> <br /> 2. So, the big thing to remember with the Orders is that membership is one of acknowledgement. If you know a bit about Free Masons, think of it like their Lodges. Mason Lodges are largely &quot;official&quot; based on mutual acknowledgement of authenticity between lodges. For example, the Mason lodges that accept women or don't require belief in a higher power aren't always acknowledged as official by more traditional lodges. The Orders are much the same, and organizations like The Company make a good example of that.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's always an advantage to having someone to turn to for your dirty work. &quot;We didnt do it, it was those Company rapscalions!&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Building on point 2 - promotions and initiation relies on having someone higher up the chain teaching you the right signs and passphrases, or performing your initiation. All it takes for a splinter sect to form is for someone High up enough to decide they have a different way they want to do things. Or for an underling to kiss the right asses.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's really important to remember that the Orders aren't monolithic organizations like a country's Army or intelligence service. They're cults, and cell-based cults to boot. They may have the same overall goal, and similar trappings, but every caucus -heck, even every individual- has their own agenda and individual interpretation of the creed. Heck, the Jnanamukti and the Daksha are great examples of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-02-2023, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:05:43-08:00","id":1502043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501981#post1501981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Different areas have different behaviors. The Company is unusual -and is more like an Arrow Free Company- but hardly impossible. Nothing wrong with ignoring it if you don't like it, but it's a good way to show how the Orders are far less homogeneous than they like to claim.<br /> <br /> 2. So, the big thing to remember with the Orders is that membership is one of acknowledgement. If you know a bit about Free Masons, think of it like their Lodges. Mason Lodges are largely &quot;official&quot; based on mutual acknowledgement of authenticity between lodges. For example, the Mason lodges that accept women or don't require belief in a higher power aren't always acknowledged as official by more traditional lodges. The Orders are much the same, and organizations like The Company make a good example of that.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's always an advantage to having someone to turn to for your dirty work. &quot;We didnt do it, it was those Company rapscalions!&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Building on point 2 - promotions and initiation relies on having someone higher up the chain teaching you the right signs and passphrases, or performing your initiation. All it takes for a splinter sect to form is for someone High up enough to decide they have a different way they want to do things. Or for an underling to kiss the right asses.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's really important to remember that the Orders aren't monolithic organizations like a country's Army or intelligence service. They're cults, and cell-based cults to boot. They may have the same overall goal, and similar trappings, but every caucus -heck, even every individual- has their own agenda and individual interpretation of the creed. Heck, the Jnanamukti and the Daksha are great examples of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Given your answers on point 2 and 3, it would then not be unusual to have a Mysterium PC that likes magic because it gives them new toys to play with, love the scientific method ((Bricoleurs faction draws) and that is its focus to be more magically skilled, to make his life easier but not necessarily crush people down (Seers), fight for Democracy (Free Council) or focused on governing (Silver Ladder).<br /> <br /> Even if this guy is not truly a believer, he can eventually get far in the order (Status 5, Egregore 5) right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Added explanation for Bricoleurs. 02-03-2023, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:45:24-08:00","id":1502048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502043#post1502043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Given your answers on point 2 and 3, it would then not be unusual to have a Mysterium PC that likes magic because it gives them new toys to play with, love the scientific method ((Bricoleurs faction draws) and that is its focus to be more magically skilled, to make his life easier but not necessarily crush people down (Seers), fight for Democracy (Free Council) or focused on governing (Silver Ladder).<br /> <br /> Even if this guy is not truly a believer, he can eventually get far in the order (Status 5, Egregore 5) right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much he embodies the spirit of it in practice. Egregores focus on preserving the knowledge that cannot be easily written down, like impressions, scenes and ineffable experiences. They also allow the mage to more effectively travel the globe on research and requisition more specialized knowledge. Should they wish to rediscover knowledge or even experiment with the limits of magic, then they will probably be fine, provided they mind the protocol.<br /> <br /> With that said, the Free Council might also attract them. Not all members focus exclusively on democracy. The Libertines allow for a non-vertical command structure, an interest in using mundane technology to redefine the bleeding edge of knowledge and a more easily accessible platform for buying and selling magical goods.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium has more exotic collections, the Free Council has lots of prototypes. Both are great for someone seeking to expand their toolkit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T15:04:19-08:00","id":1502052,"title":"","content":"I don't see why a PC would care to spent the effort, time and work to get to status 5 in the Order is they were not a true believer.<br /> <br /> Not to say mechanically they couldn't just narratively it seems like it would be rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T15:14:40-08:00","id":1502053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502052#post1502052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why a PC would care to spent the effort, time and work to get to status 5 in the Order is they were not a true believer.<br /> <br /> Not to say mechanically they couldn't just narratively it seems like it would be rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Orders have significant advantages in-game, you might want to access mystical resources, have mage allies, or get Artifacts, Imbued Items, spells casts for you, Retainers, Resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Trying to make a religious comparison: I dont really believe in the the Catholic Church dogma, but I am certain I would enjoy the perks of being a Cardinal or Bishop, I do want unrestricted access to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Library\" target=\"_blank\">Vatican Library</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Apostolic_Archive\" target=\"_blank\">Apostolic Archive</a>.<br /> <br /> Of course the church example is bad because to grow in the church you have to be seen doing church related beliefs (and not all Cardinals have reasons to be loitering around Vatican libraries) but given Cauthon examples, I am asking if its feasible to have a high status Pentacle mage that does not really focus on all aspects of its Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Expanded example with the Vatican. 02-03-2023, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T15:44:29-08:00","id":1502057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502053#post1502053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Orders have significant advantages in-game, you might want to access mystical resources, have mage allies, or get Artifacts, Imbued Items, spells casts for you, Retainers, Resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Trying to make a religious comparison: I dont really believe in the the Catholic Church dogma, but I am certain I would enjoy the perks of being a Cardinal or Bishop, I do want unrestricted access to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Library\" target=\"_blank\">Vatican Library</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Apostolic_Archive\" target=\"_blank\">Apostolic Archive</a>.<br /> <br /> Of course the church example is bad because to grow in the church you have to be seen doing church related beliefs (and not all Cardinals have reasons to be loitering around Vatican libraries) but given Cauthon examples, I am asking if its feasible to have a high status Pentacle mage that does not really focus on all aspects of its Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be possible, but likely difficult to become a Hierophant. Up to that point you can probably get away with playing politics and finding someone to kiss up to. But without a body of work as a resume most orthodox Heirophants won't want to promote you, and the person you're sucking up to probably won't want to lose their toady unless they're getting &quot;promoted&quot; to Hierophant Superior themselves.<br /> <br /> Egregore, I'm less sure of. There's an element of &quot;this is how you do the thing&quot; in all of the Order merits, but the key to their use seems to be the integration of Order symbolism into yourself. I think, personally, that the character needs to believe in order to learn Egregore, Lex Magica, Tech\u00e9, Masque, or Adamant Fist. Granted, I'm also of the opinion that you can learn them if you bought the one-dot-of-status-in-another-Order you're allowed to have. An Arrow Sentinel who works closely with the local Lictor in the course of their duties could plausibly have taken in enough Ladder symbolism to justify Lex Magica, just as a Guardian-assisting Reclamator could learn how to build Masques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T17:19:10-08:00","id":1502065,"title":"","content":"Tangentially related:<br /> You can gain one dot of Status with at most one Order besides your own. The Ally Merit would cover most social interactions, so does that mean the Status qualifies you for that order's Rote Skills and Order Tools? I house rule that it gives you access to the Order-specific merits, but I know that isn't a universal opinion and without those it seems kinda pointless. I think a 5-dot Masque can emulate Order-specific traits, but that's a bit of an edge case. <br /> Similarly, can a Pentacle Mage progress higher than one dot in a Nameless Order Mystery Cult, or is it treated like an Order in that regard? I generally assume the Status limit is political, but given the symbolic nature of the Orders I could see them creating metaphysical limitations on you. Nameless Orders using the Mystery Cult merit is a matter of design convenience anyway, so the rules on it are a bit murky.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T19:43:02-08:00","id":1502076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502065#post1502065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially related:<br /> You can gain one dot of Status with at most one Order besides your own. The Ally Merit would cover most social interactions, so does that mean the Status qualifies you for that order's Rote Skills and Order Tools? I house rule that it gives you access to the Order-specific merits, but I know that isn't a universal opinion and without those it seems kinda pointless. I think a 5-dot Masque can emulate Order-specific traits, but that's a bit of an edge case.<br /> Similarly, can a Pentacle Mage progress higher than one dot in a Nameless Order Mystery Cult, or is it treated like an Order in that regard? I generally assume the Status limit is political, but given the symbolic nature of the Orders I could see them creating metaphysical limitations on you. Nameless Orders using the Mystery Cult merit is a matter of design convenience anyway, so the rules on it are a bit murky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect Order Tools and requisitions were intended as the main benefit of multi-Order membership. Though I\u2019m away from my pdfs and will need to double-check to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T21:29:51-08:00","id":1502083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502076#post1502076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect Order Tools and requisitions were intended as the main benefit of multi-Order membership. Though I\u2019m away from my pdfs and will need to double-check to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requisitions are specifically cited as not being available to the hypothetical 1-dot-status outsider, sadly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T02:04:08-08:00","id":1502087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502076#post1502076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect Order Tools and requisitions were intended as the main benefit of multi-Order membership. Though I\u2019m away from my pdfs and will need to double-check to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>A single dot of Order Status without requisition rights is what the system suggests as part of the &quot;if your character works closely with a second Order&quot; caveat to &quot;Order status is usually limited to one Order.&quot;<br /> <br /> Being able to be treated as an honorary member of a second Order is more likely for the Status Merit benefits of that Order Status \u2014 you have access to Caucus facilities, benefit from the bonus die on the Status 0 rank-and-file, and can get a foot in the door to request meetings as though you were a ground-floor member of the Caucus in good standing instead of Some Arrow From The Local Consilium, and this is contingent upon the same level of upkeep you'd me maintaining to be in the Mob's good books as a &quot;trusted business associate.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502053#post1502053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to make a religious comparison: I dont really believe in the the Catholic Church dogma, but I am certain I would enjoy the perks of being a Cardinal or Bishop, I do want unrestricted access to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Library\" target=\"_blank\">Vatican Library</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_Apostolic_Archive\" target=\"_blank\">Apostolic Archive</a>.<br /> <br /> Of course the church example is bad because to grow in the church you have to be seen doing church related beliefs (and not all Cardinals have reasons to be loitering around Vatican libraries) but given Cauthon examples, I am asking if its feasible to have a high status Pentacle mage that does not really focus on all aspects of its Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might very well enjoy the benefits of being a bishop or a cardinal, but I guarantee you that if you aren't really committed to acting the part you are not going to want to take on the responsibilities of that post long-term to get them. Order Status is Status; it is subject to the Drawback of the Status Merit.<br /> <br /> If you want to explore in detail a bunch of hypothetical variations on &quot;how much can I distance a character's Status rating from the way they conduct themselves?&quot; I would recommend making a separate thread for that, because this is looking increasingly unlike a simple question.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T02:43:13-08:00","id":1502088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502083#post1502083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Requisitions are specifically cited as not being available to the hypothetical 1-dot-status outsider, sadly</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they not be available? Apart from the limits of availability which would really restrict them given their single dot in status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T03:07:28-08:00","id":1502089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502088#post1502088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they not be available? Apart from the limits of availability which would really restrict them given their single dot in status.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you are a member of the other Order and only a fool would give out stuff to you just so you could use it for the other order...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T04:19:52-08:00","id":1502093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502089#post1502089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you are a member of the other Order and only a fool would give out stuff to you just so you could use it for the other order...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502088#post1502088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they not be available? Apart from the limits of availability which would really restrict them given their single dot in status.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orders are allies, but even the closest allies have things they keep from each other.the Pentacle functions together for survival more than anything else.<br /> <br /> Which ultimately means that without giving you access to Order Tools, Rote Skills, and/or Order Merits, then the one dot of status is objectively pointless, given you can take an unlimited volume of Allies (X Order) dots, so long as there are Orders to befriend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2023, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T08:52:37-08:00","id":1502106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502089#post1502089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you are a member of the other Order and only a fool would give out stuff to you just so you could use it for the other order...</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the Services list, there is very little you can get (in terms of mundane services) with one dot of status.<br /> <br /> A self defense class is the only thing you could get.<br /> <br /> So what about limiting the requisitions like this doesn't make sense for close allies.<br /> <br /> For Orders requisitioning merit, it would take a week to organise, be temporary and afford you a 1 dot Alternate Identity, Retainer, Imbued Item, Artifact, Grimoire, Mentor, Hallow, Sanctum, Library, Safe Place, and Resource\u200b.<br /> <br /> That is the worst possible of grimoire, imbued items or artifacts. The weakest hallow, the most basic library resource. And the smallest amount of resources. And the worst imaginable sanctum or safe place. Which depending on how you read the pre-requisites for santumn, you can only get a safe place and not both.<br /> <br /> Most Orders could easily afford the mundane resources. Maybe they would want to be careful of their magical resources, but any 1 dot magical merit is barely worth the process that went into making it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T09:35:29-08:00","id":1502109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502106#post1502106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what about limiting the requisitions like this doesn't make sense for close allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where these are secretly-operating grand cults dealing with magical resources and societal cachet and Signs of Sorcery introduces an entire elaboration that lowers the effective Availability for a resource based on the Order's areas of focus, how long the character is willing to wait for the request to be fulfilled, and other mitigating circumstances like taking a less-popular resource or accepting Conditions. If you open up requisitioning at Status 1 for outsiders you open up requisitioning as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Orders requisitioning merit, it would take a week to organise, be temporary and afford you a 1 dot Alternate Identity, Retainer, Imbued Item, Artifact, Grimoire, Mentor, Hallow, Sanctum, Library, Safe Place, and Resource\u200b.<br /> <br /> That is the worst possible of grimoire, imbued items or artifacts. The weakest hallow, the most basic library resource. And the smallest amount of resources. And the worst imaginable sanctum or safe place. Which depending on how you read the pre-requisites for santumn, you can only get a safe place and not both. </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as a one-dot Artifact, but also the things I just mentioned above mean allowing requisitioning outside your Order would permit you to get waitlisted for a four-dot Hallow or a permanent Rank 1 Familiar with the only consistent mechanical cost being that it'd take three chapters to come through.<br /> <br /> Being able to count as a Status 1 member of another Order means you are welcome by the local Caucus as a known cooperator with the Order as though you had the standing of a normal member like a Talon, Acolyte, or Acquisitor \u2014 being Shamrock the Ladder Acanthus Who We Work With Regularly On Mysteries Relating To Irish Folklore doesn't give you the personal pull in the global organization of the Mysterium necessary to personally call on their resources in a way that can potentially propagate upwards to &quot;we'll need to check in with the Rio Atheneum, but we can probably get it for you by April&quot; or be initiated into the secrets of the Egregore.<br /> <br /> By the same token, having Allies (Silver Ladder) 5, if your ST treats that as at all coherent (because, again, global arcane cult), is going to have the favors its membership can provide you throttled by what the ST determines can be reasonably requested. More likely if you're able to swing the equivalent of renting a moderately valuable Hallow through Allies in another Order it's because you're leaning on specific Allies with that kind of requisitioning power, which comes with its own complications, and also connects you in a way with different optics than simply being The Guardian Who We Have A Working Relationship With.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T10:48:01-08:00","id":1502113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502109#post1502109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part where these are secretly-operating grand cults dealing with magical resources and societal cachet and Signs of Sorcery introduces an entire elaboration that lowers the effective Availability for a resource based on the Order's areas of focus, how long the character is willing to wait for the request to be fulfilled, and other mitigating circumstances like taking a less-popular resource or accepting Conditions. If you open up requisitioning at Status 1 for outsiders you open up requisitioning as a whole.<br /> <br /> There is no such thing as a one-dot Artifact, but also the things I just mentioned above mean allowing requisitioning outside your Order would permit you to get waitlisted for a four-dot Hallow or a permanent Rank 1 Familiar with the only consistent mechanical cost being that it'd take three chapters to come through.<br /> <br /> Being able to count as a Status 1 member of another Order means you are welcome by the local Caucus as a known cooperator with the Order as though you had the standing of a normal member like a Talon, Acolyte, or Acquisitor \u2014 being Shamrock the Ladder Acanthus Who We Work With Regularly On Mysteries Relating To Irish Folklore doesn't give you the personal pull in the global organization of the Mysterium necessary to personally call on their resources in a way that can potentially propagate upwards to &quot;we'll need to check in with the Rio Atheneum, but we can probably get it for you by April&quot; or be initiated into the secrets of the Egregore.<br /> <br /> By the same token, having Allies (Silver Ladder) 5, if your ST treats that as at all coherent (because, again, global arcane cult), is going to have the favors its membership can provide you throttled by what the ST determines can be reasonably requested. More likely if you're able to swing the equivalent of renting a moderately valuable Hallow through Allies in another Order it's because you're leaning on specific Allies with that kind of requisitioning power, which comes with its own complications, and also connects you in a way with different optics than simply being The Guardian Who We Have A Working Relationship With.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Allies (the pre-eminent Ladder Cabal in the consillium) could concievably allow you ask them if they can get access to a Hallow for the weekend. Where they use their Order status to requisition the Hallow and then let you join them when they use the Hallow... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:02:37-08:00","id":1502129,"title":"","content":"If a gun that has <i>Ephemeral Enchantment</i> applied to it hits its target in Twilight, what happens to the bullet? Does a hollow point fragment and keep &quot;floating&quot; in midair ? Does a standard bullet keep going after hitting &quot;thin air&quot; ? In short, what does it look like for those who cannot perceive that phase of Twilight, and are they at greater risk of being caught in the crossfire than a normal firefight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:05:36-08:00","id":1502130,"title":"","content":"An Exceptional Success can grant a condition that grants beats AND Fate Boons only grant beats when from an exceptional success... These are additive, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Casting the Spell p. 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Success: The spell\u2019s effect takes place better than<br /> imagined.<b> The character regains one spent point of Willpower,<br /> and the player may choose one of the following results</b>;<br /> \u2022 A bonus step in the primary spell factor.<br /> <br /> \u2022 A Reach in the primary spell factor.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 A Condition which will give Arcane Beats when resolved,<br /> on either the mage or her subject.</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 All Mana spent on the spell is refunded, and the mage<br /> receives one more point of Mana.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The spell ignores any Withstand levels and takes effect at<br /> full Potency.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boons p.134</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grant a number of beneficial Conditions (such as Charmed,<br /> Informed, Inspired, or Steadfast) equal to Potency for the<br /> Duration of the spell. None of these Conditions grant<br /> Beats when the subject resolves them (<b>unless the caster<br /> achieved an exceptional success in the casting</b>)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand here that the Condition from achieving an Exceptional Success is distinct from any Fate granted conditions which only grant beats IF you got an exceptional success, adding to the on benefit of exceptional success not replacing it.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>So if you got an Exceptional Success on Exceptional Luck praxis, assuming you get 3 successes: You get 1 Condition from Exceptional Success AND 3 from Exceptional Luck, all of them granting Beats. Right?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:45:21-08:00","id":1502135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502130#post1502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Exceptional Success can grant a condition that grants beats AND Fate Boons only grant beats when from an exceptional success... These are additive, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I understand here that the Condition from achieving an Exceptional Success is distinct from any Fate granted conditions which only grant beats IF you got an exceptional success, adding to the on benefit of exceptional success not replacing it.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>So if you got an Exceptional Success on Exceptional Luck praxis, assuming you get 3 successes: You get 1 Condition from Exceptional Success AND 3 from Exceptional Luck, all of them granting Beats. Right?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>3 from the boon? Not unless you allocated 3 levels of spell Potency. The number of successes rolled in the spellcasting roll only matter when determining if the spellcasting roll is an exceptional success or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:46:10-08:00","id":1502136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502129#post1502129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a gun that has <i>Ephemeral Enchantment</i> applied to it hits its target in Twilight, what happens to the bullet? Does a hollow point fragment and keep &quot;floating&quot; in midair ? Does a standard bullet keep going after hitting &quot;thin air&quot; ? In short, what does it look like for those who cannot perceive that phase of Twilight, and are they at greater risk of being caught in the crossfire than a normal firefight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would rule that it does &quot;float&quot; in midair, assuming it didn't have enough force to pass through whatever it hit. That would also mean Sleepers watching it would Dissonance it very quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502130#post1502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>So if you got an Exceptional Success on Exceptional Luck praxis, assuming you get 3 successes: You get 1 Condition from Exceptional Success AND 3 from Exceptional Luck, all of them granting Beats. Right?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><s>Yeeeeees... I think that parses right.</s> Nope, nvm, go with what Hermit said. Also important to note is that you can only Resolve one Condition per scene, which may limit the &quot;endless Beats&quot; utility a tiny bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2023, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:52:41-08:00","id":1502157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502135#post1502135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3 from the boon? Not unless you allocated 3 levels of spell Potency. The number of successes rolled in the spellcasting roll only matter when determining if the spellcasting roll is an exceptional success or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502136#post1502136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><s>Yeeeeees... I think that parses right.</s> Nope, nvm, go with what Hermit said. Also important to note is that you can only Resolve one Condition per scene, which may limit the &quot;endless Beats&quot; utility a tiny bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, but then it becomes: <b> 1 Condition from Exceptional Success AND Potency/Conditions from Exceptional Luck, all of them capable granting Beats (even if you get only one per scene). Right?</b>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T16:38:40-08:00","id":1502166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502157#post1502157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but then it becomes: <b> 1 Condition from Exceptional Success AND Potency/Conditions from Exceptional Luck, all of them capable granting Beats (even if you get only one per scene). Right?</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the caster got an Exceptional Success, then yes, the Conditions can indeed be resolved for Beats. That all parses correctly to me.<br /> <br /> Of note, since I think this is related to your other thread, things like this are an acknowledged part of the game design. The &quot;The Beat Goes On&quot; sidebar on page 126 touches on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2023, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T06:47:19-08:00","id":1502201,"title":"","content":"<u><b>What is exactly the Free Council* Symbolism?</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The order tools are a Yantra that have specific symbolism tied to the Order ethos (Authority, Conflict, Knowledge, Concealing Identity, Culture, Tyranny). And those are &quot;<i><u>mundane items</u> that have a symbolic link to specific kinds of magic\u200b</i>&quot; so that means physical tangible items (only the <b>Broad Dedication</b> merit allows for intangible Yantras as Dedicated Tools)\u200b.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Order Tools</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Order\u2019s Magical Tools draw upon that Order\u2019s symbols<br /> rather than those of the Supernal world directly, focusing mag-<br /> ic in a way that matches their teachings. The formal magical<br /> style of the Diamond Orders and the Seers of the Throne all<br /> resonate through the same tools \u2014 the <b>Arrow </b>uses martial Tools<br /> as <b>symbols of conflict</b>; the <b>Guardians</b> use cloaks, masks, and<br /> veils as <b>symbols of things hidden and revealed</b>; the <b>Mysterium</b><br /> teaches books, writing, and language as <b>Tools of knowledge and<br /> communication</b>; and the <b>Silver Ladder</b> uses signs of authority to<br /> as Tools of <b>status and persuasion</b>. The Seers of the Throne each<br /> choose a sigil or word that they must display to use it as a Tool.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, IF I am getting it right the Order tool of an Arrow adds +1 bonus when used as symbol of conflict (defense, attack, perhaps a social contest) and Mysterium members would add +1 from the Order tool when using a spell to find or get knowledge (perhaps also hide it?) and to spells to communicate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Order Tools</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> The <b>Free Council </b>are an oddity among all the other Orders.<br /> While every Libertine may <b>use complex mechanisms and systems</b><br /> as Order Tools, the <b>Techn\u00e9 </b>Merit allows a Libertine to focus on<br /> a personal style of magic based on Sleeper culture, using it as<br /> an additional Tool in her magic.\u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Techn\u00e9 </b>allows the &quot;<i>use cultural magical styles, sciences, and art forms as magical tools</i>&quot; so it is clear that it is talking about intangibles too (Computer Networking is the example from the merit description), so this is another exception to the physical item part.<br /> <br /> <br /> But being &quot;<i>complex mechanisms and systems</i>&quot; is a description of what tools can be, not of what they represent, so<b> in which situations do I get the +1 Order tool semiotic bonus for the Free Council? </b>The Order description talks about Culture... but I get to use the +1 bonus when I am doing what exactly?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *A similar question could be asked of the Seers, do they apply the +1 bonus of their sigil / word usage to EVERY spell not just those enforcing or aligned to Tyranny???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-05-2023, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:36:25-08:00","id":1502243,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 I\u2019d just hand-wave the exact words for that sentence, and declare the Council\u2019s Order Tools to be <i>physical items that represent </i>complex mechanisms and systems.<br /> <br /> An elected official\u2019s badge of office, for example, represents the complex system that is modern liberal democracy. (Which is something a Thearch could also use, since it symbolizes authority too.)<br /> <br /> However, that badge likely only applies to spells that relate to organization, leadership, communication, empowerment, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Seers, the particular sigil/word they brandish likely has to be that of an Exarch whose dominion aligns with the spell invoked. Invoking The General while throwing fireballs? Yup. Invoking The Eye while doing the same? Uh\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:49:32-08:00","id":1502245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21c hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502243#post1502243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invoking the Eye while doing the same? Uh\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>FBI! Open up! (NSA, open up?)<br /> <br /> More seriously, the FC has a bit of a grab-bag feel to them. Where the other Orders mostly focus on the invocation of somewhat ridged themes (simplified to Secrecy, Knowledge, Order, and Oaths/Violence), the FC focuses on &quot;Innovation&quot;. That can mean Innovation in the inventive sense, using technology, but it can also be invoked on ideas that differ from the current &quot;mainstream&quot;. The latest smartphone is just as valid as an obscure musical style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-05-2023, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:11:50-08:00","id":1502269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502201#post1502201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>What is exactly the Free Council* Symbolism?</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The order tools are a Yantra that have specific symbolism tied to the Order ethos (Authority, Conflict, Knowledge, Concealing Identity, Culture, Tyranny). And those are &quot;<i><u>mundane items</u> that have a symbolic link to specific kinds of magic\u200b</i>&quot; so that means physical tangible items (only the <b>Broad Dedication</b> merit allows for intangible Yantras as Dedicated Tools)\u200b.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, IF I am getting it right the Order tool of an Arrow adds +1 bonus when used as symbol of conflict (defense, attack, perhaps a social contest) and Mysterium members would add +1 from the Order tool when using a spell to find or get knowledge (perhaps also hide it?) and to spells to communicate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Techn\u00e9 </b>allows the &quot;<i>use cultural magical styles, sciences, and art forms as magical tools</i>&quot; so it is clear that it is talking about intangibles too (Computer Networking is the example from the merit description), so this is another exception to the physical item part.<br /> <br /> <br /> But being &quot;<i>complex mechanisms and systems</i>&quot; is a description of what tools can be, not of what they represent, so<b> in which situations do I get the +1 Order tool semiotic bonus for the Free Council? </b>The Order description talks about Culture... but I get to use the +1 bonus when I am doing what exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>You say this like tools can't be used to multiple interprertations. In the same way a meaning can be expressed in several different symbols (Like how the words &quot;tree&quot; and &quot;\u6728&quot; both signify the same thing despite not sounding or looking like each other), a symbol can be used to infer multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> Anyways, in specific, the systems represent what is reasonable to associate with those, and particularly given their context in their respective culture. The operations of an accounting office is simultaneuously a viable semiotic for unveiling hidden or lost things, divining an answer to complex question, or imparting the feelings and thoughts of tedium, innatity, and futility on someone. What it probably won't work for is conjuring a pillar of fire to smite your foes-but a religious meeting with back to back sermons about divine retribution and smiting the wicked could do quite well with that. By contrast, a Christian service is going to have different resonances to a Buddhist funeral, and both of those are going be different vehicles compared to a reconstructionist Celtic sacred festival.<br /> <br /> It takes both critical thinking, to thoroughly understand human cultures as they are AND as symbols, and imagination, to find clever ways to apply the myriad elements of the symbol of human cultures to ways to redescribe reality, to make the use of the various forms of Techne, which is fitting for a Sect that prizes the nuance and involvement of human cultures and how it interacts with reality. It's very potent for it's flexibility, and certainly in the ways it can be supported, but only for those who are willing to use the whole fruit, to borrow from an old analogy between the Diamond's juice and the Free Council's cider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-05-2023, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T17:51:38-08:00","id":1502470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502269#post1502269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say this like tools can't be used to multiple interprertations. In the same way a meaning can be expressed in several different symbols (Like how the words &quot;tree&quot; and &quot;\u6728&quot; both signify the same thing despite not sounding or looking like each other), a symbol can be used to infer multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> Anyways, in specific, the systems represent what is reasonable to associate with those, and particularly given their context in their respective culture. The operations of an accounting office is simultaneuously a viable semiotic for unveiling hidden or lost things, divining an answer to complex question, or imparting the feelings and thoughts of tedium, innatity, and futility on someone. What it probably won't work for is conjuring a pillar of fire to smite your foes-but a religious meeting with back to back sermons about divine retribution and smiting the wicked could do quite well with that. By contrast, a Christian service is going to have different resonances to a Buddhist funeral, and both of those are going be different vehicles compared to a reconstructionist Celtic sacred festival.<br /> <br /> It takes both critical thinking, to thoroughly understand human cultures as they are AND as symbols, and imagination, to find clever ways to apply the myriad elements of the symbol of human cultures to ways to redescribe reality, to make the use of the various forms of Techne, which is fitting for a Sect that prizes the nuance and involvement of human cultures and how it interacts with reality. It's very potent for it's flexibility, and certainly in the ways it can be supported, but only for those who are willing to use the whole fruit, to borrow from an old analogy between the Diamond's juice and the Free Council's cider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your answer. My questions are more focused on the Free Council physical tools, as the other others had some specific use cases (Tools of Conflict, tools of Persuasion, tools of Knowledge/Communicaiton) what are the specific use cases for Free Council tools?<br /> <br /> All the Order descriptions on the Core 2e show what the tools can be AND what can they be used for, but (At least for me) is not clear what can they be used for in the Free Council case.<br /> <br /> So I know that I can dedicate a Cellphone but what is the *standard* use case for it with the Free Council (not considering any creative cases)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T18:39:10-08:00","id":1502472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502470#post1502470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for your answer. My questions are more focused on the Free Council physical tools, as the other others had some specific use cases (Tools of Conflict, tools of Persuasion, tools of Knowledge/Communicaiton) what are the specific use cases for Free Council tools?<br /> <br /> All the Order descriptions on the Core 2e show what the tools can be AND what can they be used for, but (At least for me) is not clear what can they be used for in the Free Council case.<br /> <br /> So I know that I can dedicate a Cellphone but what is the *standard* use case for it with the Free Council (not considering any creative cases)?</div> </div> </div> </div>A cellphone would be Communication. A modern smartphone could also include themes of Information, since we can connect to the internet and google traslate just about anything we point a camera at. Similarly, you could use the ability to take a picture (and extend that symbolism to any Tool that can function as a camera) as a focus for a Shielding spell; the photo taken represents how the subject <i>should</i> be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T19:20:30-08:00","id":1502475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502470#post1502470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for your answer. My questions are more focused on the Free Council physical tools, as the other others had some specific use cases (Tools of Conflict, tools of Persuasion, tools of Knowledge/Communicaiton) what are the specific use cases for Free Council tools?<br /> <br /> All the Order descriptions on the Core 2e show what the tools can be AND what can they be used for, but (At least for me) is not clear what can they be used for in the Free Council case.<br /> <br /> So I know that I can dedicate a Cellphone but what is the *standard* use case for it with the Free Council (not considering any creative cases)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, what do you think you can use a cellphone as a symbol <i>for</i>? Strictly literal reading is not going to help you here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T06:33:55-08:00","id":1502509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502475#post1502475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, what do you think you can use a cellphone as a symbol <i>for</i>? Strictly literal reading is not going to help you here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it is my lack of English knowledge causing the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium </b>order description says that their symbol is <b>Knowledge </b>and their tools are <b>Knowledge </b>related (books, scribing tools, art that has messages) they get a +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a <b>Knowledge </b>related Yantra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Adamantine Arrow </b>order description says that their symbol is <b>Conflict </b>and their tools are <b>Conflict </b>related (weapons, protective charms) they get a +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a <b>Conflict </b>related Yantra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u200bFree Council</b> describes their tools are &quot;complex mechanisms and systems\u200b&quot; they get a +1 bonus as an order tool as a <b>XXXXX </b>related Yantra. <b>What is XXXXX for the Free Council?</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Clarified the text example, corrected names, fixed some grammar errors. 02-08-2023, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T06:50:58-08:00","id":1502510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502509#post1502509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it is my lack of English knowledge causing the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium </b>Order Description says that their symbol is <b>Knowledge </b>and their tools are <b>Knowledge </b>related (books, scribing tools, art that has messages) they get a +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a <b>Knowledge </b>related Yantra<br /> <br /> <b>Arrow Order</b> Description says that their symbol is <b>Conflict </b>and their tools are <b>Conflict </b>related (weapons, protective charms) they get a +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a <b>Conflict </b>related Yantra<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u200bFree Council</b> describes &quot;complex mechanisms and systems\u200b&quot; but when does the +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a XXXXX related Yantra, what is XXXXX for the Free Council?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Innovation. Technology is the easiest thing to default to, but more broadly the FC taps into the novel applications of pre-existing knowledge and materials.<br /> <br /> More specifically, the FC looks to Sleeper culture for their magical symbolism. The Diamond Orders have a lot of their symbolism tied into schools of thought descended from Greek philosophy. The FC on the other hand just says &quot;fuck that noise&quot;, and grabs whatever local cultural traditions resonate with them. Which can be as simple as &quot;tech bro&quot;, as derivative as &quot;new age hippy&quot; or as poignant as &quot;inheritor of ancestral practices&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Sorry I can't help much with the language barrier, best I can do would be to run it through Google Translate or DeepL. You're from Brussels, right? So Dutch, or French?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-08-2023, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T08:56:26-08:00","id":1502517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502509#post1502509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u200bFree Council</b> describes &quot;complex mechanisms and systems\u200b&quot; but when does the +1 bonus as an order tool when used as a XXXXX related Yantra, what is XXXXX for the Free Council?</div> </div> </div> </div>The base order tool is complex mechanisms and systems. Clockwork. Circuitry. Numerology. Scientific experimentation. Objects and practices that involve many things moving to achieve a defined collective practical end. Ordering things in concert with one another to the end of purposes like keeping time, collating data, making predictions, extrapolating conclusions. A base Free Council yantra is never one discrete object. It might be a watch, but a watch used in a way that exposes that it is many gears and spokes ticking together, whose movements in concert produce what we call a &quot;watch.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Free Council teaches the methods of Techne to extend their order tool to systems aimed at less concrete, defined ends: systems whose purposes are abstract and man-made. Techne allows the order tool bonus to apply to religious liturgies, traditional folk celebrations, artistic pursuits, or professional practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T13:45:32-08:00","id":1502537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502510#post1502510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Innovation. Technology is the easiest thing to default to, but more broadly the FC taps into the novel applications of pre-existing knowledge and materials.<br /> <br /> More specifically, the FC looks to Sleeper culture for their magical symbolism. The Diamond Orders have a lot of their symbolism tied into schools of thought descended from Greek philosophy. The FC on the other hand just says &quot;fuck that noise&quot;, and grabs whatever local cultural traditions resonate with them. Which can be as simple as &quot;tech bro&quot;, as derivative as &quot;new age hippy&quot; or as poignant as &quot;inheritor of ancestral practices&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Sorry I can't help much with the language barrier, best I can do would be to run it through Google Translate or DeepL. You're from Brussels, right? So Dutch, or French?)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502517#post1502517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The base order tool is complex mechanisms and systems. Clockwork. Circuitry. Numerology. Scientific experimentation. Objects and practices that involve many things moving to achieve a defined collective practical end. Ordering things in concert with one another to the end of purposes like keeping time, collating data, making predictions, extrapolating conclusions. A base Free Council yantra is never one discrete object. It might be a watch, but a watch used in a way that exposes that it is many gears and spokes ticking together, whose movements in concert produce what we call a &quot;watch.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Free Council teaches the methods of Techne to extend their order tool to systems aimed at less concrete, defined ends: systems whose purposes are abstract and man-made. Techne allows the order tool bonus to apply to religious liturgies, traditional folk celebrations, artistic pursuits, or professional practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks to both, yes this is what I was asking.<br /> <br /> I was confused about the Culture part of the text on the Order descritption, do you use &quot;complex mechanismis and systems&quot; as a symbol of <b>Culture</b> for a +1 Yantra bonus? But the way you explained makes sense, and expands the usage with Techne.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T17:29:33-08:00","id":1502552,"title":"","content":"It's outside 2e's scope, but... can Archmages go Rapt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T17:41:46-08:00","id":1502556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502552#post1502552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's outside 2e's scope, but... can Archmages go Rapt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I would say so. They still have Wisdom, and Rapture is breaking of the soul from the degradation of Wisdom, though they can probably fix it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T18:39:41-08:00","id":1502562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502556#post1502556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I would say so. They still have Wisdom, and Rapture is breaking of the soul from the degradation of Wisdom, though they can probably fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Left-Hand Path has an entire sidebar on page 52 highlighting the similarities and differences between archmages and the Enraptured \u2014 archmages who hit Wisdom 0 become Qliphoth, and ordinary mages who've hit Wisdom 0 can't cross the Threshold to achieve Imperial Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T18:50:56-08:00","id":1502565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502562#post1502562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Left-Hand Path has an entire sidebar on page 52 highlighting the similarities and differences between archmages and the Enraptured \u2014 archmages who hit Wisdom 0 become Qliphoth, and ordinary mages who've hit Wisdom 0 can't cross the Threshold to achieve Imperial Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, the same Qliphoth that one becomes with 10 Joining? Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T19:00:51-08:00","id":1502566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502565#post1502565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, the same Qliphoth that one becomes with 10 Joining? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Archmage's Golden Road pierces through the Abyss, kept secure by the force of their Wisdom keeping it metaphysically airtight. What happens to a submarine when you stop doing maintenence on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T19:18:02-08:00","id":1502568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502565#post1502565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, the same Qliphoth that one becomes with 10 Joining? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Kelly says. Same thing happens if a prospective Seeker fails the Abyssal Trial or an established archmage suffers the worst form of Imperial Paradox and fails to extricate themselves from the Greater Abyssal Being it entangles them with.<br /> <br /> Qliphoth were <i>introduced</i> as a failstate for archmages. Being able to turn yourself into one as a Scelestus is new to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:15:12-08:00","id":1502776,"title":"","content":"A Sophis item has an internal reservoir that scavenged mana filters into. If you cast <u>Mana Battery</u> on such an object, is that pool's capacity expanded? Or are there now two distinct pools, of which only one can be automatically filled by Sophis' natural effects? I assume the former, but could see the latter being the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-11-2023, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:54:44-08:00","id":1502782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502776#post1502776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sophis item has an iternal reservoir that scavenged mana filters into. If you cast <u>Mana Battery</u> on such an object, is that pool's capacity expanded? Or are there now to distinct pools, of which only one can be automatically filled by Sophis' natural effects? I assume the former, but could see the latter being the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it expands the capacity, in the same way that a Perfecting of Space expands on the carrying capacity of an item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T17:57:00-08:00","id":1502797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502776#post1502776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sophis item has an iternal reservoir that scavenged mana filters into. If you cast <u>Mana Battery</u> on such an object, is that pool's capacity expanded? Or are there now two distinct pools, of which only one can be automatically filled by Sophis' natural effects? I assume the former, but could see the latter being the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to go ahead an assume either depending on the imago of the spell. Because that feels more fun (not that i can think of any reason to do two distinct pools).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T14:56:34-08:00","id":1502961,"title":"","content":"You know, I've been assuming for years on the principle that Susceptors need to be able to do their job that a 5-Dot Masque for Guardians would be able to have dots in other Orders, but on thinking about it, I realized the thing about assuming is that it's the most powerful art of magic if carefully applied, so here I am verifying the idea that one might be able to use Masques for the purposes of acting in other Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T16:53:42-08:00","id":1502970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502961#post1502961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've been assuming for years on the principle that Susceptors need to be able to do their job that a 5-Dot Masque for Guardians would be able to have dots in other Orders, but on thinking about it, I realized the thing about assuming is that it's the most powerful art of magic if carefully applied, so here I am verifying the idea that one might be able to use Masques for the purposes of acting in other Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always assumed that a Masque with Other-Order dots needs some justification for it. Like... Status can be gained by forging the right Letters of Introduction*, or outright earning it while in that persona, but Lex Magica could be gained by Masque-ing your way into a Silver Ladder mindset and then meditating in the Silver Ladder Tenemos Realm for a while. You probably don't <i>need</i> a lot of justification to, say, pose as a 1-dot-Status member of an Order, but there still needs to be one. Masque is more psychological than magical, as far as I understand it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I misunderstood the question, I think. Using a below-5-dots Masque <i>should</i> be able to simulate Merit benefits like Status, so long as the Mage can keep up the fascade. Actually <i>having</i> the dots once you have a 5-dot Masque would then represent the role having gained enough of a papertrail to be effectively true.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">Assuming you can create a plausible backstory where one would be justified</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-13-2023, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T17:43:43-08:00","id":1502975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502970#post1502970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always assumed that a Masque with Other-Order dots needs some justification for it. Like... Status can be gained by forging the right Letters of Introduction*, or outright earning it while in that persona, but Lex Magica could be gained by Masque-ing your way into a Silver Ladder mindset and then meditating in the Silver Ladder Tenemos Realm for a while. You probably don't <i>need</i> a lot of justification to, say, pose as a 1-dot-Status member of an Order, but there still needs to be one. Masque is more psychological than magical, as far as I understand it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I misunderstood the question, I think. Using a below-5-dots Masque <i>should</i> be able to simulate Merit benefits like Status, so long as the Mage can keep up the fascade. Actually <i>having</i> the dots once you have a 5-dot Masque would then represent the role having gained enough of a papertrail to be effectively true.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">Assuming you can create a plausible backstory where one would be justified</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a psychospiritual/psycho-metaphysical change, as the effect it has on the Nimbus and Wisdom is not something so simple as to be all in the head-both are major elements of the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom/page17#post895967\">Supernal Symbol of Self</a> that allows one <i>to be</i> a Mage. The Clark Kent &quot;The way I think of myself being in this situation is how other people will see me&quot; Effect that Masques evoke is effective in it's particular way <i>partially</i> because it's a crafty bit of soul(/Supernal Symbol of Self) crafting (the Guardians being the Order with the most interested in that sort of stuff as a Mystery in a post-Tremere Diamond). Masques have more in common with angelic Cover than with really method acting, and there's a reason why a grand number of the Order's Legacies amplify their metaphysical nature, with the most extreme ends being the Austere and (Legion). (In fact, Masques are closer to a Legacy Attainment than really method acting)<br /> <br /> Anyways, Susceptors are, again, a thing, and I've always figured that, while the assumption of an Order-Mage-Signifier is too weighty to pull off for most Masques (on account of the lack of merit dots below 5 Dots), a full fledged thing is the product of enough social and metaphysical engineering that explains it. Where I got hung up is that, while I knew that argument basically would not work Masquing as a Prelate (unless you ARE a [Legionnaire] and anchoring it onto another soul, yer gonna have to work hard to convince me an Exarchially imposed seal on that Supernal Symbol of Self is something you can just shrug off on account of it being the masquerade you brought to the mascorrida), I hadn't previously considered how Egregore would technically apply under the same principle, and I figured I would start with questioning my base assumption (Order Status) before working my way back up to Egregore(soft magical hivemind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-13-2023, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T19:26:27-08:00","id":1502987,"title":"","content":"I may have a bit of trouble articulating this properly, so my apologies in advance.<br /> <br /> My take on it has always been that the Pentacle Order Merits (Lex Magica, Egregore, Adamant Hand, Techne, Masque) are augmentations to the Mage's personal symbolism and Gnostic understanding. They're associated with the individual Orders, and require an understanding -and acceptance- of the Truth as that Order espouses, but aren't fundamentally locked to the given orders beyond that*. They're techniques that can be <i>taught</i>, and almost universally <i>have </i>to be taught, unless I've drastically misunderstood. Egregore requires initiation, the Lex requires holding a position to get any milage out of, Adamant Hand is a technique... I'm not sure about Techne, but the FC is all about innovation so autodidactism would actually be pretty on-theme.<br /> <br /> Masque, by comparison to the rest, is the most invasive, in that it makes parts of your Gnosis... mutable? I think that's the right word? It's a semi-supernatural technique to make parts of your identity temporarily conform to atypical structures, which extends to your Mage-facing-only identity more strongly the more it's mastered. So while the Suspector in the Mysterium isn't part of the Egregore normally** -despite understanding the theory and practices- their 5-dot Egregore-having Masque is part of the Mysterium's noosphere whenever brought to the fore. Prelacy would be different, to my mind, because it's effectively the Seer being handed an ID Badge with admin accesses - rather than individual understanding and shaping, they're being given permission to do certain things by an outside entity.<br /> <br /> Somewhat clunky, but I like the metaphor of the Mage being a projector: the Supernal is the light source, and the Fallen is the projection screen. Gnosis/The Mage's consiousness acts as the structure of the assembly, directing the light down specific pathways. Path, Order and Legacy are the lenses, focusing and coloring the picture as it passes onto the screen. Order Merits like Lex Magica or Egregore then are peripherals that modify the lens - Masque might be one of those color-strobing attachments, allowing you to mimic other setups but never quite as consistently as a fixed assembly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*The Mysterium and the Ladder, for example, aren't <i>necessarily</i> mutually exclusive in their beliefs, but are enough so that most practitioners wouldn't bother trying to reconcile the differences beyond a working relationship.</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">**Unless they've actually bought in, mechanics-wise via spending XP on the dot of Status and however many dots of Egregore</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":".  Adamant *Hand*, not *Fist* 02-13-2023, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T01:25:50-08:00","id":1503005,"title":"","content":"Makes me wonder, what would the Oneiros of a Guardian using masques look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T01:35:11-08:00","id":1503006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503005#post1503005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me wonder, what would the Oneiros of a Guardian using masques look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the demons are wearing very realistic -but fixed and unmoving- papier-m\u00e2ch\u00e9 masks. Which they refuse to acknowledge. <br /> <br /> Or everything looks like how the Masque would present, but reveals it's true nature when observed out the corner of your eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:31:46-08:00","id":1503053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503005#post1503005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me wonder, what would the Oneiros of a Guardian using masques look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively, because Masques are the intersection of mundane psychology and Supernal Symbolic Imposition and Partition, I imagine the Onieros where it's concerned is treated in the same way a Sleeper's persona would be portrayed, just more &quot;realized&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T15:09:00-08:00","id":1503070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1502987#post1502987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have a bit of trouble articulating this properly, so my apologies in advance.<br /> <br /> My take on it has always been that the Pentacle Order Merits (Lex Magica, Egregore, Adamant Hand, Techne, Masque) are augmentations to the Mage's personal symbolism and Gnostic understanding. They're associated with the individual Orders, and require an understanding -and acceptance- of the Truth as that Order espouses, but aren't fundamentally locked to the given orders beyond that*. They're techniques that can be <i>taught</i>, and almost universally <i>have </i>to be taught, unless I've drastically misunderstood. Egregore requires initiation, the Lex requires holding a position to get any milage out of, Adamant Hand is a technique... I'm not sure about Techne, but the FC is all about innovation so autodidactism would actually be pretty on-theme.<br /> <br /> Masque, by comparison to the rest, is the most invasive, in that it makes parts of your Gnosis... mutable? I think that's the right word? It's a semi-supernatural technique to make parts of your identity temporarily conform to atypical structures, which extends to your Mage-facing-only identity more strongly the more it's mastered. So while the Suspector in the Mysterium isn't part of the Egregore normally** -despite understanding the theory and practices- their 5-dot Egregore-having Masque is part of the Mysterium's noosphere whenever brought to the fore. Prelacy would be different, to my mind, because it's effectively the Seer being handed an ID Badge with admin accesses - rather than individual understanding and shaping, they're being given permission to do certain things by an outside entity.<br /> <br /> Somewhat clunky, but I like the metaphor of the Mage being a projector: the Supernal is the light source, and the Fallen is the projection screen. Gnosis/The Mage's consiousness acts as the structure of the assembly, directing the light down specific pathways. Path, Order and Legacy are the lenses, focusing and coloring the picture as it passes onto the screen. Order Merits like Lex Magica or Egregore then are peripherals that modify the lens - Masque might be one of those color-strobing attachments, allowing you to mimic other setups but never quite as consistently as a fixed assembly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*The Mysterium and the Ladder, for example, aren't <i>necessarily</i> mutually exclusive in their beliefs, but are enough so that most practitioners wouldn't bother trying to reconcile the differences beyond a working relationship.</span>\u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">**Unless they've actually bought in, mechanics-wise via spending XP on the dot of Status and however many dots of Egregore</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So in that essay I linked to, I made the point that mundane actions can still incur Acts of Hubris against Wisdom because the things a mage does and the sort of person they are (or perhaps more accurately, presents themselves to the world as) are all things that affect and shape the Supernal Symbol of themselves, which is bound to the Watchtowers/Oracles/Dragons through the act of naming themselves onto/into/impart/etc. them, and that the things that they are radiate outward <i>unless</i> deliberately (as symbol/andsymbolically) controlled through forethought, consideration, and deliberateness of action, which culiminates into and expresses itself as Wisdom.<br /> <br /> One of the relative consequences of that take is that it softly implies that <i>everything</i> on the character sheet is correspondent in the Supernal symbol of self*. There may be nothing magical about the horde of wealth that Curator Scrooge McDuck has, but his 5 Dots in Resources is still a thing that factors into his Nimbus. Certain symbols are more potent than others, but it's on this basis that Dedication works-given Tools (or other Yantras, if Broad Dedication is used) stop being their own independent symbols it's iconography and symbolism is instead incorporated into the mage's identity, becoming &quot;the thing this Mage works magic by&quot; instead of a knife that communicates intellect and forward action or a cup that communicate intuition and communal participation.<br /> <br /> I'm getting far afield, but bringing it back in, I think there's room to make the argument that all of the Order special benefits can be rooted in the way participation changes that Supernal symbol of self. Being really reductive about the special merits, Lex Magica and Adamant Hand make Yantras out of things people normally couldn't because it makes those Particularly Meaningful for the Mage, Egregore lightly submerges the Supernal symbol of self into the larger symbol of the Mysterium, Masques allow a Mage to have a soft multiple choice symbol of self to act on the world, and Prelacy wraps the Supernal symbol of Self in the symbols of their power and command. Techne is the odd one out since it's also a low scale universal representation of particular cultural participations, but it also makes participation and cooperation potent symbols for the mage in question. Nameless Order's higher ranks of Status within them can make rote qualities for spells on the same principle. These things that are not normally available to take advantage** of are made available because they are now significant to the symbol of who you are.<br /> <br /> Bringing this down around to the problem, though-the nature of the metaphysics behind these create some odd problem where in Masque allows you to access benefits for things where it's not so much about making something particularly iconic for your own symbol, but is predicated more on making the mage's symbol particularly iconic for a larger entity (the two main arguments being the Mysterium and the Seers, and Techne being a bit of a question mark)....when the relative argument for Masques is that you're not diving in, you're more just sticking a toe in. I think it's good wisdom that any Susceptor working the Seers would have to really stick at the secular elements of &quot;Fuck you, get mine&quot;, because there no take-backsies on becoming a Priest of the Exarchs ala becoming a Prelate, that's not something you can just escape by way of the Masque (unless, again, you go the [Legion] way of cheating the system). But that same metaphysical principal clashes when you ask the question &quot;Are there any Susceptors who go so deep into the Mysterium that they become part of the Egregore?&quot; because it feels like the answer to <i>that</i> should be yes, but the logic implies a reason to be reluctant about that for the exact same reason-what are you going to do, claim that it's not you who joined to that magical hivemind, but Alexander Wayfarer who did that, when Alexandar Warfarer is litterally just a metaphysically potent persona?<br /> <br /> And of course, there's just the plain mechanical issue of it all. I have no problem arguing that a Guardian with a Arrow Masque should be able to access Adamant Hand (see my arguments on why one should always play a Carthian on the grounds of that one Law that allows them to effectively fully Dual-Covenant, because a Carthian Acolyte or Carthian Tenth Choirster is the correct choice of things to be), but I can also see other people going &quot;Gah&quot; at it.<br /> <br /> *Possibly appropriate, considering that for all intents and purposes, a character sheet is an imago of the spell players are trying to cast, being the character itself, if we wanna be metatextual about it.<br /> **Well, in the case of Prelacy, would normally be available but come with a cost, which Prelacy solves by basically just ramming you right into the cost and out the door.<br /> ***Adamant Fist is a technique mages can use, but, uh. Not on the battlefield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-14-2023, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T15:33:17-08:00","id":1503072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503070#post1503070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's good wisdom that any Susceptor working the Seers would have to really stick at the secular elements of &quot;Fuck you, get mine&quot;, because there no take-backsies on becoming a Priest of the Exarchs ala becoming a Prelate, that's not something you can just escape by way of the Masque (unless, again, you go the [Legion] way of cheating the system). But that same metaphysical principal clashes when you ask the question &quot;Are there any Susceptors who go so deep into the Mysterium that they become part of the Egregore?&quot; because it feels like the answer to <i>that</i> should be yes, but the logic implies a reason to be reluctant about that for the exact same reason-what are you going to do, claim that it's not you who joined to that magical hivemind, but Alexander Wayfarer who did that, when Alexandar Warfarer is litterally just a metaphysically potent persona?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal interpretation of it is that yes, Alexander Wayfarer is a distinct enough symbol that the Guardian is only part of the Egregore while under that Masque. To me, the Masque is creating a temporary conduit to the noosphere of the Mysterium, with the Egregore being a passive intelligence rather than an active one*. It relies on personal belief and/or psycho-spiritual conditioning to access, personal symbols that in this hypothetical Guardian's case only exist when they forcably put themself into the mindset of &quot;Alexander Wayfarer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Prelacy, on the other hand, hinges from the start on the Persistent Mystery Commands Condition, and the presence of the Black Iron Door in the Mage's Onieros. Because of that, my take on it is that Prelacy is a forced augmentation to the Mage's personal symbolism, only kept in that &quot;shape&quot; so long as the external force (i.e. the relevant Exarch) deigns to do so. Now granted, I can't remember if Prelacy can be <i>revoked</i>, but it's an assumption I'm comfortable enough to roll with unless presented with contradictory evidence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Statement subject to dispute depending on how correct hard-line &quot;Magic is alive&quot; traditionalists in the Mysterium actually are</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T15:49:24-08:00","id":1503075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503072#post1503072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal interpretation of it is that yes, Alexander Wayfarer is a distinct enough symbol that the Guardian is only part of the Egregore while under that Masque. To me, the Masque is creating a temporary conduit to the noosphere of the Mysterium, with the Egregore being a passive intelligence rather than an active one*. It relies on personal belief and/or psycho-spiritual conditioning to access, personal symbols that in this hypothetical Guardian's case only exist when they forcably put themself into the mindset of &quot;Alexander Wayfarer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Prelacy, on the other hand, hinges from the start on the Persistent Mystery Commands Condition, and the presence of the Black Iron Door in the Mage's Onieros. Because of that, my take on it is that Prelacy is a forced augmentation to the Mage's personal symbolism, only kept in that &quot;shape&quot; so long as the external force (i.e. the relevant Exarch) deigns to do so. Now granted, I can't remember if Prelacy can be <i>revoked</i>, but it's an assumption I'm comfortable enough to roll with unless presented with contradictory evidence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Statement subject to dispute depending on how correct hard-line &quot;Magic is alive&quot; traditionalists in the Mysterium actually are</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T16:42:25-08:00","id":1503081,"title":"","content":"Related question, how would you handle adding more Masque-only merit dots? Say the Masque has gained enough influence in their infiltrated Order to justify a boost in Status, but the five dots have already been distributed? Exalted 3e's Socialize tree had something similar in their Personas, which get a smaller pool of XP (50%, then 75% of the character's) to build themselves with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:14:50-08:00","id":1503085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503081#post1503081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question, how would you handle adding more Masque-only merit dots? Say the Masque has gained enough influence in their infiltrated Order to justify a boost in Status, but the five dots have already been distributed? Exalted 3e's Socialize tree had something similar in their Personas, which get a smaller pool of XP (50%, then 75% of the character's) to build themselves with.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut reaction is just &quot;You can buy merits at their normal rate to add onto the Masque&quot; but that brushes up my other gut instinct that, even if it's one of those subtly magically supported things in the way we've been gabbing about, there's a cieling to these things.<br /> <br /> My middle ground is &quot;You can only improve Merits that were part of the initial purchases made for the Immersion Tier&quot; with the obvious caveat that the Storyteller can veto an improvement if it doesn't make sense-becoming the Tetrach isn't a thing you do as part of your job, it's a Win Condition. THe only other argument I might make is that a Masque can only sustain Staus(Guardians of the Veil)+Masque(being 5)) Merits (Not Merit dots, Merits) per Masque.<br /> <br /> I can also see, unrelated, a possibly useful house rule for those worried about Masque abuse, being &quot;You can have a Masque per Status in Guardians of the Veil.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-14-2023, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T15:36:09-08:00","id":1503173,"title":"","content":"<u>Mutable Mask</u> is temporary. If you wanted to make Lasting changes to a person's appearance, would a variant of <u>Shaping</u> (either Life-conjunctive, or just an outright Life version) be reasonable? Manually reshaping their bones and shifting flesh, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T15:57:29-08:00","id":1503177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503173#post1503173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Mutable Mask</u> is temporary. If you wanted to make Lasting changes to a person's appearance, would a variant of <u>Shaping</u> (either Life-conjunctive, or just an outright Life version) be reasonable? Manually reshaping their bones and shifting flesh, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 127 in the Creative Thaumaturgy section says that, if okayed by the Storyteller/table, a +2 Reach can allow a spell to become Lasting (assumedly after everything is done to make it Indefinite first, but it does't strictly demand it), and Many Faces does what Mutable Mask does but as an actual physical change rather than &quot;illusory&quot;*, so depending on the goal, that's viable.<br /> <br /> *how Life can create illusory effects is a Mystery for the ages, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:26:33-08:00","id":1503182,"title":"","content":"EDIT: this is better an independent post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-15-2023, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:31:01-08:00","id":1503184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503177#post1503177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*how Life can create illusory effects is a Mystery for the ages, but whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed it was &quot;illusory&quot; in a... cosmetic sense? Like, shift muscle and fat around to create externally accurate breasts, but nor create actual lactation or, ah... fully functional reproductive organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-15-2023, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:58:38-08:00","id":1503188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503184#post1503184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assumed it was &quot;illusory&quot; in a... cosmetic sense? Like, shift muscle and fat around to create breasts, but nor create... ah... fully functional reproductive organs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, it might require an extended Medicine roll to essentially do the same as a plastic surgery with instant recovery.<br /> <br /> Although remember that the main benefit of using mundane solutions like a disguise or plastic surgery is that they leave no traces of a Nimbus behind. Mages might be too focused on searching for supernatural shenanigans and something like that might go right over their heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-15-2023, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T01:01:35-08:00","id":1503214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503173#post1503173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Mutable Mask</u> is temporary. If you wanted to make Lasting changes to a person's appearance, would a variant of <u>Shaping</u> (either Life-conjunctive, or just an outright Life version) be reasonable? Manually reshaping their bones and shifting flesh, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recall the reason Shaping is lasting is because the spell just makes the matter 'mutable'*. You can then shape it by hand if you want and it will hold the shape later...<br /> <br /> Does the human body work the same as a block of clay? I'd say, probably not. Maybe a Life shaping + cosmetic surgeon could do it with ease... Otherwise, i suspect it will turn out lumpy...<br /> <br /> *Recalling that is calls for a wits+craft roll to (mundanely?) shape, or at least use your mundane skill to make it look good. The magic doesn't do that part imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T04:00:00-08:00","id":1503220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503214#post1503214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recall the reason Shaping is lasting is because the spell just makes the matter 'mutable'*. You can then shape it by hand if you want and it will hold the shape later...<br /> <br /> Does the human body work the same as a block of clay? I'd say, probably not. Maybe a Life shaping + cosmetic surgeon could do it with ease... Otherwise, i suspect it will turn out lumpy...<br /> <br /> *Recalling that is calls for a wits+craft roll to (mundanely?) shape, or at least use your mundane skill to make it look good. The magic doesn't do that part imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if <u>Shaping</u> doesn't allow you to mold things with your mind (I like to think it can, but that's entirely personal preference), <u>Telekinesis</u> would probably give you a fairly steady hand-analog. But yeah, I'd imagine you'd need to be rolling some combination of Wits, Dexterity, Crafts, and Medicine, and even then complicated work would require a ridiculously high Extended Action target unless you have a bunch of other spells working in your favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T08:28:01-08:00","id":1503241,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i think the extra suggested act for Shaping does suggest you can shape with with you mind, just the magic will not grant you the Supernal reflection of a platonic microwave (say) - unlike with Prime weaving Platonic form (where it explicitly calls for +2(?) reach for complex devices).<br /> <br /> The pure Life way of doing this which draws the platonic ideal of the form you want them in, would not be lasting (equivalent to regeneration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T10:01:06-08:00","id":1503245,"title":"","content":"Yep, I am utilizing the <i>Shaping</i> spell as the baseline for the effects for a Life version. Less powerful than <i>Mutable Mask</i>, but with potential healing applications and also the capacity to create nightmare fuel should the mage decide to use it akin to the Vissicitude Discipline from Vampire:The Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T13:37:10-08:00","id":1503251,"title":"","content":"Again, Many Faces is <i>right there</i> one dot above Mutable Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T13:46:30-08:00","id":1503253,"title":"","content":"... Damnit, I always get the two confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T13:53:30-08:00","id":1503254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503253#post1503253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Damnit, I always get the two confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was really confused, like. I've already pointed out the spell for this! Why are we talking about adpating a Matter spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:20:54-08:00","id":1503257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503254#post1503254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was really confused, like. I've already pointed out the spell for this! Why are we talking about adpating a Matter spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Shaping conversation is just a consideration for if <u>Many Faces</u> or <u>Mutable Mask</u> isn't Lasting. Say, if your table vetos it. But my original question was meant to be about <u>Many Faces</u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:36:22-08:00","id":1503261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503257#post1503257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Shaping conversation is just a consideration for if <u>Many Faces</u> or <u>Mutable Mask</u> isn't Lasting. Say, if your table vetos it. But my original question was meant to be about <u>Many Faces</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>An argument to be made if a veto comes up is that Many Faces is on the same level as the proper healing spell, which is automatically Lasting. In general, the mage has enough mastery to effect that sort of change in situations where it's accepted by the castee. If they need a little more persuasion, point out that if healing was done in a conflict scenario, healing's Lastingness could be reasonably waived if dispelling it could increase the drama, particularly if the healee is a point of that overarching contention, and that in the vein, there's a fluidity of circumstance on what can and can't be Lasting.<br /> <br /> Like, yeah, you don't want to allow it to be lasting if you're making an enemy's face look like hamburger, but there's no reason to be petty about a mage who wants to make themselves a natural redhead or help their friend transition on a budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:37:37-08:00","id":1503263,"title":"","content":"Aye, not a current concern. Just seemed prudent to consider. It also got sidetracked somewhat into the question more relevant to the thread - &quot;Is <u>Shaping</u> just causing something to be like clay, or can you shape it with your mind?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-16-2023, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:59:16-08:00","id":1503265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503263#post1503263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, not a current concern. Just seemed prudent to consider. It also got sidetracked somewhat into the question more relevant to the thread - &quot;Is <u>Shaping</u> just causing something to be like clay, or can you shape it with your mind?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm inclined to answer in a tactile-y inclined way, but the reality is dependent on what range you're casting at, and if you're taking time for it. It's not dependent on, like, physically doing it, but it's probably more efficent as a spell if you do it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:01:15-08:00","id":1503270,"title":"","content":"You know, if you don\u2019t mind things tasking a while, the body does shape in self over time. My glasses have carved furrows into my head. I hear people put rings on their neck to lengthen them. I\u2019ve read about people wearing too small shoes and not properly developing their feet. Hair is bleached by the sun. I wonder if you could use tools for the process. Might be safe building off the bodies natural processes. Frankly I\u2019d worry I would accidentally cut off a vein or something. Reshaping someone would have some pretty nasty consequences for messing up. I wonder if Mages have taken up this service as a profession or legacy? Sounds like something people could develop skills in and be renowned for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:04:20-08:00","id":1503271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503270#post1503270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if you don\u2019t mind things tasking a while, the body does shape in self over time. My glasses have carved furrows into my head. I hear people put rings on their neck to lengthen them. I\u2019ve read about people wearing too small shoes and not properly developing their feet. Hair is bleached by the sun. I wonder if you could use tools for the process. Might be safe building off the bodies natural processes. Frankly I\u2019d worry I would accidentally cut off a vein or something. Reshaping someone would have some pretty nasty consequences for messing up. I wonder if Mages have taken up this service as a profession or legacy? Sounds like something people could develop skills in and be renowned for.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mage Plastic Surgeon&quot; was honestly my impetus for the question. MM and MF being transitory by RAW means you can't really (safely) run a buisness off of it, and Dissonance is a (lesser) concern.<br /> <br /> I could see the Guardians going hog-wild with it, especially for infiltrating Sleeper organizations.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Unrelated question - how many perception-expanding spells like <u>Sacred Geometry</u>, <u>Supernal Vision</u>, and <u>Interconnections</u> can you stack before it starts to be detrimental to your ability to perceive anything useful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-16-2023, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:34:01-08:00","id":1503277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503271#post1503271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT:<br /> Unrelated question - how many perception-expanding spells like <u>Sacred Geometry</u>, <u>Supernal Vision</u>, and <u>Interconnections</u> can you stack before it starts to be detrimental to your ability to perceive anything useful?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think rules as written, there isn\u2019t a limit. However, if one wanted a limit, I\u2019d say something like the lower of Wits and Gnosis would be a good starting place.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:15:43-08:00","id":1503282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503271#post1503271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Mage Plastic Surgeon&quot; was honestly my impetus for the question. MM and MF being transitory by RAW means you can't really (safely) run a buisness off of it, and Dissonance is a (lesser) concern.<br /> <br /> I could see the Guardians going hog-wild with it, especially for infiltrating Sleeper organizations.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Unrelated question - how many perception-expanding spells like <u>Sacred Geometry</u>, <u>Supernal Vision</u>, and <u>Interconnections</u> can you stack before it starts to be detrimental to your ability to perceive anything useful?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are none in RAW, which means a really paranoid mage or a very Obsessive detective could dedicate most of their spell control to it. The nice thing about Imagos is that the mage builds them to purposely interact with the senses of the recipient. Mage Sight is the opposite of this, flooding them in information that their Awakened instinct can only partially help them sort through or, with a concentrated act of will, they can focus all their processing power on a single subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:57:15-08:00","id":1503285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503282#post1503282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are none in RAW, which means a really paranoid mage or a very Obsessive detective could dedicate most of their spell control to it. The nice thing about Imagos is that the mage builds them to purposely interact with the senses of the recipient. Mage Sight is the opposite of this, flooding them in information that their Awakened instinct can only partially help them sort through or, with a concentrated act of will, they can focus all their processing power on a single subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503277#post1503277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think rules as written, there isn\u2019t a limit. However, if one wanted a limit, I\u2019d say something like the lower of Wits and Gnosis would be a good starting place.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe only thing that really touches close is one of <u>Craftsman's Eye'</u>s Reach effects, which requires a Wits+Composure when viewing a really complex item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T18:16:12-08:00","id":1503287,"title":"","content":"So Ectoplasm can be shaped, and produced by Death, and opens stuff to ghost. Do you think a similar substance can be produced for Spirit? <br /> <br /> Edit: or Mind? I\u2019ve seen arguments that it\u2019s the substance of ephemeral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-16-2023, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T18:45:03-08:00","id":1503292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503287#post1503287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ectoplasm can be shaped, and produced by Death, and opens stuff to ghost. Do you think a similar substance can be produced for Spirit?<br /> <br /> Edit: or Mind? I\u2019ve seen arguments that it\u2019s the substance of ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thematic and mechanical headspace of ectoplasm is such that it exists as a means for ghosts to cling to the world they are formed in; spirits are intruders in the material world, and rely on Manifestations to maintain their grip against the tidal force of the Moon drawing them back into Shadow.<br /> <br /> If such a substance exists, it's unusual enough to be a Mystery or at least the product of a lot of legwork to discover how to reliably produce it; even a locus isn't Open to every kind of spirit, for all that any spirit could conceivably shift its nature to align with a locus over time, and spirits aren't quite as limited in the things that support their presence to need an equivalent of the Great Equalizer in common circulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Me