 <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503577#post1503577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeppity yep yep yeppers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm never going to be able to create Lasting Perfected Blood, am I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T17:55:55-08:00","id":1503581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503578#post1503578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm never going to be able to create Lasting Perfected Blood, am I?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nopity nope no noper-Well, okay, let's hold that on the side.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery generally suggests the only way to get Perfected Blood is to cast Hone the Perfect Form as you spill it from your victim. The Lasting Condition can be applied to to it with +2 Reach, generally if there's no way to revert a material. And from what it sounds like, this is pertinent to an Aspiration/Obsession, which means the answer should probably be &quot;Yes, you can create it&quot; with just a little above the average effort.<br /> <br /> Which brings me around to the question....<i>why</i> do you want to create lasting Perfected Blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T18:09:50-08:00","id":1503582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503581#post1503581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nopity nope no noper-Well, okay, let's hold that on the side.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery generally suggests the only way to get Perfected Blood is to cast Hone the Perfect Form as you spill it from your victim. The Lasting Condition can be applied to to it with +2 Reach, generally if there's no way to revert a material. And from what it sounds like, this is pertinent to an Aspiration/Obsession, which means the answer should probably be &quot;Yes, you can create it&quot; with just a little above the average effort.<br /> <br /> Which brings me around to the question....<i>why</i> do you want to create lasting Perfected Blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Perfecting via the spell doesn't qualify for that &quot;+2 Reach&quot; rule on p127, given that Dispellation in any form would be a viable method of reverting the material. Granted, I take that stance because 2e's rules read to me as if Lasting should almost never occur as a direct result of magic. <i>Incidentally</i> occur, sure, like fire spreading even once the fireball has been hucked, but directly creating a lasting Perfected item via the spell seems like it goes against the spirit.<br /> <br /> As to <i>why...</i> mostly a thought exercise? I know you can't cast <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u>, and then pass the Perfected object through Twilight manually to make the effect Lasting*. And since blood, skin, and other organics need the spell cast on them immediately to be Perfected, manually refining them isn't an option. I like figuring out circuitous routes to create Lasting effects that would be impossible with direct spellcasting.<br /> <br /> There's also a part of me that <i>really</i> wants to know what would happen if you created an entire body piecemeal out of Perfected organics. According to SoS they're <i>still alive,</i> so long as they're Perfected, and Life sure as heck would be a good tool for fusing the pieces together into a Frankinstienien creation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*At least, the consensus when I asked the forums about it was that it isn't viable. Obviously, final ruling is table-to-table.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T18:16:53-08:00","id":1503583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503582#post1503582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure Perfecting via the spell doesn't qualify for that &quot;+2 Reach&quot; rule on p127, given that Dispellation in any form would be a viable method of reverting the material. Granted, I take that stance because 2e's rules read to me as if Lasting should almost never occur as a direct result of magic. <i>Incidentally</i> occur, sure, like fire spreading even once the fireball has been hucked, but directly creating a lasting Perfected item via the spell seems like it goes against the spirit.<br /> <br /> As to <i>why...</i> mostly a thought exercise? I know you can't cast <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u>, and then pass the Perfected object through Twilight manually to make the effect Lasting*. And since blood, skin, and other organics need the spell cast on them immediately to be Perfected, manually refining them isn't an option. I like figuring out circuitous routes to create Lasting effects that would be impossible with direct spellcasting.<br /> <br /> There's also a part of me that <i>really</i> wants to know what would happen if you created an entire body piecemeal out of Perfected organics. According to SoS they're <i>still alive,</i> so long as they're Perfected, and Life sure as heck would be a good tool for fusing the pieces together into a Frankinstienien creation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*At least, the consensus when I asked the forums about it was that it isn't viable. Obviously, final ruling is table-to-table.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I generally wouldn't particularly rule against the Lasting on this in general, but my general read is more inclined towards a sliding scale of arbitrariness vs meaningfulness, with the middle in this case being the range where I'd generally say no. The idea of a grimoire scribed in perfected blood having a time limit, as raised by Signs, strikes me as completely arbitrary in an unfun way, so I'd argue you have a textual precedent for being able to apply Lasting to it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T18:33:39-08:00","id":1503584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503583#post1503583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally wouldn't particularly rule against the Lasting on this in general, but my general read is more inclined towards a sliding scale of arbitrariness vs meaningfulness, with the middle in this case being the range where I'd generally say no. The idea of a grimoire scribed in perfected blood having a time limit, as raised by Signs, strikes me as completely arbitrary in an unfun way, so I'd argue you have a textual precedent for being able to apply Lasting to it there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. And I do generally try to stay away from declaring something badwrongfun - this is just one of those unclear areas where I default to magic being highly transitory in the Fallen. The other point that makes me lean towards <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> being inelligable for Lasting is one of supply - if all you need to make Perfected metals, tools, weapons, and doodads is a spell that any Gnosis 1 Matter 3 Mage can cast and a Desmense, why wouldn't you load the Consillium to the gills with Siderite knives and the like? Which some tables may declare the norm, not a problem! But the book reads like <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> is a shortcut with downsides that aren't really present if the Lasting Reach effect exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T18:50:53-08:00","id":1503588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503584#post1503584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. And I do generally try to stay away from declaring something badwrongfun - this is just one of those unclear areas where I default to magic being highly transitory in the Fallen. The other point that makes me lean towards <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> being inelligable for Lasting is one of supply - if all you need to make Perfected metals, tools, weapons, and doodads is a spell that any Gnosis 1 Matter 3 Mage can cast and a Desmense, why wouldn't you load the Consillium to the gills with Siderite knives and the like? Which some tables may declare the norm, not a problem! But the book reads like <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> is a shortcut with downsides that aren't really present if the Lasting Reach effect exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's the matter of the otherwise insisted limited time frame to make Perfected organic materials, particularly for blood. In the case Matter based....materials, they have an expanded window to be worked with, so allowing for Lasting to just be cast onto it (unless one is a Master of Matter or Time) isn't particularly interesting or meaningful, and perfected materials in the other circumstances are too potent a resource to deem arbitrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T20:03:19-08:00","id":1503593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503588#post1503588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, it's the matter of the otherwise insisted limited time frame to make Perfected organic materials, particularly for blood. In the case Matter based....materials, they have an expanded window to be worked with, so allowing for Lasting to just be cast onto it (unless one is a Master of Matter or Time) isn't particularly interesting or meaningful, and perfected materials in the other circumstances are too potent a resource to deem arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, can't say I'm on board with that. I mean, <i>narratively</i> I get it, Perfected Organics are generally too niche compared to the Metals, but in terms of <i>consistency</i> it rubs me wrong to have a whole class of materials just respond differently to the spell. Especially given that biological matter is constantly changing when compared to inorganic matter, which would be a big point against allowing magic to make a Lasting change to it in my mind.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, it's wierd that a Matter spell works on organics, but is never stated as needing Life conjunctive to pull off. The spell text mentions other Arcana besides Forces could theoretically produce other odd materials, but you'd think the Living Materials section would have at least mentioned it. So the easiest resolution -for me amnd my hangups, at any rate- would be a Life version of the spell. One that allows for the Lasting Reach effect you suggest on the grounds that it's a slightly different process with slightly different parameters. But even that is decidedly unsatisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-20-2023, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T20:14:52-08:00","id":1503594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503593#post1503593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, can't say I'm on board with that. I mean, <i>narratively</i> I get it, Perfected Organics are generally too niche compared to the Metals, but in terms of <i>consistency</i> it rubs me wrong to have a whole class of materials just respond differently to the spell. Especially given that biological matter is constantly changing when compared to inorganic matter, which would be a big point against allowing magic to make a Lasting change to it in my mind.<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand, it's wierd that a Matter spell works on organics, but is never stated as needing Life conjunctive to pull off. The spell text mentions other Arcana besides Forces could theoretically produce other odd materials, but you'd think the Living Materials section would have at least mentioned it. So the easiest resolution -for me amnd my hangups, at any rate- would be a Life version of the spell. One that allows for the Lasting Reach effect you suggest on the grounds that it's a slightly different process with slightly different parameters. But even that is decidedly unsatisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consistency is less my priority, but it's not hard to argue in terms of semiotics and symbolism. Other materials already have an extent implication of lasting in that their inherent transmutational properties are, in fact, much longer lasting, so it's harder to articulate it's Lasting nature, where as blood has such a rapid transmutational quality that the injection of a descriptor of lasting is much easier to inject.<br /> <br /> Or however you want to say it. Awakening is very much a game of how you say a thing as much as it is what you're saying.<br /> <br /> The other argument of substantiation is working backwards from the text-Perfected Blood has a narrow window of time to be made, so there must be something metaphysically pertinent to how it's main application readily carries the assumption of Lasting. Perfected materials are sufficiently rare enough, with the text making a particular point of noting when spell durations end, that there must be something about their metaphysical makeup or positioning that makes that the case. Those facts are there, they're just <i>text</i>. Everything else is just details to be played with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T20:59:55-08:00","id":1503597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503584#post1503584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. And I do generally try to stay away from declaring something badwrongfun - this is just one of those unclear areas where I default to magic being highly transitory in the Fallen. The other point that makes me lean towards <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> being inelligable for Lasting is one of supply - if all you need to make Perfected metals, tools, weapons, and doodads is a spell that any Gnosis 1 Matter 3 Mage can cast and a Desmense, why wouldn't you load the Consillium to the gills with Siderite knives and the like? Which some tables may declare the norm, not a problem! But the book reads like <u>Hone the Perfected Form</u> is a shortcut with downsides that aren't really present if the Lasting Reach effect exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a very real tactic that a Consilium with a persistent supernatural problem could take, or one with a member of the Council of Dragons in power. Its also a reasonable requisition for an Arrow with more experience to make (Status 2) or for two new Talons to request if the situation looks dire.<br /> <br /> Too many werewolves? Lunargent bullets. Are they instead one of those lazy werewolves that don't care to do something if a spirit crosses a line ? Start making Kassiterum weapons. Changelings runing amok ? Siderite knives.<br /> <br /> Did we cross the Godzilla threshold? Break out the Thaumium charms and Dumanium weapons.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T21:27:58-08:00","id":1503598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503594#post1503594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other materials already have an extent implication of lasting in that their inherent transmutational properties are, in fact, much longer lasting, so it's harder to articulate it's Lasting nature, where as blood has such a rapid transmutational quality that the injection of a descriptor of lasting is much easier to inject..<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Perfected Blood has a narrow window of time to be made, so there must be something metaphysically pertinent to how it's main application readily carries the assumption of Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the opposite vibe - because organics are so transitory that their window for transmutation is fleeting, then making that change last should be <i>harder</i> if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Which is basically just a summation of &quot;I wouldn't object if a game chose to allow it, but my default headcannon is that that isn't viable.&quot; Not to be argumentative! Just wanted to make my position clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503597#post1503597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably a very real tactic that a Consilium with a persistent supernatural problem could take, or one with a member of the Council of Dragons in power. Its also a reasonable requisition for an Arrow with more experience to make (Status 2) or for two new Talons to request if the situation looks dire.<br /> <br /> Too many werewolves? Lunargent bullets. Are they instead one of those lazy werewolves that don't care to do something if a spirit crosses a line ? Start making Kassiterum weapons. Changelings runing amok ? Siderite knives.<br /> <br /> Did we cross the Godzilla threshold? Break out the Thaumium charms and Dumanium weapons.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>See, it's a legitimate tactic if that's how it works. But it feels like it cheapens Perfected Materials.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-21-2023, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T05:45:58-08:00","id":1503749,"title":"","content":"Can Lasting spells be dispelled?<br /> <br /> I am confused on the Lasting example in the core rulebook spellcasting description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LASTING p.113 Core Mage 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many spells specify that some effects are <i>Lasting</i>,<br /> or give the option to create Lasting effects with<br /> Reach. <b>Lasting isn\u2019t a Duration, but instead the sys-<br /> tem term for the persisting after-effects of magic.</b><br /> A fire controlled with a Forces spell continues to<br /> burn after the spell ceases to act upon it. Wounds<br /> healed with magic do not reopen when the spell\u2019s<br /> Duration ends. <b>When a spell ends, look at what<br /> it changed, if anything, in the environment. Those<br /> are its Lasting qualities.\u200b</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For example <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>, primary factor is duration, but there is a reach to make it lasting. If I make it lasting... It can no longer be dispelled? What is the advantage/difference vs making it Indefinite?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T06:40:21-08:00","id":1503751,"title":"","content":"It means the result of the spell sticks around. If you throw a fireball, it would be weird for the scorch marks to disappear when the spell ends. As for the Oath bit\u2026it means the Mage is still going to be considered part of the oath forever/however long the oath lasts instead of dropping out when the spell ends. There is no spell to be dispelled when Lasting, the Mage is just part of the oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:07:16-08:00","id":1503774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503749#post1503749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Lasting spells be dispelled?<br /> <br /> I am confused on the Lasting example in the core rulebook spellcasting description.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For example <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>, primary factor is duration, but there is a reach to make it lasting. If I make it lasting... It can no longer be dispelled? What is the advantage/difference vs making it Indefinite?</div> </div> </div> </div>TempleBuilder addressed the main points, so two notes:<br /> <br /> 1) Making a Spell lasting is a subject of table discretion, and it's one of those things that you want to be cautious about just blanket running with. There are some applications where it's results are rather arbitrary, and results where being able to do it is meaningful for a character where it's easy to just say &quot;Yeah, go ahead&quot;. If I were in a situation where Wyrdbound Oaths was used*, I'd argue the risk of time running out or being dispelled is inherently part of the narrative it brings to the game, so I would be inclined to say no to Reaching for Lasting.<br /> <br /> 2) I feel like it should be noted that, while the nature of the Wyrd's effect on Mages as described by Kith and Kin changes matter, one of the particular hallmarks of mage's approach to oaths is that of forcing others to keep their promises but snipping off their own obligations**-indeed, this is a major iconic for the Acanthus, the Path most concerned with the subject. That the Wyrd can effectively weave being an Oathbreaker into a mage's Nimbus unless it's actually properly addressed means that Mages are doubly cautious about getting into fairy Oaths, because it's so anathemic to their own disposition regarding Oaths.<br /> <br /> *When it comes to crossover, I usually just handwave the fairy-only nature of Oaths for the purposes of a crossover motley, but that's not the rules obviously. I bring it up because we're in the realm of subjective takes on this line and I wanted full disclosure about my particular biases.<br /> **Barring mages of the Adamantine Arrow, of course. Otherwise, it's a matter of personal disposition, and it's key to remember that mages are aware of that flimsiness and, over time, are quite willing to take advantage of it if they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:39:37-08:00","id":1503775,"title":"","content":"Much lesser to Temple and Arcane's points, but it's also worth noting that some spells can be made &quot;Lasting&quot; by dint of spending XP. <u>Social Networking</u>, for example, provides Merit dots. It wouldn't be too out of line for a character to make those dots permanent even once the spell ends via spending XP on them, negating their vulnerability to dispellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:55:14-08:00","id":1503778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503751#post1503751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means the result of the spell sticks around. If you throw a fireball, it would be weird for the scorch marks to disappear when the spell ends. As for the Oath bit\u2026it means the Mage is still going to be considered part of the oath forever/however long the oath lasts instead of dropping out when the spell ends. There is no spell to be dispelled when Lasting, the Mage is just part of the oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly clear. Thanks.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503774#post1503774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> TempleBuilder addressed the main points, so two notes:<br /> <br /> 1) <b>Making a Spell lasting is a subject of table discretion</b>, and it's one of those things that you want to be cautious about just blanket running with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I thought this was part of the core rules, something that is explicitly stated that on certain specific spells you can apply no questions asked. Like <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>\u200b' reach option, you spend the reach and it becomes lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503774#post1503774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> There are some applications where it's results are rather arbitrary, and results where being able to do it is meaningful for a character where it's easy to just say &quot;Yeah, go ahead&quot;. <b>If I were in a situation where Wyrdbound Oaths was used*, I'd argue the risk of time running out or being dispelled is inherently part of the narrative it brings to the game, so I would be inclined to say no to Reaching for Lasting.</b><br /> <br /> *When it comes to crossover, I usually just handwave the fairy-only nature of Oaths for the purposes of a crossover motley, but that's not the rules obviously. I bring it up because we're in the realm of subjective takes on this line and I wanted full disclosure about my particular biases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got confused again, is the bolded text part of the rules or just your take on your games for that spell? From TempleBuilder comment a <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>\u200b\u200b lasting effect once applied no way to dispel it. Seems to be the Core rules definition of Lasting, and there is a specific reach for it. Am I missing something? I copied your complementary text that seems to support the &quot;my take on it, not the rules&quot; but again, I am confused since you are one of the most prolific and knowledgeable posters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-23-2023, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T15:36:41-08:00","id":1503781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503778#post1503778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfectly clear. Thanks.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is it? I thought this was part of the core rules, something that is explicitly stated that on certain specific spells you can apply no questions asked. Like <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>\u200b' reach option, you spend the reach and it becomes lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I got confused again, is the bolded text part of the rules or just your take on your games for that spell? From TempleBuilder comment a <b>Wyrdbound Oaths</b>\u200b\u200b lasting effect once applied no way to dispel it. Seems to be the Core rules definition of Lasting, and there is a specific reach for it. Am I missing something? I copied your complementary text that seems to support the &quot;my take on it, not the rules&quot; but again, I am confused since you are one of the most prolific and knowledgeable posters.</div> </div> </div> </div>To simplify - some spells specifically say they have Lasting Reach effects. If it DOESN'T specify that, the table needs to use their discretion to decide. Arcane was just saying that her personal ruling on <u>Wyrdbound Oath</u> is to disallow the Lasting Reach option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T15:37:48-08:00","id":1503782,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:37:34-08:00","id":1503823,"title":"","content":"I assume an Attainment giving the Mage access to a Changeling's Mantle is a bit too far outside the norm, correct? Mechanically, I could see it MAYBE being a Fate spell to bestow Potency dots in a given Court's Mantle, but fluff-wise it seems to far afield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:59:09-08:00","id":1503828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503823#post1503823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume an Attainment giving the Mage access to a Changeling's Mantle is a bit too far outside the norm, correct? Mechanically, I could see it MAYBE being a Fate spell to bestow Potency dots in a given Court's Mantle, but fluff-wise it seems to far afield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean Court Goodwill can give Mantle to Fetches, so maybe you could build off of that?<br /> <br /> Edit: Changeling\u2019s don\u2019t exist with Mantle straight away, so I imagine a legacy mimicking them wouldn\u2019t have it as an Attainment, maybe as a merit they can pick up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-24-2023, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T12:16:54-08:00","id":1503833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503823#post1503823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume an Attainment giving the Mage access to a Changeling's Mantle is a bit too far outside the norm, correct? Mechanically, I could see it MAYBE being a Fate spell to bestow Potency dots in a given Court's Mantle, but fluff-wise it seems to far afield.</div> </div> </div> </div>You dont need that to replicate, it can be done with Borrowed Favour + Court Goodwill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-24-2023, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T12:31:05-08:00","id":1503834,"title":"","content":"You can be in a cabal, and you can be a solitaire, and in both scenarios you can still be part of the Consilium (even holding positions of responsibility as a solitaire).<br /> <br /> What happens when you are part of another supernatural clique? Like those rare cases where a mage joins a Pack? Will the Consilium expel you? Censure you? Will your order do any of that?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T12:32:46-08:00","id":1503835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503828#post1503828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean Court Goodwill can give Mantle to Fetches, so maybe you could build off of that?<br /> <br /> Edit: Changeling\u2019s don\u2019t exist with Mantle straight away, so I imagine a legacy mimicking them wouldn\u2019t have it as an Attainment, maybe as a merit they can pick up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, they CAN? TIL.<br /> <br /> Fair enough. Maybe a side-benefit to Attainment-ized <u>Wyrd-Backed Oath?</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503833#post1503833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You dont need that to replicate, I can be done with Borrowed Favour + Court Goodwill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeh... by RAW, yes, but I'm not sure that's RAI. I'm pretty sure only Changelings (and Fetches, I guess?) are valid Bearers of Mantles. Y'know what? This is a question for the Changeling Simple Question thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503834#post1503834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be in a cabal, and you can be a solitaire, and in both scenarios you can still be part of the Consilium (even holding positions of responsibility as a solitaire). <br /> What happens when you are part of another supernatural clique? Like those rare cases where a mage joins a Pack? Will the Consilium expel you? Censure you? Will your order do any of that?</div> </div> </div> </div> If your association with this other clique is a threat to the Consilium/Order, absolutely. Otherwise, case-by-case<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T13:23:34-08:00","id":1503841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503835#post1503835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, they CAN? TIL.</div> </div> </div> </div> Gray area, in retrospect. The rules explicitly say both that a Fetch can have court goodwill, and that they can't have dots of Mantle. One of the listed effects of Court Goodwill is gaining the effects of having Dots of Mantle equal to Court Goodwill - 2. Here's what people said when I asked.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches#post1448259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Can fetches use the gain the mantle of a court through court goodwill?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1448259-playable-fetches?p=1449632#post1449632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I'd allow it, since otherwise they're gimped if they have Mimic Contract but their changeling counterpart uses a lot of Court Contracts over Arcadian ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would allow it, because fun, but I'm sure there is an argument to be made that it doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503835#post1503835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Maybe a side-benefit to Attainment-ized <u>Wyrd-Backed Oath?</u></div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say that's a good spot because it means the Wyrd officially recognizes them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T19:31:32-08:00","id":1503923,"title":"","content":"So, I've never, ever read Mage: the Awakening; I've always loved Mage: the Ascension and didn't buy Awakening when I had the chance. I've read a lot of Requiem and in Ascension, magik can overcome anything; so, can mages in Awakening overcome VII's Clan Akhud's curse that no clan-member can betray another one of their clan; even mind-reading won't work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T19:38:17-08:00","id":1503924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503923#post1503923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've never, ever read Mage: the Awakening; I've always loved Mage: the Ascension and didn't buy Awakening when I had the chance. I've read a lot of Requiem and in Ascension, magik can overcome anything; so, can mages in Awakening overcome VII's Clan Akhud's curse that no clan-member can betray another one of their clan; even mind-reading won't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Archmage probably can - I don't know the details of Requiem, but some combination of Death, Fate, and possibly Space should be enough at the Imperial level to work on a Clan-wide curse.<br /> <br /> Player-wise? Circumventing a curse on the individual level is likely feasible. Not necessarily removing it, but casting something to keep the curse in abeyance until the spell ends should be possible. <u>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bFabricate Fortune</u> would be my starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T20:09:48-08:00","id":1503926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503923#post1503923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've never, ever read Mage: the Awakening; I've always loved Mage: the Ascension and didn't buy Awakening when I had the chance. I've read a lot of Requiem and in Ascension, magik can overcome anything; so, can mages in Awakening overcome VII's Clan Akhud's curse that no clan-member can betray another one of their clan; even mind-reading won't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e has the Akhud as a Lost Clan whose Clan Bane manifests as a scaling penalty to knowingly take any action that would harm another Akhud, their mortal descendants, and anyone in Vinculum with one of them, along with an explicit statement that &quot;no compulsion, natural or otherwise,&quot; can force the Akhud to take such actions.<br /> <br /> As a point of comparison, prior to the crossover rules from the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, you could make the argument that the 2e corebook's statement that Disciplines not being able to coerce a frenzying vampire to act against the Beast's desires (instead of redirecting them) could be generalized to any supernatural power being incapable of stopping a vampire from frenzying, but now it's known that with two dots in Death and Mind and enough Potency to overcome the vampire's Composure a mage can cast a spell to end a frenzy. Those same rules also establish that Clan Banes can be studied in general with Fate (as curses) or in particular with appropriate other Arcana (as phenomena relating to the effects of a given Bane).<br /> <br /> Given that the Akhud's bane is described as both a curse and the product of an oath, as well as being framed in terms of knowing intent and and immunity to compulsion, it's theoretically within the power of the Arcana to allow one of the Akhud to overcome the penalty (whether by providing a corresponding bonus, negating the penalty, or messing with the Bane using the standard moderately-high-level spell for messing with oaths and other supernatural binding agreements), but e.g. forcing such an act with Psychic Domination would probably fail in the same way that you can't mind-control an angel of the God-Machine into abandoning its mission. Even outside the context of being a particular interpretation of how VII might manifest in a game, the Akhud are still rare and unusual enough for such a thing to serve as a Mystery in a game where Mage is contributing to the ludonarrative considerations.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the 1e version of this conversation, because 1e never got into the Awakened's mechanical interactions with VII in any form save that a couple of nods in its general direction inform 1e's version of the expanded backstory of the Tremere liches, which 2e instead generalized/blurred to relate less explicitly specifically to vampires. Barring any other interpretation, it should at the very least be within the power of an archmaster using the Imperial Practices, which involve spells cast using required components whose acquisition takes entire stories due to needing to be difficult to acquire by someone with the resources of a half-Ascended demigod \u2014 all of which is to say that the answer is &quot;yes&quot; with the caveat of &quot;though it might only be possible for characters that have passed the point where you can just call them mages.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T22:02:03-08:00","id":1503927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503823#post1503823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume an Attainment giving the Mage access to a Changeling's Mantle is a bit too far outside the norm, correct? Mechanically, I could see it MAYBE being a Fate spell to bestow Potency dots in a given Court's Mantle, but fluff-wise it seems to far afield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some clarity and splitting of hairs on this one, starting with a biggie-Court Goodwill does not grant <i>Mantle</i>, it grants the <i>effects</i> of Mantle.<br /> <br /> Over in Changelingland, Satchel elaborated that Mantle is an accordant change to a changeling's mien, an element of their physical presence remolded (changed, even) by the metaphysical buy in to the bargain made with a Court's patron. Court Goodwill is a sociomystical connection (though not elaborated on in Kith and Kin, likely a dramatrugical connection) which allows the one who has that Goodwill to act as though they were a fairy (a changeling, more specifically) in a roughly correlating position of buy-in, but it's not the same as actually <i>being</i> such.<br /> <br /> A Mage who has Court Goodwill is likely going to see that dramaturgy play out in their Nimbus even going so far as to add it's iconography to it.<br /> <br /> A Mage who forges a Legacy around how deep they can get in with a Patron by way of the Wyrd is in for an interesting time and is likely going to stop being a mage proper* after some work.<br /> <br /> *The phrasing is weird here because of my particular hiccup of not treating mages as humans, which I will stand by, but I will also clarify people without that hangup are more likely to say &quot;is likely to stop being human after some work.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T00:35:12-08:00","id":1503932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1503927#post1503927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage who forges a Legacy around how deep they can get in with a Patron by way of the Wyrd is in for an interesting time and is likely going to stop being a mage proper* after some work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... any Legacy predicated on the idea of &quot;ooo, Thorn wounds... shiny!&quot; is going to have some... issues. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1503714#post1503714\">Which is why the current plan is for there to have been a lot of Raptures in it's founding.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-26-2023, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:25:15-08:00","id":1504085,"title":"","content":"New to Mage the Awakening so:<br /> <br /> Why does having a higher gnosis lead to more paradox rolled on overreaching? It seems counterintuitive as the more a mage understands their magic, the more they should be able to fine tune it to avoid incurring paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:31:53-08:00","id":1504087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504085#post1504085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New to Mage the Awakening so:<br /> <br /> Why does having a higher gnosis lead to more paradox rolled on overreaching? It seems counterintuitive as the more a mage understands their magic, the more they should be able to fine tune it to avoid incurring paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, the Doylist answer is that nearly all power stats have a drawback when becoming too high. Otherwise players always will aim to maximise the power stat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Watsonian answer is that you are much more closely aligned with the supernal realms therefore much more out of sync with the fallen world, there is more push back to your will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-01-2023, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:35:11-08:00","id":1504088,"title":"","content":"Also the Abyss is more prone to noticing you. You'll make a <i>fine</i> Qliphoth, Gnosis 8 Mage!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:35:15-08:00","id":1504089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504085#post1504085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New to Mage the Awakening so:<br /> <br /> Why does having a higher gnosis lead to more paradox rolled on overreaching? It seems counterintuitive as the more a mage understands their magic, the more they should be able to fine tune it to avoid incurring paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosis isn't understanding so much as intuiting or self-revelating. While being able to better realize the ideal faster and, correspondingly, in more detail is certainly powerful, it's also means a mage has an increased ability to misconceive their imposition on reality, and it's in those cracks of imagination the Abyss slip through. Think of it like trying to solve complex math equations rapidly in your head-the more you practice at it, the more complex that computation becomes, but it also means you get used to thinking so fast that if you miss a detail or get the wrong conclusion, the more likely you're going to continue along with that error before you realize the mistake.<br /> <br /> Or, for the Doylistic reason, because the more powerful you get, the more your poorly handled power should fuck up your day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:48:07-08:00","id":1504092,"title":"","content":"Doylist? Watsonian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T17:51:53-08:00","id":1504094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504092#post1504092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doylist? Watsonian?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doylist: The writer's, or in the case, game desinger's reason, logic, and method.<br /> Watsonian: The character's/in-game reason, logic, and method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T12:03:09-08:00","id":1504131,"title":"","content":"So certain spells of Prime can interact with Twilight. Would a Prime Unveiling be able to reveal ephemeral entities in Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T12:47:11-08:00","id":1504133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504131#post1504131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So certain spells of Prime can interact with Twilight. Would a Prime Unveiling be able to reveal ephemeral entities in Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Something like this would probably reveal that there are entities in Twilight, but it would reveal all of them, and not in particular detail. Prime goes archetypal where the other Arcana for peering into Twilight are specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T14:02:47-08:00","id":1504136,"title":"","content":"Following that train of thought, could a Perfecting of Prime allow an object to count as the correct version of itself for Banes and weaknesses, similar to perfected metals ? An iron dagger counts having the same effect as cold iron, the ashes of a book counting as those of a unique tome or a vial of tears burning a spirit of corruption as if they were those of a pure hearted person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T14:36:33-08:00","id":1504137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504136#post1504136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following that train of thought, could a Perfecting of Prime allow an object to count as the correct version of itself for Banes and weaknesses, similar to perfected metals ? An iron dagger counts having the same effect as cold iron, the ashes of a book counting as those of a unique tome or a vial of tears burning a spirit of corruption as if they were those of a pure hearted person.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be amping up an object\u2019s subjective qualities, whereas Prime Perfecting feels like it would deal more with objective ones, so No for me.<br /> <br /> However, following Ephemeral Enchantment, maybe something that counts as any ephemeral\u2019s Bane could be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T18:04:13-08:00","id":1504157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504136#post1504136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following that train of thought, could a Perfecting of Prime allow an object to count as the correct version of itself for Banes and weaknesses, similar to perfected metals ? An iron dagger counts having the same effect as cold iron, the ashes of a book counting as those of a unique tome or a vial of tears burning a spirit of corruption as if they were those of a pure hearted person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T18:18:36-08:00","id":1504159,"title":"","content":"I need some help with some rules questions. <br /> We're running a relatively high power mage game. Players are single arcana masters with 5 gnosis. They have decent stats, but not crazy. Some players min-maxed, some didn't. You know how it goes.<br /> <br /> A lot of things seem unclear. Could the community help me understand some things?<br /> <br /> 1. Raising stats with magic<br /> There are a number of rank 3 spells that allow a mage to raise their skills or attributes. As I understand, these are hard capped at 10. They soft cap at 5 first, which can be overcome with a reach and a mana, and then duration increased to a year for a Mage to have 10 dexterity and say 10 firearms and athletics for the year, increasing their base defense to 15 or 20, and their firearms rolls to 20+ base. This isn't even hard.<br /> 5 gnosis + 5 arcana<br /> Yantras<br /> rote 6<br /> shadow name 3<br /> high speech 2<br /> location 2<br /> ritual 5<br /> <br /> 28 dice pool plus Fate 2 exceptional luck to add 10 more, for a 38 dice pool to cast. Make potency the primary so it starts at 5, and then -10 for 5 more potency, and a couple minuses for duration and then split it between two stats for +5 (or more) to each.<br /> <br /> Now the issue. I mentioned the cap at 10. This comes from interpretations I've seen here and the stat cap in the book. The spells are worded as such that they raise the stats up, simulating the character buying them with xp, so would hit the same caps that buying via xp would hit.<br /> <br /> The player is saying that Vigor from vampire adds to strength in the same way that the spell honing the form does, and isn't capped at 10, as a blood potency 6 vampire can have a 6 strength + 5 vigor for an 11. They are being pretty rude about the 10 cap being one rule for mage, and one for everyone else.<br /> <br /> What is your interpretation here? Should honing the form be able to give a character a 15 natural strength indefinitely?<br /> <br /> 2. Rote yantras<br /> In the section it says it is capped at 5, but the Order specialty then adds a die. So if a mage has say 5 in Intimidation, and is an Adamantine Arrow, do they add 6 to their rotes from the mudra yantra?<br /> <br /> 3. Exceptional Luck<br /> The Acanthus is using this to add 14 to their skill rolls, and literally double all their starting spell casting dice pools. This seems...insane. How do you manage this at your game? Do you care or does it affect your game?<br /> <br /> 4. Charmed Condition<br /> If it isn't clear, the Acanthus is pushing the boundaries as much as possible.<br /> So there is a spell that can grant the Charmed condition. For 3 reaches, it can be cast reflexively. So is there anything that stops him from simply casting it anytime something tries to hit him, you know, past the 19 defense and whatever armor, to grant the Charmed condition every time and then resolving it so the attacks never do more than 1 damage?<br /> <br /> I feel like the distinction between tilts and conditions would limit this to like once per combat scene. I know there will be an argument about why it cant constantly be used, so wanted to understand what others thought.<br /> <br /> 5. Paradox on long duration spells<br /> I read somewhere that when witnesses are present, at the end of the scene or chapter the spell would need to check for paradox if it originally had over reach. I can't find it now. Does anyone know anything about this?<br /> <br /> <br /> 6. Dissonance and long duration spells<br /> How do you do Dissonance with 10+ potency over reach spells? if a mage has a huge spell on them with an indefinite duration, do you consider it apparent at casual observance, or only when they do something bonkers?<br /> <br /> My thought is that high potency, over reached spells with indefinite duration 'unravel' when around sleepers naturally, and so if they go out in public just loaded with insane spells, the presence of sleepers begins to unravel their spells. This is something I'm going to constantly be rolling for, but more of a storyteller effect where they can't just super cast in their demense and then count on uber spells to always be up all the time.<br /> <br /> 7. Aimed spells and multiple targets<br /> From my understanding, when a spell is cast with touch distance, it can then be fired at a target using Gnosis + Athletics. If the spell takes the multi target factor, then you just roll full Gnosis + Athletics for each target; you do not take a multi-target penalty. I feel this is true, as the multitarget penalty is baked into the autofire rules, and isn't based on normal attacks.<br /> <br /> 8. Armor<br /> I have players with kevlar jackets and reinforced clothing coats, for 2/3 and 1/0 armor ratings. Do you think these should stack? What about using magic to make the coat a 9/0 armor and then stacking it with Mage Armor?<br /> <br /> This isn't even difficult. A starting mage can get a dice pool to cast of<br /> 3 arcana<br /> 3 gnosis<br /> 3 shadow name<br /> 6 rote yantra<br /> 5 ritual cast<br /> 8 exceptional luck<br /> <br /> 20 without Fate, 28 with<br /> 20 with potency primary, one reach for advanced duration, - 14 for 7 more potency, willpower point, gives 7 dice to cast a month long 10 potency spell.<br /> <br /> 9. Can't Raise the stat, add to it!<br /> If number 1 is so, would a creative thaumaturgy spell that added dice to strength dice pools stack with it?<br /> Say, 1 month duration, and +_9 to strength pools, so the mage rolls 10 strength + 10 brawl + 9 added strength dice + dble specialty 2 = 31 dice to swing a punch? All with 3 life and 3 mind total<br /> Does this seem right to you?<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b10. Shadow Name<br /> In the Shadow Name, it states and gives an example of say Thor as a Shadow Name. Then when the mage does things related to the idea of Thor, say lightning and thunder powers, increasing strength to hit stuff with a hammer, jumping really high, they can use their Shadow Name as a Yantra. Now lets say Thor wants to use Fate 2 to cast bigger spells; would they be able to use Shadow Name as a Yantra?<br /> How do you then use Cabal Theme in relation to this? Do your players just always have a +4 yantra at their disposal?<br /> <br /> 11. Nimbus<br /> This one is rough. So I saw the clarification that it doesn\u2019t affect the mage who is having the Nimbus effect. Does Nimbus then apply to everyone in the vicinity, friend or foe, if say it has a 9 potency? Does this mean a mage with -1 resolve, and +2 Firearms would give their foes +2 firearms and then what, 9 again on firearms checks?<br /> This happens every time a mage casts? Does this cause any issues at your table with slowing things down?<br /> <br /> 12. Spells Off Screen<br /> If a player spends time say, each week, to cast a big ol spell off screen, do you require a certain number of dice to make the spell work? Do you offer exceptional successes at a certain breaking point? Say 9 for praxis and 15 for regular spells?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T18:58:27-08:00","id":1504161,"title":"","content":"Oh, boy. You copy and pasted from that inaccessible thread from earlier, yeah? Ok, there is a lot of stuff here, so I\u2019m going to give a answer to a bit I can readily see. <br /> 7: nope, it automatically becomes a Area of Effect when cast as a aimed spell. <br /> 10: nope, it has to be in the symbolism they build for themselves. Thor might be a god, but doesn\u2019t say, make robot limbs. If you call yourself Thor to the point where your identity is a symbol, you have to stick inside those parameters. Likewise, I don\u2019t expect Thor to be casting spells, outside of lightning and hammering. So no.<br /> 11: only if everyone has Active Mage Sight on. As for the second part\u2026well there is a reason most people tend to ignore the nimbus.<br /> 12: That\u2019s up to you, but I find that idea horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:28:33-08:00","id":1504163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504161#post1504161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10: nope, it has to be in the symbolism they build for themselves. Thor might be a god, but doesn\u2019t say, make robot limbs. If you call yourself Thor to the point where your identity is a symbol, you have to stick inside those parameters. Likewise, I don\u2019t expect Thor to be casting spells, outside of lightning and hammering. So no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeeell... there's some wiggle-room. Mostly, it'll depend on which &quot;Thor&quot; they've been cultivating an association with.<br /> <br /> Marvel Movie Thor? Lightning, hammers, and arrogance.<br /> <br /> God of War Thor? Alcoholism, hammers, lightning, depression, and murder.<br /> <br /> Mythological Thor (broad strokes, because there was cultural differences)? Blacksmithing, protection (primarily of others, so you could get away with some Shielding spells, I think), genocide, Destiny-Doom (Could swing that on spells that allow you to meet your fate, like dice-adders or healing spells), thunder, hammers. He also had a pair of goats that pulled his chariot (good arguments for binding Familiars), whom he killed for dinner each night and resurrected each morning (Life, Knit/Mend. Death, Deny the Reaper). Mjolnir -and I think his Belt of Strength?- also had some Fate-esque clauses to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-01-2023, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:31:22-08:00","id":1504164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504161#post1504161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, boy. You copy and pasted from that inaccessible thread from earlier, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Context for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:38:20-08:00","id":1504165,"title":"","content":"6. Let's look at what stats represent for that answer. A score of 1 is below average, a score of 2 is average, and 3 makes you stand out for it, 4 is to be among the greats. 5 is the max for a Human. people notice you past 3. Unless one is working very hard to hide it. I'm going to be honest, anything past 6 in physical stats is going to be noticed immediately. 7 Strength, one is having to worry about not injuring people accidentally. 7 Dexterity can be seen just in how they move. Stamina is a bit harder, but nobody just walks off being smashed in the face with a baseball bat without a care in the world. Social and Mental stats may be easier to hide until one opens their mouth, and casually drops the secrets of the universe into conversation on accident because come on, it's just so simple. So yeah.<br /> <br /> There is another reason not to go all out on spells. Other Mages. How would you react IRL if someone kept walking around in the most cutting-edge weapons and armor? Because I'd get a little nervous. Nervous people do silly things like assume the other person means to use those tools. Potentially on them. That's a problem when the silly person is a Mage. And with those stats, just moving should be pinging PMS.<br /> <br /> One last thing is that it's a known phenomenon that mages with Spells on for extreme durations, especially those that push their abilities past Human limits, tend to spontaneously become raptured. That's a bad time for everyone involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-01-2023, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:41:54-08:00","id":1504166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504164#post1504164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the most recent post while I was waiting for class, but I couldn't access it. Was invisible on the main page, when I looked. Same symptoms as when others have unapproved the first post through editing. Then other stuff on the mage today came up and coved it up. I expect the mods to fix it when they have a chance, making this post kinda premature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:58:32-08:00","id":1504167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504166#post1504166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was the most recent post while I was waiting for class, but I couldn't access it. Was invisible on the main page, when I looked. Same symptoms as when others have unapproved the first post through editing. Then other stuff on the mage today came up and coved it up. I expect the mods to fix it when they have a chance, making this post kinda premature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the edit spam excess, gotcha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:13:51-08:00","id":1504168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504159#post1504159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need some help with some rules questions.<br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The player's being a pissant then. Hard-cap on Skills and Attributes is 10, you don't exceed it by RAW. As for casting it... Yeah, it's not hard at that level, but they should still be rolling for it. Remember that multiple failed attempts per scene add a cumulative -2 penalty per failiure. To say nothing of the Paradox risk per attempt.<br /> <br /> 2. +5 is the hard-cap on how many dice a given Yantra can add. In this case, it means that an AA doesn't need to be a legendary Intimidator to get 5 dice, they just need to be world-class. Any dice in excess of that are wasted, at least as I parse RAW. I can't really think of a Yantra that goes over 5 dice anyway.<br /> <br /> 3. Yeah, Time and Fate can be a bit overpowered. Keep in mind that disallowing the &quot;Affects Spellcasting&quot; Reach effect is a perfectly reasonable houserule. <br /> <br /> 4. Spamming any spell is going to risk the spell not firing, and every failed casting slaps a cumulative -2 penalty to subsequent attempts. To say nothing of Paradox risks.<br /> <br /> 5. Page 118 of core, subheading &quot;Spell control&quot;<br /> <br /> 6. Gonna be honest man, that phrasing was a bit hard to parse, but I'm asuming you mean a spell that is over-reach, and has Potency 10. Unless the spell is obviously magical -which, if we're sticking with the Attributes/Skills thread you seem to be on, will depend on what they're doing with their new stats- then Dissonance won't touch it. An Ansho might, or a thaumavore of some stripe, but RAW Dissonance doesn't destroy wat isn't being perceived.<br /> <br /> 7. Defering to TempleBuilder<br /> <br /> 8. I'd stack 'em, but Dissonance and Paradox are still factors that will come into play. There's only so many times you can take a semi to the face before &quot;I'm wearing kevlar&quot; stops being plausible.<br /> <br /> 9. I can't parse this statement.<br /> <br /> 10. Defering to TempleBuilder, with the caveat that you have wiggleroom within the associated symbolism. Leveraging Thor's Destiny to die killing the World Serpent as a Yantra for spells based around surviving to meet your Doom would work, as would increasing your strength (Belt of Strength). Increasing your Manipulation would not - a honeyed tongue is not one of Thor's commonly perceived attributes.<br /> <br /> 11. Defering to TempleBuilder<br /> <br /> 12. ...Wut. Spells aren't cast piecemetal, they don't do Extended Action rolls. At least, not by RAW. Closest you get is Imbuing a spell, and that's... not the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:14:12-08:00","id":1504169,"title":"","content":"To answer a few off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1) My understanding is that there is an intended hard cap of 10 on all Traits though it has been applied inconsistently across books.<br /> <br /> This also includes Willpower, so even if you had Resolve 10 and Composure 10, Willpower capacity would be 10 rather than 20.<br /> <br /> 2) It's debatable but I think the Mudra bonus should be capped at 5 rather than 6.<br /> <br /> 3) Exceptional Luck is contentious but I think that the only Boon that can be applied to spellcasting is the 9-again.<br /> <br /> 4) Casting Exceptional Luck reflexively costs 1 mana, which also comes out of the per turn mana limit.<br /> <br /> 9) First think what a spell is actually doing rather than just looking at the mechanics listed in Creative Thaumaturgy. How exactly is the action being empowered by magic and then what makes sense?<br /> <br /> But I will also say it is a basic rule of the system that the net modifiers to any roll can only total +5. Combined with my answer to 1) this means nobody should ever be rolling more than 25 dice.<br /> <br /> For some more general advice: if the dice pools would be really big, don't even ask for a roll, just say it succeeds and move on to something more interesting.<br /> <br /> The more time you and your players spend with the magic system and the Mage setting the more you'll come to realise that masters have a million better ways of dealing with problems than shooting them and also have enemies that cannot be shot and don't care about a mage's defence rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:38:28-08:00","id":1504171,"title":"","content":"1:...I'm not seeing any mention of a Supernal cap at 10, just that with a Reach and a Mana you can push past your current maximum. Sounds to me thank you can push your stats up as high as you want with enough potency. That being said, if you want to put a cap at 10, then they should be able to push past that with another reach and mana.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the question, yeah, if they are willing to pay the various prices to have that.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, Fate can do crazy stuff. No, I don't really care much, except on spell casting. That one is a pet peeve of mine, but it has costs. Generally speaking, Mage is more creative problem solving than rolling huge dice pools.<br /> <br /> 4: Yeah. Can't react to what you don't see coming. Also, at this point, they should be facing the Master level threats.<br /> <br /> 5: I don't think that's a thing, sorry. Paradox happens at the time of the spell, Dissonance happens afterward.<br /> <br /> 8: I think they stack, yes.<br /> <br /> 9: Yes, large dice pools* seem about right for Master level content. I remind you this is the level of spell where you can just Unmake stuff. Just poof, gone. That is stuff their peers can do. If you are worried about not being able to threaten your player with creatures and monsters, I'd advise having problems that can't be solved so easily. How does one fix a rogue cannibal timeline? What do you do about the one raving lunatic who managed to turn their soul into a near-permanent abyssal gateway, and literally can't die?<br /> <br /> *I'm not doing the math right now, but I'm noting a lot of your assumptions like everyone having a +5 Mudra isn't exactly common.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looks like other people answered the other stuff before me. I hope some of this alleviates your worries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-01-2023, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:52:35-08:00","id":1504173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504159#post1504159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the issue. I mentioned the cap at 10. This comes from interpretations I've seen here and the stat cap in the book. The spells are worded as such that they raise the stats up, simulating the character buying them with xp, so would hit the same caps that buying via xp would hit.<br /> <br /> The player is saying that Vigor from vampire adds to strength in the same way that the spell honing the form does, and isn't capped at 10, as a blood potency 6 vampire can have a 6 strength + 5 vigor for an 11. They are being pretty rude about the 10 cap being one rule for mage, and one for everyone else.<br /> <br /> What is your interpretation here? Should honing the form be able to give a character a 15 natural strength indefinitely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus stats from spells are not subject to a cap except in the sense that the character's Gnosis-derived Trait limit affects whether a spell raising a Trait costs Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Rote yantras<br /> In the section it says it is capped at 5, but the Order specialty then adds a die. So if a mage has say 5 in Intimidation, and is an Adamantine Arrow, do they add 6 to their rotes from the mudra yantra? </div> </div> </div>It's capped at 5. An Order's Rote Specialties allow you to get a +5 Yantra without needing five dots in the encoded Rote Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Exceptional Luck<br /> The Acanthus is using this to add 14 to their skill rolls, and literally double all their starting spell casting dice pools. This seems...insane. How do you manage this at your game? Do you care or does it affect your game? </div> </div> </div>The simple answer, as has come up over and over and over, is that the general mechanics for boons affecting spellcasting take precedence over a literal reading of the generally-stated verbiage repeated in each Reach effect with this effect: boons can only benefit spellcasting by providing 9-Again or 8-Again. Fools Rush In is the only published Fate spell that allows a dice bonus to apply to spellcasting rolls, and that dice bonus is conditional and Reach-intensive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Charmed Condition<br /> If it isn't clear, the Acanthus is pushing the boundaries as much as possible.<br /> So there is a spell that can grant the Charmed condition. For 3 reaches, it can be cast reflexively. So is there anything that stops him from simply casting it anytime something tries to hit him, you know, past the 19 defense and whatever armor, to grant the Charmed condition every time and then resolving it so the attacks never do more than 1 damage? </div> </div> </div>Reflexive casting costs Mana and running around with a bunch of other spells active is going to make Reach a liability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Paradox on long duration spells<br /> I read somewhere that when witnesses are present, at the end of the scene or chapter the spell would need to check for paradox if it originally had over reach. I can't find it now. Does anyone know anything about this? </div> </div> </div>You are thinking of Dissonance. Paradox rolls are made immediately before the spellcasting roll is made, and not at any other time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Dissonance and long duration spells<br /> How do you do Dissonance with 10+ potency over reach spells? if a mage has a huge spell on them with an indefinite duration, do you consider it apparent at casual observance, or only when they do something bonkers?<br /> <br /> My thought is that high potency, over reached spells with indefinite duration 'unravel' when around sleepers naturally, and so if they go out in public just loaded with insane spells, the presence of sleepers begins to unravel their spells. This is something I'm going to constantly be rolling for, but more of a storyteller effect where they can't just super cast in their demense and then count on uber spells to always be up all the time. </div> </div> </div>Most people who are not mages cannot see spells that don't have perceptible effects. The primary concerns with walking around with a bunch of spells on you are that spell control will eat through your safe Reach fairly quickly and relinquishment is expensive or risky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. Aimed spells and multiple targets<br /> From my understanding, when a spell is cast with touch distance, it can then be fired at a target using Gnosis + Athletics. If the spell takes the multi target factor, then you just roll full Gnosis + Athletics for each target; you do not take a multi-target penalty. I feel this is true, as the multitarget penalty is baked into the autofire rules, and isn't based on normal attacks. </div> </div> </div>Aimed spells explicitly must use Area instead of Number of Subjects for their Scale, centered on wherever the mage aims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8. Armor<br /> I have players with kevlar jackets and reinforced clothing coats, for 2/3 and 1/0 armor ratings. Do you think these should stack? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about using magic to make the coat a 9/0 armor and then stacking it with Mage Armor? </div> </div> </div>The Amnion explicitly doesn't stack with &quot;physical armor&quot; but does stack with Mage Armor (as an Attainment), and my assumption would be the lack of such a specific statement means Mage Armor does not stack with regular Armor, either. Chronicles of Darkness is not built under the assumption of dicepools over 15 or Durability/Armor ratings over 5 being unexceptional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't even difficult. A starting mage can get a dice pool to cast of<br /> 3 arcana<br /> 3 gnosis<br /> 3 shadow name<br /> 6 rote yantra<br /> 5 ritual cast<br /> 8 exceptional luck<br /> <br /> 20 without Fate, 28 with<br /> 20 with potency primary, one reach for advanced duration, - 14 for 7 more potency, willpower point, gives 7 dice to cast a month long 10 potency spell. </div> </div> </div>I have described above why Exceptional Luck is irrelevant and why the Mudra is not providing six dice, and most enhancement spells (including Aegis, the default Armor-boosting spell) are Duration-primary and thus need another Reach to switch the primary factor to Potency, but also &quot;A mage who has fully invested in a Shadow Name compatible with enhancing a piece of protective gear and is at or near the peak of human expertise in the Skill encoded into the spell mnemonic for the spell to perform that enhancement spends six straight hours performing ritual spellcasting to do so&quot; is &quot;easy&quot; in the very very plainly unproblematic sense of &quot;a specialist is dedicating time to getting this to work right&quot; and it's not doing anybody any favors to use it as an argument about the difficulties you are expecting to encounter throwing problems at such a specialist directly within their strike zone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11. Nimbus<br /> This one is rough. So I saw the clarification that it doesn\u2019t affect the mage who is having the Nimbus effect. Does Nimbus then apply to everyone in the vicinity, friend or foe, if say it has a 9 potency? Does this mean a mage with -1 resolve, and +2 Firearms would give their foes +2 firearms and then what, 9 again on firearms checks?<br /> This happens every time a mage casts? Does this cause any issues at your table with slowing things down? </div> </div> </div>The Nimbus Tilt applies to characters who can perceive the Nimbus, which translates to characters with Active Mage Sight up, supernatural characters having their &quot;aura&quot; abilities counteracted by a mage flaring their Immediate Nimbus in response, or any characters witnessing an isolated flare. The second of these requires the other party to lose the contested roll the aura contest entails, while the other two require the witness to have a Resolve that does not exceed the Nimbus's strength, which is either the spell's Potency or the result of a Gnosis roll from the mage, and the Tilt lasts for a turn unless it was caused by a Reach-intensive spell.<br /> <br /> &quot;Any witnesses&quot; means this does not differentiate its effects between subjects. Bonus dice applied to Skill rolls through the Nimbus Tilt also apply the 8-Again effect, while penalties to Skill rolls remove 10-Again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 12. Spells Off Screen<br /> If a player spends time say, each week, to cast a big ol spell off screen, do you require a certain number of dice to make the spell work? Do you offer exceptional successes at a certain breaking point? Say 9 for praxis and 15 for regular spells? </div> </div> </div>I do not understand this question, because spellcasting <i>specifically</i> does not use the Extended Action rules on account of how you can't leave casting a spell partway done and resume it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-01-2023, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T06:48:11-08:00","id":1504199,"title":"","content":"Thank you, this has been helpful.<br /> <br /> I'll remove the other post. It was flagged because I corrected an error and it registered as spam. I felt this had a little bit of a time crunch and apologize for the rushed nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThere are some obvious interpretation areas here. Probably expected in a storyteller game as opposed to a more mechanics focused game.<br /> <br /> For the Exceptional Luck, can anyone clarify why it can't be used to add dice? Does the bonus dice reference a skill, and therefore can't be used for spellcasting?<br /> <br /> After rereading the boons, the bonus dice says usually a skill, but doesn't say anything about spellcasting. The 9 again says it can affect spells for +2 reach. <br /> <br /> Is your interpretation that the bonus dice boon is just for skills and mundane actions as implied?<br /> <br /> Does the 9 again boon require 2 additional reach to affect spellcasting with exceptional luck in addition to the 2 reach exceptional luck lists to affect spellcasting for a total of 4 reach, or is this doubling up on the same effect?<br /> <br /> 12. My players like to have long duration buff spells up all the time, so as part of their character creation, they supply what spells they would have cast with extended duration and what the dice pool is. This &quot;off screen&quot; casting is part of the downtime system I sometimes use and was there to streamline play. I can reference this sheet to see what to expect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that it isn't an extended roll, but is using the ritual bonus to get the +5 dice, and then taking time to get the best yantras possible. This, plus the abuse of exceptional luck to add dice, allows for really high potency spells with 1 year duration. I was wondering what other thoughts of this or if they allowed these kinds of things at their tables.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller system, a lot of rules are preference and personal interpretation, and it helps to get the opinions and interpretations of others to help color and support or change my own.<br /> <br /> Quick clarification on rote yantra,<br /> <br /> The book says it caps at 5 but then states immediately after that an order specialty adds another +1, for 5+1 or 6 total. This seems like it would be rare, but Mind 3 let's you raise skills to 5 fairly easily, and some players like to min.max their skills to make their rotes stronger.<br /> <br /> Do you allow a 6 mudra yantra or refer to the hard cap of 5 and keep it there?<br /> <br /> Thank you again for all the replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","user":"Kaimuund","date":".  Added reference material about exceptional luck 03-02-2023, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T08:15:04-08:00","id":1504201,"title":"","content":"Please use the quote function. I don\u2019t know whose point you are talking about, since a lot of us answered, and so I can\u2019t answer your questions. It\u2019s a button under a particular post. Says quote.<br /> <br /> Edit: whoops, might have read your post incorrectly, sorry. Hope Kaiser helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-02-2023, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T08:15:48-08:00","id":1504202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504199#post1504199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, this has been helpful.<br /> <br /> I'll remove the other post. It was flagged because I corrected an error and it registered as spam. I felt this had a little bit of a time crunch and apologize for the rushed nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThere are some obvious interpretation areas here. Probably expected in a storyteller game as opposed to a more mechanics focused game.<br /> <br /> For the Exceptional Luck, can anyone clarify why it can't be used to add dice? Does the bonus dice reference a skill, and therefore can't be used for spellcasting?<br /> <br /> After rereading the boons, the bonus dice says usually a skill, but doesn't say anything about spellcasting. The 9 again says it can affect spells for +2 reach.<br /> <br /> Is your interpretation that the bonus dice boon is just for skills and mundane actions as implied?<br /> <br /> Does the 9 again boon require 2 additional reach to affect spellcasting with exceptional luck in addition to the 2 reach exceptional luck lists to affect spellcasting for a total of 4 reach, or is this doubling up on the same effect?<br /> <br /> 12. My players like to have long duration buff spells up all the time, so as part of their character creation, they supply what spells they would have cast with extended duration and what the dice pool is. This &quot;off screen&quot; casting is part of the downtime system I sometimes use and was there to streamline play. I can reference this sheet to see what to expect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that it isn't an extended roll, but is using the ritual bonus to get the +5 dice, and then taking time to get the best yantras possible. This, plus the abuse of exceptional luck to add dice, allows for really high potency spells with 1 year duration. I was wondering what other thoughts of this or if they allowed these kinds of things at their tables.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller system, a lot of rules are preference and personal interpretation, and it helps to get the opinions and interpretations of others to help color and support or change my own.<br /> <br /> Quick clarification on rote yantra,<br /> <br /> The book says it caps at 5 but then states immediately after that an order specialty adds another +1, for 5+1 or 6 total. This seems like it would be rare, but Mind 3 let's you raise skills to 5 fairly easily, and some players like to min.max their skills to make their rotes stronger.<br /> <br /> Do you allow a 6 mudra yantra or refer to the hard cap of 5 and keep it there?<br /> <br /> Thank you again for all the replies.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to answer your questions as clearly as possible, I will break down my explanation into 3 sections, one for rotes, one for Exceptional Luck and one for spellcasting rules.<br /> <br /> Rotes provide mudra yantras. A mudra uses the mage's rating on the encoded skill as the yantra bonus. This provides a maximum value of +5. Which means if your rote skill is Expression, for example, a mage with 5 dots and one with 10 dots will both only get a +5 (core book page 121). If the encoded skill is an Order skill for the caster (found on page 82), they get one more dice, which may push the total to +6.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck (detailed on page 135) can provide dice bonuses to mundane skills (or spellcasting rolls with 2 Reach), a bonus of [Potency] for up to [Potency] chosen rolls, which means it does have limited uses. It can also impose conditions and tilts based on the rules on page 134.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting rules dictate that, after applying penalties, the effect of all yantras put together cannot provide a total bonus beyond +5 (details on page 112). Exceptional Luck is not a yantra, so its Reach effect is not bound by this rule.<br /> <br /> Remember that there are downsides for having these spells always up. They only have [Gnosis] spell control, and every spell cast after that requires one Reach per spell above it (see the side tab on page 112). Relinquishing them unsafely requires a Willpower point, it also means they cannot cancel the spell themselves, they need to have it dispelled. It can also mutate after a while (see page 118). Socially speaking, relinquishing unsafely is illegal in many Consilia, or at least seen as grossly negligent. Best case scenario, the Guardians will dislike any long term use of unsafe relinquishment.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, safe relinquishment is always an option, but it requires a Willpower dot. The downside is that it does not make the spell immune to dispellation and it will still vanish once the duration elapses.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-02-2023, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T08:55:20-08:00","id":1504205,"title":"","content":"Suppose the Silver Ladder has a Proximus family focused on using Fate/Mind to &quot;inspire&quot; people and whose curse is that they have to take credit for anything good that happens as the result of their inspiration. These people seem like they'd annoy the Guardians of the Veil by constantly telling people they inspired everything good the local Ladder does, but the family curse would prohibit any easy solution. How do you guys think the local Guardians or the local Ladders would end up dealing with this problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T10:03:54-08:00","id":1504208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504205#post1504205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose the Silver Ladder has a Proximus family focused on using Fate/Mind to &quot;inspire&quot; people and whose curse is that they have to take credit for anything good that happens as the result of their inspiration. These people seem like they'd annoy the Guardians of the Veil by constantly telling people they inspired everything good the local Ladder does, but the family curse would prohibit any easy solution. How do you guys think the local Guardians or the local Ladders would end up dealing with this problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>THe Guardians probably wouldn't care about it so much as the fact that such a collective of Proximus is set up to be killed by opposition. Whether that's a problem in that you have to keep saving them from themselves or a boon in that you basically have a ready made patsy to soak up violence that might otherwise go to the members of the Pentacle depends on how jaded the individual Guardian is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T10:13:06-08:00","id":1504211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504205#post1504205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose the Silver Ladder has a Proximus family focused on using Fate/Mind to &quot;inspire&quot; people and whose curse is that they have to take credit for anything good that happens as the result of their inspiration. These people seem like they'd annoy the Guardians of the Veil by constantly telling people they inspired everything good the local Ladder does, but the family curse would prohibit any easy solution. How do you guys think the local Guardians or the local Ladders would end up dealing with this problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very easy to deal with. Nothing forbids them from mentioning the curse. Even if the curse did, an undocumented Proximi Dynasty would make mages curious. So at the very least someone will study the curse with their Focused Mage Sight and some Knowing spells.<br /> <br /> After that you just say &quot;they are a Proximi whose curse makes them do this. Don't judge their behavior based on how they deal with the curse, keep an eye on the full picture&quot;. Even the Guardians wouldn't really be annoyed if they knew its they need to filter that out during interactions. Do you need to find out what they really did ? Read their minds, use postcognition, ask the people they know.<br /> <br /> However, the way it was presented suggested that you intended them to take credit for everything good that happens in the faction they are in, rather than anything good that happened due to using their blessings (which would be fair enough).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T11:52:52-08:00","id":1504218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504211#post1504211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is very easy to deal with. Nothing forbids them from mentioning the curse. Even if the curse did, an undocumented Proximi Dynasty would make mages curious. So at the very least someone will study the curse with their Focused Mage Sight and some Knowing spells.<br /> <br /> After that you just say &quot;they are a Proximi whose curse makes them do this. Don't judge their behavior based on how they deal with the curse, keep an eye on the full picture&quot;. Even the Guardians wouldn't really be annoyed if they knew its they need to filter that out during interactions. Do you need to find out what they really did ? Read their minds, use postcognition, ask the people they know.<br /> <br /> However, the way it was presented suggested that you intended them to take credit for everything good that happens in the faction they are in, rather than anything good that happened due to using their blessings (which would be fair enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I was thinking about it the persistent form of their curse would be them needing to take credit if someone was talking about good things that came from their blessings, which would be annoying but mostly reasonable, while the severe form would require them to brag to an audience who was not aware. So, yes, the part where they take credit for what they helped others do is annoying, but the real problem is they might brag about something you wanted to keep secret.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504208#post1504208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THe Guardians probably wouldn't care about it so much as the fact that such a collective of Proximus is set up to be killed by opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guardians are dicks, yes, but letting a family of Proximus get themselves killed seems a bit of a stretch for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether that's a problem in that you have to keep saving them from themselves or a boon in that you basically have a ready made patsy to soak up violence that might otherwise go to the members of the Pentacle depends on how jaded the individual Guardian is. </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of it as being more towards the &quot;problem&quot; end of the spectrum where there are essentially a few dozen people willing to cast Superlative Luck or Augment Mind on command, but who keep bragging to local news about it. I just wanted to make sure the Guardians couldn't trivially solve the problem I'm trying to give them.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T12:10:37-08:00","id":1504219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504199#post1504199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Exceptional Luck, can anyone clarify why it can't be used to add dice? Does the bonus dice reference a skill, and therefore can't be used for spellcasting?<br /> <br /> After rereading the boons, the bonus dice says usually a skill, but doesn't say anything about spellcasting. The 9 again says it can affect spells for +2 reach.<br /> <br /> Is your interpretation that the bonus dice boon is just for skills and mundane actions as implied?<br /> <br /> Does the 9 again boon require 2 additional reach to affect spellcasting with exceptional luck in addition to the 2 reach exceptional luck lists to affect spellcasting for a total of 4 reach, or is this doubling up on the same effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take the text under Exceptional Luck to be basically a reminder of the text in the Boon section, so it is only +2 Reach (not 4).<br /> <br /> The interpretation that it can only give 9-again/8-again to spellcasting keeps the spell roughly in line with the power level of the Prime spell As Above, So Above. Whereas the interpretation that it can apply arbitrary dice bonuses to spellcasting creates game-breaking absurdities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 12. My players like to have long duration buff spells up all the time, so as part of their character creation, they supply what spells they would have cast with extended duration and what the dice pool is. This &quot;off screen&quot; casting is part of the downtime system I sometimes use and was there to streamline play. I can reference this sheet to see what to expect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that it isn't an extended roll, but is using the ritual bonus to get the +5 dice, and then taking time to get the best yantras possible. This, plus the abuse of exceptional luck to add dice, allows for really high potency spells with 1 year duration. I was wondering what other thoughts of this or if they allowed these kinds of things at their tables. </div> </div> </div>I'd let them have the spells at whatever Potency they can get still with positive dice without rolling. Then I'd show them there are consequences to walking around all the time like miniature Supernal suns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book says it caps at 5 but then states immediately after that an order specialty adds another +1, for 5+1 or 6 total. This seems like it would be rare, but Mind 3 let's you raise skills to 5 fairly easily, and some players like to min.max their skills to make their rotes stronger.<br /> <br /> Do you allow a 6 mudra yantra or refer to the hard cap of 5 and keep it there? </div> </div> </div>My reading is that the Mudra bonus is capped at 5. Full stop. And that bonus is made up of the relevant skill dots plus a possible one from the order rote speciality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T17:19:11-08:00","id":1504231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504199#post1504199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12. My players like to have long duration buff spells up all the time, so as part of their character creation, they supply what spells they would have cast with extended duration and what the dice pool is. This &quot;off screen&quot; casting is part of the downtime system I sometimes use and was there to streamline play. I can reference this sheet to see what to expect.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that it isn't an extended roll, but is using the ritual bonus to get the +5 dice, and then taking time to get the best yantras possible. This, plus the abuse of exceptional luck to add dice, allows for really high potency spells with 1 year duration. I was wondering what other thoughts of this or if they allowed these kinds of things at their tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about this is that if you're &quot;streamlining play&quot; by handwaving the fact that characters are spending several hours to set up something they intend to have last for a month, you can afford to have that preparation take a short scene and have them do the roll, particularly if you're specifically concerned about them walking around with absurdly powerful spells that you apparently are just letting them sideline the primary risks of creating.<br /> <br /> Like, I want to be quite plain here, pushing the limits of your Gnosis and the potential issues that can lead to are part of the reason Paradox works the way it does and why spell factors just apply penalties to a roll you only need a single success on. Dice are being rolled because there's a chance that you'll fail and have wasted six hours or a valuable reagent or a rare opportunity.<br /> <br /> If you want to math it out and remove the chances of interesting failure, a moderately reasonable shorthand is that if you still have four dice left in the spellcasting pool after penalties, you have roughly a 75% chance of rolling at least one success; if you have six or seven dice, you have roughly 90% odds of success; nine or ten dice gives about 96% odds; and at 13+ dice you're just adding decimal values to the end of 99%. Pick a probability threshold and let them put as many spell factors as they could fit into their dicepool above that number of dice onto the spells they're doing during downtime; anything more intense will require a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T18:12:59-08:00","id":1504234,"title":"","content":"Practicality question about Combined Spells - can you use <u>Supernal Veil</u> as part of a combined casting, to Veil the other spell? That is, if the Mage casts <u>Crucible</u> and <u>Supernal Veil</u> together, is the Crucilbe spell now veiled from PMS/AMS? Or does <u>Supernal Veil</u> require you to target something that already exist beforehand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T18:17:51-08:00","id":1504235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504234#post1504234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practicality question about Combined Spells - can you use <u>Supernal Veil</u> as part of a combined casting, to Veil the other spell? That is, if the Mage casts <u>Crucible</u> and <u>Supernal Veil</u> together, is the Crucilbe spell now veiled from PMS/AMS? Or does <u>Supernal Veil</u> require you to target something that already exist beforehand?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that it can be. In fact, the main design reason that the Szary Strazynik get Shadow Name 3 as part of their Mystery Cult merit is so they can get one with a hiding symbolism and use it for combined spells to stay under the radar. Its one of the reasons that they are a nightmare to track if they want to vanish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T18:50:10-08:00","id":1504237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504218#post1504218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians are dicks, yes, but letting a family of Proximus get themselves killed seems a bit of a stretch for them. I was thinking of it as being more towards the &quot;problem&quot; end of the spectrum where there are essentially a few dozen people willing to cast Superlative Luck or Augment Mind on command, but who keep bragging to local news about it. I just wanted to make sure the Guardians couldn't trivially solve the problem I'm trying to give them.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>While I generally agree with these being a problem for them, with my notation on that making it clear that the problem is less one of PR and more one of literal livelihood, it's important to note that it's not particularly off the table for them either. Sins for a just end grant Wisdom, after all, and sometimes the problems solve themselves.<br /> <br /> With the context you added, it's not like their options get any rosier. If they're not flat out breaching the Veil <i>and</i> the Precept of Secrecy, they're sure as hell flirting with it, and with the idea of the curse in particular, what you have here is not so much a moral quandry, as it is <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2006/03/23/episode-676-supernatural-selection/\" target=\"_blank\">a beast begging to be killed so it may understand the world as being capable of mercy</a>. This is the sort of scenario that really invites the Guardian's particular hubris without being challenging about it.<br /> <br /> If I were going to run this scenario, I can think of one easy fix to make it all the murkier-make it the group of Proximi's inclination, not their curse. That gives you the room to play with and manipulate the groups actions and reactions towards the Guardian's responses and efforts, which in turn makes a clear answer one way or the other more muddled as gentle guidance or misdirection can sometimes seem to work only to be completely ignored, or for the threat of the scenario to kind of get it sinking in, and of course makes it all the more muddled as a issue of dealing with a group verus dealing with the individuals in that group. The curse really just makes it seem like lemmings near a cliff scenario, and even with my general role of being the one who continually makes it clear the the Guardians are indeed merciful instead of perpetually cold-blooded killers would be hard pressed to not argue that it'd be easier to let that problem solve itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2023, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T21:41:18-08:00","id":1504241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504231#post1504231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ly if you're specifically concerned about them walking around with absurdly powerful spells that you apparently are just letting them sideline the primary risks of creating.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're concerned, remember, if they can do it, your NPCs can do it too.<br /> <br /> Though they could he walking around with an equivalent potency year long duration shielding spell, prime ward, space spell to redirect sympathic attacks to a different sympathic connection, fate spells to do miracles... Death spells to raise a zombie hoard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T22:07:20-08:00","id":1504243,"title":"","content":"Vows are significant enough to show up under Fate Sight / <u>Interconnections</u>, correct? That is, the Obligated condition would show up under spells of that vein?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T04:24:46-08:00","id":1504253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504243#post1504243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vows are significant enough to show up under Fate Sight / <u>Interconnections</u>, correct? That is, the Obligated condition would show up under spells of that vein?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at page 48 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, it registers as a contract with the Supernal, so it would appear under both of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T09:12:27-08:00","id":1504267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504237#post1504237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The curse really just makes it seem like lemmings near a cliff scenario, and even with my general role of being the one who continually makes it clear the the Guardians are indeed merciful instead of perpetually cold-blooded killers would be hard pressed to not argue that it'd be easier to let that problem solve itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself imagining the Guardians in this scenario as having the role of the documentary crew that were the actual reason those lemmings went off the cliff.<br /> <br /> Although the part where they convince everybody it was a totally natural occurrence does seem fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T12:37:59-08:00","id":1504285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504267#post1504267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find myself imagining the Guardians in this scenario as having the role of the documentary crew that were the actual reason those lemmings went off the cliff.<br /> <br /> Although the part where they convince everybody it was a totally natural occurrence does seem fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that could be an interesting story, if your players were on board from it.<br /> <br /> But the big thing about this is that the curse invites the cliff regardless of whether the Guardians do anything or not-hell, if the Guardians even know about it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T13:56:10-08:00","id":1504292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504285#post1504285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that could be an interesting story, if your players were on board from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's probably the real killer for them. &quot;A group of NPCs that are valuable allies, but constantly create problems that need to be cleaned up&quot; is probably not that fun for anyone else even though they could be tweaked until they represent a viable group in-universe.<br /> <br /> Although from that perspective, &quot;A group of NPCs that constantly create problems, but have too many political connections for you to just kill&quot; might be viable as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T16:07:19-08:00","id":1504296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504159#post1504159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <br /> <br /> 2. Rote yantras<br /> In the section it says it is capped at 5, but the Order specialty then adds a die. So if a mage has say 5 in Intimidation, and is an Adamantine Arrow, do they add 6 to their rotes from the mudra yantra?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The yantra bonus is not capped at +5. The bonus you get from the skill is capped at +5 and then you get an additional die if its a order rote. If you have the skill at 7 you'd only get +5 from the skill but still get the additional die for the order rote making a +6.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T17:23:49-08:00","id":1504303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504292#post1504292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's probably the real killer for them. &quot;A group of NPCs that are valuable allies, but constantly create problems that need to be cleaned up&quot; is probably not that fun for anyone else even though they could be tweaked until they represent a viable group in-universe.<br /> <br /> Although from that perspective, &quot;A group of NPCs that constantly create problems, but have too many political connections for you to just kill&quot; might be viable as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason I suggest changing the curse. The former can be fairly easy to get them into...if they can actually <i>do something</i> about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T07:11:26-08:00","id":1504360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504296#post1504296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The yantra bonus is not capped at +5. The bonus you get from the skill is capped at +5 and then you get an additional die if its a order rote. If you have the skill at 7 you'd only get +5 from the skill but still get the additional die for the order rote making a +6.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This was my initial impression and what I had been going with.<br /> <br /> However, the earlier responses plus this in the errata<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Mudra Yantras</b> cap at +5 each. It's still possible to, say, give yourself Athletics 5 with one spell before casting an Athletics-based rote for maximum effect, or buy a superhuman skill with a Gnosis above 5, but it <b>won't benefit rotes. </b>\u200b<br /> <br /> Pushed me to just hard cap it at 5 for any Yantra, regardless of specialty. Since I have one player who took 5 in his rote specialties, and 1's in other skills he wanted so he could just boost them with Mind 3, I think it's probably the right call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T18:21:54-08:00","id":1504395,"title":"","content":"Do Proximi Blessings gain the unlimited free Reach when their spells are kept within the bounds of a Demesne of the Realm that has the given Arcanum as Ruling ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T18:42:49-08:00","id":1504397,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it. A Demesne is an artifical conduit to the Supernal, and Proximi are drawing down Supernal power the same as a Mage is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T19:09:08-08:00","id":1504402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504395#post1504395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Proximi Blessings gain the unlimited free Reach when their spells are kept within the bounds of a Demesne of the Realm that has the given Arcanum as Ruling ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Proximi can't use Yantras, the Paradox mitigation of a Demesne or Verge is applies to spells that qualify for the Yantra bonus, and the effects of Paradox on Proximus Blessings is different from its effects on spells. I'd say &quot;no.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T08:30:31-08:00","id":1504430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504402#post1504402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proximi can't use Yantras, the Paradox mitigation of a Demesne or Verge is applies to spells that qualify for the Yantra bonus, and the effects of Paradox on Proximus Blessings is different from its effects on spells. I'd say &quot;no.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, Proximi can't use yantras, but the bonus is for *spells*, not casters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T09:22:43-08:00","id":1504437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504430#post1504430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say yes, Proximi can't use yantras, but the bonus is for *spells*, not casters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The fact that the caster can't utilize the Yantra bonus doesn't mean the spell stops qualifying for that Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T15:04:37-08:00","id":1504492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504430#post1504430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say yes, Proximi can't use yantras, but the bonus is for *spells*, not casters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I had a line that I ended up deleting saying that if you wanted to emphasize the &quot;Supernal power in their blood&quot; point I'd make a caveat for appropriate Supernal Verges, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Despite the mechanical language, Proximi are not spellcasters and their Blessings are not actually spells. They get free Reach on every Blessing as though they had exactly the number of Arcanum dots needed to cast that spell, and every further Reach applies one die of Paradox risk; seldom do I expect a Proximus will need more than six Reach on a single Blessing, nor do I anticipate Mage's equivalent of ghoul families, stigmatics, and wolf-blooded to need to avail themselves of a resource specifically built to help spellcasters push their limits without having undergone the ordeals that make pushing one's limits a tempting process by Awakening, or at least not the weak version of such a resource that doesn't insulate spells from Dissonance nor allow the Supernal to intrude upon the Phenomenal without being called.<br /> <br /> These are family lines with a limited quantity of Will-powered Supernal abilities that cash in for Arcane Experience when the character Awakens. They get the ability to perform thematically-appropriate oblations to generate Mana and spend Mana to mitigate Paradox risk, which for them translates to reducing the changes of their family curse getting worse for a while and little else. They're very clearly made to model the sort of power-with-a-price inborn abilities similarly found in other gamelines, not simply to act as Diet Magi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T18:11:40-08:00","id":1504520,"title":"","content":"Would a mobile scrying window just be a Reach effect added to <u>Scrying</u>? That is, a mobile sensory node that the mage can shift about. You can make something close using <u>Psychic Projection</u>, but that requires abandoning your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T01:09:27-08:00","id":1504554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504520#post1504520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a mobile scrying window just be a Reach effect added to <u>Scrying</u>? That is, a mobile sensory node that the mage can shift about. You can make something close using <u>Psychic Projection</u>, but that requires abandoning your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you use something like one mind two thoughts to exist in your body and psychically projected at the same time? (And is that commonly used for exploring the Astral and remaining conscious)<br /> <br /> For a Scrying window to be mobile it would have to change subject... I like the idea of an AoE effect where you could focus on anything which enters the area (as they become subject to the spell) which is almost how AoE effects actually work.<br /> <br /> So i would allow that with a reach effect on Scrying. How and Ever, i think you are looking for something more like Telekenisis, where the spell gives you a power which you can then use on different targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T01:17:00-08:00","id":1504556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504554#post1504554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you use something like one mind two thoughts to exist in your body and psychically projected at the same time? (And is that commonly used for exploring the Astral and remaining conscious)<br /> <br /> For a Scrying window to be mobile it would have to change subject... I like the idea of an AoE effect where you could focus on anything which enters the area (as they become subject to the spell) which is almost how AoE effects actually work.<br /> <br /> So i would allow that with a reach effect on Scrying. How and Ever, i think you are looking for something more like Telekenisis, where the spell gives you a power which you can then use on different targets.</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Psychic Projection</u> specifically leaves the body comatose, with the phrasing impling that there's no conscious part of you remaining in it. I don't think <u>One Mind Two Thoughts</u> can overcome that, although it is the spell I would require for multi-tasking with mobile scrying windows.<br /> <br /> As for <u>Telekinesis</u> - RAW, <u>Telekinesis</u> is cast on single targets, you cant switch subjects once it's cast. Which, sadly, greatly reduces utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T01:55:15-08:00","id":1504559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504556#post1504556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for <u>Telekinesis</u> - RAW, <u>Telekinesis</u> is cast on single targets, you cant switch subjects once it's cast. Which, sadly, greatly reduces utility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Telekinesis, that isn't clear.<br /> <br /> It states you can move an object, but not that the object is the subject of the spell (i presume casting this as an AoE spell does give greater utility with your interpretation)<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess it is the repeated concentration and instant actions which make me think that the spell isn't like other spells. You can't have a dynamic spell which changes on an instant action like that. You have to set the imago upon casting, which is fine if you are the subject of the spell and it gives you a power... But that doesn't exclude the idea that you also have to pick an object to move...<br /> <br /> Edit: (the only similar spell i can think of is Matter Shaping, where you may require a crafts roll, but it lets you continue to shape the subject until the spell duration ends).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T02:00:56-08:00","id":1504561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504559#post1504559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Telekinesis, that isn't clear.<br /> <br /> It states you can move an object, but not that the object is the subject of the spell (i presume casting this as an AoE spell does give greater utility with your interpretation)<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess it is the repeated concentration and instant actions which make me think that the spell isn't like other spells. You can't have a dynamic spell which changes on an instant action like that. You have to set the imago upon casting, which is fine if you are the subject of the spell and it gives you a power... But that doesn't exclude the idea that you also have to pick an object to move...<br /> <br /> Edit: (the only similar spell i can think of is Matter Shaping, where you may require a crafts roll, but it lets you continue to shape the subject until the spell duration ends).</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, Telekinesis grants its subject the ability to project telekinetic force; it alters how the subject interacts with physical force (by greatly loosening the \u2018You need limbs\u2019 feature).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T02:16:51-08:00","id":1504562,"title":"","content":"Huh. Yeah, I think I misinterpreted how <u>Telekinesis</u> works. Based on the first line I thought it was &quot;targeted object&quot;, but the fourth line supports it being an extension of the Mage's will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T02:21:20-08:00","id":1504563,"title":"","content":"Hang on, then what is the range on the telekinetic force? Your normal armspan? Sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T02:41:53-08:00","id":1504565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504563#post1504563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, then what is the range on the telekinetic force? Your normal armspan? Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the force appears according to casting - touch/sensory - but can be manipulated a theoretically infinite distance away from the mage. But you'll be limited in what you can do with it if you can't see what you're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:09:00-08:00","id":1504569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504563#post1504563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, then what is the range on the telekinetic force? Your normal armspan? Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch, Sensory or Sympathetic, like every other spell.<br /> <br /> The spell says &quot;The mage can conjure telekinetic force to lift or manipulate an object remotely.&quot; An object being the subject of the spell. You then can area it to include all objects in the area, or choose multiple subjects and lift 5 objects in tough/sensory range etc.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-06-2023, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:15:11-08:00","id":1504570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504569#post1504569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Touch, Sensory or Sympathetic, like every other spell. (Or area and move everything in it)</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's what I originally assumed, but the fourth line of the spell description implies that the telekine force can switch what objects it's affecting. I'm pretty sure orathiac and 21C are right about it creating a &quot;hand&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:20:57-08:00","id":1504571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504570#post1504570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, that's what I originally assumed, but the fourth line of the spell description implies that the telekine force can switch what objects it's affecting. I'm pretty sure orathiac and 21C are right about it creating a &quot;hand&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above, i edited my post. The spell says it conjures telekinetic force to manipulate an object remotely. This is then the subject of the spell (ie AN OBJECT). The later text describes what you can then do with the objects/s (since applying extra targets will get you more objects hence plural) of the spell. If you want to telekinesis more objects then you use extra targets or area so that &quot;an object&quot; becomes &quot;many or some objects&quot;. If one were being really pedantic then you could say that telekinesis cant be used on people since they aren't objects.<br /> It should probably have said, &quot;conjures tk force to manipulate a target/subject remotely...&quot;<br /> <br /> Plus what you are talking about is a spells scale, not range. If the spell did give the subject control over a tk hand then the range is still touch, sensory, etc to whoever it'd give the tk hand. This then obviously raises the question, how far could that hand go..luckily we don't have to answer that since it's now how tk works.<br /> <br /> TK's scale is how many objects you can manipulate, its range is how far away you can manipulate those objects. Touch range might seem bad but then you might have more potency than natural strength...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-06-2023, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:29:28-08:00","id":1504573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504571#post1504571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See above, i edited my post. The spell says it conjures telekinetic force to manipulate an object remotely. This is then the subject of the spell. The later text describes what you can then do with the subject/s of the spell. If you want to telekinesis more objects then you use extra targets or area so that &quot;an object&quot; becomes &quot;many or some objects&quot;..</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is why I originally assumed it has to target specific objects. But the spell description also says (emphasis mine) &quot;if the mage fails to concentrate on moving the force, it simply hangs suspended, <b>holding any objects it held before</b> but no longer pushing or pulling&quot; which implies the force exists even if it isnt holding a specific object.<br /> <br /> Alternative take, then. If you have to cast it on an area, can you cast on yourself? That is, make yourself the epicenter so the field moves with you, allowing you to affect objects within [Scale Area] around you?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:45:33-08:00","id":1504575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504573#post1504573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, which is why I originally assumed it has to target specific objects. But the spell description also says (emphasis mine) &quot;if the mage fails to concentrate on moving the force, it simply hangs suspended, <b>holding any objects it held before</b> but no longer pushing or pulling&quot; which implies the force exists even if it isnt holding a specific object.<br /> <br /> Alternative take, then. If you have to cast it on an area, can you cast on yourself? That is, make yourself the epicenter so the field moves with you, allowing you to affect objects within [Scale Area] around you?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The TK force is still manipulating the object/subject, it just doesn't do anything to it/move it without concentration.<br /> <br /> Area spells don't move after being cast. If you cast an area spell with you as the epicenter and then move, the area of the spell doesn't move with you. (It gets abit iffy with area spells inside moving vehicles...)<br /> <br /> Scale is either an area or subjects, you cant cast an area scale spell on yourself(a subject) but you can cast an area spell with yourself inside the area and then make yourself subject to the spell along with everything else in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-06-2023, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:49:02-08:00","id":1504576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504565#post1504565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the force appears according to casting - touch/sensory - but can be manipulated a theoretically infinite distance away from the mage. But you'll be limited in what you can do with it if you can't see what you're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, touch range Telekenisis... Doesn't seem very tele...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T04:55:36-08:00","id":1504577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504571#post1504571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TK's scale is how many objects you can manipulate, its range is how far away you can manipulate those objects. Touch range might seem bad but then you might have more potency than natural strength...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would dispute that last part. IF the object is the subject of the spell, for touch range you only have to be touching it while you cast the spell.<br /> <br /> Imagine a Knowing spell cast at touch range on a spacecraft, you could keep knowing about the spacecraft no matter how far it travels so long as you still have duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the spell description also says (emphasis mine) &quot;if the mage fails to concentrate on moving the force, it simply hangs suspended, <b>holding any objects it held before</b> but no longer pushing or pulling&quot; which implies the force exists even if it isnt holding a specific object.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Actually this is the most important part. If you Telekenisis a large rock into the air, and the relinquish the spell, it will just stay there until duration (or more likely dissonance) ends the spell.<br /> <br /> So you can go and built a floating city...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T05:18:21-08:00","id":1504579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504577#post1504577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually this is the most important part. If you Telekenisis a large rock into the air, and the relinquish the spell, it will just stay there until duration (or more likely dissonance) ends the spell.<br /> <br /> So you can go and built a floating city...</div> </div> </div> </div>The interesting part is that a huge bolder which would normally require a strength of say 20 to be lifted by humans can still be moved at speed 1 with a TK spell that has a strength of 1. It is unclear if that could be vertical movement. (Personally, I would only allow that if the tk spell had enough strength potency to &quot;lift&quot; the object)<br /> <br /> If you can get the strength to lift said city then sure why not. <br /> <br /> Needing to touch the object only when the cast is standard. You only need be touching something when casting an hour-long shapeshift spell on another while casting and not stay touching for the entire hour sure. But this again opens up the question of how far away can you then manipulate the objects using tk, Maybe as far away as you like barring obstacles, not being able to see, etc, but then that's prone to easy abuse..<br /> <br /> The shapeshifted person can go wherever they like after having the spell cast on them though so letting objects that can now move etc do so too isn't a stretch.<br /> <br /> The idea of remote-controlling TK'd grenades or woese around corners or miles away with enough speed &amp; duration is abit scary...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-06-2023, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T06:31:08-08:00","id":1504585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504579#post1504579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The interesting part is that a huge bolder which would normally require a strength of say 20 to be lifted by humans can still be moved at speed 1 with a TK spell that has a strength of 1. It is unclear if that could be vertical movement. (Personally, I would only allow that if the tk spell had enough strength potency to &quot;lift&quot; the object)<br /> <br /> If you can get the strength to lift said city then sure why not.<br /> <br /> &lt;Snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>What Str is required to lift an object? Normally you roll Str+Stam to do a lifting task, but are there rules outside of MtAw core related to what you can lift? Should each increase in weight subtract 1 dice from the roll?<br /> <br /> The closest i can see it welding weapons requiring a minimum str. But a Str 1 character can weild a chainsaw with only a -1 penalty<br /> <br /> To circumvent this, you could use advanced scale to target multiple objects each at the limit of your potency based weight limits... Unless the TK has to roll it's str to lift things, which would reqire lots of dice.<br /> <br /> Alternatively an advanced potency which gave +5 str per potency would make some sense (+1 reach effect, not an advanced potency reach)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T11:53:23-08:00","id":1504618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504576#post1504576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, touch range Telekenisis... Doesn't seem very tele...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I meant the force is conjured within touch range of the mage and then can be moved away at the force's speed.<br /> <br /> Essentially I take it to be a bit like D&amp;D's Mage Hand if you are familiar with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T02:37:20-08:00","id":1504739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504585#post1504585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Str is required to lift an object? Normally you roll Str+Stam to do a lifting task, but are there rules outside of MtAw core related to what you can lift? Should each increase in weight subtract 1 dice from the roll?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Scale already covers the Size of affected targets; at least for magic, it wouldn\u2019t make sense to worry about \u2018the spells strength check\u2019. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T02:43:40-08:00","id":1504741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504739#post1504739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scale already covers the Size of affected targets; at least for magic, it wouldn\u2019t make sense to worry about \u2018the spells strength check\u2019.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, yes, but Telekinesis specifically dictates that it has [Potency] dots in one of Strength, Dexterity, or Speed -or divided between all three with Reach- and a dot in the other two. Which implies it can only lift things up to a certain weight.<br /> <br /> I'd just handwave any basic rolls up to however many dots were allocated, and have the power fail on anything heavier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-07-2023, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T19:27:48-08:00","id":1504994,"title":"","content":"A Goetia can, with a little difficulty, be brought into Shadow or the Underworld. Can you bring a Ghost or Spirit into the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T20:03:31-08:00","id":1504997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1504994#post1504994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Goetia can, with a little difficulty, be brought into Shadow or the Underworld. Can you bring a Ghost or Spirit into the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e book, Astral Realms, mentions that ghosts and spirits sometimes slip through cracks in reality into the Temenos. Apparently, no one's figured out if they're physically there, or projecting their consciousness just like mages. (Though with the Begotten introduced in 2e, I suspect the former.) Ghosts in particular are relatively numerous in the various afterlife-shaped Temenotic realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T13:51:57-08:00","id":1505040,"title":"","content":"So, one can increase one's physical stats with Life Perfecting, that's pretty clear. What's not so clear is being able to do the same with other Arcana. I think it is pretty that Forces can increase a subject's Strength, but I don't think that extends to Dexterity since that's more about flexibility and precise movements. So, can Space increase Dexterity? <br /> <br /> Could a spell Forces Shielding prevent a subject from moving? The idea would be that it impedes the force generated by a body that is required in order to move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T15:08:47-08:00","id":1505058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505040#post1505040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one can increase one's physical stats with Life Perfecting, that's pretty clear. What's not so clear is being able to do the same with other Arcana. I think it is pretty that Forces can increase a subject's Strength, but I don't think that extends to Dexterity since that's more about flexibility and precise movements. So, can Space increase Dexterity?<br /> <br /> Could a spell Forces Shielding prevent a subject from moving? The idea would be that it impedes the force generated by a body that is required in order to move.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect non-Life Arcana boost Physical <i>actions</i>, not Attributes.<br /> <br /> The latter case feels like Fraying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T15:37:10-08:00","id":1505061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505058#post1505058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect non-Life Arcana boost Physical <i>actions</i>, not Attributes.<br /> <br /> The latter case feels like Fraying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Forces to increase the force you impart with your body would be represented as bonus dice on Strength based rolls.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505040#post1505040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a spell Forces Shielding prevent a subject from moving? The idea would be that it impedes the force generated by a body that is required in order to move.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Shielding is conceptually based on protecting the subject. As such, you can't really do anything with Shielding that primarily hinders the subject. That said, most ideas for effects to &quot;Shield&quot; a subject from something beneficial could probably be replicated with Fraying or Unravelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T05:24:40-08:00","id":1505107,"title":"","content":"If you turn the interior of a snowglobe / Lego castle / Tchotchke building sculpture into a <u>Secret Room</u> large enough to be the real thing, is the inside buffered against movement at all? Like, if you were camping out in said room, and someone picked it up, would you be jostled? I assume flipping it upside down would still have the normal effect, unless you applied <u>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlter Direction</u>, but the effect of spacial compression/expansion on contact vibration is kinda outside my normal wheelhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T07:39:08-08:00","id":1505115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505107#post1505107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you turn the interior of a snowglobe / Lego castle / Tchotchke building sculpture into a <u>Secret Room</u> large enough to be the real thing, is the inside buffered against movement at all? Like, if you were camping out in said room, and someone picked it up, would you be jostled? I assume flipping it upside down would still have the normal effect, unless you applied <u>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlter Direction</u>, but the effect of spacial compression/expansion on contact vibration is kinda outside my normal wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would rule it based on intent. Its generally useful enough as a mobile base, but someone actually trying to mess with the contents could. That way you can have things like a top secret Mysterium research Sanctum hidden inside the tooth filling of its guardian (werewolf, combat trained mage, etc), but still allow anyone who seizes it to try to lure the people inside out of their fortifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T16:59:03-07:00","id":1505209,"title":"","content":"What happens if someone returns from <i>Temporal Stutter</i> when someone of the same size is there, do they both become <i>Knocked Down, </i>does it only affect the person who was not stuttered ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T19:29:02-07:00","id":1505222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505209#post1505209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if someone returns from <i>Temporal Stutter</i> when someone of the same size is there, do they both become <i>Knocked Down, </i>does it only affect the person who was not stuttered ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use the method of determination that works for your game, whether that's comparing Gnosis and Arcanum ratings, comparing Physical Traits, contested Wits + Composure/Dexterity + Wits/Dexterity + Composure rolls, mutual knockdown, or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T20:35:18-07:00","id":1505279,"title":"","content":"Okay soo I'm a bit confused. <br /> <br /> If I cast a spell with touch and throw it via aimed spell at a foe, I roll gnosis plus skill vs defense, assuming I don't have the speed shot merit. <br /> <br /> If I have Space 4 or the reach and increase scale to an area effect but leave it at touch, so still an aimed spell, how does the resulting attack work?<br /> <br /> If there are 3 people in the area, 2 foes and an ally, do I roll to hit each one inside the area, or so I just roll to hit the area and then affect everyone inside? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can they make a check to jump out of the way?<br /> <br /> Been trying to find an answer or help online and am coming up short on my googlefu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T21:15:14-07:00","id":1505281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505279#post1505279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay soo I'm a bit confused.<br /> <br /> If I cast a spell with touch and throw it via aimed spell at a foe, I roll gnosis plus skill vs defense, assuming I don't have the speed shot merit.<br /> <br /> If I have Space 4 or the reach and increase scale to an area effect but leave it at touch, so still an aimed spell, how does the resulting attack work?<br /> <br /> If there are 3 people in the area, 2 foes and an ally, do I roll to hit each one inside the area, or so I just roll to hit the area and then affect everyone inside?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can they make a check to jump out of the way?<br /> <br /> Been trying to find an answer or help online and am coming up short on my googlefu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Advanced Scale (or just buying up Scale) but leaving the spell at Touch range means one of two things. Either you're:<br /> a) Casting on a large object, since the maximum size you can affect is based on Scale<br /> <br /> Or <br /> <br /> b) have physical contact with all the targets.<br /> <br /> For the mass-area cast question, as far as I can see, you would roll to check if you hit the intended target. If it hits, everything within that area is affected - aiming a spell that has no jumps in Scale would affect what it hit, plus targets in the armspan-area around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T21:18:58-07:00","id":1505282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505279#post1505279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay soo I'm a bit confused.<br /> <br /> If I cast a spell with touch and throw it via aimed spell at a foe, I roll gnosis plus skill vs defense, assuming I don't have the speed shot merit.<br /> <br /> If I have Space 4 or the reach and increase scale to an area effect but leave it at touch, so still an aimed spell, how does the resulting attack work?<br /> <br /> If there are 3 people in the area, 2 foes and an ally, do I roll to hit each one inside the area, or so I just roll to hit the area and then affect everyone inside?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can they make a check to jump out of the way?<br /> <br /> Been trying to find an answer or help online and am coming up short on my googlefu.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, spells are always cast at either touch/self or as aimed spells.<br /> <br /> If cast at touch/self, the spell can be either utilize normal scale (individual targets) or AoE (everything inside the area). When attempting to touch an unwilling target, roll Dex + Brawl or Dex + Weaponry minus the opponent's Defense (more information on page 219).<br /> <br /> When fired as an aimed spell (see page 115), its always cast as an AoE. Roll Gnosis + [highest of Athletics or Firearms] minus the target's Defense. Cover still applies, and there are shooting ranges as well. Lastly, aimed spells are never subtle, they are a bolt of magical energy flying at someone, which is what allows opponents to try to avoid them.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T21:31:43-07:00","id":1505283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505279#post1505279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay soo I'm a bit confused.<br /> <br /> If I cast a spell with touch and throw it via aimed spell at a foe, I roll gnosis plus skill vs defense, assuming I don't have the speed shot merit.<br /> <br /> If I have Space 4 or the reach and increase scale to an area effect but leave it at touch, so still an aimed spell, how does the resulting attack work?<br /> <br /> If there are 3 people in the area, 2 foes and an ally, do I roll to hit each one inside the area, or so I just roll to hit the area and then affect everyone inside?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand your question correctly, the issue is as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Aimed spells necessarily use the Area Scale.<br /> 2. The roll to hit a target with an Aimed spell is necessarily a resisted roll by default.<br /> 3. Unless all the targets in the spell's Area are Dodging, the usual &quot;resolve this roll against multiple targets&quot; method of contested rolls does not apply.<br /> 4. How is this resolved?<br /> <br /> And my understanding is that you would make the Aiming roll against whichever primary target you were aiming for, or make it unresisted if you just aimed for a stationary point.<br /> <br /> The heightened potential for unintended consequences is part of the reason Aimed spells use Area Scale to begin with, and methods exist for prospective targets to preempt the spell, get out of the way, or stave off its effects.<br /> <br /> In the meantime you have to contend with the fact that you just tossed an AoE the size of a large building likely no more than 400 yards away, where it's affecting not only your intended targets, but any other valid subjects who are in the area while the spell's Duration is active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T23:26:10-07:00","id":1505287,"title":"","content":"So, a Force Field is (usually) a science fiction concept that impedes or halts motion. Usually it acts like a projected surface, where stuff either reflects or is a bit smushed after being stopped. Would you model this with Forces Fraying or Unraveling, as per the the previous problem where I inquired on how to impede motion?<br /> <br /> Would a Forces spell to prevent combustion be a Fraying spell? Could one use that to prevent a gun from firing? Actually, catching on fire is usually considered harmful, could that potentially be a Shielding spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T00:28:19-07:00","id":1505289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505287#post1505287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a Force Field is (usually) a science fiction concept that impedes or halts motion. Usually it acts like a projected surface, where stuff either reflects or is a bit smushed after being stopped. Would you model this with Forces Fraying or Unraveling, as per the the previous problem where I inquired on how to impede motion?<br /> <br /> Would a Forces spell to prevent combustion be a Fraying spell? Could one use that to prevent a gun from firing? Actually, catching on fire is usually considered harmful, could that potentially be a Shielding spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forcefields: Depends on how you word how it functions, I guess? Plain Shielding ought to work for the iconic \u201cerect wall here; bonk anything coming through\u201d types. Something closer to a \u2018stasis field\u2019, where a \u201cno movey movey here\u201d effect is assigned to an area, is likely Fraying or Unraveling.<br /> <br /> Middle finger to gunpowder: I feel that stopping combustion could be Ruling. Robbing something of its flammability / combustibility would be Fraying or Weaving (not sure). Shielding ought to protect someone or something from gunfire or explosions, instead of stopping them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T00:38:53-07:00","id":1505290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505287#post1505287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a Force Field is (usually) a science fiction concept that impedes or halts motion. Usually it acts like a projected surface, where stuff either reflects or is a bit smushed after being stopped. Would you model this with Forces Fraying or Unraveling, as per the the previous problem where I inquired on how to impede motion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, most situations I would model it off the Forces Mage Armor, which I suppose drops the general level down around Fraying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T01:12:09-07:00","id":1505293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505279#post1505279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I have Space 4 or the reach and increase scale to an area effect but leave it at touch, so still an aimed spell, how does the resulting attack work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things.<br /> <br /> One, you don't actually need to Reach to use area for your scale factor; basic scale can either be based on number of targets or on area, it's just that the area is small. Reaching means that your basic area scale becomes as big as a house, and can move up to the size of multiple city blocks.<br /> <br /> The other is that you are, in fact, <i>obligated</i> to use area as your scale for an Aimed Spell. It becomes centred on whatever your target for throwing is.<br /> <br /> You only need to aim the spell at one person, and the rest will be affected by it if they're within the area (assuming its Potency overcomes their Withstand).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T01:43:15-07:00","id":1505294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505293#post1505293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two things.<br /> <br /> One, you don't actually need to Reach to use area for your scale factor; basic scale can either be based on number of targets or on area, it's just that the area is small. Reaching means that your basic area scale becomes as big as a house, and can move up to the size of multiple city blocks.<br /> <br /> The other is that you are, in fact, <i>obligated</i> to use area as your scale for an Aimed Spell. It becomes centred on whatever your target for throwing is.<br /> <br /> You only need to aim the spell at one person, and the rest will be affected by it if they're within the area (assuming its Potency overcomes their Withstand).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if you are using advanced scale you can touch the edge of the area instead of worrying about throwing it. Maybe project a cone of spell effect in front of you, or touch a building and affect everything inside.<br /> <br /> The shape is left very vague, mostly because it can be pretty much anything... Though i would tend to limit it to the symbolic/simple like: 'this building' or 'the left half of this room'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T12:18:25-07:00","id":1505354,"title":"","content":"Thank you, <br /> <br /> I have another I'm having some back and forth over ---&gt; <br /> <br /> Legacy Attainments -- the part about successes. <br /> <br /> I have a player that is wondering if they have Fate 4, do their Attainments count as exceptional successes, or Fate 5 for that matter based on the section talking about the number of successes the Attainment is assumed to have. <br /> <br /> I feel like since there is no spell casting roll, there can't be an exceptional success. That would let players very easily break the game if they wanted to just spam their Attainment for Exceptional Success benefits, and also would allow them to remove withstand on some abilities that use Withstand as a major balancing mechanic. <br /> <br /> Additionally, can you think of any instances when the successes would come into play? A Clash of Wills would still use the Mage's Gnosis + Arcana right, and not the successes of the Attainment?<br /> <br /> Are there any instances then where this comes up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T13:48:14-07:00","id":1505373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505354#post1505354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you,<br /> <br /> I have another I'm having some back and forth over ---&gt;<br /> <br /> Legacy Attainments -- the part about successes.<br /> <br /> I have a player that is wondering if they have Fate 4, do their Attainments count as exceptional successes, or Fate 5 for that matter based on the section talking about the number of successes the Attainment is assumed to have.<br /> <br /> I feel like since there is no spell casting roll, there can't be an exceptional success. That would let players very easily break the game if they wanted to just spam their Attainment for Exceptional Success benefits, and also would allow them to remove withstand on some abilities that use Withstand as a major balancing mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your intuition is correct, it just activates without the benefits of however many successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505354#post1505354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, can you think of any instances when the successes would come into play? A Clash of Wills would still use the Mage's Gnosis + Arcana right, and not the successes of the Attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, Clash of Wills is Gnosis + Arcana, even for attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505354#post1505354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any instances then where this comes up?</div> </div> </div> </div> Attainments that boost Mage Sight under certain conditions, like the example legacy's first optional attainment.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T05:50:27-07:00","id":1505483,"title":"","content":"Could Forces Perfecting turn <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IzUoe-9bKa0\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this kind of mundane Equipment</b></a> into something that deals Aggravated Damage with +1 Reach and 1 Mana? Or at least give it a Lethal Damage Bonus equal to Potency? The spell itself is upgrading a pre-existing weapon that definitely deals Lethal Damage, which is an indirect method. That means you don't need Forces 4 for directly causing Aggravated Damage, in theory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T06:50:15-07:00","id":1505487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505483#post1505483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Forces Perfecting turn <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IzUoe-9bKa0\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this kind of mundane Equipment</b></a> into something that deals Aggravated Damage with +1 Reach and 1 Mana? Or at least give it a Lethal Damage Bonus equal to Potency? The spell itself is upgrading a pre-existing weapon that definitely deals Lethal Damage, which is an indirect method. That means you don't need Forces 4 for directly causing Aggravated Damage, in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about granting Aggravated damage, but enhancing its (Lethal) damage rating should be perfectly okay. Pun intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T11:14:36-07:00","id":1505491,"title":"","content":"How do spells with both a subject and an area work as far as scale goes?<br /> <br /> I ask based on Lodestone which says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">As long as the</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> spell remains active, those objects within the spell\u2019s Area are drawn</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">to the spell\u2019s subject</span>\u200b </div> </div> </div> but I know I've seen other spells with similar effects.<br /> <br /> The spellcasting rules specify<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Mages must decide</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> when casting whether they are targeting specific subjects or a</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">blanket area of effect.</span>\u200b </div> </div> </div>Which seems like if Lodestone targets a subject then there's no defined area and if it targets an area, everything in that area is also the subject, so what determines where things are drawn to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T13:44:33-07:00","id":1505498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505491#post1505491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do spells with both a subject and an area work as far as scale goes?<br /> <br /> I ask based on Lodestone which says<br /> but I know I've seen other spells with similar effects.<br /> <br /> The spellcasting rules specify<br /> <br /> Which seems like if Lodestone targets a subject then there's no defined area and if it targets an area, everything in that area is also the subject, so what determines where things are drawn to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always interpreted it that you should use the AoE range to determine the area that is affected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T16:05:34-07:00","id":1505510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always interpreted it that you should use the AoE range to determine the area that is affected </div> </div> </div>Makes sense and that's what I assumed as well. But the problem I have with that interpretation is that it doesn't tell me where the Area is. Is it a sphere around the subject, or set and immovable like a normal AoE spell?<br /> <br /> Moveable sphere centered on the subject which extends to the size of the AoE range makes the most sense to me, it's just not how scale is written to work for areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","user":"TakWrote","date":". 03-16-2023, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T16:34:45-07:00","id":1505513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505510#post1505510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense and that's what I assumed as well. But the problem I have with that interpretation is that it doesn't tell me where the Area is. Is it a sphere around the subject, or set and immovable like a normal AoE spell?<br /> <br /> Moveable sphere centered on the subject which extends to the size of the AoE range makes the most sense to me, it's just not how scale is written to work for areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its the area around the subject. Think of it like a <i>Locate Object</i> spell from DND, so long as the target is within the area of effect near the subject or casting point, it will be affected. So if a Moros suddenly meets someone who gives him major bad vibes for no justifiable reason (maybe they never met a Promethean), they could cast <i>Lodestone </i>on them to make a light summer rain drench them. In another occasion, they can cast an AoE version in front of their Sanctum, so they won't have to shovel snow later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T17:27:55-07:00","id":1505518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505510#post1505510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense and that's what I assumed as well. But the problem I have with that interpretation is that it doesn't tell me where the Area is. Is it a sphere around the subject, or set and immovable like a normal AoE spell?<br /> <br /> Moveable sphere centered on the subject which extends to the size of the AoE range makes the most sense to me, it's just not how scale is written to work for areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually for AoEs you can define the area upon casting. So it depends on the Imago.<br /> <br /> You can define something as 'inside this building' or 'a cone whose tip begins at my finger tip' anything which is simple enough to form the imago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T15:57:37-07:00","id":1505606,"title":"","content":"This is really a cross over question, but:<br /> If i was looking for closest allied between Seer ministries/Exarchs and Vampire convenants, i would choose:<br /> Invictus - Mammon,<br /> Lancea - the Father,<br /> Circle - Raptor.<br /> <br /> Would there be any likely allies between the Ordo Dracul or the Cartian movement and Exarchs or their servants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T17:43:03-07:00","id":1505618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505606#post1505606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really a cross over question, but:<br /> If i was looking for closest allied between Seer ministries/Exarchs and Vampire convenants, i would choose:<br /> Invictus - Mammon,<br /> Lancea - the Father,<br /> Circle - Raptor.<br /> <br /> Would there be any likely allies between the Ordo Dracul or the Cartian movement and Exarchs or their servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Invictus would probably prefer Unity to Mammon, but it would likely depend on which was the most valuable ally for them in the region.<br /> <br /> For the Ordo Dracul, I don't think there's any ministry they would find a natural common ally; they would likely ally with whomever could help progress their research.<br /> <br /> The Carthians would likely hate most ministries, but I could see a politically repressed and violent Carthian group working with the Praetorian Ministry as an alliance of pure convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T19:33:27-07:00","id":1505626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505606#post1505606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there be any likely allies between the Ordo Dracul or the Cartian movement and Exarchs or their servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ordo's institutional mythology is that they are specifically doing what they do to spite God, which itself draws from the covenant's rules against subservience to ephemeral beings. Any of the Defiant allying with the Architects of the Lie are therefore likely to be considered whatever the best analog to &quot;heretics&quot; is in that model unless they're extremely good at bullshitting or otherwise working from a position of less-than-perfect description of where they're getting their lucky breaks from.<br /> <br /> If a given Exarch's power is aligned with a modern mode of government, you can probably find some Carthians who'd throw in their lot with it for at least as long as it seems viable among the dead, though once that group is in power they're as likely to get kicked out by other Carthians who disagree, particularly given we're talking about system aligned with the Tyrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T23:34:46-07:00","id":1505640,"title":"","content":"Three questions, only one of which is directly mechanics related.<br /> <br /> 1. Would <u>Kinetic Efficiency</u> make it harder to build muscles? Muscle growth is largely facilitated by straining them, and KE reduces that strain.<br /> <br /> 2. Neolithic Awakened saw the Watchtowers in a very different way than modern Awakened. Presumably cultural differences have an influence, which compounds over time, but what would other eras look like? Would, say, Viking era Mastigos see something closer to the endless forests rather than the Iron Gauntlet, or the hungry sea rather than the Lead Coin?<sup> Also, any theories on why the Neolithic towers were so small? Does each name add to the Watchtower's strength?</sup><br /> <br /> 3. Mechanic-ish question, for a theoretical Pocket Dimension base. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Scrying</u> can be used to make picture windows. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Co-Location</u> (with the Portal and Visibility Reach) can be used to make doorways and windows, but more importantly air holes. However, doing so has the same effect as leaving your doors and windows open - physical detritus can enter easily, as can trespassers. What would be a way to work around this? Key the portal to only allow air through, and cloak it with <u>Incognito Presence / Invisibility</u>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T00:23:11-07:00","id":1505646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505640#post1505640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Would <u>Kinetic Efficiency</u> make it harder to build muscles? Muscle growth is largely facilitated by straining them, and KE reduces that strain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell and muscle strain are largely orthogonal.<br /> <br /> If a person only did the physical actions they could do without the spell then they would experience less strain and less muscle growth.<br /> <br /> If they pushed themselves they would still experience fatigue and growth but their actual feats might be superhuman.<br /> <br /> KE doesn't help conditioning and might hinder it if used too often. An inverse of KE could be used as a kind of resistance training like weighted clothing which the mage could remove to unleash their Full Potential! at a dramatic moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:26:57-07:00","id":1505649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505640#post1505640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three questions, only one of which is directly mechanics related.<br /> <br /> 1. Would <u>Kinetic Efficiency</u> make it harder to build muscles? Muscle growth is largely facilitated by straining them, and KE reduces that strain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell says that it doesn't alter forces and instead maximizes kinetic energy use, so it's probably not as bad as it looks.<br /> <br /> I'd be more worried about how your Long-Term Nimbus develops; maybe you'll start running into more and more situations that demand more and more use of bodily force......<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Neolithic Awakened saw the Watchtowers in a very different way than modern Awakened. Presumably cultural differences have an influence, which compounds over time, but what would other eras look like? Would, say, Viking era Mastigos see something closer to the endless forests rather than the Iron Gauntlet, or the hungry sea rather than the Lead Coin?<sup> Also, any theories on why the Neolithic towers were so small? Does each name add to the Watchtower's strength?</sup> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather stick to the tower-builds-up imagery, for symbolic reasons. The Astral citadels of the Aeons have our Weird Places You Might Recognize quirk covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Mechanic-ish question, for a theoretical Pocket Dimension base. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Scrying</u> can be used to make picture windows. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Co-Location</u> (with the Portal and Visibility Reach) can be used to make doorways and windows, but more importantly air holes. However, doing so has the same effect as leaving your doors and windows open - physical detritus can enter easily, as can trespassers. What would be a way to work around this? Key the portal to only allow air through, and cloak it with <u>Incognito Presence / Invisibility</u>? </div> </div> </div>Space 3 Ban with Matter 2 for letting in only air works. Ban can't be Keyed, but if the portal's used only for ventilation, then that's actually a plus.<br /> <br /> Space 2 Secret Door should be able to hide them.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...... Or we can cast Space 4 Teleportation at empty air and at Indefinite Duration so that it repetitively brings fresh air from outside at each ritual-casting interval. Because screw Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:37:08-07:00","id":1505650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505649#post1505649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...... Or we can cast Space 4 Teleportation at empty air and at Indefinite Duration so that it repetitively brings fresh air from outside at each ritual-casting interval. Because screw Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that work, though? I guess you could AoE cast it, but that would bring everything in the area with it... but I'm iffy on whether you can target the air like that. The &quot;switch places&quot; Reach would certainly support the concept, at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:41:54-07:00","id":1505651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505650#post1505650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that work, though? I guess you could AoE cast it, but that would bring everything in the area with it... but I'm iffy on whether you can target the air like that. The &quot;switch places&quot; Reach would certainly support the concept, at any rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it\u2019s a gray area subject to ST interpretation, but I\u2019d allow it just for the absurdity and in-universe face-palming it\u2019d invite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And because I believe Space spells at least should be able to target \u2018empty space\u2019 (and the air in it), but that\u2019s getting into technicalities)<br /> <br /> EDIT: (hope editting works)<br /> <br /> On second thought, maybe the teleportative ventilator really does bring in outside junk, and the architect set up a trash pit below the \u2018air space\u2019. Maybe another co-located portal to god-knows-where, or a disintegrator field (Annihilate Matter).<br /> <br /> And now I realize I\u2019m treading into the cackling mad scientist territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-18-2023, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:51:56-07:00","id":1505652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505651#post1505651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it\u2019s a gray area subject to ST interpretation, but I\u2019d allow it just for the absurdity and in-universe face-palming it\u2019d invite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And because I believe Space spells at least should be able to target \u2018empty space\u2019 (and the air in it), but that\u2019s getting into technicalities)<br /> <br /> EDIT: (hope editting works)<br /> <br /> On second thought, maybe the teleportative ventilator really does bring in outside junk, and the architect set up a trash pit below the \u2018air space\u2019. Maybe another co-located portal to god-knows-where, or a disintegrator field (Annihilate Matter).<br /> <br /> And now I realize I\u2019m treading into the cackling mad scientist territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm not opposed to the idea of things entering. A Pocket Dimension Sanctum that has a Co-Location portal &quot;sky&quot; would be a good way to let light and air in, and rain if the realm is cultivated into a living landscape. Just slap the &quot;outside&quot; portal horizontal in the sky of some remote location, like the middle of the Amazon or Glacier National Park. It just adds a couple extra layers of work, namely whatever shelter the creator desires plus the occasional &quot;cleaning&quot; to sift out excess Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:59:38-07:00","id":1505653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505652#post1505652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I'm not opposed to the idea of things entering. A Pocket Dimension Sanctum that has a Co-Location portal &quot;sky&quot; would be a good way to let light and air in, and rain if the realm is cultivated into a living landscape. Just slap the &quot;outside&quot; portal horizontal in the sky of some remote location, like the middle of the Amazon or Glacier National Park. It just adds a couple extra layers of work, namely whatever shelter the creator desires plus the occasional &quot;cleaning&quot; to sift out excess Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, with all the Space and Matter magic being thrown around, all of this builds up nicely to the Tamers of Stone. You might also want to look around their 1e writeup \u2014 I don\u2019t remember if their book addresses magical architecture, but if any book does, that\u2019s probably it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T02:26:43-07:00","id":1505654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505640#post1505640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. Mechanic-ish question, for a theoretical Pocket Dimension base. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Scrying</u> can be used to make picture windows. Relinquished/Indefinite <u>Co-Location</u> (with the Portal and Visibility Reach) can be used to make doorways and windows, but more importantly air holes. However, doing so has the same effect as leaving your doors and windows open - physical detritus can enter easily, as can trespassers. What would be a way to work around this? Key the portal to only allow air through, and cloak it with <u>Incognito Presence / Invisibility</u>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use a portal on the moon with conjunctional force to only let sunlight through (is it conjunctional) then grow plants to produce real oxygen locally. (no ody goes to the moon, so no need to worry about veiling...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, i was misremembering the rules for additional Arcana from Ban. I would allow co-locate with additional Arcana to only allow through specific purviews of the Arcana to pass through. A 'sunlight portal' is one effect for the purpose of this spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 03-18-2023, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T02:30:34-07:00","id":1505655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505653#post1505653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, with all the Space and Matter magic being thrown around, all of this builds up nicely to the Tamers of Stone. You might also want to look around their 1e writeup \u2014 I don\u2019t remember if their book addresses magical architecture, but if any book does, that\u2019s probably it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sadly, from what I can skim it does not. I might give a builder Legacy a shot though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505654#post1505654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use a portal on the moon with conjunctional force to only let sunlight through (is it conjunctional) then grow plants to produce real oxygen locally. (no ody goes to the moon, so no need to worry about veiling...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Might get a bit prohibitive in terms of how much space 300-700 plants and their adjascent ecosystems would take up, though it's certainly a possibility.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, does <u>Scrying</u> produce actual light? 'Cause that would be the safer sunlamp option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-18-2023, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T02:58:03-07:00","id":1505656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505651#post1505651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it\u2019s a gray area subject to ST interpretation, but I\u2019d allow it just for the absurdity and in-universe face-palming it\u2019d invite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And because I believe Space spells at least should be able to target \u2018empty space\u2019 (and the air in it), but that\u2019s getting into technicalities)<br /> <br /> EDIT: (hope editting works)<br /> <br /> On second thought, maybe the teleportative ventilator really does bring in outside junk, and the architect set up a trash pit below the \u2018air space\u2019. Maybe another co-located portal to god-knows-where, or a disintegrator field (Annihilate Matter).<br /> <br /> And now I realize I\u2019m treading into the cackling mad scientist territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleportation does not have space as the subject, it specifically calls for testing the spatial co-ordinates of a non-spatial subject.<br /> <br /> If you target an individual with an indefinite teleportation, their position will reset every ritual duration to whereever you moved them.<br /> <br /> But with an AoE spell, it would automatically hit everything in the Area, so i suppose this does work ... I still think co-locate is the spell you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:04:01-07:00","id":1505657,"title":"","content":"Plants need water and carbon dioxide to make oxygen. Seems to me a Matter spell on the moon to make air is more elegant.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry misunderstood. Though using Matter for carbon dioxide filtration directly removes the need for air holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27690,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","user":"MorganG","date":". 03-18-2023, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:12:45-07:00","id":1505658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505657#post1505657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plants need water and carbon dioxide to make oxygen. Seems to me a Matter spell on the moon to make air is more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Targeting the moon has a whole another problem of...... targeting the moon. You'll need something like a moon rock to lift sympathetic connections off, and finding one of those is a challenge on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:13:53-07:00","id":1505659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505657#post1505657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plants need water and carbon dioxide to make oxygen. Seems to me a Matter spell on the moon to make air is more elegant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but then you need to be a Master of Matter and Space, at a minimum. <br /> <br /> ...how hard would it be for a dedicated Cabal to terraform another planet? You'd need, what, overlapping bubbles of Environmental Shield, where you introduce soil bacteria and progressively more complicated plant life? Keep spreading outwards... it would take a lot of Relinquishments, so there's definitely storyhooks there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:21:20-07:00","id":1505661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505659#post1505659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but then you need to be a Master of Matter and Space, at a minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put just air filtration at Matter Perfecting/Weaving, or Patterning at most. Get a Matter-using friend to make you a device or substance that can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:25:56-07:00","id":1505662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505661#post1505661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put just air filtration at Matter Perfecting/Weaving, or Patterning at most. Get a Matter-using friend to make you a device or substance that can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transmutation is an Adept spell, but creating air whole-cloth would be Create Matter. And since the moon doesn't have much of an atmosphere to transmute...<br /> <br /> Granted, you could transmute the rocks, but that would be grisly if the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T03:44:12-07:00","id":1505664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505662#post1505662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Transmutation is an Adept spell, but creating air whole-cloth would be Create Matter. And since the moon doesn't have much of an atmosphere to transmute...<br /> <br /> Granted, you could transmute the rocks, but that would be grisly if the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. My later point was just that you can create your pocket dimension, teleport in some air to begin with and then have a Matter-enhanced object that passively filters the air so you don't die of carbon dioxide poisoning.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T04:18:53-07:00","id":1505665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505655#post1505655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, from what I can skim it does not. I might give a builder Legacy a shot though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Might get a bit prohibitive in terms of how much space 300-700 plants and their adjascent ecosystems would take up, though it's certainly a possibility.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, does <u>Scrying</u> produce actual light? 'Cause that would be the safer sunlamp option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Scrying, i would presume it can produce light, but symbolically i would say no you can't grow plants by the light of a Scrying window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T13:37:39-07:00","id":1505702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505640#post1505640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Neolithic Awakened saw the Watchtowers in a very different way than modern Awakened. Presumably cultural differences have an influence, which compounds over time, but what would other eras look like? Would, say, Viking era Mastigos see something closer to the endless forests rather than the Iron Gauntlet, or the hungry sea rather than the Lead Coin?<sup> Also, any theories on why the Neolithic towers were so small? Does each name add to the Watchtower's strength?</sup></div> </div> </div> </div> I think the latter interpretation is part of the story. Remember, the Watchtowers are tools that allow the safe interaction with and changing of the Supernal. They do this by being pieces of the Supernal and preparing an environment where basic interaction won't dissolve unprepared souls. This prepared environment conforms to symbols that people can kinda readily understand. When someone signs their name, they permanently change the watchtower and build it up just a little. The put a little of themselves into the Supernatural. The environment's symbolism changes ( a little), one could say updating and growing to better be understood by people. That's just my interpretation though. It's also the best argument for the Free Council's view of As Below, so Above.<br /> <br /> As for the first part...I see it as different people experiencing different things with the same symbolic themes. Each person gets whatever symbol set that best fits their soul, so a modern person can get &quot;Angels&quot; that look like &quot;holy&quot; figures from whatever mythology you want. That way you can get stuff like Pandemonic alien abductions and cosmic horror, or an Asgard-themed Aether. I like to think that also affects the nature of the stuff they might summon later down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:07:00-07:00","id":1505716,"title":"","content":"The Runic Yantra requiring [ritual interval] to use has always been wierd to me. Quite aside from Runes already being very limited by their relative ease of disruption, it means you have to draw out new summoning circles and the like every time. A more stereotypical hermetic wizard's magic circle, inlaid into the floors and walls of a room, would be an Environmental Yantra, rather than Runic Yantra, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:30:02-07:00","id":1505723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505716#post1505716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Runic Yantra requiring [ritual interval] to use has always been weird to me. Quite aside from Runes already being very limited by their relative ease of disruption, it means you have to draw out new summoning circles and the like every time. A more stereotypical hermetic wizard's magic circle, inlaid into the floors and walls of a room, would be an Environmental Yantra, rather than Runic Yantra, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I think it would be either an environmental. Runes have an interesting application, they are a non-concentration yantra that allows you to end an unsafely relinquished spell, which gives a bit more sanity check (as well as a nice bonus). Regarding ease of disruption, it depends, you can use things like ultraviolet paint to make them non-obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:43:09-07:00","id":1505728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505723#post1505723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, I think it would be either an environmental. Runes have an interesting application, they are a non-concentration yantra that allows you to end an unsafely relinquished spell, which gives a bit more sanity check (as well as a nice bonus). Regarding ease of disruption, it depends, you can use things like ultraviolet paint to make them non-obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly find it strange with stuff like tattoo runes. It typically does not take three hours to tattoo a thumb-sized symbol on someone's shoulder, and not being able to re-use that rune is... incongruous? Needlessly limiting? Granted, three hours is a specific Gnosis level, but ten minutes to create a tattoo is also rather unusual. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, could you Imbue a tattoo? Or rather, the ink that forms the tattoo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T20:15:43-07:00","id":1505745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505728#post1505728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mostly find it strange with stuff like tattoo runes. It typically does not take three hours to tattoo a thumb-sized symbol on someone's shoulder, and not being able to re-use that rune is... incongruous? Needlessly limiting? Granted, three hours is a specific Gnosis level, but ten minutes to create a tattoo is also rather unusual.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, could you Imbue a tattoo? Or rather, the ink that forms the tattoo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 62 seems to suggest enchanting can be done with tattoos. Imbuing seems to be more permanent, but unlike Grimoires, not detrimental. However, if the imbuer has control of the imbuement, they can detonate them by spending a mana (Signs of Sorcery page 68), causing aggravated or Structure damage. A Seer could use that to create deadman switches, after all, Attainments can't be dispelled, and there is no limit on the range, no even across dimensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T20:17:25-07:00","id":1505746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505716#post1505716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Runic Yantra requiring [ritual interval] to use has always been wierd to me. Quite aside from Runes already being very limited by their relative ease of disruption, it means you have to draw out new summoning circles and the like every time. A more stereotypical hermetic wizard's magic circle, inlaid into the floors and walls of a room, would be an Environmental Yantra, rather than Runic Yantra, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to make new runes each time. You have to inscribe the runes on the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> So you can have runes for a healing spell tattooed into your cabal mates once. And then heal them with it as many times are you need to.<br /> <br /> Summoning circles are completely different, when used to summon supernal beings, and high speech runes as part of an environmental yantra don't take [ritual interval] to setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T20:28:41-07:00","id":1505747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505728#post1505728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mostly find it strange with stuff like tattoo runes. It typically does not take three hours to tattoo a thumb-sized symbol on someone's shoulder, and not being able to re-use that rune is... incongruous? Needlessly limiting? Granted, three hours is a specific Gnosis level, but ten minutes to create a tattoo is also rather unusual.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, could you Imbue a tattoo? Or rather, the ink that forms the tattoo?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hard time limits on making a runic yantra have definitely struck me as odd as well. My read is that, like with ritual casting, a low Gnosis mage is going very slowly making sure that every line and every detail is exactly correct. It might even include creating a sketch first, then making the actual rune. A higher Gnosis mage has a much greater intuitive understanding (and probably much more practice) of how to create the Supernal symbols involved and so needs much less time to draw/sketch/tattoo the rune they plan to use.<br /> <br /> It's like muscle memory for the soul - a higher Gnosis mage doesn't need to think about each individual component of the Imago as much as a lower Gnosis mage does, so they can do it much more quickly and smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T20:39:12-07:00","id":1505748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505746#post1505746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to make new runes each time. You have to inscribe the runes on the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> So you can have runes for a healing spell tattooed into your cabal mates once. And then heal them with it as many times are you need to.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was under the impression that you needed to re-scribe the runes each time, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490458#post1490458\">based on the response from the last time I asked a similar question</a>, but I may have been taking that interpretation too narrowly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Summoning circles are completely different, when used to summon supernal beings, and high speech runes as part of an environmental yantra don't take [ritual interval] to setup. </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but I meant summoning circles as in a circle that you use to facilitate <u>Goetic/Ghost/Spirit Summons,</u> a focal point for <u>Co-Location/Teleport</u>, or a circle into which your casting of <u>Ex Nihilo</u> deposits its creation. That last is... somewhat impractical, I suppose, but I can think of a few uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T20:52:06-07:00","id":1505749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505747#post1505747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard time limits on making a runic yantra have definitely struck me as odd as well. My read is that, like with ritual casting, a low Gnosis mage is going very slowly making sure that every line and every detail is exactly correct. It might even include creating a sketch first, then making the actual rune. A higher Gnosis mage has a much greater intuitive understanding (and probably much more practice) of how to create the Supernal symbols involved and so needs much less time to draw/sketch/tattoo the rune they plan to use.<br /> <br /> It's like muscle memory for the soul - a higher Gnosis mage doesn't need to think about each individual component of the Imago as much as a lower Gnosis mage does, so they can do it much more quickly and smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should also like to add that Runes Yantras are definitely not &quot;a thumb-sized symbol&quot;; their writeup explicitly compares them to the intersection between Concentration \u2014 a Yantra that only works on spells that last longer than a turn \u2014 and incanting in High Speech \u2014 a Yantra that does not allow you to cast the spell in a single turn.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Runes are done <i>in High Speech</i>, a &quot;language&quot; whose spellcasting applications are compared to blueprints and whose unformalized manifestations can be found in such diverse forms as animal calls, architecture, and glossolalia. It's fiddly to translate that into the narrative equivalent of Reach effects, spell factors, and other aspects of the spell besides &quot;I'm giving the roll to create this effect two extra dice.&quot;<br /> <br /> As you correctly observe, ritual interval is used to draw the runes <i>properly</i>; the writeup is plain that you have to do this carefully or else you've made an imperfect description of the spell's Imago in a language that can't be used to tell lies, which is what causes the spell using those runes to end prematurely. You're not going to get that from the High Speech equivalent of just putting the words &quot;healing spell&quot; on somebody's arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:11:07-07:00","id":1505751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505748#post1505748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was under the impression that you needed to re-scribe the runes each time, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490458#post1490458\">based on the response from the last time I asked a similar question</a>, but I may have been taking that interpretation too narrowly.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked the same question in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page513#post1472617\">previous &quot;Ask a Simple Question&quot;</a> thread and the answers were uniformly &quot;you can draw the runes whenever&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:18:40-07:00","id":1505753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505751#post1505751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the same question in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page513#post1472617\">previous &quot;Ask a Simple Question&quot;</a> thread and the answers were uniformly &quot;you can draw the runes whenever&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as the one who gave the answer in the linked post, I cannot fathom how one gets &quot;you have to draw the runes each time you cast the spell&quot; from &quot;you can't use the Invisible Runes spell to shortcut the need to spend at least your ritual interval scribing a Runes Yantra, because Invisible Runes writes short messages, Runes Yantras are not short messages, and if most Yantra bonuses above a +1 have some form of drawback it's probably not valid to let a Yantra whose drawback ends the spell if the runes are disrupted be made with a spell that lets you Clash any attempts to erase the message (which is also invisible to anyone without Mage Sight).&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:23:24-07:00","id":1505755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505751#post1505751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the same question in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page513#post1472617\">previous &quot;Ask a Simple Question&quot;</a> thread and the answers were uniformly &quot;you can draw the runes whenever&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I overcorrected then. Thanks! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T21:32:48-07:00","id":1505756,"title":"","content":"What kind of effects would you expect Perfecting to have on inks? No bleeding, running, or fading?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T23:38:22-07:00","id":1505762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505756#post1505756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of effects would you expect Perfecting to have on inks? No bleeding, running, or fading?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds apt. Some materials simply don't have fancy effects.<br /> <br /> Speaking of materials, I wonder if the ink's ingredient matters... likely not, since ink is just Ink symbolically speaking, but someone in-universe is probably Obsessing over that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T23:42:30-07:00","id":1505763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505762#post1505762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds apt. Some materials simply don't have fancy effects.<br /> <br /> Speaking of materials, I wonder if the ink's ingredient matters... likely not, since ink is just Ink symbolically speaking, but someone in-universe is probably Obsessing over that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be interesting with plant-based inks - they might be subject to the same rules as blood or skin. Cephalopod ink or mineral ink might have other effects, but like you said the symbology of ink is ink. Definitely an interesting Obsession possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T01:00:42-07:00","id":1505764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505748#post1505748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, but I meant summoning circles as in a circle that you use to facilitate <u>Goetic/Ghost/Spirit Summons,</u> a focal point for <u>Co-Location/Teleport</u>, or a circle into which your casting of <u>Ex Nihilo</u> deposits its creation. That last is... somewhat impractical, I suppose, but I can think of a few uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think co-locate can use runes like this, arguably with runes on both ends, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> This is because co-locate is the only one of those spells which has a space as the subject. Teleport rewrites the subject's spatial co-ordinates, so you would need to inscribe the runes on whoever or whatever you were teleporting (for each subject).<br /> <br /> Or use them as a +1 environmental bonus, (and not have all the downsides of Runes).<br /> <br /> Notable, i have seen discussion of leveraging the 'spell end of runes are broken' downside as an advantage - where you cast an unsafely relinquish the spell, followed by breaking the runes if something goes wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typo 03-19-2023, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T01:09:38-07:00","id":1505766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505764#post1505764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think co-locate can use runes like this, arguably with runes on both ends, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> This is because co-locate is the only one of those spells which has a space as the subject. <u>Teleport</u> rewrites the subject's spatial co-ordinates, so you would need to inscribe the runes on whoever or whatever you were teleporting (for each subject).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the<u> X Summons</u> spells would still work for a runic circle as a Rune yantra - you're calling the entities to the spot marked out by the runes, and thematically breaking the circle to disrupt control over the summoned entity is very on-theme. <u>Teleport</u> in my mind would be relocating one target to the targeted space marked out by the rune circle, but it would be perfectly reasonable to require the teleporting target to have a separate rune-mark to justify the +2 Yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or use them as a +1 environmental bonus, (and not have all the downsides of Runes). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Environmental yantras is the easiest option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notable, i have seen discussion of leveraging the 'spell end of runes are broken' downside as an advantage - where you cast an unsafely relinquish the spell, followed by breaking the runes if something goes wrong. </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly. It's like having the Conditional Duration Utility Attainment - how you use it depends entirely on your intent. The draw to more dice/Duration vs easier to end is entirely dependent on what the spell is meant to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T22:36:39-07:00","id":1505883,"title":"","content":"<s>An Imbued or Enhanced item shows up under <u>Supernal Vision </u>or AMS, likely covered in ephemeral sigils or something else appropriate. How about a Grimoire? The maintained version is obviously going to show up like an Enhancement, and ping PMS, but what about the Lasting application? Relevant passages of a physical book glowing with Supernal light, paintings overlaid with sacred geometry, stuff like that? Or is is unnoticable unless you already know it's there?</s><br /> Rephrased - Does a Lasting Grimoire show up under AMS, and does it ping PMS? I assume &quot;No&quot; for the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-20-2023, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T01:56:20-07:00","id":1505890,"title":"","content":"I would assume it doesn't show up under AMS, i think the closer comparison is high speech runes. But a grimoire usually has the scribe grimoire spell cast on it creating lasting effects. But lasting effects don't trigger mage sight.<br /> <br /> Matter might be the best chance to notice something odd, as a grimoire's availability/value might be higher than otherwise expected.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, you can use Focused Mage Sight to examine a grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T12:17:47-07:00","id":1505917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505883#post1505883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><s>An Imbued or Enhanced item shows up under <u>Supernal Vision </u>or AMS, likely covered in ephemeral sigils or something else appropriate. How about a Grimoire? The maintained version is obviously going to show up like an Enhancement, and ping PMS, but what about the Lasting application? Relevant passages of a physical book glowing with Supernal light, paintings overlaid with sacred geometry, stuff like that? Or is is unnoticable unless you already know it's there?</s><br /> Rephrased - Does a Lasting Grimoire show up under AMS, and does it ping PMS? I assume &quot;No&quot; for the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't ping PMS because it only pings when the supernatural effect activates. But it would ping AMS, because all phenomena under its purview become highlighted (page 90 of the core book), ones with more &quot;density&quot; are likely supernatural.<br /> <br /> So Prime sight would pick up on Grimoires because they are something with Supernal significance, the same way Fate sight would highlight a changeling or phrases with significance (like someone &quot;who looks like an angel&quot; having some importance in a metaphysical sense). Why it registers would require the mage to figure it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T12:20:30-07:00","id":1505919,"title":"","content":"Building off this question, would you say a Rote could be seen by Active Mage Sight Arcana outside of Prime, if it was the same Arcana as the Rote?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T13:34:15-07:00","id":1505927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505919#post1505919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building off this question, would you say a Rote could be seen by Active Mage Sight Arcana outside of Prime, if it was the same Arcana as the Rote?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of a stretch, but I'd allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T18:00:34-07:00","id":1505981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505919#post1505919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building off this question, would you say a Rote could be seen by Active Mage Sight Arcana outside of Prime, if it was the same Arcana as the Rote?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in the type of spell?<br /> <br /> All Awakened spells show up to all forms of Active Mage Sight as they're being cast, the same as/because of the universal visibility of a mage's Immediate Nimbus flaring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T18:04:17-07:00","id":1505985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1505981#post1505981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in the type of spell?<br /> <br /> All Awakened spells show up to all forms of Active Mage Sight as they're being cast, the same as/because of the universal visibility of a mage's Immediate Nimbus flaring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no. Sorry. It's a Rote that's encoded as part of a Lasting Grimoire. It's obvious to me Prime should be able to do it, but I think it might be interesting if others could do so with conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T03:11:48-07:00","id":1506025,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the below forum question.<br /> <br /> If you cast an AoE spell with an instantaneous effect (like healing or damage) as a long duration spell, does this then get the best of both worlds?<br /> <br /> You heal everyone who stands in the room every 3 hours? (Possibly leaving a long term healing spa in place with 'mystical powers' or a defensive system which deals 1 bashing as mental damage every 10 minutes... To <i>discourage</i> trespassers without immediately killing them ..)<br /> <br /> Are there any other uses for this AoE ritual duration effect?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-questions.795923/page-12#post-20735902\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...#post-20735902</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T03:31:03-07:00","id":1506026,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it works like that... but in any case, I have to image an effect like that would get Dissonanced <i>very</i> quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T03:59:35-07:00","id":1506027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506026#post1506026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it works like that... but in any case, I have to image an effect like that would get Dissonanced <i>very</i> quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am imagining some of this is a temple in a The Time Before with security measures which have survived any dissonance for centuries ..<br /> <br /> But also, getting a headache and bring able to blame it on &quot;oh that room is too noisey/bright&quot; might not be obviously magical.<br /> <br /> Or you are trying to dissuade ppl from exploring your natural verge, where spells are not subject to dissonance.<br /> <br /> But the principle question is how of instantaneous AoE spells work over long durations. You are assuming i am incorrect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T04:04:40-07:00","id":1506029,"title":"","content":"Less that you're incorrect, and more that I don't necessarily agree with the conclusion. AoE is a little tricky to me - in this case, is it affecting everything that &quot;<i>was in the area</i><i> when the spell was cast&quot;</i>, or &quot;<i>is in the area at each [Ritual Interval]&quot;</i>? I certainly agree that it keeps reactivating, I'm just not certain of what the targets would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T04:22:06-07:00","id":1506030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506025#post1506025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by the below forum question.<br /> <br /> If you cast an AoE spell with an instantaneous effect (like healing or damage) as a long duration spell, does this then get the best of both worlds?<br /> <br /> You heal everyone who stands in the room every 3 hours? (Possibly leaving a long term healing spa in place with 'mystical powers' or a defensive system which deals 1 bashing as mental damage every 10 minutes... To <i>discourage</i> trespassers without immediately killing them ..)<br /> <br /> Are there any other uses for this AoE ritual duration effect?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-questions.795923/page-12#post-20735902\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...#post-20735902</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that casting spells on an Area (as opposed to just many Subjects) does create a magical area. Like that teleportation room I imagined some days earlier. It\u2019s more simple, and more fun that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T05:47:03-07:00","id":1506036,"title":"","content":"Any spell with an instantaneous effect reapplies that effect every ritual interval of the mage who cast it.<br /> <br /> An AoE spell affects all valid targets within the area while they are in that area. Targets leaving the area stops being subjects to the spell, and new targets entering the area becomes subjects to the spell. (As Dave explains two posts below the one linked to on rpg.net)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T06:41:44-07:00","id":1506040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506030#post1506030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume that casting spells on an Area (as opposed to just many Subjects) does create a magical area. Like that teleportation room I imagined some days earlier. It\u2019s more simple, and more fun that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure a teleportation room which triggers every 10 minutes or every 3 hours is at all useful, contrasted with a portal/co-location. But i will think about whether it has any advantages...<br /> <br /> Yeeting potential enemies out of the Area is one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506036#post1506036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any spell with an instantaneous effect reapplies that effect every ritual interval of the mage who cast it.<br /> <br /> An AoE spell affects all valid targets within the area while they are in that area. Targets leaving the area stops being subjects to the spell, and new targets entering the area becomes subjects to the spell. (As Dave explains two posts below the one linked to on rpg.net)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI was directly inspired by Dave's answer to ask this precise question (which wasn't directly addressed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T06:50:46-07:00","id":1506042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506040#post1506040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure a teleportation room which triggers every 10 minutes or every 3 hours is at all useful, contrasted with a portal/co-location. But i will think about whether it has any advantages...<br /> <br /> Yeeting potential enemies out of the Area is one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mages with the right Obsessions and low Wisdom can get up to \u201cWhy NOT do it?\u201d territory fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> \u200bI was directly inspired by Dave's answer to ask this precise question (which wasn't directly addressed). </div> </div> </div>The man\u2019s answer, to my reading, seems to confirm that you do indeed create magical effect zones via Area-casting. Which has practically the same result as targeting an empty space to\u2026 create magical effect zones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T11:46:59-07:00","id":1506056,"title":"","content":"So I\u2019ve recently come across a style of magic in a game that manipulates \u201cthe connections that bind us all\u201d for a variety of effects. Said list of effects include summoning/creating? little bug things, manifesting threads to bind enemies in place, grappling hook, and a variety of damage effects. The narration on how it works reminded me of the Pandemonic view of Space, with effects scattered aroid the Arcana. Do you think that\u2019s essentially accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T13:39:14-07:00","id":1506061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506056#post1506056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019ve recently come across a style of magic in a game that manipulates \u201cthe connections that bind us all\u201d for a variety of effects. Said list of effects include summoning/creating? little bug things, manifesting threads to bind enemies in place, grappling hook, and a variety of damage effects. The narration on how it works reminded me of the Pandemonic view of Space, with effects scattered aroid the Arcana. Do you think that\u2019s essentially accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulating &quot;the connections that bind us all&quot; is definitely Mastigos, but in Mage these connections are not as literal as your thing seems to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T13:51:41-07:00","id":1506062,"title":"","content":"On that note, is it plausible to make a Space version of Turn Momentum? Turn Momentum cast on the self seems the best way to create a grappling hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T14:33:04-07:00","id":1506063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506062#post1506062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turn Momentum cast on the self seems the best way to create a grappling hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>While interesting, I'm gonna need you to walk me through that one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T14:42:31-07:00","id":1506064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506062#post1506062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, is it plausible to make a Space version of Turn Momentum? Turn Momentum cast on the self seems the best way to create a grappling hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alter Direction? I 'm not sure how it differs from Turn Momentum, or if you have read both. But what does Turn Momentum do that Alter Direction can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T14:49:45-07:00","id":1506066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506062#post1506062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, is it plausible to make a Space version of Turn Momentum? Turn Momentum cast on the self seems the best way to create a grappling hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Teleportation Imbued into a rope-hook-gun. The hook doesn\u2019t actually hook into anything; it merely assigns where the gun\u2019s user gets teleported to.<br /> <br /> Or Break Boundary, for the video game grappling hooks whose usage is arbitrarily restricted to crossing over chasms, rivers, lava, etc. that cut off otherwise well-defined roads (as opposed to allowing the player to zip over anywhere).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-21-2023, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T14:58:47-07:00","id":1506067,"title":"","content":"Ok, what is a grappling hook physics-wise? It's a rope that can attach to objects, and then either be climbed or swung around. I'm mostly looking at the second part, but the game uses both.<br /> <br /> So what happens when you swing around a point? Well, normal velocity becomes rotation velocity. So, you are changing the direction of your motion. Velocity is a speed plus a direction, and Momentum is Velocity times Mass. It's not as straightforward as just changing the angle of motion, instead taking place over time as it goes through the rotation, so this is probably a reach option.<br /> <br /> The other bit is weirder, but when you do something like this, you create a bit of acceleration toward the center of rotation. This is because acceleration is the changing either the speed or direction of a velocity. This is usually known as centripetal force. If one increased that with Forces Perfecting, you could technically &quot;pull&quot; oneself towards the center of rotation.<br /> <br /> Edit: clarification","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-21-2023, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T15:14:21-07:00","id":1506069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506064#post1506064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alter Direction? I 'm not sure how it differs from Turn Momentum, or if you have read both. But what does Turn Momentum do that Alter Direction can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically? (I think) When the spell ends, stuff returns to normal making a Z-shaped flight path instead of a V-shaped flight path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T01:39:10-07:00","id":1506127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506069#post1506069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically? (I think) When the spell ends, stuff returns to normal making a Z-shaped flight path instead of a V-shaped flight path.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can definitely make space curved, so that you get what appears to be circular motion and ends up with a C shaped path using Space (or apply a Force toward sthe center, but that might require potency to overcome the mass of the object).<br /> <br /> I don't know if it would our be ruling, weaving, or Perfecting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typo 03-22-2023, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:30:29-07:00","id":1506169,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the increased risk of infesting yourself with Mind Spiders, can you use <u>Psychic Domination</u> on yourself? Forcing yourself to go to the gym or other tasks that you normally shirk is my first thought, though obviously there's hubris in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T13:50:11-07:00","id":1506173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506169#post1506169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the increased risk of infesting yourself with Mind Spiders, can you use <u>Psychic Domination</u> on yourself? Forcing yourself to go to the gym or other tasks that you normally shirk is my first thought, though obviously there's hubris in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it might feel like experiencing locked in syndrome while your body is being run by something else. Hubris aside, that sounds traumatizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T14:21:10-07:00","id":1506177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506169#post1506169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the increased risk of infesting yourself with Mind Spiders, can you use <u>Psychic Domination</u> on yourself? Forcing yourself to go to the gym or other tasks that you normally shirk is my first thought, though obviously there's hubris in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>KaiserAfini nailed it, and usually the method is to make yourself actually enjoy those tasks or at least ambivalent to doing them. Or just increase your Force of Will and willpower your way through it. A lot can go wrong with all of these methods, but it\u2019s hopefully less traumatizing then Psychic Domination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T14:37:45-07:00","id":1506178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506169#post1506169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the increased risk of infesting yourself with Mind Spiders, can you use <u>Psychic Domination</u> on yourself? Forcing yourself to go to the gym or other tasks that you normally shirk is my first thought, though obviously there's hubris in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since there is already an intention to do the tasks I would have said a relatively non-sinister Mind Compelling effect could do it.<br /> <br /> Although I'm sure there are some Mastigos willing to experiment with Dominating themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T15:00:47-07:00","id":1506183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506178#post1506178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since there is already an intention to do the tasks I would have said a relatively non-sinister Mind Compelling effect could do it.<br /> <br /> Although I'm sure there are some Mastigos willing to experiment with Dominating themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure Mastigos are all about challenge, maybe they would try to trigger a clash of wills to prevent the Psychic Domination from working?<br /> <br /> Can you clash against yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T16:38:46-07:00","id":1506188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506183#post1506183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure Mastigos are all about challenge, maybe they would try to trigger a clash of wills to prevent the Psychic Domination from working?<br /> <br /> Can you clash against yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, an example is when you try to use a spell that acts in opposition another you relinquished, you are Clashing against the Gnosis + Arcanum you had at the time. Mastigos have Willpower to spend if they are good at Mind, so why not see if they can conquer their own Awakened will ?<br /> <br /> In addition, an irony of this all is that the instant version might not register. Someone is about to be sniped, <i>Psychic Domination</i> at sensory range to duck, that was close, you could swear you heard someone scream the instruction with palpable urgency. No one did, seriously ? So it was either good instincts or you have been working too hard, maybe go to sleep earlier, yeah, that's the ticket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T03:26:02-07:00","id":1506221,"title":"","content":"If you lose your soul (through placing it in a soul jar, let's say) and your wisdom drops to 1, you can now take your soul back and perform acts of Hubris for a few days with falling wisdom (so you can perform some premeditated murder, which doesn't require a roll at wisdom 1-3) and you end up with all your wisdom restored, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T05:18:32-07:00","id":1506225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506221#post1506221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you lose your soul (through placing it in a soul jar, let's say) and your wisdom drops to 1, you can now take your soul back and perform acts of Hubris for a few days with falling wisdom (so you can perform some premeditated murder, which doesn't require a roll at wisdom 1-3) and you end up with all your wisdom restored, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You regain Wisdom or Integrity lost <i>to the Soulless Condition</i>, i.e. Wisdom or Integrity lost from indulging your Vice, and Conditions <i>directly</i> resulting from that provisional Act of Hubris or breaking point go away once you get back the dot associated with the loss, but if you lose your soul and then drop your Integrity to 1 via mass murder without ever indulging your Vice you're not getting those dots back with any amount of napping.<br /> <br /> This particular bit seems like the sort of thing for which the technicality of the categories of Act of Hubris being divided less granularly than individual dot ratings runs into the narrative fact that if you seriously contemplate doing this you probably don't have higher than Falling Wisdom in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-23-2023, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T06:04:52-07:00","id":1506228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506225#post1506225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You regain Wisdom or Integrity lost <i>to the Soulless Condition</i>, i.e. Wisdom or Integrity lost from indulging your Vice, and Conditions <i>directly</i> resulting from that provisional Act of Hubris or breaking point go away once you get back the dot associated with the loss, but if you lose your soul and then drop your Integrity to 1 via mass murder without ever indulging your Vice you're not getting those dots back with any amount of napping.<br /> <br /> This particular bit seems like the sort of thing for which the technicality of the categories of Act of Hubris being divided less granularly than individual dot ratings runs into the narrative fact that if you seriously contemplate doing this you probably don't have higher than Falling Wisdom in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed that distinction, but yes.<br /> <br /> To your last point, if i use this in a game it will certainly be coming from some Rapt mage who experiments with it and lost their wisdom. Whether as an idea that is researched in some library's restricted section, or the Rapt mage going &quot;sure, of course it will be fine! Look at me!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T13:35:25-07:00","id":1506349,"title":"","content":"Ever watch a video game speed run? Especially a glitch using one? People do crazy, often immoral in the context of the game, just to shave off a few milliseconds from their time. Some the more common stuff is exploiting loopholes in reality to phase through walls, teleport, gain near infinite speed and generally break physics to their hearts content. Does that sound like good inspiration for an Abyssal Legacy to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T14:13:32-07:00","id":1506361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506349#post1506349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever watch a video game speed run? Especially a glitch using one? People do crazy, often immoral in the context of the game, just to shave off a few milliseconds from their time. Some the more common stuff is exploiting loopholes in reality to phase through walls, teleport, gain near infinite speed and generally break physics to their hearts content. Does that sound like good inspiration for an Abyssal Legacy to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does sound pretty cool. I'd probably give the Legacy two variants, one for the Free Council and one for the Scelesti, where the Free Council version absolutely hates the Abyssal version and the Abyssal one is oddly fond of the Free Council guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T15:11:06-07:00","id":1506367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506349#post1506349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever watch a video game speed run? Especially a glitch using one? People do crazy, often immoral in the context of the game, just to shave off a few milliseconds from their time. Some the more common stuff is exploiting loopholes in reality to phase through walls, teleport, gain near infinite speed and generally break physics to their hearts content. Does that sound like good inspiration for an Abyssal Legacy to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like a few unWise members of the Reality Stalkers Legacy, than an entire new Legacy. (Though novel Attainments are a thing\u2026\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T15:16:52-07:00","id":1506368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506367#post1506367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feels like a few unWise members of the Reality Stalkers Legacy, than an entire new Legacy. (Though novel Attainments are a thing\u2026\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. Though they don't really focus on speed like I am thinking of...hmm. Do we have any examples of an Abyssal version of an existing legacy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T17:16:56-07:00","id":1506383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506368#post1506368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point. Though they don't really focus on speed like I am thinking of...hmm. Do we have any examples of an Abyssal version of an existing legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, but <i>Nameless and Accursed </i>has the rules for making them on page 96, and a sample one on page 119.<br /> <br /> The description suggests Space and Forces. I could see them using a Shielding of Space and Forces to protect them them from Van Der Waals forces and pass unobstructed in the space, allowing them to glitch through walls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T04:05:36-07:00","id":1506412,"title":"","content":"How... divided can an Imbued Item be? Like, could you make a legion of <u>Golem</u>s, with an associated horn that causes them all to animate when blown? That is, the Imbuement is spread out between the golems and the horn?<br /> <br /> Context -<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I'm trying to figure out how to make the Gjallarhorn. For the most mythologically acurate incarnation, it would just need to open an Avernian Gate to an Underwold realm where a ghostly army has already been amassed. But I like alternatives.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Horn Imbued with <u>Quicken Corpse</u>, set to &quot;Area&quot; Scale so it affects everything around the sounder. Requires corpses on-hand, and prone to Dissonance unless the Imbuement includes a combined-casting of <u>Corpse Mask</u>, or you prepared the corpses with concealing clothes/armour</li> <li>Horn Imbued with <u>Golem</u>, using the same parameters as above. Again, requires you to have statues on-hand and is prone to Dissonance unless you included a Veiling spell of some sort. <u>Invisibility</u>, <u>Incognito Presence</u>, a Forces illusion, etc. Or prepare concealing apparel.</li> <li>Horn and mannequins of some stripe, Imbued with <u>Golem</u>. Limited to number-of-subjects Scale, but if the Imbuement includes the mannequins there's a plausible argument that it's only working at the &quot;Self&quot; range. So when you blow the horn, all the mannequins animate regardless of where they are. <i>Permanence</i> can get you up to a high Advanced Duration, which gives you Reach for Advanced Scale and Instant Casting.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>That being said, <i>Sympathetic</i> Range would also be a reasonable requirement, in which case you'd need to use <u>Create Sympathy'</u>s Lasting option on each mannequin and the horn. In which case you could just ignore the divided Imbuement, but it has other downsides, like the amount of Reach being used.</li> </ol></li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-25-2023, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T05:02:48-07:00","id":1506413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506412#post1506412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How... divided can an Imbued Item be? Like, could you make a legion of <u>Golem</u>s, with an associated horn that causes them all to animate when blown? That is, the Imbuement is spread out between the golems and the horn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you\u2019d be Imbuing several different statues, or piles of conveniently humanoid rocks, etc (as opposed to a single swooping Imbuement), upon which you repeat the exact same trigger of \u201cRise when I blow <i>this</i> horn.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T05:07:29-07:00","id":1506414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506413#post1506413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that you\u2019d be Imbuing several different statues, or piles of conveniently humanoid rocks, etc (as opposed to a single swooping Imbuement), upon which you repeat the exact same trigger of \u201cRise when I blow <i>this</i> horn.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I edited in some context that's somewhat relevant.<br /> <br /> In an attempt to create an army without murdering your Spell Control, Permenant Willpower, or Wisdom - Imbue a horn with <u>Golem</u>, and use <u>Create Sympathy</u>'s Lasting effect between it and every mannequin you plan to affect, maybe?<br /> <br /> EDIT: unrelated. <br /> 1. Is a &quot;weapons&quot; <u>Ban</u> possible, and if so what Conjunctive Arcana is it? Death, since they're implements of death? Matter, since they're tools?<br /> <br /> 2. For <u>Psychic Domination</u>, is &quot;serve me&quot; too broad a command? I assume so, just toying with the idea of a Shadow of Mordor-style domination Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 03-25-2023, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T10:16:37-07:00","id":1506422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506414#post1506414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I edited in some context that's somewhat relevant.<br /> <br /> In an attempt to create an army without murdering your Spell Control, Permenant Willpower, or Wisdom - Imbue a horn with <u>Golem</u>, and use <u>Create Sympathy</u>'s Lasting effect between it and every mannequin you plan to affect, maybe?<br /> <br /> EDIT: unrelated.<br /> 1. Is a &quot;weapons&quot; <u>Ban</u> possible, and if so what Conjunctive Arcana is it? Death, since they're implements of death? Matter, since they're tools?<br /> <br /> 2. For <u>Psychic Domination</u>, is &quot;serve me&quot; too broad a command? I assume so, just toying with the idea of a Shadow of Mordor-style domination Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Either one would work<br /> 2- I think what Calebrimbor does is <i>Forge Purpose</i>, given that he is using Prime and Death primarily.\u200b<br /> <br /> Regarding Gjallahorn, I think utilizing a hybrid approach might be helpful. Give it the <i>Golem</i> spell with conjunctional Fate 2 so the affected statue activates upon hearing its sound, set them to be obedient to the holder, and provide for them to have a default programming if the holder is not around and didn't give orders. Place you statues in the fallen, then install a radio receiver on them.<br /> <br /> Prepare a radio/phone tower with Perfected tranmission ability and expanded range (Forces 3), making the waves able to reach through thick materials. Now you just need to sound the horn over the radio. The best part is, even if someone finds out about the tower, there are no clues or sympathetic ties to your army. An innocuous radio project by a mage, hidden in plain sight by a mask of banality, no one would suspect its the first domino in a much grander scheme. Modular pieces that build up to more than the sum of their parts, overall it should cost 1 permanent Willpower, with the imbuement relinquished safely with an exceptional success and the radio tower having an indefinite effect that was safely relinquished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-25-2023, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T11:55:59-07:00","id":1506428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506422#post1506422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- I think what Calebrimbor does is <i>Forge Purpose</i>, given that he is using Prime and Death primarily.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Really? I'm not sure giving orcs an Obsession quite lines up with forcing them to serve you...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding Gjallahorn, I think utilizing a hybrid approach might be helpful. Give it the <i>Golem</i> spell with conjunctional Fate 2 so the affected statue activates upon hearing its sound, set them to be obedient to the holder, and provide for them to have a default programming if the holder is not around and didn't give orders. Place you statues in the fallen, then install a radio receiver on them. </div> </div> </div> Er... why does that need Fate 2? Golems will already have a basic programming, and definitely will if given the Mind/Spirit/Death Conjunctive effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prepare a radio/phone tower with Perfected tranmission ability and expanded range (Forces 3), making the waves able to reach through thick materials. Now you just need to sound the horn over the radio. The best part is, even if someone finds out about the tower, there are no clues or sympathetic ties to your army. An innocuous radio project by a mage, hidden in plain sight by a mask of banality, no one would suspect its the first domino in a much grander scheme. Modular pieces that build up to more than the sum of their parts, overall it should cost 1 permanent Willpower, with the imbuement relinquished safely with an exceptional success and the radio tower having an indefinite effect that was safely relinquished. </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I don't quite follow. Like I said, I don't understand why you'd need Fate, and it sounds more like 21c's suggestion of singular Contingent Imbuements triggered by &quot;the sound of this horn blowing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T12:05:16-07:00","id":1506429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506428#post1506428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really? I'm not sure giving orcs an Obsession quite lines up with forcing them to serve you...<br /> <br /> Er... why does that need Fate 2? Golems will already have a basic programming, and definitely will if given the Mind/Spirit/Death Conjunctive effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm afraid I don't quite follow. Like I said, I don't understand why you'd need Fate, and it sounds more like 21c's suggestion of singular Contingent Imbuements triggered by &quot;the sound of this horn blowing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Fate wouldn't be needed, my bad.<br /> <br /> The main issue is getting the sound of the horn to them. Which would need something like a massive <i>Co-Location</i> for all the statues, or for it to be sounded in a place that already had that setup so all the statues would hear it. That would have a high Willpower cost when accounting for all spells.<br /> <br /> This approach means that the horn is sounded on the tower, sent by the radio via broadcast, then the statues hear it via the radio receiver and activate. Essentially, technology is being used to make it easier to activate all of them and harder to sympathetically trace all of them, while saving a lot of Willpower as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T12:21:16-07:00","id":1506430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506429#post1506429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Fate wouldn't be needed, my bad.<br /> <br /> The main issue is getting the sound of the horn to them. Which would need something like a massive <i>Co-Location</i> for all the statues, or for it to be sounded in a place that already had that setup so all the statues would hear it. That would have a high Willpower cost when accounting for all spells.<br /> <br /> This approach means that the horn is sounded on the tower, sent by the radio via broadcast, then the statues hear it via the radio receiver and activate. Essentially, technology is being used to make it easier to activate all of them and harder to sympathetically trace all of them, while saving a lot of Willpower as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... is each <u>Golem</u> individually Imbued? Because that's a <i>lot</i> of work, and Exceptional Success on an Extended Action roll are far from guaranteed.<br /> <br /> Im guessing these would be Persistent rather than Contingent, because the amount of Mana that would eat per activation would quickly become unmanageable.<br /> <br /> Individually Imbued troops has the advantage of not disabling the entire army if one unit gets dispelled/Dissonanced, but the prep-work makes it somewhat impractical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T18:25:41-07:00","id":1506448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506430#post1506430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... is each <u>Golem</u> individually Imbued? Because that's a <i>lot</i> of work, and Exceptional Success on an Extended Action roll are far from guaranteed.<br /> <br /> Im guessing these would be Persistent rather than Contingent, because the amount of Mana that would eat per activation would quickly become unmanageable.<br /> <br /> Individually Imbued troops has the advantage of not disabling the entire army if one unit gets dispelled/Dissonanced, but the prep-work makes it somewhat impractical.</div> </div> </div> </div>The war horn is imbued with <i>Golem</i>, then used to cast for the entire army using one spell slot, then safely relinquished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T20:07:20-07:00","id":1506451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506448#post1506448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The war horn is imbued with <i>Golem</i>, then used to cast for the entire army using one spell slot, then safely relinquished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'm still confused as to why you'd set up the radio tower. If the horn is what contains the spell, then it would either need to be within Sight (or Aimed) range of the Golems, or would need to be cast at Sympathetic Range. The act of sounding the horn is the Contingent trigger that activates the spell, but the spell itself functions like a normal spell would, constrained by all the normal parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T20:38:46-07:00","id":1506453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506412#post1506412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to figure out how to make the Gjallarhorn. For the most mythologically acurate incarnation, it would just need to open an Avernian Gate to an Underwold realm where a ghostly army has already been amassed. But I like alternatives.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Horn Imbued with <u>Quicken Corpse</u>, set to &quot;Area&quot; Scale so it affects everything around the sounder. Requires corpses on-hand, and prone to Dissonance unless the Imbuement includes a combined-casting of <u>Corpse Mask</u>, or you prepared the corpses with concealing clothes/armour</li> <li>Horn Imbued with <u>Golem</u>, using the same parameters as above. Again, requires you to have statues on-hand and is prone to Dissonance unless you included a Veiling spell of some sort. <u>Invisibility</u>, <u>Incognito Presence</u>, a Forces illusion, etc. Or prepare concealing apparel.</li> <li>Horn and mannequins of some stripe, Imbued with <u>Golem</u>. Limited to number-of-subjects Scale, but if the Imbuement includes the mannequins there's a plausible argument that it's only working at the &quot;Self&quot; range. So when you blow the horn, all the mannequins animate regardless of where they are. <i>Permanence</i> can get you up to a high Advanced Duration, which gives you Reach for Advanced Scale and Instant Casting.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>That being said, <i>Sympathetic</i> Range would also be a reasonable requirement, in which case you'd need to use <u>Create Sympathy'</u>s Lasting option on each mannequin and the horn. In which case you could just ignore the divided Imbuement, but it has other downsides, like the amount of Reach being used.</li> </ol></li> </ol>[/Spoiler]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506414#post1506414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I edited in some context that's somewhat relevant.<br /> <br /> In an attempt to create an army without murdering your Spell Control, Permenant Willpower, or Wisdom - Imbue a horn with <u>Golem</u>, and use <u>Create Sympathy</u>'s Lasting effect between it and every mannequin you plan to affect, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rereading Signs of Sorcery, I think crafting the Hollering Horn may be simpler than it looks. Just... Imbue the Golem spell, or the Quicken Corpse spell, with Advanced Scale (Area) and Advanced Duration (and any other Add Arcana or Reach options), set it as a Contingent Item where the condition is &quot;blow the horn&quot;, and be done.<br /> <br /> With Advanced Area-of-Effect, Range is not a problem unless you are trying to summon your animated soldiers from somewhere far away. That's going to take effort on par with just luring your enemy to wherever you had your animated soldiers already stationed, and since the latter also indirectly solves Dissonance issues, I'd go for that instead.<br /> <br /> To meet the exact parameters of what you said, you may indeed need to Combine several spells... or hunt for an Artifact. As I reckon, Artifacts are the design space for magical effects that hand-wave away technicalities for the Creative Thaumaturgy rules. (Boons from Supernal Entities should work too, for the same reason) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: unrelated.<br /> 1. Is a &quot;weapons&quot; <u>Ban</u> possible, and if so what Conjunctive Arcana is it? Death, since they're implements of death? Matter, since they're tools?<br /> <br /> 2. For <u>Psychic Domination</u>, is &quot;serve me&quot; too broad a command? I assume so, just toying with the idea of a Shadow of Mordor-style domination Legacy. </div> </div> </div>1. Matter.<br /> <br /> 2. The book says that the caster's intentions are sent too, and lists &quot;defend&quot; as an example (which I consider broad as &quot;serve (me)&quot;), so I'd allow it. The real problem is putting enough Potency to overcome Withstand, and enough Duration to make the service last more than a few seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T20:52:51-07:00","id":1506456,"title":"","content":"On the topic of Imbued Items, I've found I'm still not wholey clear on how their activation works. Is it the same spell every time, ie same Potency, Duration, Scale, etc, regardless of who activates it? Or are you spending dice to increase steps like a normal spell? I know Reach is fixed, but not sure about the rest.<br /> <br /> The rather miniscule dice-pool makes me think the former, but I have a habit of being overly optimistic with some mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T22:05:44-07:00","id":1506459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506456#post1506456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of Imbued Items, I've found I'm still not wholey clear on how their activation works. Is it the same spell every time, ie same Potency, Duration, Scale, etc, regardless of who activates it? Or are you spending dice to increase steps like a normal spell? I know Reach is fixed, but not sure about the rest.<br /> <br /> The rather miniscule dice-pool makes me think the former, but I have a habit of being overly optimistic with some mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell's Arcanum rating + the user's Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The user gets to decide spell factors, but unless the Imbuer made the effort to bestow the Flexible Reach feature, no Advanced spell factors.<br /> <br /> From this I assume that the user can sacrifice the dice pool to raise spell factors, but since Yantras are noted to not provide dice, doing that is a rather desperate move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T22:33:53-07:00","id":1506461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506459#post1506459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell's Arcanum rating + the user's Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The user gets to decide spell factors, but unless the Imbuer made the effort to bestow the Flexible Reach feature, no Advanced spell factors.<br /> <br /> From this I assume that the user can sacrifice the dice pool to raise spell factors, but since Yantras are noted to not provide dice, doing that is a rather desperate move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then does it also get the normal free jumps in the primary factor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T22:47:05-07:00","id":1506462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506461#post1506461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then does it also get the normal free jumps in the primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, forgot about that.<br /> <br /> This one's tricky, because Primary factors are about the caster's Arcanum rating, but Imbued Items have the Imbuer and the user separated......<br /> <br /> Rereading the part in SoS about Xoristos and Memias schools' perspectives, the original Imbuer/crafter's dots being used for the Primary factor makes logical sense. <b>However</b>, because of the extra bookkeeping this brings, and the question of whether a spell's Imago also includes the Primary spell factor, I'd also be content at using the user's dots for the Primary factor.<br /> <br /> (With the usual disclaimer, of course, of how this is just one of many interpretations)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T23:17:38-07:00","id":1506463,"title":"","content":"What is the difference between Acamoth and Gulmoth\u200b?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T23:39:02-07:00","id":1506464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506463#post1506463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between Acamoth and Gulmoth\u200b?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/necro-mage-the-awakening-i-read-a-legacy-a-day.658166/post-16275475\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the 1e answer</a>. I think it's still actuate to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T11:26:46-07:00","id":1506501,"title":"","content":"The First Edition explanation of Acamoth actually was a little more elaborate; they were supposed to be Abyssal beings that became trapped in the Fallen World at the instant of the Fall, and were driven to bargain with mages and exchange powers for the opportunity to create horrific nightmares because that was the only way for them to experience a state familiar to their native reality.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Second Edition streamlines some of the Abyssal categories into Gulmoth being the ones that can exist physically (typically with Shadow spirit rules) and Acamoth being the Astral ones. These distinctions also lend some differences to what they're motivated to accomplish, with Gulmoth being more about warping matter and physics and Acamoth rendering Astral landscapes incoherent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T12:09:52-07:00","id":1506513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506501#post1506501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Edition explanation of Acamoth actually was a little more elaborate; they were supposed to be Abyssal beings that became trapped in the Fallen World at the instant of the Fall, and were driven to bargain with mages and exchange powers for the opportunity to create horrific nightmares because that was the only way for them to experience a state familiar to their native reality.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Second Edition streamlines some of the Abyssal categories into Gulmoth being the ones that can exist physically (typically with Shadow spirit rules) and Acamoth being the Astral ones. These distinctions also lend some differences to what they're motivated to accomplish, with Gulmoth being more about warping matter and physics and Acamoth rendering Astral landscapes incoherent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the 1e Acamoth wanted to return to the Abyss and try to make deals withmages (not having enough powerto do so on their own - but offering investments* to mages willing to help).<br /> <br /> I would presume by contrast Gulmoth wanted to get access to the material world (presumably to corrupt it). But they aren't mention in the index of 1e core, i am left wondering where i got that idea.<br /> <br /> *Extra power, usually temporary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T16:28:16-07:00","id":1506543,"title":"","content":"What happen if a Banisher gets to Integrity 0? Do they become Rapt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T16:37:59-07:00","id":1506544,"title":"","content":"I'd personally make them a Slasher who happens to have spells. Being Rapt implies a positive relationship to Mysteries, which Harrowed Banishers generally lack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T19:27:37-07:00","id":1506581,"title":"","content":"Tass accumulates in mundane objects within the Hallow. Would it be reasonable to rule that any Mana Batteries in the Hallow get filled with &quot;tass&quot; first, taking priority over Fallen objects until full on the grounds that it's an ideal vessel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T20:07:58-07:00","id":1506591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506543#post1506543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happen if a Banisher gets to Integrity 0? Do they become Rapt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Nameless and Accursed, p51, &quot;Harrowed Banisher Systems,&quot; Banishers can't lose their last dot of Integrity, because, per Mage 2e Core's own sidebar on Integrity (p299), Integrity doesn't drop below 1 under normal circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T01:44:10-07:00","id":1506614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506581#post1506581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass accumulates in mundane objects within the Hallow. Would it be reasonable to rule that any Mana Batteries in the Hallow get filled with &quot;tass&quot; first, taking priority over Fallen objects until full on the grounds that it's an ideal vessel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Mana Battery will no more effortlessly accumulate Mana than a mage will, and that the tass takes priority in the absence of spells or oblations to absorb Mana on the basis of how only a characteristic material within the Hallow will become it, suggesting a particular alignment of natures.<br /> <br /> Still, it's within the power of any mage who can create a Mana Battery to cast the Channel Mana spell with a long duration that will periodically attempt to draw from the Hallow, so there <i>would</i> be a process for just leaving it there to absorb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:07:42-07:00","id":1506699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506581#post1506581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass accumulates in mundane objects within the Hallow. Would it be reasonable to rule that any Mana Batteries in the Hallow get filled with &quot;tass&quot; first, taking priority over Fallen objects until full on the grounds that it's an ideal vessel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Weaving of Forces and Prime could be used on the Hallow so the mana has higher conductivity to anything that can hold it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:24:26-07:00","id":1506704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506699#post1506699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a Weaving of Forces and Prime could be used on the Hallow so the mana has higher conductivity to anything that can hold it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure about a spell of an Arcanum that makes a thing that is not under its purview act as though it is.<br /> <br /> Like, would you think you could use a spell incorporating Forces and Matter to give electricity a freezing point?<br /> <br /> Never mind that the proposition isn't really how conductivity works anyway. It's a property of materials, not electricity. Copper has high conductivity, that doesn't mean electrons move towards it wherever it goes (imagine the implications that would have for the fact we make coins out of it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:39:45-07:00","id":1506709,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know, we use river metaphors for electrical training. Giving electricity a freezing point just sounds like stopping the flow from the electricity side, not the material side. It\u2019s a neat effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:53:45-07:00","id":1506713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506581#post1506581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass accumulates in mundane objects within the Hallow. Would it be reasonable to rule that any Mana Batteries in the Hallow get filled with &quot;tass&quot; first, taking priority over Fallen objects until full on the grounds that it's an ideal vessel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this depends on your metaphysics on how Mana becomes Tass. Personally I think it\u2019s a specific property of the Hallow that makes it turn cave moss or sugar skulls or whatever, but that ignores the theory that released mana flows into the nearest Hallow. I can certainly see that being a Reach option on Mana Battery, maybe even with another stealing mana from other sources, like Pattern Scouring and Sacrifice. Maybe it\u2019s like Sophis, and can scavenge used mana. That one would need lots of Reach, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T20:55:41-07:00","id":1506715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506581#post1506581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass accumulates in mundane objects within the Hallow. Would it be reasonable to rule that any Mana Batteries in the Hallow get filled with &quot;tass&quot; first, taking priority over Fallen objects until full on the grounds that it's an ideal vessel?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506699#post1506699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a Weaving of Forces and Prime could be used on the Hallow so the mana has higher conductivity to anything that can hold it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506704#post1506704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really sure about a spell of an Arcanum that makes a thing that is not under its purview act as though it is.<br /> <br /> Like, would you think you could use a spell incorporating Forces and Matter to give electricity a freezing point?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We probably don't need Forces. A Prime Patterning/Making spell to grant a Hallow a Feature (as per <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>) ought to work. (As opposed to trying to meddle with the to-be 'batteries', or 'free' Mana)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T01:35:46-07:00","id":1506736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506713#post1506713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this depends on your metaphysics on how Mana becomes Tass. Personally I think it\u2019s a specific property of the Hallow that makes it turn cave moss or sugar skulls or whatever, but that ignores the theory that released mana flows into the nearest Hallow. I can certainly see that being a Reach option on Mana Battery, maybe even with another stealing mana from other sources, like Pattern Scouring and Sacrifice. Maybe it\u2019s like Sophis, and can scavenge used mana. That one would need lots of Reach, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love a good metaphysics conversation.<br /> <br /> I don't think it is a property of Hallows proper, i think it is a property of the Fallen world. Mana tends to crystalize into Tass as a result of not being in the Supernal, but crystalization also need super saturation - which is what happens when too much mana accumulated in a Hallow (ok maybe it is a feature of Hallows... But i would assume it could happen in other places if mana was force there too).<br /> <br /> Makes me wonder, how would mana from a Hallow in the Shadow/Underworld/Astral/Hedge (Other Realms?) behave differently? How would the Tass formed be affected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:30:17-07:00","id":1506762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506513#post1506513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure the 1e Acamoth wanted to return to the Abyss and try to make deals withmages (not having enough powerto do so on their own - but offering investments* to mages willing to help).<br /> <br /> I would presume by contrast Gulmoth wanted to get access to the material world (presumably to corrupt it). But they aren't mention in the index of 1e core, i am left wondering where i got that idea.<br /> <br /> *Extra power, usually temporary</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite motive to give abyssal creatures is that they seek to Ascend, in order to \u2018naturalize\u2019 their corrupted symbols into the tapestry. Most would not necessarily know how to do this, but it puts me in the mind for look for ways they can leverage short-term intrusions, ways they can fit into an ecosystem, and some kind of grand symbolic scheme they work toward.<br /> I had the idea once that a summoned abyssal would work toward a cannibal cult, and culminate in \u2018the Hunger\u2019 (Antagonists, 118) retroactively becoming a \u2018natural\u2019 curse. But I decided a plot where the PCs were supposed to fail was not a fun play experience. <br /> Of course, my tastes lean heavily toward metaphysics and cosmic tier stuff, so I look for chances to include Imperial Mysteries when I perhaps should not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T11:17:50-07:00","id":1506770,"title":"","content":"If someone buys the Sleepwalker Merit, which is worth 1 dot, and then later acquires any Supernatural Merit (which automatically confers Sleepwalker status IIRC), then the Sleepwalker Merit in itself no longer does anything and its 1 XP investment is refunded as per Sanctity of Merits, right? Also, is Astral Adept a valid example of a Supernatural Merit? I'm unsure, since Mages can also have it, and Supernatural Merits are usually exclusive to mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T11:45:50-07:00","id":1506774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506770#post1506770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone buys the Sleepwalker Merit, which is worth 1 dot, and then later acquires any Supernatural Merit (which automatically confers Sleepwalker status IIRC), then the Sleepwalker Merit in itself no longer does anything and its 1 XP investment is refunded as per Sanctity of Merits, right? Also, is Astral Adept a valid example of a Supernatural Merit? I'm unsure, since Mages can also have it, and Supernatural Merits are usually exclusive to mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and sure, why not? It\u2019s a merit, that gives one supernatural powers. I think Mummy has a few Supernatural that can be picked up by both Mortals, and the Arisen, if you need a precedent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T13:11:54-07:00","id":1506782,"title":"","content":"I <i>think </i>only Sleepewalker-sleepwalkers can carry spells for Mages? Definitely not listed anywhere, but I default to Wolfblooded and other half-splats not having the same relationship to the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T13:36:17-07:00","id":1506785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506782#post1506782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think </i>only Sleepewalker-sleepwalkers can carry spells for Mages? Definitely not listed anywhere, but I default to Wolfblooded and other half-splats not having the same relationship to the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can anyone become a sleepwalker? I know the merit fitful sleeper exists, but narratively you can't gain this merit without being affected by Quiessence.<br /> <br /> The other route i am aware of is failing to sign a watchtower, which requires the ability to awaken (which i assume Wolfbloddsd can't do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T14:13:33-07:00","id":1506787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506785#post1506785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can anyone become a sleepwalker? I know the merit fitful sleeper exists, but narratively you can't gain this merit without being affected by Quiessence.<br /> <br /> The other route i am aware of is failing to sign a watchtower, which requires the ability to awaken (which i assume Wolfbloddsd can't do).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Wolfblooded can (though there's debate about whether they keep their Tell or not).<br /> <br /> Personally I'd allow any Sleepwalker to hold spells. Being a Sleepwalker, whatever the origin, implies a certain openness to magic and the rest comes from the relationship with the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T00:19:57-07:00","id":1506829,"title":"","content":"Do you think Prime Veiling/Fraying can enhance already existing illusions? Like for example, a hologram, or a Changeling\u2019s Mask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T00:22:36-07:00","id":1506830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506829#post1506829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think Prime Veiling/Fraying can enhance already existing illusions? Like for example, a hologram, or a Changeling\u2019s Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect only indirectly, via layering additional Veils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T14:45:50-07:00","id":1506875,"title":"","content":"What happens if you mind is in your Temporal Pocket but your body isn't?<br /> <br /> Can you, for example, project a dream form into mind twilight, then create a Temporal pocket around your mind, possibly with indefinite duration.<br /> <br /> Maybe you are using possession, and using someone else's body, or a create Life body for indefinite life experience within the Temporal pocket... Can you just spend infinite time there before returning to your own body - possibly completely changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T16:28:04-07:00","id":1506881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506875#post1506875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you mind is in your Temporal Pocket but your body isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much exactly what you would expect. The Mind experiences the extra \u201cstopped\u201d time, the body doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506875#post1506875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you, for example, project a dream form into mind twilight, then create a Temporal pocket around your mind, possibly with indefinite duration.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean yeah? Still breaks if you interact with anything, so \u201cstopped\u201d time isn\u2019t the best for a indefinite spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506875#post1506875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you are using possession, and using someone else's body, or a create Life body for indefinite life experience within the Temporal pocket... Can you just spend infinite time there before returning to your own body - possibly completely changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh? Temporal Pocket doesn\u2019t let you really interact with world without breaking? But yeah, even if it\u2019s been a thousand years, it\u2019s still your body by default. You should to return just fine. Though, if you wanted to do a story about how someone can\u2019t return to their body and is stuck in Mind Twilight or in other people\u2019s bodies, that would be pretty cool and fun. Maybe it\u2019s similar process to whatever makes people go rapt for having superhuman stats or being an animal forever. Or maybe absorbing people\u2019s thoughts and memories isn\u2019t a great idea for keeping your identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-29-2023, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T16:33:28-07:00","id":1506883,"title":"","content":"I think Orathiac might have gotten <u>Veil of Moments</u> and <u>Temporal Pocket</u> confused. VoM would have some utility for Astral Journeys or possessing another entity, since it would suspend your metabolic functions.<br /> <br /> Of course, a high Potency <u>Body Control</u> (and maybe <u>Surpress Life</u>?) Can do much the same without limiting your ability to learn and grow. VoM would keep you from aging though, which <i>does</i> have benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T23:39:08-07:00","id":1506929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506883#post1506883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Orathiac might have gotten <u>Veil of Moments</u> and <u>Temporal Pocket</u> confused</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, though casting Ceoil of Moments while ina Temporal pocket should stop your mind from going insane...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uh? Temporal Pocket doesn\u2019t let you really interact with world without breaking? But yeah, even if it\u2019s been a thousand years, it\u2019s still your body by default. </div> </div> </div>Yes, my usual thinking is that you have to cast Temporal pocket as an AoE effect (more like faerie glade from 1e) and you can touch or interact with anything within the area. Drink the water, eat the food, probably absorb the mana from your local hallow but it not refill.<br /> <br /> Maybe all the trees die from a lack of sunlight. Or all the rest of the life dies from a lack of oxygen.<br /> <br /> But anything leaving the area exits the time pocket rather than ending it. I suspect the only way to space to 'touch' something outside of itself would be a co-locate. (Doing a combined Temporal Pocket with a Space Ban and a Veil of Moments might be best - so things can't wander out nor can they get wrecked by the natural progression of time... Actually that makes a terrifying prison.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1506881#post1506881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pretty much exactly what you would expect. &lt;Snip&gt; But yeah, even if it\u2019s been a thousand years, it\u2019s still your body by default. You should to return just fine. Though, if you wanted to do a story about how someone can\u2019t return to their body and is stuck in Mind Twilight or in other people\u2019s bodies, that would be pretty cool and fun. Maybe it\u2019s similar process to whatever makes people go rapt for having superhuman stats or being an animal forever. Or maybe absorbing people\u2019s thoughts and memories isn\u2019t a great idea for keeping your identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the going Rapt or losing your identity/being an animal forever is the kind of messed up result i am curious about.<br /> <br /> Pretty much tracks with the direction i was thinking about. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 03-30-2023, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:21:52-07:00","id":1507071,"title":"","content":"Why is the General associated with Forces? The Unity is using Mind to spread Xenophobia, the Eye is Surveillance through Space, the Father is using Prime to hide the truth and trap people in fake religions, but why is the General's Militarism associated with Forces? It seems like Militarism should be just as achievable through Death, Matter, Life, Mind, or Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:29:56-07:00","id":1507074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507071#post1507071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the General associated with Forces? The Unity is using Mind to spread Xenophobia, the Eye is Surveillance through Space, the Father is using Prime to hide the truth and trap people in fake religions, but why is the General's Militarism associated with Forces? It seems like Militarism should be just as achievable through Death, Matter, Life, Mind, or Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firearms, explosives, tazers, swords, armor, martial arts techniques, claws, fangs and many more. All of them are essentially manipulating forces to inflict or prevent violence. Even atomic weapons, which can devastate the planet, are primarily using forces. All Arcanum are tremendously flexible, but Forces is the most symbolically associated with the dehumanizing violence that defines the General.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:37:38-07:00","id":1507075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507074#post1507074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firearms, explosives, tazers, swords, armor,</div> </div> </div> </div>All forms of Matter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> martial arts techniques, claws, fangs </div> </div> </div>All forms of Life, with a bit of Mind for martial arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Arcanum are tremendously flexible, but Forces is the most symbolically associated with the dehumanizing violence that defines the General. </div> </div> </div>That's the chicken-and-the-egg problem. Forces is associated with the General's dehumanizing violence because the General is the Exarch of Forces, but if the developers had made the General an Exarch of not-Forces, then Forces would have been written differently and the not-Forces arcana would be associated with dehumanizing violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:56:28-07:00","id":1507078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507075#post1507075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the chicken-and-the-egg problem. Forces is associated with the General's dehumanizing violence because the General is the Exarch of Forces, but if the developers had made the General an Exarch of not-Forces, then Forces would have been written differently and the not-Forces arcana would be associated with dehumanizing violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've just answered your own question. Like, you're right it's fairly arbitrary, but if you want the major Exarchs to map onto the Arcana, you need to make a choice. Interestingly, Mammon actually changed from Mind to Matter (At least if I remember <i>Reign of the Exarchs </i>correct).<br /> <br /> You can see a similar thing going on with the Paths and their arcana. A lot of the reasons for inferior arcana could fairly easily be flipped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T14:12:10-07:00","id":1507080,"title":"","content":"I think generally a fist hurts because it\u2019s transferring a large amount of Force into your face, not because it\u2019s made of the right organic compounds. Swords don\u2019t hurt because they are are made of acid, they hurt because the shape is good for transferring Force into a small area, making a cut. Large amounts of Forces cause pain to our fragile bodies. Pretty much every Exarch can be covered under Mind, because they are all Symbols of Tyranny, and oppression is a mental Phenomena. Thus the Exarch\u2019s associated Arcana is on how the use of a phenomenon under an Arcana can be tyrannical.<br /> <br /> Edit: The General is the symbolism of the Unstoppable Force, and you are not an Immovable Object, but very tiny and ephemeral. You can move yourself out of the way, or be moved anyways. And one\u2019s a lot less likely to have you being trampled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-31-2023, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T20:38:29-07:00","id":1507093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507080#post1507080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think generally a fist hurts because it\u2019s transferring a large amount of Force into your face, not because it\u2019s made of the right organic compounds. Swords don\u2019t hurt because they are are made of acid, they hurt because the shape is good for transferring Force into a small area, making a cut. Large amounts of Forces cause pain to our fragile bodies. Pretty much every Exarch can be covered under Mind, because they are all Symbols of Tyranny, and oppression is a mental Phenomena. Thus the Exarch\u2019s associated Arcana is on how the use of a phenomenon under an Arcana can be tyrannical.<br /> <br /> Edit: The General is the symbolism of the Unstoppable Force, and you are not an Immovable Object, but very tiny and ephemeral. You can move yourself out of the way, or be moved anyways. And one\u2019s a lot less likely to have you being trampled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first part is a decent explanation, but the edit is what really convinced me that Forces is a good fit for the General.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T00:50:14-07:00","id":1507099,"title":"","content":"What kind of spell would you typically Imbue with <u>Imbue Room</u>? I guess you could make a Persistent defense like <u>Ward</u>, but it's not a huge step up from just casting and then relinquishing a given spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T06:54:58-07:00","id":1507107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507099#post1507099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of spell would you typically Imbue with <u>Imbue Room</u>? I guess you could make a Persistent defense like <u>Ward</u>, but it's not a huge step up from just casting and then relinquishing a given spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Veil of Moments? So you can have an emergency room where time is switched off and casualties don't bleed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T07:16:09-07:00","id":1507108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507099#post1507099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of spell would you typically Imbue with <u>Imbue Room</u>? I guess you could make a Persistent defense like <u>Ward</u>, but it's not a huge step up from just casting and then relinquishing a given spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Laying booby traps on an area comes to mind. Such as: have Imbue Room cast on your Sleeper-identity\u2019s house, then Imbue something like Hallucination with the contingent trigger of \u201cuninvited intrusion\u201d, and voila.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T09:05:27-07:00","id":1507109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507071#post1507071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the General associated with Forces? The Unity is using Mind to spread Xenophobia, the Eye is Surveillance through Space, the Father is using Prime to hide the truth and trap people in fake religions, but why is the General's Militarism associated with Forces? It seems like Militarism should be just as achievable through Death, Matter, Life, Mind, or Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Iron Seals were devised by beginning with a form of oppression and then figuring out which Arcanum accomplishes it, but starting with each Arcanum and devising a form of tyranny that could be mapped to it.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that each of the Arcana are not just their literal, materialistic expressions, but their underlying symbolism. Violence is intertwined with Forces because those are the terms that the Supernal Realm of the Aether were described in long before any Exarch was written in particular detail (which is also something that informs the Obrimos Path beyond them just harnessing Forces for things like signals intelligence). The storm is not a thing used to accomplish violence, it is a metaphor for a deeper idea of violence (albeit a metaphor that impresses itself very strongly in instances where storms destroy people's lives with all the shocking abruptness of a random mugging or home invasion).<br /> <br /> On a similar note, I would broaden the idea of what the Eye is to incorporate the metaphysics. It's not just about which Arcanum can be used for purposes of surveillance (certainly it's bigger than just using a lot of scrying), it's about the fact that in the Supernal the very idea of things being separate from one another is a perceptual phenomenon, rendered most concrete by the Lie but even without it a matter of how thinking entities are really only as far away from things as they feel (and thus also a bulwark against things they don't want to feel close to, which Pandemonium says ought to be overcome). The Eye isn't just about watching people, it's the alienation created by the sense that you're always being watched, the enforcement of conformity and feeling of being on edge by uncertainty about whether you are in any given instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T13:41:25-07:00","id":1507117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507108#post1507108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Laying booby traps on an area comes to mind. Such as: have Imbue Room cast on your Sleeper-identity\u2019s house, then Imbue something like Hallucination with the contingent trigger of \u201cuninvited intrusion\u201d, and voila.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that Imbued rooms don't have their own Mana pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T17:38:18-07:00","id":1507136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507117#post1507117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem is that Imbued rooms don't have their own Mana pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their users can, so it won't be that much of a problem.<br /> <br /> A trope about mages I often see in modern media is that trying to challenge them in their &quot;workshops&quot; or laboratories is reckless and borders on suicidal, because the mage can arm the room to the teeth with spells.<br /> Normal Imbued objects are too visible (and in danger of being separated or destroyed), just casting a long-Duration Area-of-effect spell means the spell is always on (and thus lacks the &quot;become armed when I call for it&quot; aspect), and of course there's a limit to how much spell a mage can practically throw in the heat of battle.<br /> Imbue Room gets around all that by Imbuing contingent spells, even if it's brute as &quot;the Room casts Thunderbolt when and at whomever I point my fingers at.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T02:33:13-07:00","id":1507170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507136#post1507136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A trope about mages I often see in modern media is that trying to challenge them in their &quot;workshops&quot; or laboratories is reckless and borders on suicidal, because the mage can arm the room to the teeth with spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>kind</i> of covered with what the Sanctum Merit does for spell control, but at the same time I feel as though the very premise of spell control limits its implementation in the game.<br /> <br /> Still, basilisks from Signs of Sorcery can cover some of the idea of traps that activate in response to intruders as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T06:11:39-07:00","id":1507176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507170#post1507170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's <i>kind</i> of covered with what the Sanctum Merit does for spell control, but at the same time I feel as though the very premise of spell control limits its implementation in the game.<br /> <br /> Still, basilisks from Signs of Sorcery can cover some of the idea of traps that activate in response to intruders as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good call on Basilisks. We need more gimmicky Yantras like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T13:44:07-07:00","id":1507314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507170#post1507170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's <i>kind</i> of covered with what the Sanctum Merit does for spell control, but at the same time I feel as though the very premise of spell control limits its implementation in the game.<br /> <br /> Still, basilisks from Signs of Sorcery can cover some of the idea of traps that activate in response to intruders as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Sanctum merit to be exploited, you could have a regular (let's say monthly) ritual time to cast protections on your Sanctum, and then unsafely relinquish.<br /> <br /> Each month the spells should dissipate and/or you break the Runes you used in casting them (though i might argue that a living spell which has mutated beyond the runes which spelled it out might survive even that).<br /> <br /> And recast. So, while it the ritual space in your Sanctum, you have the extra spell control. But then you relinquish before leaving.<br /> <br /> This has the downside of not knowing when something might clash against your spells... But in the example described above (conditional triggers, imbued rooms) it shouldn't matter too much.<br /> <br /> Maybe you just want one spell control given up to ward your space from Scrying/teleportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T13:59:02-07:00","id":1507315,"title":"","content":"Would <i>Control Sound</i> be enough to allow a mage to project their voice like a ventriloquist or would a dedicated spell be needed ? If I understood the spell correctly, it would need to be cast on the subject, then the AoE scale chart would need to be used to determine the valid area in which it could be projected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T14:19:43-07:00","id":1507316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507315#post1507315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <i>Control Sound</i> be enough to allow a mage to project their voice like a ventriloquist or would a dedicated spell be needed ? If I understood the spell correctly, it would need to be cast on the subject, then the AoE scale chart would need to be used to determine the valid area in which it could be projected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would say it can if the Scale Area includes both the actual source of the sound and the desired apparent source of the sound, reflecting the sound being funneled from source to target and then released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T14:25:30-07:00","id":1507317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507315#post1507315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <i>Control Sound</i> be enough to allow a mage to project their voice like a ventriloquist or would a dedicated spell be needed ? If I understood the spell correctly, it would need to be cast on the subject, then the AoE scale chart would need to be used to determine the valid area in which it could be projected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d allow it. It\u2019s a neat idea, fits with the spell, and isn\u2019t anymore complicated than keeping it in within the AoE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T21:59:44-07:00","id":1507373,"title":"","content":"Two questions! One involved enough that I might need to make a thread on it.<br /> <br /> 1. I kinda like the Krewe &quot;character sheet&quot;, and the players in my game are about to aquire a small pool of merits belonging to the Cabal as a whole. Id like to make the Cabal a &quot;character&quot; like a Krewe is. How much of the Krewe template can I keep, and how much should I discard?<br /> <br /> 2. Goetia and Astral Realms arise from any concept that at least two people are aware of. Often, you can simplify this somewhat, with specific realms/things existing as sub-realms within bigger concepts. Is it reasonable then for the Goetia of specific oaths or pledges to form as denizens of the Tenemotic Realm of Oaths? And what happens to those denizens if the thing they represent is broken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T22:55:44-07:00","id":1507376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507373#post1507373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions! One involved enough that I might need to make a thread on it.<br /> <br /> 1. I kinda like the Krewe &quot;character sheet&quot;, and the players in my game are about to aquire a small pool of merits belonging to the Cabal as a whole. Id like to make the Cabal a &quot;character&quot; like a Krewe is. How much of the Krewe template can I keep, and how much should I discard?<br /> <br /> 2. Goetia and Astral Realms arise from any concept that at least two people are aware of. Often, you can simplify this somewhat, with specific realms/things existing as sub-realms within bigger concepts. Is it reasonable then for the Goetia of specific oaths or pledges to form as denizens of the Tenemotic Realm of Oaths? And what happens to those denizens if the thing they represent is broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Drop Regalia(Cabal Theme is the closest contemporary), figure out the contextual form of some of the particulars like the organizational power (not Power) stat and health and such, good to go.<br /> <br /> 2) Goetia aren't tied to specific forms like spirits can be, so broken oaths aren't going to directly impact them in the same way. Otherwise though, yeah you might forms specific enough to what applies at a given moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T02:25:50-07:00","id":1507385,"title":"","content":"Is regrowing a knocked-out tooth more a <u>Regeneration</u> thing, or just a healing-level feat? On the one hand, it's not something you can regrow naturally. On the other, it's a rather insignificant thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T04:50:50-07:00","id":1507392,"title":"","content":"It would normally require <i>Regeneration</i>. But if they have time, a long lasting spell that gives them a body wide version of an axolotl's regeneration, alongside a spell to reduce recovery times could be paired for a Lasting effect, if the mage keeps it low key.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Fate/Life version of <i>Time Heal</i> could also do it instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T04:53:47-07:00","id":1507394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507392#post1507392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if they have time, a long lasting spell that gives them a body wide version of an axolotl's regeneration, alongside a spell to reduce recovery times could be paired for a Lasting effect, if the mage keeps it low key.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, at that point I'd just go with that &quot;Overclocked Regeneration&quot; spell we made on the Creative Thaumaturgy thread a while back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T07:17:11-07:00","id":1507398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507385#post1507385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is regrowing a knocked-out tooth more a <u>Regeneration</u> thing, or just a healing-level feat? On the one hand, it's not something you can regrow naturally. On the other, it's a rather insignificant thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Second Edition opts pretty much every time for consistency in the Practices over what might seem significant. This is most apparent when comparing to First; back then, mind control to the point of suicidal acts was significant, hence it required a Master. Conjuring light from nothing was viewed as lesser than fire, so it went at two or three dots. Now, mind control falls under Ruling (it's just that extreme calls for you to Reach) and all forms of energy need Making to get ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> Regrowing a tooth being a triviality compared to the skill it takes to do it isn't a basis for giving it to a lower power, it's a cause for mages to consider whether or not this is a worthy use of their powers.<br /> <br /> (Souped up amphibian regeneration breaks the whole dramatic basis of Supernal regeneration over its knee, so it ought to be curated a bit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T07:20:56-07:00","id":1507399,"title":"","content":"Even if we avoid axolotl regeneration, you could always go with the infinite dental regeneration of sharks. <u>Transform Life</u> in general is a great roundabout way to achieve Lasting Life effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T12:48:23-07:00","id":1507432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507399#post1507399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we avoid axolotl regeneration, you could always go with the infinite dental regeneration of sharks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could get teeth that would work like shark teeth in all respects there, including the element where they're adapted to constantly fall out and have the next one in the row replace them, whether they're damaged or not. Even if that was a form of tooth that would stick around after the spell ended*, I don't think it would be very firmly rooted in one's gums.<br /> <br /> * And I think that's a bit of a big if. Like, if you use Transform Life to grant yourself claws, the claws don't become Lasting. And I don't think it really fits the spell to do some workaround like &quot;I'm not giving myself claws, I'm giving myself the capacity to grow claws. Anything that emerges out of that won't be dependent on magic at all&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T06:49:39-07:00","id":1507477,"title":"","content":"<u>Transform Life</u> can be used to give humans true-breeding, Dissonance-free mutations from the second generation onward. Setting aside the necessary timescale, is there a point where you've added so many transformations that a generation of offspring is no longer human? As in, they have neither soul, nor inherent connection to the Tenemos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T09:10:41-07:00","id":1507484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507477#post1507477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Transform Life</u> can be used to give humans true-breeding, Dissonance-free mutations from the second generation onward. Setting aside the necessary timescale, is there a point where you've added so many transformations that a generation of offspring is no longer human? As in, they have neither soul, nor inherent connection to the Temenos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on whether symbolically we would think of them as humans. By the standards of the bronze age, we are impossibly tall beings that can be infected with certain deadly diseases and go &quot;You have no power here !&quot;, but they would likely still see us as humans. We can look at characters like Adam Jensen and David Martinez and still see them as humans. If they seem like augmented humans or post humans, then they probably count. But if, for example, they diverge to such a point that their mindset seems completely alienating, then they might be seen as something else entirely. I would give the Venusians from <i>Battle Angel Alita: Last Order</i> a pass, but not mindflayers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T09:24:00-07:00","id":1507485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507477#post1507477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Transform Life</u> can be used to give humans true-breeding, Dissonance-free mutations from the second generation onward. Setting aside the necessary timescale, is there a point where you've added so many transformations that a generation of offspring is no longer human? As in, they have neither soul, nor inherent connection to the Tenemos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can do whatever you want with that. Like, the metaphysics of the situation are so complex, and we don't even have the answers to fairly basic questions involving the soul.<br /> <br /> That said, you might wonder why the Seers aren't working on this if it's possible? (Though maybe they are?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T10:35:11-07:00","id":1507495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507485#post1507485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, you might wonder why the Seers aren't working on this if it's possible? (Though maybe they are?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyrants only exist if they have people/souls to oppress. If they are doing this, it\u2019s in only in small scales so that it may never replace humanity.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back to the main question\u2026this is pretty much the definition of a Deviant Genotypal, and it doesn\u2019t take much at all to make one. So yes.<br /> <br /> Edit:Clarification","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-05-2023, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T12:22:38-07:00","id":1507500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507477#post1507477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Transform Life</u> can be used to give humans true-breeding, Dissonance-free mutations from the second generation onward. Setting aside the necessary timescale, is there a point where you've added so many transformations that a generation of offspring is no longer human? As in, they have neither soul, nor inherent connection to the Tenemos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably the Hive-Souls are a verification of this, though it also demonstrates that it's a lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T12:23:46-07:00","id":1507501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507485#post1507485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you can do whatever you want with that. Like, the metaphysics of the situation are so complex, and we don't even have the answers to fairly basic questions involving the soul.<br /> <br /> That said, you might wonder why the Seers aren't working on this if it's possible? (Though maybe they are?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't the Seers already have some Soulless servants? Althought considering some of the creations they have mutated/breed, if they all have souls that does reflect on the answer to the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:20:17-07:00","id":1507507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507501#post1507501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't the Seers already have some Soulless servants? Althought considering some of the creations they have mutated/breed, if they all have souls that does reflect on the answer to the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hollow Ones. Artificially created via Lower Depths Entity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:30:04-07:00","id":1507508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507507#post1507507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hollow Ones. Artificially created via Lower Depths Entity</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? I thought they still had a soul, just with a removed ego.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:31:11-07:00","id":1507509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507508#post1507508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh? I thought they still had a soul, just with a removed ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, true. Never mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T13:48:24-07:00","id":1507511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507501#post1507501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't the Seers already have some Soulless servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order has lots of stuff, that doesn't mean that individual Seers wouldn't be interested.<br /> <br /> Additionally, who even knows if that's what you'd get? Like, is it a straight cut-off? You either have one or you don't? Maybe your highly modified humans would still have souls, but weaker ones as they stray further from the platonic ideal of what a human is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T14:10:53-07:00","id":1507512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507511#post1507511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, who even knows if that's what you'd get? Like, is it a straight cut-off? You either have one or you don't? Maybe your highly modified humans would still have souls, but weaker ones as they stray further from the platonic ideal of what a human is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming Deviant is canon to your metaphysics\u2026no, it\u2019s not a cut off. Any warping, mutilation, stunting, or breaking of souls that isn\u2019t channeled into a more stable form results in one of the Remade. This is something that someone can be born with. I\u2019d guess the soul gets progressively more warped until an after certain point they have only something barely resembling a soul. Past that point they would become more and more animal like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T20:46:05-07:00","id":1507545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507500#post1507500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably the Hive-Souls are a verification of this, though it also demonstrates that it's a lot of work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would like to note also that &quot;Dissonance-free&quot; is an assumption; the spell doesn't say the inherited traits aren't subject to Dissonance, the Reach effect requires the spell to be Indefinite to work, the 1e spell that Reach effect is carrying forward made its more fantastical products take damage from Disbelief not unlike the way Supernal beings take damage from Dissonance, and allowing any Disciple of Life to circumvent one of the main incentives for subtlety in the Art provided they maintain an indefinite spell long enough for a single new generation to be born doesn't feel like an edition difference in the same vein as &quot;you no longer need different levels of Life to try to affect both people and bugs with the same spells.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T04:14:27-07:00","id":1507574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507545#post1507545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would like to note also that &quot;Dissonance-free&quot; is an assumption; the spell doesn't say the inherited traits aren't subject to Dissonance, the Reach effect requires the spell to be Indefinite to work, the 1e spell that Reach effect is carrying forward made its more fantastical products take damage from Disbelief not unlike the way Supernal beings take damage from Dissonance, and allowing any Disciple of Life to circumvent one of the main incentives for subtlety in the Art provided they maintain an indefinite spell long enough for a single new generation to be born doesn't feel like an edition difference in the same vein as &quot;you no longer need different levels of Life to try to affect both people and bugs with the same spells.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say it becomes lasting, and lasting effects are by default immune to dissonance; but the reach effect is pretty clear it doesn't make it lasting. As it usually says for +2 reach effects.<br /> <br /> So no? Though i like this interpretation where the offspring as not subjects of the spell (vulnerable to dispellation) but are supernal (subject to dissonance).<br /> <br /> Edit: so question, would it be dissonance free only in a natural verge? (Not in a pocket dimension, even though there is no paradox there?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 04-06-2023, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T04:41:37-07:00","id":1507576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507574#post1507574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to say it becomes lasting, and lasting effects are by default immune to dissonance; but the reach effect is pretty clear it doesn't make it lasting. As it usually says for +2 reach effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that offspring are Lasting by dint of &quot;contagious&quot; spells being the purview of Imperial spells. That is, unless it's mutating from unsafe relinquishment or Abyssal corruption, spells shouldn't be switching or expanding targets once cast.<br /> <br /> Plus, the spell requires you to go to Indefinite independent of the Reach effect. That, Combined with the cost of +2 Reach (which is the &quot;normal&quot; cost for Lasting) implies to me that this <i>is</i> a Lasting effect, just behaving slightly differently than the norm.<br /> <br /> On this topic, then - say you use <u>Create Life</u> to make a few instances of a species, and have them reproduce.<br /> Do the offspring disappear when the spell ends?<br /> How about if each of the parents is created by a separate spell? <br /> How about if only one parent is a spell-created entity, and the other is a natural creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-06-2023, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T10:59:52-07:00","id":1507591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507576#post1507576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that offspring are Lasting by dint of &quot;contagious&quot; spells being the purview of Imperial spells. That is, unless it's mutating from unsafe relinquishment or Abyssal corruption, spells shouldn't be switching or expanding targets once cast.<br /> <br /> Plus, the spell requires you to go to Indefinite independent of the Reach effect. That, Combined with the cost of +2 Reach (which is the &quot;normal&quot; cost for Lasting) implies to me that this <i>is</i> a Lasting effect, just behaving slightly differently than the norm.<br /> <br /> On this topic, then - say you use <u>Create Life</u> to make a few instances of a species, and have them reproduce.<br /> Do the offspring disappear when the spell ends?<br /> How about if each of the parents is created by a separate spell?<br /> How about if only one parent is a spell-created entity, and the other is a natural creature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not proposing a situation where the spell affects the offspring (in a non-lasting way) or they become a target of the spell (which would then become subject to dispellation).<br /> <br /> Merely that the offspring can suffer from dissonance despite the effect being lasting.<br /> <br /> That is, obviously magical creatures are subject to the same dissonance effect as supernal beings would be when summoning into the world - with immunity only when they happen to be in a verge - especially since this increases the likelihood that you will find all manner of magical creatures in supernal Verges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T13:33:07-07:00","id":1507599,"title":"","content":"But Dissonance is very much an effect of a spell being erroded by the Lie. If the spell's effect is Lasting, then there isn't anything to be Dissonanced. The only entities that are affected similarly to spells in that regard are Supernal Entities, which exist as sentient extensions of the Supernal. An oversimplification perhaps, but they're effectively autonomous and self-perpetuating spells. <br /> <br /> in the case of <u>Transform Life</u>'s Reach effect, my assumption is that it causes the subject's reproductive material to also be affected, rather than just their phenotypic expressions. Once that material has joined with it's counterpart and become a new entity, they've become enough of a discreet symbol that they aren't part of the spell.<br /> <br /> I really can't think of any examples of obviously magical creatures -that arent a <i>direct</i> creation of a spell- that are affected by Dissonance. No to say you can't use it at your table, obviously, but it wouldn't fly at mine and there isn't anything I can remember that directly backs it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:08:31-07:00","id":1507619,"title":"","content":"Somewhat on the topic, I would say there are ways magic can alter DNA in a Lasting way such as by manipulating a retrovirus. But I'd treat such a thing as a long-term project for a mage who was also a molecular biologist - not as something that can be dreamed up in three seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:26:59-07:00","id":1507623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507599#post1507599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Dissonance is very much an effect of a spell being erroded by the Lie. If the spell's effect is Lasting, then there isn't anything to be Dissonanced. The only entities that are affected similarly to spells in that regard are Supernal Entities, which exist as sentient extensions of the Supernal. An oversimplification perhaps, but they're effectively autonomous and self-perpetuating spells.<br /> <br /> in the case of <u>Transform Life</u>'s Reach effect, my assumption is that it causes the subject's reproductive material to also be affected, rather than just their phenotypic expressions. Once that material has joined with it's counterpart and become a new entity, they've become enough of a discreet symbol that they aren't part of the spell.<br /> <br /> I really can't think of any examples of obviously magical creatures -that arent a <i>direct</i> creation of a spell- that are affected by Dissonance. No to say you can't use it at your table, obviously, but it wouldn't fly at mine and there isn't anything I can remember that directly backs it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, a big thing in Mage is that magic is volatile and dangerous. Permanent genetic alterations that last generations don\u2019t quite add up with that premise, which is why it invites questions.<br /> <br /> Like, yeah Dissonance as-is shouldn\u2019t affect them, but maybe they eventually become Cryptids and unable to sustain themselves outside a Verge. Or the alterations end up (de-)mutating themselves out of the genome a few generations down. Better yet, maybe they mutate into unintended monstrosities much like the homebrew Spell Weavers in this forum. And I reckon that mages in-universe would likely refer to such side effects as Dissonance, even if it strictly isn\u2019t. <br /> <br /> The point here being answering the \u201cCan I?\u201d question with \u201cYes But\u201d not \u201cNo\u201d. Masters should be able to pull such feats off, but can they satisfy their own perfectionism, OSHA requirements, and the ethics board?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:38:18-07:00","id":1507625,"title":"","content":"OSHA has no power here! Plus, my question was &quot;is there a cut-off point for being human&quot; rather than &quot;can I do this&quot;.<br /> <br /> On this topic, then - say you use <u>Create Life</u> to make a few instances of a species, and have them reproduce.<br /> Do the offspring disappear when the spell ends?<br /> <br /> How about if each of the parents is created by a separate spell?<br /> <br /> How about if only one parent is a spell-created entity, and the other is a natural creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-06-2023, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:48:18-07:00","id":1507626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507625#post1507625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OSHA has no power here! Plus, my question was &quot;is there a cut-off point for being human&quot; rather than &quot;can I do this&quot;.<br /> <br /> On this topic, then - say you use <u>Create Life</u> to make a few instances of a species, and have them reproduce.<br /> Do the offspring disappear when the spell ends?<br /> <br /> How about if each of the parents is created by a separate spell?<br /> <br /> How about if only one parent is a spell-created entity, and the other is a natural creature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the Occupational Safety and Health Administration does not, but the Ordinators of Sorcerous Hazards and Adversities do! Be careful the next time you order take-out coffee\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> For the humanity-cut off; yeah there ought to be, but a mage witnessing one in her lifetime would be an Obsessive feat.<br /> <br /> For the below vivimancer antics, my gut ruling gives a largely similar answer: Unexpected Side Effects (that creates the maximum enjoyment for your table).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:34:26-07:00","id":1507630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507625#post1507625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OSHA has no power here! Plus, my question was &quot;is there a cut-off point for being human&quot; rather than &quot;can I do this&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! But also, No!<br /> <br /> Depends on your parameters.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:56:41-07:00","id":1507633,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, is being a Hollow One hereditary? Hive-Souled are true-breeding, but their initial creation isn't outlined (as far as I can remember). The Hollow Ones are suffering from the sting of a Lower Depths entity, which is probably an argument against it, but it's certainly a disconcerting possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T18:24:07-07:00","id":1507635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507633#post1507633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, is being a Hollow One hereditary? Hive-Souled are true-breeding, but their initial creation isn't outlined (as far as I can remember). The Hollow Ones are suffering from the sting of a Lower Depths entity, which is probably an argument against it, but it's certainly a disconcerting possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so.<br /> <br /> If I'm recalling my Seers of the THrone right, I believe the Hive-Souled were literally a gift from an Exarch, but I haven't read the sourcebook in years. I don't think Signs explains it, and I don't have it on my at the moment, though I can check later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T18:37:59-07:00","id":1507638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507635#post1507635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm recalling my Seers of the THrone right, I believe the Hive-Souled were literally a gift from an Exarch, but I haven't read the sourcebook in years. I don't think Signs explains it, and I don't have it on my at the moment, though I can check later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs states that legend attributes their creation to a now-Ascended Hegemonic Minister called the Progenitor working on orders from the Unity, and also states that they're a species of their own \u2014 they can only reproduce among their own kind, which is not quite the same as the quality breeding true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T02:20:55-07:00","id":1507677,"title":"","content":"First and Second Edition agree on the Hive-Souled having been the creation of a tetrarch (and I think might even have had the idea that the feat secured Ascension), but actually differ on how they reproduced.<br /> <br /> In Seers of the Throne, it was stated that they needed to impregnate a person and then for that pregnancy to produce multiple foetuses, something that was stated to mean that throughout much of their history it was actually pretty difficult to perpetuate them and Hegemony had a tendency to treat them with utmost care. Modern fertility technology made the process more reliable.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery does indeed state that they only work with one another, but work consistently, which does help to streamline the concept a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T18:00:35-07:00","id":1507726,"title":"","content":"Hey, which Realm would you most associate with Farming and Agriculture? I'm thinking of a Seer-owned Proximi bloodline of people unable to leave their Lands, kinda like the feudalistic notion of Serfs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T18:05:21-07:00","id":1507728,"title":"","content":"Thrysus. Life for growing things, Spirit for animism related to crops, the wild, and livestock<br /> <br /> Moros might be interesting in the sense of soil=Matter, and Death as a natural part of the cycle.<br /> <br /> The other three <i>could</i> be linked, but it'd be tenous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T18:20:32-07:00","id":1507730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507726#post1507726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, which Realm would you most associate with Farming and Agriculture? I'm thinking of a Seer-owned Proximi bloodline of people unable to leave their Lands, kinda like the feudalistic notion of Serfs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering in regards to what the question is for, I'd say a lineage drawing on the Obrimos or Acanthus Arcana fits thematically, depending on whether you want to benefit agriculture through geomantic effects or messing around with time and fortune.<br /> <br /> Life's almost certainly the third Arcanum in either case, but it's probably worth bearing in mind e.g. what flavor of sellout you want Seers who Awaken to the lineage's associated Path to be, whether it's Visionaries who don't want to share their freedom of movement after they got out or Templars who keep their kinsmen working the land with the threat of storms and violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T22:01:35-07:00","id":1507739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507726#post1507726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, which Realm would you most associate with Farming and Agriculture? I'm thinking of a Seer-owned Proximi bloodline of people unable to leave their Lands, kinda like the feudalistic notion of Serfs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Satchel. The obvious arcanum at work is Life which deals with plants, growth, and food, but I understand the Primal Wilds as being the place specifically without human civilisation.<br /> <br /> The concept of serfdom could fit with the Aether as part of the Great Chain of Being. And I usually associate Arcadia aesthetically with themes of gardens, the countryside and nature tamed, so I could see it there too, with the conceptual link of being bound by the circumstances of your birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T01:36:13-07:00","id":1507746,"title":"","content":"Can you take a Hobgoblin or a Hedge Ghost as a Familiar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T01:37:46-07:00","id":1507747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507739#post1507739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with Satchel. The obvious arcanum at work is Life which deals with plants, growth, and food, but I understand the Primal Wilds as being the place specifically without human civilisation.<br /> <br /> The concept of serfdom could fit with the Aether as part of the Great Chain of Being. And I usually associate Arcadia aesthetically with themes of gardens, the countryside and nature tamed, so I could see it there too, with the conceptual link of being bound by the circumstances of your birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Arcadia and oaths to feudal lords makes sense.<br /> <br /> You are a serf because your parents were serfs.... And so on back up the generations, sounds very Arcadian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T02:02:23-07:00","id":1507748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507746#post1507746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take a Hobgoblin or a Hedge Ghost as a Familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can\u2019t Changelings get Hob servants? May be a similar bargain. I forget if the familiar bond requires Spirit, or can be done with any ephemeral Arcana, but definitely needs a Mind and Fate component. Otherwise, why not? Well I guess Rank vs Wyrd might be an issue, but I think you can divide by two and round up for a rough equivalency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-08-2023, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T02:18:36-07:00","id":1507750,"title":"","content":"Wow. Sounds like Acanthus to me, especially considering that's Kyrian's MO, and they serve the Ruin and the Prophet. I'm glad I asked, I had completely forgotten about them until y'all brought up Arcadia. I was leaning towards Styiga due to the idea of growing things to harvest later one, and Matter being associated with working the Earth, but I felt like I was missing something. Thanks, y'all helped a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T03:36:48-07:00","id":1507757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507746#post1507746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take a Hobgoblin or a Hedge Ghost as a Familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by RAW, but homebrewing a spell that \u2018inverts\u2019 Fate 4 Masking the False Fae wouldn\u2019t be unreasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T05:36:36-07:00","id":1507759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507748#post1507748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t Changelings get Hob servants?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Merit that gives them the general respect of hobgoblins they can get a Hollow enhancement that costs one Goblin Debt per story to maintain, with the Discreet Summons Royal Contract they can summon a low-Wyrd hobgoblin to perform a single task (requiring the changeling's attention if they didn't learn the Contract from or as a Fairest), Goblin Queens get Status 4 (Hobgoblins) and their Wyrd in Merit dots of hobgoblin Retainers, and of course nothing stops you from representing hobgoblin connections with normal Social Merits, but there is no special &quot;Hobgoblin Servant(s)&quot; Merit or power published at this time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I forget if the familiar bond requires Spirit, or can be done with any ephemeral Arcana, but definitely needs a Mind and Fate component. </div> </div> </div>The normal Familiar spell is a Patterning effect using Spirit or substituting Death or Mind for the appropriate non-spirit invisible entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise, why not? Well I guess Rank vs Wyrd might be an issue, but I think you can divide by two and round up for a rough equivalency. </div> </div> </div>Main argument against that comes to mind is that hobs and Hedge ghosts are markedly more tied to the Hedge than ephemeral beings are to their respective otherworlds in a way that the Familiar Manifestation doesn't really help with, hobs tend to do things quid-pro-quo, and Hedge ghosts halving their effective Wyrd for all purposes outside the Hedge kind of plays merry havoc with the Rank limits on Familiar.<br /> <br /> In other words, it is probably worth considering what is actually meant by &quot;take a hobgoblin or a Hedge ghost as a Familiar&quot; to answer the question affirmatively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T16:08:35-07:00","id":1507792,"title":"","content":"Can <u>Temporal Summoning</u> (temporarily) revert a Rapt Soulstone to a normal Soulstone, assuming it was one at some point? The spell can't remove Supernatural transformations, which Rapture edges on being. The fact that the Rapt have different mechanics from standard Mages makes me think it wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T06:01:13-07:00","id":1507935,"title":"","content":"When using <u>Psychic Genesis</u> to create a Goetia, which conjunctive Arcana would be necessary to grant it a native Materialize Manifestation? Just Spirit, or would Death be acceptable? <u>Revenant</u> and the <u>Summon Goetia</u>'s Death Conjunctive effect makes me inclined the think Death works.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> &quot;Normal&quot; Exarchs have Ochema and Supernal Entities at their command. What would ephemeral servants of The Gate primarily be? Suborned Abyssal Entities? Corrupted Ochema? Nightmares beyond simple classification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T08:01:06-07:00","id":1507938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1507935#post1507935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using <u>Psychic Genesis</u> to create a Goetia, which conjunctive Arcana would be necessary to grant it a native Materialize Manifestation? Just Spirit, or would Death be acceptable? <u>Revenant</u> and the <u>Summon Goetia</u>'s Death Conjunctive effect makes me inclined the think Death works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Normal&quot; Exarchs have Ochema and Supernal Entities at their command. What would ephemeral servants of The Gate primarily be? Suborned Abyssal Entities? Corrupted Ochema? Nightmares beyond simple classification?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acamoth and Gulmoth do seem to fit, although I think the Gate would still reside in the Supernal if she's meant to be among Ascended beings, and I think for the most part his Ochemata would be conventional. [i]Possibly[i] they'd have some powers over Paradox similar to the Scelesti; I feel such a thing is not a given when the natural state of Ochemata equips them so much to not deal with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T04:28:56-07:00","id":1508524,"title":"","content":"I just noticed my version of the core (despite supposedly being post-errata) has the various Attribute/Skill boosting/lowering spells with different primary factors. Augment Mind and Befuddle are Potency-primary, while the rest (including Enhance/Gain Skill) are all Duration-primary. Which one's correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T05:54:37-07:00","id":1508527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508524#post1508524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed my version of the core (despite supposedly being post-errata) has the various Attribute/Skill boosting/lowering spells with different primary factors. Augment Mind and Befuddle are Potency-primary, while the rest (including Enhance/Gain Skill) are all Duration-primary. Which one's correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the function of those spells and the fact that only two of the six aren't listed as Duration-primary, I'd say it's Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:21:21-07:00","id":1508611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508524#post1508524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed my version of the core (despite supposedly being post-errata) has the various Attribute/Skill boosting/lowering spells with different primary factors. Augment Mind and Befuddle are Potency-primary, while the rest (including Enhance/Gain Skill) are all Duration-primary. Which one's correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the two with potency primary debuffs which would typically be withstood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:30:38-07:00","id":1508615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508611#post1508611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are the two with potency primary debuffs which would typically be withstood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, no. Both <u>Honing The Form</u> and <u>Degrading the Form</u> are Duration-Primary, as is <u>Gain Skill</u> and <u>Enhance Skill</u>. <u>Befuddle</u> and <u>Augment Mind</u>**, however, are Potency-Primary. My speculations as to why it is that way mostly don't make sense in the broader context of spells.<br /> <br /> * Physical Attribute boost and debuff, respectively<br /> ** Mental/Social Attribute debuff and booster, respectively","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:25:39-07:00","id":1508654,"title":"","content":"To what extent would high-level things from other splats know and use High Speech? Like mystically-inclined True Fae and Spirits would learn it just out of having the time and inclination, but if you try to make nWoD a coherent setting then wouldn't everyone be interested in the language that encodes(?) reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T12:04:08-07:00","id":1508663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508654#post1508654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent would high-level things from other splats know and use High Speech?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less as you please. Like, it says something about those beings in your setting that they know High Speech. By default though, there's no indication of it being used outside of Supernal-related beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like mystically-inclined True Fae and Spirits would learn it just out of having the time and inclination, but if you try to make nWoD a coherent setting then wouldn't everyone be interested in the language that encodes(?) reality? </div> </div> </div>Thing is, it's not a normal language you can just learn by copying. It's more an inherent ability tied to the Supernal.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T14:53:25-07:00","id":1508671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508654#post1508654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent would high-level things from other splats know and use High Speech? Like mystically-inclined True Fae and Spirits would learn it just out of having the time and inclination, but if you try to make nWoD a coherent setting then wouldn't everyone be interested in the language that encodes(?) reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Coherent? in an infinite mystery setting?<br /> <br /> 2) High Speech doesn't encode reality, it's an idea/tool for those whose main tool for encoding reality is through the Supernal. Archmaster equivalent entities don't need the same sort of access as the Awakened-their Titles and Influences affect the Phenomenal World just as surely (if not more so because of the limits of the Abyss) as any Archmaster.<br /> <br /> Rank 6 entities (outside of the Pangaeans, who aren't a major concern for most of the setting) may not be limited by the language and perspective of their respective splats to affect reality as they approach ascendancy-the lines between Spirit God Moon and Astral God Moon probably doesn't actually exist, and a True Fae exercising the full extent of their Title's consitituions is likely affecting change in the Supernal and Phenomenal as much as the domains of Arcadia- but they still do it by virtue of the powers, forms, and authorities of their paradigm. True Fae neither need nor want Arcana to reshape reality, Moon exerts themselves according to their rank, not their Gnosis, and the God-Machines affectation of the heavens is engineered under the grasp of it's mission statements, not any kind of Wisdom. This is one of those reasons the exploration and consumption of the Fallen World's Mysteries are valuable to the Awakened-it's ways of throttling the heavens that cannot be imagined by just the Awakened themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T15:51:10-07:00","id":1508676,"title":"","content":"Plus, High Speech is less a language, and more the <i>idea</i> of language, acting as a simple interface for beings connected to the Supernal to understand the Supernal. At least, that's how I've always understood it, based on how the books describe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". Kinda changes the point of the sentence. 04-17-2023, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T03:47:19-07:00","id":1508732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508663#post1508663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, it's not a normal language you can just learn by copying. It's more an inherent ability tied to the Supernal.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you can just learn it. It's a two dot Merit with the only prerequisite that the character isn't Awakened (since they already know how).<br /> <br /> The thing is, just knowing High Speech doesn't really do much. Outside of spellcasting, High Speech functions basically as a cipher; you could write (and speak short sentences) of it, as well as understand others who write or speak with High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:39:39-07:00","id":1509616,"title":"","content":"Is it ever explicitly stated what the silver ladder of the Silver Ladder's title actually refers to?<br /> <br /> Like, I originally assumed it meant that they want to create a second Celestial Ladder, (silver being a poetic way of saying second). But I've seen people assume it's just a straight reference to the Celestial Ladder, like it's a different name for it. <i>To The Strongest</i> has their progenitor Darshana use a ladder as a metaphor for spiritual hierarchy.<br /> <br /> It could well be all three at once, but I'm curious if there's ever an explicit statement that I've missed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:20:43-07:00","id":1509650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509616#post1509616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it ever explicitly stated what the silver ladder of the Silver Ladder's title actually refers to?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the hierarchy one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:48:27-07:00","id":1509659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509616#post1509616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it ever explicitly stated what the silver ladder of the Silver Ladder's title actually refers to?<br /> <br /> Like, I originally assumed it meant that they want to create a second Celestial Ladder, (silver being a poetic way of saying second). But I've seen people assume it's just a straight reference to the Celestial Ladder, like it's a different name for it. <i>To The Strongest</i> has their progenitor Darshana use a ladder as a metaphor for spiritual hierarchy.<br /> <br /> It could well be all three at once, but I'm curious if there's ever an explicit statement that I've missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fancy way of refering to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_chain_of_being\" target=\"_blank\">great chain of being</a> as organized by wizards interested in that sort of thing. We've even talked about<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964827#post964827\"> it</a>, and you even <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504442-what-stops-mages-from-killing-insert-hostile-supernatural-here-en-masse?p=1504650#post1504650\">went on about it</a> previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T01:23:28-07:00","id":1509695,"title":"","content":"Thank you, I honestly forgot. <hr />Wait, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> where in that thread did we talk about it? We talked about the hierarchy itself, but I can't see us discussing the name.<br /> <br /> Also, that's not the answer I was really looking for. By explicit, I was meaning the books themselves. Like, I wouldn't be surprised if the Silver Ladder of Being turns up in <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, but that post was six years old. It also doesn't expand on why it's a <i>silver</i> ladder specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 04-26-2023, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T02:45:18-07:00","id":1509700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509695#post1509695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, I honestly forgot. <hr />Wait, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> where in that thread did we talk about it? We talked about the hierarchy itself, but I can't see us discussing the name.<br /> <br /> Also, that's not the answer I was really looking for. By explicit, I was meaning the books themselves. Like, I wouldn't be surprised if the Silver Ladder of Being turns up in <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, but that post was six years old. It also doesn't expand on why it's a <i>silver</i> ladder specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-reading the Silver Ladder section (in 1e and 2e core books) i don't see anything explicit.<br /> <br /> That said, they are the one order in 1e who not only believe the Exarchs ascended using the Celestial Ladder, but also that this is still a good idea.<br /> <br /> On the other hand they seem to claim everyone (sleepers included) should find the right ring of the ladder for themselves. Which sounds very much like it is describing a caste system (and something the Seers could get on board with, so long as the Silver Ladder accept their place below the Seers on the Ladder).<br /> <br /> So, both metaphor and crushing model of social relations with sleepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T04:02:39-07:00","id":1509703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509700#post1509700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading the Silver Ladder section (in 1e and 2e core books) i don't see anything explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, they are the one order in 1e who not only believe the Exarchs ascended using the Celestial Ladder, but also that this is still a good idea. </div> </div> </div>I do wonder if it maybe changed during 2e development. Like, it being a reference to the Celestial Ladder makes sense when Atlantis is at the forefront, and re-reading the section on their hierarchy in the SL book, I don't think it even uses a ladder metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T05:58:30-07:00","id":1509707,"title":"","content":"Forcing someone to only speak what they believe is the truth would be... Mind? Prime? I'm assuming both are viable, but want to make sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:48:28-07:00","id":1509726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509695#post1509695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't expand on why it's a <i>silver</i> ladder specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I can get my books again I'd look for if there's any talk about the colour, but my first instinct is silver is just there to evoke the image of something with a pure and unbroken colour.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:50:19-07:00","id":1509728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509707#post1509707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forcing someone to only speak what they believe is the truth would be... Mind? Prime? I'm assuming both are viable, but want to make sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Mind can affect how people communicate and Prime has Truth under its purview.<br /> <br /> Although I think both are going to be limited on Sleepers, in the face of Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T16:57:30-07:00","id":1509796,"title":"","content":"Would <i>Create Ghost</i> allow one to make a flying Barghest mount ? If not, what would be another way to go about it ? The objective is to create a version of Bucephalus, the nightmare horse from <i>Curse of Strahd</i>. In short, a flying horse with the ability to use the Reach version of <i>Ghost Gate</i> to strand people in Twilight or deliver reinforcements. I imagine Spirit might make more sense, but its the trope image for Hellish Horse and has a very Ghost Rider style to it, so Death feels more stylistically appropriate.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"229\" height=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-26-2023, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:11:45-07:00","id":1509800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1509796#post1509796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <i>Create Ghost</i> allow one to make a flying Barghest mount ? If not, what would be another way to go about it ? The objective is to create a version of Bucephalus, the nightmare horse from <i>Curse of Strahd</i>. In short, a flying horse with the ability to use the Reach version of <i>Ghost Gate</i> to strand people in Twilight or deliver reinforcements. I imagine Spirit might make more sense, but its the trope image for Hellish Horse and has a very Ghost Rider style to it, so Death feels more stylistically appropriate.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"229\" height=\"250\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://db4sgowjqfwig.cloudfront.net/images/5363883/Bucephalus.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an easy &quot;Sure, go ahead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T08:02:08-07:00","id":1510360,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Word of Command</b>, when used with a relevant Arcana can activate other supernatural devices. Can you use the relevant Arcana (at higher level of course) to get the same result <i>without </i>Prime?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mind 4 + Fate 4 to activate a Token?</li> <li>Spirit 4 to activate a Werewolf Fetish?</li> </ol></li> <li>A complementary question is, can you use yourself as source for another supernatural fuel (Essence, Glamour) without Prime? Seems possible at least with Glamour to use a spell on yourself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Players Guide to the Contagion Chronicle p.13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The above spell can\u2019t remove Glamour from people without a Wyrd trait, but a Mind Patterning spell with conjunctional Fate can\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div></li> <li><b>IF </b>the answer to the previous question is &quot;Yes&quot; , could you activate a Token <b>only </b>with said Glamour, no spell needed? Bribe a Fetish with the generated Essence?</li> </ol><br /> I am thinking that some supernatural fuels can be produced with the right Arcana, and that should suffice to activate the relevant devices... But even if the power source on its own does not suffice for the activation, the fuel PLUS a Patterning spell ought to do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Clarity of the text 05-01-2023, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T10:56:57-07:00","id":1510377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1510360#post1510360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the relevant Arcana (at higher level of course) to get the same result <i>without </i>Prime?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mind 4 + Fate 4 to activate a Token?</li> <li>Spirit 4 to activate a Werewolf Fetish?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>If <i>Word of Command </i>is compelling at 1 dot, then I'd suggest ruling at 2 dots for the others. Like, that's the practice that's explicitly supposed to be a stronger version of compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T09:02:18-07:00","id":1510985,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy the Curse 2ed. pg 332</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Mummies and Awakened Magic</b></u><br /> For those with Mage: The Awakening, at-<br /> tempts to use the Fate or Time Arcana magic on<br /> an Arisen, except Knowing or Unveiling Practices,<br /> automatically fail. Mages have no innate aware-<br /> ness of this and still compile and roll their dice<br /> pool, but gain no effect for disallowed Practices<br /> regardless of the number of successes achieved.<br /> Additionally, the spellcaster automatically incurs<br /> Paradox dice equal to the highest Fate or Time<br /> Arcana used, even with permitted Practices. If<br /> the Paradox dice pool achieves success (or ex-<br /> ceptional success), the caster suffers the Abyssal<br /> Backlash Condition as the Judges in Duat take<br /> notice of the mage\u2019s meddling, as if they were an<br /> Annunaki in the Abyss. Similarly, magic affecting<br /> the Arisen\u2019s Memory also automatically fails, but<br /> such spells don\u2019t invoke additional Paradox or<br /> incur a backlash unless they also incorporate the<br /> Fate or Time Arcana.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can Legacy attainments by pass these restrictions and work as higher lever Fate/Time practices?</li> <li>Do Fate / Time attainments still cause Paradox?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T09:18:35-07:00","id":1510987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1510985#post1510985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan Legacy attainments by pass these restrictions and work as higher lever Fate/Time practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>They come from the mage's soul instead of the framework the Rite of Return imposed on the world and thus fail automatically as described in the very next paragraph of the sidebar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Fate / Time attainments still cause Paradox? </div> </div> </div>They aren't rolled, so no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:33:04-07:00","id":1510994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1510987#post1510987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They come from the mage's soul instead of the framework the Rite of Return imposed on the world and thus fail automatically as described in the very next paragraph of the sidebar.<br /> <br /> They aren't rolled, so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Can you give it a look at my post about supernatural fuel<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1510360#post1510360\"> about 4 messages before</a> and give you opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T18:23:20-07:00","id":1511574,"title":"","content":"A Pentacle character wants to have an Order tool that is either a ring or a <a href=\"https://www.sikhkaras.com/shop/engraved/engraved-aad-guru-nameh-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Kara</a> made of perfected materials.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If it is a <b>Mysterium </b>member, does it suffice that it has relevant writing in the tool (like the sample Kara has, the text has a very &quot;Sophia&quot; feel) ?</li> <li>Will a <b>Free Council </b>member cultural related order tool be enough to accept a Sikh Kara, even if the mage is not a Sikh themselves?</li> </ol>The question is not about dedicated tools, it is about how to make any of those items (ring, bracelet) function as an Order tool for either of those orders.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T01:26:24-07:00","id":1511590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511574#post1511574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Pentacle character wants to have an Order tool that is either a ring or a <a href=\"https://www.sikhkaras.com/shop/engraved/engraved-aad-guru-nameh-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Kara</a> made of perfected materials.[LIST=1][*]If it is a <b>Mysterium </b>member, does it suffice that it has relevant writing in the tool (like the sample Kara has, the text has a very &quot;Sophia&quot; feel) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ibeaumanior</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Will a <b>Free Council </b>member cultural related order tool be enough to accept a Sikh Kara, even if the mage is not a Sikh themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it would take the Techne Merit to be able to count such a thing, but that the Libertine who does so does not need to personally adhere to whatever practice they invoke. I wouldn't say that objects alone typically count as cultural tools, but looking at the significance and handling of the kara specifically I think it would suffice to carry and incorporate one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T02:03:50-07:00","id":1511594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511574#post1511574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a <b>Mysterium </b>member, does it suffice that it has relevant writing in the tool (like the sample Kara has, the text has a very &quot;Sophia&quot; feel) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>From quickly looking at it, a kara, (even a standard plain one) in itself actually sounds like an interesting take on a Mysterium tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:12:57-07:00","id":1511611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511594#post1511594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From quickly looking at it, a kara, (even a standard plain one) in itself actually sounds like an interesting take on a Mysterium tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I thought that knowledge had to be represented on the tool to count for the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511590#post1511590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it would take the Techne Merit to be able to count such a thing, but that the Libertine who does so does not need to personally adhere to whatever practice they invoke. I wouldn't say that objects alone typically count as cultural tools, but looking at the significance and handling of the kara specifically I think it would suffice to carry and incorporate one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would a ring or bracelet of any kind (Kara or not) inscribed with relevant mathematical / chemical formulae be representative enough for Free Council? The idea is to have a portable, discrete Order tool made of the Perfected Metal... Cups, Rods and Wands are too conspicuous; Coins are easy to lose, and Knives are alarming to any security forces. Bracelets and rings are always with you and hard to lose without being forcibly removed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought about Karas because they can count as weapons (Adamantine Arrow) and can be engraved with writing (Seers surely and <i>perhaps </i>Mysterium or Free Council). It does not seem to be a symbol of authority so Silver Ladder is out, but if I am mistaken please correct me.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-14-2023, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:37:22-07:00","id":1511627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511611#post1511611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? I thought that knowledge had to be represented on the tool to count for the Mysterium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what the Order Tools section says. However if you read the magical symbolism in their Order section, it adds:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond tomes and scribing tools, the Mysterium dedicates objets d\u2019art containing symbolic messages and imagery deliberately crafted by the artist, such as Masonic paintings or cave paintings. </div> </div> </div>I'd count the karas as an example of that. From what I gather, they're not meant to be practical, they're primarily symbolic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T19:20:40-07:00","id":1511955,"title":"","content":"Some Tool questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is a pen a sufficiently complex device to count as a Free Council tool?</li> <li>Can a pen count as a Rod?</li> <li>How much of a Magical Tool needs to be made of a Perfected Metal, to gain the Yantra and 9-again casting bonus? 100%?</li> <li>Does engraving a simple object (meaning no electronic or moving parts: bracelet, coin, ring, etc) with scientific and/or cultural paraphernalia suffice to count as an Order tool for Free Council? For an example look at these coins: <a href=\"https://www.jmbullion.com/2022-1-oz-tokelau-vivat-humanitas-gold-coin-proof-like/\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://www.jmbullion.com/2020-1-oz-tokelau-vivat-humanitas-silver-coin-proof-like/\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>.</li> </ol>Might have to post them in an independent thread. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-18-2023, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T19:58:24-07:00","id":1511959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511955#post1511955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Tool questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is a pen a sufficiently complex device to count as a Free Council tool?</li> <li>Can a pen count as a Rod?</li> <li>How much of an object needs to be made of a Perfected Metal, to gain the Yantra and 9-again casting bonus? 100%?</li> <li>Does engraving a simple object (meaning no electronic or moving parts: bracelet, coin, ring, etc) with scientific and/or cultural paraphernalia suffice to count as an Order tool for Free Council? For an example look at these coins: <a href=\"https://www.jmbullion.com/2022-1-oz-tokelau-vivat-humanitas-gold-coin-proof-like/\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://www.jmbullion.com/2020-1-oz-tokelau-vivat-humanitas-silver-coin-proof-like/\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>.</li> </ol>Might have to post them in an independent thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head, w/o cross-checking the books for hiccups:<br /> <br /> For the third question, I\u2019d say symbolism matters as always. A knife with a Siderite handle but a mundane iron blade lifts my eyebrow. A fountain pen with an Orichalcum nib and a steel body gets a pass. <br /> <br /> For all the other questions, I\u2019d say Yes\u2026 as long as both the player and character can spin and internalize the symbol-speak to justify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T01:26:12-07:00","id":1511984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1511955#post1511955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a pen a sufficiently complex device to count as a Free Council tool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. They're mechanical devices, if rather simple ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a pen count as a Rod? </div> </div> </div>I've used them as such before. Just find a fancy pen made of the right materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does engraving a simple object (meaning no electronic or moving parts: bracelet, coin, ring, etc) with scientific and/or cultural paraphernalia suffice to count as an Order tool for Free Council? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. It having some kind of motive power or mechanism of it's own seems pretty explicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T15:40:58-07:00","id":1512155,"title":"","content":"Moving from the Temenos to the Anima Mundi can grant an Arcane Beat; and moving from a region of the Anima Mundi to another can grant other beat, some questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you obtain multiple Arcane Beats from this process or it is a single category (deciphering the challenge) for the purposes of &quot;<i>You can only receive one Beat from a given category in a given scene</i>\u200b&quot;?</li> <li>How many regions for the Anima Mundi are for the purposes of the beat granting mechanic? I <i>think </i>it is: <b>Swath </b>OR <b>Spire</b>, <b>Dreaming Earth</b>, <b>Sidereal Wastes</b> AND <b>Ocean Ouroboros shore</b>. Is that right?</li> <li>Does the <b>Ecstatic Wind </b>apply while on the Ocean Ouroboros shores? (<u><i><b>Ignore this question, answered in the Core book already</b></i></u>)</li> <li>Non-Astral question: Can you forget a rote? (And recoup the experience spent on learning it)</li> <li>Non-Astral question: Can you forget a Praxis? (And recoup the experience spent on learning it, or get &quot;free&quot; XP from your free Gnosis granted Praxis)</li> </ol>Thanks.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Expanded the questions. Found the answer to 3. 05-20-2023, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:48:52-07:00","id":1512174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512155#post1512155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you obtain multiple Arcane Beats from this process or it is a single category (deciphering the challenge) for the purposes of &quot;<i>You can only receive one Beat from a given category in a given scene</i>\u200b&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going through multiple Astral challenges in a single scene to the degree of deciphering the symbolism or mystery of the challenge and unearthing hidden truth multiple times, something is going weird with your Storyteller system, because a scene is the time spent dealing with a single specific event \u2014 like, say, surmounting the challenge posed to you to cross into a new layer of the Astral.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many regions for the Anima Mundi are for the purposes of the beat granting mechanic? I <i>think </i>it is: <b>Swath </b>OR <b>Spire</b>, <b>Dreaming Earth</b>, <b>Sidereal Wastes</b> AND <b>Ocean Ouroboros shore</b>. Is that right? </div> </div> </div>Per Astral Realms, it's the Omphalos and then every region that changes the frequency with which the Ecstatic Wind hits, i.e. Oroboros isn't a separate layer but the Omphalos is. Switching from one of the two Anthropic Redoubts to the other also requires an ordeal, as does entering an Aeonic Citadel for the first time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the <b>Ecstatic Wind </b>apply while on the Ocean Ouroboros shores? </div> </div> </div>By default, the only parts of the Anima Mundi commonly safe from the Wind are the Aeonic Citadels, which run in normal time instead of the subjective time common to the Wastes that makes the Wind hit every turn, but given the relatively short list of things to do at Oroboros besides visit the Citadels I don't think much breaks either way if you do or don't check for the Wind every turn in that one zone of the Wastes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Non-Astral question: Can you forget a rote? (And recoup the experience spent on learning it) </div> </div> </div>In theory, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T08:39:37-07:00","id":1512214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512174#post1512174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going through multiple Astral challenges in a single scene to the degree of deciphering the symbolism or mystery of the challenge and unearthing hidden truth multiple times, something is going weird with your Storyteller system, because a scene is the time spent dealing with a single specific event \u2014 like, say, surmounting the challenge posed to you to cross into a new layer of the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, I was thinking in terms of chronological time, 1 Scene = 1 Hour. But if this is narrative time, and every time you deal with a specific event is a scene, then the Astral Adept merit becomes really valuable for daily (nightly?) XP farming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512174#post1512174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Astral Realms, it's the Omphalos and then every region that changes the frequency with which the Ecstatic Wind hits, i.e. Oroboros isn't a separate layer but the Omphalos is. Switching from one of the two Anthropic Redoubts to the other also requires an ordeal, as does entering an Aeonic Citadel for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in my example, <u>assuming you decipher the challenge every time</u>, you could get Arcane Beats from Temenos to Omphalos; from Swath OR Spire to Dreaming Earth, Dreaming Earth to Sidereal Wastes, for a total of 3 <i>potential</i> Arcane Beat per astral trip, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512174#post1512174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, the only parts of the Anima Mundi commonly safe from the Wind are the Aeonic Citadels, which run in normal time instead of the subjective time common to the Wastes that makes the Wind hit every turn, but given the relatively short list of things to do at Oroboros besides visit the Citadels I don't think much breaks either way if you do or don't check for the Wind every turn in that one zone of the Wastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just found the text that explains it on the core book &quot;<i>The Ecstatic Wind vanishes when a mage reaches the shores of Oroboros and the homes of the Aeons.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512174#post1512174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn theory, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you also forget a Praxis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T10:40:17-07:00","id":1512224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512214#post1512214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, I was thinking in terms of chronological time, 1 Scene = 1 Hour. But if this is narrative time, and every time you deal with a specific event is a scene, then the Astral Adept merit becomes really valuable for daily (nightly?) XP farming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astral Adept costs a Willpower, navigation takes time, and this is a storytelling game. Unless you're playing in an extremely sandboxy game where the ST is giving you lots of functional downtime to get stronger on your own, &quot;farming&quot; is generally going to be nonviable in actual play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in my example, <u>assuming you decipher the challenge every time</u>, you could get Arcane Beats from Temenos to Omphalos; from Swath OR Spire to Dreaming Earth, Dreaming Earth to Sidereal Wastes, for a total of 3 <i>potential</i> Arcane Beat per astral trip, right? </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that that's a &quot;may earn&quot; at the discretion of the Storyteller, and bearing in mind that that's time spent not getting other stuff done, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you also forget a Praxis? </div> </div> </div>The spells you've practiced so much you learn them by heart, that can become the basis of Legacy Attainments, that you get for free from gaining Gnosis?<br /> <br /> Nah.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T02:56:59-07:00","id":1512266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1512214#post1512214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, I was thinking in terms of chronological time, 1 Scene = 1 Hour. But if this is narrative time, and every time you deal with a specific event is a scene, then the Astral Adept merit becomes really valuable for daily (nightly?) XP farming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking at it, and nowhere does the core book state that 1 Scene = 1 hour. A scene is a scene, and sometimes it is useful to measure spell duration in hours rather than scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in my example, <u>assuming you decipher the challenge every time</u>, you could get Arcane Beats from Temenos to Omphalos; from Swath OR Spire to Dreaming Earth, Dreaming Earth to Sidereal Wastes, for a total of 3 <i>potential</i> Arcane Beat per astral trip, right? </div> </div> </div>Most arcane beats like this seem to be for the first time you discover a mysterious arcane piece of information (for example the first time your character enters the Underworld they earn a beat).<br /> <br /> I don't know that the Astral is that different (though i does arguably contain more arcane knowledge... It should be a good place to learn stuff).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you also forget a Praxis? </div> </div> </div>By RAW sanctity of merits doesn't apply to rotes or praxis, Afaik, you might be able to lose a rote by going to your Oneiros and removing/destroying the associated knowledge, but i wouldn't necessarily allow a refund of XP (if it was just being done for XP farming... ) As you are literally having your character reduce themselves...<br /> <br /> Praxises are different, they are based on the shape of your soul, and soul-shaping (aka legacy creation) is typically fairly one-way. Ripping off a part of your soul seems fairly dangerous and potentially Abyssal (ie if you removed a part to replace it with some kind of Abyssal entity) - given that it seems like a more extreme version of soul stone creation (where you reduce your potential Gnosis max, and performing an Act of Hubris - explicitly damaging your soul health) the downsides of more extreme soul damage to remove a praxis should be worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typos 05-21-2023, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T11:04:11-07:00","id":1513092,"title":"","content":"Varied questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc) use Supernatural (Clairvoyance, Telepathy, etc) merits?</li> <li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc)\u200b be simultaneously another type of minor supernatural creature (<b>Ghoul</b>, <b>Sadikh</b>, <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>, <b>Stigmatic</b>)?</li> <li>On Teamwork spells, how are Yantras applied? Only the main caster uses them or every participant can use their own?</li> </ol>Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T14:44:27-07:00","id":1513114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513092#post1513092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Varied questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc) use Supernatural (Clairvoyance, Telepathy, etc) merits?</li> <li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc)\u200b be simultaneously another type of minor supernatural creature (<b>Ghoul</b>, <b>Sadikh</b>, <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>, <b>Stigmatic</b>)?</li> <li>On Teamwork spells, how are Yantras applied? Only the main caster uses them or every participant can use their own?</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Likely not intended. They aren\u2019t \u2018pure human\u2019 enough to qualify.<br /> <br /> 2. Hmm. 2e is more permissive to cross-splat stuff, so Maybe Yes. Forgot the rulings on this. Even if you allow so, you\u2019ll want a compelling in-universe reason as to how the cross-template happened.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, keep it single-splat but make it resemble another; like a Proximus Dynasty whose Curse involves addiction to blood and relationships, and whose Blessings involve physical enhancements.<br /> <br /> 3. Gut instinct is \u2018only the main caster,\u2019 buuut I\u2019ll need to check that one later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T01:04:17-07:00","id":1513174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513114#post1513114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> 3. Gut instinct is \u2018only the main caster,\u2019 buuut I\u2019ll need to check that one later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure each full participant cast the spell full as normal, including for paradox risk.<br /> <br /> Which includes penalties and thus requires any yantra bonuses aswell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T11:00:01-07:00","id":1513212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513092#post1513092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Varied questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc) use Supernatural (Clairvoyance, Telepathy, etc) merits?</li> <li>Can servitors (<b>Hive Souls</b>, <b>Hollow Ones</b>) and Proximi (<b>Myrmidons</b>, etc)\u200b be simultaneously another type of minor supernatural creature (<b>Ghoul</b>, <b>Sadikh</b>, <b>Wolf-Blooded</b>, <b>Stigmatic</b>)?</li> <li>On Teamwork spells, how are Yantras applied? Only the main caster uses them or every participant can use their own?</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Probably not, they are not using the mortal baseline minor template.<br /> 2- Yes, there is a precedent in page 36 of <i>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</i> where a Proximi is simultaneously a Hero. Her Curse is that, once she loses her original soul, she must constantly digest souls or else suffer Soulessness. A mortal soul lasts a week, but she can also gain 3 months by digesting a Horror that was finished off by anyone else, plus she can impose Anathema. However, I would double check with the GM, since each minor template might come with strings attached. An example would be that a Proximi could become a psychic vampire, but now they need to manage the Curse and the need for Ephemera.<br /> 3- Page 119 of the core book states that each secondary actor rolls their own casting. Looking at the <i>Casting the Spell </i>section in page 115: &quot;<i>Once all dice penalties and bonuses are calculated, including any penalties from Paradox, the player rolls dice. A single success on the casting means the spell effect takes place.&quot;</i>, yantras apply bonuses, so I think its reasonable to allow them to be used individually. Thematically speaking, it makes sense that powerful magic requires the casters to complete different steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:54:40-07:00","id":1513338,"title":"","content":"Arcana and Attainment questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Present as Past</b> spell description references &quot;subjects&quot; so <u>if you had this as a Legacy Attainment</u>, every time you wanted the effect on Initiative and Doors do you need to cast over a target or will apply to everyone you interact with a single casting upon yourself?</li> <li><u>If both spells are a Legacy Attainment</u>, does the bonus to Doors from <b>Present a Past </b>and the one from <b>Prophecy</b> stack?</li> <li>&quot; <i>Aimed spells appear<br /> as bolts of energy or projections coming from the casting mage, as<br /> opposed to spells cast at sensory range which materialize at the point<br /> of the subject.</i>\u200b&quot;<br /> Are these visible to Sleepers or just to Mage Sight?</li> <li>Are Legacy Attainments that do not have reach assigned to Sensory range also visible projections?</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Additional questions and clarity on them. 05-30-2023, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T17:43:00-07:00","id":1513345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513338#post1513338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>&quot; <i>Aimed spells appear<br /> as bolts of energy or projections coming from the casting mage, as<br /> opposed to spells cast at sensory range which materialize at the point<br /> of the subject.</i>\u200b&quot;<br /> Are these visible to Sleepers or just to Mage Sight?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure this is elaborated in anywhere, but my best guess is:<br /> It depends on the kind of energy<br /> <br /> Forces using ligthening would be visible, space using a warp would be less obvious what it was but still visible, Mind using a Psychic assault would not be visible to entities which can not detect raw minds - so maybe goetia could see it? Similarly with Spirit and spirits, Death using darkness could blind a target but would be visible. But generally the subtle Arcana would be less obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T18:13:34-07:00","id":1513349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513338#post1513338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Aimed spells appear as bolts of energy or projections coming from the casting mage, as opposed to spells cast at sensory range which materialize at the point of the subject.</i>\u200b&quot;<br /> Are these visible to Sleepers or just to Mage Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're subject to Defense, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T04:14:58-07:00","id":1513371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513345#post1513345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forces using ligthening would be visible</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not throwing the effect of the spell though, you're throwing the spell itself.<br /> <br /> Don't think about fireballs. Think about casting Nightvision as an aimed spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:34:56-07:00","id":1513700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513371#post1513371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not throwing the effect of the spell though, you're throwing the spell itself.<br /> <br /> Don't think about fireballs. Think about casting Nightvision as an aimed spell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case then they would only be visible to those with Prime sight, as spells are not visible to the naked eye (only spell effects) unless someone has used Prime to make them appear (like how magic is depicted in Dr Strange?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T04:14:18-07:00","id":1514105,"title":"","content":"I remember from both old forum posts and conversations on the Discord server something about Astral (or maybe Supernal?) reflections / embodiments of the other splats, combined with a statement in Imperial Mysteries that each splat has its own advocates in the Supernal which may or may not be involved with Archmasters - stuff like Old Gods of the Thistle having ties to Changeling's True Fae and such. Is there any more information on entities like this, like, is there an Astral or Supernal god of vampires, etc.?<br /> <br /> I know that the Aeons embody each of the Arcana, I was wondering if there is similar logic at play for other splats even if they might not often interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T05:28:28-07:00","id":1514109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514105#post1514105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember from both old forum posts and conversations on the Discord server something about Astral (or maybe Supernal?) reflections / embodiments of the other splats, combined with a statement in Imperial Mysteries that each splat has its own advocates in the Supernal which may or may not be involved with Archmasters - stuff like Old Gods of the Thistle having ties to Changeling's True Fae and such. Is there any more information on entities like this, like, is there an Astral or Supernal god of vampires, etc.?<br /> <br /> I know that the Aeons embody each of the Arcana, I was wondering if there is similar logic at play for other splats even if they might not often interact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember a mention that the progenitor-Beasts roaming in the Mother\u2019s Land are Aeons of the Begotten\u2019s Families. That\u2019s the only thing I remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T14:21:10-07:00","id":1514129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1513700#post1513700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that was the case then they would only be visible to those with Prime sight, as spells are not visible to the naked eye (only spell effects) unless someone has used Prime to make them appear (like how magic is depicted in Dr Strange?)</div> </div> </div> </div>They are when you make them aimed. It's right there in the book.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, but how does that work?&quot; I don't know, use a bit of creativity to come up with some explanation. It needs to create some kind of visible medium to carry the imago or something.<br /> <br /> The point, as with the fact that it needs to have the area scale factor, is to afford an option for casting a spell at range without Reaching (as well as invoke some of the general iconography of the wizard throwing bolts of power) that comes with its own drawbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:10:08-07:00","id":1514209,"title":"","content":"I believe I am over-thinking this, but are attainments something that are gained automatically once a certain arcana level is reached (I think this is the rule) or do you have to buy them somehow? I only ask because of this text in the core book:<br /> <br /> As a mage\u2019s rating in an Arcanum increases, she gains access<br /> to new Attainments. <u>The Orders instruct their members on<br /> how to use these abilities, but the instruction bears more resemblance<br /> to conditioning in athletics or fundamental principles<br /> in mathematics</u>. (Pg 192)<br /> <br /> Is the underlined text just fluff?<br /> <br /> Thanks\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T13:17:49-07:00","id":1514234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514105#post1514105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember from both old forum posts and conversations on the Discord server something about Astral (or maybe Supernal?) reflections / embodiments of the other splats, combined with a statement in Imperial Mysteries that each splat has its own advocates in the Supernal which may or may not be involved with Archmasters - stuff like Old Gods of the Thistle having ties to Changeling's True Fae and such. Is there any more information on entities like this, like, is there an Astral or Supernal god of vampires, etc.?<br /> <br /> I know that the Aeons embody each of the Arcana, I was wondering if there is similar logic at play for other splats even if they might not often interact.</div> </div> </div> </div>My memory of imperial mysteries has it that there are Archmaster/God level entities which have a vested interest in the various beings that exist.<br /> <br /> So it could be the Crone worshipped by some vampires who would be pissed at an Archmaster for messing with what it is to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> No details were really given, as it was up to the storyteller in each case. Other possible entities include the God-Machine, rank 7-10 spirits and astral beings (the human concept of Death is represented by a rank 7 Goetia...) Cthonic gods of the Underworld. The Judges of Mummy? The True Fae, Exarchs, other gods of the Supernal. <br /> <br /> The most detailed info we have i suspect are about the Judges and Luna/various Werewolf entities. But i wouldn't say there are specific patrons required for each splatt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T10:01:06-07:00","id":1514714,"title":"","content":"Here's a question:<br /> <br /> Do players know that Paradox is about to be rolled and how many dice the Paradox pool has?<br /> Because I've got someone who is telling me otherwise and even the parts of the book they're quoting don't seem to support that in my opinion, but their argument is that every spell has the potential to be paradoxical and that ST rolls are secret. That the players on <b><i>every</i></b> spell can spend mana to mitigate it by removing dice they don't actually know exist from the pool and then choose to Contain or Release the paradox even if there won't actually be any Paradox rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:54:03-07:00","id":1514752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514714#post1514714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question:<br /> <br /> Do players know that Paradox is about to be rolled and how many dice the Paradox pool has?<br /> Because I've got someone who is telling me otherwise and even the parts of the book they're quoting don't seem to support that in my opinion, but their argument is that every spell has the potential to be paradoxical and that ST rolls are secret. That the players on <b><i>every</i></b> spell can spend mana to mitigate it by removing dice they don't actually know exist from the pool and then choose to Contain or Release the paradox even if there won't actually be any Paradox rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which piece of information about the paradox dice pool would be unknown to the player? They choose whether to over-reach and by how much. They know if they have inured the spell, or if they are using a dedicated magical tools.<br /> <br /> The only thing which might not be known is whether there are any sleeper witnesses, and even then it has to be obviously magical (so if, say, they are watching on a security camera, and it could be CGI then maybe it isn't too obvious...)<br /> <br /> So the maximum unknown is +1 dice in the paradox dice pool. Usually the player will definitely know they have paradox to mitigate, because usually the majority of the paradox dice pool is from overreaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 06-12-2023, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:17:36-07:00","id":1514766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514714#post1514714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question:<br /> <br /> Do players know that Paradox is about to be rolled and how many dice the Paradox pool has?<br /> Because I've got someone who is telling me otherwise and even the parts of the book they're quoting don't seem to support that in my opinion, but their argument is that every spell has the potential to be paradoxical and that ST rolls are secret. That the players on <b><i>every</i></b> spell can spend mana to mitigate it by removing dice they don't actually know exist from the pool and then choose to Contain or Release the paradox even if there won't actually be any Paradox rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut instinct says the player should know. That supports mages being cavalier with magic and Paradox risks, taunting danger until it bites them in the ass, which is the attitude I assoicate with Awakening\u2019s mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T22:42:51-07:00","id":1514797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514752#post1514752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So the maximum unknown is +1 dice in the paradox dice pool. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for every spell which risks paradox that you think is safe your paradox pool grows cumulatively.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking I get where this ST is coming from but I think the ruling in most cases is just going to be a tedious way of getting the players to waste mana.<br /> <br /> I think the ChoD philosophy in general is to share information with players and trust them to make dramatic choices anyway.<br /> <br /> If I was going to run a story where this was relevant I'd be up front and say like, 'while you are within the range of influence of this Gulmoth paradox works differently. You won't know how much it is and it's probably more than you think.' And then let the players be paranoid and/or figure out how it's working differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T00:22:45-07:00","id":1514806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514797#post1514797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for every spell which risks paradox that you think is safe your paradox pool grows cumulatively.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking I get where this ST is coming from but I think the ruling in most cases is just going to be a tedious way of getting the players to waste mana.<br /> <br /> I think the ChoD philosophy in general is to share information with players and trust them to make dramatic choices anyway.<br /> <br /> If I was going to run a story where this was relevant I'd be up front and say like, 'while you are within the range of influence of this Gulmoth paradox works differently. You won't know how much it is and it's probably more than you think.' And then let the players be paranoid and/or figure out how it's working differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, interesting, i think you should know when a spell has caused a paradox after the fact... But i suppose those doesn't necessarily apply if the ST rolls and fails to cause any paradox.<br /> <br /> I think i agree with the rest of your assessment. But also, i think it is unusual for you not to know there is a sleeper witness, so you should know how many spells have risked a paradox in each scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T15:24:56-07:00","id":1514886,"title":"","content":"As much as I agree with you all\u2014particularly the bit about how it just results in players wasting mana, and just seems unintuitive and not how the write up implies things to work\u2014I was sort of hoping for something more definitive, like a reference page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T18:05:17-07:00","id":1514903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514886#post1514886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I agree with you all\u2014particularly the bit about how it just results in players wasting mana, and just seems unintuitive and not how the write up implies things to work\u2014I was sort of hoping for something more definitive, like a reference page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I'm not aware of anything more definite. The few relevant lines in the Paradox section just confirm that it is a ST roll. Then it's a matter of interpretation as to whether the player choices to spend mana or contain/release imply some knowledge of the roll and pool.<br /> <br /> What you could do though is ask the ST where it is written that ST rolls are secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T23:17:31-07:00","id":1514923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1514903#post1514903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid I'm not aware of anything more definite. The few relevant lines in the Paradox section just confirm that it is a ST roll. Then it's a matter of interpretation as to whether the player choices to spend mana or contain/release imply some knowledge of the roll and pool.<br /> <br /> What you could do though is ask the ST where it is written that ST rolls are secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>ST rolls being secret are fine. You also can do things like not tell the player what a target's withstand is before they roll (especially since they could use a knowing spell to figure that out if that really wanted to...)<br /> <br /> But i would assume the ST says, ok I'm going to roll for paradox, you have overreached by 3, and at Gnosis 3 that means 6 dice, do you want to spend any mana to mitigate?<br /> <br /> And then the result is secret, and you get asked if you want to contain or release...<br /> <br /> So if you contain you don't know how much damage you risk taking (if any). This makes it more tense and the player has a meaningful decision to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:11:33-07:00","id":1514967,"title":"","content":"This is one of those cases of being made to argue a negative, I think. Dice rolls are visible by default; something would need to actively state that one should be made in secret. If that is not the case, then there's no cause to even assume it, rather than it being necessarily to tediously state &quot;just a reminded, this is an openly made roll&quot; every single time.<br /> <br /> This troublesome individual should be asked to point out any other instance where it's actively stated the roll is visible, or else everybody should be using their dice behind screens and nobody has any idea what any result is.<br /> <br /> And the choice on whether or not to contain a Paradox is made before the dice for it are rolled","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T11:03:47-07:00","id":1515154,"title":"","content":"Since I don\u2019t think it\u2019s been mentioned in 2e, would you say Chthonians still need the Spirit aspect to be summoned and stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T11:25:45-07:00","id":1515164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1515154#post1515154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I don\u2019t think it\u2019s been mentioned in 2e, would you say Chthonians still need the Spirit aspect to be summoned and stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Geist 2e, Chthonians don't have Manifestations, entering the living world as solid beings, and take an agg per turn away from an Underworld Gate.<br /> <br /> You'd probably need Spirit to give it Manifestations, similar to how goetia work, but otherwise I don't think Spirit is necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:47:04-07:00","id":1515369,"title":"","content":"Hypothetical situation:<br /> <br /> A Moros mage has had a spirit of hunger fetter itself to him. The mage has not noticed (there was a lot of magical things going on when the fettering thing happened, and the mage has no arcana that would easily detect a spirit).<br /> <br /> In trying to avoid an enemy, the Moros uses ghost gate w/ reach to shift directly into ghost twilight.<br /> <br /> The spirit in question has no influences or numina that affect ghost or deaths. Ghost twilight is normally as undetectable and untouchable to it as to a normal human.<br /> <br /> So, when the mage shifts to ghost twilight does the spirit just get pulled along? (if so, how does effectively being changed to a new type of ephemera affect the spirit?)<br /> Or does the spirit stay in normal state, with the fetter intact but the spirit no longer able to detect the mage (aside from perhaps his physical location)<br /> Or does the fetter manifistation just dissolve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T08:13:24-07:00","id":1515372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1515369#post1515369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypothetical situation:<br /> <br /> A Moros mage has had a spirit of hunger fetter itself to him. The mage has not noticed (there was a lot of magical things going on when the fettering thing happened, and the mage has no arcana that would easily detect a spirit).<br /> <br /> In trying to avoid an enemy, the Moros uses ghost gate w/ reach to shift directly into ghost twilight.<br /> <br /> The spirit in question has no influences or numina that affect ghost or deaths. Ghost twilight is normally as undetectable and untouchable to it as to a normal human.<br /> <br /> So, when the mage shifts to ghost twilight does the spirit just get pulled along? (if so, how does effectively being changed to a new type of ephemera affect the spirit?)<br /> Or does the spirit stay in normal state, with the fetter intact but the spirit no longer able to detect the mage (aside from perhaps his physical location)<br /> Or does the fetter manifistation just dissolve?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are still on the material world, just in a different frequency, so I suppose the second \u2014 the spirit stays in spirit-Twilight, still Fettered to the mage, but rightly confused since the latter just vanished from its perspective. It\u2019ll probably intuit what\u2019s going on, given some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T01:21:04-07:00","id":1515448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1515372#post1515372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both are still on the material world, just in a different frequency, so I suppose the second \u2014 the spirit stays in spirit-Twilight, still Fettered to the mage, but rightly confused since the latter just vanished from its perspective. It\u2019ll probably intuit what\u2019s going on, given some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may decide to unfetter if it thinks its fetter is gone and no longer useful... But it may just stick to it.<br /> <br /> If the mage used ghost gate to walk into twilight drsgging the spirit through too then that might be a different question.<br /> <br /> Infact I'll ask it. What happens if a spirit or other non-death twilight entity goes through a ghost gate? Are they valid target for the effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T01:52:55-07:00","id":1515449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1515448#post1515448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Infact I'll ask it. What happens if a spirit or other non-death twilight entity goes through a ghost gate? Are they valid target for the effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing invalidates the usual effect, as I see it. The spirit is phased into death-Twilight, and probably perplexed as hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T12:50:00-07:00","id":1515471,"title":"","content":"So, I\u2019m looking into making a ghost familiar, so I\u2019ve been reading Giest for a better understanding of Ghosts/the Underworld. Some things came to my attention, mostly the Memory trade, and Ghostly Merits. Basically, I\u2019m not sure how they interact with being a familiar. Can Familiars even have merits? Can the Ghost Familiar take the Reap Memory Numen, and use Memories as described in Giest? Can Memories be interacted with Mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:56:35-07:00","id":1515483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1515471#post1515471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I\u2019m looking into making a ghost familiar, so I\u2019ve been reading Giest for a better understanding of Ghosts/the Underworld. Some things came to my attention, mostly the Memory trade, and Ghostly Merits. Basically, I\u2019m not sure how they interact with being a familiar. Can Familiars even have merits? Can the Ghost Familiar take the Reap Memory Numen, and use Memories as described in Giest? Can Memories be interacted with Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merits are usually for player characters (and \u2018important\u2019 npcs); nothing precludes familiars from having those Merits iirc, but I\u2019d be inclined to just say \u201cThey do this and are like that\u201d rather than write something down. Unless, of course, you feel the Merits actually help with bookkeeping and mental shortcuts.<br /> <br /> Memories are similar, in that they\u2019re meant for player ghosts. Whose concept involves staving off the Underworld\u2019s pull\u2026 which iirc the Familiar Manifestation protects them from? Ghost familiars shouldn\u2019t need them, though I suppose they can still have the Numen.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think the Player\u2019s Guide to the Contagion Chronicles had rules for Memories, but if it lacks one, I\u2019d rule that it requires both Death and Mind. Similar to how Glamour requires both Fate and Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T16:19:13-07:00","id":1516923,"title":"","content":"If a ghost is given the ability to interact with the material via a Weaving of Death, then the target would be effectively Blinded from the attack's source. Would a werewolf's Wolf senses allow them to compensate for it, since all the sensory information is in Death Twilight ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T19:20:20-07:00","id":1516937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1516923#post1516923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a ghost is given the ability to interact with the material via a Weaving of Death, then the target would be effectively Blinded from the attack's source. Would a werewolf's Wolf senses allow them to compensate for it, since all the sensory information is in Death Twilight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly confused to the situation you're describing. First, I assume the ghost is trying to blind a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Is the ghost 'merely' given the ability to interact with the Material? Then it would be still in ghost-Twilight, thus unseen to werewolves regardless of wolf-senses. But this would mean that the ghost also needs to do something other than just covering up the woof's eyes with its own body, since it's invisible. Like trying to gouge the wolf's eyes out, or throwing sand or something.<br /> <br /> If the ghost is fully Materialized <b>or</b> the werewolf has access to ghost-Twilight (namely, the Barghest Facet of the Gift of Death), then the ghost could normally cover the werewolf's eyes to Blind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T21:30:55-07:00","id":1516943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1516937#post1516937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slightly confused to the situation you're describing. First, I assume the ghost is trying to blind a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Is the ghost 'merely' given the ability to interact with the Material? Then it would be still in ghost-Twilight, thus unseen to werewolves regardless of wolf-senses. But this would mean that the ghost also needs to do something other than just covering up the woof's eyes with its own body, since it's invisible. Like trying to gouge the wolf's eyes out, or throwing sand or something.<br /> <br /> If the ghost is fully Materialized <b>or</b> the werewolf has access to ghost-Twilight (namely, the Barghest Facet of the Gift of Death), then the ghost could normally cover the werewolf's eyes to Blind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah sorry, I explained that poorly. I meant in the sense that, if you cannot perceive the ghost in Twilight, then you would have a version of the Blind tilt related to its attacks. I was wondering if the Wolf senses would allow them to compensate for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T21:52:36-07:00","id":1516944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1516943#post1516943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah sorry, I explained that poorly. I meant in the sense that, if you cannot perceive the ghost in Twilight, then you would have a version of the Blind tilt related to its attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you do not. A Tilt is an effect applied to a character, not shorthand for any issue a character experiences that is not a Condition. You don't get the Blind Tilt for a different character being invisible to you, because everything other than that character is as visible to you as it would be normally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was wondering if the Wolf senses would allow them to compensate for it. </div> </div> </div>No. Wolf senses compensate for being deprived of your senses. The werewolf's eyes work just fine in this scenario, they're just in a scene with something that happens to be invisible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T05:21:23-07:00","id":1516963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1516943#post1516943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if the Wolf senses would allow them to compensate for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is happening in the fiction that is represented by the rules of werewolf senses being able to compensate in the event that they're blinded?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T02:13:55-07:00","id":1517044,"title":"","content":"I've railed a bit about <u>Telekinesis</u>' impracticality before, especially when it comes to trying to make it into an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1497622#post1497622\">Attainment</a>. <br /> <br /> How practical/kosher would it be to use a Deviant's Variation as an Attainment? For example, use Deviant!Telekinesis with a Magnitude equal to Forces for a Disciple Attainment of a TK Legacy.<br /> <br /> There are other Variations this could potentially work with too. Scars are also a consideration - if this model is acceptable, should Scars be brought over as well? Probably the same one for every Legacy member, in all likelihood...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T03:55:40-07:00","id":1517050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517044#post1517044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've railed a bit about <u>Telekinesis</u>' impracticality before, especially when it comes to trying to make it into an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1497622#post1497622\">Attainment</a>.<br /> <br /> How practical/kosher would it be to use a Deviant's Variation as an Attainment? For example, use Deviant!Telekinesis with a Magnitude equal to Forces for a Disciple Attainment of a TK Legacy.<br /> <br /> There are other Variations this could potentially work with too. Scars are also a consideration - if this model is acceptable, should Scars be brought over as well? Probably the same one for every Legacy member, in all likelihood...</div> </div> </div> </div>May end up <i>too</i> practical, considering how this way one single Attainment gives potential access to multiple spell-effects. Perhaps something like, give the D!Telekinesis as the <i>First</i> Attainment, but it 'grows' such that its Magnitude scales with the Attainment tier and not Forces dots? Of course, the 2nd-5th Attainments would need some minor extra boosts to prevent Legacy progression becoming boring.<br /> <br /> As for being kosher, well, Variations come from breaking the human soul, so it has interesting implications about the Legacy members' souls... It will be kin to those dubious Legacies that are more affliction than cultivation; the Unforgotten Scions, the Path of the Book, the Followers of the True Soul.<br /> <br /> As for Scars, mages being mages, they probably should run on Mental Scars (and thus Mental Scar Attributes). It's natural to see this as a Controlled Variation, so a Controlled Scar should go along with it. The Concentration Scar is the most obvious choice here then. Though given how mages can already develop novel Attainments, <i>any</i> Scar could suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T16:48:44-07:00","id":1517429,"title":"","content":"So Ghost Mages retain a measure of their powers, or rather have uniquely broad Influences and strange Numina. Would a Castoff retain some of its supernatural power? Like would a Castoff of an Artifact diverge from other Castoffs? If a Haunted Grimoire gets completely destroyed, along with it\u2019s associated entity, would that alter a resultant Castoff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T17:48:32-07:00","id":1517432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517429#post1517429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ghost Mages retain a measure of their powers, or rather have uniquely broad Influences and strange Numina. Would a Castoff retain some of its supernatural power? Like would a Castoff of an Artifact diverge from other Castoffs? If a Haunted Grimoire gets completely destroyed, along with it\u2019s associated entity, would that alter a resultant Castoff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the situations described are weird and rare enough to excuse the Storyteller introducing any thematic quirk.<br /> <br /> Looking at Geist 2e, Castoffs have 'all the Traits of the objects they were before becoming ghosts'. That's enough excuse for me to give them broad Influences and unique Numina like Ghost Mages (speaking of which, did we ever get the rules for 'real' Ghost Mages?)<br /> <br /> For the Haunted Grimoire; if it got <i>that</i> thoroughly destroyed, there's not much to hang on for the Castoff to be special... maybe it looks like a flimsy Deathmask, without the turn-to-Reaper part?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T18:20:03-07:00","id":1517434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517432#post1517432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(speaking of which, did we ever get the rules for 'real' Ghost Mages?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Not that I\u2019m aware of. If I remember right, the homebrew versions all basically say stuff like, the resulting Ghost gets Influence of the Arcana they knew in life, and Rotes/Praxises are converted into Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:06:28-07:00","id":1517458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517434#post1517434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not that I\u2019m aware of. If I remember right, the homebrew versions all basically say stuff like, the resulting Ghost gets Influence of the Arcana they knew in life, and Rotes/Praxises are converted into Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's conflating a couple of things.<br /> <br /> See, there are two types of ghost mage. One is just &quot;sometimes when mages die, they turn into ghosts same as everybody else does&quot;. I believe that was the one where Dave said that it would make sense for them to have an Influence based on their best Arcanum and some Numina structured after some or all of their rotes.<br /> <br /> The other kind of ghost mage is a form of lich (Tome of the Pentacle appears to have introduced the term &quot;Wight&quot; to differentiate them). Those are basically mages who transformed themselves into a kind of living ghost, and I believe they're supposed to retain their full Awakened powers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looking into it, not even Arcana and Rotes; regular ghosts of mages can have Influence and Numina based on their Praxes, and that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-08-2023, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:17:15-07:00","id":1517460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517458#post1517458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other kind of ghost mage is a form of lich (<b>Tome of the Pentacle</b> appears to have introduced the term &quot;<b>Wight</b>&quot; to differentiate them). Those are basically mages who transformed themselves into a kind of living ghost, and I believe they're supposed to retain their full Awakened powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphases mine.<br /> <br /> Ah, my lacking of that book is catching up with me! I suspect they look somewhat like Supernal entities, then. Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:55:38-07:00","id":1517464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517460#post1517460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, my lacking of that book is catching up with me!</div> </div> </div> </div>To not give a misleading impression, when I say &quot;appears to&quot;, I mean that the book mentions them all of twice in the history section*, in terms where I'm not entirely clear if it's the terminology for ghost mage liches on the whole or more for their specific situation.<br /> <br /> I think there's supposed to be a point that your typical Wight has to deal with needing Anchors for sustenance as well.<br /> <br /> * One is the mage who revealed the dark secrets of the Tremere to the Orders, resulting in their expulsion from the Diamond; her pursuit of power led her down a similar path to their Captivity, resulting in experiments with a Strix that led to her own death and being remade into a ghost mage who can function without Anchors by drinking the souls of other mages. The others are a group of Neolithic mages who rendered themselves immortal to engage in an almost permanent state of Astral travelling of the furthest reaches of the Anima Mundi, believing that a way to escape the Fallen World could be found in the night sky; they periodically return to their bodies to make astronomical adjustments and renew their sustaining spells, and after more than six thousand years in this state are quite insane (Spanish mystagogues place great value in attempting to interview them when they return).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect they look somewhat like Supernal entities, then. Makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that they have Arcana and probably a Ban and Bane I suppose, but I think most of the relevant distinguishing details will differ, and doubt they'd have unlimited Reach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T16:08:06-07:00","id":1517718,"title":"","content":"How much Paradox-free Reach is an Imbued Item supposed to have? As much as the creator had at the time of Imbuing? Only one? Something else?<br /> <br /> Specifically, page 67 of Signs of Sorcery mentions that it should be treated as a Mage, which is casting the spell on behalf of the user. Which still leaves the question of how much Paradox-free Reach it has. By default it only has a dice pool of ([Spell's Arcanum Dots] + [User's Gnosis]), which implies that it only has the standard one PFR you get from meeting the spell's Arcanum rating.<br /> <br /> (All that being said, you can obviously work around this by including one or all of Everywhere/Permanence/Time In A Bottle, but that requires a crafter with more high-level Arcanum.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T17:40:01-07:00","id":1517722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517718#post1517718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Paradox-free Reach is an Imbued Item supposed to have? As much as the creator had at the time of Imbuing? Only one? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>My read is it gets free reach based on the Arcanum rating of the Imbuer at the time of imbument, but has default factors and gives dice equal to the dot rating of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T00:56:48-07:00","id":1517743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517718#post1517718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Paradox-free Reach is an Imbued Item supposed to have? As much as the creator had at the time of Imbuing? Only one? Something else?<br /> <br /> Specifically, page 67 of Signs of Sorcery mentions that it should be treated as a Mage, which is casting the spell on behalf of the user. Which still leaves the question of how much Paradox-free Reach it has. By default it only has a dice pool of ([Spell's Arcanum Dots] + [User's Gnosis]), which implies that it only has the standard one PFR you get from meeting the spell's Arcanum rating.<br /> <br /> (All that being said, you can obviously work around this by including one or all of Everywhere/Permanence/Time In A Bottle, but that requires a crafter with more high-level Arcanum.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is based on how much Arcana rating you decide to Imbue.<br /> The minimum rating is that of the spell imbued, but you can decide to imbue more if your actual rating is higher.<br /> Of course this would cost more Mana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T06:23:51-07:00","id":1517757,"title":"","content":"Signs of Sorcery states under &quot;Reach&quot; that the base Reach of an Imbued Item is set by the creator, always defaulting to the same Advanced Factors and spell Reach options, and says that the item entails Paradox risk if the imbued spell exceeds the user's free Reach. An item creator can provide the option for flexible Reach, but this only allows the item's user to reduce the amount of Reach used by the spell, not increase it.<br /> <br /> Hence, if an Initiate in an Arcanum imbues an item with a spell of that Arcanum, they have the option of giving it advanced factors in everything and all the extra widgets, which will mean the item entails a lot of Paradox no matter who uses it. If the creator opts to provide the option (which makes the process of creating it require double successes), a user can elect to reduce the factors and remove the extra spell effects. If the creator opts to only stick to their free Reach, the imbued item cannot use additional advanced factors or spell effects at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T07:22:34-07:00","id":1517764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517757#post1517757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and says that the item entails Paradox risk if the imbued spell exceeds the <b>user's</b> free Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not say this. If this were true then an imbued item of a spell exceeding the user's dots would always risk Paradox, which it does not.<br /> <br /> You are misreading the flexible reach blurb.<br /> <br /> It also specifically says that removing factors via flexible reach does <i>not</i> reduce Paradox risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T07:29:08-07:00","id":1517766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1517764#post1517764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does not say this. If this were true then an imbued item of a spell exceeding the user's dots would always risk Paradox, which it does not.<br /> <br /> You are misreading the flexible reach blurb.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I misapplied one word in a post that has to navigate a ton of jargon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also specifically says that removing factors via flexible reach does <i>not</i> reduce Paradox risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing, that was a line that I overlooked when reviewing the Signs of Sorcery rules, but it didn't end up mattering because my post didn't actually mention the prospect of reducing Paradox risk at all.<br /> <br /> So the only inaccuracy in my post was mixing up &quot;user&quot; with &quot;creator&quot;, once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T08:29:46-07:00","id":1518036,"title":"","content":"Assuming you have a way to enter the Astral (Demesne, 5 dot Hallow, Astral Adept merit), and you spend your night there instead of sleeping:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you actually wake up rested?</li> <li>Do you recover a Willpower point?</li> <li>Can you choose to &quot;wake up&quot; (leave the Astral) after a specific number of real-time hours? (or is there any way to track real time, so you can start the Astral departure process)</li> </ol>Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:04:12-07:00","id":1518048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518036#post1518036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you have a way to enter the Astral (Demesne, 5 dot Hallow, Astral Adept merit), and you spend your night there instead of sleeping:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you actually wake up rested?</li> <li>Do you recover a Willpower point?</li> <li>Can you choose to &quot;wake up&quot; (leave the Astral) after a specific number of real-time hours? (or is there any way to track real time, so you can start the Astral departure process)</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li> If the entire time is spent in your own Oneiros (likewise your own dream). Otherwise &quot;no.&quot;</li> <li> This is the mechanical representation of being well-rested, so see above.</li> <li> Yes.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T10:04:55-07:00","id":1518049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518036#post1518036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you have a way to enter the Astral (Demesne, 5 dot Hallow, Astral Adept merit), and you spend your night there instead of sleeping:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you actually wake up rested?</li> <li>Do you recover a Willpower point?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>These are mechanically the same question, and the answer is no, because you're not sleeping, much less resting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Can you choose to &quot;wake up&quot; (leave the Astral) after a specific number of real-time hours? (or is there any way to track real time, so you can start the Astral departure process) </div> </div> </div>The time that passes in the Oneiros is however much time you experienced subjectively regardless of how much time passed in the real world, and the Sidereal Wastes' reduction of everything to actions (and need to make use of the right shortcuts to avoid actually experiencing the amounts of time involved for physically traveling astronomical distances) plays havoc with assumptions of outside duration, but between their proximity to collective humanity and the world it experiences and the fact that Beast doesn't make any special statements about the passage of time in the Primordial Dream I think it's safe to say an hour in the Temenos, the Dreamtime, and the Anthropic Redoubts is generally the same as an hour in the physical world.<br /> <br /> You could probably rig a spell to let you keep track of the outside time despite any differentials through combining the same principles as One Mind, Two Thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T03:09:17-07:00","id":1518138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518036#post1518036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you have a way to enter the Astral (Demesne, 5 dot Hallow, Astral Adept merit), and you spend your night there instead of sleeping:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you actually wake up rested?</li> <li>Do you recover a Willpower point?</li> <li>Can you choose to &quot;wake up&quot; (leave the Astral) after a specific number of real-time hours? (or is there any way to track real time, so you can start the Astral departure process)</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>One note: 5-dot Hallow was a requirement in 1st Ed. The rules now require a N dot Hallow, along with absorbing and spending (6 - N) mana from the hallow.<br /> <br /> So it may take longer to get to the astral from a weaker Hallow, but you can still do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T21:15:53-07:00","id":1518165,"title":"","content":"I always forget, what impact does an Astral Entity have when it enters a person's Onieros? It isn't causing a possession at that point, right? Just causing the host to exhibit behaviors in line with the entity's nature, much like a Spirit using the Urged Manifestation?<br /> <br /> Unrelated, does a Baali retain the effects of the Elder Diadem if they flip back to Wisdom? Obviously the Diadem has few benefits without Joining, but if they fall again will they need to renegotiate with The Old Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-17-2023, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T05:03:07-07:00","id":1518174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518165#post1518165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always forget, what impact does an Astral Entity have when it enters a person's Onieros? It isn't causing a possession at that point, right? Just causing the host to exhibit behaviors in line with the entity's nature, much like a Spirit using the Urged Manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if it's not a native part of the Oneiros, just being present in somebody's Oneiros doesn't affect a person's waking nature, regardless of the origins of the intruder. The way it was presented in the original Astral Realms book, Oneiros changes that have effects on a person's real psychology need to be things that engage with the native aspects of the Oneiros in a way that build some form of persistent change.<br /> <br /> The relationship between the Oneiros and waking mind is fairly subtle, there's no Inside Out style control panel in there from which you can puppet them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T13:23:56-07:00","id":1518196,"title":"","content":"Is a museum full of fossils close enough to a graveyard to have a associated Avernian Gate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T13:53:22-07:00","id":1518201,"title":"","content":"If the exhibit has been there a while, I'd allow it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T13:56:51-07:00","id":1518202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518196#post1518196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a museum full of fossils close enough to a graveyard to have a associated Avernian Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T17:33:28-07:00","id":1518206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518196#post1518196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a museum full of fossils close enough to a graveyard to have a associated Avernian Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a place of Death? Because the Resonance of Death \u2014 &quot;this is a place where a lot of death has occurred and/or been been thought about&quot; \u2014 is the distinguishing factor moreso than &quot;are there the remains of living creatures kept here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Fossils being many many thousands of years past the point of being actual dead matter, it would have to go to the judges whether the fossils are enough to shift a museum's vibe toward the deathly. Some of the mineralized skulls and bones might put visitors and staff in the right frame of mind, but while fossils are likely to make solid material for Moros Path Tools, petrified wood has been a material for the Obrimos for ages.<br /> <br /> Symbols are tricky, but it's important to remember that &quot;Avernian Gates appear in places with a Resonance of Death&quot; is a fact with narrative weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T03:59:40-07:00","id":1518233,"title":"","content":"Unless Geist describes Resonance of Death for graveyards specifically in terms of being a place where it's thought about, I'd even wonder if it shouldn't be about somewhere heavily invested with the <i>ritual</i> of death. A graveyard accumulates the qualities that lead to the formation of a passage to the Underworld because, well, they're where people conduct the rites of quite literally committing a deceased person to their next destination. The creation of the gate is the literal expression of what the symbolic and social function of the graveyard is.<br /> <br /> A museum has none of that, and is arguably contrary to it; it's taking remains and keeping them in a context of preservation, removed from the association of the vessel of the dead that must be committed to a final resting place and into being mere objects for study and observation. There's no passage to the next life innate to a museum, just a superficial association. You might as well say that a Halloween supply store can become the foundation for an Avernian Gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T19:56:19-07:00","id":1518291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518233#post1518233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Geist describes Resonance of Death for graveyards specifically in terms of being a place where it's thought about, I'd even wonder if it shouldn't be about somewhere heavily invested with the ritual of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should clarify: &quot;has been thought about&quot; is me shorthanding &quot;not a lot of people die in graveyards or morgues, but they have a Resonance of Death just as surely as a battlefield or a hospice does&quot; \u2014 that's &quot;a Resonance of Death makes observers inclined to think of it as a place of Death,&quot; not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Geist's bullet-point list of the continuum of Underworld areas describes the cenotes/low places in Twilight around an Avernian Gate as &quot;keenly attuned to the energies of death.&quot; The Persephone's Return Ceremony, which creates or re-establishes an Avernian Gate, does so from the living world through symbolism associated with death, grief, and mourning, which are also the components to the less codified rituals used to open an existing Gate from the living side (explicitly doing so through the leveraging of things that accompany death if not the significant presence of actual death).<br /> <br /> Geist's explanation for how ghosts are sustained links grief and mourning to the sensation of loss experienced by the living with relation to the things whose destruction formed the ghost \u2014 &quot;the instinctive expectation for something to be present while knowing that it won't be&quot; \u2014 and describes Avernian Gates as standing in &quot;every place associated with death: sites stained by murders or disease, quiet, lonely places, as well as every graveyard, morgue, crematorium, and even pet cemetery in the world\u200b&quot;; &quot;anywhere that death has marked as its own&quot; is another way it's worded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T00:40:26-07:00","id":1518300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518174#post1518174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if it's not a native part of the Oneiros, just being present in somebody's Oneiros doesn't affect a person's waking nature, regardless of the origins of the intruder. The way it was presented in the original Astral Realms book, Oneiros changes that have effects on a person's real psychology need to be things that engage with the native aspects of the Oneiros in a way that build some form of persistent change.<br /> <br /> The relationship between the Oneiros and waking mind is fairly subtle, there's no Inside Out style control panel in there from which you can puppet them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Isator is right, but I would caveat that once in an Oneiros an entity can definitely affect the way that person's mind works, it is just usually very slowly and subtly that any changes will be felt.<br /> <br /> The dream actors and daimon might react negatively and try to undo those changes, so you might he able to subtly help by engaging with scenes and helping resolve them positively, but if you try to make dramatic shifts without the interest of the person in mind, then you are more likely to be attacked and either kicked out/destroyed or at least walled off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518165#post1518165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always forget, what impact does an Astral Entity have when it enters a person's Onieros? It isn't causing a possession at that point, right? Just causing the host to exhibit behaviors in line with the entity's nature, much like a Spirit using the Urged Manifestation?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the time to become integrated would likely end up more akin to the urged condition, but again, more subtle - because there would be no way beyond actually going into the Onerios for someone to find out what changed... Also integration might be a two way thing, where the process changes the astral entity to fit in too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T06:21:43-07:00","id":1518305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518291#post1518291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should clarify: &quot;has been thought about&quot; is me shorthanding &quot;not a lot of people die in graveyards or morgues, but they have a Resonance of Death just as surely as a battlefield or a hospice does&quot; \u2014 that's &quot;a Resonance of Death makes observers inclined to think of it as a place of Death,&quot; not the other way around.<br /> <br /> Geist's bullet-point list of the continuum of Underworld areas describes the cenotes/low places in Twilight around an Avernian Gate as &quot;keenly attuned to the energies of death.&quot; The Persephone's Return Ceremony, which creates or re-establishes an Avernian Gate, does so from the living world through symbolism associated with death, grief, and mourning, which are also the components to the less codified rituals used to open an existing Gate from the living side (explicitly doing so through the leveraging of things that accompany death if not the significant presence of actual death).<br /> <br /> Geist's explanation for how ghosts are sustained links grief and mourning to the sensation of loss experienced by the living with relation to the things whose destruction formed the ghost \u2014 &quot;the instinctive expectation for something to be present while knowing that it won't be&quot; \u2014 and describes Avernian Gates as standing in &quot;every place associated with death: sites stained by murders or disease, quiet, lonely places, as well as every graveyard, morgue, crematorium, and even pet cemetery in the world\u200b&quot;; &quot;anywhere that death has marked as its own&quot; is another way it's worded.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly sounds like it would exclude any museum that isn't specifically commemorating some event of noteworthy death.<br /> <br /> Certainly, nobody expects dinosaurs to be around.<br /> <br /> I think even in those cases where a museum is carrying the remains of actual humans, it's done in a context significantly removed from that funereal sense; an ancient mummy or bog body doesn't tend to elicit feelings of loss or mourning, just a general fascination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:34:40-07:00","id":1518381,"title":"","content":"Assuming you had ink and a willing subject, what would a spell to make tattoos look like? Life+Matter? Ruling or Weaving?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T17:02:50-07:00","id":1518392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518381#post1518381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you had ink and a willing subject, what would a spell to make tattoos look like? Life+Matter? Ruling or Weaving?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Shaping alone could be enough to make the ink stick on someone\u2019s skin, without the scars. So Matter 2 alone. Maybe with some Reach, since this isn\u2019t what Shaping\u2019s normally assumed to do.<br /> <br /> If you just want the tattooed looks, Mutable Mask could do it without any ink. So Life 2 alone.<br /> <br /> With both Matter 2 and Life 2, \u2018real\u2019 tattooing should be more than possible. (I\u2019m trying to justify even lower Arcana requirements, but it\u2019s not working lol)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T18:09:10-07:00","id":1518468,"title":"","content":"If you choose to have your familiar fettered in an animal or object, can it return to Twilight state or only if the fetter is destroyed?<br /> <br /> Also can they use any Influence or Numina while fettered? The Fettered manifestation implies they can\u2019t at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T18:22:15-07:00","id":1518469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518468#post1518468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you choose to have your familiar fettered in an animal or object, can it return to Twilight state or only if the fetter is destroyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have the Unfetter Manifestation they can remove or suppress the Fettered Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also can they use any Influence or Numina while fettered? The Fettered manifestation implies they can\u2019t at all. </div> </div> </div>It directly states that they can't use Numina or Influences on targets other than the Fetter; the tradeoff is that they pay one less Essence to use their Influences on their Fetter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T18:36:23-07:00","id":1518470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518469#post1518469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have the Unfetter Manifestation they can remove or suppress the Fettered Condition.<br /> <br /> It directly states that they can't use Numina or Influences on targets other than the Fetter; the tradeoff is that they pay one less Essence to use their Influences on their Fetter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a fettered Goetia familiar is kinda borked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T19:23:37-07:00","id":1518473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518470#post1518470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a fettered Goetia familiar is kinda borked</div> </div> </div> </div>A Fettered Goetia Familiar has presumably been put in that state for a reason, and can have the Manifestation removed through the usual means of removing any Manifestation Condition, and in the meantime it can pretty much constantly Strengthen its Fetter for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T21:09:19-07:00","id":1518480,"title":"","content":"The Genius Perfected Adepts in Tome of the Pentacle, their Initiate Attainment replicates <u>Web Of Life</u> keyed to human life*. The normal spell can be fine-tuned to include or exclude whatever categories of living entity the caster knows, but how do other Supernaturals register as humans for the spell or the Attainment? Vampires -and maybe Sin Eaters?- probably don't show up (which is good for IDing them), but does a werewolf? Does an Uratha only register as human while in human form, or not even then? Does a Promethean count? A Demon in Cover probably does, or at least provokes a Clash. Changelings <i>should</i> register fine, I think?<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">unrelated, why does their Attainment bother with specifying Potency? <u>Web of Life</u> doesn't use Potency at all. If you're gonna allocate those free jumps, move it into Scale. Otherwise, you may as well not specify. The Attainment works fine as-is -and is infinitely better/more functional than the Night Horrors version- it's just oddly presented.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-22-2023, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T23:46:20-07:00","id":1518485,"title":"","content":"I believe a Vampire under the Blush of Life would show up. Werewolves in human form would count, Mages would count, Promethean pre New Dawn wouldn\u2019t count. Changeling is\u2026hard. I\u2019d argue no. Beasts would, Demons in Cover would, Bound would, Mummies probably get a weird result like Time spells. Deviant is worse than Changeling, but I\u2019d argue no for most cases. <br /> <br /> So I used for my tests two qualifications: Is it alive, and is it Human? I\u2019m also giving a bit of leeway in either direction due to theme.<br /> <br /> My case for Vampires is that they are fully alive under the Blush of Life last I checked. I think they would also count as a Human too, but that\u2019s a point I can see people having a different perspective. I think it\u2019s fitting that a Vampire can be human, if they want, but it\u2019s temporary, comes a definite cost to those around them, and doesn\u2019t truly counteract any of the downsides of being a Vampire. But I can definitely see room to quibble.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are truly Human while in human form. I\u2019d argue any other form wouldn\u2019t register.<br /> <br /> Mages are Human and Alive in general, so easy yes.<br /> <br /> Prometheans aren\u2019t human, and arguably not alive, so easy no.<br /> <br /> Changeling are scarred by thorn and nightmare. They never come back from Arcadia unchanged. They are alive, but I think they wouldn\u2019t be human to a Supernal understanding. So hesitant no.<br /> <br /> Demons in Cover are Human as far as the Supernal is concerned. Unless they are in cover as a chair or a cat or a vampire or something, but Cover genuinely turns them into the thing they pose as.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters are both alive and Human, them also being a ghost and having a second ghost a soul doesn\u2019t change that. So they registered.<br /> <br /> Mummies are both alive and dead. As I understand, they are like if every moment of their Life and Death are compressed into one moment. So, yes, I think they count? Would also count as a corpse, if using Death.<br /> <br /> Beasts are alive and Human. Easy yes.<br /> <br /> Deviant\u2019s whole thing is being changed to something other than human against your will, so for thematic purposes I\u2019d say no\u2026but the Remade have a tendency to not fit neatly into boxes. Depends on the Deviant, and the what the Storyteller is using them for narratively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T02:41:23-07:00","id":1518503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518485#post1518485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons in Cover are Human as far as the Supernal is concerned. Unless they are in cover as a chair or a cat or a vampire or something, but Cover genuinely turns them into the thing they pose as.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters are both alive and Human, them also being a ghost and having a second ghost a soul doesn\u2019t change that. So they registered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the bound were dead.<br /> <br /> And that a Demon would have to roll a Spoof check (not a clash of Wills) to pass as human... So a demon whose cover was falling apart would more easily fail the spoof and show up as not human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T06:16:51-07:00","id":1518519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518468#post1518468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you choose to have your familiar fettered in an animal or object, can it return to Twilight state or only if the fetter is destroyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, the entity is still in Twilight while it's fettered.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518503#post1518503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the bound were dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely yes, in a way. But they're also very much biologically alive (moreso than vampires under Blush of Life). So if you're just asking if they're alive or if they're dead, you'd get a yes on both questions. Unless the question is specific enough. If you ask &quot;are they metaphysically alive&quot; or &quot;biologically dead&quot;, then the answer instead becomes no.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for different splats registering as human, it really depends on how you define human when you ask the question.<br /> If by &quot;human&quot; you only mean Sleepers/Sleepwalkers, then all splats (including mages) would fail. From the perspective of a mage, I'm pretty sure they'd also include themselves in that definition, being the splat closest to being humans (even having souls that are mutually compatible with each other).<br /> <br /> But if you instead mean biologically human, then mages, vampires (if they successfully pass for alive), werewolves in hishu, Bound (again, if they successfully pass for alive), beasts, mummies, and certain deviants would definitely pass. Some (probably most) deviants, the vast majority of changelings, werewolves outside hishu, beasts merged with their horrors, etc, would not pass as human in this case.<br /> <br /> And regardless of how you define human, demons would certainly not pass (never having been human in the first place, and certainly not biologically human), unless they successfully Spoof the Attainment. It's exactly for this kind of situation the Spoof rule exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:22:34-07:00","id":1518532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518519#post1518519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~snip~<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree re: Deviants. The vast majority would read as human, only the minority that were not created from humans would register as non-human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:39:25-07:00","id":1518536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518519#post1518519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to clarify, the entity is still in Twilight while it's fettered.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Definitely yes, in a way. But they're also very much biologically alive (moreso than vampires under Blush of Life). So if you're just asking if they're alive or if they're dead, you'd get a yes on both questions. Unless the question is specific enough. If you ask &quot;are they metaphysically alive&quot; or &quot;biologically dead&quot;, then the answer instead becomes no.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for different splats registering as human, it really depends on how you define human when you ask the question.<br /> If by &quot;human&quot; you only mean Sleepers/Sleepwalkers, then all splats (including mages) would fail. From the perspective of a mage, I'm pretty sure they'd also include themselves in that definition, being the splat closest to being humans (even having souls that are mutually compatible with each other).<br /> <br /> But if you instead mean biologically human, then mages, vampires (if they successfully pass for alive), werewolves in hishu, Bound (again, if they successfully pass for alive), beasts, mummies, and certain deviants would definitely pass. Some (probably most) deviants, the vast majority of changelings, werewolves outside hishu, beasts merged with their horrors, etc, would not pass as human in this case.<br /> <br /> And regardless of how you define human, demons would certainly not pass (never having been human in the first place, and certainly not biologically human), unless they successfully Spoof the Attainment. It's exactly for this kind of situation the Spoof rule exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that for Demons, i think of it like a grey area, like a low cover (1-3) rated cover has a pretty poor chance of passing the spoof check. While a high cover (?7-10?) Is almost certain to pass and always register as human...<br /> <br /> With a Changeling, likewise, i would have expected Beasts and Elementals to register as not human; Ogres, Darklings and Wizened more human than that, and Fairest the most human.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the Life arcanum alone, how inhuman they are depends on how they were changed by their durance.<br /> <br /> They won't count as fully human, but i think the life arcanum is looking at their biology only (rather than their mental humanness or their soul...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T10:04:16-07:00","id":1518541,"title":"","content":"I think a thing is human if it doesn't have anything like a Ban and/or Bane, or some kind of profound alteration to the function of its biology.<br /> <br /> If it has something like an explicit innate stealth power that can Clash against something trying to register it than fair enough, but Blush of Life won't change a vampire's vulnerability to sunlight and fire and the potential to Frenzy, and an Uratha in hishu form still has vulnerabilities to silver and certain heightened senses, and regeneration, and the capacity to Death Rage that all put it firmly in the camp of &quot;thing that looks human but isn't&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell, at higher Primal Urge, Uratha even become obligate carnivores. Not very high Primal Urge either, it's pretty much the first departure (the greater extremes are needing to do things like eat what you've hunted and only eat other carnivores).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T11:51:07-07:00","id":1518550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518503#post1518503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the bound were dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only in the philosophical sense. They died, and they are ghosts\u2026but that doesn\u2019t make them Dead. As part of the Bargain, they are fully resurrected. Kinda like if they had the Reach of Deny the Reaper cast on them. It also ties into Giest\u2019s thematics of having a second chance at life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518503#post1518503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that a Demon would have to roll a Spoof check (not a clash of Wills) to pass as human... So a demon whose cover was falling apart would more easily fail the spoof and show up as not human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. As long as the Cover holds, reality/the Supernal considers them to be humans/whatever. When it fails, they don\u2019t.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:03:14-07:00","id":1518552,"title":"","content":"I may be mistaken, but I believe it\u2019s possible to inflict a Bane/Ban on someone with the right supernatural power. (The Cleverquick Kith comes to mind.) So you can absolutely give someone a supernatural Sunlight allergy. Does that make humans inhuman for the duration of the effect? Or does the temporary nature of curse prevent that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:23:46-07:00","id":1518556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518536#post1518536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the perspective of the Life arcanum alone, [..]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any Arcanum is that binary. It really depends on what the caster is actually looking for. And Legacy Attainments can also use conditions that a simple Life spell wouldn't be able to.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518550#post1518550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only in the philosophical sense. They died, and they are ghosts\u2026but that doesn\u2019t make them Dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Bound are metaphysically dead, even though they are medically alive.\u200b&quot;<br /> Page 189 in Geist 2e core book. Which is why &quot;are they alive&quot; will give different answers depending on what you mean by &quot;alive&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T14:09:55-07:00","id":1518567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518552#post1518552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mistaken, but I believe it\u2019s possible to inflict a Bane/Ban on someone with the right supernatural power. (The Cleverquick Kith comes to mind.) So you can absolutely give someone a supernatural Sunlight allergy. Does that make humans inhuman for the duration of the effect? Or does the temporary nature of curse prevent that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes them a human with an external affliction. Even if it lasts forever, it comes from without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T16:28:02-07:00","id":1518582,"title":"","content":"Do other Supernaturals counts as &quot;non-Awakened&quot; for the purposes of the <i>High Speech Perception</i> merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T17:23:14-07:00","id":1518585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518582#post1518582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other Supernaturals counts as &quot;non-Awakened&quot; for the purposes of the <i>High Speech Perception</i> merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, only Mages are Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T17:50:01-07:00","id":1518587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518585#post1518585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, only Mages are Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but High Speech is a human-only thing, due to the necessary connection to the Astral. I think? It feeds back into the <u>Web of Life</u> human-detection question, just from a different angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T20:36:52-07:00","id":1518607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518587#post1518587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but High Speech is a human-only thing, due to the necessary connection to the Astral. I think? It feeds back into the <u>Web of Life</u> human-detection question, just from a different angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Speech as nothing to do with the Astral besides being the vector by which mages open the Omphalos to enter the Anima Mundi and it shows up in all sorts of places that aren't human communication.<br /> <br /> It would be really weird for Signs of Sorcery to say that High Speech Perception is a suitable Merit to be provided by Mystery Cult Initiation for an Exarchal cult of non-mage supernatural beings if nonhuman supernatural beings couldn't benefit from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:44:14-07:00","id":1518627,"title":"","content":"Besides, it's exclusion from the Temenos that tends to be common to non-human playable groups. Some connection to the Anima Mundi persists for a few of them, and Beasts essentially live next to the Omphalos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-23-2023, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T19:01:25-07:00","id":1518730,"title":"","content":"What'd be a good name for a Pantechion-backed Mystery Cult dedicated to industrial espionage (of the &quot;steal your data and patent it before you can&quot; variety)? <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> \u25cf Gain the Science Specialty &quot;Theory Appraisal&quot;<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain a dot in Contacts (R&amp;D), representing the Cult's network of scientists and developers who've received &quot;fortuitous&quot; tips and hints<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain the Eidetic Memory Merit, to better facilitate extracting sensitive data<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of the Library (Science) Merit, representing access to the Cult's accumulated store of data and research<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of Resources, representing income from various patents and discoveries. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T19:32:10-07:00","id":1518731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518730#post1518730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What'd be a good name for a Pantechion-backed Mystery Cult dedicated to industrial espionage (of the &quot;steal your data and patent it before you can&quot; variety)?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> \u25cf Gain the Science Specialty &quot;Theory Appraisal&quot;<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Gain a dot in Contacts (R&amp;D), representing the Cult's network of scientists and developers who've received &quot;fortuitous&quot; tips and hints<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain the Eidetic Memory Merit, to better facilitate extracting sensitive data<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of the Library (Science) Merit, representing access to the Cult's accumulated store of data and research<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Gain three dots of Resources, representing income from various patents and discoveries.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Free Technologies</b>. A law firm slash tech counseling firm that specializes in fighting against copyright and intellectual property laws that allow technological innovations to be hoarded and privatized\u2026.. by making sure the patents go to the government and megacorps who can mass-produce the tech to better the society as a whole. It\u2019s a Lie, of course. They don\u2019t care jack about the public sector benefitting from innovation; only that they crush individual flashes of brilliance, and that everyone \u2018understands\u2019 how even true genius is reductible into commodities. Of course, gullible Sleepers who don\u2019t bother to track how the case ultimately ends up to whose benefit (and who only care about the current hot issue) are roped into thinking that these are the good guys. I mean, look at the name! Surely they must mean well, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T19:35:31-07:00","id":1518732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518731#post1518731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Free Technologies</b>. A law firm slash tech counseling firm that specializes in fighting against copyright and intellectual property laws that allow technological innovations to be hoarded and privatized\u2026.. by making sure the patents go to the government and megacorps who can mass-produce the tech to better the society as a whole. It\u2019s a Lie, of course. They don\u2019t care jack about the public sector benefitting from innovation; only that they crush individual flashes of brilliance, and that everyone \u2018understands\u2019 how even true genius is reductible into commodities. Of course, gullible Sleepers who don\u2019t bother to track how the case ultimately ends up to whose benefit (and who only care about the current hot issue) are roped into thinking that these are the good guys. I mean, look at the name! Surely they must mean well, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T19:28:52-07:00","id":1518865,"title":"","content":"Occultation sets the minimum Sympathy Withstand, which is straightforward.<br /> <br /> It also penalizes rolls to discern thing about the Occulted via magic. I assume that means someone trying to cast a direct spell like <u>Analyze Life</u> or <u>Know Nature</u> is going to take a penalty to their Casting pool, but is it going to then have any impact on an enhancement spell like <u>Supernal Vision</u>? SV doesn't directly target the things it's getting information about, it just enhances perception\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T12:58:22-07:00","id":1518952,"title":"","content":"Is there any limitation on using multiple Arcana in a single spell (not a Combined Spell for multiple effects)? I thought there was, but maybe I\u2019m thinking about 1e.<br /> <br /> What would you say is necessary for a cabal to watch the memories of a coterie of vampires? Some of which have met the final death? I was thinking a tweak on Mind 3 - Read the Depths, but with Death 1 for the vampire/ghost minds.<br /> <br /> Do familiars (and spirits in general) need to be manifested to use Numina on the material realm? That would mean Goetia can\u2019t affect the material realm without a Mage helping them manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T13:53:47-07:00","id":1518957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518952#post1518952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any limitation on using multiple Arcana in a single spell (not a Combined Spell for multiple effects)? I thought there was, but maybe I\u2019m thinking about 1e.<br /> <br /> What would you say is necessary for a cabal to watch the memories of a coterie of vampires? Some of which have met the final death? I was thinking a tweak on Mind 3 - Read the Depths, but with Death 1 for the vampire/ghost minds.<br /> <br /> Do familiars (and spirits in general) need to be manifested to use Numina on the material realm? That would mean Goetia can\u2019t affect the material realm without a Mage helping them manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No limitation, as far as I'm aware<br /> <br /> 2. Mind is explicitly able to affect Vampires and Ghosts without added Arcana - as long as there is a mind, Mind can affect it.<br /> <br /> 3. I think it can be used from Twilight, but don't quote me on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:03:21-07:00","id":1518958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518952#post1518952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any limitation on using multiple Arcana in a single spell (not a Combined Spell for multiple effects)? I thought there was, but maybe I\u2019m thinking about 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as such, although I think there's a stronger priority this time around on making sure an additional Arcanum is really needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you say is necessary for a cabal to watch the memories of a coterie of vampires? Some of which have met the final death? I was thinking a tweak on Mind 3 - Read the Depths, but with Death 1 for the vampire/ghost minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, you don't need to add Death to a spell just to make it target an undead being. It has a mind, the Mind Arcanum is perfectly cromulent to do its thing with it.<br /> <br /> If it's actually dead properly... if vampires can leave ghosts and the one in question did so, still just casting the spell. Otherwise it becomes a problem of trying to target a thing that no longer exists. There'd need to be some way to reconstruct the non-existent mind, but I feel as though that's a bit trickier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do familiars (and spirits in general) need to be manifested to use Numina on the material realm? That would mean Goetia can\u2019t affect the material realm without a Mage helping them manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:29:24-07:00","id":1518961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518957#post1518957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I think it can be used from Twilight, but don't quote me on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518958#post1518958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh \ud83e\udd26\ud83c\udffb So that\u2019s one yes and one no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T14:37:04-07:00","id":1518964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518961#post1518961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Doh \ud83e\udd26\ud83c\udffb So that\u2019s one yes and one no.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Reaching Manifestation implies that they can't use it from across the Gauntlet without that specific Manifestation, but that's the only limitation I'm aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T15:33:22-07:00","id":1518966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518952#post1518952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do familiars (and spirits in general) need to be manifested to use Numina on the material realm? That would mean Goetia can\u2019t affect the material realm without a Mage helping them manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by Manifested. Your reference to Goetia seems to imply that you meant \u2018manifested\u2019 as \u2018on the material world\u2019. Ephemerals can normally use their Numina on the material world (unless it\u2019s a homebrew Numen that only targets the Shadow/Underworld/Astral itself or something). When doing so, whether they\u2019re in Twilight or Materialized doesn\u2019t matter. Whether they\u2019re Fettered or not restricts the target of their Numina, though.<br /> <br /> And if my English is correct, I believe Isator Levi above is actually saying Yes to the idea of spirits using Numina on the material world without Materializing? (Again, assuming that what you really intended by \u2018manifested on the material realm\u2019 was actually \u2018Materialized\u2019).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T19:31:28-07:00","id":1518981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1518966#post1518966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you mean by Manifested. Your reference to Goetia seems to imply that you meant \u2018manifested\u2019 as \u2018on the material world\u2019. Ephemerals can normally use their Numina on the material world (unless it\u2019s a homebrew Numen that only targets the Shadow/Underworld/Astral itself or something). When doing so, whether they\u2019re in Twilight or Materialized doesn\u2019t matter. Whether they\u2019re Fettered or not restricts the target of their Numina, though.<br /> <br /> And if my English is correct, I believe Isator Levi above is actually saying Yes to the idea of spirits using Numina on the material world without Materializing? (Again, assuming that what you really intended by \u2018manifested on the material realm\u2019 was actually \u2018Materialized\u2019).</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re right. I forgot the way I phrased it meant saying no was in agreement to my point. Your English was actually better than mine in this case and it\u2019s my native language \ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T02:32:08-07:00","id":1518997,"title":"","content":"To get a dead Vampire's (final death) memories, you might try use Death to summon their ghost (which may fail if they left no ghost or if it is withstood by the Underworld for some reason). And Time to bring them back...<br /> <br /> You could see the past with Time alone (as opposed to Mind).<br /> <br /> Multiple Arcana would be rare, so like Teleportation requires Death to go directly to and from the Underworld, and Spirit to go to and from the Spirit, so you could use Death/Spirit/Space to teleport (or open an iris) directly between the Shadow and the Underworld. There would be no limits on the number of arcanum needed. But it is pretty rare, and i can't think of an example which would need more than 3 arcanum (2 would he far more common).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-28-2023, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T16:25:23-07:00","id":1519132,"title":"","content":"<i>Disclaimer about separating game mechanics from in-game physics</i><br /> <br /> Assuming the one presented in Night Horrors is the orthodoxy, the Genius variant of the Perfected Adepts shows you can develop a different Initiate Attainment for a Legacy, but still be metaphysically part of said Legacy. Mechanically, would that just be novel Initiation at Gnosis 3 via Mystery Play? Meaning you don't necessarily have to be inducted into a specific Legacy by a teacher/Daimonomikon/Aeon, as long as you can internalize sufficient fundamental symbology of the archetype?<br /> <br /> Similarly, for the Optional Attainment stuff - are they part-and-parcel of learning the Attainment? That is, if you wanted to learn the Genius &quot;Web of Life&quot; Attainment, but replace the Forces Optional Attainment with Prime's &quot;Supernal Vision&quot;, is that going to require entering that tier as a Novel Attainment?<br /> <br /> <br /> Addendum - can Legacies merge, over time? I could see the multiple Intitiate Attainments for the Adepts being the result of several similar Legacies being practiced by the Arrow, and slowly falling under the umbrella term of &quot;Perfected Adepts&quot;. Eventually they could just become one Legacy, with many branches. The Tremere have something similar going on with their Houses, but given they had to break their Souls and Gnosis to achieve that they aren't the <i>best</i> example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-29-2023, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:13:50-07:00","id":1519208,"title":"","content":"Can Sever Oaths (Fate 4) liberate a Ghost from its anchor (with or without its cooperation), or can it only break unatural bindings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:39:32-07:00","id":1519211,"title":"","content":"Unless the Anchor was in some way related to a promise or oath (Ie a spouse/wedding band, a soldier bound to the standard they swore to follow into battle, etc), I'd say no","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T20:48:34-07:00","id":1519222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519208#post1519208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Sever Oaths (Fate 4) liberate a Ghost from its anchor (with or without its cooperation), or can it only break unatural bindings?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Anchor doesn't actually bind a ghost except in the sense that being a ghost starkly limits your ability to exist in the land of the living without an Anchor. You could free a ghost bound into a Memento through the Ghost Binding Ceremony or locked into their body to create a revenant, but simply having an Anchor isn't being bound so much as being a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T02:19:23-07:00","id":1519232,"title":"","content":"I think it is more like a Space connection (metaphysical sympathy) which binds a ghost to their anchor. Though Death could likely break it too.<br /> <br /> Fate doesn't seem to have any power, Sever Oaths says 'free a bound ephemeral entity' but Anchors are not binding, a ghost can simply walk away from their anchor (and suffer from essence bleed, eventuall y going into hibernation and being drawn back to their anchor which provides them with essence...).<br /> <br /> In a sense the anchor is binding the ghost to the material plane, preventing them being drawn into the Underworld, so i can see why you would argue that. But i don't think it is really the intention of sever oaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:59:33-07:00","id":1519509,"title":"","content":"<u>Ban</u> with Forces can make the target invisible, but not necessarily in a useful way. Using Space to mess with perspective and angles to make a subject invisible is reasonable, right? Possibly requiring sentient targets to also have <u>Outward and Inward Eye</u> cast on them to see properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T15:44:36-07:00","id":1519517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519509#post1519509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Ban</u> with Forces can make the target invisible, but not necessarily in a useful way. Using Space to mess with perspective and angles to make a subject invisible is reasonable, right? Possibly requiring sentient targets to also have <u>Outward and Inward Eye</u> cast on them to see properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a toned down version of Quarantine, so yeah I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:07:29-07:00","id":1519520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519517#post1519517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a toned down version of Quarantine, so yeah I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd probably be, what, Fraying or Weaving? Patterning or Unraveling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:10:24-07:00","id":1519532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519509#post1519509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Ban</u> with Forces can make the target invisible, but not necessarily in a useful way. Using Space to mess with perspective and angles to make a subject invisible is reasonable, right? Possibly requiring sentient targets to also have <u>Outward and Inward Eye</u> cast on them to see properly.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519520#post1519520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd probably be, what, Fraying or Weaving? Patterning or Unraveling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like...<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Garbled Perspectives (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Science, Subterfuge, Firearms<br /> <br /> A warlock understands just how much people rely on &quot;line of sight&quot;, and how easily that can be warped. This spell messes up angles of sight within its subject Area such that looking at something straightly is impossible; everything looks off-kilter and out-of-place, as if looking through a wrongly adjusted camera. Add Potency as bonuses on rolls to hide, misdirect, and ambush within the area. Also, enable such actions to be possible outside common sense, such as 'turning invisible' right in front of someone. Also impose Potency as penalties on Perception rolls relying on sight.<br /> <br /> Spatial senses such as Active Mage Sight (Space) and that granted by &quot;The Outward and Inward Eye&quot; are unaffected by this spell. Supernaturally enhanced vision, and sensory powers that home in designated targets (such as &quot;Scrying&quot;) trigger Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Extend the sensory garble to another sense among hearing, smell, taste, and touch. 1 Reach per sense added this way.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022 </b>: Selectively designate not only who are affected by the spell within the Area, but also whether that target enjoys only the bonuses, suffers only the penalties, or both.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Instead of garbling sight or others among the five senses, distort the senses of proportions, depths, and distance to manipulate Size. Add or subtract Potency to the effective Size trait of an object or creature within the subject Area, such that everyone else within the Area interacts with the target under that changed Size. The Size-shifted target's true mass or volume isn't changed. 1 additional Reach per additional Size-shifted target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T22:40:35-07:00","id":1519931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519509#post1519509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Ban</u> with Forces can make the target invisible, but not necessarily in a useful way. Using Space to mess with perspective and angles to make a subject invisible is reasonable, right? Possibly requiring sentient targets to also have <u>Outward and Inward Eye</u> cast on them to see properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ban blocking forces isnt making the target invisible, its making them hidden because light cant travel through the ban. As much the same way entering a wooden shed makes doesnt make the person invisible...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T22:59:57-07:00","id":1519935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519931#post1519931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A ban blocking forces isnt making the target invisible, its making them hidden because light cant travel through the ban. As much the same way entering a wooden shed makes doesnt make the person invisible...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for the pedantic summation of &quot;not necessarily in a useful way.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T23:18:25-07:00","id":1519938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519935#post1519935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, thank you for the pedantic summation of &quot;not necessarily in a useful way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between being invisible and having a glowing outline AND not being invisible because you are inside a ward/shed. One is a non useful example of invisibility the other isnt invisibility at all.<br /> <br /> Glad i could keep you straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T09:15:00-07:00","id":1519963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spell Stacking</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When multiple spells affect the same aspect of a character the<br /> effects of the spells do not stack, and instead the spell with the<br /> highest Potency takes effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Does Mage Armor stack with spells that grant armor? Like Body Control 1/0 armor with Life Mage Armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T13:05:37-07:00","id":1519979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1519963#post1519963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Does Mage Armor stack with spells that grant armor? Like Body Control 1/0 armor with Life Mage Armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T13:09:05-07:00","id":1521347,"title":"","content":"Can a Goetia or a Ghost Claim someone? Since Goetia typically can't leave the Astral and both have a different skillset than Spirits, I imagine &quot;no&quot;, at least not without outside interference such as Magely empowerment. Sin-Eaters and their Giests are close, but not the same as Claimed, as I understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-24-2023, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T13:26:20-07:00","id":1521348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1521347#post1521347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Goetia or a Ghost Claim someone? Since Ghost typically can't leave the Astral and both have a different skillset than Spirits, I imagine &quot;no&quot;, at least not without outside interference such as Magely empowerment. Sin-Eaters and their Giests are close, but not the same as Claimed, as I understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The peculiarities of ghostly Rank mean geists are more likely to have the Claim Manifestation than other ghosts (and, if they aren't inclined to offer the Bargain, might do so as a different approach to pursuing whatever their Remembrance drives them toward), and it works the same for them as it does for spirits.<br /> <br /> Goetia are not Claiming anything without plot-driver shenanigans or other outside interference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T02:19:57-07:00","id":1521368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1521347#post1521347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Goetia or a Ghost Claim someone? Since Goetia typically can't leave the Astral and both have a different skillset than Spirits, I imagine &quot;no&quot;, at least not without outside interference such as Magely empowerment. Sin-Eaters and their Giests are close, but not the same as Claimed, as I understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the book, Ghost can claim ppl, they are native to the materials world and get a number of manifestations equal to their rank. Thus they may struggle to get all the required manifestations to actually claim until higher rank (or by giving up numena). Of course higher rank ghost can exist due to unusual circumstances, created by occult alignment/rare mysterious events (aka st fiat) so if you want a higher rank ghost - as opposed to a Geist - you can have one.<br /> <br /> The other options are geists, reapers, kerberori and Chthonians.<br /> <br /> To which i would just say:<br /> <br /> Yes to Geists (the pack they make with Bound is not the same but equivalent level).<br /> <br /> Reapers are unlikely to be able to do so as it doesn't align with their task, and are more likely to want to drag a ghost who has claimed someone into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Kerberori and Chthonians are less likely to be out of the Underworld and Chthonians in particular don't fair well in the material.<br /> <br /> That said, i see no reason a kerberos couldn't have claimed someone and then brought that body back to the Underworld as punishment for violating their old laws. In 1e they got manifestations, so why not?<br /> <br /> Goetia on the other hand, don't even get twilight manifestation by default, so summon goetia should really bring over an entity with no manifestation at all. But I suspect this is an oversight in the rules. Errata that they gain twilight manifestation by default. Without manifestations (or a mystery like LA's signature mystery) claiming isn't possible, but also goetia has less motivation to leave the astral. And if they could claim they wouldn't be able to bring their claimed body back to the astral physically. So you would want to have an entity which has a reason to want to stay... Maybe a personal goetia from the Onerios of someone who has died*, with nowhere to go back to... Maybe a temenotic goetia who is trying to restore worship of their religion - the avatar of some ancient God trying to spread more belief. Or maybe a goetia of some aspect of the world trying to restore the eco-system... Some possible interesting plot hooks there. But it would be rare.<br /> <br /> *It is possible that on the death of their human this personal goetia becomes a ghost.<br /> <br /> Edit: i did find the Claim manifestation in the Geist book, so yes, ghosts definitely can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-25-2023, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:17:46-07:00","id":1521669,"title":"","content":"I'm about to run my first Mage campaign (Yay!) and I have a question about the Teleportation spell to help set up my opening scenario.<br /> <br /> It says that you can add an Arcana with an associated realm to teleport the subject to that realm or vice versa. I'd assume, then, that if you add Mind 2, you can teleport into or from the Astral. If a Mage teleported someone into the astral, would it just send their consciousness there and the bodies would fall limp?<br /> <br /> To further elucidate my aim, the campaign is centered around the Pentacle's first (modern) magic academy with newly Awakened teenagers being initiated into Mage society through the school's curriculum. Of course, it's going to go horribly wrong down the road, but we'll get there.<br /> <br /> My opening scenario involves an initiation in which the players are sent to the Astral, have their memories temporarily rewritten to believe they are going to detention for some wrong doing and to forget that they're in the Astral, and have them placed in the Temenos' &quot;Twilight Zone&quot;. Specifically, they'll be in the setting of &quot;Five Characters in Search of an Exit&quot;. They will have to realize where they are, force themselves awake, and then they'll have a scavenger hunt back in the real world to discover all the nooks and crannies of their school.<br /> <br /> My initial thought was to have a guided meditation into the Astral by the school's Hallow, do the memory alterations, and leave it at that. However, teleporting to the Astral would be a lot less messy. So any thoughts on how to accomplish this would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12268-touchofdivine","name":"TouchofDivine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:55:19-07:00","id":1521672,"title":"","content":"The short version, since their bodies are left where they are there should be no Space requirement to re-write their physical location... This is not a teleportation spell...<br /> <br /> Getting physically go the Astral is probably a bigger mystery by default.<br /> <br /> But since that doesn't seem to be what you want, i think a guided meditation followed by a AoE effect to make anyone entering the particular Temenos realm forget how they got there would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:12:29-07:00","id":1521675,"title":"","content":"Artificial Synesi (Page 243) would be your best move. Just modify the <u>Reaching</u> or <u>World Walker</u> spells from Spirit into a Mind spell that forcibly sends the targets to the Astral, or with a Reach creates a Synesi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T13:28:56-07:00","id":1521833,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts 4 makes the character's unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage. <u>Kinetic Blow</u> does the same (plus a weapon bonus of [Potency], and whatever Reach effects). <br /> <br /> If a character with Martial Arts 4 gets empowered with <u>Kinetic Blow</u>, does it make more sense to have their unarmed damage upgrade to Aggravated, or to just accept it as a redundant effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T13:39:17-07:00","id":1521836,"title":"","content":"Redundant, maybe add bonus dice of damage, or modify the spell to take an extra 2 reach and spend a mana to do aggravated damage (but only for those with martial arts already supplying the lethal?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T05:32:12-07:00","id":1522054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1521833#post1521833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or to just accept it as a redundant effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could swap it out for a reasonable alternative Maneuver. If you have Hurt Locker, that book has an alternate list of options for Martial Arts, and otherwise it also has the Style Tags tool which can give other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T07:41:56-07:00","id":1522055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1521833#post1521833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts 4 makes the character's unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage. <u>Kinetic Blow</u> does the same (plus a weapon bonus of [Potency], and whatever Reach effects).<br /> <br /> If a character with Martial Arts 4 gets empowered with <u>Kinetic Blow</u>, does it make more sense to have their unarmed damage upgrade to Aggravated, or to just accept it as a redundant effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say redundant, because they are already being more efficient in where and how they are concentrating the force. A brawler with Forces that wanted to get some extra damage in could use a Shielding to prevent fire damage, set themselves on fire and then deliver blazing punches. Not only would this make them horrifying in a grapple, but it would be a major intimidation tactic. If they also increased the light of the fire to be blinding, it would make them a true nightmare to fight. It could possibly make a spirit pause and consider if they want to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T10:27:10-07:00","id":1522058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1521833#post1521833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character with Martial Arts 4 gets empowered with <u>Kinetic Blow</u>, does it make more sense to have their unarmed damage upgrade to Aggravated, or to just accept it as a redundant effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd note that Kinetic Blow has a reach effect to include weapons, which would already be dealing lethal damage, and it says nothing about upgrading the damage to aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T16:26:26-07:00","id":1522435,"title":"","content":"So lets say a group of mages are doing a bollywood dance/singing number. Does the mage get a penalty for spellcasting while doing athletics checks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T17:05:18-07:00","id":1522436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522435#post1522435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets say a group of mages are doing a bollywood dance/singing number. Does the mage get a penalty for spellcasting while doing athletics checks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on exactly what the Bollywood performance is supposed to be here, I reckon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T04:42:02-07:00","id":1522453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522435#post1522435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets say a group of mages are doing a bollywood dance/singing number. Does the mage get a penalty for spellcasting while doing athletics checks?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But if the dancing requires instant actions, the mage can't take any non-reflexive actions for spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T07:35:00-07:00","id":1522457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522435#post1522435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets say a group of mages are doing a bollywood dance/singing number. Does the mage get a penalty for spellcasting while doing athletics checks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on what Tessie said, you can use <i>Stored Spell</i> and <i>Hung Spell</i> to create special effects or, should you have Fate, have the actors utilize Basilisks to create short duration ones.<br /> <br /> Lastly, remember that changing from Withstanding a spell to not doing so can be done reflexively, which means Duration primary spells can be &quot;turned on/off&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T12:10:22-07:00","id":1522476,"title":"","content":"This may be a little beyond the scope of a 'simple question', but how would Perfected blood mechanically work in the context of vampires and Vitae? I was imagining it never counts as cold blood for the purposes of feeding (negating the necessity to consume pints of cold blood equal to Blood Potency x2 for a single point of Vitae), but would it also potentially bypass feeding restrictions regardless of a human, Kindred, or animal source? Could it inflict Vitae Addiction by merit of its Perfected nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T12:20:32-07:00","id":1522477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522476#post1522476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a little beyond the scope of a 'simple question', but how would Perfected blood mechanically work in the context of vampires and Vitae? I was imagining it never counts as cold blood for the purposes of feeding (negating the necessity to consume pints of cold blood equal to Blood Potency x2 for a single point of Vitae), but would it also potentially bypass feeding restrictions regardless of a human, Kindred, or animal source? Could it inflict Vitae Addiction by merit of its Perfected nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, with the addiction being only for Kindred. In the case of mortals, I would also add that its perfectly compatible with any blood transfusion and will not coagulate naturally. It would also be useable in any magical key or ritual that requires specific blood, like all perfected materials.<br /> <br /> It would not, however, allow a vampire to use it to learn a new Discipline, since it makes no sense for perfected blood to be afflicted by the curse of vampirism.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T13:33:12-07:00","id":1522481,"title":"","content":"Would it be reasonable to allow the 2 Reach option of <i>Kinetic Blow</i> to apply Armor Piercing to unarmed attacks ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T14:29:34-07:00","id":1522484,"title":"","content":"I'd be OK with it, personally. Maybe make it a conversion of Potency; you choose how much Potency to allocate to the weapon bonus, and/or convert two points of Potency per AP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T16:19:01-07:00","id":1522491,"title":"","content":"Can Siderite be magnetized? Like, say, to make a compass needle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T16:42:19-07:00","id":1522492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522491#post1522491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Siderite be magnetized? Like, say, to make a compass needle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Awakened magic operates on symbolism and magnets were seen as magical by occultists, then I think the most perfect version of iron, the one most attuned with the Supernal, being magnetic would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T17:15:47-07:00","id":1522493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522491#post1522491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Siderite be magnetized? Like, say, to make a compass needle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Via electricity or rubbing other magnets, sure.<br /> <br /> Since iron/Siderite is associated with Pandemonium, which is of the Mastigos Path, which is associated with path-finding, maybe it's actually easier to turn Siderite into a compass than turning iron is. Perhaps, not even without magnetic force?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't make it 'naturally' magnetic, though. It doesn't feel like Supernal iron-ness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T17:50:05-07:00","id":1522494,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of it from the perspective of an Invisible Path member making a compass Order Tool, so the pathfinding symbology works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T15:42:20-07:00","id":1522538,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of it is supernally attuned it might find leylines or point towards the accumulations of mana within the Fallen world, rather than being attuned to magnetic field lines... it would still look like a compass to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T08:16:44-07:00","id":1522827,"title":"","content":"Being aware of your name being spoken (or just people talking about you) is a supernatural power that crops up in media. I imagine a spell to give you that awareness on a global/universal scale would be an Imperial spell, but a standard Mage could still get some mileage out of normal Scale. What would be an appropriate Arcana for such a spell? Space (momentary, incredibly weak Sympathy between speaker and subject) and <i>maybe</i> Fate or Mind are all i can think of. Possibly a combination of several.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T09:27:43-07:00","id":1522829,"title":"","content":"Sympathetic connections reflect your closeness with others, so someone who knows your true name ought to be closer to you than someone who doesn't all else being equal. I'd have to look up how sympathetic connections work again to say for sure but I feel like it should be possible to swing it with just Space, assuming all you want is a nudge and maybe a direction when someone says your name. IIRC Fate has some other spells which deal in &quot;recognizing when someone says something significant&quot; so Fate/Space could work for when people say your name in a significant way, or Forces to flag any given sound pattern and Space to broaden the range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T10:28:09-07:00","id":1522832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522827#post1522827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being aware of your name being spoken (or just people talking about you) is a supernatural power that crops up in media. I imagine a spell to give you that awareness on a global/universal scale would be an Imperial spell, but a standard Mage could still get some mileage out of normal Scale. What would be an appropriate Arcana for such a spell? Space (momentary, incredibly weak Sympathy between speaker and subject) and <i>maybe</i> Fate or Mind are all i can think of. Possibly a combination of several.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory if you take a small vial of bacteria, and cast a knowing spell on them, then you can spread them all over the world and still have an active spell (though perhaps that would be multiple seperate subjects...)<br /> <br /> In principle, having a simple Knowing spell spread to locations all over the world shouldn't be impossible with this work around (someone else proposed using a knowing spell on a space-probe before launch, and being able to keep in constant contact no matter how far it gets from you).<br /> <br /> So maybe that can get around the scale part... but otherwise the following still applies to whatever scale you do target.<br /> <br /> So I think you could try to cast a Space Knowing spell on your Sympatethic name, or maybe a Mind Knowing spell on the purview of communication targeting the specific communication of your name - but i think that may be too abstract a thing (you are not able to target the concept of communication, just specific examples of communication, so your name being communicated by any means would fall under mind... but Symbolically your Sympatethic name definitely exists as a thing you can target...)<br /> <br /> Like Mind, Fate could be used with the purview of Intentions, which might cover anyone who is speaking with the intention of refering to you... that covers mispronounciation, or secret codenames used for you - though perhaps only if they know they are referring to you.<br /> <br /> I think in any case you may need to use Sympatethic range with yourself as the sympathy yantra (as if your name is a part of you... which i think is Symbolically how the Mage magic system works, not using Science).<br /> <br /> However your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for mind, shouting your name and casting on that specific communication (which then travels around the world as the sound waves dilute? I guess Symbolically it stops being your name after nobody can make it out, maybe... but it would still be a solid example of the name to use as a strange yantra.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-20-2023, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T16:22:16-07:00","id":1522860,"title":"","content":"Can/should a Mage be able to measure the power stats of other splats, and if so what Arcana would be appropriate? <u>Supernal Vision</u> can measure Gnosis, and with the Reach effect it doesn't seem <i>too </i>out of line to use it for that purpose if you've studied that kind of entity before. But a more specialized spell might be necessary.<br /> <br /> More importantly, can a Mage measure Integrity, and which Arcana does it fall under? Mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T16:52:39-07:00","id":1522863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522860#post1522860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can/should a Mage be able to measure the power stats of other splats, and if so what Arcana would be appropriate? <u>Supernal Vision</u> can measure Gnosis, and with the Reach effect it doesn't seem <i>too </i>out of line to use it for that purpose if you've studied that kind of entity before. But a more specialized spell might be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the entire purpose of Supernal Vision's Reach effect, so yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly, can a Mage measure Integrity, and which Arcana does it fall under? Mind? </div> </div> </div>It's soul-health, so probably Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T17:15:58-07:00","id":1522864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522827#post1522827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being aware of your name being spoken (or just people talking about you) is a supernatural power that crops up in media. I imagine a spell to give you that awareness on a global/universal scale would be an Imperial spell, but a standard Mage could still get some mileage out of normal Scale. What would be an appropriate Arcana for such a spell? Space (momentary, incredibly weak Sympathy between speaker and subject) and <i>maybe</i> Fate or Mind are all i can think of. Possibly a combination of several.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate 1 Oaths Fulfilled already lists &quot;speaks the mage's name&quot; as an example trigger, so I'd start from there.<br /> <br /> Some beefed up 5-dot version, perhaps. Maybe as an Artifact, to allow for narrative leeway on fudging how the spell factors exactly work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T18:50:51-07:00","id":1522870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522864#post1522864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some beefed up 5-dot version, perhaps. Maybe as an Artifact, to allow for narrative leeway on fudging how the spell factors exactly work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do spell factors need to be fudged if the original query already permitted for something being done within normal scale rules?<br /> <br /> The thing about Awakened magic, <i>even compared to other forms of power in Chronicles games</i>, is that all of its versatility, flexibility, and the fact that you get massive amounts of it for small purchases, are built around the necessity of casting individual spells that have specific requirements for their range and duration. If you want to know when somebody is speaking your name, you need to lay the groundwork for that.<br /> <br /> Even Imperial magic has that. If anything, it has it harder. The way spell factors need to be decided upon before the spell gets cast? That goes double for archmastery, because you get it in the quintessence as well as the dice pool penalties. A spell to target the whole world requires a more difficult to acquire quintessence than one cast on a building, even for the same effect. That's a big part of why archmasters aren't casting many spells on the entire world.<br /> <br /> (That said, I think Imperial magic would be more efficient to use an Entity practice spell to modify the nature of a certain word, to bestow the innate property of alerting the caster if it is spoken. That's the level at which they're playing the game; better to cast small effects that drill deep than reshape continents. It's less work intensive, and flies under the radar of the Exarchs.)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T19:05:06-07:00","id":1522872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522832#post1522832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In theory if you take a small vial of bacteria, and cast a knowing spell on them, then you can spread them all over the world and still have an active spell (though perhaps that would be multiple seperate subjects...)<br /> <br /> In principle, having a simple Knowing spell spread to locations all over the world shouldn't be impossible with this work around</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay...<br /> <br /> What exactly does it mean to &quot;spread them around the world&quot; in this scenario? What, you go around with your vile filled with what I presume is a liquid medium culture of bacteria and, what, pluck an individual drop of it down somewhere and let the spell remain with the cells in it? Presuming they don't immediately die of exposure or sudden transference.<br /> <br /> And spreading them &quot;all over the world&quot;? What, like, one drop in every country? In every city? It couldn't be blanketing the world in a very thin film of culture media, there still wouldn't be enough of that to go in what could reasonably be called a vial (or an Olympic sized swimming pool), so there's probably going to be some shortfall.<br /> <br /> And the end result of this is that you have bacteria that have had a spell to tell you something about the bacteria that are scattered haphazardly over what is ultimately a very small number of places.<br /> <br /> What does that accomplish?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(which then travels around the world as the sound waves dilute?</div> </div> </div> </div>All other considerations aside, that's not really what a wave is. When something makes a noise, it does create an individual physical wave that moves in a direction; waves are the propagation of energy through an otherwise relatively static but flexible medium. That's why plucking a guitar string is different than throwing it.<br /> <br /> The energy doesn't &quot;run out&quot; as such, but it ultimately (and fairly quick in the form of something like a shout) converts into a form that will no longer propagate through air like that. A sound isn't something that becomes a perpetual, but very quiet, part of the atmosphere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T19:09:41-07:00","id":1522873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522870#post1522870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do spell factors need to be fudged if the original query already permitted for something being done within normal scale rules?<br /> <br /> The thing about Awakened magic, <i>even compared to other forms of power in Chronicles games</i>, is that all of its versatility, flexibility, and the fact that you get massive amounts of it for small purchases, are built around the necessity of casting individual spells that have specific requirements for their range and duration. If you want to know when somebody is speaking your name, you need to lay the groundwork for that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>* rereads original post<br /> <br /> Oops.<br /> <br /> Hmm, then something like a Fate Making spell that creates a symbolic banner or call signal of sorts that can be activated later, with an Add Space option to use a sympathetic name as the sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T19:37:29-07:00","id":1522876,"title":"","content":"I mean... I was thinking &quot;Cast spell on area, I am aware of any mentioning of my name within spell area&quot;. Which isn't exactly <u>Sworn Oaths</u>, but SO is still a good base to work off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T02:33:27-07:00","id":1522883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522872#post1522872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay...<br /> <br /> What exactly does it mean to &quot;spread them around the world&quot; in this scenario? What, you go around with your vile filled with what I presume is a liquid medium culture of bacteria and, what, pluck an individual drop of it down somewhere and let the spell remain with the cells in it? Presuming they don't immediately die of exposure or sudden transference.<br /> <br /> And spreading them &quot;all over the world&quot;? What, like, one drop in every country? In every city? It couldn't be blanketing the world in a very thin film of culture media, there still wouldn't be enough of that to go in what could reasonably be called a vial (or an Olympic sized swimming pool), so there's probably going to be some shortfall.<br /> <br /> And the end result of this is that you have bacteria that have had a spell to tell you something about the bacteria that are scattered haphazardly over what is ultimately a very small number of places.<br /> <br /> What does that accomplish?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just the idea that a spell which had a relatively small scale can continue to he active over a large area.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of aerosolizing the bacteria, and seeing how far they spread. Might work better with water molecules than bacteria inany case.. the principle was how can you get global scale without global scale.<br /> <br /> For Life, instead of a knowing spell on it's own, maybe you could use weaving to add traits to a bacteria which it will pass down the generations (of course this is questionable as to how the scale/spell works anyway, but assuming it does) a combined weaving and knowing could essentially tag bacteria which you then grow and spread everywhere (assuming you weave sufficient advantages into it that it out competes other bacteria around the globe).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All other considerations aside, that's not really what a wave is. When something makes a noise, it does create an individual physical wave that moves in a direction; waves are the propagation of energy through an otherwise relatively static but flexible medium. That's why plucking a guitar string is different than throwing it.<br /> <br /> The energy doesn't &quot;run out&quot; as such, but it ultimately (and fairly quick in the form of something like a shout) converts into a form that will no longer propagate through air like that. A sound isn't something that becomes a perpetual, but very quiet, part of the atmosphere. </div> </div> </div>The sound energy convert to different vibrations absorbed and dissipated. But it is still there in the air mixed with all the other sounds and pressure changes, from an information theory perspective, i think the information becomes mixed up and difficult to extract, but not meaningfully lost.<br /> <br /> However that is science, the Lie in Mage, a distraction from the symbolism of the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T05:57:26-07:00","id":1522887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522876#post1522876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... I was thinking &quot;Cast spell on area, I am aware of any mentioning of my name within spell area&quot;. Which isn't exactly <u>Sworn Oaths</u>, but SO is still a good base to work off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might have mixed up some spell names. The 1-dot spell that alerts one to if a named circumstance has come to pass is called &quot;Oaths Fulfilled&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given that &quot;speaking the mage's name&quot; is given as an actual example of what it can alert one to, I don't see why it doesn't fulfil all the conditions you've specified as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T06:10:59-07:00","id":1522888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522883#post1522883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the idea that a spell which had a relatively small scale can continue to he active over a large area.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of aerosolizing the bacteria, and seeing how far they spread. Might work better with water molecules than bacteria inany case.. the principle was how can you get global scale without global scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's without global scale, then it doesn't have global scale. Casting a spell on somebody while you're in Australia and then hopping on a plane to France doesn't mean you've achieved some grand expansion of the spell, it's still one thing on one tiny spec on the face of the Earth that is very far away.<br /> <br /> And individual bacteria will not spread that far; motility is not that high, and the lifespan of cells is often measured in the hours.<br /> <br /> I'm almost getting an impression that you think a spell cast on bacteria will spread into newly created cells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Life, instead of a knowing spell on it's own, maybe you could use weaving to add traits to a bacteria which it will pass down the generations (of course this is questionable as to how the scale/spell works anyway, but assuming it does) a combined weaving and knowing could essentially tag bacteria which you then grow and spread everywhere (assuming you weave sufficient advantages into it that it out competes other bacteria around the globe).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how combined spells work, and certainly it's not a case that the spell to create Lasting heredity actually spreads itself to offspring, let alone any spells that might be combined with it.<br /> <br /> It also still kind of sounds like describing a Knowing spell in terms of providing information on anything other than their actual subject, as though it would make the bacteria some kind of surveillance beacon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sound energy convert to different vibrations absorbed and dissipated. But it is still there in the air mixed with all the other sounds and pressure changes, from an information theory perspective, i think the information becomes mixed up and difficult to extract, but not meaningfully lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that in these terms &quot;information&quot; means something a lot more specific than its colloquial use, and not something meant to imply that the actual content of the sound is something that becomes encoded in the waste heat that it gets converted into. That the information in question is just the quantity of energy that it contained; measurable, but not something that could be backtracked into an understandable form.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think you're completely off the mark here. Look at the description of mandelas seen by Obrimos Sight; the idea that all forms of energy are ultimately interconnected and in a continuous state of transition is actually covered in the symbolism of the Forces Arcanum as expressed in the Realm where it is strongest. But I think still in a form that regards individual instances as only themselves for so long as they exist in their particular forms. Not really the kind of thing where any given noise eventually becomes part of the background radiation of everything, especially not in a way that could carry a spell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T07:36:34-07:00","id":1522893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522887#post1522887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might have mixed up some spell names. The 1-dot spell that alerts one to if a named circumstance has come to pass is called &quot;Oaths Fulfilled&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, indeed, muddle <u>Sworn Oaths</u> and <u>Oaths Fulfilled.</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that &quot;speaking the mage's name&quot; is given as an actual example of what it can alert one to, I don't see why it doesn't fulfil all the conditions you've specified as is. </div> </div> </div>Because -and I readily admit this is possibly me being too narrow with how I read the spell subject/area rules- OF cast on a wide area doesn't add new subjects who enter the area after the casting, although subjects who were within the area when it was initially cast continue to be affected if they leave. Which is a enough of a distinction that I'd personally disallow a Rote/Praxis of <u>Oaths Fulfilled</u> to be used to create this &quot;zone of awareness&quot;. Still works fine for tagging a bunch of people, which potentially serves the same purpose if there isn't much traffic into or out of the designated area.<br /> <br /> It's the same distinction I make with Prime's <u>Dispel Magic</u>. DM, cast on an area, isn't an ani-magic field. It can blanket-supress all affected spells currently active in the area, but it's not going to affect new spells entering or being cast. It justifies an anti-magic field spell being perfectly viable, just one I'd require have a separate Rote/Praxis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:17:23-07:00","id":1522895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522888#post1522888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's without global scale, then it doesn't have global scale. Casting a spell on somebody while you're in Australia and then hopping on a plane to France doesn't mean you've achieved some grand expansion of the spell, it's still one thing on one tiny spec on the face of the Earth that is very far away.<br /> <br /> And individual bacteria will not spread that far; motility is not that high, and the lifespan of cells is often measured in the hours.<br /> <br /> I'm almost getting an impression that you think a spell cast on bacteria will spread into newly created cells.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not really how combined spells work, and certainly it's not a case that the spell to create Lasting heredity actually spreads itself to offspring, let alone any spells that might be combined with it.<br /> <br /> It also still kind of sounds like describing a Knowing spell in terms of providing information on anything other than their actual subject, as though it would make the bacteria some kind of surveillance beacon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, this example was to highlight you could get information from all over the world of you could spread a thing all over... arguably it requires each bacterium to be targeted seperately, which would require a lot of scale (but Afaik only Area is limited, number of subjects just keeps going up, right?)<br /> <br /> But yeah, you would get no surveillance beyond the subject. But if your name is the subject, and isn't too abstract a concept (like you can't target the concept of Life, just actual examples of life) then why couldn't you do something similar... it is still your name even if it isn't localised in one place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that in these terms &quot;information&quot; means something a lot more specific than its colloquial use, and not something meant to imply that the actual content of the sound is something that becomes encoded in the waste heat that it gets converted into. That the information in question is just the quantity of energy that it contained; measurable, but not something that could be backtracked into an understandable form.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think you're completely off the mark here. Look at the description of mandelas seen by Obrimos Sight; the idea that all forms of energy are ultimately interconnected and in a continuous state of transition is actually covered in the symbolism of the Forces Arcanum as expressed in the Realm where it is strongest. But I think still in a form that regards individual instances as only themselves for so long as they exist in their particular forms. Not really the kind of thing where any given noise eventually becomes part of the background radiation of everything, especially not in a way that could carry a spell. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you might be right. I think the information content is also a conserved quantity, in that information can not be destroyed (except maybe in black holes, but that is considered a flaw in our physics rather than a clear fundamental law). So in some sense, i am pretty sure it is next to impossible to decode the information, but i think as far as Supernal symbology goes it would not count.<br /> <br /> But it is like trying to claim if i target enough molecule of air that I will Know when they are used to say my name. Except the molecules may be moving around when someone speaks, i just don't think a spell attached to them would know what they are being used for.<br /> <br /> What would a local version of the be? Cast on all the air in the room a matter/mind spell to know when the arrangement of molecules contains the information of my name? Seems unnecessary to involve matter in that spell at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:22:50-07:00","id":1522896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522893#post1522893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did, indeed, muddle <u>Sworn Oaths</u> and <u>Oaths Fulfilled.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> Because -and I readily admit this is possibly me being too narrow with how I read the spell subject/area rules- OF cast on a wide area doesn't add new subjects who enter the area after the casting, although subjects who were within the area when it was initially cast continue to be affected if they leave.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am pretty sure that is exactly the opposite of how the rules are meant.<br /> <br /> Area of effect spells auto-check that subjects are still in the area.<br /> <br /> Spells which have specific subjects continue to effect them where-ever they go.<br /> <br /> These are the two options for spell casting Afaik. This has been discussed several times.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Aside: spells also auto-check the withstand rating hasn't changed and alter their potency if it has, or check the size of the subject (so if it gets bigger it may shrug off the spell while larger than the biggest valid size for a given scale of spell). Arguably spells also check the time/duration hasn't expired, but this is a qualitative difference becuase in all the other cases the spell continues to exist even if it is suppressed temporarily (though maybe the spell continues to exist in the past...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:30:59-07:00","id":1522900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522896#post1522896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am pretty sure that is exactly the opposite of how the rules are meant.<br /> <br /> Area of effect spells auto-check that subjects are still in the area.<br /> <br /> Spells which have specific subjects continue to effect them where-ever they go.<br /> <br /> These are the two options for spell casting Afaik. This has been discussed several times.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Aside: spells also auto-check the withstand rating hasn't changed and alter their potency if it has, or check the size of the subject (so if it gets bigger it may shrug off the spell while larger than the biggest valid size for a given scale of spell). Arguably spells also check the time/duration hasn't expired, but this is a qualitative difference becuase in all the other cases the spell continues to exist even if it is suppressed temporarily (though maybe the spell continues to exist in the past...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells that have an Instant effect (<u>Mend, Mind Flay, etc)</u> reapply themselves every [ritual interval], if cast at Advanced Duration. That's the closest to an auto-check I'm aware of. If there's been a consensus contrary to how I'm reading the Scale rules... fine? I haven't exactly combed the forum for it, and my reading is internally consistent enough that I haven't really questioned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:38:01-07:00","id":1522909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522900#post1522900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells that have an Instant effect (<u>Mend, Mind Flay, etc)</u> reapply themselves every [ritual interval], if cast at Advanced Duration. That's the closest to an auto-check I'm aware of. If there's been a consensus contrary to how I'm reading the Scale rules... fine? I haven't exactly combed the forum for it, and my reading is internally consistent enough that I haven't really questioned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i think your reading is consistent enough that there have been a number of aruments about it.<br /> <br /> I suspect i was on the other side the first time I came across it. There is a clear Word of God statement on it floating around somewhere, that is, you make a choice between Area of Effect type spell and a Subject type spell. And each has a downside.<br /> <br /> For a spell with duration longer than the caster's gnosis-derived ritual duration, you could have a house which heals you as you spend time there, or a damaging effect to ward off anyone who tries to invade your Sanctum/temple/Ruin of the Time Before, or a cabinet which repairs objects you put inside... Targeting all valid subjects at the time of triggering.<br /> <br /> But if you have an AoE which turns people into frogs (or raises the dead as zombies) then it automatically applies while they are valid targets but ends as soon as the leave the area (i think it would be nice to have symmetry with leaving the 'time' which the spell has duration, like leaving the end of a finite duration spell also means you are no longer affected by it .. but not sure that is applicable to all time-travel use-cases. Like does using Temporal Stutter to escape a curse work?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T10:57:24-07:00","id":1522910,"title":"","content":"Here's the deal:<br /> <br /> Continuous effect spells cast on a number of subjects will affect those subjects until the spell ends, no matter where they are.<br /> Continuous effect spells cast on an area will affect all valid subjects within the area and all valid subjects who enters that area until they leave or the spell ends.<br /> Instantaneous effect spells cast on a number of subjects will periodically take effect on those subjects until the spell ends, no matter where they are.<br /> Instantaneous effect spells cast on an area will periodically take effect on all valid subjects who are within that area at the time, until the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T12:40:58-07:00","id":1522916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522893#post1522893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cast on a wide area doesn't add new subjects who enter the area after the casting, although subjects who were within the area when it was initially cast continue to be affected if they leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big problem with this interpretation is that it renders Subjects as the Range factor for a spell basically pointless.<br /> <br /> How many people can you fit into a supermarket? A couple hundred? If you can do that with a -4 penalty, why would you ever bother casting a spell to affect 160 subjects with a -10 penalty?<br /> <br /> I'm sure a person could say that they'd want to cast on a large number of people but not <i>everybody</i> within the area, but I think the circumstances in which one is being so discriminating are just so uncommon as to not justify the distinction. I have to imagine that in the majority of cases, if you're casting a spell to affect a large group of people, you intend to cast it on all of them together.<br /> <br /> So then having a Range factor based in numbers and based in Area that do the same thing ends up favouring the latter to the point that the former becomes irrelevant.<br /> <br /> (Plus the fact that there is Fate magic to already selectively exclude subjects from Area spells.)<br /> <br /> So Area works on everything valid that walks in, and stops working on whatever walks out. It's the targeting factor for when you want to bestow a quality on a location. If you want the spell to travel with the targets, it needs to go by numbers, with all the penalties that go with that.<br /> <br /> It makes it a steeper penalty to cast a spell on the same number of people as an area that gets to go with them, but conversely the largest area you can cast on could affect hundreds or thousands of people for the cost of it staying in place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a enough of a distinction that I'd personally disallow a Rote/Praxis of <u>Oaths Fulfilled</u> to be used to create this &quot;zone of awareness&quot;. Still works fine for tagging a bunch of people, which potentially serves the same purpose if there isn't much traffic into or out of the designated area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with that approach is that it's trying to make range into a function of spell effect, when that isn't how any other magic in the game works. What a spell affects is very thoroughly consolidated under the Range spell factor; there's no such thing as a spell that creates a zone, there is a spell whose targeting has been calibrated to the scale of a zone. Effect is what you make happen within the zone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It justifies an anti-magic field spell being perfectly viable</div> </div> </div> </div>What would an anti-magic field do if its Range factor only gave it a target of one?<br /> <br /> What would it do if its Range was made into the area of a college campus?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T17:53:32-07:00","id":1522929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522916#post1522916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would an anti-magic field do if its Range factor only gave it a target of one?<br /> <br /> What would it do if its Range was made into the area of a college campus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you asking what Dispel Magic does? And what it would do with a potency of 6 in an area of affect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T18:18:16-07:00","id":1522930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1522929#post1522929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you asking what Dispel Magic does? And what it would do with a potency of 6 in an area of affect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm asking how a person proposes a spell that acts as an anti-magic field distinct from Dispel Magic could function in the context of how the range spell factor works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T18:22:32-07:00","id":1523110,"title":"","content":"As per Signs of Sorcery:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brontium<br /> offers a +2 tool Yantra to spells that deflect, protect, or<br /> redirect magic. Additionally, items crafted of Brontium<br /> grant the user a +2 bonus to defend against <b>debilitating<br /> effects</b>.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Questions arise:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What exactly are &quot;<b>debilitating effects</b>\u200b&quot; for this purpose? Just Supernal magic effects? Any supernatural attack? Will it work on a sickness / poison roll?</li> <li>The +2 Yantra bonus is to (bolded part is mine): deflect <b>magic</b>, protect <b>from magic</b>, or redirect magic right? Or is a +2 to <b>any </b>deflective spell, +2 to <b>any </b>protective magic?</li> <li>How much material percentage would a tool need to be made to have the 9-again / Yantra bonus from being a Perfected Material? For example, I want a Lunargent Pen for a Free Council character, the pen exterior and some internal parts can be silver, but certainly it will have other components made from plastic.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-25-2023, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T20:39:27-07:00","id":1523115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1523110#post1523110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per Signs of Sorcery:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Questions arise:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What exactly is are &quot;<b>debilitating effects</b>\u200b&quot; for this purpose? Just Supernal magic effects? Any supernatural attack? Will it work on a sickness / poison roll?</li> <li>The +2 Yantra bonus is to (bolded part is mine): deflect <b>magic</b>, protect <b>from magic</b>, or redirect magic right? Or is a +2 to <b>any </b>deflective spell, +2 to <b>any </b>protective magic?</li> <li>How much material percentage would a tool need to be made to have the 9-again / Yantra bonus from being a Perfected Material? For example I want a Lunargent Pen for a Free Council character, the pen outside and some internal parts can be silver, but certainly it will have other components.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head, without knowledge of whether someone confirmed otherwise:<br /> <br /> 1. It should work on 'all' debilitating effects (that do allow for resistance or contests) like poison, disease, infirmity, pain, etc. But only for those that somehow work on the body, since it's of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> 2. The former sounds more logical. Again, thinking of the supernatural vigor of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd say only the core symbolic part counts. So for a metal-tipped pen, only the tip itself. Now, an exact percentage, I wouldn't know... best let in-universe mages Obsess over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T20:12:04-07:00","id":1523250,"title":"","content":"Tome of the Pentacle briefly mentions a group of Abyssal mages who live in the 11 missing days left over from the switch to the Gregorian calendar. Is this expanded on anywhere else or is it just a fun riff on Faction Paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T21:28:00-07:00","id":1523251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1523250#post1523250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tome of the Pentacle briefly mentions a group of Abyssal mages who live in the 11 missing days left over from the switch to the Gregorian calendar. Is this expanded on anywhere else or is it just a fun riff on Faction Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t recall anything concrete, but that sounds like something higher-standing members of the Cult of the Doomsday Clock Legacy would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T01:54:23-07:00","id":1523265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1523250#post1523250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or is it just a fun riff on Faction Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking that up, it looks too neat not to be just a reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T08:11:54-07:00","id":1523274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1523115#post1523115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off the top of my head, without knowledge of whether someone confirmed otherwise:<br /> <br /> 1. It should work on 'all' debilitating effects (that do allow for resistance or contests) like poison, disease, infirmity, pain, etc. But only for those that somehow work on the body, since it's of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> 2. The former sounds more logical. Again, thinking of the supernatural vigor of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd say only the core symbolic part counts. So for a metal-tipped pen, only the tip itself. Now, an exact percentage, I wouldn't know... best let in-universe mages Obsess over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Another two questions<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Amalgams are said to &quot;retain the Supernal properties of both combined metals&quot;, so it means that all Amalgams materials count as Mastigos and Acanthus magical tools (providing the 9-again bonus)?</li> <li>Fabricating Perfected Metals &quot;requires an object made entirely out of the intended Perfected metal\u2019s mundane counterpart.\u200b&quot;, so if I buy this <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cross-Classic-Sterling-Ballpoint-H3002/dp/B000F0QMBG/ref=sr_1_4?keywords=sterling%2Bsilver%2Bpens&amp;qid=1695913767&amp;sr=8-4&amp;th=1\" target=\"_blank\">pen</a>, that is 92% silver and I pass it enough times through Twilight it will never become a Lunargent pen? Do I need to get the Lunargent first and then mould it into the pen?</li> </ol>Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T12:25:08-07:00","id":1523283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1523274#post1523274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Another two questions<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Amalgams are said to &quot;retain the Supernal properties of both combined metals&quot;, so it means that all Amalgams materials count as Mastigos and Acanthus magical tools (providing the 9-again bonus)?</li> <li>Fabricating Perfected Metals &quot;requires an object made entirely out of the intended Perfected metal\u2019s mundane counterpart.\u200b&quot;, so if I buy this <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cross-Classic-Sterling-Ballpoint-H3002/dp/B000F0QMBG/ref=sr_1_4?keywords=sterling%2Bsilver%2Bpens&amp;qid=1695913767&amp;sr=8-4&amp;th=1\" target=\"_blank\">pen</a>, that is 92% silver and I pass it enough times through Twilight it will never become a Lunargent pen? Do I need to get the Lunargent first and then mould it into the pen?</li> </ol>Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can get a pen, remove the non-silver parts (so long as the silver bits are pure silver) pass them in and out of twilight, and then once you have Lunargent you should be able to put the pen back together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T21:57:25-07:00","id":1524615,"title":"","content":"Does it particularly break/affect anything to houserule that spells like <u>Analyze Life</u>, <u>Soul Marks</u>, or <u>Know Nature</u> instead work like <u>Supernal Vision</u>? That is, instead of it giving a detailed readout of the target, the spell allows the target to study valid subjects for the Duration and get [Potency] points of information each turn they do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T23:28:32-07:00","id":1524619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524615#post1524615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it particularly break/affect anything to houserule that spells like <u>Analyze Life</u>, <u>Soul Marks</u>, or <u>Know Nature</u> instead work like <u>Supernal Vision</u>? That is, instead of it giving a detailed readout of the target, the spell allows the target to study valid subjects for the Duration and get [Potency] points of information each turn they do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any that I can see immediately. Although, someone will probably ask why fix what's not broken.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically, since Soul Marks is an Unveiling spell just like Supernal Vision, and since Unveiling spells expand the subject's senses, Soul Marks has ground for working like Supernal Vision. Less so for the other two, which are Knowing spells that directly plant knowledge in the caster's mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T02:01:04-07:00","id":1524624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524619#post1524619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not any that I can see immediately. Although, someone will probably ask why fix what's not broken.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically, since Soul Marks is an Unveiling spell just like Supernal Vision, and since Unveiling spells expand the subject's senses, Soul Marks has ground for working like Supernal Vision. Less so for the other two, which are Knowing spells that directly plant knowledge in the caster's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just on the last part. If they are knowing spells, then there is an equivalent unveilib spell which would act like supernal vision, right (using creative thaumatergy as required).<br /> <br /> So what are the relevant upsides and downsides to casting a knowing spell vs an unveiling spell to gain the same info?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T04:34:19-07:00","id":1524628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524624#post1524624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just on the last part. If they are knowing spells, then there is an equivalent unveilib spell which would act like supernal vision, right (using creative thaumatergy as required).<br /> <br /> So what are the relevant upsides and downsides to casting a knowing spell vs an unveiling spell to gain the same info?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I can't answer that, since it's an intuitive thing for me, in the sense that I don't put much conscious thought on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T05:23:07-07:00","id":1524630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524615#post1524615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it particularly break/affect anything to houserule that spells like <u>Analyze Life</u>, <u>Soul Marks</u>, or <u>Know Nature</u> instead work like <u>Supernal Vision</u>? That is, instead of it giving a detailed readout of the target, the spell allows the target to study valid subjects for the Duration and get [Potency] points of information each turn they do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than how knowledge is gained through each of the two Practices, Unveiling spells are easier to turn into Legacy attainments since they don't have to waste Reach on range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T08:03:35-07:00","id":1524638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524630#post1524630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than how knowledge is gained through each of the two Practices, Unveiling spells are easier to turn into Legacy attainments since they don't have to waste Reach on range.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of why I'd want to change them, or at least AL. Night Horrors combines <u>Analyze Life</u> with <u>Supernal Vision</u> for the Perfected Adepts, and the result is functionally incomprehensible.<br /> <br /> It's also kinda inconsistent - what makes the information gained from AL Knowing, but SV or SM Unveiling? Both seem like Knowing, going purely off their effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-28-2023, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:18:12-07:00","id":1524643,"title":"","content":"Unveiling spells reveal hidden or abstract things, whereas Knowing spells give you information about a targeted subject \u2014 before Mage Sight was an Attainment, all the spells that provided a form of Mage Sight were Unveiling spells, and Soul Marks and Supernal Vision similarly are Unveiling because without supernatural powers a character simply would not be able to perceive souls or Arcana competency without being shown them in another manner. There are a few outliers on this front, like Tune In or Web of Life, but generally speaking if a spell deals with a specified target instead of opening up a new avenue of perception it's a Knowing spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:38:58-07:00","id":1524645,"title":"","content":"But there's no particular reason you couldn't make an Unveiling version of <u>Analyze Life,</u> right? Through Creative Thaumaturgy, if nothing else. Because on the laundry list of stuff that AL gives you with one Casting, an entity's Attributes and whether or not they are supernatural (even if shapeshifted into human form) isn't usually something you could discern. At least with Unveiling the logic would be that the spell is aiding your ability to interpret subtle cues, like how <u>Heightened Senses</u> enhances how you process sensory information.<br /> <br /> It's already weird that AL is a Duration-primary spell. I guess it's so you can monitor the subject? Like a videogame HUD of your party's health and status effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-28-2023, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T05:10:59-07:00","id":1524683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524645#post1524645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an entity's Attributes and whether or not they are supernatural (even if shapeshifted into human form) isn't usually something you could discern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that a being's strength is something that can be determined by having them lift things, and some of the features that constitute being supernatural could be identified with a few observations.<br /> <br /> Mind, it isn't expressed as identifying the supernatural explicitly, just that such beings are a bit beyond the scope of the spell until the caster becomes familiar with them.<br /> <br /> I think the problem with &quot;use Creative Thaumaturgy to make any Knowing spell an Unveiling one&quot; is that the method of acquiring the information through imagery that one can look at doesn't really change the scope or experience of the spell, it's just looking for a way to get what is functionally the exact same effect without needing to worry about Scale factors.<br /> <br /> I think your Unveiling spell along similar lines would be something like being able to perceive the influences that come in and potentially affect a subject's physical well being. You could go into somewhere with some significant contamination and be able to trace that back to its source. Or follow the lines of influence back to a source of food that is improving somebody at the moment.<br /> <br /> As far as Web of Life being Knowing goes, I think that's a spell that is more functionally direct if it's just a tally popped into somebody's brain rather than requiring them to look around and see all of the green lights hanging over living things or whatever.<br /> <br /> I do think Tune In is simply given its Practice in error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T06:40:47-07:00","id":1524688,"title":"","content":"If you want to differentiate Knowing and Unveiling, I think these guidelines might help:<br /> <br /> Knowing is about gaining the information you want to know about. It grants knowledge unfiltered by your senses.<br /> Unveiling is about perceiving more of the world around you. It expands your senses and allows you to observe more information through them.<br /> <br /> So with Knowing you should be able to gain relatively deep or targeted* information by casting the spell directly on a subject. Analyze Life, Know Nature and Soul Marks (despite being listed as Unveiling) are definitely this type of spell.<br /> <br /> Unveiling complements this by granting you the ability to perceive similar information by augmenting your own senses. The information granted should be cursory or, if relatively deep, require a turn's studying to discern. Speak With the Dead** (the reveal Rank and Anchors part) and Interconnections are good examples of this type of spell.<br /> <br /> Supernal Vision breaks this by being the expanded perception type of Unveiling spell that requires a turn's studying, but also grants both deep and targeted information like a knowing spell. I'd absolutely split it into two: One Unveiling spell which grants the common information from the first part, and one Knowing spell which grants a number of facts from the list in the second part of the spell.<br /> <br /> There are also other types of spells for both Practices, which helps differentiate the two:<br /> Knowing can grant real-time updates on certain triggers on the subject (like Oath's Fulfilled), or surrounding information like the intended fuction of a tool (like Craftman's Eye***), or by simply locating something within an AoE that you couldn't perceive (Locate Object).<br /> Unveiling can, of course, expand your senses in various wild and interesting ways (Nightvision, Receiver, Heightened Senses, the Outward and Inward Eye, Exorcist's Eye, etc).<br /> A less common type of Unveiling spell which kinda infringes on Knowing by virtue of bringing forth information that simply isn't perceptible, is the one that brings forth that information in order to allow you to perceive it through your senses (Postcognition)***.<br /> <br /> Now, for detection spells like Web of Life (listed as Knowing) and Detect Matter (listed as Unveiling), I can't really say which Practice fits best. It really depends on how you envision them. They do grant information you can't perceive directly to you like a Knowing spell, but you could absolutely argue that you're given a new sense that picks up these things outside of your regular senses. As written, I think both those spells should be Knowing as they are written in the book (gaining information about a specific area rather than being sensed by the mage), but changing them to work in an area around the subject (subject detects all things within X meters per Potency rather than using AoE on a specific area) would definitely turn them into Unveiling spells.<br /> If you don't want both versions to be possible, I'd slot this type of spell into Knowing because that's how the two (or three with Locate Object) spells of this type is already written to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tune In is absolutely the wrong Practice because &quot;the ability to hear radio waves&quot; is specifically listed as an example under Unveiling.<br /> <br /> *Any spell which grants a number of facts equal to Potency is an example of a spell giving you targeted information. You choose the <br /> <br /> **Speak With the Dead should not be cast as an AoE spell, and instead instead work more like Exorcist's Eye. It makes little sense under these guidelines, and is just weird regardless because you can have a conversation with a ghost be cut short because the ghost walked a few steps in the wrong direction left the AoE.<br /> <br /> ***Craftman's Eye is listed as a Knowing spell and grants information that I think fits Knowing, but is cast on a subject who then studies the tool for a turn like an Unveiling spell. I'd definitely remove that part and have the tool be the spell's subject.<br /> <br /> ****A Knowing version of Postcognition could instead grant you more targeted information, such as the exact time a specific event happened as well as a number of facts surrounding that event, but not allow you to view it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T07:14:38-07:00","id":1524691,"title":"","content":"I mean, the biggest reason it's all inconsistent is that a bunch of different people wrote the spells. Quoting Daveb in a Discord comment from 03Oct2023:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Arcana were written by five people - 1) Time, 2) <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/478634844532768768/534428245211217940/1158845411889524916\" target=\"_blank\">Forces, Life, 3) Death, Mind, 4) Spirit, Prime, Space, Matter, 5) Fate</a> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T10:18:39-07:00","id":1524693,"title":"","content":"Would an Unveiling of Life and Spirit be able to detect vampires? The idea would be that it highlights beings with external life forces within them (vitae), with the cursed, bloody and predatorial Resonances on them, which I think are passively emitted due to the nature of vampirism. With a Reach allowing them to differentiate between ghoul and vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T12:35:23-07:00","id":1524701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524693#post1524693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an Unveiling of Life and Spirit be able to detect vampires? The idea would be that it highlights beings with external life forces within them (vitae), with the cursed, bloody and predatorial Resonances on them, which I think are passively emitted due to the nature of vampirism. With a Reach allowing them to differentiate between ghoul and vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Arcana are relevant to Vitae varies. In first edition (Tome of the Mysteries) you'd need Prime and Death to detect it. In second edition (PGttCC) it's instead Death and Life. Unless your table has houseruled how Vitae relates to the Arcana, you'd need one of those combinations depending on the edition.<br /> <br /> Spirit (specifically Active Spirit Sight) can tell you which Resonant Conditions apply, which in turn means the resonances need to be strong enough that spirits can be sustained by them. Not the most reliable way of deducing whether someone is a vampire. If you want a less brute force method for discerning resonances, you'd have to use Prime instead.<br /> <br /> As for discerning between vampires and ghouls, if you have either Life or Death in the spell then detecting whether they're alive or dead should be child's play and not require a Reach, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T08:50:21-07:00","id":1524808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524688#post1524688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> Tune In is absolutely the wrong Practice because &quot;the ability to hear radio waves&quot; is specifically listed as an example under Unveiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree with most of the above, the weakness of Tune In (if it was unveiling) would be that seeing/hearing radio waves doesn't tell you what they mean (which would arguably involve the Mind arcanum's communication purview).<br /> <br /> But as a Knowing spell is has been argued that the symbolic meaning of the radio waves can be directly known to the caster.<br /> <br /> So it sounds like it is a weird mix of Knowing and Unveiling as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T21:21:34-07:00","id":1524957,"title":"","content":"If an Attainment is cast at sensory range, can the mage be given the option to pay a mana to activate sympathetic range, or does it always need to default to sympathetic range ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T22:03:36-07:00","id":1524958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1524957#post1524957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Attainment is cast at sensory range, can the mage be given the option to pay a mana to activate sympathetic range, or does it always need to default to sympathetic range ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it\u2019s fixed, unless the Attainment states otherwise. Either cast it as a normal spell, or learn the other version as a novel Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T06:53:20-07:00","id":1524973,"title":"","content":"The target for <i>Transmission</i> is the somewhere where the signal is, rather than whoever is editing the data, correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T11:15:38-08:00","id":1525263,"title":"","content":"Multiple social and magical questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can Tremere create soul stones? Their soul status is unusual to say the least.</li> <li>If previous question answer is YES, can you learn the Tremere transformation from said soul stones?</li> <li>As per Signs of Sorcery characters that awaken during play would need to acquire all normal advantages (High Speech, Order Status, Rotes, etc), how much would cost to buy Rote Skills? 1 xp per skill?</li> <li>Tied with the previous question. Can you be part of the Order if you buy only the Status dot, and no Rotes nor Rote Skills? (I imagine that this is easier for Free Council, almost impossible for lets say Mystagoges).</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T13:25:08-08:00","id":1525267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525263#post1525263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Tremere create soul stones? Their soul status is unusual to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can make hollowstones, as described in Nameless and Accursed, but the mechanical costs of soul stones and don't really mesh with the changeover to Hollow, nor does the demesne-based usage really scan for beings who no longer have a Path, so I'd say &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If previous question answer is YES, can you learn the Tremere transformation from said soul stones? </div> </div> </div>Even if the answer was &quot;yes,&quot; the Tremere transformation requires an external actor with the highest degree of status among the Tremere to perform the Hollowing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As per Signs of Sorcery characters that awaken during play would need to acquire all normal advantages (High Speech, Order Status, Rotes, etc), how much would cost to buy Rote Skills? 1 xp per skill? </div> </div> </div>Rote Specialties are conventionally provided as the third-dot benefit of a Mystery Cult Initiation representing a Nameless Order. (The Sects provide them with the first dot and the Tremere provide them at the second dot, but they're more potent/organized groups.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T13:31:16-08:00","id":1525268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525267#post1525267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rote Specialties are conventionally provided as the third-dot benefit of a Mystery Cult Initiation representing a Nameless Order. (The Sects provide them with the first dot and the Tremere provide them at the second dot, but they're more potent/organized groups.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, just to be clear, I am asking for an awakened character in play, normal human becomes mage, not starting the game as a mage.<br /> <br /> If I am Jack McNormal, I awaken (1 Gnosis, 3 dots of Ruling Arcana), and when I buy the first dot of Order status I get the 3 rote specialties? No extra XP cost to learn them, that is you what you are saying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-09-2023, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T14:51:56-08:00","id":1525271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525268#post1525268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer, just to be clear, I am asking for an awakened character in play, normal human becomes mage, not starting the game as a mage.<br /> <br /> If I am Jack McNormal, I awaken (1 Gnosis, 3 dots of Ruling Arcana), and when I buy the first dot of Order status I get the 3 rote specialties? No extra XP cost to learn them, that is you what you are saying?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of mechanical notes to the contrary and with the caveat that Status dots are narratively acquired with more investment than their Experience cost would suggest, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T18:00:54-08:00","id":1525280,"title":"","content":"Project Nightfall, from 1e's Guardian book, would be what in 2e? Faction? Mystery Cult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T14:08:30-08:00","id":1525327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525280#post1525280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Project Nightfall, from 1e's Guardian book, would be what in 2e? Faction? Mystery Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it really qualifies as a Mystery Cult (beyond the extent to which that just codifies how the Labyrinth worked before anyway), just because I didn't get the impression that it was based on initiating members of the US intelligence community.<br /> <br /> I suppose it kind of resembles what the game calls factions (which was already a thing in First Edition anyway, and was indeed first introduced to the line in the same book as Project Nightfall).<br /> <br /> I don't think everything necessarily requires a box to go in, and indeed I think what was supposed to make Project Nightfall most ominous was the sense that there wasn't really anything else like it in the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose, recalling some of how Dave described it once, it could be kind of described as something like a quasi-Nameless Order growing within the ranks of the Guardians, diverging away from their usual creeds and hierarchy in a state of concealment.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps just something like a heretical sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T15:47:04-08:00","id":1525331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525280#post1525280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Project Nightfall, from 1e's Guardian book, would be what in 2e? Faction? Mystery Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the impression that they were a cabal whose numbers placed them within range of becoming a Nameless Order, and orbiting dangerously close to Panopticon's train of thought. By that I mean that I wouldn't be surprised if they had stolen souls stones and Daimonomika of the <i>Architects of the Future</i> and <i>Princes of Many Masks.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T23:55:10-08:00","id":1525339,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the Princes would be a perfectly acceptable Legacy for the Faceless or the Legion of the Lost. It's <i>creepy</i>, and pretty morally questionable/easy to abuse, but it's in-line with the Order.<br /> <br /> The <i>Architects</i> though... yeah, hard to justify one predicated on divining the will of the Exarchs, beyond maybe learning their plans to better counter them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T06:21:34-08:00","id":1525398,"title":"","content":"A couple of Rote Skills and Mystery Cults questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you get more than 3 rote skills? (Like being part of a regular order and infiltrating another? Or being part of an order and using the Mystery Cult Initation in another nameless order? Using a masque, etc).</li> <li>If you switch orders, what happens with the previous order rote skils? Are replaced by the new ones? A blend of your choosing? You keep them?</li> <li>How do start a Mystery Cult in Game? What is the minimum number of &quot;believers&quot; you need for it to be functional?</li> <li>Can I be part of an Order (using Order Status) and a Nameless Order (using Mystery Cult Initation)?</li> </ol>Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T07:43:06-08:00","id":1525399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525398#post1525398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of Rote Skills and Mystery Cults questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you get more than 3 rote skills? (Like being part of a regular order and infiltrating another? Or being part of an order and using the Mystery Cult Initation in another nameless order? Using a masque, etc).</li> <li>If you switch orders, what happens with the previous order rote skils? Are replaced by the new ones? A blend of your choosing? You keep them?</li> <li>How do start a Mystery Cult in Game? What is the minimum number of &quot;believers&quot; you need for it to be functional?</li> <li>Can I be part of an Order (using Order Status) and a Nameless Order (using Mystery Cult Initation)?</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I tend to rule that if you have the honorary &quot;Status 1&quot; in another Order, you get their Rote Skills and Yantras. It's entirely predicated on you buying into that Order's philosophy <i>and</i> syncratisizing it with that of your own order, though. Masque is likely limited to the Yantras/Rote Skills of the personality they take on - while using their Silver Ladder personal, they can only use SL trappings and not Guardian trappings.<br /> <br /> 2. Since I think Rote Skills work off of how much you buy in to the Order's philosophy, leaving your Order loses you those Rote Skills IMO.<br /> <br /> 3. Good question... does Giest specify? I know they have pretty good Mystery Cult rules. I'd say three people minimum, but that's entirely baseless.<br /> <br /> 4. If anyone can do it, the Free Council would. They're meant to be an alliance of many Nameless Orders anyway. I'd <i>generally</i> say yes, but maybe tweek it so the Rote Skills at tier 3 are instead a new Yantra. Or borrow the mechanics for Court Goodwill from Changeling. Far from a hill I'd die on though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T09:11:27-08:00","id":1525402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525398#post1525398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you get more than 3 rote skills? (Like being part of a regular order and infiltrating another? Or being part of an order and using the Mystery Cult Initation in another nameless order? Using a masque, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Tome of the Pentacle, being a member of an Order Faction with three dots in the Merit for membership gives you a fourth Rote Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do start a Mystery Cult in Game? What is the minimum number of &quot;believers&quot; you need for it to be functional? </div> </div> </div>Per the unabbreviated Merit from the ChroD corebook, the things you need for a Mystery Cult in the Merit system (rather than the organizational system) are a Purpose, a Relic, and a Doctrine; Geist's expansion into the organizational rules posits that a krewe has about ten members per dot of the group's Resistance Attribute (Esotery 1 krewes start with six dots to distribute between their three Attributes on top of the first dots, to a maximum of 5 in any Attribute, so that's 10-50), not counting the PCs, and the krewe creation process recommends every player create at least one living krewe member and at least one ghost krewe member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T17:06:41-08:00","id":1525667,"title":"","content":"Can Mages cast the rotes in the books as improvised spells? For example, if I have Time 3 and want to cast Acceleration but don't have it as a rote, can I do that and simply not gain the Mudra Yantra bonus for it? If so, can I use the additional reach effects listed under the power, or only use the baseline description for Acceleration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T17:13:15-08:00","id":1525668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525667#post1525667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages cast the rotes in the books as improvised spells? For example, if I have Time 3 and want to cast Acceleration but don't have it as a rote, can I do that and simply not gain the Mudra Yantra bonus for it? If so, can I use the additional reach effects listed under the power, or only use the baseline description for Acceleration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes in the books, as in, the corebook's Chapter 4 and such? Yeah. All printed spells are example spells, not example Rotes. Reach effects are likewise fully accessible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T19:05:11-08:00","id":1525669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525667#post1525667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages cast the rotes in the books as improvised spells? For example, if I have Time 3 and want to cast Acceleration but don't have it as a rote, can I do that and simply not gain the Mudra Yantra bonus for it? If so, can I use the additional reach effects listed under the power, or only use the baseline description for Acceleration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell you have the Arcana ratings for can be cast as an improvised spell with the printed Reach options and any others you and your Storyteller can come up with and agree on; the benefits of rotes are chiefly in being safer to cast and/or push one's limits with than improvised spells, particularly early on when low Gnosis and Arcana limit your casting pool, available Mana, and free Reach otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T19:36:59-08:00","id":1525670,"title":"","content":"Really, none of the spells printed in the core book are innately rotes, and it actually is just a master list of sample (and probably common in-character) improvised spells. A person has the option to learn them as rotes in play, because the mechanical distinction between those types of spell are fairly small (if quite consequential).<br /> <br /> That's why they all get potential rote skills, something to select and attach in the event of learning a rote version of any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T23:54:00-08:00","id":1525710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525667#post1525667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages cast the rotes in the books as improvised spells? For example, if I have Time 3 and want to cast Acceleration but don't have it as a rote, can I do that and simply not gain the Mudra Yantra bonus for it? If so, can I use the additional reach effects listed under the power, or only use the baseline description for Acceleration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick note: you don't gain the yantra bonus unless you are casting from memory (or you created the rote). Casting from a grimoire gives you the rote quality instead and doubles the casting time.<br /> <br /> Basically you can either learn the rote (spend XP) and cast it from memory, gaining the mnemonic benefit. Or you can cast it from a grimoire and not from your memory and gain all the other benefits of a rote while casting a ritual speed and doubling your ritual time.<br /> <br /> Only the creator of a rote can get both the rote quality and the mnemonic benefit (yantra bonus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T05:56:19-08:00","id":1525724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525710#post1525710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the creator of a rote can get both the rote quality and the mnemonic benefit (yantra bonus).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. Casting a rote as its creator or casting it from a grimoire as a double-length ritual to gain the rote benefit is an additive trade, not a swap for the availability of the Mudra Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T12:28:18-08:00","id":1525744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525724#post1525724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is incorrect. Casting a rote as its creator or casting it from a grimoire as a double-length ritual to gain the rote benefit is an additive trade, not a swap for the availability of the Mudra Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I think the phrasing of &quot;casting the rote from memory, using an Order's recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra&quot; is very specific.<br /> <br /> Likewise, it states that the rote bonus comes from casting out of a Grimoire, not from memory (or if you invented it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T13:28:41-08:00","id":1525745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525744#post1525744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I think the phrasing of &quot;casting the rote from memory, using an Order's recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra&quot; is very specific.<br /> <br /> Likewise, it states that the rote bonus comes from casting out of a Grimoire, not from memory (or if you invented it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in the text does it state that a Mudra Yantra is mutually incompatible with casting it from a grimoire. The Scribe Grimoire spell describes the process as giving physical form to the mudras of the rote. The section on Rotes where the &quot;from memory&quot; section comes from also describes the benefits in terms of efficiency. The Spellcasting Quick Reference section just says &quot;May use Mudra Yantras&quot; with no conditional aspects.<br /> <br /> The mechanical functions of rotes are to be safer to cast and thereby easier to consistently push one's limits with. The rote quality primarily makes a roll less likely to fail and spellcasting has a hard floor for automatic failure based on dice penalties (chiefly from spell factors), which Yantras chiefly serve to offset.<br /> <br /> It makes zero sense for casting from a grimoire to remove one of the largest benefits they offer in exchange for doubled ritual casting time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T14:18:55-08:00","id":1525747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525745#post1525745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the text does it state that a Mudra Yantra is mutually incompatible with casting it from a grimoire. The Scribe Grimoire spell describes the process as giving physical form to the mudras of the rote. The section on Rotes where the &quot;from memory&quot; section comes from also describes the benefits in terms of efficiency. The Spellcasting Quick Reference section just says &quot;May use Mudra Yantras&quot; with no conditional aspects.<br /> <br /> The mechanical functions of rotes are to be safer to cast and thereby easier to consistently push one's limits with. The rote quality primarily makes a roll less likely to fail and spellcasting has a hard floor for automatic failure based on dice penalties (chiefly from spell factors), which Yantras chiefly serve to offset.<br /> <br /> It makes zero sense for casting from a grimoire to remove one of the largest benefits they offer in exchange for doubled ritual casting time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are entirely explicit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Casting a Rote from a Grimoire rather than from memory, or casting a Rote she designed herself, gives the mage\u2019s spellcasting dice pool the rote quality. When casting a Rote from memory, using an Order\u2019s recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra </div> </div> </div>When casting from memory you gain the Yantra bonus.<br /> <br /> When casting from a grimoire <b>rather than from memory</b> you can get the rote quality.<br /> <br /> It is spelt out really clearly.<br /> <br /> As to why, you get free reach, don't have to spend XP to learn the rote, and your Nimbus is obscured when casting from a grimoire, all advantages of a rote.<br /> <br /> The downside of swapping a +1-5 (*6 with order rote specialisation) yantra bonus for rote quality (effectively doubling your chances of at least 1 success) is likewise very strong/worthwhile tradeoff, even with the ritual duration (doubled).<br /> <br /> *The is an argument that you can't get +6 for the yantra bonus even with the specialisation, and I think Word of God on the issue. But by the rules it seems to be allowed, and I think an additional rule in SoS let's you get to +7 for certain characters.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, it is Exoteric Rote from TotP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  corrections 11-21-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T14:35:32-08:00","id":1525748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525745#post1525745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the text does it state that a Mudra Yantra is mutually incompatible with casting it from a grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it doesn't use that exact sequence of words. It just has text attaching the rote benefit to &quot;rather than from memory&quot; and the mudra bonus to &quot;when using Order recall techniques&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scribe Grimoire spell describes the process as giving physical form to the mudras of the rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spells of that Arcanum were written by a different person to whomever wrote the rote rules, I do not think a piece of flavour text overrides the meaning of actual text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spellcasting Quick Reference section just says &quot;May use Mudra Yantras&quot; with no conditional aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think being a quick reference makes it necessarily abridged, in a manner that does not give it equal or greater standing than the actual text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes zero sense for casting from a grimoire to remove one of the largest benefits they offer in exchange for doubled ritual casting time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it creates a harder incentive to actually spend XP on learning the rote, rather than constantly needing to reference a book.<br /> <br /> Like, the mudras are described primarily as memory mnemonics, I think that by itself renders it incompatible with the process of reading the precise formula of the spell's Imago off of a reference point. The mnemonic adds the Skill rating by basis of being the foundation of how the Imago is remembered at all; your Computers Skill is helping to stand in for having a detailed description of the spell's mental image. If you actually have the detailed description in front of you, your Skill is unnecessary and irrelevant, in a way that also has a consequence of meaning that it can't really be used to fill out the Imago. But the precise formula provides the alternative way to build it that gets represented as the rote quality.<br /> <br /> I think they get set apart by virtue of the fact that a Grimoire is a means of forming an Imago completely different from all other spellcasting, the rote quality being the mechanical benefit representing the relief of that mental burden. Mudras are what you get out of knowing a rote in a way that makes casting it a lot more like the conventions of an improvised spell; it takes place fully within the mind, and hence requires the mental reference points that Yantras provide.<br /> <br /> If I was concerned with elaborating the flavour text of Scribe Grimoire, it would be in terms of how it seems like the formulae that a Grimoire's form consists of are translated out of the Imago shortcuts provided by the Mudras, but the translation is such that it still quite changes the manner in which mages can read them; like converting a tonal language into a series of Latin characters that approximate the same sounds. The formula of the Grimoire can be studied in a manner that a mage can internalise the codified Imago, but they still need the reference points of a Mudra to make that work.<br /> <br /> That the Orders know how to teach a way to translate Grimoire formulae and Yantra mnemonics back and forth is a sophisticated and proprietary piece of information that is part of the benefit of having done this for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> I would consider the description of the Create Rote Attainment not specifically stating that Mudras are a requirement to teach rotes from mage to mage to be a <i>possible</i> complication in this argument, but the point that Mudras <i>must</i> be utilised in casting a rote from memory and that Mudras are taught specifically by Orders is so clearly stated by their respective sections that I don't think an inference by omission overrides that. So for lone Nameless who become Masters, their only recourse for spreading their own rotes is to turn them into Grimoires, and any other Nameless who read those can only cast them out of the book and with the rote benefit. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T14:48:19-08:00","id":1525750,"title":"","content":"Aside; masters who create a rote are not getting any extra free reach (since they already have mastery) but instead get both rote quality and the rote mundras, which seems like a nice bit of balance.<br /> <br /> I don't see anything in the rote creation which suggests a nameless Master can't teach the rote mundras to another nameless. What they don't get is Order specialisation bonus for rotes encoded with the skills the order is better at.<br /> <br /> (And I think understanding this better by looking at how to alter the skill used to encode mundras would be illustrative... )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scribe Grimoire spell describes the process as giving physical form to the mudras of the rote. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how this is relevant at all.<br /> <br /> Scribe grimoire let's you imprint the specific Supernal meanings (not just a textual description) which allows another mage to learn the rote.<br /> <br /> But it is only when casting <b>from memory</b> that you get the mundra bonus. When casting from a physical representation you are not doing the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T15:05:22-08:00","id":1525751,"title":"","content":"I think I get where the disconnect comes from: interpreting \u201cIf P, then Q\u201d phrases.<br /> <br /> Casual reading tends to equate that with \u201cIf NotP, then NotQ\u201d and then interprete \u201cIs NotP, and is NotQ\u201d instances as supporting it.<br /> <br /> But reading it via deductive reasoning, an \u201cIf P, then Q\u201d statement implies nothing about the truthfulness of instances that include \u201cIs NotP\u201d, because that\u2019s not what the statement deals with.<br /> <br /> So when the text says \u201cIf CastFromMemory, then Mudra\u201d, an argument could be made that this text doesn\u2019t actually say anything about whether \u201cIs NotCastFromMemory, and Is Mudra\u201d is true or \u201cIs NotCastFromMemory, and Is NotMudra\u201d is true. Judging which one is true would require one to look at other parts of the corpus\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026 which kinda mixes up lore and mechanics as usual for CofD books, hence the confusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> For myself, I\u2019m inclined to let Mudras apply to Grimoire-cast Rotes too. Less because of the logics stuff I wrote above, but more because I like the aesthetics of Rotes being this bridge between Fallen knowledge and Supernal practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T16:34:15-08:00","id":1525758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525751#post1525751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> &lt;Snip&gt;<br /> So when the text says \u201cIf CastFromMemory, then Mudra\u201d, an argument could be made that this text doesn\u2019t actually say anything about whether \u201cIs NotCastFromMemory, and Is Mudra\u201d is true or \u201cIs NotCastFromMemory, and Is NotMudra\u201d is true. Judging which one is true would require one to look at other parts of the corpus\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026 which kinda mixes up lore and mechanics as usual for CofD books, hence the confusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> For myself, I\u2019m inclined to let Mudras apply to Grimoire-cast Rotes too. Less because of the logics stuff I wrote above, but more because I like the aesthetics of Rotes being this bridge between Fallen knowledge and Supernal practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right it doesn't say &quot;only when cast from memory&quot;, but that isn't the style of the book. Mixing lore with mechanics leads to things like &quot;Mundras are Supernal mnemonics taught by orders&quot; (not Only the orders, or nameless order are a type of order?)<br /> <br /> I think that is a fair application of your logic. Not sure the crunch should have it applied the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T19:27:14-08:00","id":1525766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525747#post1525747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to why, you get free reach, don't have to spend XP to learn the rote, and your Nimbus is obscured when casting from a grimoire, all advantages of a rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am specifically talking about casting a rote you know with the aid of a grimoire. I have no issue with &quot;casting a spell you don't know as a rote from a grimoire does not give you access to its encoded Mudra Yantra,&quot; but I don't forget how ROYGBIV and SOHCAHTOA work just because I have my textbooks open and I firmly believe a character should not be rendered <i>less</i> able to increase the Potency of a spell by spending <i>more</i> time on casting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T22:26:51-08:00","id":1525770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525766#post1525766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't forget how ROYGBIV and SOHCAHTOA work just because I have my textbooks open</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can be taken as a case where priorities for game balance can align with an idea that the mental processes that create a spell are distinct from other ones.<br /> <br /> It can be thought of as similar to how the Conditions that arise from Acts of Hubris aren't valid as subjects for pattern restoration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T00:11:17-08:00","id":1525774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525766#post1525766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am specifically talking about casting a rote you know with the aid of a grimoire. I have no issue with &quot;casting a spell you don't know as a rote from a grimoire does not give you access to its encoded Mudra Yantra,&quot; but I don't forget how ROYGBIV and SOHCAHTOA work just because I have my textbooks open and I firmly believe a character should not be rendered <i>less</i> able to increase the Potency of a spell by spending <i>more</i> time on casting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are quite clear, the only exception is when you are the creator of the rote, not when you happen to know it.<br /> <br /> You can either cast from memory and use mnemonics, or cast from the physical representation of those rotes in a grimoire.<br /> <br /> I don't know what your argument is, but the difference between reading a text a book and remembering what is in the book seems obvious.<br /> <br /> Mechanically the game is very specific, unless your are the creator of the rote you have to make a choice.<br /> <br /> Game balance, being the creator makes perfect sense, and having a menaingful choice otherwise almost makes perfect sense from a game design perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T04:44:22-08:00","id":1525786,"title":"","content":"Lorewise, when you cast a Rote from a Grimoire you construct the imago from the instructions within. When you use the Mudra, you're using mnemonics to aid constructing the imago from your memory.<br /> Using both would be the same as constructing something using two sets of instructions. If it's two instructions for two different Rotes (even if the base spell is the same) then it's obvious to me you can't combine them. But if the Grimoire contains the same Rote you've memorized, then it wouldn't be illogical to supplement your following of the instructions with the information you already have, but on the other hand for IRL skills that generally just means it doesn't take as long as you don't have to spend as much time interpreting the instructions in front of you.<br /> <br /> Textwise, it's clear as day. The book separates casting from a Grimoire and casting from memory, and gives two different sets of rules associated with each. You can't use the Mudra when casting from a Grimoire.<br /> <br /> Dev clarification-wise, I don't think we have any explicit confirmation either way, but we do have some strong evidence leaning towards a literal interpretation of the book. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page174#post1062962https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062741#post1062741\">Here</a> I answered a different question about Rotes, and mentioned that you probably can't combine Grimoires and Mudras as an aside. The lead dev at the time <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062962#post1062962\">confirmed</a> my answer, and even though he didn't directly refer to this subject I strongly doubt he'd ignore an error in a post he otherwise agreed with as an answer to a rules question.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:14:46-08:00","id":1525800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525786#post1525786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dev clarification-wise, I don't think we have any explicit confirmation either way, but we do have some strong evidence leaning towards a literal interpretation of the book. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page174#post1062962https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062741#post1062741\">Here</a> I answered a different question about Rotes, and mentioned that you probably can't combine Grimoires and Mudras as an aside. The lead dev at the time <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1062962#post1062962\">confirmed</a> my answer, and even though he didn't directly refer to this subject I strongly doubt he'd ignore an error in a post he otherwise agreed with as an answer to a rules question.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>He refers to &quot;just borrowing a Grimoire,&quot; which is the specific thing I am saying I am <i>not</i> contesting doesn't give you access to a mudra you haven't internalized. Dave was answering a question about whether you <i>had to </i>use the Mudra Yantra when casting a spell as a rote (which you don't).<br /> <br /> Grimoires give you the rote action quality because having the steps laid out in front of you is one of the textbook sources for rote actions. You can learn the mudras for a rote's encoded Skill by studying the grimoire and spending Experiences to learn it, but you don't lose the ability to perform mnemonic gestures just because you have instructions in front of you.<br /> <br /> Rote action is a dice trick. It gives better returns with bigger dicepools and worse returns with smaller ones. On a failed initial roll, rote action alone translates to a single reroll of the base pool, and unlike in 1e where extended casting was a thing, 2e handles all casting in the fashion that provides extra spell factors by making the dicepool smaller.<br /> <br /> The bonus from a Mudra Yantra being based on your dots in an encoded Skill is 2e's carryover of 1e making rote spells an Attribute + Skill + Arcanum roll instead of a Gnosis + Arcanum roll. 1e's grimoire-creating spell had no other benefit than allowing a character who didn't know the rote to cast it and giving characters who <i>do</i> know the rote a +1 bonus to the casting roll, with the net result being that (provided a character with high Gnosis + Arcanum ratings isn't using a rote whose roll involves Traits they have bad ratings in) using a grimoire increases your odds of success.<br /> <br /> I do not believe the intention of an edition where grimoires were specifically tweaked to be more desirable (and where scribing a grimoire does not remove your knowledge of a rote) is to make using your own notation on a codified spell that you know <i>stop</i> you from using the tools you have for casting efficiently to reliably add more spell factors to its casting, particularly given that spellcasting is not a purely intellectual process and doubling your casting time can translate to as little as twenty minutes (without factoring in extremely powerful Time magic) and Signs of Sorcery notes that rotes created without the Sects' compression techniques can't even be cast instantly \u2014 i.e. if a Nameless Order mage learns a rote from one of their Masters and then scribes a grimoire of it, they can benefit from its encoded Skill if they take half an hour to cast it, but under the reading being proposed they can't do so if they take a full hour to cast it.<br /> <br /> It is clear as day that if you didn't create the rote you only get rote action on the casting if you're casting with the benefit of a grimoire. The core developer clarified that you don't <i>have to </i>use a Mudra Yantra when you're casting a spell as a rote and that simply casting out of a borrowed grimoire doesn't allow you do so. These things do not directly imply that you cannot mechanically combine reading from a spellbook and doing ritual gestures over an extended period of time despite being able to spend that same amount of time without the book and get a <i>bigger</i> bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T14:58:25-08:00","id":1525812,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that Dave didn't directly address this point. <i>I specifically and explicitly stated as much.</i><br /> <br /> I might address the rest of your post when I have the energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T17:26:30-08:00","id":1525815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525812#post1525812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that Dave didn't directly address this point. <i>I specifically and explicitly stated as much.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And I specifically and explicitly stated that I wasn't talking about the thing that Dave <i>was</i> unambiguously talking about in his parenthetical, after it had already been pointed out that a statement that casting a rote from a grimoire instead of from memory being a condition for getting the dice trick on a rote does not logically necessitate that you cannot benefit from the tools the study of that grimoire will grant a character to cast the rote without it at the same time. You can presumably understand why I moved to bring in additional points instead of simply repeating my initial statement in frustration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I might address the rest of your post when I have the energy. </div> </div> </div>I would frankly not bother unless you can come up with a direct citation or dev clarification, because so far the &quot;clear rules&quot; that have been cited are the contrapositive of the statement under discussion and the fact that the book mechanically distinguishes casting from a Grimoire and casting from memory alone.<br /> <br /> Stylistically there is no reason a character should lose the benefits of their rote's ritual gestures while they are opting to benefit from a reference Imago. Mechanically there is no reason a character referencing a Grimoire they have already studied should be required to substitute different Yantras or spend <i>even more time</i> on the casting to get the same dicepool with the same factors they would get ritual casting without the Grimoire when no other method of applying rote action to spellcasting rolls applies this restriction on top of their existing risks or costs. Historically the game has made Grimoires allow for an additive bonus to spellcasting rolls in addition to their function as learning implements, with the only possibility of the tool making you do a worse job is if you are specifically worse at the skills that tool uses.<br /> <br /> Given all this, &quot;You cannot use what is probably the single biggest Yantra bonus you could get from knowing this spell if you also use its blueprints as a reference&quot; is an extraordinary claim which requires much more definite evidence than the separation of Grimoires' mechanical effects on casting a rote from the mechanical effects of knowing its Mudra. Changing my mind on this would take at the very least a persuasive argument concerning what genre emulation conceits or game balance concerns are supported by removing a substantial dice bonus from consideration in return for a dice trick instead of allowing the two to be combined when both are available, and if neither that nor a direct statement by the books or the developers or writers are readily available then it may be prudent to save your energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T22:31:00-08:00","id":1525824,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've made as much argument as I think is necessary, and I only intend or expect it to be convincing to external observers anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T13:22:31-08:00","id":1525863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525824#post1525824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've made as much argument as I think is necessary, and I only intend or expect it to be convincing to external observers anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The rules are quite clear.<br /> <br /> There is no reason stylistic or mechanical for it to work the way it does, except that this is precisely how the rules say it works.<br /> <br /> I was surprised when someone first pointed this out, because it seemed odd and coming from 1st ed hadn't noticed it, but upon reading the rules a few more times, I had to admit I was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T15:10:45-08:00","id":1525887,"title":"","content":"Since Space has the purview of sympathy, would a Knowing allow one to learn a target's sympathetic name ? If so, would a Reach be enough to learn their Shadow Name as well or would conjunctional Prime be needed instead ? Would it be viable for a 2 Reach effect to tell them the power it holds, such as how many dots of the Shadow Name merit they have or detecting a Rapt by checking if the person's sympathetic name still holds power ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T16:12:20-08:00","id":1525889,"title":"","content":"Shadow Name stuff tends to be Mind-adjascent, so I'd probably lean with that over Prime. I could certainly see the argument for Prime though, since that largely deals with symbolism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T17:01:38-08:00","id":1525890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525887#post1525887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Space has the purview of sympathy, would a Knowing allow one to learn a target's sympathetic name ? If so, would a Reach be enough to learn their Shadow Name as well or would conjunctional Prime be needed instead ? Would it be viable for a 2 Reach effect to tell them the power it holds, such as how many dots of the Shadow Name merit they have or detecting a Rapt by checking if the person's sympathetic name still holds power ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Yes for a Space Knowing spell to learn a sympathetic name..... but I feel it's just as viable to say No, since that the efforts of ferreting out someone's name (or protecting it) is an important enough genre convention that powering through it with a single spell is too crude.<br /> <br /> For expanding from sympathetic names to Shadow Names, looking at the Unnaming spell, I'd say you need Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T20:49:09-08:00","id":1525896,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, how would you represent a PC Suscepter embedded in a different Order? Masque 5, with some of the &quot;free&quot; dots at tier 5 going to Order Status? Or just use the &quot;honorary&quot; 1-dot and call it a day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T22:15:37-08:00","id":1525901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525896#post1525896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, how would you represent a PC Susceptor embedded in a different Order? Masque 5, with some of the &quot;free&quot; dots at tier 5 going to Order Status? Or just use the &quot;honorary&quot; 1-dot and call it a day?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than using a Masque, I think you could take a page from how D'Eon does it in page 32 of <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i>, by giving equivalent Order status dots that would become Notoriety dots if they are found out and they don't justify themselves extremely well before the Lex Magicka (they could probably expect a challenge to a Duel regardless). <br /> <br /> Infiltrating the other Orders is covered by a tab about it in page 55 of the <i>Guardians of the Veil</i> book. In short, the philosophy of each Order deeply shapes how one practices the Art, not being able to use the rote skills, mudras and not being familiar with the secret society's small details would be a dead giveaway. So they would need some kind of strategy to dodge that bullet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T22:20:59-08:00","id":1525902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525901#post1525901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infiltrating the other Orders is covered by a tab about it in page 55 of the <i>Guardians of the Veil</i> book. In short, the philosophy of each Order deeply shapes how one practices the Art, not being able to use the rote skills, mudras and not being familiar with the secret society's small details would be a dead giveaway. So they would need some kind of strategy to dodge that bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing a long-con of a supposed Red Veil failure would be my go-to choice, but that has broader implications about the state of the Consillium","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T10:12:20-08:00","id":1525912,"title":"","content":"I feel as though a Susceptor actually going undercover in another Order is unnecessarily difficult and risky for getting the kind of information that they're looking for. I would expect that it is both more suitable for their remit and more engaging narrative if they identify somebody within the other Order that can be leveraged to act as the observer on their behalf.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that &quot;members of other Orders&quot; isn't just the mages. There are probably a lot more things one can get Sleepwalkers on to have them pass information. They might even be a bit easier to utilise, if they can often not be so heavily scrutinised by Order members.<br /> <br /> For that matter, if a Susceptor did want or need to get hands on with the work, passing oneself off as a Sleepwalker might be easier than seeking full initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T12:02:25-08:00","id":1525915,"title":"","content":"The Sleepwalker approach is really elegant. They are privy to important information and are not expected to cast anything. With a mix of Space and Prime, they could make a spell to fake the ability to hold spell control for Medium sympathetic connections (taxing their own spell slots) and they would be good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T13:43:44-08:00","id":1525976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525915#post1525915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker approach is really elegant. They are privy to important information and are not expected to cast anything. With a mix of Space and Prime, they could make a spell to fake the ability to hold spell control for Medium sympathetic connections (taxing their own spell slots) and they would be good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean hiring a sleepwalker or a guardian using a masque to pretend to be a sleepwalker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-26-2023, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T14:47:07-08:00","id":1525982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1525976#post1525976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean hiring a sleepwalker or a guardian using a masque to pretend to be a sleepwalker?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using a Masque to pretend to be one. Keep your spells and Nimbus Veiled, get some entry level Order status, then position yourself to get information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T06:11:30-08:00","id":1526055,"title":"","content":"I don't think Masques are strictly necessary, or even specifically useful, to pass for a Sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T11:41:21-08:00","id":1526072,"title":"","content":"Would a Making of Life and Mind be enough to make a gate to bodily enter any part of the Astral the mage has been to before ? If so, would it be reasonable that casting it inside an Oneiros would allow them to re-enter the material in front of the person ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T12:00:02-08:00","id":1526074,"title":"","content":"IIRC, one needs Archmastery to bodily enter the Astral. At least, that's how I remember 1e's writeup on entering the Astral via the Golden Road","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T15:03:36-08:00","id":1526083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526072#post1526072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Making of Life and Mind be enough to make a gate to bodily enter any part of the Astral the mage has been to before ? If so, would it be reasonable that casting it inside an Oneiros would allow them to re-enter the material in front of the person ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll have to reread stuff, but I think it\u2019s one of the few things standard Awakened magic can\u2019t do?<br /> <br /> IF it\u2019s possible in the first place, I think Life 4 + Mind 4 will suffice. Homing in to realms you\u2019ve visited before will require extra spellwork involving Space (and maybe Mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T17:05:58-08:00","id":1526090,"title":"","content":"Making spells don't fully limit you to things that currently exist, but I do think they have certain limitations on how far their creations can depart from the normal functions of reality. Something like the strictures for what Life can conjure.<br /> <br /> I think transferring your full physical existence into the Astral Realms falls under that, primarily because it seems weird given the nature of what the Astral and travel into it even is. There's no substance to it, it's an intense shift in perception through the structure of your self and connection to the wider universe. <br /> <br /> On top of everything, what's really the use of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T17:44:44-08:00","id":1526095,"title":"","content":"Transit, maybe? I feel like Patterning yourself into a Goetia would be a more productive effort than Bodily walking into the Astral though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T17:47:27-08:00","id":1526096,"title":"","content":"The two published unambiguous vectors for bodily entry into the Astral are through Primordial Pathways \u2014 the sympathy/resonance-based power of a monster that is explicitly rarer than mages to overlap its unusually material corner of the Astral with an external location, which specifically needs to be used instead of the method resembling ordinary travel to accomplish this outcome because otherwise you simply switch to functional Astral projection from the Lair \u2014 and the Rip the Gates Exploit \u2014 a sideways hack of the metaphysical framework of a world-spanning occult engine, powered by the magical entropy of that system under the direction of its not-entirely-real rogue processes, or a volatile material expression of that power.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, much as Mage's systems do not enable Travelers to accomplish the sort of time-travel shenanigans that the Arisen can drift into (or, if the stories are to be believed, some Reborn can manage with intent), they also present a perspective on the Astral where, without a Mystery saying otherwise, the types of Goetia characters are most likely to deal with do not possess means of affecting the physical world without spells from other Subtle Arcana to grand them those capabilities and Irises into the Astral are means of quickly projecting your senses to a given part of the Dreamtime or the collective unconscious.<br /> <br /> The implication being that bodily messing around with the inner worlds is the domain of archmasters, half-natives, metaphysical outcasts, and other weird exceptions. Mastery of Life and Mind lets you instantiate a thinking body <i>ex nihilo</i>, but so far 2e has not presented anything to contradict Astral Realms' statement that you can't scry or transport yourself out of the Astral (and, by implication, similarly cannot leverage external sympathy in other ways without leaving its frame of reference).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T18:47:45-08:00","id":1526098,"title":"","content":"Activated Attainments, like the 11Q's The Chance Answer, or a Metropolitan's Geomantic Peregrination, twig Peripheral Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> What about always-on Attainments, like a Metropolitan's Follow The Thread, 11Q's The Undisturbed Scene, or any of the Genius Perfected Adept Attainments? On the one hand, they're Attainments, but on the other they are more like fundamental changes to the very nature of the Mage. Does someone with an always-on Attainment constantly ping on PMS?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T19:21:34-08:00","id":1526100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526098#post1526098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Activated Attainments, like the 11Q's The Chance Answer, or a Metropolitan's Geomantic Peregrination, twig Peripheral Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> What about always-on Attainments, like a Metropolitan's Follow The Thread, 11Q's The Undisturbed Scene, or any of the Genius Perfected Adept Attainments? On the one hand, they're Attainments, but on the other they are more like fundamental changes to the very nature of the Mage. Does someone with an always-on Attainment constantly ping on PMS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per SoS, PMS detects <i>active</i> unconcealed effects, with provided examples that are activated effects. Much as I wouldn't make every vampire with a physical Discipline set a mage's thumbs a-prickling just from having more dots of Strength or Stamina than their build might suggest, in the absence of a modification like the &quot;Eyes&quot; Attainments of the Subtle Arcana or the Mana Sensitivity Merit my reading would be that Legacy Attainments that are a thing about the way the character interacts with the world rather than a thing they actively do do not trigger the Periphery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T06:53:54-08:00","id":1526110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526095#post1526095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transit, maybe? I feel like Patterning yourself into a Goetia would be a more productive effort than Bodily walking into the Astral though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the idea was to teleport out of danger without using Space. But the Goetia transformation solves it, being a reliable panic button feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:46:41-08:00","id":1526122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526110#post1526110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, the idea was to teleport out of danger without using Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like an unnecessarily extreme method of achieving a fairly mundane outcome, not least because Mastery of at least one of those Arcana already affords a few means of getting out of danger.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T16:22:47-08:00","id":1526140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526110#post1526110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the idea was to teleport out of danger without using Space. But the Goetia transformation solves it, being a reliable panic button feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like if you are a Master of Life and Mind you have a number of better panic-button options than trying to Pattern yourself into a phase of Twilight that doesn't normally interface with physical reality, particularly given that both Paths for which this double-Mastery would come easiest have a second Ruling Arcanum that manages it without trying to ignore everything the games say about how accessible the Astral is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T16:26:24-08:00","id":1526141,"title":"","content":"OK, that's great and all, but Kaiser's question wasn't &quot;<i>should</i> I do this?&quot;, it was &quot;<i>can</i> I do this?&quot;. We answered that, criticizing the question really isn't adding anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T17:21:26-08:00","id":1526142,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Left-Handed Legacy based on mindflayers, utilizing Life and Mind. Mindflayers have a once a day teleport on themselves, so I was trying to see if there was a way to do it with that Arcana combination. Move to the Astral and then to an ally in the material, not exactly a true teleport, but close enough. So asking if that Arcana combination could do it was deliberate.<br /> <br /> Cauthon's goetia idea provides another thematic approach, which is becoming a being of pure psychic energy, which is a different type of psychic horror, but could go in a direction similar to the Ethereals from XCOM 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T23:48:55-08:00","id":1526160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526142#post1526142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for a Left-Handed Legacy based on mindflayers, utilizing Life and Mind. Mindflayers have a once a day teleport on themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can capture the essence of the concept without needing to reproduce every small detail.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T05:51:09-08:00","id":1526179,"title":"","content":"Its still in the sketching phase, thinking about possible approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T06:55:15-08:00","id":1526201,"title":"","content":"The Paternoster's Prelacy Crown allows them to heal Resistant damage. What, if any, scenarios would allow a Pentacle Mage a similar power? A Legacy Attainment that allows them to heal from even Resistant Damage at an accelerated rate, ala the <u>Body Mastery</u> spell? A Mystery Cult Initiation whose capstone allows them use Pattern Restoration like a Paternoster Prelate? Something else entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T11:15:33-08:00","id":1526204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526201#post1526201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paternoster's Prelacy Crown allows them to heal Resistant damage. What, if any, scenarios would allow a Pentacle Mage a similar power? A Legacy Attainment that allows them to heal from even Resistant Damage at an accelerated rate, ala the <u>Body Mastery</u> spell? A Mystery Cult Initiation whose capstone allows them use Pattern Restoration like a Paternoster Prelate? Something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoning an appropriate Supernal Being, and artifact with Imperial level effects, befriending an Archmaster, a boon from on of the Aeons, maybe a side effect of some unusual emanation realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T22:37:26-08:00","id":1526265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526201#post1526201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Paternoster's Prelacy Crown allows them to heal Resistant damage. What, if any, scenarios would allow a Pentacle Mage a similar power? A Legacy Attainment that allows them to heal from even Resistant Damage at an accelerated rate, ala the <u>Body Mastery</u> spell? A Mystery Cult Initiation whose capstone allows them use Pattern Restoration like a Paternoster Prelate? Something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Atlantean Ruin that was used for healing (likely Arrow or Mysterium), &quot;selling&quot; the injury away as part of an Unchained Pact, a healing goblin fruit, altering a blood bather's ritual so the life energy is used to heal you instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T02:09:31-08:00","id":1526270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526265#post1526265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Atlantean Ruin that was used for healing (likely Arrow or Mysterium)</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the orders didn't exist until much later, so it would be the hypothetical pre-fall equivalents which may or may not have inspired the Arrow and Mysterium to varying degrees, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Alae Draconis, the Wings of the Dragon </div> </div> </div>And<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Ungula Draconis, the Talon of the Dragon </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T13:17:34-08:00","id":1526329,"title":"","content":"So Detect Substance feels has always felt to me like it should've been a Knowing spell, but what would a more standard Unveiling Matter spell be like? Perception of invisible substances (ex. dark matter)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T14:05:02-08:00","id":1526330,"title":"","content":"A <i>Detect Cyborg</i> spell, which highlights any beings that have a high level of technology in their organism. So the Unchained would stand out (since it is not detecting the power source), the Lost Boys' mechanical augmentations as well and members of the Austere Legacy too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T19:28:05-08:00","id":1526337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526329#post1526329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Detect Substance feels has always felt to me like it should've been a Knowing spell, but what would a more standard Unveiling Matter spell be like? Perception of invisible substances (ex. dark matter)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Steel Windows spell from 1e is a Ruling spell that makes an opaque object the caster touches transparent, or vice-versa. That should be a Weaving spell in retrospect, but you could make it an Unveiling spell, e.g. see through [Potency] feet of continuous matter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T04:47:33-08:00","id":1526398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526337#post1526337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Steel Windows spell from 1e is a Ruling spell that makes an opaque object the caster touches transparent, or vice-versa. That should be a Weaving spell in retrospect, but you could make it an Unveiling spell, e.g. see through [Potency] feet of continuous matter</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to understand the difference between ruling and weaving here.<br /> <br /> For matter, transparency is a question of wavelengths of light and the electrons interacting with them. Some things, like wood, should require weaving (because science) while others like metal should only require a sligth tweak to the plasma frequencies of their electron seas, ie ruling.<br /> <br /> But this Mage not physics class. Symbolically what is transparency m, and how does one determine whether it should be ruling or weaving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T05:44:15-08:00","id":1526399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526398#post1526398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to understand the difference between ruling and weaving here.<br /> <br /> For matter, transparency is a question of wavelengths of light and the electrons interacting with them. Some things, like wood, should require weaving (because science) while others like metal should only require a sligth tweak to the plasma frequencies of their electron seas, ie ruling.<br /> <br /> But this Mage not physics class. Symbolically what is transparency m, and how does one determine whether it should be ruling or weaving?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaving simply changes the property itself, increasing transparency. The effect goes away once the spell ends.<br /> <br /> Accomplishing the same with Ruling would require you to perceive the molecular structure, such as by using the 2 Reach version of <i>Zoom In</i>, plus an Intelligence + Science roll to make sure you know exactly what you are doing. Well, if you are manipulating electrons, it probably needs a Forces spell as well. But by the end, you could make permanent changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T13:29:05-08:00","id":1526418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526398#post1526398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to understand the difference between ruling and weaving here.<br /> <br /> For matter, transparency is a question of wavelengths of light and the electrons interacting with them. Some things, like wood, should require weaving (because science) while others like metal should only require a sligth tweak to the plasma frequencies of their electron seas, ie ruling.<br /> <br /> But this Mage not physics class. Symbolically what is transparency m, and how does one determine whether it should be ruling or weaving?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rely on intuition and aesthetics a lot when determining Practices, so it\u2019s hard for me to explain succintly\u2026\u2026 Looking at other spells as given examples, Matter Ruling includes things like Shaping and Find the Balance, while Matter Weaving includes things like Alter Conductivity and State Change. Changing transparency certainly seems closer to the latter, so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T20:24:49-08:00","id":1526435,"title":"","content":"Does a Demesne's effects extend to the Twilight of the area it covers, and, similarly, would a Demesne whose &quot;heart&quot; is located in Twilight still extend its normal effects to the material plane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T20:38:08-08:00","id":1526436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526435#post1526435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Demesne's effects extend to the Twilight of the area it covers, and, similarly, would a Demesne whose &quot;heart&quot; is located in Twilight still extend its normal effects to the material plane?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say Yes for both, with the oft-repeated reminder of Twilight being a state in the Material World. Of course, exceptions like Neter-Khertet may complicate things, and random Mysteries could screw enough with local reality I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T07:45:59-08:00","id":1526449,"title":"","content":"Since the Reach effect of <i>Supernal Vision</i> establishes that Prime can tell what is supernatural or not (even if it cannot provide finer details by itself), then would adding Prime 2 to a <i>Ban</i> allow it to only block the supernatural ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T01:25:20-08:00","id":1526510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526449#post1526449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Reach effect of <i>Supernal Vision</i> establishes that Prime can tell what is supernatural or not (even if it cannot provide finer details by itself), then would adding Prime 2 to a <i>Ban</i> allow it to only block the supernatural ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Prime has &quot;Magic&quot; in its purviews, I guess it depends on whether they are magical creatures.<br /> <br /> I would lean towards yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T16:55:33-08:00","id":1526539,"title":"","content":"On p. 193 of the corebook, it says that Mage Armors that increase Defense work on surprise attacks. However, p. 217 under &quot;Surprise&quot; being successfully ambushed means you can't apply your Defense. Does this mean that:<ul><li>those particular Armors allow you to apply Defense to surprise attacks?</li> <li>while you can increase your Defense with Mage Armor, it doesn't do anything for that attack (but it would apply on subsequent attacks)?</li> <li>only the boost from those Armors apply to the surprise attack?</li> </ul><br /> Book's a little unclear on the matter. Personally, I'd run with the second option since a surprised mage should be a sitting duck, it generates a feeling of paranoia within players when they know they're dealing with enemies who know how to effectively fight mages, and it encourages mage characters to engage in <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">Xanatos Gambits</a>; which I absolutely love.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe I'm missing something, so an official word on the matter would be nice. Unofficial answers are just as welcome, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T17:22:20-08:00","id":1526542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526539#post1526539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>only the boost from those Armors apply to the surprise attack?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Specific rules trump general ones, so: the PC has an effective defense of zero when surprise attacked, then Mage Armor kicks in and provides its benefit (which does not include applying *full* defense against surprise attacks, just the defense it provides).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T18:20:48-08:00","id":1526543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526539#post1526539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book's a little unclear on the matter. Personally, I'd run with the second option since a surprised mage should be a sitting duck, it generates a feeling of paranoia within players when they know they're dealing with enemies who know how to effectively fight mages, and it encourages mage characters to engage in <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">Xanatos Gambits</a>; which I absolutely love.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe I'm missing something, so an official word on the matter would be nice. Unofficial answers are just as welcome, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of their mechanism, the function of Mage Armor is to reduce damage from or through the medium of their Arcana. Activating Mage Armor being reflexive is the main way that allowing non-Armor Mage Armors to apply against surprise attacks is relevant; if you want to circumvent a mage's Mage Armor, you hit them with something their current Armor doesn't apply to.<br /> <br /> My reading is your third option, under the same math as Inodiv describes above; the Armor is still reducing damage, just not to the degree it would if you were fully aware of the attack instead of reacting to it by reflexively triggering your magical defenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T19:21:18-08:00","id":1526544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526543#post1526543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of their mechanism, the function of Mage Armor is to reduce damage from or through the medium of their Arcana. Activating Mage Armor being reflexive is the main way that allowing non-Armor Mage Armors to apply against surprise attacks is relevant; if you want to circumvent a mage's Mage Armor, you hit them with something their current Armor doesn't apply to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a very good point; I like it. So I take it that Mage Armor which grants an actual armor rating or downgrades damage can also be applied to surprise attacks, as well? If not, that seems to be a huge benefit the Defense Armors are getting that the other Armors aren't, unless I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526543#post1526543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading is your third option, under the same math as Inodiv describes above; the Armor is still reducing damage, just not to the degree it would if you were fully aware of the attack instead of reacting to it by reflexively triggering your magical defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering what Inodiv said about specific rules trumping general rules, that would make the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T20:41:18-08:00","id":1526546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526544#post1526544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a very good point; I like it. So I take it that Mage Armor which grants an actual armor rating or downgrades damage can also be applied to surprise attacks, as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The most reliable way to stop a mage who has Mage Armors for all your avenues of attack from applying them is to catch them without enough Mana to raise or switch to an applicable one; the cost is the balancing mechanism for the fact that a Mage Armor can be activated at any point without taking appreciable time in the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T08:50:18-08:00","id":1526678,"title":"","content":"<i>Word of Command</i> bypasses the activation conditions of Supernal related items. So does that mean that if, for example, if the mage was using an imbued item of an Arcana that they have no dots in, they could activate it like they had scored [Prime] successes on the spellcasting roll ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T16:58:52-08:00","id":1526688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526678#post1526678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Word of Command</i> bypasses the activation conditions of Supernal related items. So does that mean that if, for example, if the mage was using an imbued item of an Arcana that they have no dots in, they could activate it like they had scored [Prime] successes on the spellcasting roll ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be so.<br /> <br /> Although, Imbued Items roll the <i>Imbued spell's</i> Arcanum rating + the user's Gnosis, so the user's own Arcana dots (or lack thereof) won't matter in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T01:45:52-08:00","id":1526694,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, imbued items aren't totally useless to people who already possess the Arcana to cast those spells, but the value is so much higher for people that do not that I think it would naturally provoke questioning the idea that such people would be severely disadvantaged in using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T07:33:43-08:00","id":1526704,"title":"","content":"I don't recall seeing this clarified.<br /> <br /> The rule for Liches which become ephemerals (ghosts, goetia, or spirits) are to retain their gnosis and arcana, while using the rules for Supernal beings (on pg 253).<br /> <br /> Page 253 starts a whole set of rules for invisible entities, not much specific to Supernals on that page, so I am assuming it means that whole section.<br /> <br /> But I was assuming it meant &quot;use the rules for ghosts/goetia/spirits, except when spellcasting , in which case use the rules for Supernal beings&quot;.<br /> <br /> That would mean they get infinite reach, but paradox pool has the rote quality and deals aggravated damage (no paradox conditions).<br /> <br /> And rolling Power + Finesse (instead of Gnosis+Arcana) despite it explicitly saying you retain your gnosis and arcana?<br /> <br /> So now I am rather confused what it means about following the rules for Supernals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T10:37:08-08:00","id":1526707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526704#post1526704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall seeing this clarified.<br /> <br /> The rule for Liches which become ephemerals (ghosts, goetia, or spirits) are to retain their gnosis and arcana, while using the rules for Supernal beings (on pg 253).<br /> <br /> Page 253 starts a whole set of rules for invisible entities, not much specific to Supernals on that page, so I am assuming it means that whole section.<br /> <br /> But I was assuming it meant &quot;use the rules for ghosts/goetia/spirits, except when spellcasting , in which case use the rules for Supernal beings&quot;.<br /> <br /> That would mean they get infinite reach, but paradox pool has the rote quality and deals aggravated damage (no paradox conditions).<br /> <br /> And rolling Power + Finesse (instead of Gnosis+Arcana) despite it explicitly saying you retain your gnosis and arcana?<br /> <br /> So now I am rather confused what it means about following the rules for Supernals...</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that &quot;ghost mages&quot; who are just ghosts that used to be mages exist indicates to me that &quot;retain access to their Gnosis and Arcana&quot; means &quot;liches who have become invisible entities still cast Supernal magic rather than replicating their old rotes and Praxes with Numina and Influences.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T12:50:53-08:00","id":1526710,"title":"","content":"I don't know, it's under the systems header and is specifically phrased as &quot;retain access to their Gnosis and Arcana, using the systems for Supernal beings&quot;. Gnosis and Arcana both being system terms as well as in-character ideas. If it was intended to make the point more abstractly or poetically, I don't think it was a good place for it, but it does kind of read to me as an error.<br /> <br /> I have some reservations against ephemeral liches just straight up using Supernal being casting across the board, because it seems way too powerful. I think that's acceptable with actual Supernal beings because they're supposed to occupy a formidable place in the setting, in addition to some significant limitations and the assumption of personalities that give them specific ends they'd use their powers towards, but I think the place an immortal mage holds makes that a much more fraught prospect with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T12:59:45-08:00","id":1526711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526710#post1526710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, it's under the systems header and is specifically phrased as &quot;retain access to their Gnosis and Arcana, using the systems for Supernal beings&quot;. Gnosis and Arcana both being system terms as well as in-character ideas. If it was intended to make the point more abstractly or poetically, I don't think it was a good place for it, but it does kind of read to me as an error.<br /> <br /> I have some reservations against ephemeral liches just straight up using Supernal being casting across the board, because it seems way too powerful. I think that's acceptable with actual Supernal beings because they're supposed to occupy a formidable place in the setting, in addition to some significant limitations and the assumption of personalities that give them specific ends they'd use their powers towards, but I think the place an immortal mage holds makes that a much more fraught prospect with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend towards agreeing with this.<br /> <br /> On reading the casting rules for Supernals, the main thing it says is they &quot;follow the same rules as Awakened*&quot;... So following that, why wouldn't Ephemeral Liches just say they follow the normal rules too?<br /> <br /> My interpretation would be A) Liches don't have Rank, Manifestations or Influences, B) they do have Gnosis, Arcana and Attainments, C) the have Power/Finesse/Resistance - so you could infer they roll Power+Finesse and can/can't** use Yantras in the same way as Supernal beings... D) they are otherwise still mages, so paradox and reach should affect them normally. And E) the may have Essence instead of Mana, and I don't know, maybe I would err on assuming they have Mana as none of their powers work based on Essence... So I could kinda gpneither way on this one (or imagine different lich legacies actually result in different transformations, like a Spirit Life Patterning could leave you with an Essence pool and in the Spirit twilight, able to consume Essence like a spirit - but you could also have a seperate legacy which used only Mana to power their spells, or a third which had both Essence and Mana, and had different powers running off different fuel stats - maybe with essence driven powers lifted from the Shadow Occultist or Purified).<br /> <br /> I am pretty confident of A and B, I like D from a metaphysics point of view, I am less keen on being prescriptive about E and I am guessing about C as being the writer's intention in saying they use the rules for Supernals.<br /> <br /> *Does this mean Supernal beings can use Yantras, take part in teamwork rituals, and use Arcana attainments like a Mage?<br /> <br /> ** See the answer to the previous post script. And delete as appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"accidentally posted before i finishes writing). 12-12-2023, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T13:12:56-08:00","id":1526712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526707#post1526707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that &quot;ghost mages&quot; who are just ghosts that used to be mages exist indicates to me that &quot;retain access to their Gnosis and Arcana&quot; means &quot;liches who have become invisible entities still cast Supernal magic rather than replicating their old rotes and Praxes with Numina and Influences.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure, if that was the case they could have just said 'casts spell as per the usual spellcasting rules'...<br /> <br /> Also, are there Purified mages (ie the equivalent of ghost mages, who happen to have mundanely turned themselves into spirits?) Who wouldn't have Gnosis or Arcana, but would have whatever powers the Pruified get? (Plus replicating their old rotes and praxes with Numina and Influences).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T13:21:55-08:00","id":1526714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526707#post1526707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that &quot;ghost mages&quot; who are just ghosts that used to be mages exist indicates to me that &quot;retain access to their Gnosis and Arcana&quot; means &quot;liches who have become invisible entities still cast Supernal magic rather than replicating their old rotes and Praxes with Numina and Influences.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I am not sure, if that was the case they could have just said 'casts spell as per the usual spellcasting rules'... Also, are there Purified mages (ie the equivalent of ghost mages, who happen to have mundanely turned themselves into spirits?) Who wouldn't have Gnosis or Arcana, but would have whatever powers the Pruified get? (Plus replicating their old rotes and praxes with Numina and Influences).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T13:33:08-08:00","id":1526715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526712#post1526712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure, if that was the case they could have just said 'casts spell as per the usual spellcasting rules'...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, is the thing. They cast like Supernal beings do.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery's mechanics for ochemata has the avatars described therein cast like normal mages as a specific exception to their working like Supernal beings if they're the creations of archmasters. No manner of exception is described for ephemeral liches, who have stopped being things that can casually pass for a player character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, are there Purified mages (ie the equivalent of ghost mages, who happen to have mundanely turned themselves into spirits?) Who wouldn't have Gnosis or Arcana, but would have whatever powers the Pruified get? (Plus replicating their old rotes and praxes with Numina and Influences). </div> </div> </div>The Scions of God Legacy is the primary published example of where spirit-mages might come from \u2014 see page 77 of Legacies: the Sublime for a sidebar describing something that's definitely not a spirit-lich in 2e terms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T15:03:40-08:00","id":1526717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526715#post1526715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't, is the thing. They cast like Supernal beings do.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery's mechanics for ochemata has the avatars described therein cast like normal mages as a specific exception to their working like Supernal beings if they're the creations of archmasters. No manner of exception is described for ephemeral liches, who have stopped being things that can casually pass for a player character.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you are saying they have infinite reach, but take aggravated damage from paradox? And otherwise cast like Supernals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T15:58:04-08:00","id":1526719,"title":"","content":"<i>Cleanse the Body</i> mentioned it can allow a subject to purge toxins from their body, it also has a Reach option to make a roll to resist the toxin. What are the results for a failure or dramatic failure of the Reach effect ?<br /> <br /> How many of these rolls are needed to purge a toxin from a character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T17:49:39-08:00","id":1526726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526717#post1526717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are saying they have infinite reach, but take aggravated damage from paradox? And otherwise cast like Supernals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526719#post1526719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Cleanse the Body</i> mentioned it can allow a subject to purge toxins from their body, it also has a Reach option to make a roll to resist the toxin. What are the results for a failure or dramatic failure of the Reach effect ?<br /> <br /> How many of these rolls are needed to purge a toxin from a character?</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Poison&quot; on page 225 and &quot;Drugs&quot; on page 224. The Reach effect allows a character to make the same roll they would be making at the normal interval immediately as well as the next &quot;scheduled&quot; roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T02:01:57-08:00","id":1526734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526717#post1526717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are saying they have infinite reach, but take aggravated damage from paradox? And otherwise cast like Supernals?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what's written in the book, but I want to add that those are definitly just stopgap rules put in place to allow STs to use ephemeral liches before the actual rules are released (see how much Tremere and Scelesti were changed and expanded on in Nameless and Accursed). Unfortunately the book where they would've been included is cancelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T03:18:49-08:00","id":1526736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526734#post1526734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly what's written in the book, but I want to add that those are definitly just stopgap rules put in place to allow STs to use ephemeral liches before the actual rules are released (see how much Tremere and Scelesti were changed and expanded on in Nameless and Accursed). Unfortunately the book where they would've been included is cancelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see that interpretation of the books rules. I just thought it was vague and unclear (because there are no rules on pg. 253, just a section of rules starting there, and to make thing more confusing, Liches are supposed to be ephemerals and those exact rules starting there are the rules for ephemerals and Supernals... So it doesn't specify which bit of the rules for Supernals to use - like twilight manifestations seem to make sense, but no, per my reading a Supernal has to use their Arcana to move their body into twilight as they have no manifestations... I guess all Ephemeral Lich Legacies should have this as a Legacy Attainment).<br /> <br /> Seperate question, would it Lich Angels? (ie since Angles, Spirits and Ghosts are the main three ephemerals in the Blue book...). Should that be a Prime based legacy? Prime/Fate? God-Machine dedicated legacy? Has anyone written up such a thing?<br /> <br /> Can you use Prime to covert your body into an &quot;Angel twilight&quot; attuned one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T06:33:43-08:00","id":1526741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526736#post1526736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it doesn't specify which bit of the rules for Supernals to use - like twilight manifestations seem to make sense, but no, per my reading a Supernal has to use their Arcana to move their body into twilight as they have no manifestations...</div> </div> </div> </div>They're ephemeral beings of the type that they are, cast spells using the Supernal being mechanics, and presumably determine Rank by the Arcana they knew in line with the way Supernal beings have their maximum Arcana by Rank set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seperate question, would it Lich Angels? (ie since Angles, Spirits and Ghosts are the main three ephemerals in the Blue book...). </div> </div> </div>An angel of the type employed by the God-Machine was never human and becoming one would at best produce an extremely weird exile. Do what you like for you game, but this isn't a symmetry that makes natural sense in the cosmology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you use Prime to covert your body into an &quot;Angel twilight&quot; attuned one? </div> </div> </div>The angelic phase of Twilight exists and can presumably be accessed bodily using Prime and Fate the same as you would to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T07:07:39-08:00","id":1526747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526741#post1526741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're ephemeral beings of the type that they are, cast spells using the Supernal being mechanics, and presumably determine Rank by the Arcana they knew in line with the way Supernal beings have their maximum Arcana by Rank set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have assumed they have no rank, in the same way Ochemata are treated like supernal beings but have Gnosis rather than rank...<br /> <br /> And no influences/manifestations/numina - being that they have Arcana instead.<br /> <br /> And further assumed that they need mana rather than essence as their fuel stat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An angel of the type employed by the God-Machine was never human and becoming one would at best produce an extremely weird exile. Do what you like for you game, but this isn't a symmetry that makes natural sense in the cosmology. </div> </div> </div>I think it makes sense for a Mage to be obsessed with the God-Machine, but whether they would like to serve it as an exile would be much more unusual... But that approach to the conclusion does make sense. Any legacy dedicated to becoming an Angelic Lich ending up as Exiles seems the most reasonable... Trying to become a more Religious Angel might be more popular. I do like the concept of creating arbitrary twilights and being closer to the Supernal beings from their path...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The angelic phase of Twilight exists and can presumably be accessed bodily using Prime and Fate the same as you would to see it. </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Wasn't sure about the Fate part, I confuse the Promethean 'angels' and the Arcana required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:03:51-08:00","id":1526753,"title":"","content":"As I think about it, the other issue I'd take with just using unabridged Supernal being rules for such transformations is that it feels like a profound increase in power that strikes me as disconnected to whatever means of getting it, and arguably of much greater value than the immortality itself does.To me it seems to dilute the concept of liches a bit, coming across as more focused on becoming a ghost or spirit because it means you'll basically never have to worry about Paradox or advanced spell factors ever again, for some reason. To me, that feels like a greater negative than even what it might provide to their position as antagonists (or allies, really).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T10:27:59-08:00","id":1526766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526747#post1526747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have assumed they have no rank, in the same way Ochemata are treated like supernal beings but have Gnosis rather than rank...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ochemata have Rank, and the ones that cast like mages use their Rank as effective Gnosis. The same writeup also specifies that ochemata who aren't created by archmasters use their Arcana like other Supernal entities do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no influences/manifestations/numina - being that they have Arcana instead.<br /> <br /> And further assumed that they need mana rather than essence as their fuel stat.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This is also my reading.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526753#post1526753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I think about it, the other issue I'd take with just using unabridged Supernal being rules for such transformations is that it feels like a profound increase in power that strikes me as disconnected to whatever means of getting it, and arguably of much greater value than the immortality itself does.To me it seems to dilute the concept of liches a bit, coming across as more focused on becoming a ghost or spirit because it means you'll basically never have to worry about Paradox or advanced spell factors ever again, for some reason. To me, that feels like a greater negative than even what it might provide to their position as antagonists (or allies, really).</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox dealing aggravated damage, aggravated damage draining Mana from Supernal beings, and Mana being marginally scarcer in 2e (plus Paradox having more concretely-defined causes compared to 1e's application of intrinsic vulgarity to certain spells), as well as Supernal beings not benefiting from Yantras (besides for sympathetic casting), coupled with the fact that turning yourself wholesale into an invisible entity is at least a Patterning effect and that the various types of ephemeral lich are discussed in terms of the otherworlds relating to those forms of ephemera due to related Obsessions, suggest to me that the trade of essentially needing to stick to other worlds and/or poach Mana to keep up activities beyond day-to-day existence is not ideal but still preferable to death for someone Obsessed enough to discard their humanity.<br /> <br /> Fallen Worlds would doubtless have more particular mechanics for ephemeral liches, but &quot;they cast spells using the systems for things that aren't human and have to worry about running out of Mana&quot; is close enough to function in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T16:08:08-08:00","id":1526781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526766#post1526766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ochemata have Rank, and the ones that cast like mages use their Rank as effective Gnosis. The same writeup also specifies that ochemata who aren't created by archmasters use their Arcana like other Supernal entities do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I missed that. Assumed they had gnosis instead of rank. What difference does this make? (Also this adds to my types of Supernal Beings: Summoned, Greater Tulpa, Bound and Ochemata (of both Archmaster and Ascended flavours, greater and lesser Ochemata by rank...)<br /> <br /> At least I think that is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T16:15:08-08:00","id":1526782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526766#post1526766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paradox dealing aggravated damage, aggravated damage draining Mana from Supernal beings, and Mana being marginally scarcer in 2e (plus Paradox having more concretely-defined causes compared to 1e's application of intrinsic vulgarity to certain spells), as well as Supernal beings not benefiting from Yantras (besides for sympathetic casting)</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think Paradox becomes kind of a non-issue if you have infinite Reach and are inclined, even obligated, to reside somewhere that you will almost definitely never encounter a Sleeper witness to your magic. And I think even low level ephemeral entity dice pools render Yantras kind of irrelevant. Like, a Rank 2 entity can be rocking the kinds of base dice pool that it otherwise takes a Master of the Arcana to achieve, even before the potential to spend Mana to get as many as four extra points to each of their Power and Finesse. I think a Rank 5 entity pretty much laughs at the idea of such a requirement. &quot;Oh no, I can't arrange a specific symbolic time of day at which to cast my spell for a +1 bonus. However will I manage with my thirty to forty four dice that can boost most or all factors to maximum and still have about five left over to roll the one success I need.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">coupled with the fact that turning yourself wholesale into an invisible entity is at least a Patterning effect and that the various types of ephemeral lich are discussed in terms of the otherworlds relating to those forms of ephemera due to related Obsessions, suggest to me that the trade of essentially needing to stick to other worlds and/or poach Mana to keep up activities beyond day-to-day existence is not ideal but still preferable to death for someone Obsessed enough to discard their humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing though, when liches are described in terms of survival being the paramount priority for them, I'm not really buying needing to stay to the Shadow, Temenos, or Underworld as a trade off (indeed, when you yourself are phrasing it in terms of their Obsessions, it seems like a positive boon alongside the desired immortality). I don't really feel as though they're giving up anything they care to lose to not only have immortality but a far stronger standard of spell casting.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I find referring to the Mana to actually bring up more of the ambiguities or weaknesses of falling back on the Supernal entity rules. Do ephemeral liches automatically generate Mana equal to their Rank each day like Supernal beings do? Supernal beings don't lose Mana the way actual ghosts and spirits do Essence, they just gradually lose Corpus for being in the Fallen World, but the reason why Phenomenal existence damages them don't really translate to liches at all, so do they lose nothing or lose Mana? We're not really given rules for Supernal entities recovering Mana besides drawing it from other entities with that, so do they at least recover energy the ways that mages can (including through sacrifice, which I think takes a lot of the sting off for people that might be presumed to not have reservations about that), or how the ephemeral entity they resemble does, or not at all besides the stealing rule? How does all of that work for Morpheans?<br /> <br /> Mind, the biggest sink mortal mages have for Mana is probably Paradox anyway, so as long as a lich avoids casting around Sleepers or taking aggravated damage from other sources (which I think is not a tall order), how much do they really need? <i>Why</i> do they need to worry about running out of it again?<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, while these are ambiguities that require addressing even with a basic comment that they cast the way Supernal entities do, I don't think the answers are hard for people to reasonably arrive at. I just still think they all ultimately arrive in a place of &quot;none of this is onerous enough to offset the proposition of casting spells with double digits at the low end of power&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T16:23:30-08:00","id":1526784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526753#post1526753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I think about it, the other issue I'd take with just using unabridged Supernal being rules for such transformations is that it feels like a profound increase in power that strikes me as disconnected to whatever means of getting it, and arguably of much greater value than the immortality itself does.To me it seems to dilute the concept of liches a bit, coming across as more focused on becoming a ghost or spirit because it means you'll basically never have to worry about Paradox or advanced spell factors ever again, for some reason. To me, that feels like a greater negative than even what it might provide to their position as antagonists (or allies, really).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would homebrew something along the lines of Gnosis+ Arcana, usually reach rules, mana obtained through oblations (maybe with some modification related to the otherworld the lich is associated with), and probably still use Yantras instead of Power+Finesse (even that dice pool is strong).<br /> <br /> In principle a Spirit is vulnerable to being preyed on by other spirits, but a Mage by the point they can turn themselves into a spirit lich can likely handle most low rank spirits and tithe essence to higher ranked ones.<br /> <br /> A ghost Lich likewise can probably handle the average Reaper, and take/create essence in such a way as to be able to hold their own against most ghost and geists.<br /> <br /> Morpheans on the other hand... They get all kinds of messed up.<br /> <br /> Not having Rank would be a bit messy for some things, but the Honourary Rank attainment for Spirit already exists and could be adapted. And maybe they should gain a rank, I am unsure.<br /> <br /> That way drinking from the river of the underworld for a Ghostly Lich would have the expected side effects - ie making a Geistly Lich.<br /> <br /> Starting a google doc here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IxQOsPpqHLu7kaCBT5ecv_M4kpnpkYjZq-RdAmUmrIU/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t?usp=drivesdk</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  adding link to homebrew document 12-13-2023, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T17:29:49-08:00","id":1526786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526782#post1526782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing though, when liches are described in terms of survival being the paramount priority for them, I'm not really buying needing to stay to the Shadow, Temenos, or Underworld as a trade off (indeed, when you yourself are phrasing it in terms of their Obsessions, it seems like a positive boon alongside the desired immortality). I don't really feel as though they're giving up anything they care to lose to not only have immortality but a far stronger standard of spell casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending new mechanics to the contrary Morpheans literally can't internalize new experiences, the Underworld is arguably the most hostile of the commonly-known otherworlds, and even the Shadow is decidedly not built to discourage the Awakened tendency to eventually bite off more than they can chew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On top of that, I find referring to the Mana to actually bring up more of the ambiguities or weaknesses of falling back on the Supernal entity rules. Do ephemeral liches automatically generate Mana equal to their Rank each day like Supernal beings do? </div> </div> </div>They're not in the Supernal World, so strong odds are &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're not really given rules for Supernal entities recovering Mana besides drawing it from other entities with that, so do they at least recover energy the ways that mages can (including through sacrifice, which I think takes a lot of the sting off for people that might be presumed to not have reservations about that), or how the ephemeral entity they resemble does, or not at all besides the stealing rule? </div> </div> </div>Channel Mana, Devouring the Slain, and other spells for moving or converting Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Why</i> do they need to worry about running out of it again? </div> </div> </div>Because invisible entities who die without Essence or Mana in their systems are dead for good, to which I should hope the connection with &quot;this is a person who is seeking to evade death by extraordinary means&quot; is self-evident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just still think they all ultimately arrive in a place of &quot;none of this is onerous enough to offset the proposition of casting spells with double digits at the low end of power&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And part of my point is that when you are engaging in a process that almost certainly requires at least the penultimate lore accessible to mortal mages in one of the Subtle Arcana, if not more, to make an irreversible change that discards your humanity to become e.g. your own Oneiros sealed into a goetic scavenger-ship or a Holy Guardian Angel who can't, it's not a productive line of thought to try to demand especially onerous drawbacks to that power on top of &quot;these characters have ceased to be human, cannot participate in human society in a straightforward manner, and are variously sealed off from material reality or poking around in a deep-sea vent or a tiger pit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Characters in this setting powerful enough to hit failstates of &quot;became a ghostly monstrosity and vanished into the night, where they might yet be the subject of more campfire horror stories&quot; are already not on the low end of power. Being able to manage particularly impressive feats of spellcasting in another dimension by going semi-native doesn't particularly affect much about the setting when casting in the presence of Sleepers is commensurately more dangerous.<br /> <br /> All this is setting aside the other point of assumption: In a reading where an ephemeral lich's Rank is determined by their known Arcana, Geist's mechanics for raising your geist's Rank doesn't give it more Attribute dots, and neither of the two main presented methods for determining the Attributes of a character's ghost or Dream Form give them Attribute dots either, there is little to suggest a ghost mage, spirit mage, or Morphean gets Finesse 12 just because their Arcana are commensurate with those of a minor god \u2014 more likely they use the Attributes of their old Dream Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T18:04:33-08:00","id":1526787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526784#post1526784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morpheans on the other hand... They get all kinds of messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you say that? Of all those Realms, I would imagine the Astral has to be the least threatening on the whole, both to its native inhabitants and external visitors.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are some specific parts of the Temenos it's a good idea to involve unless ready for a struggle, but I think most is relatively benign.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T18:20:59-08:00","id":1526788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526787#post1526787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you say that? Of all those Realms, I would imagine the Astral has to be the least threatening on the whole, both to its native inhabitants and external visitors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until and unless 2e says differently, becoming a Morphean has the limitations described in their writeup on Astral Realms page 102. They're not simply mages who happen to be goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T09:39:36-08:00","id":1526810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1526788#post1526788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until and unless 2e says differently, becoming a Morphean has the limitations described in their writeup on Astral Realms page 102. They're not simply mages who happen to be goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this.<br /> <br /> Morpheans don't transform their bodies into Ephemera and they travel to the Astral, they invert their Oneiros and become astral beings with a weird memory collecting thing where they can't learn normally (because of the invert Oneiros, i guess).<br /> <br /> At least that is the 1e version. There is no 2e re-write, so that is what we have... Aside from that, sure, the Astral is relatively non-threatening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:25:26-08:00","id":1527256,"title":"","content":"What Arcana would the mushi from <i>Mushishi</i> fall under ? Life is a given, but what else ? Prime, maybe because of ley lines ?<br /> <br /> They are not searching for Essence like spirits, they have physical forms as well. Perhaps Death ? Ginko says mushi are &quot;born from darkness, gathering in the gloom at the borders with the light&quot; and that staring at the River of Light, the source of all mushi, causes your eyelids to wither and die. Maybe they ones in the river are motes of them, liminal beings between life and death that manifest as unusual living beings once they rise in Rank (maybe by skimming off life Resonance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:24:42-08:00","id":1527272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1527256#post1527256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Arcana would the mushi from <i>Mushishi</i> fall under ? Life is a given, but what else ? Prime, maybe because of ley lines ?<br /> <br /> They are not searching for Essence like spirits, they have physical forms as well. Perhaps Death ? Ginko says mushi are &quot;born from darkness, gathering in the gloom at the borders with the light&quot; and that staring at the River of Light, the source of all mushi, causes your eyelids to wither and die. Maybe they ones in the river are motes of them, liminal beings between life and death that manifest as unusual living beings once they rise in Rank (maybe by skimming off life Resonance).</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was the <i>wine</i> of light, and that it really is made up of motes of mushi?<br /> <br /> Anyways, rereading the notes about mushi, if I include them in the CofD I\u2019d substitute them for / make them the expansions of the weird Cryptids found inside the Gauntlet. Naturally, as Pangaean descendants, the Arcana would be Life + Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T17:52:37-08:00","id":1528236,"title":"","content":"Besides fully understanding an Iron Seal Aedes, what other ways are to remove the Exarchal Dreams condition when granted by a Tyrannic Awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Fixed the grammar. 01-08-2024, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T18:37:25-08:00","id":1528238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528236#post1528236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides fully understanding an Iron Seal Aedes, what other ways are to remove the Exarchal Dreams condition when granted by a Tyrannic Awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poking around another Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T08:54:33-08:00","id":1528262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528238#post1528238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poking around another Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. How exactly will this be done? Will it make the other awakening fail or become Tyrannic now?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T13:56:29-08:00","id":1528283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528262#post1528262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer. How exactly will this be done? Will it make the other awakening fail or become Tyrannic now?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They would need to dynamically direct the Mystery Play. They need to be part of the cast members and then make sure the Lucid proceeds through in such a way that it frees them from the Exarchial influence, which may involve actually summoning an appropriate being. If all goes well, the Awakening might have a metamorphic effect that frees the mage.<br /> <br /> Even if the process is successful, most Consilia rule that the Defiler owes the new mage a life-threatening service. If the Lucid fails or is debilitated, its normally grounds for execution of the Defiler. Regardless of the result, interfering with an Awakening is a Falling Wisdom sin.<br /> <br /> So they would probably need the help of the Alethian faction to help find a prospective candidate. They might also require a member of the Awakening Gambit to help push them towards Awakening, create safeguards and help direct the Mystery Play. Lastly, they would need a political safety net in case of the worst case scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T09:40:39-08:00","id":1528324,"title":"","content":"If a mage used <i>Touch of the Grave</i> on himself to pull a stone tablet from Death Twilight, but recasts it before duration runs out (he casts spell 2 and ends spell 1), does the tablet dissipate back into its original location or does it continue to exist in the material ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T10:27:06-08:00","id":1528328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528324#post1528324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage used <i>Touch of the Grave</i> on himself to pull a stone tablet from Death Twilight, but recasts it before duration runs out (he casts spell 2 and ends spell 1), does the tablet dissipate back into its original location or does it continue to exist in the material ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, Touch of the Grave is an odd one for the way that it can have an effect bound by the Duration on something that is not the actual subject of the spell...<br /> <br /> In most cases I would think it's valid for Spell Stacking to create a continuity in effect as the initial spell lapses, without subjecting the target to any interim period of not being under an effect. But I feel as though Touch of the Grave would be one where the object drawn from Twilight is tied more specifically to the spell cast on the person who drew it, such that when that Duration ends the materialized object does indeed go with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T17:05:30-08:00","id":1528460,"title":"","content":"Where can I learn more about the Fang Shih, which are mentioned in page 12 of <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T21:50:49-08:00","id":1528472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528460#post1528460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I learn more about the Fang Shih, which are mentioned in page 12 of <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they've ever been mentioned before that book. At least, not under that name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T05:14:24-08:00","id":1528481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528460#post1528460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I learn more about the Fang Shih, which are mentioned in page 12 of <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd look to sources on Ancient Chinese culture and religion. My understanding is that the Fang Shih were a type of ritual specialist in China. So presumably, the mages of Foundation Age China were organised in a similar manner.<br /> <br /> That seems to be the basic idea of the Great Cults: mages organise themselves as a part of, or in imitation of how their society organises general religion and ritual specialists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T19:02:45-08:00","id":1528512,"title":"","content":"Elements of the history chapter refer to pre-Atlantean Chinese mages, which can probably be regarded as falling under the umbrella of their Great Cult even if the name in the lexicon isn't used again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T18:34:05-08:00","id":1528632,"title":"","content":"What book and page does it's said that Mortal with Supernatural Merit have a harder time awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T21:24:01-08:00","id":1528636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528632#post1528632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What book and page does it's said that Mortal with Supernatural Merit have a harder time awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say that, but the relevant information is in Signs of Sorcery on pages 129-130:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alethians understand that the confrontation needs to be symbolic as well as Fallen, in keeping with the Prospect\u2019s nascent obsessions, and that what shocks one Prospect into Lucidity does nothing for another (at best). <b>They also know that the confrontation must be new to the Prospect, which poses difficult questions Consilia still grapple with. Put simply, a Sleeper who remains ignorant of the magical world has a much wider breath of potential confrontations compared to a Sleepwalker raised in the Orders\u2019 service, as the existence of magic in the world is a surprise to her.</b> By keeping Sleepwalkers close to the Orders, mages damage those Sleepwalkers\u2019 chances of joining them.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T06:52:42-08:00","id":1528646,"title":"","content":"When a mage gains the Renowned Artisan merit, what are the strings attached ? Let's say an alchemist wants to learn about the Mesen-Nebu, can they learn through their own research and would that trigger a Judge to target them ? Do they need to believe the Judges are the ultimate arbitrers of Dedwen ? Do they need to keep constantly working for an Arisen cult ? How would the knowledge color their perception of Awakened and Promethean alchemy ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T11:06:11-08:00","id":1528656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528646#post1528646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a mage gains the Renowned Artisan merit, what are the strings attached ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in a cult?<br /> <br /> To me, it's not terribly clear what the merit is meant to be in-universe. Like, the text restricts it to Arisen, or followers of an Arisen, and to skills related to the Guilds which perhaps suggests that there's something supernatural going on... Though that might just be because the social-side of the merit makes little sense outside that context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's say an alchemist wants to learn about the Mesen-Nebu, can they learn through their own research and would that trigger a Judge to target them ? </div> </div> </div>Not without changing the merit. The text seems relatively clear that it's for either the Guild you or your <i>Arisen Master</i> belongs to. That said, what you're suggesting sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they need to believe the Judges are the ultimate arbitrers of Dedwen ? </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem to be a requirement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they need to keep constantly working for an Arisen cult ? </div> </div> </div>Doesn't exactly say so. You <i>could</i> read it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T08:55:05-08:00","id":1528802,"title":"","content":"Would Mummy Relics (likely Regia or Uter) count as or be made of Perfected Materials?<br /> <br /> It seems very in the spirit of what they wanted to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T09:15:21-08:00","id":1528805,"title":"","content":"Perfected Materials are Supernal in nature - close the &quot;most ideal&quot; expression of a substance, purified of any identity of their own. Iremite Relics are very idiosyncratic, holding powers and curses dependent or circumstances of their creation. In that respect I'd say &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Mummy's metaphysics seems to be at an odd angle to Awakened magic. So on the other hand, it might be interesting to assume that their Relics are halfway-perfected, but resisting any changes to that balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T10:48:19-08:00","id":1528812,"title":"","content":"For a start, I think that the world featured in the Chronicles of Darkness contains more than enough things possessed of magical powers that it's not really necessary for any given one of them to become made out of Perfected Material in the process, nor is anything about the process likely to track to the established premise of how material becomes perfected. On the face of it, I find it no more necessary than any random imbued item qualifying for such. Hell, actual Artifacts are often supposed to have a premise of quite literally being Supernal objects, and even those aren't intrinsically made of Perfected Material.<br /> <br /> Perfected Material has the quality of an idealised form of what might be regarded as that material's purpose and function, which mages regard as a thing being brought as close as possible to becoming its symbolic form. That's not my understanding of what the likes of Relics are. I gather that they're more like objects that have been deeply imbued with meaning, often particularly placed in their cultural context and perception. A Relic object that is made of glass is not necessarily the idealised form of what glass can be used for, but possesses properties evocative of what the object represents or how it was valued. If Sekhem can be described as the vividness of life, then my impression is that Relics are instances of that being literally captured in objects that express or represent that vividness. I find that distinct from some Supernal metaphysics in general, and Perfected Materials in particular.<br /> <br /> Besides, the description of what Perfected glass actually is probably precludes any written example of a Relic that is made of glass.<br /> <br /> With regards to how Mummy metaphysics might interact with Mage ones (a subject I think is prompted when some crossover references go out of their way to describe mage ideas of what the magic of the Shan'iatu was like), I speculate that it's something like... when you look at a place with Mage Sight, the Supernal symbols you can perceive are the lens through which you recognise its meaning, the underlying emotional quality native to it. Sekhem is the actual aspect of the place that provides the basis for those symbols appearing. Any given Awakened may or may not believe that the Supernal and its symbols are the actual origin point of all that, but Sekhem as Mummies recognise and interact with it could probably be seen as its presence in the world as actually experienced.<br /> <br /> Think of it like how Mage Sight through the Matter Arcanum might tell you many and true things about a crystal of some salt, and you can even cast spells to affect it, but at the end of the day (barring certain philosophical abstractions) the crystal is still a thing that exists for itself rather than just in terms of the symbols it's seen through, and a chemist can have the expertise of that existence to do things with it that are distinct from Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> I'd say that if a Mummy well versed in their own metaphysics gained a good grounding in mage philosophy, they'd be of the opinion that Sekhem is a quality of the world that precedes any Supernal nature to it, and there can even be mages who would agree with them. Not all sects necessarily regard the relationship of Phenomenal and Supernal in the neo-Platonic terms of &quot;the idealised Forms of which the Supernal is composed are the original template for all phenomena&quot;, and the core book describes some of the ambiguities of their cosmology from which comes a speculation that things might exist first in the Fallen World and then become rarefied to the point of becoming the pure symbols they perceive as transmitting reality (even before getting into the question of influences brought in by strange and alien dimensions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T16:58:21-08:00","id":1529365,"title":"","content":"With knowledge of Prime or Life, a Node can bring any plant put there to any point it its life cycle, as long as that point would take a year or less. Lets say a mage has a peach seed, which takes up to 4 years to bear fruit, could a they use the effect of the ley line during 4 continuous days to hasten the process ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T18:00:16-08:00","id":1529367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529365#post1529365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With knowledge of Prime or Life, a Node can bring any plant put there to any point it its life cycle, as long as that point would take a year or less. Lets say a mage has a peach seed, which takes up to 4 years to bear fruit, could a they use the effect of the ley line during 4 continuous days to hasten the process ?</div> </div> </div> </div>My read would be no, because the intention seems to be to specifically to prevent characters from crossing two leylines and thereafter being able to get drastically accelerated production on e.g. the Sierra Redwood's usual decades-to-centuries-long timeline for viable seeds.<br /> <br /> The idea is pretty clearly for things that would hit the flowering/fruiting/etc stage within the year to be able to have that stage brought about with a day's work rather than that a non-Time-based Node effect allows you to accelerate growth at an arbitrary rate of up to one year per day without additional magic. It's for gardening and for getting more out of an orchard that you've got ready moreso than for making oaks from acorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixing typos. 01-24-2024, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T01:23:07-08:00","id":1529495,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any theories (or is it indicated anyway) why <i>Lictors</i> in the Silver Ladder are called that?<ul><li>Like, Lictors were originally quasi-ceremonial bodyguards for Roman magistrates, which doesn't seem that relevant. Though, a lot of Roman titles shifted over the millennia, so I wouldn't be terribly surprised if there's some society where a lictor is a judge, I just haven't found it.</li> <li>I've wondered if maybe Lictor was a reference to something in Mage: The Ascension? Though again, I've not found anything.</li> <li>It could be just a cool name, though honestly, the titles in <i>Awakening</i> are pretty good at not doing that.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T03:14:34-08:00","id":1529496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529495#post1529495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any theories (or is it indicated anyway) why <i>Lictors</i> in the Silver Ladder are called that?<ul><li>Like, Lictors were originally quasi-ceremonial bodyguards for Roman magistrates, which doesn't seem that relevant. Though, a lot of Roman titles shifted over the millennia, so I wouldn't be terribly surprised if there's some society where a lictor is a judge, I just haven't found it.</li> <li>I've wondered if maybe Lictor was a reference to something in Mage: The Ascension? Though again, I've not found anything.</li> <li>It could be just a cool name, though honestly, the titles in <i>Awakening</i> are pretty good at not doing that.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that it is more like a Judge Dredd style of judge which may fit well with the original legal role of Lictors in ancient Rome.<br /> <br /> Tbh, having not read the Silver Ladder book, I just assumed they were responsible for carrying out executions... Probably because of the Lictor from warhammer 40k's Tyranid army list (as a lone scout/assassin type of role, maybe judging what species to be absorbed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-26-2024, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T06:33:09-08:00","id":1529505,"title":"","content":"How much can a Dedicated Tool be modified before it loses connection to you as dedicated?<br /> <br /> For example, let's say you are a Moros with Matter 3 and a dedicated lead knife (pure lead), you find yourself needing a mirror so you use <i>Shaping</i> on your knife to make it a lead mirror, latter you need a Rod and shape it again, then after the needs have passed you restore it to the original knife shape.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Will it behave as a dedicated mirror/rod when transformed or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>When returning to the original shape, is it still dedicated or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, is it still dedicated or the mass separation breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, do the coins count as Dedicated coins?</li> </ol>Thanks<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T08:30:12-08:00","id":1529508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529505#post1529505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much can a Dedicated Tool be modified before it loses connection to you as dedicated?<br /> <br /> For example, let's say you are a Moros with Matter 3 and a dedicated lead knife (pure lead), you find yourself needing a mirror so you use <i>Shaping</i> on your knife to make it a lead mirror, latter you need a Rod and shape it again, then after the needs have passed you restore it to the original knife shape.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Will it behave as a dedicated mirror/rod when transformed or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>When returning to the original shape, is it still dedicated or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, is it still dedicated or the mass separation breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, do the coins count as Dedicated coins?</li> </ol>Thanks<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine only the original one counts. A Dedicated Tool is a specific instance of a yantra which the mage habitually incorporates into his spells. Its the form and symbol of the tool that are important, rather than the material. Its their lead knife, similar to how Excalibur wouldn't have the same symbolic gravitas if melted into steel coins. By that same logic, modifying it with <i>Wonderful Machine</i>, for example, would build upon its capabilities without removing the core of its identity.<br /> <br /> I think it might also count as Dedicated once more after being restored to the original shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T08:41:30-08:00","id":1529509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529505#post1529505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much can a Dedicated Tool be modified before it loses connection to you as dedicated?<br /> <br /> For example, let's say you are a Moros with Matter 3 and a dedicated lead knife (pure lead), you find yourself needing a mirror so you use <i>Shaping</i> on your knife to make it a lead mirror, latter you need a Rod and shape it again, then after the needs have passed you restore it to the original knife shape.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Will it behave as a dedicated mirror/rod when transformed or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>When returning to the original shape, is it still dedicated or the shape change breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, is it still dedicated or the mass separation breaks the Dedication?</li> <li>If I separate the mass of the knife to make something (coins), and reunite it again to make the knife, do the coins count as Dedicated coins?</li> </ol>Thanks<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say 1) no.<br /> 2) yes 3) yes, and 4) no.<br /> <br /> A dedicate magical tool is synchronized with your Nimbus, but not imprinted with it like a Soul stone.<br /> <br /> It helps your understanding of magic, so I would not allow it change form like in 1) to be symbolically a different expression of magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T10:03:32-08:00","id":1529512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529509#post1529509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say 1) no.<br /> 2) yes 3) yes, and 4) no.<br /> <br /> <b>A dedicate magical tool is synchronized with your Nimbus, but not imprinted with it like a Soul stone.</b><br /> <br /> It helps your understanding of magic, so I would not allow it change form like in 1) to be symbolically a different expression of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> The same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> Also thanks for your reply, what do you think of the same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T13:18:53-08:00","id":1529516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529495#post1529495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any theories (or is it indicated anyway) why <i>Lictors</i> in the Silver Ladder are called that?<ul><li>Like, Lictors were originally quasi-ceremonial bodyguards for Roman magistrates, which doesn't seem that relevant. Though, a lot of Roman titles shifted over the millennia, so I wouldn't be terribly surprised if there's some society where a lictor is a judge, I just haven't found it.</li> <li>I've wondered if maybe Lictor was a reference to something in Mage: The Ascension? Though again, I've not found anything.</li> <li>It could be just a cool name, though honestly, the titles in <i>Awakening</i> are pretty good at not doing that.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's any real world instance of the office or title of lictor assuming that kind of function. I won't speculate as to why whomever first wrote it settled on that name, but I could buy it as an in-character development that the Order's lexicon would take such a term and recontextualize it over time to their own functions. The etymology of the word, coming from Latin meaning &quot;to bind&quot;, seems to me like it could wind up as applicable to a jurist function.<br /> <br /> Hmm, it occurs to me that the title might have been adopted less because of the position they occupied than the badge of office they were identified with. The fasces seems like a fitting symbol for the Silver Ladder to be drawn to, not just as a badge of authority but the connotations of disparate elements being stronger when bound together. Lictors of the Order could be seen as serving a particularly significant point in maintaining the Diamond Precept (and lending a bit more credibility to the Star Precept), so I could see the name sticking through that avenue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529496#post1529496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, having not read the Silver Ladder book, I just assumed they were responsible for carrying out executions...</div> </div> </div> </div>Execution as a function of the Interfector, a Consilium post invariably reserved for Guardians of the Veil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T13:45:34-08:00","id":1529519,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I like those ideas. The first one especially accords with how I've used them. Less powerful judges and more legal notaries who act as intermediaries.<br /> <br /> That second one has the addition of implying why no one mentions the origin; given that fasces are now the symbol of one of the Seer Ministries (plus fascism in general I suppose).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T13:59:15-08:00","id":1529520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529512#post1529512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> The same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> Also thanks for your reply, what do you think of the same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would lean towards yes, except for the coins, wherein I would lean towards one of the coin's acting as the soulstone or it breaking as per the rules for destroying a soulstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T14:17:12-08:00","id":1529521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1529512#post1529512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> The same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> Also thanks for your reply, what do you think of the same questions but applied to a Soul Stone that is your Dedicated Tool, would mean YES to all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help. In the case of the knife, I would say it remains a soul stone, since its still a piece of the mage's Gnosis stored in a material. All that would change is the types of spells the new yantra could be used in. Which means a mage with <i>Shaping</i> and crafting ability could have added versatility, which is pretty cool.<br /> <br /> In the case of the coins, the material separation might cause the soul stone to be destroyed and potential Gnosis to be restored. Alternatively, it might go into one of the coins, which might constitute a Mystery in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T13:12:17-08:00","id":1530107,"title":"","content":"Hello, I have a question regarding of how can mages interact with the world from Twilight. The Death arcanum spell Death Gate can transfer mages into Twilight. Quite obviously, they cannot touch anything material or do harm to anything. However:<ul><li>Can they read text of an open book?</li> <li>Can they listen to a conversation?</li> <li>Can they cast spells on the material world?</li> </ul>I am particularly interested about the last one. It seems to me like a pretty strong move: mages move to Twilight, they go after any enemy who does not posess the Death arcanum or ability to interact with Twilight, and they start casting attack spells without risk of being hurt. Is this intended use of the spell? If not, what are the obstacles?<br /> <br /> Bonus question: How would you describe Twilight? Is the material world dimmed, both colors and sounds? Are there many twilight objects that are now visible? (Would the world be rich in them?) What else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T13:16:17-08:00","id":1530108,"title":"","content":"Bonus question 2: Death gate destroys all material objects, that can later be brought back by Touch of the Grave. This spell, however, is temporary if not cast as indefinite, and returns objects with Durability 1. Does it mean that the objects brought through the Death gate are for most practical purposes destroyed? (Or even if cast as lasting, would steel knife be suddenly be very fragile?<br /> <br /> Also, if I bring object with Touch of the Grave and it gets destroyed, does it return to Twilight? (Sorry, so many questions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T17:19:53-08:00","id":1530123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530107#post1530107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I have a question regarding of how can mages interact with the world from Twilight. The Death arcanum spell Death Gate can transfer mages into Twilight. Quite obviously, they cannot touch anything material or do harm to anything. However:<ul><li>Can they read text of an open book?</li> <li>Can they listen to a conversation?</li> <li>Can they cast spells on the material world?</li> </ul>I am particularly interested about the last one. It seems to me like a pretty strong move: mages move to Twilight, they go after any enemy who does not posess the Death arcanum or ability to interact with Twilight, and they start casting attack spells without risk of being hurt. Is this intended use of the spell? If not, what are the obstacles?<br /> <br /> Bonus question: How would you describe Twilight? Is the material world dimmed, both colors and sounds? Are there many twilight objects that are now visible? (Would the world be rich in them?) What else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yes, but.<br /> <br /> You can still cast spells on anything in sensory range, but your sensesay not work as well as usual (and it costs a reach to cast at sensory range rather than touch range - though I suspect Death magic can resolve that).<br /> <br /> I have always imagined it as a sort of ghostly filter over the material world, you can see and hear, but everything is washed out, sounds muted, generally deadened. Maybe Spirit or Mind twilight is different, but that is how being a ghost works. You get to mess with people who can't even preceive you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T17:31:50-08:00","id":1530126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530108#post1530108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus question 2: Death gate destroys all material objects, that can later be brought back by Touch of the Grave. This spell, however, is temporary if not cast as indefinite, and returns objects with Durability 1. Does it mean that the objects brought through the Death gate are for most practical purposes destroyed? (Or even if cast as lasting, would steel knife be suddenly be very fragile?<br /> <br /> Also, if I bring object with Touch of the Grave and it gets destroyed, does it return to Twilight? (Sorry, so many questions).</div> </div> </div> </div>First some context and terminology.<br /> <br /> 1) Ephemera is the default state of being of spirits in the shadow or ghosts in the Underworld, there it is solid and real, but in twilight ephemera is intangible to non-twilight entities.<br /> <br /> 2) when a object/building is destroyed it can leave a &quot;ghost&quot; like entity (called a castoff) made of ephemera, usually requires the lose to be felt strongly by a mortal (breaking Point/integrity loss?) Ephemeral items are thus relatively rare, but useful tools for what they are (whether they will get pulled into the Underworld like a Ghost without anchors is an interesting question).<br /> <br /> In the context of Ghost gate and Touch of the Grave, these spells mess with the normal context.<br /> <br /> Touch of the grave explicitly states that if the subject is broken it dissipates back into ephemera.<br /> <br /> Ghost gate is two sligthly different spells, one which can trap you in twilight (you pass through the gate and it now has a lasting effect on you, if the gate closes before you return it appears you are stuck in twilight. But your items are just destroyed (and guarenteed to leave ephemeral 'ghosts' behind).<br /> <br /> The reach option seems different, iirc several interpretations seem to suggest the subjects will automatically return to their material form when the duration ends. And maybe that items don't get destroyed?<br /> <br /> Not sure where this interpretation came from, probably this thread, or the previous archived version of it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T17:43:04-08:00","id":1530127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530107#post1530107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I have a question regarding of how can mages interact with the world from Twilight. The Death arcanum spell Death Gate can transfer mages into Twilight. Quite obviously, they cannot touch anything material or do harm to anything. However:<ul><li>Can they read text of an open book?</li> <li>Can they listen to a conversation?</li> <li>Can they cast spells on the material world?</li> </ul>I am particularly interested about the last one. It seems to me like a pretty strong move: mages move to Twilight, they go after any enemy who does not posess the Death arcanum or ability to interact with Twilight, and they start casting attack spells without risk of being hurt. Is this intended use of the spell? If not, what are the obstacles?<br /> <br /> Bonus question: How would you describe Twilight? Is the material world dimmed, both colors and sounds? Are there many twilight objects that are now visible? (Would the world be rich in them?) What else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, a mage in Twilight is potentially terrifying. In order to cast touch spells and manipulate material items, they would need to either use <i>Death Touched Item</i> on themselves (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 64), <i>Ephemeral Enchantment</i> (core book page 169), <i>Touch of the Grave </i>(core book page 130) and maybe <i>Eyes of the Dead</i> (core book page 192), but they can be hit back while the spells are active. Otherwise they need sensory range.<br /> <br /> However, they are not fully safe. A mage might think they are safe retreating into Twilight, only for a Sin Eater to fire their gun and hit them anyway. Being in Twilight does allow them to pass through walls, which is very useful.<br /> <br /> Within Twilight <a href=\"https://youtube.com/clip/UgkxhD4WvSAu7pGB05xJiBV3JScOaJxuGWy_?si=fJATJMCtT3Kj1Kuc\" target=\"_blank\">lights are dimmer, colors muted, objects look less solid, physical sounds are like echoes</a>.<br /> <br /> Death Twilight has everything that was destroyed, made into ephemera. An old house that was demolished, a library the earthquake destroyed, those old pictures a flooded basement ruined, the love letters that were burn in the fireplace, your pet dog, etc. They are constantly being drawn by the currents of Plasm towards the nearest Avernian Gate, then down through the Underworld, ultimately falling to the Ocean of Fragments and dissolving. The more living people miss the object, the longer they withold its descent (so a broken paperclip would be pulled down in seconds).<br /> <br /> Hope that is helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-06-2024, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T01:55:09-08:00","id":1530145,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, my comment about integrity loss caused by the destruction of an item is only applicable to rank of the castoff produced.<br /> <br /> Every other item destroyed produces a rank 0 castoff.<br /> <br /> I guess the difference is that Rank 1 and 2 castoffs get numina and influences. And are thus more useful as magical tools? I think Touch of the Grave is specifically referring to Rank 0 castoffs by default.<br /> <br /> Interesting to think a Mage can bind a castoff sword as a familiar? Or maybe a fetish/fetter since familiar requires consent and castoffs don't have minds.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, you can walk through walls, but you may find ghost walls blocking your way where there was a previous structure there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-07-2024, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T06:01:29-08:00","id":1530155,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your answers, they are very helpful!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530123#post1530123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Spirit or Mind twilight is different, but that is how being a ghost works. You get to mess with people who can't even preceive you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can ephemeral entities of different kinds (spirits, ghosts, goetia) interact with each other? (If yes, then I guess there is just one Twilight, with different kinds of ephemera?) If they can interact with each other, I assume that mage that came into Twilight using Death arcanum could also see spirits that reside there?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it possible to drag spirit/goetia/ghost in Twilight through Death Gate, materializing them? At least for ghosts, I guess the answer is probably no, but then what is the reason the mage can return to material form and the ghost not? Is the mage in Twilight from yet another kind of ephemera than spirits, ghosts and goetia, and this ephemera is reversible, but the others are not?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T07:18:22-08:00","id":1530159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530155#post1530155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you all for your answers, they are very helpful!<br /> <br /> Can ephemeral entities of different kinds (spirits, ghosts, goetia) interact with each other? (If yes, then I guess there is just one Twilight, with different kinds of ephemera?) If they can interact with each other, I assume that mage that came into Twilight using Death arcanum could also see spirits that reside there?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it possible to drag spirit/goetia/ghost in Twilight through Death Gate, materializing them? At least for ghosts, I guess the answer is probably no, but then what is the reason the mage can return to material form and the ghost not? Is the mage in Twilight from yet another kind of ephemera than spirits, ghosts and goetia, and this ephemera is reversible, but the others are not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight is shorthand for &quot;a frequency of reality that exists layered atop the material&quot;. Spirit Twilight, death Twilight and mind Twilight are different frequencies from each other. A being in Twilight can only perceive and interact with others in the same frequency and they can perceive beings in the material. But beings in the material require supernatural means to perceive or interact with Twilight, and those are usually specialized to a single frequency (like an occultist knowing a ritual to make a polaroid camera photograph ghosts).<br /> <br /> <i>Touch of the Grave</i> is attuned only to Death Twilight, so it cannot pull spirits or goetia, which are under the purviews of the Mind and Spirit Arcana<br /> <br /> Materializing an ephemeral entity requires at least 4 dots in the Arcanum that corresponds to it (it falls under the Practice of Patterning). Material beings can return from Twilight because they have living bodies, a Materialized entity is basically consuming Essence to force the ephemera that composes them into a solid form. <i>Touch of the Grave</i> is a weird edge case that is able to only pull castoff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T07:57:50-08:00","id":1530161,"title":"","content":"We know there is at least those three frequencies of twilight, along with God-Machine angels in their own twilight - which is Fate+Prime to interact with (CofD core rules) and Qashmallim of the Principle - which exist in Fate twilight (Promethean the Created).<br /> <br /> We have similarities but none of them are exactly the same, like the only Manifestation (apart from twilight form) which goetia can be given with Mind is Possession. And Essence as Spirits consume it (from the material world) is in the Purview of Spirit, though it is arguably that goetia and ghosts use the same kind of essence... I think this is unclear RAW.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, with Patterning of Mind you can project your mind into mind twilight (or into someone's dreams) without an ephemeral form, only an incorporeal, intangible mental image (using the dream form rules). This is pretty distinct from how entering Spirit or Death twilight works...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T05:31:16-08:00","id":1530267,"title":"","content":"Questions about the scope of Arcana.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I have a liquid mainly made of organics (orange juice, blood), which arcana makes them move and react? Matter or Life?</li> <li>Does it depend whether the substances are inside an organic container (an orange, a living animal) for the Arcana to be used?</li> <li>When I want to create/alter/sense organic based materials it is Life mandatory, or can I create/alter organic molecules from enough base materials/chemical reactions using Matte/Forcesr?</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T07:27:03-08:00","id":1530271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530267#post1530267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about the scope of Arcana.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I have a liquid mainly made of organics (orange juice, blood), which arcana makes them move and react? Matter or Life?</li> <li>Does it depend whether the substances are inside an organic container (an orange, a living animal) for the Arcana to be used?</li> <li>When I want to create/alter/sense organic based materials it is Life mandatory, or can I create/alter organic molecules from enough base materials/chemical reactions using Matte/Forcesr?</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>If the substance is inside a living organism, it requires Life.<br /> <br /> When its outside of them, page 63 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> states that a material that has been separated from a living being will be symbolically &quot;dead&quot; (affected by Matter rather than Life) minutes after separation. This is reinforced by the Kitchen Alchemists (<i>Dark Eras 2</i> page 372) Legacy using Matter to affect food, but then contradicted in the core book by citing food as part of Life's purview (page 148), so who knows for the orange juice. But blood seems to have the clearerest answer, depends on how recently it was collected.<br /> <br /> In the case of organic material synthesis, there are many roads to the same result. You could use Life exclusively on symbolically living materials. But you could also use Zoom In and a Ruling of Matter to construct the new material at the molecular level, which might require a Science roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T07:44:12-08:00","id":1530273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530267#post1530267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]When I want to create/alter/sense organic based materials it is Life mandatory, or can I create/alter organic molecules from enough base materials/chemical reactions using Matte/Forcesr?[/LIST]Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>When speaking in terms of molecules and the like, as relevant to the Matter Arcanum, keep in mind that &quot;organic chemicals&quot; is the term for all substances that contain carbon. They interact to a significant degree with living beings, but the scope of that is technically much larger.<br /> <br /> Like, I expect that most people don't necessarily think of carbon dioxide as &quot;organic&quot;, but its respiration by plants is pretty much the major thing that continuously reabsorbs carbon back into the food chain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T10:09:45-08:00","id":1530285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1530273#post1530273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When speaking in terms of molecules and the like, as relevant to the Matter Arcanum, keep in mind that &quot;organic chemicals&quot; is the term for all substances that contain carbon. They interact to a significant degree with living beings, but the scope of that is technically much larger.<br /> <br /> Like, I expect that most people don't necessarily think of carbon dioxide as &quot;organic&quot;, but its respiration by plants is pretty much the major thing that continuously reabsorbs carbon back into the food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is important in Mage is not the formal Chemical definition but the symbolic one. And I'm not sure about the rules, but the general the common usage of organic outside of chemistry has drifted significantly, even it is doesn't mean that, I am pretty sure &quot;organic matter&quot; usually refers (in lay speak) to things which can be broken by bacteria.<br /> <br /> That said, the many paths side bar suggestions Arcana purviews are not exclusive, food can be a solid, and thus falls under both Matter and Life. But what you do with something which symbolically is food is different to what you do with a solid, some items might even be Death aswell as food (though arguable not Matter at that point, as the are still fresh corpses/meat rather than being a worked material - like leather or a crafter bone wand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T21:24:06-08:00","id":1531048,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know of examples of Matter's purview of stasis ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T04:00:15-08:00","id":1531099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531048#post1531048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of examples of Matter's purview of stasis ?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Alter Integrity</i>? <i>Nigredo and Albedo</i>? <i>Self-Repairing Machine</i>?<br /> <br /> I think the passage underneath the purview explains it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is at once the Arcanum of stasis and transformation, <b>creating objects that will last a thousand years </b>and reshaping objects at a whim. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T04:08:23-08:00","id":1531101,"title":"","content":"Alter Integrity was one of my thoughts, but I'm not sure it qualifies, also you can use it to reduce integrity...<br /> <br /> Statis is an odd one, more closely aligned with time in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T05:03:13-08:00","id":1531104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531101#post1531101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alter Integrity was one of my thoughts, but I'm not sure it qualifies, also you can use it to reduce integrity...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was why I gave that quote. Stasis is described in a relationship with 'transformation'. So I take it that the spell fulfils both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T06:45:29-08:00","id":1531192,"title":"","content":"I think Alchemist's Touch and Machine Invisibility could qualify under stasis, in that they're forms of preventing substances or objects from carrying out their functions or nature. Perhaps even Lodestone, if one takes stasis as a purview that can be affected along multiple angles. Like, taking the fact that an object without force acting upon it, or a mechanism without input, will naturally exist in a static state and turning that on its head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T07:45:39-08:00","id":1531198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531192#post1531192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Alchemist's Touch and Machine Invisibility could qualify under stasis, in that they're forms of preventing substances or objects from carrying out their functions or nature. Perhaps even Lodestone, if one takes stasis as a purview that can be affected along multiple angles. Like, taking the fact that an object without force acting upon it, or a mechanism without input, will naturally exist in a static state and turning that on its head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a statis veilign would hide from stasis or hide a static thing.<br /> <br /> Likewise a shielding of stasis would protect against the effects of stasis... Not sure what that means, maybe would have a ruling of stasis forcing a gun to freeze up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T11:26:19-08:00","id":1531203,"title":"","content":"I wonder why <i>Self-Repairing Machine</i> is a Making, wouldn't it need Patterning to redefine what happens in stasis (maybe even a Weaving) ? <i>Machine Invisibility</i> would say things never changed, the subject is &quot;background noise&quot; to the machine. <i>Alchemist's Touch</i> shields the subject by saying this has a static interaction with the matter, like how noble gases are unreactive.<br /> <br /> I was thinking if, for example, it could be used to stop a Materialized spirit by using stasis to keep them from moving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T13:19:56-08:00","id":1531215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531203#post1531203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why <i>Self-Repairing Machine</i> is a Making, wouldn't it need Patterning to redefine what happens in stasis (maybe even a Weaving)?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason as Ex Nihilo is Making: giving an object the ability to regenerate Structure is Making stuff.<br /> <br /> Objects do not tend to spontaneously restore missing pieces. It's not a normal quality of Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T12:40:39-08:00","id":1531245,"title":"","content":"The <i>Imposter </i>spell (core book page 162) says that it confuses the subject's senses, which gives the impression that its cast on the person being fooled and is withstood by Composure. Would that be the case or is it cast on the person being disguise and withstood by each individual observer ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-21-2024, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T17:39:37-08:00","id":1531258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531245#post1531245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Imposter </i>spell (core book page 162) says that it confuses the subject's senses, which gives the impression that its cast on the person being fooled and is withstood by Composure. Would that be the case or is it cast on the person being disguise and withstood by each individual observer ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that sounds right.<br /> <br /> The veiling equivalent would be something like incognito presence, but with a reach option to make you appear to be someone else (not a specific person, but a general vaguely 'other person') and would not be withstood...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T23:55:16-08:00","id":1531494,"title":"","content":"How... do persistent imbued items work?<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I have Signs of Sorcery open on page 67 right now, but the only thing I'm seeing is that they exist, and that you can turn them back on with Prime if they get dispelled. Am I just blind? I suppose there's nothing stopping you from using a contingent imbued item to cast an indefinite duration spell, but then there'd be no reason to act like persistent items are different, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T04:53:29-08:00","id":1531504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531494#post1531494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How... do persistent imbued items work?<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I have Signs of Sorcery open on page 67 right now, but the only thing I'm seeing is that they exist, and that you can turn them back on with Prime if they get dispelled. Am I just blind? I suppose there's nothing stopping you from using a contingent imbued item to cast an indefinite duration spell, but then there'd be no reason to act like persistent items are different, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>A persistent item provides its effect for as long as the spell is supposed to last and the item exists, in contrast to a contingent item requiring a trigger. Since Imbued Items do not gain a dice bonus from Yantras and cannot contain Paradoxes to mitigate the resulting penalties to the spellcasting pool, using a contingent item to trigger an indefinite effect is less likely to succeed without exploiting Word Of Command (and, considering that without Flexible Reach such an item would have the indefinite duration baked in, it would seem reasonable to ask why such an item wasn't persistent already).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T10:19:33-08:00","id":1531528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531504#post1531504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A persistent item provides its effect for as long as the spell is supposed to last and the item exists, in contrast to a contingent item requiring a trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, obviously, I know that, but <i>how</i>? Mechanically speaking. Reach? Spell factors?<br /> <br /> I know how it works for contingent items. The creator sets Reach while imbuing, if it exceeds their free Reach the item always has a risk of Paradox when activated, even if you reduce it later with Flexible Reach. Spell factors are set by the user every time they activate it, affecting the spellcasting dice pool as usual.<br /> <br /> And like I said, I can see how I could use those rules to make an item that casts a spell with an indefinite (or at least long) duration, but I don't see where anything is said about how persistent items work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531504#post1531504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">using a contingent item to trigger an indefinite effect is less likely to succeed without exploiting Word Of Command</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the consensus of how Word of Command interacts with imbued items? That seems rather ripe for abuse. Since it would basically bypass the roll completely, wouldn't that mean you could max out every spell factor and tank the dice pool into the deep negatives... and then not care at all, because you just get Potency successes automatically (in a game where a single success is pretty much always enough)?<br /> <br /> I would have assumed the only thing it does is let you bypass the trigger to activate the item directly (handy if some joker made it annoyingly complicated to use their item), letting spellcasting happen as normal. Since imbued items can be used by anyone, the trigger is the only condition that decides whether the item &quot;will release its magic&quot;. By comparison, a werewolf fetish requires that you be Uratha and that you succeed a Resolve+Composure roll, so the spell lets you bypass the Uratha condition and also automatically succeed that roll. But if you use a talen, those don't have activation rolls, so that part of the spell does nothing, and you just roll normally for the Facet or Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531504#post1531504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">without Flexible Reach such an item would have the indefinite duration baked in</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I miss something? Flexible Reach only talks about <i>reducing</i> Reach, going from Advanced to Basic and removing options, not the reverse. Whether or not you picked Flexible Reach would change nothing to the need to have indefinite duration baked in. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T12:15:32-08:00","id":1531532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531528#post1531528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, obviously, I know that, but <i>how</i>? Mechanically speaking. Reach? Spell factors?</div> </div> </div> </div>And obviously &quot;How do they work?&quot; is a hopelessly vague question to try and figure out particulars for, which means going over basics is what I would consider a reasonable part of trying to provide an answer prior to getting clarification on what you actually meant.<br /> <br /> The spell factors are set when you make the thing. Reach is set for the defined effects unless you use Flexible Reach, as described on the page introducing that quality. The spell is presumably not able to be made stronger than you would be able to cast it normally without Yantra bonuses, so spell factors that would drop you below a dicepool of -10 wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did I miss something? Flexible Reach only talks about <i>reducing</i> Reach, going from Advanced to Basic and removing options, not the reverse. Whether or not you picked Flexible Reach would change nothing to the need to have indefinite duration baked in. Right? </div> </div> </div>Indefinite Duration costs two Reach by itself and therefore a contingent item made to produce an indefinite effect would have that extra reach locked in for the purposes of determining if it has a Paradox risk from the jump, which matters because contingent items roll to cast their spells and therefore have cause to worry about Paradox reducing their dicepool. If the item has dedicated its normally fixed Reach to producing an Indefinite effect, the question then arises as to why the item isn't persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T16:46:19-08:00","id":1531561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531532#post1531532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell factors are set when you make the thing. Reach is set for the defined effects unless you use Flexible Reach, as described on the page introducing that quality. The spell is presumably not able to be made stronger than you would be able to cast it normally without Yantra bonuses, so spell factors that would drop you below a dicepool of -10 wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you just... use as much Reach as you care to, comfortable in the fact that there's no casting roll and thus no Paradox risk? No limit?<br /> <br /> And where does that -10 number come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T17:58:19-08:00","id":1531567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531561#post1531561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you just... use as much Reach as you care to, comfortable in the fact that there's no casting roll and thus no Paradox risk? No limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the understanding that there is a finite amount of things Reach can be spent on without homebrew, that persistent items are for things like &quot;these glasses let you see ghosts&quot; or &quot;this cloak turns the wearer invisible,&quot; and that Reach is not a useful ablative quality against Dissonance, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And where does that -10 number come from? </div> </div> </div>Misremembering the number while being away from my books in a fashion that further underlines my point: Per the bit on the first page of the Spellcasting section (p111), if spell factors would reduce the casting pool below -5 after Yantra bonuses (which Imbued Items cannot benefit from), it's too complex and automatically fails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T18:25:51-08:00","id":1531570,"title":"","content":"Malleable Thorns is a spells that has 2 arcana at the same rating (Fate 2 / Mind 2):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Which Arcana do I need to increase to increase the dice pool? Fate or Mind? (I assume Fate, but you could say this is also a Mind spell).</li> <li>If my ruling Arcana is either of those (Mastigos or Acanthus), can I cast the spell without spending Mana?</li> </ol><br /> I am inclined to think the main arcana is Fate, as most of the spells in that section of Dark Eras 2 are Fate spells, but doubts linger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T18:34:37-08:00","id":1531572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531570#post1531570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Arcana do I need to increase to increase the dice pool? Fate or Mind? (I assume Fate, but you could say this is also a Mind spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>Highest Arcanum included in the spell, per the Spellcasting section on p111 of the corebook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If my ruling Arcana is either of those (Mastigos or Acanthus), can I cast the spell without spending Mana? </div> </div> </div>Same page as above indicates improvising a spell using a non-Ruling Arcanum costs Mana; either way it uses a Common Arcanum for the other Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T18:59:09-08:00","id":1531574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531567#post1531567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the understanding that there is a finite amount of things Reach can be spent on without homebrew, that persistent items are for things like &quot;these glasses let you see ghosts&quot; or &quot;this cloak turns the wearer invisible,&quot; and that Reach is not a useful ablative quality against Dissonance, sure.<br /> <br /> Misremembering the number while being away from my books in a fashion that further underlines my point: Per the bit on the first page of the Spellcasting section (p111), if spell factors would reduce the casting pool below -5 after Yantra bonuses (which Imbued Items cannot benefit from), it's too complex and automatically fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Thank you very much for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T03:24:18-08:00","id":1531610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531572#post1531572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highest Arcanum included in the spell, per the Spellcasting section on p111 of the corebook.<br /> Same page as above indicates improvising a spell using a non-Ruling Arcanum costs Mana; either way it uses a Common Arcanum for the other Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> So, if I have Fate 2 and Mind 2, with Gnosis 2, my pool is 4 dice, but if I increase my Mind to 3, the dice pool becomes 5?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do I always spend Mana with a complementary arcana? So a Mastigos casting a Mind 4, Fate 1 spell, does it need 1 Mana?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T05:33:33-08:00","id":1531676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531610#post1531610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> So, if I have Fate 2 and Mind 2, with Gnosis 2, my pool is 4 dice, but if I increase my Mind to 3, the dice pool becomes 5?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do I always spend Mana with a complementary arcana? So a Mastigos casting a Mind 4, Fate 1 spell, does it need 1 Mana?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fyi: in 1e they refered to these as conjunctional spells, the wording still slips in in a few spell examples in 2e. Otherwise rules for conjunctional spells don't appear.<br /> <br /> Pg 111 is odd, since it deals with &quot;the highest arcanum included in the spell&quot;, for a Mind \u00b7\u00b7, Fate \u00b7\u00b7 spell either both or neither arcanum are the highest.<br /> <br /> NB, it is not your character's highest arcanum.<br /> <br /> Usually I would go with &quot;this is a Mind 2 spell with conjunctional Fate&quot;, and thus use Gnosis+Mind to cast it... Not Gnosis+Mind+Fate, or Gnosis+nothing (since neither is highest).<br /> <br /> Taking the first example spell in the book Exorcism (Death Unravelling) the optional extras (Spirit/Mind 4) don't make this not a Death spell. So I would still have this cost mana if Death was not one of your Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> Contrast that with the Spirit example spell Banishment, which has conjunctional Death/Mind 4. It would be a Spirit ruling equivalent to pretty much the exact same spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T12:39:18-08:00","id":1531692,"title":"","content":"Can Shaping(Matter 2) be used to construct whole houses with enough material and area factor?<br /> This is one of the spells that gives me a lot of questions. But just assuming that you have all the materials(pipes, steel, foundations, etc), could you just put them together with Shaping or constructing a house with raw materials is more akin to Weaving spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T13:11:24-08:00","id":1531695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531692#post1531692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Shaping(Matter 2) be used to construct whole houses with enough material and area factor?<br /> This is one of the spells that gives me a lot of questions. But just assuming that you have all the materials(pipes, steel, foundations, etc), could you just put them together with Shaping or constructing a house with raw materials is more akin to Weaving spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shaping is more akin to sculpting materials than assembling existing objects, which would be more the function of spells like Telekinesis from Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T17:32:28-08:00","id":1531712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531692#post1531692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Shaping(Matter 2) be used to construct whole houses with enough material and area factor?<br /> This is one of the spells that gives me a lot of questions. But just assuming that you have all the materials(pipes, steel, foundations, etc), could you just put them together with Shaping or constructing a house with raw materials is more akin to Weaving spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would need a custom Ruling for solids. But it does mean you could &quot;fly&quot; by levitating a jumsuit or use free bricks to create a floating ladder. It also means a mage with enough scale could levitate a building before letting it freefall, which is a terrifying idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T06:47:01-08:00","id":1531780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531712#post1531712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you would need a custom Ruling for solids. But it does mean you could &quot;fly&quot; by levitating a jumsuit or use free bricks to create a floating ladder. It also means a mage with enough scale could levitate a building before letting it freefall, which is a terrifying idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reach on Shaping can affect solids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T12:42:26-08:00","id":1531794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1531780#post1531780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reach on Shaping can affect solids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, but the Reach also gives the ability to sculpt them like clay, which I believe is the main reason for requiring it. However, using a spell that only focuses on moving matter without shaping it could arguably be done with a Ruling, allowing more Reach to be freed. Narrowing the focus of the spell for a small optimization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:22:55-08:00","id":1531806,"title":"","content":"This is one of those cases where I'm going to think that the principle that different Arcana can cover similar spaces shouldn't allow for achieving equal or better results with a much lower dot rating.<br /> <br /> It takes three dots in Forces to create an effect that simulates Strength for the sake of lifting things, and four dots to simply make things float. No Ruling should be rendering those as chump options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T10:50:37-07:00","id":1532659,"title":"","content":"How would you model a spell that creates a time loop, a la the Environmental Tilt in Mummy 2e? I'd peg it at Time 5, but not sure about the Practice, though leaning more towards Unmaking, where the spell is flavoured as excising the subject from regular temporal progression and locking them in a repeating timeline. This same description can be used for Making though, &quot;creating&quot; the loop. What I'm having difficulty with is the actual mechanics of implementing the spell beyond inflicting the Tilt, like how does Duration work for the spell? Does it just dictate how long the spell lasts from the perception of those outside the loop, or does it determine how long the loop lasts in terms of its own internal time, or both? Does the loop start when the spell is cast or does the loop start from the past (according to Duration?) and end at the point the spell is cast, making it naturally withstood by temporal sympathy? Would you allow the spell in the first place before Archmastery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T03:01:24-07:00","id":1532692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1532659#post1532659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd peg it at Time 5, but not sure about the Practice, though leaning more towards Unmaking, where the spell is flavoured as excising the subject from regular temporal progression and locking them in a repeating timeline. This same description can be used for Making though, &quot;creating&quot; the loop.</div> </div> </div> </div>My head goes to Making, for the image of creating a kind of bypass in time that functions as the underlying mechanic that becomes experienced as a time loop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm having difficulty with is the actual mechanics of implementing the spell beyond inflicting the Tilt, like how does Duration work for the spell? Does it just dictate how long the spell lasts from the perception of those outside the loop, or does it determine how long the loop lasts in terms of its own internal time, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's consistent with how other such spells work that Potency functions as the measure of how much it imposes upon the target (with Reach to determine how many units each point of Potency corresponds to), while Duration remains consistent as how long the spell continues to exist from an objective stand point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the loop start when the spell is cast or does the loop start from the past (according to Duration?) and end at the point the spell is cast, making it naturally withstood by temporal sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the most straightforward way it works is that it hits the target and basically points their forward momentum through time back upon themselves, in a way that shunts them back through time into as much of their own past as the Potency can grasp. It basically becomes like an advanced form of Shifting Sands, causing them to disappear from the perspective of people in the present, but it's locked in on itself in a way that means it can't actually create Lasting effects on the past. I'd say that by default, the person experiencing it is aware of the loop, but Reach can make it so that they continuously reset as well.<br /> <br /> I don't think this would require temporal sympathy, as it's not actually casting magic on the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you allow the spell in the first place before Archmastery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fair game within the scope of as many targets as such a spell could normally get and a loop that can probably only encompass days at best, with archmastery having space to create something more complex or with greater scope and longer lasting impact. A Traveller's spell is mostly an elaborate way to trap somebody for a while, maybe something that they can reflect on, while archmastery creates an effect that kind of distorts which past for the target even remains true, for instance. Or creating a time loop that keeps forcing a scenario to repeat itself until it cultivates a specifically desired outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T04:01:24-07:00","id":1532695,"title":"","content":"Making is unnecessary since you are just working with Time which is already there.<br /> <br /> Patterning should be enough to alter the time which is already there into a loop.<br /> <br /> The question is what gets reset and how often, not familiar with the Mummy example you are trying to replicate, so I am assuming it is like groundhog day...<br /> <br /> In which case wiping the time at the end of each interval might be Unmaking... Or almost a temporal summoning (which again doesn't require Mastery).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 03-16-2024, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T14:34:59-07:00","id":1532870,"title":"","content":"How do you run an actual Awakening(s) in a semi major city that has a healthy Mage population?<br /> <br /> The Consilium is around 100 mages, the city itself is ~3million but the greater metro area, and the Consilium's reach, being around 10 million over about a 10k square mile area.<br /> <br /> I have always started games with PCs post Awakening (and post-training), but my players might want to start with their Awakenings in play and I'm unsure how to actually do this. Some Orders might be fine with them mingling but others might take a more hands on and secluding training. Or should I make the Orders weaker/less caring about training? Or just something that should be handled in multiple sessions zeros and them actually coming together would be after such training is complete?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T01:38:22-07:00","id":1532890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1532870#post1532870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have always started games with PCs post Awakening (and post-training), but my players might want to start with their Awakenings in play and I'm unsure how to actually do this. Some Orders might be fine with them mingling but others might take a more hands on and secluding training. Or should I make the Orders weaker/less caring about training? Or just something that should be handled in multiple sessions zeros and them actually coming together would be after such training is complete?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there are two things one can do with this.<br /> <br /> One is to emphasize the presence of an established cabal in onboarding the characters. Cabals have members of multiple Orders as a matter of course, and one can opt to make it on the larger end to provide a decent range. I think that would be a reasonable basis for the characters being brought in along different lines while still maintaining decent contact with one another.<br /> <br /> The other is that I think it ought to tailor circumstances down to the level of the characters specifically, rather than make such accommodations the local norm. It's not necessary for the caucuses to have a general standard of mentoring from afar in hands off fashion for that (or something similar) to be the decided course of action for those characters in particular.<br /> <br /> Hmm...<br /> <br /> Another consideration is the premium that Awakened society places on the institution of the cabal itself, the sovereignty and sanctity of it. If a bunch of Nameless form a cabal and then become involved in seeking initiation into multiple Orders, Consilium tradition and law could have it that no standard of education and training has a right to split them up against their will. It might be a bit more inconvenient for the caucus to manage, but you make that effort in respect to this. It stands out just because it's not usual for lone Awakened to form groups with one another before the Pentacle comes upon them and they can be directed to a suitable Order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T04:29:28-07:00","id":1532898,"title":"","content":"what would the exarches look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T04:59:56-07:00","id":1532900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1532898#post1532898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what would the exarches look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exarchs are never seen directly. They occupy a place in the cosmology where what they look like would be a filtered-down mask to prevent their visitor's soul from exploding, and their closest servants (ochemata) are all capable of very broad shapeshifting to look however they need to in a given situation.<br /> <br /> If you somehow encountered one in person, it looks however it's necessary for them to look. The symbolic cues of their Resonance/Nimbus equivalent make them look wildly out of harmony with their surroundings and take cues from their controlling nature (for which chain and shackle imagery is often a quick shorthand).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T06:50:59-07:00","id":1533003,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m trying to use one splat as a simple fight against my players. How normally a cabal of mages(Arcanas 3 max, Gnosis 2) tend to view other supernatural splats in terms of power?<br /> Assume a &quot;monster of the week&quot; situation, without strings attached to secret societies. Does a Cabal of 3 mages(different paths) have difficulties against Kindred, Lost, Beggoten, etc?<br /> <br /> The objective is to scare them with some cool supernatural powers, but I don't want this to be a cakewalk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T07:35:08-07:00","id":1533007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1533003#post1533003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u00b4m trying to use one splat as a simple fight against my players. How normally a cabal of mages(Arcanas 3 max, Gnosis 2) tend to view other supernatural splats in terms of power?<br /> Assume a &quot;monster of the week&quot; situation, without strings attached to secret societies. Does a Cabal of 3 mages(different paths) have difficulties against Kindred, Lost, Beggoten, etc?<br /> <br /> The objective is to scare them with some cool supernatural powers, but I don't want this to be a cakewalk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will depend on a lot of things, including available tools and general preparedness, as well as what &quot;a simple fight&quot; entails. An enemy with intel who's choosing their moment to act when and where the PCs aren't on their guard has different approaches to an enemy who is on a berserk rampage due to external circumstances. A lone enemy going into a three-on-one fight without backup has worse odds of making a dent than a team with equal or greater headcount and/or support.<br /> <br /> Conventional wisdom would be to have the opposition fight smart and/or hit hard and fast before the character(s) have time to marshal their resources; at the described Gnosis and Arcana, what rotes everybody's got will have a strong impact on what can be safely done in a turn, and taking the action to somewhere Sleepers can see will crank up the risk of Paradox and loss of Wisdom (this relates to the Kindred's classical approach in the old &quot;the Big Three splats have a tactical rock-paper-scissors thing going on&quot; idea).<br /> <br /> Generally speaking the more lasting scare in Mage's thematics will be &quot;dealing with this with direct magic could blow up in a way we can't walk back,&quot; such that forcing avenues that might trigger Quiescence and/or Paradox is a big push. If &quot;without strings attached to secret societies&quot; includes the more general phenomenon of mortal retinues being attached to monsters, that means leaning into the fact that most non-Supernal magic doesn't have operational constraints based around the presence of witnesses and pushing the fight near crowded areas.<br /> <br /> The general balance of power for gameline-having supernatural beings with a conventional Supernatural Potency progression tends to taper off to the 4-6 range, and specializing powers and skills toward the available heights of a specific ability will tend to make a stronger impression. Monster lairs and nests will generally give the benefit of preparation and home field advantage.<br /> <br /> Even outside of the particulars of the monster, how a mage or group of mages will view them threatwise will vary by experience, Wisdom, and overall personality. Confidence (misplaced or otherwise) based on prior encounters or study, as well as the degree to which one's magic has gone to one's head, will directly affect the difference between &quot;I'm an Obrimos, this is the fifteenth vampire I've encountered in the last decade, and I wrote my thesis on how to deal with them&quot; and &quot;what is that clockwork birdman?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T16:45:29-07:00","id":1533337,"title":"","content":"I am confused with the spell factors on legacy attainments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacy Attainments</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Automatic Activation: In most cases, a Legacy Attainment<br /> can be activated with an instant action and does not require<br /> dice rolls. Like a spell, <b>the Attainment automatically acquires<br /> primary spell factor ranks (in Potency or Duration) equal to the<br /> mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum<br /> minus one.</b><br /> <b>When required, the Attainment is also considered to have ac-<br /> quired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast<br /> as a spell) up to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum.</b><br /> If the Attainment would require a measurement of its suc-<br /> cesses, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the<br /> mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have an example, a Legacy member has Arcana at 4. The attaiment is Potency Primary, and uses Advanced Duration, how long it lasts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Duration</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Dice Penalty</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One scene/hour</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>None (basic success)</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One day</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-2</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One week</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-4</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One month</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-6</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One year</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-8</i></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So being at Arcana 4, if I use Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty, do I get One week (-4 in the table), or One day (-2)? The example in the book is with Arcana 5 and Arcana 3, so I am not sure if I have to be <i>superior </i>or at least <i>equal </i>to the penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legacy Attainments</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who<br /> possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency<br /> automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as<br /> per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.<br /> If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed<br /> three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to<br /> two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two<br /> ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T17:52:35-07:00","id":1533342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1533337#post1533337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused with the spell factors on legacy attainments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have an example, a Legacy member has Arcana at 4. The attaiment is Potency Primary, and uses Advanced Duration, how long it lasts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Duration</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Dice Penalty</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One scene/hour</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>None (basic success)</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One day</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-2</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One week</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-4</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One month</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-6</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>One year</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>-8</i></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So being at Arcana 4, if I use Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty, do I get One week (-4 in the table), or One day (-2)? The example in the book is with Arcana 5 and Arcana 3, so I am not sure if I have to be <i>superior </i>or at least <i>equal </i>to the penalty.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lets say you have a Time primary, Space optional Legacy. You currently have Time 4 and Space 2. If you are using the main Attainment, with only time, you have 4 pseudo-dice to distribute in spell factors. Lets say its Potency primary, you have advanced duration and normal scale. You could use all 4 dice to boost duration to a week. Alternatively, you could boost duration to a day and scale for two people. A third option is to keep duration to a scene and boost the Potency from 4 to 6 (since primary factor rules still apply).<br /> <br /> Now lets say you have the optional Attainment, same factors, so you have 3 pseudo-dice to use, since the number is the minimum between the Time and Space ratings. So in this case you could make it last a day or affect a second target, but not both.<br /> <br /> The pseudo-dice can be allocated on the fly and represent the most flexibility an Attainment can have for adjusting factors. Hope that proves helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T19:17:20-07:00","id":1533586,"title":"","content":"Knit (Life 3) and Mend (Life 4) both can heal wounds (of different severity) and have the following reach in common:<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The spell heals damage done by deprivation and<br /> charges the subject\u2019s system as though she had received a full<br /> meal and plenty of water.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell reproduces the effects of a full night\u2019s rest in<br /> the subject, including regaining a point of Willpower if applicable.<br /> <br /> <br /> But Knit can fix personal tilts with one reach, as a higher spell, is the same effect implicit on Mend? Was this an omission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T20:30:33-07:00","id":1533589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1533586#post1533586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Knit can fix personal tilts with one reach, as a higher spell, is the same effect implicit on Mend? Was this an omission?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's omitted because most Personal Tilts in the vein of Arm Wrack are caused by some amount of damage to the relevant limbs or sense organs and Mend heals lethal damage at a higher rate than Knit; it would be redundant, unlike Knit's Reach effect which is presumably there to allow you to heal a Personal Tilt before restoring the leftmost box of damage that caused it.<br /> <br /> On the other end of things, Tilts caused by aggravated damage tend to result in permanent loss of function of those body parts, and regenerating missing limbs and organs is a separate spell, so Mend doesn't have much need for a specific extra effect on its &quot;heal a good amount of lethal damage&quot; to turn a broken arm into an unbroken arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:43:15-07:00","id":1533609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> thanks for answering my questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T18:15:54-07:00","id":1534114,"title":"","content":"Is there a source for what mage relationship is like with mortal who have supernatural merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T21:27:06-07:00","id":1534119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534114#post1534114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a source for what mage relationship is like with mortal who have supernatural merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire section of the Appendix about Sleepwalkers in the 2e corebook. Beyond that, &quot;mortals with Supernatural Merits&quot; is a broad category that would need to filter &quot;what mages are like in general&quot; and &quot;what these mages in particular are like&quot; through &quot;what these mortals with these Supernatural Merits are like.&quot; Everyone involved is still a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T03:54:08-07:00","id":1534124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534119#post1534119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an entire section of the Appendix about Sleepwalkers in the 2e corebook. Beyond that, &quot;mortals with Supernatural Merits&quot; is a broad category that would need to filter &quot;what mages are like in general&quot; and &quot;what these mages in particular are like&quot; through &quot;what these mortals with these Supernatural Merits are like.&quot; Everyone involved is still a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>This\u261d\ufe0f.<br /> <br /> To give some specific examples, some Exarchs tend to use mortal agents in preference to using Seers. In fact they would be happy to use Forsaken, or mortals with other supernatural powers/merits asuch as anyone else (so long as they are useful). But in terms of the Seer Hierarchy, they are always on the bottom of the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> So I imagine Seers interactions with Mortals with Supernatural Merits would fall into that category. Useful tools to be used as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T07:47:45-07:00","id":1534128,"title":"","content":"Does<b> Mental Shield</b> protect against mind reading effects or only against attacks and mind control?<br /> <br /> <br /> I got confused since <b>Alter Mental Pattern</b> has &quot;Supernatural powers that read the surface thoughts or emotions of the subject provoke a Clash of Wills.&quot; And I thought this was also covered by <b>Mental Shield</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T08:31:22-07:00","id":1534129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534128#post1534128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does<b> Mental Shield</b> protect against mind reading effects or only against attacks and mind control?<br /> <br /> I got confused since <b>Alter Mental Pattern</b> has &quot;Supernatural powers that read the surface thoughts or emotions of the subject provoke a Clash of Wills.&quot; And I thought this was also covered by <b>Mental Shield</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's overlap. Mental Shield protects against mind-affecting abilities targeting the subject (including any Mind spells and Goetic Numina), and Alter Mental Pattern changes the way the subject projects themselves in such a way that (like any conflict between one supernatural power and another) attempting to magically discern their mental/emotional state while it's active provokes a Clash in addition to making relevant Subterfuge rolls easier for them.<br /> <br /> Basically, Alter Mental Pattern isn't going to do anything to stop you from getting mind-controlled, but Mental Shield isn't going to help you project an air or honesty or pretend to be having a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T08:39:58-07:00","id":1534130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534128#post1534128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does<b> Mental Shield</b> protect against mind reading effects or only against attacks and mind control?<br /> <br /> <br /> I got confused since <b>Alter Mental Pattern</b> has &quot;Supernatural powers that read the surface thoughts or emotions of the subject provoke a Clash of Wills.&quot; And I thought this was also covered by <b>Mental Shield</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Mental Shield</i> mentions it gives protection against Mind spells and similar effects. <i>Alter Mental Pattern</i> allows the mage to lie more easily, to mask their intentions. Since the effect is attempting to hide their thoughts and the mind reading effect is attempting to uncover the truth, both effects are in conflict, creating a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> The main difference is that <i>Mental Shield</i> is a broader defense against mental powers, whereas <i>Alter Mental Pattern</i> is a Veiling and will not trigger Peripheral Mage Sight. So while mages always know when their controlled spells are Clashing, other supernaturals don't. So unless a vampire with Auspex knows some mind effect is going on, they might not even know they can spend Willpower and, should the mage win the roll, they might think the person is being geniune, or thinking about random stuff (what movie they will watch, the project they have at work, that they really want one of their favorite foods, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T09:02:20-07:00","id":1534131,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a><br /> <br /> Some other questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>both <b>Quantum Flux</b> and <b>Perfect Timing</b> have an effect that require standing still and losing Defense, if you have both spells active at the same time, do you benefit from both effects with a single turn of immovility and lost defense?</li> <li><b>Serendipity </b>has an option to reach to use other skills, is this reach usage dependant on the spell being active?<br /> I cast the spell, with the +1 Reach, now I know what I need to do, and I could use the skills of the same group, but the spell expires, do I lose the insight on what and how to use the skills? Do I need to recast the spell with the same reach to be able to use the skills?</li> <li><b>Warding Gesture</b> as a +2 reach option for &quot;<i>The mage may selectively grant protection from supernatural effects that target an area instead of individuals</i>&quot;, those are not supposed to be Fate effects right, but any type of area effects?</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-13-2024, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T09:26:58-07:00","id":1534134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534131#post1534131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a><br /> <br /> Another question, both <b>Quantum Flux</b> and <b>Perfect Timing</b> have an effect that require standing still and losing Defense, if you have both spells active at the same time, do you benefit from both effects with a single turn of immovility and lost defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the spell stacking rule from page 118 would apply. I would rule it as the character getting the bonus from the spell with the highest Potency, plus the reduction of any penalties by <i>Quantum Flux</i>'s Potency (which arguably makes it the most useful spell of the two).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T10:00:39-07:00","id":1534137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1534131#post1534131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Warding Gesture</b> as a +2 reach option for &quot;<i>The mage may selectively grant protection from supernatural effects that target an area instead of individuals</i>&quot;, those are not supposed to be Fate effects right, but any type of area effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Warding Gesture is specifically called out in the discussion of Scale on page 113, so yes, my reading would that the Reach effect applies to any area-based supernatural effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T20:15:42-07:00","id":1535124,"title":"","content":"Lets say we are using a Space spell to increase the power of the threshold of an area, such that when someone enter the area of effect, without being invited by the people who consider it a home, then circumstances would conspire immediately to prevent them or throw them out. What would be required to do that ? I imagine a Compelling of Space and Time (mixing elements of <i>Red Light, Green Light</i>) or perhaps it would be a Space 2 and Time 1 Shielding ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T20:35:10-07:00","id":1535125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1535124#post1535124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say we are using a Space spell to increase the power of the threshold of an area, such that when someone enter the area of effect, without being invited by the people who consider it a home, then circumstances would conspire immediately to prevent them or throw them out. What would be required to do that ? I imagine a Compelling of Space and Time (mixing elements of <i>Red Light, Green Light</i>) or perhaps it would be a Space 2 and Time 1 Shielding ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is almost certainly a Fate effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T20:40:00-07:00","id":1535126,"title":"","content":"There are many paths to accomplish the same effect. In this case, I am looking for a way that it can be accomplish by nudging sympathy via Space. I was thinking it could possibly be done using elements of <i>Isolation </i>and <i>Red Light, Green Light</i>, but maybe a Ruling or Shielding would be needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T21:14:41-07:00","id":1535128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1535126#post1535126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many paths to accomplish the same effect. In this case, I am looking for a way that it can be accomplish by nudging sympathy via Space. I was thinking it could possibly be done using elements of <i>Isolation </i>and <i>Red Light, Green Light</i>, but maybe a Ruling or Shielding would be needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally describing a conditional effect. Regardless of what other Arcana you use, triggering effects based on conditions without creating or conscripting a secondary actor to determine when those conditions are met requires Fate.<br /> <br /> Red Light/Green Light is a largely narrative spell whose effects revolve around hastening or delaying someone's attempts to reach their destination. Isolation is a spell that uses Space to impose a psychological effect on the subject. Neither of these things translate to the equivalent of making an intelligent combination of Ban and Teleportation to ward an area against people who weren't explicitly invited to the target area.<br /> <br /> The effects of nudging sympathy alone are subtle enough to not be practical to rely on for immediate results. Making a Ban or similar mid-level Space distortion with a Key of being invited by a resident accomplishes the practical effect of barring casual intruders. Throwing up an Area-based Exceptional Luck or similar to penalize attempts to gain entry accomplishes the narrative effect of &quot;circumstances conspire to keep intruders from getting in.&quot; No amount of Time is going to give a spell the intelligence or probabilistic qualities necessary for it to identify who has an invitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T09:21:27-07:00","id":1535175,"title":"","content":"Regarding Warding &amp; Binding using the Occult skill, page 140 of the CofD core book cites it as Presence + Occult - Rank and modified by Integrity. However, the Geist core book cites it as Resolve + Composure vs Power + Resistance, making it unlikely to be able to ward an area after a certain Rank. But what do the Awakened roll instead, the standard Presence + Occult - Rank ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T11:11:30-07:00","id":1535179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1535175#post1535175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Warding &amp; Binding using the Occult skill, page 140 of the CofD core book cites it as Presence + Occult - Rank and modified by Integrity. However, the Geist core book cites it as Resolve + Composure vs Power + Resistance, making it unlikely to be able to ward an area after a certain Rank. But what do the Awakened roll instead, the standard Presence + Occult - Rank ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gnosis + the appropriate Arcanum - spell factors.<br /> <br /> The roll in Geist is presumably made to account for the fact that the Bound don't have an Integrity score that can modify the roll (and the closest Trait they have to a substitute doesn't numerically operate like Integrity), so if for whatever reason you want a wizard to try the equivalent of a less effective version of a Shielding spell (or a slightly more effective version of Invoke Bane) you could pick whether the process uses the roll in Geist or substitute Wisdom for Integrity in the core version.<br /> <br /> Remember that Warding &amp; Binding requires the target entity's Bane to work and ephemeral beings above Rank 2 or 3 are rare in the material world \u2014 higher-Rank entities being extremely difficult to bind without supernatural powers backed by a template-level framework is par for the course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T11:55:38-07:00","id":1535180,"title":"","content":"Since I am looking for a way for the mundane Occult skill to complement spellcasting options, I think I will go with the core version of Warding and Binding, with Wisdom modifying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-06T20:08:44-07:00","id":1535207,"title":"","content":"Would an Unveiling of Time be able to act as an advanced version of Danger Sense, perhaps warning the subject of a likely surprise or ambush [Potency] turns in advance ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T07:28:36-07:00","id":1535902,"title":"","content":"Path tools and materials question.<br /> <br /> The core book mentions that the five tools \u2014 coins, cups, mirrors, rods, and weapons \u2014 must be from specific materials.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery expands upon that, giving new categories (colours, jewels, vehicles, fabrics, etc), it also mentions Ars Nova giving the original categories new items. <b>Must those new items be made of the original Path materials?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let me put an example; Mastigos materials are iron, brass, and leather. Ars Nova says for Weapons you can have brass knuckles, so far good. But what about<b></b>:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Iron knuckles? </b>Path material, no issues here.</li> <li><b>Siderite knuckles?</b> Siderite is iron for all purposes. So good.</li> <li><b>Steel knuckles?</b> I am unsure.</li> <li><b>Hermium (Path aligned perfected material) + Brontium knuckles? </b>Fuzzy. Perhaps Hermium path aligment makes it count?</li> </ol>Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-19-2024, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T08:21:30-07:00","id":1535903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1535902#post1535902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of Sorcery expands upon that, giving new categories (colours, jewels, vehicles, fabrics, etc), it also mentions Ars Nova giving the original categories new items. <b>Must those new items be made of the original Path materials?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A china coffee mug is notmade of lead, bone, or gems, nor is a depleted uranium rod composed of steel, gold, or petrified wood. For that matter, most bows aren't made of glass, crystal, or silver, and a mule is demonstrably not made of wood, stone, or copper.<br /> <br /> The tool needs to be resonant with the Path in some way. The materials are largely relevant for setting a tool apart from otherwise identical tools, hence coins, mirrors, rods and cups not having their own separate qualities in the corebook like weapons do. The question to ask is &quot;does this tool fit into the category of tool it's being used for in a way that is appropriate to the symbolism of the mage's Path?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T09:23:37-07:00","id":1535907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1535903#post1535903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A china coffee mug is notmade of lead, bone, or gems, nor is a depleted uranium rod composed of steel, gold, or petrified wood. For that matter, most bows aren't made of glass, crystal, or silver, and a mule is demonstrably not made of wood, stone, or copper.<br /> <br /> The tool needs to be resonant with the Path in some way. The materials are largely relevant for setting a tool apart from otherwise identical tools, hence coins, mirrors, rods and cups not having their own separate qualities in the corebook like weapons do. The question to ask is &quot;does this tool fit into the category of tool it's being used for in a way that is appropriate to the symbolism of the mage's Path?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. For my example an Amalgam Brontium Knuckle would fit the Mastigos right? Mainly due to being a cruel weapon AND having Hermium in the composition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T13:38:55-07:00","id":1536079,"title":"","content":"Does <i>Gain Skill </i>work on a target who unknowingly had that ability? Lets say its cast on a Sleepwalker to give them the expression skill, but they already had two dots, would it still boost the ones that were there by the spell's Potency ?<br /> <br /> An additional question, lets say a mage casts Telepathy between themselves and subject A, with Reach for intended messages and free communication. Then they cast it separately on subject B with the same parameters. Considering that information can flow freely if the mage acts as a central hub, would it allow subjects A and B to gain the bonuses and penalties from being &quot;on the same network&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-21-2024, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T10:58:57-07:00","id":1536160,"title":"","content":"If I'm reading this right, a mage in her own Oneiros can't risk paradox. So how much reach can a mage in her own Oneiros pull above the limit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T14:22:08-07:00","id":1536168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536160#post1536160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm reading this right, a mage in her own Oneiros can't risk paradox. So how much reach can a mage in her own Oneiros pull above the limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>An arbitrary amount, as they would with appropriate spells in a Demesne or Supernal Verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T15:00:01-07:00","id":1536169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536168#post1536168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An arbitrary amount, as they would with appropriate spells in a Demesne or Supernal Verge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or in a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> Except for some reason (iirc) all three places have sligthly different rules for this one thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T18:42:59-07:00","id":1536180,"title":"","content":"I think in cases where you aren't at risk of Paradox, it's perfectly reasonable to make use of as many factor enhancements and little spell improvements as you please (within any limits on things like range proscribed by the source of the boon), but think some reasonable limitation ought to be placed on a few things that scale linearly with Reach spent.<br /> <br /> The big thing to my mind is Shifting Sands. I think that even if it isn't an unintended intersection that anybody freed from Paradox (or any Supernal being) could use it to go back enough scenes to be equivalent to something like several years, it's a bit of an absurd one that should be reined in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T21:01:59-07:00","id":1536186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536169#post1536169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or in a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> Except for some reason (iirc) all three places have sligthly different rules for this one thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>They all describe the same root mechanical quality, emphasized differently based on what those places are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pocket Dimension, p178</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells cast within the Pocket Dimension do not incur Paradox, unless they are cast sympathetically on someone outside the Pocket Dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verges and Demesnes (Systems), p243</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, as long as a spell that qualifies for the bonus doesn\u2019t leave the Verge, it doesn\u2019t risk Paradox unless a Sleeper is present at some point during the spell\u2019s duration.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Astral Realms (Systems), p249</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sorcerer in his own Oneiros is formidable; his spells never risk Paradox as long as the magic doesn\u2019t leave the confines of his own soul.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T03:44:32-07:00","id":1536196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536180#post1536180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in cases where you aren't at risk of Paradox, it's perfectly reasonable to make use of as many factor enhancements and little spell improvements as you please (within any limits on things like range proscribed by the source of the boon), but think some reasonable limitation ought to be placed on a few things that scale linearly with Reach spent.<br /> <br /> The big thing to my mind is Shifting Sands. I think that even if it isn't an unintended intersection that anybody freed from Paradox (or any Supernal being) could use it to go back enough scenes to be equivalent to something like several years, it's a bit of an absurd one that should be reined in a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I tried to show my players how trivial paradox can be by making a character shifting sands with 49 reach (rolling a 19 on the paradox successes).<br /> <br /> Doing ridiculous things with paradox conditions isn't actually a problem.<br /> <br /> Especially if you shifting sands back out of trouble and don't need to cast any spells for [wisdom linked time interval]...<br /> <br /> So being able to do unparadoxed shifting sands seems less problematic to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They all describe the same root mechanical quality, emphasized differently based on what those places are. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so when reading i focussed on one (the simplest which is pocket dimension) and assumed it applied to all.<br /> <br /> Which would be great, except only sympathetic range out of the pocket causes paradox, and if you run things that way verges become far more powerful.<br /> <br /> Arguable this IS the same as Onerios, but in that case you can cast on yourself and then argue that when you wake up/leave your soul the spell also leaves your soul and triggers a paradox, which makes use ask the &quot;how to deal with delayed paradox&quot; question in a new circumstance.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I would prefer that they all referenced each other and had one set of rules. But bringing sleepers into a pocket dimension and never having them trigger paradox is fun (pity they still get dissonance and quiescense...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T06:27:38-07:00","id":1536200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536196#post1536196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, I tried to show my players how trivial paradox can be by making a character shifting sands with 49 reach (rolling a 19 on the paradox successes).<br /> <br /> Doing ridiculous things with paradox conditions isn't actually a problem.<br /> <br /> Especially if you shifting sands back out of trouble and don't need to cast any spells for [wisdom linked time interval]...<br /> <br /> So being able to do unparadoxed shifting sands seems less problematic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure what point you mean to make with this, so I'll just respond that casually overwriting the previous 49 scenes is not a good thing to be able to do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, just don't cast any other spells in the meantime.&quot; If you cast any spells at all the first time around, you're rewriting history. How far do the consequences of it go?<br /> <br /> More importantly, how much of it ends up overwriting the actions of other players without their input?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T06:47:33-07:00","id":1536201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536196#post1536196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would be great, except only sympathetic range out of the pocket causes paradox, and if you run things that way verges become far more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Pocket Dimension does not interact with the rest of the world except through sympathetic casting or preparations that require sympathetic casting. I believe reasonable people would interpret the fact that an extradimensional space maintained by a spell, which you obviously don't want people who degrade Awakened magic through their awareness of magical effects to be aware of, is written to have innate effects on Paradox risk analogous to those of places similarly &quot;outside the world&quot; and that this innate quality does not negate the normal effect Sleepers have on obvious magic if you for some reason brought them into a place made of obvious magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arguable this IS the same as Onerios, but in that case you can cast on yourself and then argue that when you wake up/leave your soul the spell also leaves your soul and triggers a paradox, which makes use ask the &quot;how to deal with delayed paradox&quot; question in a new circumstance. </div> </div> </div>There's no Paradox to deal with; mages projecting into the Astral are not converting their body into a Dream Form, the Dream Form is being created and ceases to exist outside of the context of that Astral journey. That the Astral is bigger than a mage's individual soul is the reason for the wording of the Paradox stipulation on the Oneiros, not because spells cast by Travelers are somehow capable of breaching the Astral Barrier to affect the outside world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T07:03:32-07:00","id":1536203,"title":"","content":"The phrasing of &quot;a Sleeper is present at some point during the spell's duration&quot; for Verges is weird because Paradox by definition can only happen at the time that a spell is cast (like, a spell that you cast within your Reach <i>outside</i> of a Verge doesn't acquire a Paradox roll if a Sleeper encounters it), so I think it's reasonable to disregard it and otherwise let subjects that had spells exceeding Reach cast on them walk out of a Verge or similar space without incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T08:28:58-07:00","id":1536206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536203#post1536203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The phrasing of &quot;a Sleeper is present at some point during the spell's duration&quot; for Verges is weird because Paradox by definition can only happen at the time that a spell is cast (like, a spell that you cast within your Reach <i>outside</i> of a Verge doesn't acquire a Paradox roll if a Sleeper encounters it), so I think it's reasonable to disregard it and otherwise let subjects that had spells exceeding Reach cast on them walk out of a Verge or similar space without incident.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of that line has always been that it's just an odd way of wording the usual &quot;a Sleeper is present during the casting,&quot; given the lengths ritual casting can reach.<br /> <br /> Leaving the Astral frame of reference entirely in the typical fashion is notably different from teleporting out of a Pocket Dimension or walking out of a Verge; spells cast on one's Dream Form have generally been treated as separate from those targeting the material body one projects from for good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T08:52:42-07:00","id":1536207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536206#post1536206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading of that line has always been that it's just an odd way of wording the usual &quot;a Sleeper is present during the casting,&quot; given the lengths ritual casting can reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It seems especially pertinent given that Demesnes at least are supposed to mostly have semiotics that only really function as a Yantra (the prerequisite for relieving Paradox) to rituals in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving the Astral frame of reference entirely in the typical fashion is notably different from teleporting out of a Pocket Dimension or walking out of a Verge; spells cast on one's Dream Form have generally been treated as separate from those targeting the material body one projects from for good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; it seems like a good way to balance the fact that theoretically the Oneiros can function like a larger space than pocket dimensions or Verges and Demesnes, but the scope of impact from within it and means of crossing into and out of it are somewhat more constrained.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T09:48:02-07:00","id":1536210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536201#post1536201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no Paradox to deal with; mages projecting into the Astral are not converting their body into a Dream Form, the Dream Form is being created and ceases to exist outside of the context of that Astral journey. That the Astral is bigger than a mage's individual soul is the reason for the wording of the Paradox stipulation on the Oneiros, not because spells cast by Travelers are somehow capable of breaching the Astral Barrier to affect the outside world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right about the dream form, but what stops you from casting a spell to enhance your mind? Restore willpower, or cure some permanent condition on someone else's mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 05-24-2024, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T09:50:17-07:00","id":1536211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536200#post1536200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not quite sure what point you mean to make with this, so I'll just respond that casually overwriting the previous 49 scenes is not a good thing to be able to do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, just don't cast any other spells in the meantime.&quot; If you cast any spells at all the first time around, you're rewriting history. How far do the consequences of it go?<br /> <br /> More importantly, how much of it ends up overwriting the actions of other players without their input?</div> </div> </div> </div>The pooint was that mechanically allowing this kind of thing to happen isn't a big deal since it can already happen with the paradox.<br /> <br /> In my case a player had missed several sessions, and we ran through all those missed scenes with the extra player present to get a new timeline where they hadn't missed things, it worked as a recap and allowed some minor changes, and the players all had a great time.<br /> <br /> But whether you should do this or not isn't really relevant to the discussion of can unlimited reach be broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 05-25-2024, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T10:23:41-07:00","id":1536213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536211#post1536211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The poet not was that mechanically allowing this kind of thing to happen isn't a big deal since it can already happen with the paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to point out that the rules state that the severity of a Paradox Condition is supposed to be based on the number of successes left over after the Wisdom roll, so I think that if a person is left with almost four times as many successes as what qualifies as exceptional and the Storyteller doesn't make that something that they feel heavily, that Storyteller really kind of went out of their way to softball the whole thing for them.<br /> <br /> I feel comfortable saying that the rules as presented are the kind of thing where rolling a Paradox dice pool of over fifty would be effectively disincentivized anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T03:10:16-07:00","id":1536240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536213#post1536213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to point out that the rules state that the severity of a Paradox Condition is supposed to be based on the number of successes left over after the Wisdom roll, so I think that if a person is left with almost four times as many successes as what qualifies as exceptional and the Storyteller doesn't make that something that they feel heavily, that Storyteller really kind of went out of their way to softball the whole thing for them.<br /> <br /> I feel comfortable saying that the rules as presented are the kind of thing where rolling a Paradox dice pool of over fifty would be effectively disincentivized anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The severity of the Paradox Condition is based on the number of remaining successes gained on the Paradox roll. </div> </div> </div>This is mechanically represented by the paradox conditions, and mostly involves attracting Abyssal entities and generating more paradox if you cast more spells...<br /> <br /> I can't remember if I used an Abyssal Imago or Abyssal backlash, but neither have any reference to exceptional successes.<br /> <br /> For Imago, with 19 successes you can't resolve it &quot;the good way&quot; as casting a spell with 19 additional reach and not risking a paradox would be impossible.<br /> <br /> So you are forced to risk (a lot of) paradox if you cast anything or wait until it lapsed.<br /> <br /> For backlash, an extra 19 dive to the paradox pool (if you risk one) is likewise rather risky, but you can cast spells so long as you avoid any paradox risk.<br /> <br /> If you are just ignoring paradox and happen to he playing a low wisdom character (such that containing can only do a small number of bashing damage each time) then you may still be limited in combat scenes, and that is the main drawback RAW.<br /> <br /> If I had a player actually try to push the limits i would get more creative with my paradox conditions, and have &quot;attracting the attention of an Annunkai&quot; eventually lead to things like the creation of an Abyssal verge, and Abyssal Nimbus with open conditions leading to possession by various Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> But since my players avoided all paradox all the time, and this one simply avoiding casting anything for the duration of the paradox condition, I found that satisfactory.<br /> <br /> Basically from what I can tell, paradox only gets bad when you create paradox anomolies. Creating an Abyssal Environment tilt, or summoning an Abyssal entity of rank [Reach -3] is pretty serious, and having a -19 to your dice pool for the spell casting almost guarentees that the spell will fail, so in a last ditch effort to cast a spell without being able to contain it, you are guarenteed to fail.<br /> <br /> That makes the after always incentivised to contain paradoxes, even when it kills the character (unless they are explicitly trying to create a paradox anomoly...)<br /> <br /> So unfortunately paradox RAW lacks teeth IMO. Especially for low wisdom characters (who are unlikely to take much damage from attempting to contain a paradox).<br /> <br /> Infact, if I wanted to encourage players to release paradox, I would likely reverse the dice penalty on spellcasting and turn it into a dice bonus.<br /> <br /> Allowing the player extra power (but also messing with the outcome of the spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T04:08:24-07:00","id":1536245,"title":"","content":"You wouldn't create a custom Condition for nineteen successes?<br /> <br /> To The Strongest has a Condition where your aura becomes so abhorrent that animals constantly attack you. I would think something like that would put one in a mind set of not being limited to the Conditions offered in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T07:14:44-07:00","id":1536250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536210#post1536210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right about the dream form, but what stops you from casting a spell to enhance your mind? Restore willpower, or cure some permanent condition on someone else's mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think either of those has anything to do with the effects of one's own Oneiros on Paradox in the first place, and the limitations of Awakened access to the Astral, particularly in a context that allows bringing other people in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536240#post1536240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Imago, with 19 successes you can't resolve it &quot;the good way&quot; as casting a spell with 19 additional reach and not risking a paradox would be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally just use a Demesne, a Verge, your own Oneiros, or a Pocket Dimension. That is the incentivized resolution for characters who have so fucked themselves that it's mathematically impossible to fit the extra Reach into their safety margin: retreat from the Fallen World to clear out the Abyss's interference with your imagination.<br /> <br /> Notably, being unable to effectively cast means being cut off from the Willpower-recovering potential of exceptional success on spellcasting rolls, which will have its impact on a character's behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That makes the after always incentivised to contain paradoxes, even when it kills the character (unless they are explicitly trying to create a paradox anomoly...)<br /> <br /> So unfortunately paradox RAW lacks teeth IMO. Especially for low wisdom characters (who are unlikely to take much damage from attempting to contain a paradox).<br /> <br /> Infact, if I wanted to encourage players to release paradox, I would likely reverse the dice penalty on spellcasting and turn it into a dice bonus. </div> </div> </div>You encourage players to release Paradox on spells they cast frequently and would not want to spend Mana on. The baseline function of it is &quot;magic is buggy,&quot; not &quot;magic will explode on you at a moment's notice.&quot; The most common effects of Paradox on a spell are that its parameters are a little off or the subject takes a Condition. Containing Paradoxes at low Wisdom is a fast track to nigh-permanent Abyssal taint that needs to be dug out with a ritual knife.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allowing the player extra power (but also messing with the outcome of the spell). </div> </div> </div>There is a direct throughline from &quot;casting spells you don't fully understand makes it more likely something completely different from what you intended will happen&quot; to &quot;the endpoint of Scelesti evolution is that you are stuck inside your own soul and can't affect anyone with your magic who isn't trapped in there with you.&quot; That's intentional and encourages characters who don't have the Wisdom to fully contain a Paradox to instead release it and burn Mana on noise-reduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T09:12:31-07:00","id":1536433,"title":"","content":"Does anything prevents a non Seer mage from participating on the Chosen of Mammon cult? If a member of the cult awakened, it would need to be a Seer or it would have the free will to choose another Order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T09:25:31-07:00","id":1536434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536433#post1536433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything prevents a non Seer mage from participating on the Chosen of Mammon cult? If a member of the cult awakened, it would need to be a Seer or it would have the free will to choose another Order?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers do not own the name &quot;Mammon&quot; and unless your game directly attaches that specific sample Mystery Cult to the Ministry in particular or the Seers in general it does not have any direct connection besides sharing the use of the name for the personification of Wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T09:34:09-07:00","id":1536435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536433#post1536433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a member of the cult awakened, it would need to be a Seer or it would have the free will to choose another Order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel has answered the point on whether the cult named &quot;Chosen of Mammon&quot; from the blue book has anything at all to do with Seers of the Throne, but even for those cases where one <i>does</i> Awaken while a member of a Seer Mystery Cult, they have no less free will than any other mage.<br /> <br /> That said, they're realistically going to be likely to be noticed first by Seers of the Throne (who may very well throw off their attempt to Awaken in the first place, if seen early enough and deemed unworthy), and as a group the Seers don't offer a choice to any Awakened who encounter them first.<br /> <br /> (An idea people have often seemed to strangely overlook when seeking an answer to the question of &quot;why would people join the Seers&quot;. For most of them, being a Seer sucks. It's paranoia and uncertainty, being beholden to commands that might encompass every level of your life, and having little real opportunity to advance in the ranks, not to mention likely having to do things that seem messed up to you. There are material benefits, but those are less of a salve after a while. But the Order has plenty of ways to sweep up the newly Awakened before anybody in the Pentacle can get to them, and they're hardly offering an opportunity to join the other side, nor likely to give an entirely honest image of what they're about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T05:00:08-07:00","id":1536498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536435#post1536435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(An idea people have often seemed to strangely overlook when seeking an answer to the question of &quot;why would people join the Seers&quot;. For most of them, being a Seer sucks. It's paranoia and uncertainty, being beholden to commands that might encompass every level of your life, and having little real opportunity to advance in the ranks, not to mention likely having to do things that seem messed up to you. There are material benefits, but those are less of a salve after a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a lot like many jobs with a slightly negative spin put on it. It's what happens to people who Awaken but aren't driven to seek out mysteries. Sign up to be a middle manager of sorts, steady paycheck, easy job most of the time, and someone else has to make the hard decisions. Occasionally you get involved in some stuff that is messed up but someone has to keep things working right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T05:14:24-07:00","id":1536499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536498#post1536498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds a lot like many jobs with a slightly negative spin put on it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is in the small thing of the Seers of the Throne being an organisation of people with mystical powers who entice with promises of the prospect of contribution to the governance of the world and ultimately rising to the status of actual divinity.<br /> <br /> My point was that the group isn't exactly holding on to its members in the long term with a positive feedback loop, but at the same time one isn't really necessary when most of their prospective members are not made aware of alternative sects and probably don't just walk away if even the most positive and curated pitch for joining up doesn't appeal to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T06:33:46-07:00","id":1536504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536498#post1536498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what happens to people who Awaken but aren't driven to seek out mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was a possibility in 1e, but as of 2e, if you aren't interested in mysteries then you're not becoming a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T07:18:48-07:00","id":1536506,"title":"","content":"Oh, I missed that part.<br /> <br /> Yeah, an inquiring mind is a necessity to be a candidate for Awakening in the first place, and an active Gnosis makes that yearning more acute. I think the Order descriptions provide for a decent amount of latitude in what constitutes a fulfilling Mystery (for Seers of the Throne, that's often discerning the will of the Exarchs in the first place), but one is often drawn to understanding <i>something</i>. And even if they think they don't, the alerts of their Peripheral Mage Sight are likely to become quite nagging after a while. The tagline doesn't use the word &quot;addicted&quot; lightly. <br /> <br /> It may not exactly be elaborated upon, but I've always been compelled by statements from DaveB in the past that the mage who takes great pains to ignore that impulse isn't really doing themselves any favours. The nagging becomes an increasing pressure, and if one doesn't give that an outlet from investigation and learning then it will discharge itself through a mage's own soul.<br /> <br /> And that can create Rapture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T18:30:39-07:00","id":1536777,"title":"","content":"Does Shadow Names can appear radically different from a human on the Astral? If yes, is it possible for a mage, using legacies, Life Arcana or other means, to permanently change her physical appearance to something more mystical, like something closely resembling her Shadow Name?<br /> <br /> Use the Shadow Name &quot;Medusa, the Snake Haired Maiden&quot; as an example. It would be too difficult to actually create a functional living snake hair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T00:46:24-07:00","id":1536789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536777#post1536777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Shadow Names can appear radically different from a human on the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>If one has the Shadow Name Merit, yes. The core book describes how a person like that can appear radically different in their dream form, although possibly still within certain boundaries of humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If yes, is it possible for a mage, using legacies, Life Arcana or other means, to permanently change her physical appearance to something more mystical, like something closely resembling her Shadow Name?<br /> <br /> Use the Shadow Name &quot;Medusa, the Snake Haired Maiden&quot; as an example. It would be too difficult to actually create a functional living snake hair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Legacies apparently do still come with some physical alterations. The Daksha, for instance, with their third eyes in the back of their heads. But otherwise, the Life Arcanum is still going to be subject to the usual standards of limitations of time and what can be witnessed by Sleepers, and something like growing snakes from one's head is going to be part of that. Under normal circumstances, the Shadow Name is not sacrosanct under that.<br /> <br /> However, I personally like the premise introduced in Signs of Sorcery that there can occasionally be yantras that provide benefits other than the usual dice bonuses, and could accommodate the idea that a mage might uncover something rare and obscure that can make the likes of certain Life magic Lasting in a way that it wouldn't otherwise be.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's always the option of Mysteries that might enhance one in a way a bit beyond the scope of usual spellcasting. It could be something that enhances the capacity to cast like the runewalking of London, or a place with its own capacity for transformation. An Emanation Realm in particular could possess the properties that one requires; go in pursuit of some place embodying Metamorphosis or the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T06:39:35-07:00","id":1536979,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if there is any book that covers Venice, its history and Mysteries ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T06:55:34-07:00","id":1536980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536979#post1536979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if there is any book that covers Venice, its history and Mysteries ?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Light of the Sun,</i> from Dark Eras 2, covers the Italian Renaissance with a focus on the Awakened, the Unchained, and the Remade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T15:08:04-07:00","id":1537118,"title":"","content":"Mages have the functional effects of the <b>Lucid Dreamer</b> merit (Changeling 2e p.123)? It is not needed for mages right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-09-2024, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T19:15:59-07:00","id":1537127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1537118#post1537118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have the functional effects of the <b>Lucid Dreamer</b> merit (Changeling 2e p.123)? It is not needed for mages right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lucid Dreamer Merit allows a non-changeling to enter the Gate of Ivory by rolling Resolve + Composure to meditate while going to sleep or sleeping, which is also the way Mage's section on the Astral describes entering their own dreams with the additional note that Mind spells can bypass the need to meditate, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T07:12:34-07:00","id":1537257,"title":"","content":"Does spells listed on the core book that add another arcanas count as Combined Spells? Or combined spells are two different spells mashed into one for the purpose of Spell Control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T07:22:49-07:00","id":1537258,"title":"","content":"They are not combined spells. Combined spells are multiple spells cast at the same time. Spells with added Arcana (also known as conjunctional spells by the community) are still a single spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T08:45:09-07:00","id":1537261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1537258#post1537258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not combined spells. Combined spells are multiple spells cast at the same time. Spells with added Arcana (also known as conjunctional spells by the community) are still a single spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also known as conjunctional spells in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed tends to avoid conjunctional spells, and never uses that term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T10:51:58-07:00","id":1537864,"title":"","content":"Would a Weaving of Forces be enough to alter the Pauli Exclusion Principle on a subject, allowing them to phase through [Potency] objects, such as walls, bullets and trees ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T07:55:48-07:00","id":1537896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1537864#post1537864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Weaving of Forces be enough to alter the Pauli Exclusion Principle on a subject, allowing them to phase through [Potency] objects, such as walls, bullets and trees ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly sure if this element of quantum mechanics would have anything to do with letting objects pass through one another in the first place. Nevertheless, it doesn't really strike me as Forces the way it exists in Supernal symbolism, at least at that level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T17:40:08-07:00","id":1537915,"title":"","content":"Applying Forces to anything on the quantum level is basically throwing Matter away, as those &quot;forces&quot; are basically the setup for the properties of matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T03:53:39-07:00","id":1537937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1537915#post1537915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Applying Forces to anything on the quantum level is basically throwing Matter away, as those &quot;forces&quot; are basically the setup for the properties of matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I would assume that it was a matter spell.<br /> <br /> Though the Pauli exclusion principle is vital to applying to forces that prevent Bose condensates from forming (in fermionic matter) I think symbolically it is a matter spell.<br /> <br /> But if you go with many roads, that I think it is at least Patterning to turn a Fermion into a Bosom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T02:43:57-07:00","id":1538074,"title":"","content":"If a mage wanted to help a ghost who'd resolved their Anchors pass on would they be able to do so with the Death Arcanum, or would they need the 'Pass On' Ceremony from Geist to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T10:16:16-07:00","id":1538089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538074#post1538074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage wanted to help a ghost who'd resolved their Anchors pass on would they be able to do so with the Death Arcanum, or would they need the 'Pass On' Ceremony from Geist to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a ruling Death spell would be enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T10:23:55-07:00","id":1538090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538089#post1538089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that a ruling Death spell would be enough</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe even compelling.<br /> <br /> Also, the passing on ceremony can be done without any particular magic, a Mage could spend a tiny bit of time researching to figure out what different culture's passing on ceremonies require. Without Death it is not a hard thing to organise (or get someone else to).<br /> <br /> In fact it may be harder to prevent a ghost from passing on once they resolve their anchors (or so I have been told... They usually have nothing to remain for).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T11:06:21-07:00","id":1538092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538090#post1538090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe even compelling.<br /> <br /> Also, the passing on ceremony can be done without any particular magic, a Mage could spend a tiny bit of time researching to figure out what different culture's passing on ceremonies require. Without Death it is not a hard thing to organise (or get someone else to).<br /> <br /> In fact it may be harder to prevent a ghost from passing on once they resolve their anchors (or so I have been told... They usually have nothing to remain for).</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make sense from an in-universe perspective I think, as Ceremonies are less magic and more just a part of the way the world works. I mainly ask because mechanically 'Pass On' is a five dot Ceremony meaning it would be more expensive for a mage to learn than a new dot in an Arcana. If I'm remembering correctly from Geist, ghosts with resolved Anchors don't automatically pass on, they just kind of stick around until the Ceremony is performed. I don't think it says anything explicitly about them being able to choose to pass on at any point once they've reached the resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T04:32:42-07:00","id":1538117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538092#post1538092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does make sense from an in-universe perspective I think, as Ceremonies are less magic and more just a part of the way the world works. I mainly ask because mechanically 'Pass On' is a five dot Ceremony meaning it would be more expensive for a mage to learn than a new dot in an Arcana. If I'm remembering correctly from Geist, ghosts with resolved Anchors don't automatically pass on, they just kind of stick around until the Ceremony is performed. I don't think it says anything explicitly about them being able to choose to pass on at any point once they've reached the resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a ghost which resolves their anchors becomes immune to essence bleed, but still requires 1 essence per day to stay active. And without anchors to provide them with that they would quickly go dormant... Unless they have another source of Essence. Otherwise they are rather potent, as the don't get dragged into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Easiest way to get essence seems to be eating castoffs/barghests.<br /> Fulfilling a Krewe Virtue/Creed.<br /> Absent can gain the Wake merit.<br /> Remain in a Deep Dominion for a full day.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T08:07:16-07:00","id":1538131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538117#post1538117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a ghost which resolves their anchors becomes immune to essence bleed, but still requires 1 essence per day to stay active. And without anchors to provide them with that they would quickly go dormant... Unless they have another source of Essence. Otherwise they are rather potent, as the don't get dragged into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Easiest way to get essence seems to be eating castoffs/barghests.<br /> Fulfilling a Krewe Virtue/Creed.<br /> Absent can gain the Wake merit.<br /> Remain in a Deep Dominion for a full day.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked the rulebook and it says:<br /> <br /> ''A ghost who resolves all her Anchors is no longer subject to Essence bleed and is not dragged into the Underworld. She may Pass On with the appropriate Ceremony''<br /> <br /> So I think you are correct for the most part, though it does seem to me that the ghost needs the Ceremony (or equivalent spell) to pass on. I don't think they can choose to do so at any time themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T08:43:59-07:00","id":1538132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538131#post1538131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just checked the rulebook and it says:<br /> <br /> ''A ghost who resolves all her Anchors is no longer subject to Essence bleed and is not dragged into the Underworld. She may Pass On with the appropriate Ceremony''<br /> <br /> So I think you are correct for the most part, though it does seem to me that the ghost needs the Ceremony (or equivalent spell) to pass on. I don't think they can choose to do so at any time themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the ceremony section also states <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Virtually every religion\u2019s funerary rites include the Pass On Ceremony </div> </div> </div>And the rituals for the Pass On include the example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perform the last rites of the ghost\u2019s religion. </div> </div> </div>So if a ghost wants to, and their religion isn't rare/extinct, then they should be able to find someone to perform it for them.<br /> <br /> Also, Sin-Eaters can't buy the ceremony, it is free as an innate ceremony, so it isn't clear that it can be bought, or at what cost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T10:11:30-07:00","id":1538136,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about how Geist Second Edition elaborated on the mechanics of ghosts, but it does sound to me like a Ruling of Death could achieve the desired effect. <br /> <br /> My question would be if it would be something that functions as Lasting as a given, or requires a Reach effect. I feel as though it would be both consistent with the usual mechanics for such things and provide some reasonable leeway to resistant ghosts if it was the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T10:33:31-07:00","id":1538137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538132#post1538132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the ceremony section also states<br /> <br /> And the rituals for the Pass On include the example:<br /> <br /> <br /> So if a ghost wants to, and their religion isn't rare/extinct, then they should be able to find someone to perform it for them.<br /> <br /> Also, Sin-Eaters can't buy the ceremony, it is free as an innate ceremony, so it isn't clear that it can be bought, or at what cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding someone to perform the Ceremony should indeed be possible and relatively easy from an in-universe perspective I agree, personally I was more thinking that the mechanical cost (Ceremonies are one experience per dot making Pass On cost five experience) was relatively high given that this is the only explicit way mentioned as to how a ghost might pass on mechanically. But it does make sense that a Death mage could do something similar without needing to purchase the Ceremony (or just find someone who knows the Ceremony.<br /> <br /> As for purchasing, the rulebook say this about the innate Sin-Eater Ceremonies: ''All Sin-Eaters can perform these Ceremonies. Other characters may purchase them as normal.'' So other characters should be able to purchase it if they're interested in helping ghosts move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T10:35:48-07:00","id":1538138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538136#post1538136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about how Geist Second Edition elaborated on the mechanics of ghosts, but it does sound to me like a Ruling of Death could achieve the desired effect.<br /> <br /> My question would be if it would be something that functions as Lasting as a given, or requires a Reach effect. I feel as though it would be both consistent with the usual mechanics for such things and provide some reasonable leeway to resistant ghosts if it was the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it makes sense it would be inherently Lasting since the Ceremony is essentially putting a ghost to rest after it's burdens have been resolved. I think it would be a bit strange (if funny) if you send a restless ghost off to the after-afterlife only for them to pop back up a week later because you forgot to make your spell's duration indefinite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T12:13:18-07:00","id":1538145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538138#post1538138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be a bit strange (if funny) if you send a restless ghost off to the after-afterlife only for them to pop back up a week later because you forgot to make your spell's duration indefinite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well like I said, there are spells where you can Reach to make them Lasting, in which case no duration has to be expended at all.<br /> <br /> Still, it sounds like I had mistaken the nature of Passing On, and it's actually that one thing where ghosts fade away from apparent existence peacefully.<br /> <br /> And that <i>does</i> sound like it would innately be Lasting in the same way that healing or destroying them would be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T13:19:05-07:00","id":1538147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538137#post1538137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...personally I was more thinking that the mechanical cost (Ceremonies are one experience per dot making Pass On cost five experience) was relatively high given that this is the only explicit way mentioned as to how a ghost might pass on mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the implication is that the <i>C</i><i>eremony </i>is meant to be a generic one, so it can allow anyone who knows the ritual to pass on any ghost in a semi-predictable manner. The Imam from the intro-text isn't doing a Ceremony, they're leading the practices of their religion, which <i>might</i> happen to function as a Ceremony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:39:53-07:00","id":1538267,"title":"","content":"Casting a spell that requires multiple Arcana cost mana if one of them is not a Ruling Arcana for the mage?<br /> <br /> For example, casting a Time 3 + Spirit 1 Spell for an Acanthi or a Mind 2 + Forces 2 spell for a Mastigoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T19:09:37-07:00","id":1538272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538267#post1538267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting a spell that requires multiple Arcana cost mana if one of them is not a Ruling Arcana for the mage?<br /> <br /> For example, casting a Time 3 + Spirit 1 Spell for an Acanthi or a Mind 2 + Forces 2 spell for a Mastigoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would seem to be the intuitive reading of &quot;Improvising a spell using a Common or Inferior Arcanum costs one point of Mana,&quot; yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T06:48:33-07:00","id":1538299,"title":"","content":"If <i>Postcognition </i>is active and you want to use <i>Divination</i> or <i>Prophecy</i> on the observed subject, does that count as sensory range ? Temporal Sympathy would suggest so, but one could also argue that, similar to a scrying window, it requires remote viewing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:17:57-07:00","id":1538366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538299#post1538299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>Postcognition </i>is active and you want to use <i>Divination</i> or <i>Prophecy</i> on the observed subject, does that count as sensory range ? Temporal Sympathy would suggest so, but one could also argue that, similar to a scrying window, it requires remote viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see what Temporal Sympathy has to do with it, since that is only about a target's connections to its own past selves.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can cast a spell on a subject that you're viewing through Postcognition any more than you could do it on a recording of them. I think targets need some manner of real time perception of them, whether through physical contact or senses or a live video feed or sympathetic bond, because the imago of the spell needs to incorporate the target as it currently is in order to inflict a spell upon them. An image of them created through an Unveiling spell is just too insubstantial and disconnected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T22:17:42-07:00","id":1538508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538366#post1538366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see what Temporal Sympathy has to do with it, since that is only about a target's connections to its own past selves.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can cast a spell on a subject that you're viewing through Postcognition any more than you could do it on a recording of them. I think targets need some manner of real time perception of them, whether through physical contact or senses or a live video feed or sympathetic bond, because the imago of the spell needs to incorporate the target as it currently is in order to inflict a spell upon them. An image of them created through an Unveiling spell is just too insubstantial and disconnected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically you can't cast on the past version of the subject without actually going back in time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T07:21:40-07:00","id":1538561,"title":"","content":"Does the Resources bonus from Seer Status stack with the normal merit, allowing a mage to go beyond Resources 5 ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T12:22:37-07:00","id":1538577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538561#post1538561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Resources bonus from Seer Status stack with the normal merit, allowing a mage to go beyond Resources 5 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, it stacks, but doesn't goes beyond 5.<br /> <br /> Instead, in the eventuality that you should go beyond 5, you'd either get no benefit or get the extra dot back by the Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T07:48:16-07:00","id":1538656,"title":"","content":"Just a bit confused about quiescence. <br /> <br /> I thought the big difference between it and Ascention was that it's an actual curse, NPT disbelief. Like as long as a spell was vulgar/could be seen, it would activate. But I've read stuff like the invisible rifle as an imbued item a mage could convince others is just an oddity of a gun, or that change weather could be used to conceal the lightning strike spell. <br /> <br /> i just thought that wasn't possible, that if a spell is vulgar, and seen, it's going to be under the curse whether or not the person believes it mundane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T08:11:31-07:00","id":1538659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538656#post1538656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a bit confused about quiescence.<br /> <br /> I thought the big difference between it and Ascention was that it's an actual curse, NPT disbelief. Like as long as a spell was vulgar/could be seen, it would activate. But I've read stuff like the invisible rifle as an imbued item a mage could convince others is just an oddity of a gun, or that change weather could be used to conceal the lightning strike spell.<br /> <br /> i just thought that wasn't possible, that if a spell is vulgar, and seen, it's going to be under the curse whether or not the person believes it mundane</div> </div> </div> </div>See the &quot;Obvious magic&quot; sidebar on page 298 of the corebook. The spell's effect has to be clearly, openly supernatural in effect and the Sleeper needs to be both conscious and cognizant of the magic's impossibility, which affects whether the effect is subject to Paradox (at the time of casting) or Dissonance (if encountered later). If there's not a Sleeper present and aware that something that shouldn't be mundanely possible happening, the Curse doesn't make things any worse than it would be if the mage was casting in an isolated mundane area.<br /> <br /> Quiescence means the Sleepers either forget or misremember what they see of Supernal or Abyssal phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T12:45:41-07:00","id":1538670,"title":"","content":"I do wonder what the boundaries for that are with something like mind control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-16-2024, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:50:50-07:00","id":1538785,"title":"","content":"Does a hex allow you to choose whether the subject receives the moderate or grave version of the Sick or Poisoned tilts ? Does the grave version instead require a second application, similar top what happens with Arm Wrack ? Would the Toxicity be determined by Potency after applying Withstand ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-17-2024, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:11:29-07:00","id":1538828,"title":"","content":"Narratively, how does Withstanding work? Is it just the subtle Arcana that make up a soul fighting to resist manipulation? I don't think it could considering all sentient can withstand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:27:36-07:00","id":1538832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538828#post1538828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, how does Withstanding work? Is it just the subtle Arcana that make up a soul fighting to resist manipulation? I don't think it could considering all sentient can withstand</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the qualities that make subjects harder to affect with spells. Sympathetic links and inanimate objects can Withstand magic. Conscious beings are notable primarily for their ability to choose <i>not</i> to Withstand an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:37:56-07:00","id":1538835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538832#post1538832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the qualities that make subjects harder to affect with spells. Sympathetic links and inanimate objects can Withstand magic. Conscious beings are notable primarily for their ability to choose <i>not</i> to Withstand an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>So as an example, the spell &quot;eradicate Forces&quot; can be withstood by a human because of sympathetic links he has? As well as the material energy makeup part of refusing to be changed?<br /> <br /> Is the ability to withstand partially due to supernal reflection?<br /> <br /> EDIT: final question. As Time travel changes can be dispelled, does this extend to people who are killed in the past? As in the event being dispelled would bring that person back to life? Just asking because I thought a story in the Fallen World Anthology had someone kill a mage by Time travel, which was treated as very definitely final (I thought)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 07-18-2024, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T09:33:43-07:00","id":1538843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1538835#post1538835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as an example, the spell &quot;eradicate Forces&quot; can be withstood by a human because of sympathetic links he has? As well as the material energy makeup part of refusing to be changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Sympathy makes it harder/riskier to affect the target sympathetically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the ability to withstand partially due to supernal reflection? </div> </div> </div>There is no textual universal statement of how Withstand works. The inference to be made is that it's for the same reason supernatural powers that aren't Awakened spells find it harder to affect a target that is sturdier/more distant/more mentally defended/etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> : final question. As Time travel changes can be dispelled, does this extend to people who are killed in the past? As in the event being dispelled would bring that person back to life? Just asking because I thought a story in the Fallen World Anthology had someone kill a mage by Time travel, which was treated as very definitely final (I thought) </div> </div> </div>Once an alteration to history has caught up to the present (or the caster dies in the past) the changes are set and cannot be dispelled; if you want them to not die in the past you would have to change the past again, with all the risk that entails.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T09:59:39-07:00","id":1538844,"title":"","content":"I take Withstand as just being a case of some spells have binary effects that still require a certain Potency to effect change the way some scaling effects do.<br /> <br /> Like, if you want to use a Ruling of Forces to make a size 1 flame into a size 4 flame, that requires Potency 3 in all circumstances. The only difference is that you have options for lower Potency that you don't for certain other effects on other targets.<br /> <br /> So it's not resistance to change so much as the level of applied force necessary to cause change. Take a steel bar. The bar isn't resisting you if it doesn't bend beneath your hands, it's just that the composition dictates certain minimum requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T01:52:18-07:00","id":1539415,"title":"","content":"MtAW 1E. The cabal of my game want to make some research about some other races (in particular True Fae and changeling stuff), is there any example of research for this kind of stuff? I found the rule about researching abyss stuff in <b>Intruders Encounters with the Abyss </b>that I think I will use, but I haven't found anything similar for a research like that, I'm ok even if it's from another splat book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","name":"Pyro165","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T06:29:02-07:00","id":1539419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyro165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1539415#post1539415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MtAW 1E. The cabal of my game want to make some research about some other races (in particular True Fae and changeling stuff), is there any example of research for this kind of stuff? I found the rule about researching abyss stuff in <b>Intruders Encounters with the Abyss </b>that I think I will use, but I haven't found anything similar for a research like that, I'm ok even if it's from another splat book</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silver Ladder book has some bits on what research might turn up about vampires, werewolves, ghosts, Prometheans, changelings, and hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T09:54:20-07:00","id":1540993,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do mages know all the new accessible Practices when achieving a new rank in an Arcana? i.e. if I go from Arcana 1 to Arcana 2, do I know the Ruling, Veiling and Perfecting things that this Arcana can do instinctively?</li> <li>Are Archmages actually immortal by default? I mean without needing an imperial spell, just by virtue of the Archmage abilities?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw Core 2e P. 252</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An<br /> archmaster has transcended her Path, forging her own, person-<br /> al connection to the Supernal Realms called a Golden Road.<br /> This manifests as a shimmering Astral Realm, separate from<br /> all the known Inner Realms, which a handful of archmasters<br /> have revealed to actually be their half-Ascended souls<b>. Rather<br /> than meditating into the Astral, archmasters meditate out of<br /> themselves; an archmage\u2019s seemingly physical body is no more<br /> crucial to him than a mage\u2019s dream form.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperial Mysteries p. 25, 26 </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She adds gateways leading from herself to other worlds<br /> when they prove useful, her astral or<b> physical body<br /> forming whenever she leaves the Road</b>.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Entering the Road is as simple as success on an instant<br /> Wits + Composure roll.\u200b<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> <b>Archmasters can survive indefinitely within their own Roads<br /> without aging or requiring sustenance</b>, but can only cast spells<br /> that target their own patterns, the Road itself, or anyone else<br /> inside\u200b.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Where the Astral Barrier would be, t<b>he Road ends with<br /> an image of the archmage herself </b>\u2014 refl ecting pools, mir-<br /> rors, statues and doorways containing mirror images have<br /> been recorded by archmages exploring the Roads of others.<br /> By spending one point of Mana and stepping into the im-<br /> age of herself, the archmage enters the material world.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So IF I am reading those right, every Archmage can live forever in the Road, if they leave they go as a they see themselves... So you dont need any other magic to be immortal, right? You simply imagine yourself younger, or at least at the age you became an archmage, or whatever your self-image is (20 years old self? a different gender perhaps?) and if you get sick or maimed, you just return to your Road and rebuild your body again with out sickness and with full body parts, right?<br /> <br /> An Archmage can be <b>killed</b>, but natural death is a thing of the past.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T12:23:52-07:00","id":1540998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1540993#post1540993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do mages know all the new accessible Practices when achieving a new rank in an Arcana? i.e. if I go from Arcana 1 to Arcana 2, do I know the Ruling, Veiling and Perfecting things that this Arcana can do instinctively?</li> <li>Are Archmages actually immortal by default? I mean without needing an imperial spell, just by virtue of the Archmage abilities?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So IF I am reading those right, every Archmage can live forever in the Road, if they leave they go as a they see themselves... So you dont need any other magic to be immortal, right? You simply imagine yourself younger, or at least at the age you became an archmage, or whatever your self-image is (20 years old self? a different gender perhaps?) and if you get sick or maimed, you just return to your Road and rebuild your body again with out sickness and with full body parts, right?<br /> <br /> An Archmage can be <b>killed</b>, but natural death is a thing of the past.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember <i>The Soul Cage </i>correctly, which set some of the baselines for the <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> book, an archmage can have eternal youth and I think perfect health, but can choose not to as well, according to Dave B. Cobalt's future self is one such case, looking noticeably older, because he didn't see natural death as something that should be avoided. But in theory, it is part of base package of becoming a post-human Gnostic being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T13:14:48-07:00","id":1541001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1540993#post1540993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So IF I am reading those right, every Archmage can live forever in the Road, if they leave they go as a they see themselves... So you dont need any other magic to be immortal, right? You simply imagine yourself younger, or at least at the age you became an archmage, or whatever your self-image is (20 years old self? a different gender perhaps?) and if you get sick or maimed, you just return to your Road and rebuild your body again with out sickness and with full body parts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Road ends with an image of herself&quot; doesn't have anything to do with the character's capacity to age; they're still subject to mortal frailties when they're not literally outside of reality, they just have the capacity to instantly return to a place that suspends those frailties. It's one of the reasons they act through agents (or subsouls, once they pick up Dominions or adopt a sub-soul through Entities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T14:36:19-07:00","id":1541003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541001#post1541001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Road ends with an image of herself&quot; doesn't have anything to do with the character's capacity to age; they're still subject to mortal frailties when they're not literally outside of reality, they just have the capacity to instantly return to a place that suspends those frailties. It's one of the reasons they act through agents (or subsouls, once they pick up Dominions or adopt a sub-soul through Entities).</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is, and that is what I am trying to confirm.<br /> <br /> Outside of the road, all those frailties apply, agreed. BUT when returning to the road, they seem able to reset the point for themselves outside reality.<br /> <br /> So, I am MENTOK archmaster of some Arcana, I have been in my Road for 200 years, not aging a day since I entered... I want to go outside and then spend 20 years in the Fallen World, in those 20 years I get older, sicker, I might even lose a finger... When I return to my Road, I stop aging again, and IF I return outside, I can pick my self image as younger version of myself. If the only thing that matter when returning to reality is my self image, I can form a new physical body at whatever age / appearance that is my self concept. That is my question / statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T15:17:06-07:00","id":1541004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541003#post1541003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is, and that is what I am trying to confirm.<br /> <br /> Outside of the road, all those frailties apply, agreed. BUT when returning to the road, they seem able to reset the point for themselves outside reality.<br /> <br /> So, I am MENTOK archmaster of some Arcana, I have been in my Road for 200 years, not aging a day since I entered... I want to go outside and then spend 20 years in the Fallen World, in those 20 years I get older, sicker, I might even lose a finger... When I return to my Road, I stop aging again, and IF I return outside, I can pick my self image as younger version of myself. If the only thing that matter when returning to reality is my self image, I can form a new physical body at whatever age / appearance that is my self concept. That is my question / statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;An image of herself&quot; doesn't mean &quot;an idealized image&quot;, or &quot;an imagined image&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert here, but by how this is phrased I see no reason to read in it that the archmage has any sort of control on how this image is, or any reason to think this image is anything other than a exact reflection of their present self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T15:36:47-07:00","id":1541006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541004#post1541004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;An image of herself&quot; doesn't mean &quot;an idealized image&quot;, or &quot;an imagined image&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert here, but by how this is phrased I see no reason to read in it that the archmage has any sort of control on how this image is, or any reason to think this image is anything other than a exact reflection of their present self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. I thought it was part of the thing. But you are right, nothing would really favour that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T18:27:03-07:00","id":1541009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541003#post1541003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of the road, all those frailties apply, agreed. BUT when returning to the road, they seem able to reset the point for themselves outside reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, the reset you are talking about is not implied by the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I am MENTOK archmaster of some Arcana, I have been in my Road for 200 years, not aging a day since I entered... I want to go outside and then spend 20 years in the Fallen World, in those 20 years I get older, sicker, I might even lose a finger... When I return to my Road, I stop aging again, and IF I return outside, I can pick my self image as younger version of myself. If the only thing that matter when returning to reality is my self image, I can form a new physical body at whatever age / appearance that is my self concept. That is my question / statement. </div> </div> </div>Your self-image is not the same thing as simply picturing yourself differently. If it worked that way it would obviate the utility of the Life Arcanum for archmasters and render the Mind Arcanum disproportionately effective for them.<br /> <br /> What Seekers get as a part of simply having attained archmastery of any type is more akin to how, in Mummy, the sahu is subject to the character's own self-concept. Unless I am <i>severely</i> deluding myself as a being who exists in the world, I am not going to perceive the effects of aging on my body as akin to forgetting I put on some makeup that I can wash off when I get home. You would need magic to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> The comparison that most immediately comes to mind is that there's a wizard in the Discworld books who lives in the timeless realm of Death's domain because the hourglass that counts down his remaining lifespan stops while he's there and he has seconds left to live if he goes out into the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T03:24:10-07:00","id":1541016,"title":"","content":"I would note, I think you can change your self-image, in the same way your dream form is liable to change if you develop a new shadow name.<br /> <br /> You can't simply imagine it is different, or use it to disguise yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dream form may look nothing like the sorcerer, because this is her self-image as influenced by contact from the Supernal, and divorced from the limitations of flesh. Characters with the Shadow Name Merit often appear radically different in age, race, sex, or fitness, as their dream forms conform to their magical selves. </div> </div> </div>The rules for Archmages don't specify that their physical bodies are actually dream forms, but I would happily allow them to appear in bodies of the age, race, sex and fitness that conform to their magical selves...<br /> <br /> But spend 90 years in the material realm and it will change your self-image significantly.<br /> <br /> I just think, in the same sense mages can take on a Shadow Name, Archmages should be able to alter their self-image by investing significant time and effort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T13:04:51-07:00","id":1541031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1540993#post1540993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mages know all the new accessible Practices when achieving a new rank in an Arcana? i.e. if I go from Arcana 1 to Arcana 2, do I know the Ruling, Veiling and Perfecting things that this Arcana can do instinctively?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's looking at it too much in terms of gameplay being how something is experienced in character.<br /> <br /> In character, developing a new Arcanum dot is not a matter of spending the currency to move you up a level and then it being a question of whether or not you even know what to do with that level.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of how becoming more powerful in an Arcanum is a function of the learning and discovery and introspection that allows you to comprehend further ways those symbols can be assembled into imagos with greater sophistication (as well as greater depth of understanding of how to effectively assemble already known symbols, which is represented by greater Reach and primary spell factors).<br /> <br /> The game positions Ruling, Veiling, and Shielding as applications of the Arcana that all organically reside at about the same level of understanding, which I do think holds up.<br /> <br /> In short, it's not that becoming an Apprentice means you might then be able to realise that you're capable of Ruling spells, it's that the process of coming to understand how to cast Ruling spells (as an advancement of Compelling spells) is what becoming an Apprentice even is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T06:03:53-07:00","id":1541056,"title":"","content":"Mage 1E, Incognito Presence spell from mind 2.<br /> I'm not sure how effective it is, for some part of it seems similar to vampire's Cloak of Night but at the same time it's just something that anyone can see through (with enough success) am I right? Plus, seems like you can be basically &quot;invisible&quot; if it's ok to have people around, like a crowd or some place with people moving around, but for example, a museum, at night, with only one security guard around, would the spell help or being seen by the guard would count as &quot;attention grabbing&quot;? Since area is off-limits to anyone and such<br /> <br /> Another question, about spirits and mages, always 1E. Book of the spirits says that they speak a different language, mage with spirit Arcana that cast spells to speak with spirit, can be understood and speak with them? Not sure since I'm not finding anything about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","user":"Pyro165","date":". 08-27-2024, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","name":"Pyro165","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T14:28:35-07:00","id":1541244,"title":"","content":"When using the Reach effect of <i>Prophecy</i>, does the mage keep the reduced Doors after it ends because they know how the conversation will play out or does it only work while duration lasts ? I imagine once they know, they know, but wanted to confirm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T03:12:56-07:00","id":1541280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541244#post1541244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using the Reach effect of <i>Prophecy</i>, does the mage keep the reduced Doors after it ends because they know how the conversation will play out or does it only work while duration lasts ? I imagine once they know, they know, but wanted to confirm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right. I mean, is it not an immediate effect as written? Like, mechanically, you ask questions, but is the implication not that the character is just having information dumped into their head at the moment they cast the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T10:20:43-07:00","id":1541299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541280#post1541280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're right. I mean, is it not an immediate effect as written? Like, mechanically, you ask questions, but is the implication not that the character is just having information dumped into their head at the moment they cast the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even for Divination, part of how it's able to interact with the Duration factor is that a person doesn't have to ask all of the questions they'd get out of the spell's Potency at once. For Prophecy, I would say that the level of detail one might get out of their explored hypothetical is an additional consideration for how long the spell lasts.<br /> <br /> I want to say that the benefit to the social interaction system of the spell would not last beyond its Duration for a combination of how factors can now take place outside of its hypotheticals and that the user is no longer navigating in real time. You might have applicable knowledge of the responses, but lack the same deft agility, and will undermine yourself with the need to think about it and try to recall which branching path goes where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T18:15:46-07:00","id":1541369,"title":"","content":"The Spirit Familiar spell stats:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage creates a Familiar bond between a spirit and a mage,<br /> who must both be subjects of the spell. <b>The spirit may not be<br /> greater than Rank 2.</b> The mage gains the Familiar Merit and the<br /> spirit the Familiar Manifestation Condition for the Duration of<br /> the spell. Both parties must be willing, and can end the bond<br /> whenever they wish. </div> </div> </div>What happens if you use Bolster Spirit on it to increase rank? Does it break the Familiar bond permanently? Only for the Bolster Spirit duration? Does not break the bond?<br /> <br /> What about Shape Spirit? Which, if any effect, does it have on the bond? Break, suspend, or not affected at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-01T18:34:51-07:00","id":1541371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541369#post1541369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spirit Familiar spell stats:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What happens if you use Bolster Spirit on it to increase rank? Does it break the Familiar bond permanently? Only for the Bolster Spirit duration? Does not break the bond?<br /> <br /> What about Shape Spirit? Which, if any effect, does it have on the bond? Break, suspend, or not affected at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the spell would remains on them, doing nothing, similar to a spell that is fully Withstood. When they return to Rank 2, the Familiar bond returns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T16:08:12-07:00","id":1541415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541371#post1541371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the spell would remains on them, doing nothing, similar to a spell that is fully Withstood. When they return to Rank 2, the Familiar bond returns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, what about Shape Spirit? Can it break / suspend the bond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-02T19:24:01-07:00","id":1541427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541415#post1541415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, what about Shape Spirit? Can it break / suspend the bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Familiar bond is maintained through both the spell's effect and the mutual agreement of the mage and the familiar. Shape Spirit does not have any effects that would make a spirit cease to be a viable subject of the Familiar spell, but depending on the spirit, the change, and the circumstances, it may prompt the spirit to end the Familiar Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T10:59:28-07:00","id":1541465,"title":"","content":"Some background:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Familiar merit p. 101 Mage Awakening Core 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character has been bonded to a Familiar, an<br /> ephemeral entity (a ghost, <b>spirit</b>, or Goetia) <b>that has agreed<br /> to partner her in exchange for safety from bleeding Essence.</b><br /> Design your familiar with the rules for ephemeral entities in<br /> Chapter Six; it may be wholly in Twilight or Fettered to an item<br /> or animal. Two dots in this Merit indicate a Rank 1 entity. Four<br /> dots indicate a Rank 2 entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Familiar spell p. 183 Mage Awakening Core 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage creates a Familiar bond between a spirit and a mage,<br /> who must both be subjects of the spell. The spirit may not be<br /> greater than Rank 2. The mage gains the Familiar Merit and the<br /> spirit the Familiar Manifestation Condition for the Duration of<br /> the spell. <b>Both parties must be willing, and can end the bond<br /> whenever they wish.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laws of the Lawless p. 216 Werewolf Forsaken Core 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As<br /> strange and alien as they may appear, the idigam are spirits and<br /> broadly follow the same rules\u200b</b><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Both Formless and Coalesced are<b> immune to supernatural<br /> powers that would command them, master them, or reshape<br /> their abilities, whether from Gifts, rites, or the witchcraft of<br /> other beings</b>. The idigam can be bound or forced into dormancy,<br /> but they <b>can never simply be leashed like a dog and forced into<br /> obedience</b>. Their ancient, ever-flowing Essence simply shrugs<br /> off any such attempts to chain them to docility.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does this mean that Rank 2 Idigam (if any exist) are a valid target for the <b>Familiar </b>spell? It is a willing partnership.</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to <b>Shape Spirit, Coaxing the Spirits, Command Spirit</b>? Seems to be right, but not sure about Coaxing.</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to<b> Bind Spirit</b>? Making them Manifest would could as reshaping them?</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to <b>Craft Fetish</b>? Would this cound as obedience or the dormancy bypasses this?</li> </ol>\u200bThanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:23:41-07:00","id":1541469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541465#post1541465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does this mean that Rank 2 Idigam (if any exist) are a valid target for the <b>Familiar </b>spell? It is a willing partnership.</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to <b>Shape Spirit, Coaxing the Spirits, Command Spirit</b>? Seems to be right, but not sure about Coaxing.</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to<b> Bind Spirit</b>? Making them Manifest would could as reshaping them?</li> <li>Are Idigams immune to <b>Craft Fetish</b>? Would this cound as obedience or the dormancy bypasses this?</li> </ol>Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>1. There is no such thing as a Rank 2 idigam; the weakest ones are Rank 3 Formless, and Coalescing grants an idigam an additional Rank.<br /> 2. Immune to all three.<br /> 3. They can explicitly be bound. Image and Materialize might be on shakier ground, but using Fetter or Possess to keep it stuck in a rock is within spec.<br /> 4. On the one hand, the basic effect is definitely &quot;bound or forced into dormancy&quot; and there's an inbuilt end condition. On the other hand, using its powers is almost definitely commanding it. I'd say they're immune for the same reason that &quot;bind an idigam to be unable to use its Numina&quot; is an example of a spell that would require a Quintessence from Imperial Mysteries and there's no way in Werewolf or Mage to use a published spell to create a fetish that contains a spirits and doesn't have any supernatural abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:32:07-07:00","id":1541474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541469#post1541469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. There is no such thing as a Rank 2 idigam; the weakest ones are Rank 3 Formless, and Coalescing grants an idigam an additional Rank.<br /> 2. Immune to all three.<br /> 3. They can explicitly be bound. Image and Materialize might be on shakier ground, but using Fetter or Possess to keep it stuck in a rock is within spec.<br /> 4. On the one hand, the basic effect is definitely &quot;bound or forced into dormancy&quot; and there's an inbuilt end condition. On the other hand, using its powers is almost definitely commanding it. I'd say they're immune for the same reason that &quot;bind an idigam to be unable to use its Numina&quot; is an example of a spell that would require a Quintessence from Imperial Mysteries and there's no way in Werewolf or Mage to use a published spell to create a fetish that contains a spirits and doesn't have any supernatural abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the replies, for the question number one please note that assuming that one exists, would it be a valid target? I am aware that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laws of the Lawless p. 216 Werewolf Forsaken Core 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weakest idigam encountered have been Formless, usu-<br /> ally freshly descended onto the world from their lunar prison.<br /> Such idigam are merely as powerful as an Ensih (Rank 3).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That does not mean a Rank 1 Formless doesnt exist somewhere. In the hypothetical scenario one exists... Would it be a valid target for the Familiar spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T13:18:30-07:00","id":1541480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541474#post1541474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not mean a Rank 1 Formless doesnt exist somewhere. In the hypothetical scenario one exists... Would it be a valid target for the Familiar spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to homebrew a thing that isn't mechanically supported by the text, you are free to make whatever call you like about how that thing interacts with powers that would not normally apply to it. Given that Formless change their Ban and Bane every scene and Rank 1 Bans and Banes are common substances and you cannot use magic to alter its traits or compel it to Coalesce, the Familiar bond would likely be exceedingly fragile at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T13:30:27-07:00","id":1541481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541480#post1541480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If you want to homebrew a thing that isn't mechanically supported by the text, you are free to make whatever call you like about how that thing interacts with powers that would not normally apply to it.</b> Given that Formless change their Ban and Bane every scene and Rank 1 Bans and Banes are common substances and you cannot use magic to alter its traits or compel it to Coalesce, the Familiar bond would likely be exceedingly fragile at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel you sound hostile for no reason.<br /> <br /> <i>The weakest idigam <b>encountered </b>have been Formless... </i>bolded for your convenience<i>, </i>English is not my forte, but ENCOUNTERED means that the ones that have been found have been at that that level, not that there are not weaker examples. Why it is not possible some at lower level? The same way that Rank 6, what is not to say there are not higher Rank Idigams?<br /> <br /> So, I posited a hypothetical scenario (perfectly feasible due to the rulings and text), why do you say it is non-supported?<br /> <br /> It is different for Pangaeans, where the minimum is clearly stated in the ruleset:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras p.58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pangaeans are always at least Rank 3</b>, and usually Rank<br /> 5 or more.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-03-2024, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T17:44:05-07:00","id":1541496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541415#post1541415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, what about Shape Spirit? Can it break / suspend the bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Familiar bond allows either side to terminate it at any time, if the spirit was displeased with the effect or had a change of mind, they could end it. However, the mage can also overwrite their Ban, so they could work a condition into that to prevent them from doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T20:06:35-07:00","id":1541502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541481#post1541481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel you sound hostile for no reason.<br /> <br /> <i>The weakest idigam <b>encountered </b>have been Formless... </i>bolded for your convenience<i>, </i>English is not my forte, but ENCOUNTERED means that the ones that have been found have been at that that level, not that there are not weaker examples. Why it is not possible some at lower level? The same way that Rank 6, what is not to say there are not higher Rank Idigams?<br /> <br /> So, I posited a hypothetical scenario (perfectly feasible due to the rulings and text), why do you say it is non-supported?\\</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread is for simple questions.<br /> <br /> You're asking whether a version of a thing designed as an out-of-context problem in its own gameline that is weaker than any that the book bothers to talk about can be taken as a familiar using a spell that explicitly doesn't work on spirits of the same Rank as the weakest specimens of that thing ever encountered.<br /> <br /> Insofar as a literalistic reading of the text is concerned, that nobody has encountered an idigam lower than Rank 3 despite there having been idigam on Earth before the return of the Moon-Banished most practically suggests that either they don't exist, they can't survive long enough on Earth to become relevant, they stay out of the way enough that their being a protean blob of Essence doesn't draw attention, or they can't get off the moon at that level of power.<br /> <br /> Rank 3 is broadly marked as the point in a normal spirit's evolution where it's surpassed the conceptual bounds of being the spirit of a singular instance of the thing it represents; a dog spirit strong enough to join a descant is no longer the spirit of a specific dog, but a spirit of Dogs. Below that level, spiritual society broadly regards Gafflings as children and animals. Idigam aren't naturally the spirits of anything and develop proper consistent spiritual qualities in a process that also increases their Rank and gives them massively disruptive outward control over Essence.<br /> <br /> Much like how Geist's mechanics for ghosts becoming geists does not strictly forbid a Rank 1 ghost from drinking from the Rivers and somehow surviving to become a Rank 2 geist despite most geists being Rank 3 or higher, the books do not provide anything to support a Rank 2 idigam beyond a lack of explicit forbiddance and so any interaction you come up with for such an edge case is firmly up to you to figure out the broader implications of.<br /> <br /> You're likewise free to imagine what Rank 7+ idigam can get up to, because an Earthbound or Moon-Banished as strong as a tribal totem is running on plot-device levels of power approximately systematized in Imperial Mysteries, but that has more textual support than a shapeshifting blob of spiritual ephemera with no Influences, no natural capacity to manifest, and the ability to constantly alter its traits being viable as a familiar in a way predictable enough to have answers that aren't tailored to the story this situation was contrived for.<br /> <br /> Pangaeans in the context they're introduced in are beings you can go out and encounter and are loosely incentivized to seek out. The idigam are a broad category of shapeshifting weirdoes who may most reliably be encountered on the Moon, where most Chronicles of Darkness games are not set. They had their first rules published in a Night Horrors book. They're sufficiently on the edge of consistent mechanics that asking about a never-before-seen subset of them is not going to get much more than speculation for the same reason you're not going to get hard answers on what you can find in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> If I sound hostile it's because you sound insistent for answers that aren't established. I have provided my take on how one might answer the question. That is all you are going to get for something this far into hypotheticals about an outside-context problem from another gameline. Further answers will need to be come up with in a different thread than the one for asking simple questions about the setting and mechanics, because this is not the Brainstorm About Primordial Ooze-Spirits thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T21:34:08-07:00","id":1541505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541481#post1541481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Satchel you sound hostile for no reason.<br /> <br /> <i>The weakest idigam <b>encountered </b>have been Formless... </i>bolded for your convenience<i>, </i>English is not my forte, but ENCOUNTERED means that the ones that have been found have been at that that level, not that there are not weaker examples. Why it is not possible some at lower level? The same way that Rank 6, what is not to say there are not higher Rank Idigams?<br /> <br /> So, I posited a hypothetical scenario (perfectly feasible due to the rulings and text), why do you say it is non-supported?<br /> <br /> It is different for Pangaeans, where the minimum is clearly stated in the ruleset:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ib, you're the one who asked a question only to rail against the reasonable response given. Not only is that arguably more hostile, it's threadcrapping, because it implies you weren't really here to ask a question in the ask a simple question thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio