eonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T06:30:55-07:00","id":1541573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541570#post1541570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if the onmy\u014dji are referenced in any books ?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Fallen Blossoms </i>Dark Era has some discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T06:43:16-07:00","id":1541574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541570#post1541570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if the onmy\u014dji are referenced in any books ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fallen Blossoms section of Dark Eras makes a couple of mentions of them in contexts suggesting at least some of them are Awakened mages, but as a Hunter-based Era there's not much else. Onmy\u014dd\u014d is a real-world thing, so research should be straightforward enough to do to find material to build stuff on, but published Chronicles-specific stuff is pretty thin on the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T07:08:31-07:00","id":1541578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541574#post1541574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fallen Blossoms section of Dark Eras makes a couple of mentions of them in contexts suggesting at least some of them are Awakened mages, but as a Hunter-based Era there's not much else. Onmy\u014dd\u014d is a real-world thing, so research should be straightforward enough to do to find material to build stuff on, but published Chronicles-specific stuff is pretty thin on the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, thank you, I just started taking a look at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541574#post1541574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fallen Blossoms section of Dark Eras makes a couple of mentions of them in contexts suggesting at least some of them are Awakened mages, but as a Hunter-based Era there's not much else. Onmy\u014dd\u014d is a real-world thing, so research should be straightforward enough to do to find material to build stuff on, but published Chronicles-specific stuff is pretty thin on the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I am currently looking into the real world information for them as well. I wanted to check if there was something published I could build upon or avoid contradicting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T19:30:57-07:00","id":1541625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clash of Wills p.118 Core 2ed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages may spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll,<br /> and are always aware when their spells are clashing. Spells with<br /> Advanced Durations and Potency are more enduring in a Clash.<br /> Day-long spells add +1 die to the Clash roll, weeklong spells add<br /> +2, month-long +3, and year-long and indefinite effects add +4.<br /> Advanced Potency adds +1 die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Legacy attainments using Advanced Duration benefit of from the +X die for Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T20:19:04-07:00","id":1541629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541625#post1541625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Legacy attainments using Advanced Duration benefit of from the +X die for Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're treated the same as natural phenomena (the specific example being described as as easy to negate as a similar ordinary instance of the same phenomenon) and can be used as frequently as their casting time allows (metered further to &quot;as many times as you have points of Mana&quot; for the ones that have a Mana cost).<br /> <br /> They're narratively and mechanically things you can Just Do, and their reliability comes at the cost of the flexibility and scope available to a spell cast using the same principles; Mage Armor and Greater Utility Attainments fill the role that made it prudent in First Edition to have a Legacy's First Attainment be based on the spells for Mage Armor and Mage Sight, so much of the &quot;defensive&quot; applications of a Clash are gone for Legacy Attainments, particularly when you also retain the ability to replicate the effect as a spell if you need a stronger version.<br /> <br /> Given all of that, in the unlikely event a Legacy Attainment with Advanced Duration conflicts with a supernatural power in a way that isn't bypassed by the Attainment not being a supernatural effect (e.g. attempting to compel a character with Unbound Fate whose Withstand is less than the Potency the Attainment can muster with the non-Duration factors, whether because it's Potency-primary or the target's Withstand is very low), yes, the Duration adds dice as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T04:19:59-07:00","id":1541641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541625#post1541625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Legacy attainments using Advanced Duration benefit of from the +X die for Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says they don't, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T13:53:11-07:00","id":1541661,"title":"","content":"When using a <i>Goetic Summons</i> with the Reach to target a subject's Oneiros, does the goetia vanish once the duration ends or does it have to find its way back ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-06T17:57:01-07:00","id":1541666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1541661#post1541661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using a <i>Goetic Summons</i> with the Reach to target a subject's Oneiros, does the goetia vanish once the duration ends or does it have to find its way back ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell calls them out and may create the Conditions to keep them out, but like Ghost Summons and Spirit Summons it doesn't do anything to put them back once it ends. The Goetia will return to where it belongs once it runs out of Essence due to bleed and starts to hibernate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T07:07:52-07:00","id":1541683,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you. This has all sorts of interesting implications for the Clavicularius summoning their vices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:53:01-07:00","id":1542179,"title":"","content":"Are there any conversion guidelines for merits from 1ed? I am thinking mainly of the <i>Grimoire of Grimoire</i> merits. The fluff of the books still works, and it is an amazing book for plot ideas.<br /> <br /> But most of the merits, like the Vird merit (my favourite) and others simply do not survive conversion due to the prerequisites no longer being valid (mage armor is not a spell now, there are not vulgar/covert spells, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T09:30:30-07:00","id":1542185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542179#post1542179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any conversion guidelines for merits from 1ed? I am thinking mainly of the <i>Grimoire of Grimoire</i> merits. The fluff of the books still works, and it is an amazing book for plot ideas.<br /> <br /> But most of the merits, like the Vird merit (my favourite) and others simply do not survive conversion due to the prerequisites no longer being valid (mage armor is not a spell now, there are not vulgar/covert spells, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not any conversion guidelines for 1e Merits, particularly not for unusual ones like those found in Grimoire of Grimoires or the Night Horrors books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T14:35:14-07:00","id":1542200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542185#post1542185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are not any conversion guidelines for 1e Merits, particularly not for unusual ones like those found in Grimoire of Grimoires or the Night Horrors books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T15:56:19-07:00","id":1542204,"title":"","content":"<i>Removed for clarity.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-16-2024, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T16:26:58-07:00","id":1542207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542179#post1542179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But most of the merits, like the Vird merit (my favourite) and others simply do not survive conversion due to the prerequisites no longer being valid (mage armor is not a spell now, there are not vulgar/covert spells, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Vird specifically, I think it should be able to function in 2e fine exactly as written in 1e, except substitute Fleet of Foot for Increased Speed, and I would remove the Striking Looks effects, noting that 2e Striking Looks incorporates unusual and memorable appearances of any kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T01:14:32-07:00","id":1542234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542207#post1542207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...except substitute Fleet of Foot for Increased Speed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Was 'Increased Speed' even a merit in 1e? Like, the merit that increases Speed in 1e was also called Fleet of Foot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T03:31:01-07:00","id":1542240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542234#post1542234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was 'Increased Speed' even a merit in 1e? Like, the merit that increases Speed in 1e was also called Fleet of Foot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grimoire of Grimoires says Vird grants &quot;2 dots of the Increased Speed Merit&quot; which doesn't exist. It's likely referring to Fleet of Foot, which exists in both editions (with very minor changes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T06:13:41-07:00","id":1542243,"title":"","content":"<i>Augment Mind</i> is Potency primary. But <i>Honing the Form</i> and <i>Enhance Skill</i>, that are arguably equivalent are Duration primary.<br /> <br /> Is this an oversight, an error that was errated, or a deliberate decision on this particular spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T08:53:26-07:00","id":1542248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542243#post1542243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Augment Mind</i> is Potency primary. But <i>Honing the Form</i> and <i>Enhance Skill</i>, that are arguably equivalent are Duration primary.<br /> <br /> Is this an oversight, an error that was errated, or a deliberate decision on this particular spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508524#post1508524\">I asked this same question before on this very thread</a>. It seems this is an error and all the Attribute/Skill buff/debuff spells are supposed to be Duration-primary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T13:20:33-07:00","id":1542265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542248#post1542248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1508524#post1508524\">I asked this same question before on this very thread</a>. It seems this is an error and all the Attribute/Skill buff/debuff spells are supposed to be Duration-primary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that was my analysis too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T13:21:22-07:00","id":1542266,"title":"","content":"<b>Serendipity </b>has an option to reach to use other skills, is this reach usage dependant on the spell being active?<br /> <br /> I cast the spell, with the +1 Reach, now I know what I need to do, and I could use the skills of the same group, but the spell expires, do I lose the insight on what and how to use the skills? Do I need to recast the spell with the same reach to be able to use the skills? Or do I need to keep the duration on until I can use the Skills as per the Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T13:50:39-07:00","id":1542268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542266#post1542266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Serendipity </b>has an option to reach to use other skills, is this reach usage dependent on the spell being active?<br /> <br /> I cast the spell, with the +1 Reach, now I know what I need to do, and I could use the skills of the same group, but the spell expires, do I lose the insight on what and how to use the skills? Do I need to recast the spell with the same reach to be able to use the skills? Or do I need to keep the duration on until I can use the Skills as per the Reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since its a Knowing spell, the information just pops into your mind. Once you know what opportunity calls for that skills, you simply know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T12:37:01-07:00","id":1542333,"title":"","content":"While in principle I agree that Knowing spells should provide knowledge that is Lasting, I think there's a degree to which something that is a bit more active and transformative ought to be retained when a spell ends, especially if it's tied to Potency.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what, can you just pile spells one after the other with Durations of only a turn but that yield tens of enhanced dice rolls because oh it's fine, you remember all of the insights provided?<br /> <br /> I think that especially matches up with some of the themes of Fate and Acanthus, the Tarot image of the Fool, where there might be knowledge but it's a bit more of a tacit, intuitive form of knowledge that could plausibly require a spell to hold up, compared to something that is a hard fact.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a person intellectually retaining what it was that made using Streetwise to socially interact with a librarian feel like a good idea, but something is lacking in the moment of it, some sense of proper timing and coordination, in a way that means when you try to pull it off it just feels awkward and gangly. You're like Bill Murray in the later parts of Groundhog Day, where his attempts to recreate something spontaneous and charismatic ends up feeling forced, despite how all the surrounding details should be exactly the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T11:07:52-07:00","id":1542377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542333#post1542333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in principle I agree that Knowing spells should provide knowledge that is Lasting, I think there's a degree to which something that is a bit more active and transformative ought to be retained when a spell ends, especially if it's tied to Potency.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what, can you just pile spells one after the other with Durations of only a turn but that yield tens of enhanced dice rolls because oh it's fine, you remember all of the insights provided?<br /> <br /> I think that especially matches up with some of the themes of Fate and Acanthus, the Tarot image of the Fool, where there might be knowledge but it's a bit more of a tacit, intuitive form of knowledge that could plausibly require a spell to hold up, compared to something that is a hard fact.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a person intellectually retaining what it was that made using Streetwise to socially interact with a librarian feel like a good idea, but something is lacking in the moment of it, some sense of proper timing and coordination, in a way that means when you try to pull it off it just feels awkward and gangly. You're like Bill Murray in the later parts of Groundhog Day, where his attempts to recreate something spontaneous and charismatic ends up feeling forced, despite how all the surrounding details should be exactly the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I jump between both approaches depending on the feel of the spell. In the case of <i>Perfect Recall</i>, for example, I tend to prefer the memory needing a check after the duration expires, as its normally not easy to recall a moment to that exacting level of detail. But in the case of <i>Serendipity</i>, I see it as Fate giving a hint, not terribly difficult to act upon. In cases like the Reach effect of <i>Craftsman's Eye</i>, I prefer saying you retain the benefit, counterbalanced by it only affecting the latest tool you inspected. It all depends on what feels fun for your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:30:31-07:00","id":1542389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1542377#post1542377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the case of <i>Serendipity</i>, I see it as Fate giving a hint, not terribly difficult to act upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is not giving due consideration to the range of potentially applied Skills to situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-19-2024, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T12:18:03-07:00","id":1543275,"title":"","content":"So finally got around to reading the Tome of Pentacles book, and noticed almost all the newly referenced Legacies had some attainment provide a constant effect. Has their ever been any guidance provided in errata or books about how this is balanced within the Legacy Fixed Reach rules, or is it just handwaved within the Strange Attainments sidebar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T04:15:23-07:00","id":1543412,"title":"","content":"How would you describe powers of other supernaturals as seen by mages? Would vampiric Dominate be seen by the mage sight as Mind spell? Or would you describe that differently? Do powers of other supernaturals constitute magical Mysteries, or they are completely unrelated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T05:22:23-07:00","id":1543414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McLugh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1543275#post1543275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So finally got around to reading the Tome of Pentacles book, and noticed almost all the newly referenced Legacies had some attainment provide a constant effect. Has their ever been any guidance provided in errata or books about how this is balanced within the Legacy Fixed Reach rules, or is it just handwaved within the Strange Attainments sidebar?</div> </div> </div> </div>The constant <i>Veil of Moments</i> kind of makes sense for the <i>House of Ariadne</i>, since you would have enough Reach to get indefinite duration by then, although it should probably cost a point of mana, but I think its waived since it can only affect the mage and only works inside cities. No clue on how the <i>Genius Perfected Adepts</i> maintain a constant <i>Web of Life </i>active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T07:23:24-07:00","id":1543423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1543412#post1543412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you describe powers of other supernaturals as seen by mages? Would vampiric Dominate be seen by the mage sight as Mind spell? Or would you describe that differently? Do powers of other supernaturals constitute magical Mysteries, or they are completely unrelated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any other supernaturals could be a whole career's worth of Obsessions, depending on the mage. Where do vampires come from ? Were they made or spawned of an unknown occult law ? How do they transform vitae into so many effects ? What is the Beast ? Why are they weak to fire and sunlight specifically ? What is their connection to the Strix ? If they are empowered by the Lower Depths, would they be able to manipulate Scars ? The only way to know is to study their powers.<br /> <br /> In regards to Dominate, it would ping as a non-Supernal Mind ability and could be examined with Mind Focused Sight, which would probably allow them to see something as the Beast cowing / charming / tricking the target's lizard brain into complying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T07:43:42-07:00","id":1543424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1543412#post1543412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would vampiric Dominate be seen by the mage sight as Mind spell? Or would you describe that differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference between a spell of the Mind Arcanum and another supernatural effect upon a person's mind could be perceived in terms of the former having the appearance of an assembly of symbols that are actually causing the effect and the latter images that merely signify what the state of the target's mind is. A vampire's mind control is something that the Supernal can describe, but is not causing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do powers of other supernaturals constitute magical Mysteries, or they are completely unrelated?</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of all Mysteries are not directly Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T03:19:42-07:00","id":1544192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1543414#post1543414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The constant <i>Veil of Moments</i> kind of makes sense for the <i>House of Ariadne</i>, since you would have enough Reach to get indefinite duration by then, although it should probably cost a point of mana, but I think its waived since it can only affect the mage and only works inside cities. No clue on how the <i>Genius Perfected Adepts</i> maintain a constant <i>Web of Life </i>active.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the low low cost of activating powers, would it not be possible to just assume they auto activate when needed?<br /> <br /> Without needing an indefinite spell, or is an instant action too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:37:33-07:00","id":1544218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1544192#post1544192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the low low cost of activating powers, would it not be possible to just assume they auto activate when needed?<br /> <br /> Without needing an indefinite spell, or is an instant action too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its no issue to use, but it does mean the benefit cannot be extended to someone else who is bleeding out, for example.<br /> <br /> I also find it funny that you need an excuse to leave the city every time you need to spend XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T21:35:57-07:00","id":1544623,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is the right place; I'm finally reading the <i>Mage: the Awakening</i> and, I didn't see the Order of Hermes mentioned; did they leave out their flagship star, order? I remember them from <i>Ars Magica</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T01:05:46-07:00","id":1544631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1544623#post1544623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is the right place; I'm finally reading the <i>Mage: the Awakening</i> and, I didn't see the Order of Hermes mentioned; did they leave out their flagship star, order? I remember them from <i>Ars Magica</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exactly what the thread is for.<br /> <br /> But yeah. There's no Order of Hermes (there <i>are</i> groups that resemble them to varying degrees). Aside from anything else, I'd guess that there are copyright issues.<br /> <br /> I'd bear in mind that the OoH weren't in <i>Ascension</i> as just a reference. They were supposed to be the same group in the modern day. <i>Awakening</i> doesn't have that direct continuity with a previous game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T11:15:25-07:00","id":1544662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1544631#post1544631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd guess that there are copyright issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the beginning at least, wasn't all the copyright owned by the same people? It's not as if Requiem didn't reuse several Clan names.<br /> <br /> I think the main reason not to have an actual Order of Hermes is to create some distinction between games. Nevertheless, the Legacy called the Thrice-Great (which is the literal translation of Hermes' epithet &quot;Trismegistus&quot;) gives a home to many of the same concepts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T20:29:07-07:00","id":1544768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1544631#post1544631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's exactly what the thread is for.<br /> <br /> But yeah. There's no Order of Hermes (there <i>are</i> groups that resemble them to varying degrees). Aside from anything else, I'd guess that there are copyright issues.<br /> <br /> I'd bear in mind that the OoH weren't in <i>Ascension</i> as just a reference. They were supposed to be the same group in the modern day. <i>Awakening</i> doesn't have that direct continuity with a previous game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's understandable; much like Requiem, they did a total re-vamp, (pun intended), of the game-system and removed the Order. <br /> <br /> I often regret no buying The Awakening when I found it at a used book store, for over $30; I didn't buy it because it was too expensive, what I considered, at the time and, I was, and always have been, a fan of Mage: the Ascension. That's probably why I didn't get it back then. And when I played Requiem, I had Second-Sight, which, was enough for mortal NPCs and players that used any sort of magic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T09:43:20-08:00","id":1545645,"title":"","content":"<b>Keen Periphery </b>states<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keen Periphery p.26 Signs of Sorcery</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Your Peripheral Mage Sight is unusually perceptive. When sensing an effect via Peripheral Mage Sight you can also sense the Arcanum under which the effect falls</i></div> </div> </div> </div>If you do not know the Arcana in question, you still know what is the effect purview? Let's say a mental effect happens, the merit pings you it is under the Mind Arcana even when you have no Mind dots and no way to understand the actual scope of said arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T10:00:12-08:00","id":1545648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1545645#post1545645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do not know the Arcana in question, you still know what is the effect purview? Let's say a mental effect happens, the merit pings you it is under the Mind Arcana even when you have no Mind dots and no way to understand the actual scope of said arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It gives you no other information and this is the same book that introduces the ability to determine what Arcana a Mystery falls under with a successful Revelation roll using any Focused Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T10:09:15-08:00","id":1545649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1545645#post1545645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Keen Periphery </b>states<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you do not know the Arcana in question, you still know what is the effect purview? Let's say a mental effect happens, the merit pings you it is under the Mind Arcana even when you have no Mind dots and no way to understand the actual scope of said arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>In page 25 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, it states the Peripheral Sight pings when something supernatural happened or an ability is active. It all you tells you where it came from. But not what it is or the related Arcana.<br /> <br /> If someone used the Telekinesis Numen, you know where the effect targeted and you know the source is from the center of the third cubical on the fourth row. But did it come from a ghost, a goetia, a spirit, something else ? Who knows. If you have the corresponding Attainments, you can at least see it.<br /> <br /> Which means that abilities like Keen Periphery and Piercing Glance are invaluable for mages in high danger situations or those that require rapid response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-28T13:23:19-08:00","id":1547296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><i>The following does not aim to cause controversy nor to make fun/light of mental conditions and illnesses. </i></b></u><br /> <br /> That being said, which known behaviours (positive or negative), characteristics, mental conditions (positive or negative) and/or mental illness could be associated with each Path, if any?<br /> <br /> I was reading the Schizoid personality description and their internal Fantasy world and JUST THAT PART sounded very Acanthus to me. And I remember from first edition how the Mastigos Path was prone to either sociopathy or psychopathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T15:41:27-08:00","id":1547316,"title":"","content":"Well, it will be not a simple questions... I`m trying to build my Time Legacy, so...<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does time under Veil of Moments still counts as <i><b>natural aging</b></i>?</li> <li>Can I do temporal summoning of myself, then send myself (by leaving instructions) with Corridors of Time? And <b><i>will it be cancelled if duration of summoning ends before CoT</i></b>?</li> <li>There is some lack of attainment-making instructions. But from what I understand, they works similar to basic attainments or spell. <i><b>Can someone share example of atypical attainment?</b></i> Or is it something similar to 1st edition attainments with merits?</li> <li>By the way, core book said that each attainment can have optional arcanum. Does that mean one and <u>only one optional arcanum per attainment</u>, or <u>one active</u> (aka we have fire shield and can combine it with either life or death to get something)?</li> <li>From what I know, there are groups of mages who became spirits/goetia/ghosts etc. I dont remember their Legacies in books, but I suspect they just change their nature if they got 5th attainment. I believe same attainment will have slightly different effect, maybe inverted version of similar spell = temporarily transform from spirit to flesh. <i><b>C<b>a</b>n someone explain where is a border or red line of such powers?</b></i> What about Time 5 keeping Acanthus (partially) detached from normal time &amp; causality &amp; ability to shift her age/temporal state by whim? It sounds slightly questionable; at least in comparison with Life 5 and hypothetical biological immortality &amp; perfect health.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T16:21:54-08:00","id":1547319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547316#post1547316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does time under Veil of Moments still counts as <i><b>natural aging</b></i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>While a subject is under Veil of Moments, any effects that get worse over time are suspended, aging being the most consistent example of &quot;the deleterious effects of advancing time&quot; on a subject.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I do temporal summoning of myself, then send myself (by leaving instructions) with Corridors of Time? And <b><i>will it be cancelled if duration of summoning ends before CoT</i></b>? </div> </div> </div>There's no point in using Temporal Summoning on yourself before using Corridors of Time, because Temporal Summoning replaces a subject with an earlier version of itself and Corridors of Time sends a subject back in time to inhabit their past self.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is some lack of attainment-making instructions. But from what I understand, they works similar to basic attainments or spell. <b>Can someone share example of atypical attainment?</b> Or is it something similar to 1st edition attainments with merits? </div> </div> </div>The Attainment-making instructions in the book are that you create an effect like you would create a spell, with limits on Reach and spell factors based on the level of the Attainment and your current rating in the Arcanum used to derive its effect. The example of an atypical Attainment the book provides is that a fire-worshipping Legacy that derives their Attainments from the Forces Arcanum might be limited to developing Attainments to do with heat and fire \u2014 so no Attainments that e.g. replicate Transform Energy to turn sound into electricity for them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, core book said that each attainment can have optional arcanum. Does that mean one and <u>only one optional arcanum per attainment</u>, or <u>one active</u> (aka we have fire shield and can combine it with either life or death to get something)? </div> </div> </div>It's one optional Arcanum per Attainment.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I know, there are groups of mages who became spirits/goetia/ghosts etc. I dont remember their Legacies in books, but I suspect they just change their nature if they got 5th attainment. I believe same attainment will have slightly different effect, maybe inverted version of similar spell = temporarily transform from spirit to flesh. <i><b>C<b>a</b>n someone explain where is a border or red line of such powers?</b></i> What about Time 5 keeping Acanthus (partially) detached from normal time &amp; causality &amp; ability to shift her age/temporal state by whim? It sounds slightly questionable; at least in comparison with Life 5 and hypothetical biological immortality &amp; perfect health. </div> </div> </div>Becoming an ephemeral lich after death may be a side effect of reaching particular Attainments in certain Legacies, but the mechanical effects of a Legacy Attainment are constrained by the mechanics in the book that use spell creation as a baseline. Anything more involved than the reliable tricks provided by Attainments requires the use of actual magic, with the risks that entails.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T05:02:10-08:00","id":1547329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547319#post1547319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no point in using Temporal Summoning</div> </div> </div> </div>It take what exist now and summons / change their state of existence on previous version aka me-month-ago. But it never said anything about real summoning from the past; subject exists and was never teleported into the future and past was never changed. The whole idea is to use that to summon your competent younger version with memories of the past, which you can send back with Sands or Corridors ~ after that they can write some report, and you will just read it, no aging due to Shifting Sands, no strange behaviour in that moment of the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The example of an atypical Attainment </div> </div> </div>I thought it was more about powers beyond normal spellcasting. At least that may explain why it is hard to mimic such powers &amp; requires ST and player to think. Like even Tremeres in nameless have few words about this. And I doubt fire-only attainment can count as atypical. We literally have separate heat/fire spells, but even if we have non -&gt; it is just specific dedication to flame. I looked at 11th question again, they tried to use mage sight in specific form - looks better than just normal spell, but still no information about atypical. Anyway...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Legacy Attainment are constrained by the mechanics in the book that use spell creation as a baseline </div> </div> </div>That answer didn`t answer anything. There are nuances: Basic spellcasting is ok, using of basic attainments as part of Legacy attainment was mentioned; and then you found lich-legacies. Normal spells don`t have side effect like transforming you in the spirit. And second free reach is slightly not in the spellcasting rules. But we know they exist &amp; even more - others can transform into something similar (Tremere) or can do even more without getting any Legacy.<br /> <br /> There is just no explanation: shedding your body to become ghost-lich is ok; but can I do the same to become closer to Beasts instead of goetia or what about my Time 5 example? In both cases its unclear if its ok, or maybe beyond mage power &amp; closer to some mystery, or maybe even archmage deeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T06:55:30-08:00","id":1547330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547329#post1547329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It take what exist now and summons / change their state of existence on previous version aka me-month-ago. But it never said anything about real summoning from the past; subject exists and was never teleported into the future and past was never changed. The whole idea is to use that to summon your competent younger version with memories of the past, which you can send back with Sands or Corridors ~ after that they can write some report, and you will just read it, no aging due to Shifting Sands, no strange behaviour in that moment of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have the competency in Time to functionally erase your memories of the subjective future before traveling to the past, you have the competency to look into the past and/or Shifting Sands yourself past any immediate errors you're worried will make unwanted changes. If you use Temporal Summoning to replace your current self with your past self and then use Corridors of Time to inhabit your past self at that same point in time, once the duration on TS ends you will cease to be your past self inhabiting your past self and instead be your present self inhabiting your past self, a difference that largely will not matter if you traveled back in time to change something while knowing what you want to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought it was more about powers beyond normal spellcasting. At least that may explain why it is hard to mimic such powers &amp; requires ST and player to think. Like even Tremeres in nameless have few words about this. And I doubt fire-only attainment can count as atypical. We literally have separate heat/fire spells, but even if we have non -&gt; it is just specific dedication to flame. I looked at 11th question again, they tried to use mage sight in specific form - looks better than just normal spell, but still no information about atypical. </div> </div> </div>The section on Atypical Attainments <i>specifically</i> says the differences should not make the attainment significantly more or less powerful than an equivalent spell after using the fire-only Legacy as an aexample.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That answer didn`t answer anything. There are nuances: Basic spellcasting is ok, using of basic attainments as part of Legacy attainment was mentioned; and then you found lich-legacies. Normal spells don`t have side effect like transforming you in the spirit. And second free reach is slightly not in the spellcasting rules. But we know they exist &amp; even more - others can transform into something similar (Tremere) or can do even more without getting any Legacy.<br /> <br /> There is just no explanation: shedding your body to become ghost-lich is ok; but can I do the same to become closer to Beasts instead of goetia or what about my Time 5 example? In both cases its unclear if its ok, or maybe beyond mage power &amp; closer to some mystery, or maybe even archmage deeds. </div> </div> </div>Attainments that also cause a mage who develops them to become a lich after death, like the Scions of God becoming spirit-mages in 1e, do so without engaging with the systems for Attainment construction, in part because ephemeral liches are not currently fully supported as player characters and won't be through official supplements until and unless Paradox Interactive reverses their decision as the license-holder to allow new Chronicles of Darkness books to be published, at which point it would presumably be in Fallen Worlds or whatever its equivalent book would end up being. Ephemeral liches are also already mechanically likely to have enough mastery in their respective Arcana to disguise themselves, possess or manifest material bodies, etc, and do not need to worry about Paradox from overReaching.<br /> <br /> The Tremere transform into what they are by changing their entire template in 2e and their base template should not be looked to as an example of what Legacy Attainments can do for you as a whole. Legacies are for providing Mysteries social connections, and Awakened powers that have a greater degree of reliability than spells, not to do the equivalent of replicating the template of a whole other type of monster, which would involve specific Mysteries and/or a similar whole-template remix like the Tremere and the Nasnasi get in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T08:45:30-08:00","id":1547332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547329#post1547329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It take what exist now and summons / change their state of existence on previous version aka me-month-ago. But it never said anything about real summoning from the past; subject exists and was never teleported into the future and past was never changed. The whole idea is to use that to summon your competent younger version with memories of the past, which you can send back with Sands or Corridors ~ after that they can write some report, and you will just read it, no aging due to Shifting Sands, no strange behaviour in that moment of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't use the Time Arcanum at conventional Practices to pull things physically out of &quot;the past&quot; (which is not a place that exists separately, it is part of a subject), you can only transform a subject's nature relative to its timeline.<br /> <br /> The spell is called &quot;summoning&quot; by way of analogy, but it works by transforming a subject into a state at a different point of its own timeline. There's no separately existing version of the subject in a different time dimension that can be pulled up to exist alongside it simultaneously.<br /> <br /> That's why the version of time travel allowed by mastery needs to work on a logic of temporarily removing all of a subject's timeline between the present and the desired moment in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547319#post1547319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Attainment-making instructions in the book are that you create an effect like you would create a spell, with limits on Reach and spell factors based on the level of the Attainment and your current rating in the Arcanum used to derive its effect. The example of an atypical Attainment the book provides is that a fire-worshipping Legacy that derives their Attainments from the Forces Arcanum might be limited to developing Attainments to do with heat and fire \u2014 so no Attainments that e.g. replicate Transform Energy to turn sound into electricity for them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is talking about the sidebar entitled &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; that talks about things like Attainments to provide useful Conditions or unusual powers.<br /> <br /> I think in First Edition, the Attainments of the Free Council Legacy called the Blank Badges worked along lines that differed from replicating spell effects, so it could be stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T09:27:27-08:00","id":1547334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't use the Time Arcanum at conventional Practices to pull things physically out of &quot;the past&quot; </div> </div> </div>I know, the whole idea was in using past version of yourself for Shifting Sands so you will not age, because its &quot;past&quot; you. Or just to send version of you who keep memories.<br /> <br /> By the way... I checked posts and found one post about Perfected Adepts. They have Life 2, Prime 1 (Nameless) &amp; Life 2, optional Force 1 (Pentacle) attainments.<br /> So, is there some limit to numbers of arcana in attainment? There is nothing about limits for a main effect of attainment -&gt; it could be a complex but limited spell. And definitely there is no words that forbids optional arcanum for such attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 12-30-2024, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T10:36:17-08:00","id":1547337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547334#post1547334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, the whole idea was in using past version of yourself for Shifting Sands so you will not age, because its &quot;past&quot; you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sequence of logic between &quot;use a Weaving of Time to transform into a younger version of yourself&quot;, using Shifting Sands to go back in time, and ceasing to age is not clear to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just to send version of you who keep memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Memories of what? And saying &quot;send version of you&quot; still seems to suggest that a person is interacting with a separate instance of themselves. <br /> <br /> If a character has Shifting Sands cast on them, that character is zapped backwards a bit through time. That's the only thing that will happen to them because of that spell; if they've been transformed, by the Time Arcanum or any other, they'll either go back in time transformed (if they're the ones who cast every spell involved), or those other powers will be cancelled.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-30T12:04:32-08:00","id":1547338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547337#post1547337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is not clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just some thoughts. If mage physically goes into the past, that means some could do it quite often. Or maybe its just tired mage who thinks that past-me was more motivated to anything. But it is just a few thoughts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Memories of what? </div> </div> </div>Ok, lets look at 2 potential usage with Shifting Sands &amp; Corridors.<br /> 1) Sands | You summon &quot;yourself&quot; 3 scenes ago, who still remember some information which you didn`t care to remember or it was useless until recent event -&gt; leave instruction to write that information if you need that. Or leave an order to go back in time and change few things, specifically because you know <b>that </b>half-forgotten information is important.<br /> <br /> 1.1) Or maybe mage has low wisdom. And to prevent early death, he decided to make few magical sticks which have triggers. So, he just trigger stick, go back in time and did not waste more sanity and time. I mean, he still age in Sands, or at least I think so. | Well, I made that hypothetical anti-aging exploit after thinking about Sands &amp; that small fact - it send our body back into the past. You know, just thoughts.<br /> <br /> 2) Corridors | I summon past-me 3-6 months ago (or year, or two) and I can do the same: Past-me can share information. Or I can order him to go back, keep the same behaviour etc, but do some important actions. The whole idea is in keeping minimal temporal distortion. Which is good if you go back too far or in some delicate situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And saying &quot;send version of you&quot; still seems to suggest that a person is interacting with a separate instance of themselves. </div> </div> </div>Maybe mage has some emergency-basement, created specifically for such situations. You write few orders before summoning, past-you do magic, victory. Its obviously that mage will be replaced for some time; I even specifically mentioned writing report.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":".  just minor details 12-30-2024, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T19:00:41-08:00","id":1547656,"title":"","content":"What are the &quot;conflict&quot; weakness of Fate and Time magic? By this i mean if a mage has great enmity with a mage who's adept (Disciple if you want to say minimum level) at Fate and Time and DOESNT have any ability in those Arcana themselves, what are they to do? Can they even fight defend against such a foe? Or am I wildly blowing out of proportion the effectiveness of the two arcana? Like is it ultimately up to Fate how it screws the enemy over, so a mage adept in Life could have his car crash into a lake in a hurricane and just grow gills and now ONLY have to deal with the debris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T21:41:03-08:00","id":1547661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547656#post1547656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the &quot;conflict&quot; weakness of Fate and Time magic? By this i mean if a mage has great enmity with a mage who's adept (Disciple if you want to say minimum level) at Fate and Time and DOESNT have any ability in those Arcana themselves, what are they to do? Can they even fight defend against such a foe? Or am I wildly blowing out of proportion the effectiveness of the two arcana? Like is it ultimately up to Fate how it screws the enemy over, so a mage adept in Life could have his car crash into a lake in a hurricane and just grow gills and now ONLY have to deal with the debris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate and Time are notable in rivaling Forces for sheer &quot;if you aren't being subtle this Arcanum goes off the rails fast&quot; potential re: Paradox risk, which means managing more than preparing the stage to cause problems for you is really going to be pushing their luck with a toolset that largely amounts to adding bonuses to mundane actions \u2014 against which &quot;fortune favors the prepared&quot; cuts both ways. Feats of improbability out of legend and Looney Tunes may have good odds of success, but they'd either be stretching the bounds of Reach at higher degrees of mastery or involve a great deal more micromanagement than casting a single spell.<br /> <br /> This is to say nothing of the usual rejoinder about casting spells on people who aren't around, i.e. it's Reach-intensive, possibly requires multiple supporting spells before they can even target you, and increases the likelihood of failure unless they go to extra trouble.<br /> <br /> In bigger-picture terms, there's reasons none of the core Paths have Fate or Time as an Inferior Arcanum, and one of them is so nobody needs special tutelage to reach below the heights of mastery in the most generally-useful Arcana for preparing the way ahead of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T01:01:25-08:00","id":1547676,"title":"","content":"I think it's a decent idea to follow that while high level Fate can make events continue bending disastrously towards you, the mundane nature of the actual avenues of attack can often be effectively softened by Shielding spells.<br /> <br /> As for Time... Time can certainly take you out of commission for a while, but if the enemy can't prevent you from coming back it's more of a delaying tactic. And other options such as predicting the future, altering timelines, or hiding themselves in pockets of stretched time... your best options are to really try and work things to limit the options they can yield out of such.<br /> <br /> In a conversation about a different game related to predicting the future, I once made a point about how the only thing you get out of seeing the train coming while your feet are tied to the tracks is that it won't be a surprise when you're crushed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T02:58:40-08:00","id":1547711,"title":"","content":"Has there ever been an offset/deluxe traditional print edition of Mage: The Awakening 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T19:37:28-08:00","id":1547723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1547711#post1547711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there ever been an offset/deluxe traditional print edition of Mage: The Awakening 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The Kickstarter campaigns with their traditionally printed &quot;prestige editions&quot; didn't start for the 2e corebooks (of preexisting 1e gamelines; Demon did have one) until Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T08:32:32-08:00","id":1548054,"title":"","content":"When casting the Knit spell (Life 3), do I need to cast with the Indefinite duration to make it Lasting, or the Lasting duration is assumed in the basic form of the spell just because it is healing? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T08:42:27-08:00","id":1548055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1548054#post1548054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting the Knit spell (Life 3), do I need to cast with the Indefinite duration to make it Lasting, or the Lasting duration is assumed in the basic form of the spell just because it is healing? Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wounds healed with magic do not reopen when the spell's Duration ends&quot; is one of the two examples provided in the Lasting sidebar on page 113 and Knit is a spell with an immediate effect, meaning extending its Duration would simply cause its effect to recur at the same interval as the caster's ritual casting time.<br /> <br /> (Regenerate works differently because the narrative implications of being dependent upon a spell \u2014 possibly one cast by someone else \u2014 for continued limb or organ function creates interesting narrative complications.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T10:34:56-08:00","id":1548058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1548055#post1548055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Regenerate works differently because the narrative implications of being dependent upon a spell \u2014 possibly one cast by someone else \u2014 for continued limb or organ function creates interesting narrative complications.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's also something to be said for the idea that the spell is creating a form of tissue restoration that is not natural, and hence can only be logically maintained by the spell. Healing spells for wounds might not invoked a premise of accelerating a natural process, but there's at least a point that it's putting back together things that are already there in a manner consistent with that process, in a way that would make sense to not then fall apart.<br /> <br /> (I'm admittedly phrasing it like that to keep it consistent with being able to use Matter to repair broken objects as Lasting... which I assume it ought to be.)<br /> <br /> But yeah, it's otherwise along the same lines as how a spell to wound somebody won't have them heal at the end of a duration.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm thinking about the implications of a mage deliberately crafting a spell intended to cause terrible harm but only until it runs out, but... I think that would make more sense to depict as a kind of painful transformation modelled as a debilitating Condition rather than temporarily wounding their health track.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T19:18:54-08:00","id":1548386,"title":"","content":"Tinkering with some rules--is there any rule against the Guardians of the Veil all using a single Masque? In my DC comics RP, I am considering having the whole GoV caucus use &quot;the Riddler&quot; as their Masque. The Riddler mostly only interacts via email, snail mail, clues, graffiti, dead drops, etc. But the players have already figured out that the Riddler isn't a single person, but an organization. Is there anything wrong with the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T23:00:36-07:00","id":1549895,"title":"","content":"If a mage casts Correspondence over one or more sympathetic links and thus finds another mage with Space arcanum, will the target mage be able to sense the spell, e.g. using his peripheral mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T23:09:59-07:00","id":1549896,"title":"","content":"And here is another one: There is a Death 3 spell Ghost Gate opening a gate to death Twilight. If I want spell leading to Spirit twilight or Mind twilight, should the Spirit and Mind arcana have the similar spell? Or should it be Ghost gate with +2 spirit/+2 mind?<br /> <br /> The same question for the spell Know Spirit. Should Death and Mind have the equivalent spell targeting ghosts and goetia, or should it be cast through Know Spirit with added death or mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T04:06:06-07:00","id":1549904,"title":"","content":"Ghost Gate is a bit specific to ghost-aligned Twilight because it destroys the original objects and guarantees castoffs of those objects in Twilight. That's not possible with the other two (though similar effects could be simulated with Patterning, imo). Basically all other spells should have equivalent spells for all three Arcana, with one exception: Goetia doesn't naturally have Manifestations, which is why Goetic Summons require adding Death or Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T04:24:32-07:00","id":1549907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1549895#post1549895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage casts Correspondence over one or more sympathetic links and thus finds another mage with Space arcanum, will the target mage be able to sense the spell, e.g. using his peripheral mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you cast Correspondence on a subject, and find the link to another mage, that mage won't notice anything because the spell isn't actually targetting them. If, however, you use the Reach option to chain connections and look for a sympathetic connection on that mage, then they'd notice because that mage basically becomes a new subject of the spell (not exactly since the spell isn't cast on them, but effectively the spell takes effect on them).<br /> It's like grabbing the original subject's phone and finding the mage in the contacts list (no direct contact), and calling the mage to check their phone's contacts in turn (direct contact).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T17:40:23-07:00","id":1550180,"title":"","content":"What would be the exact requirements for a mage to cast a turn enemy to stone permament spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T21:11:26-07:00","id":1550186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550180#post1550180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the exact requirements for a mage to cast a turn enemy to stone permament spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming 2e rules: Transubstantiation, p. 158. Matter 4, Life 4. Reach for Advanced Duration. Reach again and spend Mana for Indefinite Duration. This is not a Lasting effect, meaning you need to either maintain this spell in your limited active spells, or reliably relinquish it by spending a dot (not point) of Willpower, to make sure the subject remains stone. Dispellation by another sorcerer can undo the transformation, bringing the enemy back to life. Dying without spending the dot of Willpower to safely relinquish will result in a weak relinquishment that will eventually decay and release the enemy in <i>some</i> form.<br /> <br /> How to do it as a Lasting effect? This is explicitly barred off as not intended game design, as per the &quot;I Turn Him Into a Frog!&quot; sidebar on p. 127.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T08:15:58-07:00","id":1550190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550180#post1550180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the exact requirements for a mage to cast a turn enemy to stone permament spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option is to use the <i>Shaping</i> spell with the solid manipulation Reach to encase a subject in stone, concrete, inside walls, or whatever surface they are on. But then they have no air and nourishment, and could still try to break out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T14:40:35-07:00","id":1550248,"title":"","content":"Whats the difference between doing damage with fraying, waveing and patterning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T17:24:28-07:00","id":1550252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550248#post1550248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the difference between doing damage with fraying, waveing and patterning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaving only changes the properties of the subject, which could create new ways to do damage (like adding bullets to a wristwatch or claws to a mage).<br /> <br /> Fraying can only do bashing damage, as it just degrades a phenomenon under its purview, it can only cause bashing damage. Unraveling severely impairs and damages the subject, causing lethal damage, or aggravated with a Reach. Lastly, Unmaking simply annihilates the phenomenon.<br /> <br /> So lets use the Life Arcanum as an example. A Weaving could give the mage the ability to crush a foe like a constrictor snake. A Fraying can bruise their opponents, which means they can just rest up and be fine. An Unraveling can do damage akin to stab wounds, being shot and bone breaking damage. An Unraveling with a Reach can end up destroying arms and legs, necrotizing an eye, causing permanent damage that requires a long amount of intensive care or powerful spells to heal. An Unmaking is simple, you Withand and live, or fail and die instantly.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I recommend keeping in mind the nuances that exist within each Arcana's damaging spells. Time has a great example. <i>Rend Lifespan</i> is better than <i>Weight of Years</i> for damaging a living target. However, <i>Weight of Years</i> is even better than <i>Decay</i> when you want to destroy structures (such as cover) or equipment (like enhanced gear and spell tools).<br /> <br /> Hope that proves helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-18-2025, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T09:11:20-07:00","id":1550271,"title":"","content":"Could you give the same example for fire based damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T09:58:58-07:00","id":1550272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550271#post1550271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give the same example for fire based damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to manipulate fire, you need Forces. Fire damage is covered on page 224 of the core book. It's greatest advantage is the continuous damage it does, which most attack spells can't replicate.<br /> <br /> So you would need a source to manipulate via <i>Control Fire</i>, or to transform into fire with <i>Transform Energy</i>. You can also produce fire via <i>Create Energy</i> or producing the Inferno environmental tilt via <i>Control Weather</i> and <i>Adverse Weather</i>. The main challenges are that, without additional preparations or spellwork (such as using <i>Environmental Shield</i> on allies or the mage using the <i>Environmental Immunity</i> Attainment on themselves), the fire could spread to unintended targets, or burn the caster and their allies as well.<br /> <br /> So probably the simplest way to harness it (and least Reach intensive) would be for the mage to have a fuel container of gasoline in their car and carry a lighter, then just use <i>Control Fire </i>to do controlled burns. It would require some coordination with the cabal to pull off in combat, but fire damage is powerful, so it would be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T22:53:39-07:00","id":1550312,"title":"","content":"Are there any aquatic themed legacies? I\u2019m a pretty big ocean geek and a Thyrsus themed around the ocean seems pretty cool. I was just wondering if there was a legacy which was also similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T04:37:39-07:00","id":1550317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550312#post1550312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any aquatic themed legacies? I\u2019m a pretty big ocean geek and a Thyrsus themed around the ocean seems pretty cool. I was just wondering if there was a legacy which was also similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489404-homebrew-benthic-walkers-legacy\">Benthic Walkers</a> would be my recommendation, they have a great mix of flavor and utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T04:05:59-07:00","id":1550372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550248#post1550248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the difference between doing damage with fraying, waveing and patterning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, you don't have to use Fraying/Unravelling to do direct damage.<br /> <br /> A perfecting of Death to perfect an injury or perfect the inherent entropy of a subject would be the equivalent of a Fraying of Life to bruise them (dealing Bashing damage).<br /> <br /> Whether the practice should be Fraying or Perfection depends on the thig you are doing.<br /> <br /> Possibly even a Weaving of fate to ensure they take damage (like how Monkey's Paw or Shared Fate example spells use weaving). Weaving Space for example might make more sense than Fraying it to deal direct damage - the author of the space section may have mistakenly put Warp as a Fraying practice. But it doesn't really matter since there is already an example of Fraying for the Space Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T13:13:37-07:00","id":1550384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550372#post1550372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving Space for example might make more sense than Fraying it to deal direct damage - the author of the space section may have mistakenly put Warp as a Fraying practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is the other way around. If you read the entry for 'Fraying' on pg.123:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can also directly attack targets using the energies of the Arcanum: inflicting damage via the chill of the grave (Death), psychic overload (Mind), or a blast of electricity (Forces). </div> </div> </div>To me that seems pretty unambiguous that direct damage spells were all meant to be fraying. So in fact, 'Warp' is written consistently with the Practices but about half the arcana don't follow this rule.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe there's some subtle difference I'm not seeing. And to be fair, it doesn't seem to matter all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-26T05:17:00-07:00","id":1550394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me that seems pretty unambiguous that direct damage spells were all meant to be fraying. So in fact, 'Warp' is written consistently with the Practices but about half the arcana don't follow this rule. </div> </div> </div>Look at spell effects two pages ahead:<br /> &quot;Direct damage spells <b>can use many Practices depending on Arcanum</b>, but always inflict damage equal to Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> While Fraying and Unravelling are the <i>natural</i> fit for many direct-damage spells (as they &quot;degrade&quot; the subject), they were never intended as the <i>only</i> fit. Determining Practice is just a matter of what makes sense flavour-wise when intending to deal damage with a spell. For Life, Fraying makes a ton of sense, but you could reflavour it as Weaving as you maliciously reshape the subject's body in damaging ways. It's technically a different spell from Bruise Flesh, and you might be able to come up with a different bonus Reach effect, but otherwise it's literally no difference.<br /> The only actual rule is that third dot Practices deals Bashing, and fourth dot Practices deals Lethal when used for direct damage spells, (also that they don't have a Withstand rating, even though that's not explicitly spelled out).<br /> <br /> However, indirect damage does not follow any hard rules. If you manage to use Compelling to jumpstart a rockslide, anyone caught in it will still be in a pretty bad place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T01:46:12-07:00","id":1550430,"title":"","content":"There is several ways how to enter Astral Realms. The simplest is that the mage meditates before entering his dreams. The other ones constitute setting Astral Path and meditating at a place of power. What is the difference between the se two approaches? Can mage entering his own dreams continue to Temenos and further, or are the Astral Path and place of power ritual required for that? Is there a fundamental difference between these two approaches? (And if not, why would anyone bother with the places of power?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T03:29:23-07:00","id":1550432,"title":"","content":"It's not two separate approaches; you need to do both: Meditating to enter your dreams is <b>how</b> you use a place of power to reach the Astral Realms proper. Otherwise you only ever end up in your own lucid dreams (which is the first layer of the Astral Realms, before the Oneiros).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-28-2025, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T04:30:14-07:00","id":1550436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550430#post1550430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is several ways how to enter Astral Realms. The simplest is that the mage meditates before entering his dreams. The other ones constitute setting Astral Path and meditating at a place of power. What is the difference between the se two approaches? Can mage entering his own dreams continue to Temenos and further, or are the Astral Path and place of power ritual required for that? Is there a fundamental difference between these two approaches? (And if not, why would anyone bother with the places of power?)</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can enter their own dreams with lucidity by meditating anywhere. In order to enter their Oneiros, they must do so by meditating into a place of power (more details on pages 249 and 243 of the core book), and they must follow the Astral Path from their Oneiros to the Temenos, surmounting any challenges that come with a second meditation roll. Once they pass, they stand at the threshold of the Temenos and may start their journey into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T10:05:25-07:00","id":1550450,"title":"","content":"Thank you to both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T08:30:46-07:00","id":1550663,"title":"","content":"Any advice how to distinct when one sphere ends and another is needed considering the effects? I have a problem with this since im coming from ascension and it seems unintuitive to me when i need other spheres and when i dont (for example here making a golem is just matter when in ascension it would require Spirit and Matter or Matter, Prime and Mind). A few examples how it works would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T11:30:20-07:00","id":1550666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550663#post1550663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice how to distinct when one sphere ends and another is needed considering the effects? I have a problem with this since im coming from ascension and it seems unintuitive to me when i need other spheres and when i dont (for example here making a golem is just matter when in ascension it would require Spirit and Matter or Matter, Prime and Mind). A few examples how it works would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the broad descriptions of the Practices in page 123 of the core book, as well as the general effect in page 125 to be great allies in helping me figure out spells. When in doubt, the section for each Arcana has a purview in the opening section, which helps define what they affect.<br /> <br /> Regarding the example, there are many ways to make an animated statue. A traditional golem can be made with Matter, but it will be a Retainer rather than combatant. It can also be made as an <i>Eidolon</i> with Prime and mana, with a limited amount of uses based on its charges. A spirit, goetia or ghost can be bound to it by using a Pattterning to force the Possession Manifestation using Spirit, Mind and Death respectively. A Making of Forces could be used to create a program and power a properly engineered robot. Many roads to the same path, all with different strengths and weaknesses to their approaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T20:44:27-07:00","id":1550676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1550663#post1550663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice how to distinct when one sphere ends and another is needed considering the effects? I have a problem with this since im coming from ascension and it seems unintuitive to me when i need other spheres and when i dont (for example here making a golem is just matter when in ascension it would require Spirit and Matter or Matter, Prime and Mind). A few examples how it works would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the specific example of golems, it's worth noting that without Mind to create a more sophisticated field of expertise or Spirit/Death to turn it into a body for an invisible entity, the construct is limited in scope to simple fetch-and-carry tasks and has no Defense; Matter alone will suffice to make a dumb lump of material that can lift and push and hit stuff, but if you want it to assemble circuitboards or use Numina with greater than 83% odds of success, you need other Arcana, partially because &quot;make spells intrinsically smart enough to dynamically adjust their effects&quot; is the lowest tier of archmastery.<br /> <br /> As for more generally, the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/361809/player-s-guide-to-the-contagion-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle</a> includes some notes on page 12 that Afini has effectively summarized in the post above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T02:57:28-07:00","id":1551012,"title":"","content":"Mage 1E. The postcognition spell let the user only to &quot;see&quot; the past or also it can use other senses? Like hearing a phone conversation. Also, it's possible to use other spell (like magic sight) through the vision?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11488-pyro165","name":"Pyro165","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T19:35:18-07:00","id":1551091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyro165</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551012#post1551012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 1E. The postcognition spell let the user only to &quot;see&quot; the past or also it can use other senses? Like hearing a phone conversation. Also, it's possible to use other spell (like magic sight) through the vision?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell description mentions that they scene is perceived with perfect clarity, as if a camera was placed in the scene. I believe Unveiling spells and similar would work, allowing the scene to be examined from different angles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T03:02:29-07:00","id":1551182,"title":"","content":"How do healing and damaging effects over time work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T03:24:51-07:00","id":1551183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551182#post1551182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do healing and damaging effects over time work?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is to be found under the Duration rules in the descriptions of spell factors. Namely, if a spell has an immediate effect but Advanced Duration, its effect will recur at intervals equal to the mage's ritual casting time. So a spell to heal or damage a person with a duration of a day cast by a mage with Gnosis 1 will apply its Potency to their health levels every three hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T05:41:18-07:00","id":1551186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551183#post1551183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is to be found under the Duration rules in the descriptions of spell factors. Namely, if a spell has an immediate effect but Advanced Duration, its effect will recur at intervals equal to the mage's ritual casting time. So a spell to heal or damage a person with a duration of a day cast by a mage with Gnosis 1 will apply its Potency to their health levels every three hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have read that but it does not explain what are the intervals when the spell is not a ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T06:03:15-07:00","id":1551187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551186#post1551186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have read that but it does not explain what are the intervals when the spell is not a ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage who cast the spell has a ritual casting interval based on their Gnosis regardless of whether they cast the spell as a ritual. That is what the interval is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-21T06:04:50-07:00","id":1551188,"title":"","content":"It's still the same intervals, according to the Gnosis chart. Spending a Reach on Instant Casting doesn't change the length of the ritual interval, you just ignore it for casting purposes, and still use it for determining when immediate effects reoccur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-24T10:26:43-07:00","id":1551263,"title":"","content":"1. Does the kinetic blow limit extend to weapons (when reach is used to allow those)? For example is the weapon bonus limit 5 or is it 5+ the base weapon in question bonus? Or is there no cap at all in this case?<br /> 2. Does weapon bonus add to your hit chance or just to damage or both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 05-24-2025, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-24T11:14:42-07:00","id":1551264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551263#post1551263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does the kinetic blow limit extend to weapons (when reach is used to allow those)? For example is the weapon bonus limit 5 or is it 5+ the base weapon in question bonus? Or is there no cap at all in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would expect so. +5 is pretty massive damage (like, the only weapon that does that is a big game rifle), and +5 tends to be the standard cut-off for bonuses.<br /> <br /> That said, the game probably won't break if you allow the base weapon damage on top.<br /> <br /> The game might well break if you allow for no cap. Or at least, it could easily go to some odd places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Does weapon bonus add to your hit chance or just to damage or both? </div> </div> </div>Just damage. That was a pretty big change for 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T16:37:37-07:00","id":1551370,"title":"","content":"Any advice how to deal mind control powers? If i read the rules correctly the mage just have to cast a spell with potency higher than the enemies withstand attribute, spend 2 reach and he made the enemy suicide? any extra protection for supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T17:31:22-07:00","id":1551373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551370#post1551370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice how to deal mind control powers? If i read the rules correctly the mage just have to cast a spell with potency higher than the enemies withstand attribute, spend 2 reach and he made the enemy suicide? any extra protection for supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any supernatural ability whose effect would contradict the command, whether a mental shield or a conflicting compulsion, engages in a Clash of Wills against the spell, with the winning power taking effect.<br /> <br /> It's worth pointing out that Psychic Domination's &quot;anything goes&quot; Reach effect is being applied on a spell whose primary factor is Potency (because it needs to overcome Withstand to take effect), meaning that, unless the caster takes penalties or spends Reach to increase the Duration (Duration also affecting which effect is more likely to win the Clash), the subject attempts to kill themselves for one turn and then the spell ends whether they succeeded or not, and in either case casting the spell with that bonus costs a point of Mana each time.<br /> <br /> In addition to the above, casting any spell as an instant action instead of a ritual takes another Reach (when having enough dots in the Arcanum to cast the spell at all gives you a single free Reach), casting the spell without needing to touch the target or hit them with a Gnosis+Athletics/Firearms roll that (barring the Fast Spells Merit) subtracts the target's Defense requires spending another Reach, and spending Willpower to raise Resolve by 2 for a turn only requires the character to be aware a spell is being cast on them.<br /> <br /> Even if you have Psychic Domination as a rote, your free Reach for it tops out at 4, half of which goes to allowing you to make the command for the enemy to kill themselves if you can touch them (or hit them with a magic dodgeball as though you were as Dextrous as you are magically insightful) immediately after a ritual that lasts for several minutes at best; getting rid of both of those drawbacks means either taking penalties or risking Paradox to give them more than three seconds to do it, and if you don't have Mind 4 or higher then chances are you'll still have to take penalties to overcome their Withstand even if they don't know you're casting a spell on them and spend Willpower to at least buy time to deploy countermeasures (even countermeasures as simple as &quot;ensure there are no bullets in your gun and get away from the edge of the rooftop&quot;).<br /> <br /> tl;dr The extra protection for supernaturals is that suicidal commands are difficult/situational enough to deploy effectively that being a monster tips it over the edge mainly by supernatural targets having greater access to defenses against magical compulsion and more openness to the idea that someone could be casting a spell on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T18:44:43-07:00","id":1551374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551370#post1551370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice how to deal mind control powers? If i read the rules correctly the mage just have to cast a spell with potency higher than the enemies withstand attribute, spend 2 reach and he made the enemy suicide? any extra protection for supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the mage in question would have to make an act of hubris role for killing someone, either falling or understanding. And then they'd have to deal with the consequences of killing someone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T21:01:20-07:00","id":1551375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551370#post1551370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any extra protection for supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than potentially having powers to shield them from influence, no.<br /> <br /> Don't pick fights with morally dubious Mind mages where they can see you.<br /> <br /> (Considering that most Mind mages also have Space, also not the best idea where they can not see you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T21:35:59-07:00","id":1551379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551370#post1551370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice how to deal mind control powers? If i read the rules correctly the mage just have to cast a spell with potency higher than the enemies withstand attribute, spend 2 reach and he made the enemy suicide? any extra protection for supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Indomitable merit (<i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, page 45) can be used by everyone, as well as using the Occult skill to make a temporary charm to diminish the mage's casting dice pool (<i>Hurt Locker</i>, page 62). Everyone can add 2 to Withstand by spending a Willpower point (<i>Mage: The Awakening 2ed</i>, page 114), should they know they are being hit by a spell. In the case of mortals, they might be able to detect it if they have the Unseen Sensemerit (<i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, page 60), specialized to mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-01-2025, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T00:32:57-07:00","id":1551383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551379#post1551379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Indomitable merit (<i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, page 45) can be used by everyone</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of useless against Awakened magic though, isn't it, seeing as it is neither contested nor resisted?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T04:39:13-07:00","id":1551385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551383#post1551383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of useless against Awakened magic though, isn't it, seeing as it is neither contested nor resisted?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but it's also reasonable to just consider Withstand traits the same as resistance traits in this case, allowing you to add +2 to your Withstand for such spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T07:14:51-07:00","id":1551387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551385#post1551385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true, but it's also reasonable to just consider Withstand traits the same as resistance traits in this case, allowing you to add +2 to your Withstand for such spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, I think that ends up disproportionately powerful for the Merit conferred to its other advantages and its dot rating. Contested and resisted rolls become a bit up in the air, but increasing Withstand can just hard shut some spells down, and be two points means that a mage is obligated to take a dice penalty of another four to overcome it.<br /> <br /> On the other, I think it isn't compatible with what Withstand represents, both in characterisation and gameplay functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T09:45:27-07:00","id":1551390,"title":"","content":"The joys of the forum software detecting changing one word as spam are evergreen; I made a fairly lengthy post that should be visible <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551373#post1551373\">here</a> once the mods clear it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551375#post1551375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than potentially having powers to shield them from influence, no.<br /> <br /> Don't pick fights with morally dubious Mind mages where they can see you.<br /> <br /> (Considering that most Mind mages also have Space, also not the best idea where they can not see you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the simple fact that, like a lot of instant-kill effects, without a fair amount of setup or risking Paradox, it's only remotely consistently practical against unsuspecting mortals and other people who don't realize you're about to murder them with a handshake, and using the Reach effect on an instant-cast spell with a Duration that gives them more than one turn to do the deed eats up the entirety of conventional free Reach for an Apprentice-level spell cast by a Master (or as a rote); casting at sympathetic range adds to the Withstand you need to overcome on top of relying on Borrow Threads to work if you don't already have an applicable connection.<br /> <br /> As with most other things in the game, a sufficiently dedicated mage can kill just about anyone, and that's a thematic point, but most of the &quot;easy&quot; methods only work on people for which there are methods with less dire risks and consequences involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T19:59:45-07:00","id":1551400,"title":"","content":"The thing is that most supernatural powers to control minds are predicated on the idea that there are degrees to which it's harder to push people, and they can actively struggle against that. For a contested action, that's represented by an actual roll to represent the exertion; a more objectionable thing is something that they will fight harder against. For a resisted action, that will be in a greater penalty against it, which is significant because the extent of powers that are resisted is usually determined by how many successes they roll. These are the context of a Merit like Indomitable.<br /> <br /> But Mage doesn't place the extent of how objectionable the outcome is in the part that represents effort, or even opposition. It's in Reach, a somewhat abstract representation of something like the depth of what the spell can affect. A mage might have to Reach further for an imago that can Rule a mind towards all ends, but once that cost has been paid it's in the same space as any other spell, a binary of &quot;rolls a success and works, or doesn't&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's something in the metaphysics that lets a thinking being spend Willpower to make it require more Potency for a spell to work in this binary, but that's still not really in the space of an active struggle against an objectionable effect, so it's comfort against something like mind control is kind of limited.<br /> <br /> Never mind that spells with exceptional success can choose to just ignore Withstand altogether, so it could conceivably cut through Indomitable even if it was ruled to make for higher Withstand.<br /> <br /> Really, I think often the greatest defence against being mind controlled by a mage, at least over the relatively long term, is being able to erode that spell with Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T01:36:07-07:00","id":1551409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551400#post1551400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something in the metaphysics that lets a thinking being spend Willpower to make it require more Potency for a spell to work in this binary, but that's still not really in the space of an active struggle against an objectionable effect, so it's comfort against something like mind control is kind of limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it reads like an artifact of magic having it's own mechanical structure. Like, the entire design ethos of 2e magic seems to be to narrow it down to a single roll. The need to know that you're being targeted makes me think this is in fact meant to be an active struggle; simply one that doesn't require messing around with additional rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:29:41-07:00","id":1551418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551409#post1551409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me it reads like an artifact of magic having it's own mechanical structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has its own mechanical structure because the idea of contested rolls against it was deemed to be nonsensical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the entire design ethos of 2e magic seems to be to narrow it down to a single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make it consistent with the baseline for how the Second Edition system resolves actions. Other supernatural powers that base degrees of effect on number of successes are the aberration.<br /> <br /> I'd put it in terms of &quot;Mage already had a premise of penalties as a way to determine spell factors, and something resembling Yantras in terms of several unconsolidated mechanics for ritual actions to enhance spells. So it made sense to make it consistent with the core system that determines success or failure with the result of a single die, and turns assets and liabilities into dice bonuses and penalties rather than how many successes you roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the thing is, that system made the only time it matters how many successes you roll into when trying to exert yourself in opposition to somebody else. Magic could have continued to line itself up with that, but the idea of resisted rolls against it was explicitly rejected as not being consistent with the character of how Awakened magic works. I think being able to spend Willpower to increase Withstand needs to consistent with that decision.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I wouldn't put it in terms of struggle given the context of how Withstand works mechanically. You're not shaking off the spell, it's just that the Potency needs to be higher to do anything. It's like, a person of Resolve 4 who had a Potency 3 spell targeted at them wouldn't feel that as a spell trying to grab them and then shaking it off, the spell would just do nothing because it can do nothing.<br /> <br /> So I guess it could be something like a conscious pattern that is actively knowing itself takes on additional complexity that the imago needs to account for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T07:53:42-07:00","id":1551423,"title":"","content":"Actually, in searching for the text of Dave describing the basis of the Withstand mechanic, I found an instance of him outright stating that Indomitable does nothing for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits#post951869\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits#post951869\"> [2E] Withstanding + Merits - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits#post951869\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950999-2e-withstanding-merits#post951869 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Topic for talking about interaction between Withstanding mechanics with particular Merits. On last game session two my players were put under Mind 2 Psychic Domination spell. It says it resisted with Resolve. One PC is very high in Attribute ( it has Resolve 4 ) but also have Indomitable Merit ( CoD rulebook, page 45 ). Merits write up says about dice penalty to it's pool for 'monster' when activating power. What to do if he is casting it on two targets ( two PCs ) and only one of them have Indomitable? How to run Withstanding with that Merit? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T08:33:06-07:00","id":1551425,"title":"","content":"Huh, didn't know that, cool.<br /> <br /> Does <i>Shield of Chronos'</i> protection from temporal senses mask the fact the subject is time traveling or accelerated, or would that require a different spell ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T10:41:57-07:00","id":1551428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551425#post1551425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does <i>Shield of Chronos'</i> protection from temporal senses mask the fact the subject is time traveling or accelerated, or would that require a different spell ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanna say that's veiling a different phenomenon, yeah (although I'm not sure what you mean by accelerated).<br /> <br /> I feel as though such a spell might also be applied towards masking the fact that a subject is in the process of having its past changed, and that one or the other should be something to Reach for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T00:46:00-07:00","id":1551436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has its own mechanical structure because the idea of contested rolls against it was deemed to be nonsensical. </div> </div> </div>Well yes, that was what I was getting at. These are mechanical compromises in the system to allow it to function better. <br /> <br /> My point is that you're drawing an inference about the setting from a mechanic that is (I think) there for ease-of-use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T11:29:37-07:00","id":1551444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551436#post1551436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes, that was what I was getting at. These are mechanical compromises in the system to allow it to function better.<br /> <br /> My point is that you're drawing an inference about the setting from a mechanic that is (I think) there for ease-of-use.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is this easier to use than the mechanics that the rest of the system use?<br /> <br /> Between the fact that it was changed at all, some things that Dave has said, and just general observations of the process by which Awakened magic works, I see no reason to have changed the mechanics <i>but</i> to better represent the setting.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, the fact that Dave said Indomitable wouldn't do anything against Awakened mind control seems like enough by itself to say that simply struggling against it is not enough to provide extra defence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T15:39:45-07:00","id":1551449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551444#post1551444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, the fact that Dave said Indomitable wouldn't do anything against Awakened mind control seems like enough by itself to say that simply struggling against it is not enough to provide extra defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what spending Willpower to increase your Withstand rating does.<br /> Anyway, I think Dave spoke from an official position, where the rules clearly state that Indomitable doesn't do anything against Awakened magic because it simply doesn't interact with it (due to it predating the entire Withstand system). It wouldn't be the first time Dave said &quot;this is how it is&quot; while actually thinking it should be different, but to be fair that's purely speculation on my part.<br /> Either way, Dave's rules clarification doesn't mean it's not reasonable to houserule how Indomitable works when running the game for your own group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T01:17:29-07:00","id":1551454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551444#post1551444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this easier to use than the mechanics that the rest of the system use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the magic system doesn't use the standard mechanics. Like, the stacking of yantra and then trading those for modifiers - it's not totally alien to the core system of equipment and penalties, but I think it's different enough that it makes sense to do resistance via Withstand rather than through an opposed roll like how Vampire (for example) work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If nothing else, the fact that Dave said Indomitable wouldn't do anything against Awakened mind control seems like enough by itself to say that simply struggling against it is not enough to provide extra defence. </div> </div> </div>Aside from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> 's point, you're arguing that the opinion of a writer/developer takes precedence over the words in the actual book. Like, if spending willpower to increase your Withstand was intended to be different to spending willpower normally, that probably should have been made explicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T02:44:27-07:00","id":1551455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551454#post1551454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not totally alien to the core system of equipment and penalties</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unconvinced by the idea that it is not basically identical to it.<br /> <br /> At least one reason why spending Willpower doesn't constitute struggling is because a mage will generally have to do it while having no idea what a spell is even going to do. Without even knowing if the spell is targeted at them. They see a nimbus forming and have to brace themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-04-2025, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T11:07:28-07:00","id":1551461,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I feel we've wandered off the point a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character possesses an iron will. The powers of the supernatural have little bearing on her behavior. She can stand up to a vampire\u2019s mind control, a witch\u2019s charms, or a ghost\u2019s gifts of fright. </div> </div> </div>Even if we accept your version of what Withstand is, I don't see how that's incompatible with this. (Accepting that we are changing the merit's mechanical effect.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T01:49:48-07:00","id":1551472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551461#post1551461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we accept your version of what Withstand is, I don't see how that's incompatible with this. (Accepting that we are changing the merit's mechanical effect.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would observe that the first thing I said for the subject is that any effect on Withstand should not constitute a higher imposition than the other effects of the Merit.<br /> <br /> Like, at best it should only increase by one, to constitute a different route to imposing a -2 penalty on the caster.<br /> <br /> Still, as far as compatibility goes, it's in the idea that with the way Awakened magic works, an iron will is quite irrelevant to it. All that matters is whether the imago accounts for all the details.<br /> <br /> You can have an iron constitution, and all that means is that the appropriately potent Unmaking spell will leave behind something that might be cast into gates.<br /> <br /> (Besides, there are plenty of things you could call witches that aren't the Awakened for mortals to play around with)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T03:41:18-07:00","id":1551473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551472#post1551472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, as far as compatibility goes, it's in the idea that with the way Awakened magic works, an iron will is quite irrelevant to it. All that matters is whether the imago accounts for all the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Withstand trait for mind control spells is <i>Resolve</i>. That's half of the traits making up your Willpower. Your resistance to Awakened magic literally scales with your iron will!<br /> Additionally, you can also spend Willpower points to increase your Withstand rating. <i>Any</i> Withstand rating (based on your Resistance Attributes), I might add, including Stamina. <i>You can literally exert your will to overcome Awakened magic!</i><br /> <br /> And how does a mage adapt their imago to account for these details? <i>By increasing Potency to overcome Withstand.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As a fun aside, there's a Sleepwalker Merit named Deadpan that makes the character immune to supernaturally imposed fear. The way it works against spells is that it automatically Withstands them. Still, you could argue that it's a Supernatural Merit since it's Sleepwalker-only and actual immunity goes way harder than anything mundane, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T11:22:35-07:00","id":1551482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551425#post1551425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, didn't know that, cool.<br /> <br /> Does <i>Shield of Chronos'</i> protection from temporal senses mask the fact the subject is time traveling or accelerated, or would that require a different spell ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting.<br /> <br /> I think Shield of Chronis explicitly stops you from being seen in prophecy or postcognitions spells, right? So someone predicting the future but failing to (is it win a clash of will? That seems unusual, since they're clashig with something which hasn't happened yet?) or postcognition looking back provoke a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> If you want to veil your time travelling or other time effect (not sure how Veiling acceleration would work) then you would cast a different veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T15:16:59-07:00","id":1551483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551473#post1551473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your resistance to Awakened magic literally scales with your iron will!</div> </div> </div> </div>And then rendered completely irrelevant once Potency is higher than it.<br /> <br /> I don't view it as a resistance because it is so binary. When a spell has high Potency (or an exceptional success, some of the time), you submit completely, regardless of what told to do. If the spell has low Potency, it simply fails to work, without you having had to do anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, you can also spend Willpower points to increase your Withstand rating. <i>Any</i> Withstand rating (based on your Resistance Attributes), I might add, including Stamina. <i>You can literally exert your will to overcome Awakened magic!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back, this appears to be just a function of how spending Willpower technically increases a Resistance trait temporarily.<br /> <br /> Still, given the parameters of how spell factors work, I would find that not so much a matter of &quot;a spell tried to take hold of my, but I shook it off&quot; as &quot;a spell wasn't calibrated properly to make me a valid subject of it&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's like casting a spell on somebody who you can't tell is Size 6 because they're sitting down. They didn't shake the spell off by standing up. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T15:30:51-07:00","id":1551484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551482#post1551482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is interesting.<br /> <br /> I think Shield of Chronis explicitly stops you from being seen in prophecy or postcognitions spells, right? So someone predicting the future but failing to (is it win a clash of will? That seems unusual, since they're clashig with something which hasn't happened yet?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two things to consider here. <br /> <br /> One is that Divination is still a spell that requires factors, including the need to include the target. You can only find out the future of a thing by being able to cast the spell at the thing, through whatever range you have Reached for.<br /> <br /> The other is that Divination does not &quot;see&quot; the future, as consistent with the game metaphysics that the future doesn't exist. It's a Knowing spell to provide raw information on possibilities for a subject's future.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell specifies that it protects a subject from having their future read in the present.<br /> <br /> So all of this together means that it doesn't work to retroactively veil from people that cast Divination on you some time in the past. After all, they already got that information when they cast the spell on you.<br /> <br /> Like, think about how that would work. I cast a spell on somebody to know what they'll probably be doing this time next week. I have that information now. A week passes and their plans don't change, but upon arriving they decide &quot;wait, better cast Shield of Chronos&quot;. Am I going to lose information that I already have? Is a spell going to change my pattern without having targeted me?<br /> <br /> Now you might ask &quot;but what if the future contains a very strong probability, if not absolute certainty, that the person will cast Shield of Chronos at that time&quot;? To which I say... I suppose Divination would then predict a future in which the person goes about their plans, and includes the detail of them casting a spell to Veil from time. The Veil can't do anything to affect the Divination because it doesn't exist yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T15:40:07-07:00","id":1551506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551484#post1551484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are two things to consider here.<br /> <br /> One is that Divination is still a spell that requires factors, including the need to include the target. You can only find out the future of a thing by being able to cast the spell at the thing, through whatever range you have Reached for.<br /> <br /> The other is that Divination does not &quot;see&quot; the future, as consistent with the game metaphysics that the future doesn't exist. It's a Knowing spell to provide raw information on possibilities for a subject's future.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell specifies that it protects a subject from having their future read in the present.<br /> <br /> So all of this together means that it doesn't work to retroactively veil from people that cast Divination on you some time in the past. After all, they already got that information when they cast the spell on you.<br /> <br /> Like, think about how that would work. I cast a spell on somebody to know what they'll probably be doing this time next week. I have that information now. A week passes and their plans don't change, but upon arriving they decide &quot;wait, better cast Shield of Chronos&quot;. Am I going to lose information that I already have? Is a spell going to change my pattern without having targeted me?<br /> <br /> Now you might ask &quot;but what if the future contains a very strong probability, if not absolute certainty, that the person will cast Shield of Chronos at that time&quot;? To which I say... I suppose Divination would then predict a future in which the person goes about their plans, and includes the detail of them casting a spell to Veil from time. The Veil can't do anything to affect the Divination because it doesn't exist yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds coherent with how games play, I think I would allow that a very likely future in which you are veiled from temporal scrying would result in a clash of wills. Like if you do a divination asking &quot;will party A cast Shield of Chronos, the answer should either the &quot;No, of course now&quot; or (winning a clash of wills) &quot;yes, but you did just win a clash of wills...&quot;<br /> <br /> It is a bit messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-07T06:05:36-07:00","id":1551513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551506#post1551506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that sounds coherent with how games play, I think I would allow that a very likely future in which you are veiled from temporal scrying would result in a clash of wills. Like if you do a divination asking &quot;will party A cast Shield of Chronos, the answer should either the &quot;No, of course now&quot; or (winning a clash of wills) &quot;yes, but you did just win a clash of wills...&quot;<br /> <br /> It is a bit messy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then what if you use your foreknowledge that they're going to cast Shield of Chronos to intercept them and counter or dispel it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-07T17:45:37-07:00","id":1551518,"title":"","content":"I ve probably asked this before but can t find it.<br /> Sign of sorcery at page 67 states that Persistent imbued item spells have a duration.<br /> How it is determined?<br /> Also, i suppose that after it expires you can use the duration of the Word of command spell used to re-activate it, am i right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-08T02:57:10-07:00","id":1551522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551513#post1551513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then what if you use your foreknowledge that they're going to cast Shield of Chronos to intercept them and counter or dispel it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you change the future in a way which invalidates your spell.<br /> <br /> Isn't that the point of looking at possible futures in general? So you can alter them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 06-16-2025, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-08T08:46:40-07:00","id":1551525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551522#post1551522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you change the future in a way which invalidstes your spell.<br /> <br /> Isn't that the point of looking at possible futures in general? So you can alter them...</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference I see in this is that it's proposing to change the future in a way that directly affects how things played out in the past.<br /> <br /> I think there's also an issue with the idea of using a spell in a way that affects the past but doesn't bring temporal sympathy into play.<br /> <br /> Although mostly, I'd say the problem is that it brings the wrong approach to how predicting the future works in Mage. Like with using the shorthand of scrying; it creates an implication of creating a viewing window through which future events can be seen, which would be how it interacts with something like a veil. I think it's important, for both applicability in gameplay and consistency in the metaphysics, to emphasize it as a Knowing spell; it doesn't perceive a thing, it provides information about a present subject's possible trajectory through time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T19:23:10-07:00","id":1551610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost Gate p. 130 Mage Awakening 2ed Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Items can be carried through the<br /> gate, but doing so destroys their material forms, though they may<br /> be retrieved later with \u201cTouch of the Grave.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Death Touched Item p. 64 Signs of Sorcery</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the item is<br /> brought into Twilight, it does not lose its material form while<br /> under the effects of this spell.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is <b>destroys their material forms</b>?<br /> <br /> Before reading Signs of Sorcery I assumed that if I open a Ghost Gate, the item travels with me, it has transformed into Death attuned Twilight Ephemera. It just moved realms. <br /> <br /> BUT what does it mean that when a Death Touched Item goes into Twilight? You see a floating version in the material world? You leave the object behind and work with a copy in Twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T21:11:02-07:00","id":1551613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551610#post1551610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is <b>destroys their material forms</b>?<br /> <br /> Before reading Signs of Sorcery I assumed that if I open a Ghost Gate, the item travels with me, it has transformed into Death attuned Twilight Ephemera. It just moved realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you carry an item into Deathly Twilight through Ghost Gate, the material object is destroyed and a ghostly version of it remains in Twilight, where it can be accessed with Touch of the Grave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BUT what does it mean that when a Death Touched Item goes into Twilight? You see a floating version in the material world? You leave the object behind and work with a copy in Twilight? </div> </div> </div>You have the actual item, which is not materially destroyed from being converted to Deathly ephemera but instead comes back like your body does once you leave Twilight with it. The object does not universally have Durability 1 like the items you can retrieve with Touch of the Grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T13:03:21-07:00","id":1551630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551613#post1551613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If you carry an item into Deathly Twilight through Ghost Gate, the material object is destroyed and a ghostly version of it remains in Twilight, where it can be accessed with Touch of the Grave. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply, but the ghost gate does not reconstitute the objects as normal when you open it from Twilight to Real World?<br /> <br /> The text on the perfect metals seems to imply that the return makes the item normal, otherwise, passing things back and forth would be impossible:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perfected Metallurgy, Signs of Sorcery p. 61</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>she can repeatedly<br /> convert the base material to ephemera and back again</b>, either<br /> <b>by passing it into and out of Twilight </b>or carrying it into and out<br /> of the Shadow or Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551613#post1551613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have the actual item, which is not materially destroyed from being converted to Deathly ephemera but instead comes back like your body does once you leave Twilight with it. The object does not universally have Durability 1 like the items you can retrieve with Touch of the Grave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as previous question. Could you describe the flow please for using Ghost Gate and Death Touched item?<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I am Moira the Moros.</li> <li>I am dressed with a simple shirt, pants, socks, underwear, and boots.</li> <li>I own a Death Touched Item.</li> <li>I have an iron coin I want to perfect (by passing to and from Twilight a couple of times)</li> <li>I open a Ghost Gate from Material to Twilight and enter Twilight</li> <li>???? What happens to my clothes?</li> <li>???? What happens to my the Death Touched Item?</li> <li>???? What happens to my iron coin?</li> <li>I open a Ghost Gate from Twilight to Material and leave Twilight.</li> <li>???? What happens to my clothes?</li> <li>???? What happens to my the Death Touched Item?</li> <li>???? What happens to my iron coin?</li> </ol><br /> And please clarify if the Reach of Ghost Gate modifies this in any form.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T13:27:34-07:00","id":1551631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551630#post1551630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the reply, but the ghost gate does not reconstitute the objects as normal when you open it from Twilight to Real World?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The text on the perfect metals seems to imply that the return makes the item normal, otherwise, passing things back and forth would be impossible: </div> </div> </div>The base effect of Ghost Gate is not the sole method of converting items to Deathly Twilight; note the conjunctional effect of the Matter 4 spell &quot;Ghostwall,&quot; as well as the fact that the Spirit spell for turning something into spiritual ephemera is a four-dot spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I open a Ghost Gate from Material to Twilight and enter Twilight<br /> ???? What happens to my clothes?<br /> ???? What happens to my the Death Touched Item?<br /> ???? What happens to my iron coin?<br /> I open a Ghost Gate from Twilight to Material and leave Twilight.<br /> ???? What happens to my clothes?<br /> ???? What happens to my the Death Touched Item?<br /> ???? What happens to my iron coin? </div> </div> </div>Going through the Ghost Gate into Twilight destroys your clothes and the coin and replaces them with ghostly duplicates; the Death Touched item is turned into a ghostly version of itself, but will come back with you when you return to the material phase of existence.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect of Ghost Gate changes the spell's function from &quot;make an Iris into Death-aspected Twilight, which permanently converts items into less Durable ephemeral versions of themselves by destroying them&quot; to &quot;convert a target into Deathly ephemera.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as spirits crossing the Gauntlet into the Flesh don't become automatically material because they were naturally ephemeral, baseline Ghost Gate shortcuts the transition to Twilight for anything that wouldn't produce a ghost in isolation by destroying it, whereas the Reach effect approaches an effect similar to Patterning by directly converting the matter into ephemera in a way that's tied to the Duration of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T14:18:16-07:00","id":1551632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551631#post1551631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not.<br /> <br /> The base effect of Ghost Gate is not the sole method of converting items to Deathly Twilight; note the conjunctional effect of the Matter 4 spell &quot;Ghostwall,&quot; as well as the fact that the Spirit spell for turning something into spiritual ephemera is a four-dot spell.<br /> <br /> Going through the Ghost Gate into Twilight destroys your clothes and the coin and replaces them with ghostly duplicates; the Death Touched item is turned into a ghostly version of itself, but will come back with you when you return to the material phase of existence.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect of Ghost Gate changes the spell's function from &quot;make an Iris into Death-aspected Twilight, which permanently converts items into less Durable ephemeral versions of themselves by destroying them&quot; to &quot;convert a target into Deathly ephemera.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as spirits crossing the Gauntlet into the Flesh don't become automatically material because they were naturally ephemeral, baseline Ghost Gate shortcuts the transition to Twilight for anything that wouldn't produce a ghost in isolation by destroying it, whereas the Reach effect approaches an effect similar to Patterning by directly converting the matter into ephemera in a way that's tied to the Duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Got it, so what happens to those 3 category of items when I open the gate from Twilight to Material?<br /> <br /> And thanks again for all the explanations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T14:24:28-07:00","id":1551633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551632#post1551632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it, so what happens to those 3 category of items when I open the gate from Twilight to Material?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the spell as written? Nothing. It's a plane that converts material entities into a Twilight state, which presumably lasts until the Duration of the spell elapses for anything that it doesn't destroy; calling it an Iris was a mistake on my part. Retrieving items from Twilight is managed through Touch of the Grave, as described in the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T15:12:44-07:00","id":1551635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551633#post1551633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the spell as written? Nothing. It's a plane that converts material entities into a Twilight state, which presumably lasts until the Duration of the spell elapses for anything that it doesn't destroy; calling it an Iris was a mistake on my part. Retrieving items from Twilight is managed through Touch of the Grave, as described in the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Moira enters dressed and emerges naked?<br /> <br /> Open to Twiligth, spend 10 seconds, open to Material (or reuse the one that was already opened), and then she only keeps the Death Touched Item?<br /> <br /> That is why I did the question with the whole flow, because it is not clear to me, and I wanted to avoid piecemeal questions.<br /> <br /> What happens in steps 9 and onwards of my question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T15:33:30-07:00","id":1551636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551635#post1551635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Moira enters dressed and emerges naked?<br /> <br /> Open to Twiligth, spend 10 seconds, open to Material (or reuse the one that was already opened), and then she only keeps the Death Touched Item?<br /> <br /> That is why I did the question with the whole flow, because it is not clear to me, and I wanted to avoid piecemeal questions.<br /> <br /> What happens in steps 9 and onwards of my question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Moira leaves naked.<br /> <br /> The clothes and the coin are destroyed by the first Gate, so only their &quot;ghost&quot; exist in Twilight.<br /> <br /> When Moira crosses back to the Material world/phase, the ephemeral items remain in Twilight, because converting ephemera into matter isn't something <i><b>this spell</b></i> does.<br /> <br /> Reach or other spells can be used to circumvent this problem. But if baseline Ghost Gate is the only spell used, then everything but the Death Touched item will be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Ghostly copies of those items will remain in Twilight, for whatever that's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T22:00:08-07:00","id":1551646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551635#post1551635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Moira enters dressed and emerges naked?<br /> <br /> Open to Twiligth, spend 10 seconds, open to Material (or reuse the one that was already opened), and then she only keeps the Death Touched Item?<br /> <br /> That is why I did the question with the whole flow, because it is not clear to me, and I wanted to avoid piecemeal questions.<br /> <br /> What happens in steps 9 and onwards of my question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note also that Moira could bypass all this problem by opening an Avernian Gateway and going back and forth from it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-14T07:19:03-07:00","id":1551675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551636#post1551636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Moira leaves naked.<br /> <br /> The clothes and the coin are destroyed by the first Gate, so only their &quot;ghost&quot; exist in Twilight.<br /> <br /> When Moira crosses back to the Material world/phase, the ephemeral items remain in Twilight, because converting ephemera into matter isn't something <i><b>this spell</b></i> does.<br /> <br /> Reach or other spells can be used to circumvent this problem. But if baseline Ghost Gate is the only spell used, then everything but the Death Touched item will be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Ghostly copies of those items will remain in Twilight, for whatever that's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks,<br /> <br /> If Moira only has access to Ghost Gate, then will the reach allow to return to the Material with clothes? Essentially, what would avoid the sartorial issue at the lower possible level of the arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-14T07:57:29-07:00","id":1551676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551675#post1551675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Moira only has access to Ghost Gate, then will the reach allow to return to the Material with clothes? Essentially, what would avoid the sartorial issue at the lower possible level of the arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Reach avoids the problem of the base effect destroying material objects that pass through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T01:46:04-07:00","id":1551709,"title":"","content":"Unrelated question. If you carry something into the Underworld it remains material, if you have a castoff with you it becomes substantial.<br /> <br /> While in the Underworld, is there any obvious way to tell the difference between an items which is merely a castoff (ie most of the items you are likely to find in the Underworld) and a material object (ie most of the objects you are likely to bring with you?).<br /> <br /> Specifically, without using Mage sight or a unveiling spell. Would it be easy to tell, &quot;oh this is a Stygian attuned iron coin, this is a death touched iron coin, and this is a castoff of an iron coin&quot;?<br /> <br /> Or would they all be equivalent to the locals in the Underworld? (Really I'm worried more about the flavour and describing the Underworld than any mechanics, which I think are fairly clear... )<br /> <br /> The only possible mechanical difference, a ghost would be able to eat the castoff to gain essence, but would have to first destroy the other objects to create a castoff, right?<br /> <br /> Edit: if you leave a physical object in the Underworld, or lose it, or it gets washed away into the rivers of the Underworld, is there are reason to assume it will be destroyed by natural processes? (Ie apart from a ghost/Chthonic entity destroying it intentionally, assuming that is possible...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 06-17-2025, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T20:02:41-07:00","id":1551748,"title":"","content":"Additionally , would there be an obvious way to tell the difference between Underworld natives and a Stygian Supernal Being ( the recondite Shades of Stygia, or specters <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;associated with death \u2014 spectral, robed figures, black dogs, crows, maggots, or obviously dead people. Sometimes they take the form of deities of death (Hades, Baron Samedi,<br /> Mrtyu-Mara, etc.). </div> </div> </div>) ??<br /> <br /> So like you meet a random entity, I guess just talking to it should determine pretty well that it isn't a Chthonic being, maybe a Kerberos would be similar enough, given both may be willing to make a deal. But I think a Specter could look very like a Ferryman or guardian, or certain ghosts/Geists/reapers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T21:52:12-07:00","id":1551751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551748#post1551748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally , would there be an obvious way to tell the difference between Underworld natives and a Stygian Supernal Being ( the recondite Shades of Stygia, or specters<br /> ) ??<br /> <br /> So like you meet a random entity, I guess just talking to it should determine pretty well that it isn't a Chthonic being, maybe a Kerberos would be similar enough, given both may be willing to make a deal. But I think a Specter could look very like a Ferryman or guardian, or certain ghosts/Geists/reapers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Underworld natives mostly stay in the underworld, while Stygian shades mostly stays in the Supernal.<br /> Even if you find a Cthtonian elsewhere the trail of plasm leaved by the creature would left no doubt, and if you find a Kerberos in a Dominion it s relatively safe to assume it s not a Supernal shade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T08:42:48-07:00","id":1551754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551751#post1551751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Underworld natives mostly stay in the underworld, while Stygian shades mostly stays in the Supernal.<br /> Even if you find a Cthtonian elsewhere the trail of plasm leaved by the creature would left no doubt, and if you find a Kerberos in a Dominion it s relatively safe to assume it s not a Supernal shade.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of my previous question, I am talking about in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Obviously if you find a Spectre there, it has either been summoned, there is a Verge there and it is merely wandering around, or someone has gone rapt and it is actually a Greater Tulpa hanging around in the wake of their Nimbus... As those are the most common ways of getting a Supernal Being to the Underworld (and in my context, it is likely one of these three methods happening... Depending on when it happens, of if the character in question goes Rapt).<br /> <br /> But in principle, there is nothing preventing a Stygian Verge existing in the Underworld that I am aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T12:34:27-07:00","id":1551756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551754#post1551754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in principle, there is nothing preventing a Stygian Verge existing in the Underworld that I am aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but given that the player characters are mortal mages who live in the material world instead of the much more inherently hostile environment of the Underworld, and given the same rationale Inferno and Intruders use to justify saying that you're less likely to run into Abyssal incursions or Infernal demons in the Great Below, the supernatural nesting-doll situation of a Verge in the Underworld is not the first thing that comes to mind as a concern.<br /> <br /> Now, you're asking if mages can identify at a glance, <i>without</i> using their primary tool for supernatural observation, the difference between an item that is supernatural because it is a ghost and an item that is supernatural because it is enchanted with Death magic, or the difference between a ghost and a humanlike Specter?<br /> <br /> The answer is no, of course not, because without Looking At the thing with supernatural senses you have no way of identifying what kind of magical something is (or, with concealment effects blocking the Periphery, if it <i>is</i> magical) besides an educated guess that something that looks weirder probably comes from farther away from the everyday human experience. Scrutiny and other observational powers are needed to get particulars, which is why the protagonists of Hunter: the Vigil have so many things mixed up from their more mundane perspective \u2014 a mage with the Supernal Taxonomy Merit has a quicker road to identifying phenomena similar to ones they've seen before, but that still requires Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T13:33:18-07:00","id":1551772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551756#post1551756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but given that the player characters are mortal mages who live in the material world instead of the much more inherently hostile environment of the Underworld, and given the same rationale Inferno and Intruders use to justify saying that you're less likely to run into Abyssal incursions or Infernal demons in the Great Below, the supernatural nesting-doll situation of a Verge in the Underworld is not the first thing that comes to mind as a concern.<br /> <br /> Now, you're asking if mages can identify at a glance, <i>without</i> using their primary tool for supernatural observation, the difference between an item that is supernatural because it is a ghost and an item that is supernatural because it is enchanted with Death magic, or the difference between a ghost and a humanlike Specter?<br /> <br /> The answer is no, of course not, because without Looking At the thing with supernatural senses you have no way of identifying what kind of magical something is (or, with concealment effects blocking the Periphery, if it <i>is</i> magical) besides an educated guess that something that looks weirder probably comes from farther away from the everyday human experience. Scrutiny and other observational powers are needed to get particulars, which is why the protagonists of Hunter: the Vigil have so many things mixed up from their more mundane perspective \u2014 a mage with the Supernal Taxonomy Merit has a quicker road to identifying phenomena similar to ones they've seen before, but that still requires Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is really, when describing to my players stuff in the Underworld, what it looks like before they investigate, would there be any obvious differences between a cast-off item vs a physical object or even supernal artifact. <br /> <br /> Like-wise telling a Supernal being which happens to look fairly Death adjacent, from the Underworld Natives (we can assume an NPC Mage has summoned the supernal being in question, for plot reasons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T14:14:08-07:00","id":1551774,"title":"","content":"No, there's no inherent descriptive difference, or even descriptive similarity that let you identify the kind of being just by looking at it.<br /> <br /> IIRC supernal objects and beings tend to look more idealized, and things from the underworld tend to mute colors over time, but neither effect is strong enough to make for a clear distinction. Not to say that an &quot;idealized underworld thing&quot; is probably very similar to an actual underworld thing.<br /> <br /> All in all, description alone shouldn't let players notice the nature of those things, or distinguish them from each other. This kind of information is always meant to come from supernatural senses or investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T03:25:35-07:00","id":1551799,"title":"","content":"Shadows are under Forces or Death Arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T03:36:01-07:00","id":1551800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551799#post1551799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadows are under Forces or Death Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Primarily Death, but Forces has significant overlap when worked as a &quot;negative&quot;. (I.e. Forces can absolutely create/manipulate shadows by blocking/removing/redirecting light.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T03:40:56-07:00","id":1551801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551800#post1551800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primarily Death, but Forces has significant overlap when worked as a &quot;negative&quot;. (I.e. Forces can absolutely create/manipulate shadows by blocking/removing/redirecting light.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces can create light or remove it, but not directly manipulate shadows themselves.<br /> <br /> Like you can create complete darkness with Forces by blocking all the light out, and Inflict a blindness tilt.<br /> <br /> But with Death you can turn shadows into equipment which can be worn.<br /> <br /> You can turn people into animate 2/3d shadows which literally makes then unphysical and intangible... Those are very different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typos 06-22-2025, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T14:16:50-07:00","id":1551885,"title":"","content":"how do exactly spells that contain multiple spells work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T16:22:14-07:00","id":1551886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551885#post1551885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do exactly spells that contain multiple spells work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean combined spells ? You can find them on page 118 of the core book, they share a spell slot and spell factors. Your casting pool is Gnosis + lowest Arcanum of all the ones used. You suffer a -2 penalty on the spellcasting roll for each spell added after the first. The maximum amount of spells you can combine is limited by your Gnosis, starting at 2 spells on Gnosis 3, and 4 at Gnosis 9 (core book page 86).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T03:53:18-07:00","id":1551894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551886#post1551886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you mean combined spells ? You can find them on page 118 of the core book, they share a spell slot and spell factors. Your casting pool is Gnosis + lowest Arcanum of all the ones used. You suffer a -2 penalty on the spellcasting roll for each spell added after the first. The maximum amount of spells you can combine is limited by your Gnosis, starting at 2 spells on Gnosis 3, and 4 at Gnosis 9 (core book page 86).</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules are really unclear.<br /> <br /> They don't specificy whether you can select different subjects. Have different reaches, or the you are required to have the same spell factors.<br /> <br /> Some if the intention is to have two spell which have the same dice pool (due to the same spell factors) and an extra -2 for being combined. This isn't made clear by pg 118.<br /> <br /> If you can split the subjects and potentially have one at touch range while another is at sensory or sympathetic range, that isn't clear either.<br /> <br /> Whether yantras used need to be applicable to both spells is also unclear.<br /> <br /> The only thing seems to be clear is that you share one dice pool between the two spells (with a -2 dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T04:50:57-07:00","id":1551896,"title":"","content":"Combined spells are honestly a pain to deal with, and there are many threads and posts in this thread about how they are unclear (and I have personally never seen anyone bothering using them during play).<br /> Despite that, the rules are <i>mostly</i> comprehensive; it's just difficult to parse exactly what they mean if you're not used to the language. <i>Most</i> of the gaps can be inferred pretty easily once you have a grasp of the core rules of the system (and use the presumption that anything which could be used to boost a spell above a non-combined casting of it is an indication that it's not how it's supposed to work).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551894#post1551894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't specificy whether you can select different subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have different reaches, </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reach to alter spell factors applies to all spells, but additional Reach effects in a spell\u2019s listing must be bought separately.&quot;<br /> <br /> How you calculate the number of Reaches is unfortunately not stated. The simplest, likliest (and least abusable) way is to simply calculate it for both spells and take the lowest (just like the dice pool).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or the you are required to have the same spell factors. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spell modifications such as Yantras and spellfactors affect the entire spellcasting pool and spell effects.&quot;<br /> &amp;<br /> &quot;Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this doesn't tell us how to calculate free steps in the primary factor, but, again, taking the lowest from both spells is a safe bet.<br /> <br /> As for what happens if both spells have different primary factors, that's also unstated. This is not as simple to adjudicate, but if we read the text as a directive, you might have to spend a Reach to change one of the spells' primary factor to make them align.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some if the intention is to have two spell which have the same dice pool (due to the same spell factors) and an extra -2 for being combined. </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you're asking by this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can split the subjects and potentially have one at touch range while another is at sensory or sympathetic range, that isn't clear either. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reach to alter spell factors applies to all spells, but additional Reach effects in a spell\u2019s listing must be bought separately.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether yantras used need to be applicable to both spells is also unclear. </div> </div> </div>It's likely, since it would be abusable to combine your spell with few available Yantras with a spell with more accessible or even better Yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T08:48:45-07:00","id":1551899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551896#post1551896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't specificy whether you can select different subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so reach doesn't answer this.<br /> <br /> I can touch two subjects and apply one spell with my right hand to Tim and the other spell to Bill with my left hand?<br /> <br /> Or spend one reach and cast both spells at advanced scale and affect up to five subjects? (Can these all be five different targets?).<br /> <br /> It just says that if I spend a reach going to advanced scale, it applies to both spells, but also they have to be the same scale unless you spend a reach to seperate the effects.<br /> <br /> Unless your reading is that the &quot;same scale&quot; means the same subjects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551896#post1551896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether yantras used need to be applicable to both spells is also unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's likely, since it would be abusable to combine your spell with few available Yantras with a spell with more accessible or even better Yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems fair. The third way would be to allow alternative yantras to build the same dice pool (extra time taken as a downside) but with the usual number of Yantra slots per spell... This would avoid making it strictly worse or more difficult to get a full Yantra bonus for either spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T09:35:54-07:00","id":1551900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551899#post1551899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so reach doesn't answer this.<br /> <br /> I can touch two subjects and apply one spell with my right hand to Tim and the other spell to Bill with my left hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's two spells affecting two different people. Basic semantics would indicate a combined spell is a spell that applies multiple different effects \u2014 a combined spell is not just &quot;multiple spells activate at the same time and only use one spell control slot.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or spend one reach and cast both spells at advanced scale and affect up to five subjects? (Can these all be five different targets?).<br /> <br /> It just says that if I spend a reach going to advanced scale, it applies to both spells, but also they have to be the same scale unless you spend a reach to seperate the effects. </div> </div> </div>As in &quot;if you use Area Scale for one of the constituent spells, all of them have to use Area unless you spend a Reach to have one or more of the other spells use Targets instead&quot; and/or &quot;if you want a combined spell to have an effect affect less Area or fewer Targets than the other(s), you need to spend a Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about the concept of a combined spell suggests anything about them that diverges from it being a systems object that can be observed in time and space as experienced by the characters. Without archmastery, a spell's factors set the upper limits of what it can do and affect and the ability of the spell itself to work within those boundaries can only go down. If you want to cast a combined spell that affects two people, you cast a spell with factors that allow it to affect at least two people. If you want it to affect two buildings it needs to be able to affect an area that encompasses those two buildings.<br /> <br /> 2e could do with more examples of spellcasting than it had the wordcount for, but &quot;two different effects, neither of which has any overlap in target or area of influence nor any shared symbolic support&quot; does not fit the common sense reading of the term &quot;combined <i>spell</i>&quot; as a singular noun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T16:00:41-07:00","id":1551901,"title":"","content":"To try to put it succinctly: Combined spells are not a mechanic for multicasting spells simultaneously. They're a mechanic for when you want to cast <i>one</i> spell whose effects incorporate multiple individual spells. You could cast a spell that, for example, crafts a shadow into a physical form (Shadow Crafting, Death 3) and crafts that physical form into pure silver (Transubstantiation, Matter 4). It's one spell, one thing you're doing to a shadow, but the one thing you're doing is multiple spell effects. You wouldn't use a single combined spell to craft one shadow into silver and another into gold. That would be two castings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T04:15:45-07:00","id":1551913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551900#post1551900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's two spells affecting two different people. Basic semantics would indicate a combined spell is a spell that applies multiple different effects \u2014 a combined spell is not just &quot;multiple spells activate at the same time and only use one spell control slot.&quot;<br /> <br /> As in &quot;if you use Area Scale for one of the constituent spells, all of them have to use Area unless you spend a Reach to have one or more of the other spells use Targets instead&quot; and/or &quot;if you want a combined spell to have an effect affect less Area or fewer Targets than the other(s), you need to spend a Reach.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about the concept of a combined spell suggests anything about them that diverges from it being a systems object that can be observed in time and space as experienced by the characters. Without archmastery, a spell's factors set the upper limits of what it can do and affect and the ability of the spell itself to work within those boundaries can only go down. If you want to cast a combined spell that affects two people, you cast a spell with factors that allow it to affect at least two people. If you want it to affect two buildings it needs to be able to affect an area that encompasses those two buildings.<br /> <br /> 2e could do with more examples of spellcasting than it had the wordcount for, but &quot;two different effects, neither of which has any overlap in target or area of influence nor any shared symbolic support&quot; does not fit the common sense reading of the term &quot;combined <i>spell</i>&quot; as a singular noun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a whole lot of unwritten assumptions right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T07:34:07-07:00","id":1551917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551913#post1551913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a whole lot of unwritten assumptions right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not going to waste my time trying to rehash in detail the premise that if you come to a thread for simple questions you have about a point of ambiguity in a set of books that does not explicitly resolve that ambiguity you do not get to complain about the lack of explicit textual support for any interpretations used in the answers you get. If you automatically disagree with the answers you get in that circumstance there was little point in asking the question. &quot;Given the general tenor of the rest of the game and the basic definition of what the thing you're asking about is&quot; is the closest to <i>written</i> assumptions we have.<br /> <br /> Spells that use Area Scale to apply non-Lasting effects apply those effects to any valid targets in the area as long as they remain in the area. Spells that use Subjects Scale can have their separate targets move wherever they like from the Range they were cast at and are Withstood by their separate targets as usual, with the number of affected targets being permitted to be less than the maximum allowed by its Scale factor; you can dispel a spell on one subject without disrupting it on the others, but you can't increase the number of subjects a non-Area spell is affecting without re-casting the spell because those subjects weren't part of the original casting. Increasing a spell's factors is done at the time of casting by accepting penalties and/or through the free steps available to the primary factor, and spell factors that are used more than once use the largest applicable one to determine what is necessary for the effect to work as intended. Dissonance lowers spell factors by steps on the chart and Paradox both only affects them by toggling Reach effects and only applies at the point of casting, while the Hung Spell effect can only delay when a spell starts to take effect, not stretch out its effective Duration. Spells cast with the Practice of Dynamics can be viral or self-repairing and the nature of their casters means they automatically win any Clash of Wills with sub-transcendent beings, but a general question about how Travelers use combined spells cannot be answered with mechanics specific to Seekers. Combined spells cannot incorporate the benefits of Rotes and require all component spells be Praxes to get the benefit of casting them as a Praxis, meaning the largest possible common Yantra type for the most codified type of spell can't be used in a combined spell and having practiced one spell so much that casting it is second nature to you doesn't extend those benefits to combined casting with other spells you haven't internalized to that degree.<br /> <br /> Set aside the idea that a combined spell is multiple spells cast in a single action: if you saw a magician cast a spell in a piece of fiction where magic spells are concretely defined in what they do, chances are good that a Spell That Does More Than One Thing acts on the same targets, creates a shared area of effect, or involves a degree of oversight/micromanagement we would recognize as casting or re-casting separate instances of spells.Similarly, if the narrative device of a spell has symbolic grounding, it's grounding relevant to the whole effect, because while burying someone's personal effects might be symbolically resonant with hiding them from sight it's not going to do anything to improve the odds of making them fly, which has different semiotics altogether even if both are part of carrying out a larger scheme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T07:56:17-07:00","id":1551919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551917#post1551917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not going to waste my time trying to rehash in detail the premise that if you come to a thread for simple questions you have about a point of ambiguity in a set of books that does not explicitly resolve that ambiguity you do not get to complain about the lack of explicit textual support for any interpretations used in the answers you get. If you automatically disagree with the answers you get in that circumstance there was little point in asking the question. &quot;Given the general tenor of the rest of the game and the basic definition of what the thing you're asking about is&quot; is the closest to <i>written</i> assumptions we have.<br /> <br /> Spells that use Area Scale to apply non-Lasting effects apply those effects to any valid targets in the area as long as they remain in the area. Spells that use Subjects Scale can have their separate targets move wherever they like from the Range they were cast at and are Withstood by their separate targets as usual, with the number of affected targets being permitted to be less than the maximum allowed by its Scale factor; you can dispel a spell on one subject without disrupting it on the others, but you can't increase the number of subjects a non-Area spell is affecting without re-casting the spell because those subjects weren't part of the original casting. Increasing a spell's factors is done at the time of casting by accepting penalties and/or through the free steps available to the primary factor, and spell factors that are used more than once use the largest applicable one to determine what is necessary for the effect to work as intended. Dissonance lowers spell factors by steps on the chart and Paradox both only affects them by toggling Reach effects and only applies at the point of casting, while the Hung Spell effect can only delay when a spell starts to take effect, not stretch out its effective Duration. Spells cast with the Practice of Dynamics can be viral or self-repairing and the nature of their casters means they automatically win any Clash of Wills with sub-transcendent beings, but a general question about how Travelers use combined spells cannot be answered with mechanics specific to Seekers. Combined spells cannot incorporate the benefits of Rotes and require all component spells be Praxes to get the benefit of casting them as a Praxis, meaning the largest possible common Yantra type for the most codified type of spell can't be used in a combined spell and having practiced one spell so much that casting it is second nature to you doesn't extend those benefits to combined casting with other spells you haven't internalized to that degree.<br /> <br /> Set aside the idea that a combined spell is multiple spells cast in a single action: if you saw a magician cast a spell in a piece of fiction where magic spells are concretely defined in what they do, chances are good that a Spell That Does More Than One Thing acts on the same targets, creates a shared area of effect, or involves a degree of oversight/micromanagement we would recognize as casting or re-casting separate instances of spells.Similarly, if the narrative device of a spell has symbolic grounding, it's grounding relevant to the whole effect, because while burying someone's personal effects might be symbolically resonant with hiding them from sight it's not going to do anything to improve the odds of making them fly, which has different semiotics altogether even if both are part of carrying out a larger scheme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so looking at 1e since it had some more word count. The example it gives does use two forces spells (turn projectile and control velocity) on the same bullets.<br /> <br /> With most of the mechanics otherwise being exactly as described in 2e. Infact large portions of the 2e section seem to be word for word the same as 1e.<br /> <br /> And again, there is nothing in 1e which says you can or can't have different subjects.<br /> <br /> I would default to assume you can. For example, you necessarily do when in 2e it says explicitly that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are allowed to use reach to change the scale. So two spell effects using an area of effect will automatically affect different subjects (because of how AoE spells typically work on subjects).<br /> <br /> My unanswered question remains, but I have never seen anyone interpret combined spells as having to target the same subject before.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T08:36:51-07:00","id":1551921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551919#post1551919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are allowed to use reach to change the scale. So two spell effects using an area of effect will automatically affect different subjects (because of how AoE spells typically work on subjects).</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? AoE spells always affect all valid subjects inside the AoE. Two different spells with the same AoE would affect the same subjects unless one only affects people and the other only affects objects, or if the two spells have different Withstand traits so that there could be some differences in which subjects Withstands the spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My unanswered question remains, but I have never seen anyone interpret combined spells as having to target the same subject before. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spell modifications such as Yantras and <b>spell factors</b> affect the entire spellcasting pool and <b>spell effects</b>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T08:43:47-07:00","id":1551922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551919#post1551919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so looking at 1e since it had some more word count. The example it gives does use two forces spells (turn projectile and control velocity) on the same bullets.<br /> <br /> With most of the mechanics otherwise being exactly as described in 2e. Infact large portions of the 2e section seem to be word for word the same as 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other most prominent example of &quot;combined spells&quot; in the gameline is the Bundle Enhancements spell from Tome of the Mysteries, which uses the phrase outside of its application as a type of casting.<br /> <br /> To move up to three different Matter spells that affect the same Enhanced Item onto the spell control of a single mage as a single spell for the purposes of relinquishing or canceling all of them together.<br /> <br /> Because the notion of a combined spell is that it's one spell that does more than one thing in a system where most spells do one thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, there is nothing in 1e which says you can or can't have different subjects.<br /> <br /> I would default to assume you can. For example, you necessarily do when in 2e it says explicitly that </div> </div> </div>So, again, if you're going to make your own assumption solely on the basis of &quot;doesn't say,&quot; and disagree with any interpretation to the contrary, there was little point in asking the question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are allowed to use reach to change the scale. So two spell effects using an area of effect will automatically affect different subjects (because of how AoE spells typically work on subjects). </div> </div> </div>They aren't using Subjects as the Scale. They're still affecting the same Area and unless the valid subjects of the spell have no overlap (such as a combined Death and Matter spell to open the ground and raise the dead) the combined spell will not automatically affect different subjects. Area is the Scale used to make Aimed Spells risk collateral damage, it doesn't have an intrinsic capacity to be selective in what valid subjects it can affect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T13:49:28-07:00","id":1551925,"title":"","content":"Whats the best suplement (mechanics wise) for MtAw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T14:29:21-07:00","id":1551928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551925#post1551925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What is the best supplement (mechanics wise) for MtAw?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Signs of Sorcery</i> to expand on magic mechanics across the board, from crafting, to new yantras, supernal summon boons and even different types of Awakenings. <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> for mage society, character building, history, culture and build a globetrotting chronicle. <i>Night Horrors: Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> to expand on antagonists and their templates. So I would say <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> would give you the best cost benefit, but the other 2 are really great as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T12:20:22-07:00","id":1551955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551922#post1551922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other most prominent example of &quot;combined spells&quot; in the gameline is the Bundle Enhancements spell from Tome of the Mysteries, which uses the phrase outside of its application as a type of casting.<br /> <br /> To move up to three different Matter spells that affect the same Enhanced Item onto the spell control of a single mage as a single spell for the purposes of relinquishing or canceling all of them together.<br /> <br /> Because the notion of a combined spell is that it's one spell that does more than one thing in a system where most spells do one thing.<br /> <br /> So, again, if you're going to make your own assumption solely on the basis of &quot;doesn't say,&quot; and disagree with any interpretation to the contrary, there was little point in asking the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can make the assumption since it wouldn't have been hard to make a clear statement either way but they didn't.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> They aren't using Subjects as the Scale. They're still affecting the same Area and unless the valid subjects of the spell have no overlap (such as a combined Death and Matter spell to open the ground and raise the dead) the combined spell will not automatically affect different subjects. Area is the Scale used to make Aimed Spells risk collateral damage, it doesn't have an intrinsic capacity to be selective in what valid subjects it can affect. </div> </div> </div>Yes, two AoE effects will affect all valid subjects, and thus since you are combining two different effects they can have different subjects. <br /> <br /> If you cast a Death/Life spell, adding dexterity to the living and making the valid deathly objects (castoffs, ghosts, etc) manifest. Then I can't see anything saying this isn't a perfectly valid area of effect.<br /> <br /> But does it need to be an AoE spell to be cast? Can you just target one ghost and one human ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T14:13:43-07:00","id":1551958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551955#post1551955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, two AoE effects will affect all valid subjects, and thus since you are combining two different effects they can have different subjects.<br /> <br /> If you cast a Death/Life spell, adding dexterity to the living and making the valid deathly objects (castoffs, ghosts, etc) manifest. Then I can't see anything saying this isn't a perfectly valid area of effect.<br /> <br /> But does it need to be an AoE spell to be cast? Can you just target one ghost and one human ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: a shared area of effect on a single combined spell has the areas of effect on its effect overlap, and the number of affected targets within that area is arbitrarily large because the effect only affects targets while they remain in the area. That doesn't work for Subjects, because a combined spell shares its spell factors across all its effects \u2014 if you target one human and one ghost you are making the spell target two subjects, and those subjects will remain under the spell's effects until it ends regardless of where they go afterward.<br /> <br /> A combined spell shares its targeting just like it shares Potency and Duration. Unless you spend a Reach to split the effects, every effect applies to valid targets in the whole Area or every nominated Subject. Just because a spell effect doesn't do anything to a given target doesn't mean they don't have a spell on them; an Area effect that reanimates corpses and binds ghosts is &quot;touching&quot; everything in the assigned Scale and applying the relevant effects to any applicable targets, but the equivalent of being in the spell's Area for Subjects Scale is &quot;at the time of casting, is the spell being targeted at these subjects, the upper limit of which is determined by the Scale factor?&quot;<br /> <br /> You can target a smaller area or number of subjects than the limit set by a spell's Scale factor with that effect, so you could, say, link the fates of everyone in an apartment building and make everyone on a specific floor look like the same person, give a classroom full of people heightened Intelligence and only give the teacher extra dots in Expression, or make a house more valuable and give its owner increased Presence, but all of those would necessitate a Reach to split the effects in that way and none of them are completely unconnected in concept.<br /> <br /> One more time: the purpose of combined spells is to let a single spell have multiple discrete effects. To draw a comparison to Changeling, spell effects are Goblin Contracts \u2014 conceptually simple and highly focused on doing one thing \u2014 whereas combined spells fold multiple effects into one like some Arcadian and Court Contracts. The spell is still <i>one spell</i>, conceptually speaking, and that means anything it does or uses to work has to work with the whole framework of a unified spell. If you can come up with a solid symbolic reason for an area to both manifest ghosts and make living people more coordinated, you can use any symbolism that supports that combined effect as an appropriate type of Yantra, but the Scale still sets the outer bounds for how big an area or how many free-roaming subjects it can affect overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T15:33:14-07:00","id":1551962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1551955#post1551955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can make the assumption since it wouldn't have been hard to make a clear statement either way but they didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can. Then it doesn't make sense to ask if you're keeping to your own assumption regardless.<br /> <br /> But you chose to ask if it is the correct interpretation, you asked this explicitly in posts <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/1126\" >1</a>126 and 1128<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/1128\" >.</a><br /> <br /> And while you said you never saw anyone interpret Combined Spells as having to target the same subject (which was, again, your very question), that's exactly what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> (post #1130), <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> (several posts) and, indirectly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> (posts #1127 and #1134) did, while no one saw reason to defend your interpretation.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, I'm adding myself to the list: Combined Spells are spells that work as a combination of effects in the same spell. While it isn't explicitly said in the text, there's no reasonable interpretation where they're anything else, there's no indication that the intent is to cast two completely distinct spells with a single action. Otherwise it would be a far easier rule to write down, and would be written differently.<br /> <br /> If your Combined Spell affects a living target and a ghost differently, and <b>both can affect two targets</b>, sure, you can target a living person and a ghost, as long as it's reasonable for this spell to be a single spell.<br /> <br /> Other than that, you're free to keep your own interpretation, but at this point defending it is just dragging a thread about Simple Questions. Open a thread about Combined Spells if you want. If you're the ST in your games, you can freely use your interpretation, you don't need anyone's approval or agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Numbering the posts with # made them into links to unrelated threads. 07-01-2025, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T01:57:11-07:00","id":1552185,"title":"","content":"Are Artifacts physically destructible in Second Edition or not? If so, why Word of Unmaking makes an exception specifically for them to be non-destructible by this spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T02:05:22-07:00","id":1552186,"title":"","content":"Not physically. No.<br /> <br /> The supernal symbol which they represent can't be destroyed by Unmaking though (not indeed created by Making). That requires Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T05:47:46-07:00","id":1552195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552185#post1552185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Artifacts physically destructible in Second Edition or not? If so, why Word of Unmaking makes an exception specifically for them to be non-destructible by this spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have Structure, with the exception of Astras, and even in 1e they simply had higher Durability than normal objects, so yes, they are.<br /> <br /> Considering that Artifacts cannot be easily made or procured without archmastery, I suspect the exception in Word of Unmaking is there to prevent the situation where one-of-a-kind random drops from Heaven can be obliterated by blanketing a storehouse in a high-Scale burst of magic meant to shut down the likes of fetishes and Imbued or Enhanced Items; it's basically the same type of rider as &quot;you can't affect Rank 6+ spirits with Annihilate Spirit&quot; but one step removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T10:10:33-07:00","id":1552198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552195#post1552195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have Structure, with the exception of Astras, and even in 1e they simply had higher Durability than normal objects, so yes, they are.<br /> <br /> Considering that Artifacts cannot be easily made or procured without archmastery, I suspect the exception in Word of Unmaking is there to prevent the situation where one-of-a-kind random drops from Heaven can be obliterated by blanketing a storehouse in a high-Scale burst of magic meant to shut down the likes of fetishes and Imbued or Enhanced Items; it's basically the same type of rider as &quot;you can't affect Rank 6+ spirits with Annihilate Spirit&quot; but one step removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Astras, but... Like &quot;don't have a merit cost, so can never be bought at character creation&quot;, and also like so powerful... Astras are exceptional in more than one way (and I only read their rules today).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T14:06:04-07:00","id":1552312,"title":"","content":"If <i>Shrink and Grow</i> is cast on a subject to make them bigger, but they are already under spells like <i>Transform Life</i> or <i>Wonderful Machine</i>, can their new size potentially make it so those spells no longer affect them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T14:35:21-07:00","id":1552313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552312#post1552312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>Shrink and Grow</i> is cast on a subject to make them bigger, but they are already under spells like <i>Transform Life</i> or <i>Wonderful Machine</i>, can their new size potentially make it so those spells no longer affect them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as spells to alter the traits used to Withstand another spell do so, my interpretation would be that increasing the Size of a subject beyond the scope of an existing spell's Scale factor would prevent the existing spell from working until their Size goes below the threshold.<br /> <br /> I would note that this makes shapeshifters with larger alternate forms troublesome, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T05:57:21-07:00","id":1552326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552313#post1552313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as spells to alter the traits used to Withstand another spell do so, my interpretation would be that increasing the Size of a subject beyond the scope of an existing spell's Scale factor would prevent the existing spell from working until their Size goes below the threshold.<br /> <br /> I would note that this makes shapeshifters with larger alternate forms troublesome, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly as designed. Pretty sure we have Word of God on it from the designers.<br /> <br /> Notably, if the subject leave the area of an AoE, or forward in time beyond the duration of a non-indefinite spell (or indeed backwards in time to before the duration began) the spell effects are also suppressed.<br /> <br /> Becoming multiple subjects seems to be the only case which is handled differently*.<br /> <br /> But we have &quot;Werewolves increasing size beyond 5 is a problem for mages&quot; as a definite ruling.<br /> <br /> I think becoming an invalid subject for the spell might also work, like if you managed to change who you are (like a Demon swapping covers) then a spell should also be suppressed while the subject doesn't exist (but afaik there is no ruling to this effect).<br /> <br /> *See the sidebar on Swarms Pg 151.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-13-2025, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T07:06:14-07:00","id":1552329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552326#post1552326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notably, if the subject leave the area of an AoE, or forward in time beyond the duration of a non-indefinite spell (or indeed backwards in time to before the duration began) the spell effects are also suppressed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have a recollection that Shifting Sands has limits on what spells it can carry back, but I think that's mostly just a function of regressing one's position rather than something that interacts with Duration.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I think that if a subject is moved forward in time, the intervening time counts towards a spell's duration no more than it does to the subject's age.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that the only way to do that without Imperial magic is to create an effect of &quot;basically stop existing for a while&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T09:00:23-07:00","id":1552331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552329#post1552329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a recollection that Shifting Sands has limits on what spells it can carry back, but I think that's mostly just a function of regressing one's position rather than something that interacts with Duration.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I think that if a subject is moved forward in time, the intervening time counts towards a spell's duration no more than it does to the subject's age.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that the only way to do that without Imperial magic is to create an effect of &quot;basically stop existing for a while&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can move forward in time without magic. Usually by one second per second.<br /> <br /> If you go past the spell's duration, then you are no longer affected by it (in exactly the same way going outside of an AoE's area). <br /> <br /> Now I am unclear how spells are supposed to react if someone temporal stutter s you into the future, or indeed if you spend a month in a Temporal pocket - is there a seperate absolute timeframe which the spell's duration is ticking against, or is it time as experienced by the subject? Shifting Sands might guide the answer, but it is a specific example not a general rule. So I don't think we have any RAW general rule.<br /> <br /> Acceleration might also be generalized (in that case nothing happens despite expericing time faster).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T23:46:04-07:00","id":1552353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552326#post1552326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think becoming an invalid subject for the spell might also work, like if you managed to change who you are (like a Demon swapping covers) then a spell should also be suppressed while the subject doesn't exist (but afaik there is no ruling to this effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify (or not) here, if a Demon is affected by a spell, it would be necessary to determine if the spell affects the actual Demon or the Cover, and it isn't unreasonable to assume that most of the time it would affect the Demon, unless the spell specifically relies on traits unique to the Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T02:43:42-07:00","id":1552361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552353#post1552353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to clarify (or not) here, if a Demon is affected by a spell, it would be necessary to determine if the spell affects the actual Demon or the Cover, and it isn't unreasonable to assume that most of the time it would affect the Demon, unless the spell specifically relies on traits unique to the Cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> I don't think that by design Demons are meant to work the way I proposed. But I also don't think their is a better example of an entity which can change itself so thoroughly that you might consider it no longer the same subject.<br /> <br /> Spirits dissipating and reforming would not change. A person dying and becoming a ghost would invalidate a spell because the ghost isn't the person, so maybe that is a better example.<br /> <br /> Cow skin becoming leather (going from Life -&gt; Death -&gt; Matter) changes dramatically though I'm not sure it is no longer the same subject even then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T06:44:38-07:00","id":1552365,"title":"","content":"The example stands, in practice there's still quite a number of effects that may end up affecting the Cover rather than the Demon, depending on how the Mage defined the target (and potentially if they know the true nature of the target). It's just not the majority.<br /> <br /> But the details depend a lot on context and on how the ST interpret some things. It isn't unreasonable to think that most effects affect the Demon directly, but thinking that you need to be aware of the Demon to affect it directly isn't unreasonable, either. Further discussing it would be a topic for a whole thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T12:59:30-07:00","id":1552387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552331#post1552331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can move forward in time without magic. Usually by one second per second.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a very odd way of saying that before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go past the spell's duration, then you are no longer affected by it (in exactly the same way going outside of an AoE's area).</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. Only in one of those scenarios does the spell continue to actually exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T13:04:38-07:00","id":1552388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552387#post1552387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a very odd way of saying that before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No it isn't. Only in one of those scenarios does the spell continue to actually exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it always continues to exist in the past. Just like AoE spells continue to exist in the space they are localized to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T06:00:34-07:00","id":1552408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552388#post1552388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it always continues to exist in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>The past does not exist. It has to be created with magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like AoE spells continue to exist in the space they are localized to.</div> </div> </div> </div>A suppressed or otherwise inapplicable spell continues to have a capacity to apply itself or be observed by other mages with few or no metaphysical obstacles. It is distinct from a spell that has ceased to exist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T16:09:31-07:00","id":1552466,"title":"","content":"Can someone help me understand why Ghost/Goetic/Spirit Summons are Perfecting spells instead of Ruling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","name":"csctnfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T16:19:09-07:00","id":1552467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>csctnfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552466#post1552466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone help me understand why Ghost/Goetic/Spirit Summons are Perfecting spells instead of Ruling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral entities can detect Resonant conditions on people and objects within a certain radius. The caster is making the subject emit a signal its target entity can universally detect and is drawn to, then the signal is amplified using a Perfecting. So rather than &quot;taking the controller away from them&quot; and walking them to the target, they are making a very compelling beacon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T16:24:17-07:00","id":1552468,"title":"","content":"That is a perfect answer, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28872-csctnfire","name":"csctnfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T00:35:26-07:00","id":1552479,"title":"","content":"I have a doubt about Resonance<br /> What is the difference of the mana charged Resonance in Ley lines and the essence charged Resonant condition?<br /> In other words do Ley lines generate a &quot;stream&quot; of Resonant condition for spirits?<br /> I m not sure, because Werewolves should surely perceive such a ubiquous phenomenon but the core book treat essence Resonance more like &quot;springs&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T06:28:48-07:00","id":1552484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552479#post1552479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a doubt about ResonanceWhat is the difference of the mana charged Resonance in Ley lines and the essence charged Resonant condition?<br /> In other words do Ley lines generate a &quot;stream&quot; of Resonant condition for spirits?<br /> I m not sure, because Werewolves should surely perceive such a ubiquous phenomenon but the core book treat essence Resonance more like &quot;springs&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ley lines do generate the Resonant Condition tagged to spirits compatible with its resonance.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do not directly perceive resonance and they frequently interact with locuses, which can apply the Resonant Condition (and the Open Condition) to areas as large as a city block. The narrative effects of resonance on the material world, of which spirits are one vector of influence, mean that a ley line will also gradually affect its surroundings to be appropriate to its resonance, so it's quite possible nothing would be noticeably out of the ordinary without long-term observation that the average werewolf wouldn't have the time or inclination for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T07:48:11-07:00","id":1552489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552484#post1552484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ley lines do generate the Resonant Condition tagged to spirits compatible with its resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok but probably they don t create a Resonant condition on all of the line extention, or else werewolves would have noted that spirits tend to flock along areas linear shaped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T07:58:08-07:00","id":1552490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552489#post1552489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but probably they don t create a Resonant condition on all of the line extention, or else werewolves would have noted that spirits tend to flock along areas linear shaped</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits get most of their Essence from consuming other spirits and as vulnerable concrete entities they're liable to stick to places that are safe for them.<br /> <br /> Also, the three provided examples of ley line Resonances are all generalizable qualities that wouldn't be substantially more out of place than a developing trend that didn't have a ley line attached to it; an increasing tendency for spirits of fishlike concepts to spawn around a particular street is not especially unusual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T08:54:25-07:00","id":1552492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552490#post1552490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits get most of their Essence from consuming other spirits and as vulnerable concrete entities they're liable to stick to places that are safe for them.<br /> <br /> Also, the three provided examples of ley line Resonances are all generalizable qualities that wouldn't be substantially more out of place than a developing trend that didn't have a ley line attached to it; an increasing tendency for spirits of fishlike concepts to spawn around a particular street is not especially unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>About this, you seem to imply that a Resonant condition mostly originates by causes unrelated to Ley lines.<br /> <br /> Considering the first part of my first question are Resonance and Resonant the same thing?<br /> <br /> Because Prime states Resonance in its purview, but the spell Geomancy seems only capable of manipulating Ley lines Resonance<br /> <br /> The Spirit Arcana states Essence in its purview, but actually lists spells that can manipulate the Resonant condition<br /> <br /> Am i missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T09:35:10-07:00","id":1552494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552492#post1552492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About this, you seem to imply that a Resonant condition mostly originates by causes unrelated to Ley lines.<br /> <br /> Considering the first part of my first question are Resonance and Resonant the same thing?<br /> <br /> Because Prime states Resonance in its purview, but the spell Geomancy seems only capable of manipulating Ley lines Resonance<br /> <br /> The Spirit Arcana states Essence in its purview, but actually lists spells that can manipulate the Resonant condition<br /> <br /> Am i missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Parts of the world produce Resonance, and things that match the description of one or more Influences of a spirit have the Resonant Condition tagged to that spirit.<br /> <br /> Much as Anchors can only sustain ghosts who aren't spending or losing Essence at a faster rate than one point per day, the Resonant Condition can only help a spirit stay awake and active at the basic level and spirits inhabit an ecosystem where they're constantly stealing Essence from each other. In games where Resonance is a phenomenon with trackable importance, all Essence carries Resonance that affects spirits that consume it; some of that Resonance will not necessarily wholly match the Influences of that spirit, but narratively the form and nature of a spirit is affected by and adapted to the Resonance of the places it operates in and the things that it eats \u2014 the classic example being that urban and rural specimens of spirits of the same type of animal being discernibly different.<br /> <br /> On the Werewolf end of things, it's pretty much never mentioned anywhere else, but there's a relatively early 1e supplement called Territories that includes &quot;Essence Current/Ley Line&quot; on its list of Territory Descriptors; an Essence Current allows the pack that controls it to funnel Essence from one locus to another, and the entire list of Territory Descriptors includes appropriate Resonances for each different type of feature.<br /> <br /> It may also be worth noting that, while it's a 1e supplement, Sanctum and Sigil has a fairly extensive discussion of ley lines, their shape and direction, and the effects of their resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T09:47:29-07:00","id":1552495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552494#post1552494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parts of the world produce Resonance, and things that match the description of one or more Influences of a spirit have the Resonant Condition tagged to that spirit.<br /> <br /> Much as Anchors can only sustain ghosts who aren't spending or losing Essence at a faster rate than one point per day, the Resonant Condition can only help a spirit stay awake and active at the basic level and spirits inhabit an ecosystem where they're constantly stealing Essence from each other. In games where Resonance is a phenomenon with trackable importance, all Essence carries Resonance that affects spirits that consume it; some of that Resonance will not necessarily wholly match the Influences of that spirit, but narratively the form and nature of a spirit is affected by and adapted to the Resonance of the places it operates in and the things that it eats \u2014 the classic example being that urban and rural specimens of spirits of the same type of animal being discernibly different.<br /> <br /> On the Werewolf end of things, it's pretty much never mentioned anywhere else, but there's a relatively early 1e supplement called Territories that includes &quot;Essence Current/Ley Line&quot; on its list of Territory Descriptors; an Essence Current allows the pack that controls it to funnel Essence from one locus to another, and the entire list of Territory Descriptors includes appropriate Resonances for each different type of feature.<br /> <br /> It may also be worth noting that, while it's a 1e supplement, Sanctum and Sigil has a fairly extensive discussion of ley lines, their shape and direction, and the effects of their resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>But considering all of that, and the fact that Goetia also uses the Resonant condition, shouldn t the Resonant condition fully be under the Prime Arcanum ONLY and Essence under Spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T10:04:45-07:00","id":1552496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552495#post1552495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But considering all of that, and the fact that Goetia also uses the Resonant condition, shouldn t the Resonant condition fully be under the Prime Arcanum ONLY and Essence under Spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resonant Condition as it is most conventionally encountered is a function of the existence of spirits. Resonance as a phenomenon is broader than the Resonant Condition, but the Shadow is the main reinforcing vector for the effects of Resonance on the world, and Goetia do not typically leave the Astral in normal circumstances nor use the Resonant Condition for sustenance.<br /> <br /> Prime can affect Resonance because Resonance affects Hallows, Mana, and ley lines, but Spirit is where Resonance most fully expresses itself; there's bound to be some overlap when the Watchtower of the Golden Key draws upon the part of the soul that marks a thing as living or dead, but the Pillar of the Heart that the Watchtower of the Singing Stone empowers is one's connection to and capacity for sympathy with the wider world, while the Pillar of the Essence concerns itself with the essential nature and qualities of a thing. Outside the context of magical meddling you change the Resonance of a thing or place by changing that thing or place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T10:17:11-07:00","id":1552498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552496#post1552496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Resonant Condition as it is most conventionally encountered is a function of the existence of spirits. Resonance as a phenomenon is broader than the Resonant Condition, but the Shadow is the main reinforcing vector for the effects of Resonance on the world, and Goetia do not typically leave the Astral in normal circumstances nor use the Resonant Condition for sustenance.<br /> <br /> Prime can affect Resonance because Resonance affects Hallows, Mana, and ley lines, but Spirit is where Resonance most fully expresses itself; there's bound to be some overlap when the Watchtower of the Golden Key draws upon the part of the soul that marks a thing as living or dead, but the Pillar of the Heart that the Watchtower of the Singing Stone empowers is one's connection to and capacity for sympathy with the wider world, while the Pillar of the Essence concerns itself with the essential nature and qualities of a thing. Outside the context of magical meddling you change the Resonance of a thing or place by changing that thing or place.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as an example:<br /> <br /> We imagine a park, childs plays often here, a good place.<br /> <br /> -Case 1 (no ley line intersecting the park)<br /> Is it possible that the park has Resonant(joy) condition?<br /> If yes, if i understand it rightly a mage with Prime wouldn t detect anything, right ?<br /> What spell could i use to change the condition to Resonant (dogs) ?<br /> <br /> -Case 2 (a ley line (joy) intersect the park)<br /> Is it correct to assume that the park MUST have the Resonant (joy) condition?<br /> If i use the spell Geomancy to change the Ley line Resonance to (cats) the Resonant condition would slowly change to match it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T10:40:24-07:00","id":1552499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552498#post1552498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We imagine a park, childs plays often here, a good place.<br /> <br /> -Case 1 (no ley line intersecting the park)<br /> Is it possible that the park has Resonant(joy) condition?<br /> If yes, if i understand it rightly a mage with Prime wouldn t detect anything, right ?<br /> What spell could i use to change the condition to Resonant (dogs) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The park has the Resonant Condition tagged for any spirit whose Influences would describe it, which ostensibly includes spirits of joy. Prime Mage Sight would not reveal its Resonance and Sacred Geometry would not show a ley line or Node in the park.<br /> <br /> No singular published spell allows the nature of the Resonant keyword to be changed, but Erode Resonance would allow you to remove the existing Resonant Condition and a Compelling spell might allow you to stretch the presence of a dog or doglike thing into an instance of Resonant (Dogs) that covers the whole park in similar fashion to Invoke Bane. Otherwise, spells to make the park resonate more with the concept of dogs and less with the concept of joy (materially or otherwise) are the only Awakened magical methods that suggest themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Case 2 (a ley line (joy) intersect the park)<br /> Is it correct to assume that the park MUST have the Resonant (joy) condition?<br /> If i use the spell Geomancy to change the Ley line Resonance to (cats) the Resonant condition would slowly change to match it? </div> </div> </div>Per Sanctum and Sigil, typically only things directly on the line are affected by its resonance, but they can carry that resonance with them if they absorb it regularly and are then moved elsewhere. The ley line will affect any park structures it touches and any of the children who spend a lot of time there, and it will almost certainly give rise to spirits who will propagate more joyful resonance, such that in practice the whole park may become Resonant with joy; likewise, if the ley line's Resonance changes to a feline one the things that its flow affects will start to take on feline qualities over time, but unless the park ceases to be a source of joy through other means than the ley line it still has a Resonant condition that supports spirits of joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T11:01:38-07:00","id":1552500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552499#post1552499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No singular published spell allows the nature of the Resonant keyword to be changed, but Erode Resonance would allow you to remove the existing Resonant Condition and a Compelling spell might allow you to stretch the presence of a dog or doglike thing into an instance of Resonant (Dogs) that covers the whole park in similar fashion to Invoke Bane. Otherwise, spells to make the park resonate more with the concept of dogs and less with the concept of joy (materially or otherwise) are the only Awakened magical methods that suggest themselves.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be a stretch to suppose that a level 4 spirit (similar to Shape Spirit) could do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T11:26:39-07:00","id":1552503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552500#post1552500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be a stretch to suppose that a level 4 spirit (similar to Shape Spirit) could do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the lack of published spells to change the nature of an ordinary instance of the Resonant Condition is deliberate, given that the Condition pulls double duty as a marker for valid subjects of a spirit's Influences, but yes, as far as the basic descriptions of the Practices go Patterning would be the one to use for turning one type of Resonant Condition into another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T03:08:40-07:00","id":1552536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552503#post1552503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the lack of published spells to change the nature of an ordinary instance of the Resonant Condition is deliberate, given that the Condition pulls double duty as a marker for valid subjects of a spirit's Influences, but yes, as far as the basic descriptions of the Practices go Patterning would be the one to use for turning one type of Resonant Condition into another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Patterning not extreme, weaving is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving spells can alter nearly any property of a target without transforming it into something completely different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that not sound like turning resonance keyed to one thing into still resonance but keyed to the same thing?<br /> <br /> Infact, Ruling or Compelling sound like the should he able to change a resonance aswell, but in the way the resonance naturally changes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T06:17:54-07:00","id":1552541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552536#post1552536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infact, Ruling or Compelling sound like the should he able to change a resonance aswell, but in the way the resonance naturally changes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance doesn't naturally change in the sense of turning one thing into another; you couldn't use Compelling or Ruling to directly change Resonance any more than you can use those Practices to cause a healthy person to immediately die.<br /> <br /> If Shape Spirit is Patterning despite only turning a spirit into a different kind of spirit, it stands to reason that a spell to change the Resonance of a quantity of Essence from one kind to another would also be Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T10:33:32-07:00","id":1552544,"title":"","content":"I think this is one of those areas where &quot;something completely different&quot; is a bit of a vague statement that needs to be taken somewhat artistically and maybe used as a justification for when one thinks it's just plain an effect that should require a higher Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Like, is a cup made of glass &quot;completely different&quot; from a cup made of plastic? One might think that's only a minor characteristic and the essential substance of the thing is being a cup, and yet the spell we're given for changing materials is Patterning on the apparent logic that the material is actually the essential thing.<br /> <br /> The same might go for Resonance, particularly if one interprets Resonance as a thing that doesn't really have any substance beyond the thing that it Resonates with. <br /> <br /> (Although I suppose that raises questions of if Resonance is a thing in and of itself with properties, or is just a property of other things. I suppose even in that interpretation, a Weaving spell might alter the current Resonance of a subject into another thing it could be plausibly resonant with, while Patterning is how to bestow Resonance that makes no innate sense to the spell target.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T11:52:21-07:00","id":1552545,"title":"","content":"Symbolically a cup is a cup, but does one of the arcana have cup-ness in its purview? Matter can alter the material properties, without needing to reference the cup-ness...<br /> <br /> The question of resonance is whether it can change by itself, what is the natural state. Are we saying there is Resonance in the room which will be dramatically different when something dramatic happens to change it? Or is the resonance a thing in itself which is replaced by a new resonance, pushed out by the dramatic event?<br /> <br /> In one case, Ruling spells might work (which may well not be a valid interpretation). Unfortunately I don't know how much depth this really gets anywhere in the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T12:26:17-07:00","id":1552546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552545#post1552545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question of resonance is whether it can change by itself, what is the natural state. Are we saying there is Resonance in the room which will be dramatically different when something dramatic happens to change it? Or is the resonance a thing in itself which is replaced by a new resonance, pushed out by the dramatic event?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Werewolf is concerned as the game that directly deals with the impact of Resonance on spirits and the Shadow, it's definitely the latter.<br /> <br /> The tool Werewolf has for changing Resonance without necessarily changing the phenomena itself (the Resonance Shaper Merit) uses extended actions to act on loci and other wellsprings of Essence, with the latter changing the Resonance of singular points of Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T14:18:28-07:00","id":1552551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552546#post1552546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Werewolf is concerned as the game that directly deals with the impact of Resonance on spirits and the Shadow, it's definitely the latter.<br /> <br /> The tool Werewolf has for changing Resonance without necessarily changing the phenomena itself (the Resonance Shaper Merit) uses extended actions to act on loci and other wellsprings of Essence, with the latter changing the Resonance of singular points of Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you are saying, that Essence has Resonance and you remove one to add another.<br /> <br /> In that case, Essence isn't changed but a feature is, so would you suggest it is weaving to change the resonance of some essence? is this already a Spirit effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T14:24:15-07:00","id":1552552,"title":"","content":"Does the resilennce vampire discipline count as a resist trait for body based spells since it adds stamina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-20T15:25:53-07:00","id":1552556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552551#post1552551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you are saying, that Essence has Resonance and you remove one to add another.<br /> <br /> In that case, Essence isn't changed but a feature is, so would you suggest it is weaving to change the resonance of some essence? is this already a Spirit effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Essence <i>is</i> the feature; in any game where Essence is generated for spirits, the resonance of the Essence is at least narratively tracked due to its suitability as a thing that affects spirits that consume it or are offered it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552552#post1552552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the resilennce vampire discipline count as a resist trait for body based spells since it adds stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>The extra Stamina counts as the character's Stamina for the purposes of Withstand; anything that increases the actual Attribute instead of simply giving a dice modifier does likewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Extra word. 07-21-2025, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T15:27:29-07:00","id":1552658,"title":"","content":"Irises to the Supernal can be found at the hearts of Emanations, any non-archmage who crosses them is Ret Gone as they lose the ability to perceive their own existence amidst the overload of Supernal symbols (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 14 and the concept of Lustrum from <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>). What happens if a scrying window is sent through that Iris ? What happens if one uses <i>Divination</i> to predict the consequences of entering it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T17:39:58-07:00","id":1552661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552658#post1552658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irises to the Supernal can be found at the hearts of Emanations, any non-archmage who crosses them is Ret Gone as they lose the ability to perceive their own existence amidst the overload of Supernal symbols (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 14 and the concept of Lustrum from <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>). What happens if a scrying window is sent through that Iris ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The subject of the Scrying spell no longer exists and the spell following them fizzles out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens if one uses <i>Divination</i> to predict the consequences of entering it ? </div> </div> </div>As with trying to divine whether someone will Awaken, I'm pretty sure using Time magic to try to figure out what will happen if you chuck someone into direct contact with the part of the cosmology that affects Time in unpredictable ways when touched improperly doesn't work in any way useful to the purpose of doing so. You will get answers that negate themselves or ignore the presence of the Iris or something weirder yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T17:49:03-07:00","id":1552662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552661#post1552661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of the Scrying spell no longer exists and the spell following them fizzles out.<br /> <br /> As with trying to divine whether someone will Awaken, I'm pretty sure using Time magic to try to figure out what will happen if you chuck someone into direct contact with the part of the cosmology that affects Time in unpredictable ways when touched improperly doesn't work in any way useful to the purpose of doing so. You will get answers that negate themselves or ignore the presence of the Iris or something weirder yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the same apply if the caster sends just a <i>Scrying</i> window in through remote viewing ? Could they, for example, use the Reach effect of <i>The Outward &amp; Inward Eye</i> to see through, perhaps get a splitting headache (seeing some symbols but not all) and then somehow being able to roll well enough to send a <i>Scrying</i> spell through ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T18:55:20-07:00","id":1552663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552662#post1552662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the same apply if the caster sends just a <i>Scrying</i> window in through remote viewing ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything you would send into the Iris would likewise be obliterated. The section of Signs of Sorcery you referenced doesn't say anything about the effects being perception-related \u2014 &quot;Nothing survives unprotected contact with the Supernal Realm&quot; and &quot;Everyone and everything that has ever gone through, however, vanishes, and in many cases suffers additional effects&quot; are extremely clear about this, especially taken in combination with the in-setting theory that the metaphysical cause of these consequences is the thing fatally interfering with the symbol of itself.<br /> <br /> You need a Lustrum to interact with the Supernal without destroying yourself as a Phenomenal entity, in the reverse phenomenon of needing Spirit to attune your senses to spiritual ephemera before you can see into the Shadow from the material world on your own. (Similarly, even if you haven't got the ability to form a Lustrum, a third party who can make one \u2014 like a Watchtower or an archmage or a Supernal god \u2014 can allow you to experience the Supernal just as a moderately powerful spirit can manifest a Shadow Gateway that people can see the Shadow through, but by definition a Lustrum is not part of most Emanation Realms' passages to the Supernal.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T00:26:34-07:00","id":1552688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552658#post1552658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a scrying window is sent through that Iris ?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you &quot;send&quot; a scrying window?<br /> <br /> Scrying is a spell. It is cast on a subject. It has an effect of &quot;create a close up projection of the subject in front of the caster&quot;. It's not a remote drone that can be piloted.<br /> <br /> The only thing I would think of as a scrying spell that can relocate itself to focus on different things would be cast with the Imperial Practices anyway. <br /> <br /> As far as using the spell to flatten all planes of vision around you goes, I'm going to go with &quot;an Iris to the Supernal is almost never a literal hole in the world, and even when it is it's not something that is adhering to the normal dimensions that most Space spells interact with&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T04:46:08-07:00","id":1552697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552688#post1552688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you &quot;send&quot; a scrying window?<br /> <br /> Scrying is a spell. It is cast on a subject. It has an effect of &quot;create a close up projection of the subject in front of the caster&quot;. It's not a remote drone that can be piloted.<br /> <br /> The only thing I would think of as a scrying spell that can relocate itself to focus on different things would be cast with the Imperial Practices anyway.<br /> <br /> As far as using the spell to flatten all planes of vision around you goes, I'm going to go with &quot;an Iris to the Supernal is almost never a literal hole in the world, and even when it is it's not something that is adhering to the normal dimensions that most Space spells interact with&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can scry on a subject which is able to fit through an iris, a stone perhaps which you throw.<br /> <br /> But the answer above seems to be consistent no matter how you project your sense through ... (Perhaps only your senses are obliterated..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T12:59:54-07:00","id":1552726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552697#post1552697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can scry on a subject which is able to fit through an iris, a stone perhaps which you throw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the answer to that of &quot;the spell just ends when its subject is obliterated&quot; not only makes sense, but seems quite elementary.<br /> <br /> Mind, given how scrying on such a subject will only ever show you the subject, even if the stone wasn't rendered non-existent, all you'd get is continuing to scry on a stone without any context as to its surroundings.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel that this is a point worth reminding that while Irises often align along something with the symbolism of a passageway, they're very rarely just lying open. The Key for them is both typically a wilful act, and something that coincides with the act of crossing them to their destination. You probably shouldn't really have a situation in which it's possible to get the passage to the Supernal open and then toss something through it, and I think any additional questions of trying to tease out implications to the concept are readily resolved with &quot;every single Supernal Iris requires a Key, and the Key would coincide with the act of crossing through one&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the only thing that you can do with a Supernal Iris is either pass through it to your doom or wait for an entity to emerge from it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T15:14:45-07:00","id":1552732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552726#post1552726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think the answer to that of &quot;the spell just ends when its subject is obliterated&quot; not only makes sense, but seems quite elementary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the answer is fine, I was just pointing out that you can treat a scrying window like a drone camera...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Mind, given how scrying on such a subject will only ever show you the subject, even if the stone wasn't rendered non-existent, all you'd get is continuing to scry on a stone without any context as to its surroundings.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Although this is a point...I suppose if it collides with its own supernal symbol, then you get to use Mage sight to see the symbols and the stone become one and obliterate? <br /> <br /> Which still doesn't show you the surroundings... I suppose a soul stone which you can project your senses out of might be better ... For a certain value of better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Also, I feel that this is a point worth reminding that while Irises often align along something with the symbolism of a passageway, they're very rarely just lying open. The Key for them is both typically a wilful act, and something that coincides with the act of crossing them to their destination. You probably shouldn't really have a situation in which it's possible to get the passage to the Supernal open and then toss something through it, and I think any additional questions of trying to tease out implications to the concept are readily resolved with &quot;every single Supernal Iris requires a Key, and the Key would coincide with the act of crossing through one&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the only thing that you can do with a Supernal Iris is either pass through it to your doom or wait for an entity to emerge from it.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but can you use Fabricate fortune to &quot;trick&quot; the Iris into believing the stone is satisfying the Key's requirement (that is what Fabricate fortune is for, right?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T16:45:01-07:00","id":1552735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552732#post1552732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but can you use Fabricate fortune to &quot;trick&quot; the Iris into believing the stone is satisfying the Key's requirement (that is what Fabricate fortune is for, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the fact that the term &quot;Iris&quot; is not used to describe the passageway/gateway to the Supernal deep in the inhospitable depths of an Emanation is deliberate \u2014 I don't think the thresholds in question work that way any more than you can look into a Hellmouth and see an objective view of Abaddon \u2014 but also Fabricate Fortune is not a skeleton key for supernatural Keys; a Keyed effect is not the same thing as messing with the Conditional Durations or conditional triggers of spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T23:50:24-07:00","id":1552743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552735#post1552735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the fact that the term &quot;Iris&quot; is not used to describe the passageway/gateway to the Supernal deep in the inhospitable depths of an Emanation is deliberate \u2014 I don't think the thresholds in question work that way any more than you can look into a Hellmouth and see an objective view of Abaddon \u2014</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the 2e book doesn't say much about the process at all. Just that the unfiltered experience annihilates you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but also Fabricate Fortune is not a skeleton key for supernatural Keys; a Keyed effect is not the same thing as messing with the Conditional Durations or conditional triggers of spells. </div> </div> </div>Well I actually disagree with you there.<br /> <br /> But there isn't any text which backs up either position, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T10:53:16-07:00","id":1552749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552732#post1552732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the answer is fine, I was just pointing out that you can treat a scrying window like a drone camera...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Although this is a point...I suppose if it collides with its own supernal symbol, then you get to use Mage sight to see the symbols and the stone become one and obliterate?<br /> <br /> Which still doesn't show you the surroundings... I suppose a soul stone which you can project your senses out of might be better ... For a certain value of better.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, but can you use Fabricate fortune to &quot;trick&quot; the Iris into believing the stone is satisfying the Key's requirement (that is what Fabricate fortune is for, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My understanding is that it would only work on conditions imposed by Fate, such as oaths, promises, contracts, etc. So it wouldn't work on an Avernian Gate, for example.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\">According to Dave Brookshaw</a>, in order to open an Iris of any nature, you would need a Weaving of the corresponding element, such as Death for the Avernian Gate, Mind and Fate for a Hedge gate or Time for something like <i>A Crack in The Sla</i>b (from <i>Dishonored 2</i>) type of temporal phenomenon. So if you were in the Emanation of Mars (<i>Signs of Sorcery </i>page 111) and found a Supernal Iris, you could theoretically open it with a Weaving of Prime and toss something inside it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T07:09:58-07:00","id":1552769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552749#post1552749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">My understanding is that it would only work on conditions imposed by Fate, such as oaths, promises, contracts, etc. So it wouldn't work on an Avernian Gate, for example.<br /> <br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> I am pretty sure that with a Fate Knowing spell (Serendipity) you can find out what a key is - just have your goal be going through the Iris in question. <br /> <br /> You could also use Fate Compelling to luckily find the key. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/872952-a-changeling-related-question?p=873580#post873580\">According to Dave Brookshaw</a>, in order to open an Iris of any nature, you would need a Weaving of the corresponding element, such as Death for the Avernian Gate, Mind and Fate for a Hedge gate or Time for something like <i>A Crack in The Sla</i>b (from <i>Dishonored 2</i>) type of temporal phenomenon. So if you were in the Emanation of Mars (<i>Signs of Sorcery </i>page 111) and found a Supernal Iris, you could theoretically open it with a Weaving of Prime and toss something inside it. </div> </div> </div></span>Dave is pretty explicitly talking about when you don't have the relevant Key, and using Weaving of the appropriate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> This is not what getting a Key is about.<br /> <br /> And the fact that Keys are talked about in the general section on Space (because they have the most Iris related content) doesn't mean keys are particularly Space related. <br /> <br /> But faking the key with Fate veiling seems entirely within the ability of Fabricate Fortune to me. You need some specific condition to be met, sure Fate will do that just fine (as per the Knowing and Compelling examples above).<br /> <br /> Fate isn't Weaving some doors open, it is making the conditions of the key appear to have happened... Not sure what other Purview's Knowing Arcanum you would use to find what a particular key is...but that is how I run things at my table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T06:26:58-07:00","id":1552795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552735#post1552735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the fact that the term &quot;Iris&quot; is not used to describe the passageway/gateway to the Supernal deep in the inhospitable depths of an Emanation is deliberate</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, though? Signs of Sorcery page 14: &quot;Nothing survives unprotected contact with the Supernal Realm. Entering it is not as difficult as many assume \u2014 every Emanation Realm has an Iris to it as its heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that it would matter if it wasn't, though. It's not as if there's a distinction between an Iris and some non-Iris portal, given that &quot;Iris&quot; is established as just the common mage term for passages that lead somewhere otherwise not connected by conventional travel.<br /> <br /> It just seems to be the nature of the universe that almost any time such a passageway exists, it requires something additional to make it functional or accessible.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T06:44:50-07:00","id":1552797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552769#post1552769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am pretty sure that with a Fate Knowing spell (Serendipity) you can find out what a key is - just have your goal be going through the Iris in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the text of Serendipity, the overall tone of the Arcanum, and the expected reach of a one-dot spell mean the effect is more subtle than that.<br /> <br /> If you're faced with a door that you don't have the key to, Serendipity won't tell you precisely where the key is. It will provide you with a sense of an action to take that will begin a series of events leading you to the key.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also use Fate Compelling to luckily find the key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luck can't create things where they don't exist, and a Compelling of Fate is given an example of making something vaguely fortunate or unfortunate of minor significance happen randomly to you somewhere within a day or an hour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But faking the key with Fate veiling seems entirely within the ability of Fabricate Fortune to me. You need some specific condition to be met, sure Fate will do that just fine (as per the Knowing and Compelling examples above).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well why stop there? What, you need a person to be killed? Good news, you've faked that the conditions that would lead to that just happening were already present, and so it just does. Brings a whole new meaning to &quot;fake it till you make it&quot;.<br /> <br /> This actually points me towards a general oddity with how people often talk about spells. They'll insist upon some pre-existing spell having applications beyond what the published form of it does, and it's like... you have creative thaumaturgy and improvised casting. If the effect is fitting to the Arcanum and the Practice, you don't need to brute force it into some existing spell, you can just cast a spell to do it.<br /> <br /> The only reason to have spells differentiated in such a fashion at all is because you can only have specific effects gain the benefits of rotes, praxes, and Legacy Attainments. If those things are acknowledged in such discussions, that absolutely sounds like somebody saying &quot;I want to be able to accomplish as much as possible without spending more XP for it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So Fabricate Fortune can't do the thing you're talking about. A different kind of Fate Veiling spell that would need a separate purchase for rote benefits can probably do some of it, but not to the extent of shortcutting the entire process of Keys for Irises beyond the established point that doing so is a function of the Weaving Arcanum. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T01:58:28-07:00","id":1552826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552797#post1552797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the text of Serendipity, the overall tone of the Arcanum, and the expected reach of a one-dot spell mean the effect is more subtle than that.<br /> <br /> If you're faced with a door that you don't have the key to, Serendipity won't tell you precisely where the key is. It will provide you with a sense of an action to take that will begin a series of events leading you to the key.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Luck can't create things where they don't exist, and a Compelling of Fate is given an example of making something vaguely fortunate or unfortunate of minor significance happen randomly to you somewhere within a day or an hour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well why stop there? What, you need a person to be killed? Good news, you've faked that the conditions that would lead to that just happening were already present, and so it just does. Brings a whole new meaning to &quot;fake it till you make it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This actually points me towards a general oddity with how people often talk about spells. They'll insist upon some pre-existing spell having applications beyond what the published form of it does, and it's like... you have creative thaumaturgy and improvised casting. If the effect is fitting to the Arcanum and the Practice, you don't need to brute force it into some existing spell, you can just cast a spell to do it. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, you see it as an oddity that people use the example spells to suggest other things you should be able to do with similar magic?<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter to me if this is Fabricate Fortune or a creative Thaumetergy effect. It is still a Fate Veiling effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason to have spells differentiated in such a fashion at all is because you can only have specific effects gain the benefits of rotes, praxes, and Legacy Attainments. If those things are acknowledged in such discussions, that absolutely sounds like somebody saying &quot;I want to be able to accomplish as much as possible without spending more XP for it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So Fabricate Fortune can't do the thing you're talking about. A different kind of Fate Veiling spell that would need a separate purchase for rote benefits can probably do some of it, but not to the extent of shortcutting the entire process of Keys for Irises beyond the established point that doing so is a function of the Weaving Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>I entirely disagree, the function of weaving is to rip a door open. The function of a key is to open a door the way it is meant to he opened. The point of this is more like picking the lock, you don't have the key, but you also don't need to force it.<br /> <br /> And ultimately if Fabricate Fortune can convince Excalibur the the random person is the King that was Promised, and draw the sword from the stone (yes I know those are different Swords...) then I don't see how opening a lock is that far fetched for the same Fate Veiling. <br /> <br /> Keys aren't particularly different from Conditional effects. That is just how Fate works as written, now *maybe* you could argue Date should not have conditional duration, and this is a hold over from 1e, and that Fate is OP, and further that effects like Keying spells, Conditionality, and things like the Baslisk Yantra, should all be free for anyone to use regardless of the Arcana they weild.<br /> <br /> But that is a seperate question.<br /> <br /> To whit. Does Space Knowing let you learn the key of any Iris? Or does it depend on the Arcanum?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T04:46:17-07:00","id":1552828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552826#post1552826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sorry, you see it as an oddity that people use the example spells to suggest other things you should be able to do with similar magic?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is clearly not the thing that I said at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552826#post1552826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And ultimately if Fabricate Fortune can convince Excalibur the the random person is the King that was Promised, and draw the sword from the stone (yes I know those are different Swords...) then I don't see how opening a lock is that far fetched for the same Fate Veiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one of those things is a subject of Destiny and the other is not.<br /> <br /> Like, conditional duration is not generic &quot;thing happens in response to other thing&quot;. The spell to create false readings to subjects of destiny interacts with it because it is an Attainment of the Fate Arcanum<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keys aren't particularly different from Conditional effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of how they work, sure, but not in terms of <i>why</i> they work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To whit. Does Space Knowing let you learn the key of any Iris?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have some mixed ideas of how the Space Arcanum should interact with Irises, given that the reason they're called that is specifically to invoke that Arcanum's thesis on the connection between perception and location.<br /> <br /> At the very least, I think Space should be able to tell somebody where an Iris leads, regardless of its type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T06:01:07-07:00","id":1552829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552828#post1552828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is clearly not the thing that I said at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for missing what you actually said.<br /> <br /> I guess my point is, I don't see a problem saying &quot;this examples spells suggests to me an alternative option where you could also do X or Y&quot; compared to going directly to &quot;just use creative Thaumetergy for everything&quot; <br /> <br /> Adding a reach effect to an example spell is often optimal mechanically instead of re-inventing an entire spell. Though it might be more fun sometimes to have to discover a Grimoire with that rote in it. For Praxis and Legacy attainments, it is just fine for players to add whatever spells they regularily cast <i>the way they cast them</i> as a Praxis (or when making their own legacy attainments... Obviously learning legacy from other Mages is closer to the Grimoire example).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because one of those things is a subject of Destiny and the other is not.<br /> <br /> Like, conditional duration is not generic &quot;thing happens in response to other thing&quot;. The spell to create false readings to subjects of destiny interacts with it because it is an Attainment of the Fate Arcanum<br /> <br /> In terms of how they work, sure, but not in terms of <i>why</i> they work. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure i agree at all. The &quot;why&quot; they work is some metaphysics that I don't know is outlined in canon.<br /> <br /> The other examples of rules and Gates we have are the Old Laws of Deep Dominions and Irkalla Gate; Books of the Dead explicitly calls out Fate as being able to manipulate the Old Laws. It even gives an example of using Fabricate Fortune (though it is a 1e version of Fabricate Fortune, which requires 3 dots) to hide the fact that you have broken one of the Old Laws.<br /> <br /> It seems like the rules for bypassing an Irkalla Gate would be the same as messing with an Old laws - but apparently I am wrong about it being written. I can't find any reference to Fate being used in Irkalla Gates in Book of the Dead of the Player's guide to the Contagion Chronicle.<br /> <br /> The only other thing I saw was that a Geist's Bargain with their Sin-eater is &quot;seen as&quot; a Destiny by Fate magics... Which seems tangential.<br /> <br /> But my point is, it is typical to apply Fate magic this way across other Laws and Rules - despite Prime often being seen as laying down rules and order. I don't think there is a case for having a Prime based Attainment for meta-magical effects (like adding Keys to spells).<br /> <br /> The game just seems to allow them whenever necessary because it makes the game better. But this is the Ludo-narrative reasoning, not a metaphysics of the game's answer for why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have some mixed ideas of how the Space Arcanum should interact with Irises, given that the reason they're called that is specifically to invoke that Arcanum's thesis on the connection between perception and location.<br /> <br /> At the very least, I think Space should be able to tell somebody where an Iris leads, regardless of its type. </div> </div> </div>Would you consider &quot;An Otherworld&quot;as a valid location, without necessarily telling them which -unless they have reason to know what that other world is.<br /> <br /> Ie: this is a place where there are no connections to this world - though actythat doesn't really work for the Shadow, which is connected to the things on the other side of the Gauntlet... Infact Hedgegates also have some psycho-reactive connection between the Hedge on one side and the material world on the other ...<br /> <br /> Only really the Underworld has in some sense no connection - or at least n\u00f3 two way connection, thing that get dragged through an Avernian gate don't really have connections (once they have lost all their anchors) but might still be seen as connected to what once was, but it feels like a very one way thing, like stuff only goes into an Avernian Gate (which would then make sense to show up when viewed through the lens of the Arcanum of Space).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  failure to finish the message. 08-02-2025, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T06:58:59-07:00","id":1552830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552829#post1552829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding a reach effect to an example spell is often optimal mechanically instead of re-inventing an entire spell. Though it might be more fun sometimes to have to discover a Grimoire with that rote in it. For Praxis and Legacy attainments, it is just fine for players to add whatever spells they regularily cast <i>the way they cast them</i> as a Praxis (or when making their own legacy attainments... Obviously learning legacy from other Mages is closer to the Grimoire example).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a substantial point of ludonarrative balance for mages' ability to improvise any spell effect within the scope of their knowledge of the Arcana that they do not get the benefits of specialization on spells they have not spent advancement resources to specialize in, and a Praxis is a Praxis regardless of how it is usually used.<br /> <br /> A spell does what it says it does, modified by Reach effects, Paradox, and whatever limitations its Yantras and spell factors impose. In the absence of explicit statement or at-the-table agreement based on the same criteria that determines what Mage Sight can tell the character about the subject (a la the corebook's &quot;Theory, Practice, and Crossover&quot; sidebar), an existing spell that does a specific thing cannot be used to do a notably different specific thing. Fate and Spirit are not omnitools just because lots of supernatural objects have if-then effects or resonate with a theme or motif.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure i agree at all. The &quot;why&quot; they work is some metaphysics that I don't know is outlined in canon. </div> </div> </div>The metaphysical reason is &quot;there is a pseudo-sentient supernatural force with a complex agenda that causes events to unfold in particular ways through subtle means&quot; \u2014 Fate is one of the Arcana used to interact with the frameworks of the God-Machine, the Wyrd, and the Divine Fire because all of those are supersystems of occult rules that hang together as part of an interconnected whole whose parts and partners are moving toward specific aims. The Shadow is an ecosystem routinely in need of oversight, the Underworld is a broken world whose theoretical evil gods are notionally distinct from its intrinsic nature, and the Astral does not serve a theoretically-unified agenda without deep speculation on the nature of reality as a whole. &quot;Consequences follow cause&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;an invisible force of destiny makes this thing happen&quot; any more than you can naturally use Fate to trick a spirit into thinking something is its Bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other examples of rules and Gates we have are the Old Laws of Deep Dominions and Irkalla Gate; Books of the Dead explicitly calls out Fate as being able to manipulate the Old Laws. It even gives an example of using Fabricate Fortune (though it is a 1e version of Fabricate Fortune, which requires 3 dots) to hide the fact that you have broken one of the Old Laws. </div> </div> </div>Book of the Dead is also written for an edition of Geist where the Kerberoi are not uniformly at least Rank 5, that application of Fabricate Fortune is resisted by the enforcing Kerberos, and &quot;fooling the enforcer of a supernatural law in a place where breaking the law draws supernatural attention into thinking you haven't broken the law&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;this supernatural object operates in this fashion.&quot; 1e Changeling's justification for not being able to teleport out of the Hedge notwithstanding, a gateway is not a supernatural agreement or destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T05:01:15-07:00","id":1552852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552829#post1552829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess my point is, I don't see a problem saying &quot;this examples spells suggests to me an alternative option where you could also do X or Y&quot; compared to going directly to &quot;just use creative Thaumetergy for everything&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of that thing that I said about artificially inflating the value of things like rotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding a reach effect to an example spell is often optimal mechanically instead of re-inventing an entire spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to be too hard on optimisation as a motivation in roleplaying games, but I think this is one of the instances of where it is at fault.<br /> <br /> Not just about the rote thing, although that is significant. I think it stifles creativity, turns reading spells into an exhausting exercise in litigating precisely what they do, and adds a premise of &quot;individual spells can be complex and multifaceted&quot; in a way that I think has problem implications for the scope of mage powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other examples of rules and Gates we have are the Old Laws of Deep Dominions</div> </div> </div> </div>To the extent that I think this First Edition has relevance, I think it's only as far as I would find the idea of a cross-section between &quot;laws as in a local legal code&quot; and &quot;laws as metaphysical things&quot; to fall under the purview of the Fate Arcanum, in its more mythic connotations. It might be of the dead, but there's something kind of fae about it.<br /> <br /> I would hold that, in the vast majority of cases, the Keys to Irises are more like... literal keys. They're processes that initiate a response. Being metaphysical might mean there's a certain narrative logic to them, but they don't have that premise that falls under Fate.<br /> <br /> It would be like saying that a Veiling of Fate can trick fuel into thinking the conditions for ignition are present.<br /> <br /> It also kind of leads into a point that conditional duration ends up keyed as something responding to information that can be concealed from it (or falsified to it). Positioning a Veiling as being able to substitute for a Key is kind of acting like an Iris opens because it becomes aware of something. I would posit that it would make more sense in the majority of circumstances that they Key is a component in a process of opening the Iris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">despite Prime often being seen as laying down rules and order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen by what, by whom?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T11:14:59-07:00","id":1552921,"title":"","content":"Thinking of a &quot;I was preapred for this&quot; spell. It works the way that in the past i did divination for this moment now when i cast the spell that for example i will neeed to open a lock so i bring lockpicks. Not sure thought what practice that would be so what arcanum levels would be nneded for this. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T11:28:02-07:00","id":1552923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552921#post1552921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of a &quot;I was preapred for this&quot; spell. It works the way that in the past i did divination for this moment now when i cast the spell that for example i will neeed to open a lock so i bring lockpicks. Not sure thought what practice that would be so what arcanum levels would be nneded for this. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>For mages this is just accomplished through time travel, quick reaction, and preparation, since the counterbalance of Mage's versatility is that they need to cast their spells to benefit from them; the alternative would be through Fate spells that happen to make something you saw or did earlier relevant, which isn't as good at ensuring that the thing you're prepared for is the thing you thought you were preparing for. Otherwise, you model being prepared to pick locks by having lockpicks or a spell that can pick locks or produce or acquire lockpicks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T11:38:05-07:00","id":1552924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552923#post1552923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For mages this is just accomplished through time travel, quick reaction, and preparation, since the counterbalance of Mage's versatility is that they need to cast their spells to benefit from them; the alternative would be through Fate spells that happen to make something you saw or did earlier relevant, which isn't as good at ensuring that the thing you're prepared for is the thing you thought you were preparing for. Otherwise, you model being prepared to pick locks by having lockpicks or a spell that can pick locks or produce or acquire lockpicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how would you judge this spell? Time 4? Time 3 + Fate 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T12:20:15-07:00","id":1552925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552924#post1552924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how would you judge this spell? Time 4? Time 3 + Fate 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that the spell to have retroactively prepared for something is the one where you travel back in time and prepare for that something, frequent or long-term casting of the ones that lets you see the future, or the one where you got lucky and what happens is what you were prepared for, all of which are existing spells. Unless there is a different mechanical or narrative effect you have in mind, those are the tools at hand, unless your ST is very lenient with how they allow Alter History to be applied; &quot;I was retroactively prepared for this&quot; as a spell is kind of conceptually ruinous to the concept of a splat that needs lots of preparation for their biggest swings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T12:32:40-07:00","id":1552926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552925#post1552925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that the spell to have retroactively prepared for something is the one where you travel back in time and prepare for that something, frequent or long-term casting of the ones that lets you see the future, or the one where you got lucky and what happens is what you were prepared for, all of which are existing spells. Unless there is a different mechanical or narrative effect you have in mind, those are the tools at hand, unless your ST is very lenient with how they allow Alter History to be applied; &quot;I was retroactively prepared for this&quot; as a spell is kind of conceptually ruinous to the concept of a splat that needs lots of preparation for their biggest swings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a time 4 spell that lets you rewrite someones entire past including making a vampire human so this is not true.<br /> Im thinking of something smaller, lets rephrase it &quot;warn myself in the past that i will need X&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T12:53:37-07:00","id":1552927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552926#post1552926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a time 4 spell that lets you rewrite someones entire past including making a vampire human so this is not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>See again: &quot;unless your ST is very lenient with how they allow <s>Alter</s> Rewrite History to be applied.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Im thinking of something smaller, lets rephrase it &quot;warn myself in the past that i will need X&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And that's time travel, which needs to go through the mechanics of time travel. Either you prepare ahead of time or you go through the trouble of going back and redoing things so that you were prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T13:38:46-07:00","id":1552929,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Satchel;n1552928] See again: &quot;unless your ST is very lenient with how they allow <s>Alter</s> Rewrite History to be applied.&quot; /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I dont really get why would someone have to be lentient with using a offical rote effect from the main book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 08-05-2025, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T14:04:34-07:00","id":1552931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552929#post1552929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont really get why would someone have to be lentient with using a offical rote effect from the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a conversation in this thread immediately before you asked your question going over this and if you don't think there's an issue with using Rewrite History to retroactively have prepared for something you didn't know about before you cast the spell then I'm not sure why you would need a separate spell, but also that spell as written does not do anything to, for instance, bring tools into the scene that weren't already there; it still needs to contend with Temporal Sympathy to make changes from further back than the same scene or so, and without Reaching for Advanced Duration it's going to last a matter of seconds at most.<br /> <br /> Rewrite History lets you bring in a version of a target whose past went differently. This is broadly different from allowing you to have been wearing a bulletproof vest the whole time even though you weren't wearing one ten minutes ago \u2014 that kind of sleight of hand is the domain of supernatural powers with a metaphysical framework that supports them, like Embeds in Demon or Contracts in Changeling or Affinities or Utterances in Mummy, barring Atypical Attainments or weird Paradoxical quirks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T15:14:36-07:00","id":1552932,"title":"","content":"I admit i really dont see the issue. Rewriting someones history is way more powerful than geting a gun. And if you can rewrite a vampire to be human again you for sure can rewrite yourself to bring a lockpick just in case. My goal was to see if there is a simpler way to achive the effect that is in my opinion weaker and smaller in scale. Instead of time 4 maybe time2 + fate 2 or fate 3 +time 3.<br /> I never imagined that the fact this could be done would be contested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T16:29:06-07:00","id":1552934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552932#post1552932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit i really dont see the issue. Rewriting someones history is way more powerful than geting a gun. And if you can rewrite a vampire to be human again you for sure can rewrite yourself to bring a lockpick just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rewriting the vampire to be human again is temporary, requires two extra Reach, comes after the capacity to replace the vampire with their past self, which doesn't change the history of anything other than the character themselves nor create equipment out of nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My goal was to see if there is a simpler way to achive the effect that is in my opinion weaker and smaller in scale. Instead of time 4 maybe time2 + fate 2 or fate 3 +time 3.<br /> I never imagined that the fact this could be done would be contested. </div> </div> </div>To repeat:<br /> <br /> This is a game where the necessity of preparation is a major counterbalance to the power and versatility of its characters' toolkit. The consequences of impulsive and ill-considered actions are a substantial thematic point to the use of magic for a type of magician who is more likely to lose some of their ability to keep a leash on their magic from manslaughter than from planned murder. The ability to freely improvise effects within the scope of one's Ruling Arcana and use Praxes from other Arcana without spending Mana, coupled with the ability to cast any spell coming with the ability to cast it instantly with the basic free Reach, is one of the ways mages are meant to be able to dig themselves a hole they can't get out of. Spells from higher-rated Practices are less able to have their limits safely pushed even with the Reach of a Master provided by a Rote.<br /> <br /> All of this does not paint a picture where being able to never have to have a plan as long as you have this one spell as a Rote that gets three free Reaches doesn't immediately alter the setting around it unless it's the jealously guarded province of a paradoxically hyper-cautious secret society. You prepare by preparing, you do the legwork, or you scramble to fix the issue if neither is feasible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T20:02:38-07:00","id":1552940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552932#post1552932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never imagined that the fact this could be done would be contested.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not being contested, it's being contextualized.<br /> <br /> You can certainly do so, but the gist of it is that you can only do so if bringing the lock-picks would have been a reasonable course of action back them, as you don't really warn your past self, you bring about the version of yourself that did bring the lock-pick just in case.<br /> <br /> The vampire-turned-human isn't an extremely powerful example, it's an extremely circumstantial example. In some cases, what sealed the fate of a vampire-to-be was simply to be at the wrong place at the wrong time. The more someone's Embrace was &quot;fated&quot; to be, for example because the sire was grooming them for a long time before, the the less likely it is that Rewrite History will be able to affect this vampire.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if you do have a lock-pick at home and deciding to bring it was a reasonable idea, then by all means Rewrite History should work. But if you should go out of your way to have a lock-pick in the first place, and no reasonable line of thought in the past that would justify acquiring one, then it shouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T02:15:34-07:00","id":1552946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552940#post1552940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vampire-turned-human isn't an extremely powerful example, it's an extremely circumstantial example. In some cases, what sealed the fate of a vampire-to-be was simply to be at the wrong place at the wrong time. The more someone's Embrace was &quot;fated&quot; to be, for example because the sire was grooming them for a long time before, the the less likely it is that Rewrite History will be able to affect this vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That then becomes much harder to rewrite.<br /> <br /> If their sire groomed them, can you go back further and change something about them that caught their sire's eye?<br /> <br /> Do you need to know what the change should be or do you just decide the outcome you want and expect Time itself to sort out the details?<br /> <br /> If their Sire had been following their family l\u00edne for generations and picked them out because of some genetic quirk, do you instead have to target their (presumably long dead) parents? (So they are born without that genetic quirk)...<br /> <br /> All sound like reasonable limitations of rewrite history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T04:58:25-07:00","id":1552948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552946#post1552946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That then becomes much harder to rewrite.<br /> <br /> If their sire groomed them, can you go back further and change something about them that caught their sire's eye?<br /> <br /> Do you need to know what the change should be or do you just decide the outcome you want and expect Time itself to sort out the details?<br /> <br /> If their Sire had been following their family l\u00edne for generations and picked them out because of some genetic quirk, do you instead have to target their (presumably long dead) parents? (So they are born without that genetic quirk)...<br /> <br /> All sound like reasonable limitations of rewrite history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant you go around that with fate? Make fate pick the right things to rewrite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T06:35:12-07:00","id":1552949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552948#post1552948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cant you go around that with fate? Make fate pick the right things to rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is verging on Archmastery actually. <br /> <br /> That said, Dynamic spells are only needed when the spell need to change how it is acting in the instant, if it is a fixed effect on a fixed past, then you may get away with Patterning...<br /> <br /> But still, compared to Conditional Duration, this seems like a big ask to me.<br /> <br /> You can use Time however. Acombination of Postcognition and Prophecy should allow looking at alternate timeline that have no possibility... And then cast a Rewrite history to bring about that alternative you wanted... That is assuming you need to know the details of what you are doing rather than just the outcome (like you don't need to know the details inner workings of a modern printer to create one with Master of Matter, you just need to know the correct supernal symbols for a modern printer...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T06:55:21-07:00","id":1552950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552946#post1552946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That then becomes much harder to rewrite.<br /> <br /> If their sire groomed them, can you go back further and change something about them that caught their sire's eye?<br /> <br /> Do you need to know what the change should be or do you just decide the outcome you want and expect Time itself to sort out the details?<br /> <br /> If their Sire had been following their family l\u00edne for generations and picked them out because of some genetic quirk, do you instead have to target their (presumably long dead) parents? (So they are born without that genetic quirk)...<br /> <br /> All sound like reasonable limitations of rewrite history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rewrite History lets you adjust the target's history as you please past the selected divergence point (transforming someone into a supernatural being typically reducing their temporal sympathy with their mortal/Sleeper past self as low as the connection can go and you need a sympathy Yantra for the point of divergence). The operative problem with using this to have done other stuff is that the target's past is the only one that changes, meaning if you're affecting anything other than their body and mind and the possessions they have on them at the time of casting you need to include those things among the targets, because Rewrite History is not a time travel spell; you can temporarily replace someone with a version of themselves that went to college and lost an arm in a fishing accident, but you can't make that mean they now have their mom's old station wagon in their garage with its keys in their pocket without altering the history of that car and those keys as well, because the spell alters the history of its targets as they exist in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T10:56:55-07:00","id":1552955,"title":"","content":"Really, Rewrite History is somewhere between just a fanciful way of being able to transform an individual subject into a form they would have if circumstances in their past had been different (possibly with a bit of a contingent &quot;postcognition cast on them shows a fake past&quot; thing going on), and something that intersects with the larger cosmological premise that manipulation of time can let contradictory things be simultaneously true, such as how you can continue to exist despite having prevented your own birth.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I lean more towards the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T18:30:08-07:00","id":1552962,"title":"","content":"I think Rewrite History is better explained as &quot;simply&quot; dimension hopping: you're not changing the actual past, you're bringing an alternate version of the target from an alternative timeline.<br /> <br /> The corollary is that the timeline in question must &quot;exist&quot; on its own, so to speak, and you need to know the point of divergence enough to have an idea of which &quot;timelines&quot; to look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T22:05:40-07:00","id":1552970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552962#post1552962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Rewrite History is better explained as &quot;simply&quot; dimension hopping: you're not changing the actual past, you're bringing an alternate version of the target from an alternative timeline.<br /> <br /> The corollary is that the timeline in question must &quot;exist&quot; on its own, so to speak, and you need to know the point of divergence enough to have an idea of which &quot;timelines&quot; to look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this words it in a way that Mage's metaphysics of Time doesn't really interact with and makes the phenomenon sound broader than it is; as far as Awakened magic is concerned, alternate timelines that you can interact with don't concretely exist without something maintaining them like major Infrastructure, an Annunaki, or some other Mystery, with most conventional what-if products existing purely in the abstract possibility space to be queried with divination and prophecy or used as a basis for Making things. Time spells aren't engaging with parallel timelines in a sense where you could hypothetically produce a doppelganger of an existing person.<br /> <br /> To use a straightforward example, if you cast Rewrite History on a laptop, you can change the content of the files or the amount of wear and damage it's undergone, maybe even alter the marks someone made in permanent marker on the lid, but Rewrite History alone will not allow you to produce an external hard drive it didn't have or replace it with a completely different computer, because extra parts have their own histories that would need to be altered as well. You're altering the experiences the target has had since the divergence point, but the rest of the world does not change to adhere to those alterations without also being subjected to Rewrite History, and past a certain critical mass it becomes less troublesome to just go back in time normally or use Space and/or Matter if you need to put a bunch of pieces together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T01:13:06-07:00","id":1552974,"title":"","content":"How do time sympathetic connections work exactly? the descriptions in the book are unclear for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T03:14:25-07:00","id":1552976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552974#post1552974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do time sympathetic connections work exactly? the descriptions in the book are unclear for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is unclear? They work as connections between objects and a past version of themselves.<br /> <br /> You don't need a Sympathetic connection to (for example) look back as far as the unchanged past - though looking at the past of an object when it hasn't changed probably isn't actually useful, unless you can see other things changing around it.<br /> <br /> Beyond that you need a Temporal sympathy. And that then depends on how much they have changed, look at a mage who has just awakened, and they likely have a weak connection to the Mage they were just before awakening. So any attempt to use post cognition to look at them before their awakening will have the highest possible withstand.<br /> <br /> Look at the past of anything ancient, and the absolute further you can see is the last Lacuna where the world dramatically changed (to the point of breaking, the Sundering event is something Mages can't use time magic to research before... This is an event from Werewolf which changed the nature of the world, involving the death of a god).<br /> <br /> I guess a person's birth is also a Lacuna, you can't see back before the person was born. <br /> <br /> But everything in between is smaller or larger changes over time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T03:26:22-07:00","id":1552977,"title":"","content":"Thats what i wanted thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T12:55:22-07:00","id":1552984,"title":"","content":"Given that a thing cannot have temporal sympathy outside of itself, I think it's ultimately just a way of saying &quot;spells to see or affect the past are Withstood by the extent of how much they have changed over time&quot; that is rooted in some existing jargon.<br /> <br /> The main ambiguity that I read myself in the rules is what exactly constitutes a valid yantra to use for the temporal sympathy attainment. Personally, I'm inclined to be more restrictive with it than a straight reading might imply; the yantra needs to not only symbolise the spell's target, but the time period that you wish to work with. If you want to see a person's childhood, you need to have something evocative of them at that time.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, this is mostly because I want postcognition to be something that can't just readily solve mysteries by looking freely at the timeline of any person or place. You need to have an idea of where you're looking and something that can connect to that time. I would have it that this can be surprisingly tricky for times and places that don't really have anything obvious that would be symbolic of them, for how prosaic they are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1552962#post1552962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Rewrite History is better explained as &quot;simply&quot; dimension hopping: you're not changing the actual past, you're bringing an alternate version of the target from an alternative timeline.<br /> <br /> The corollary is that the timeline in question must &quot;exist&quot; on its own, so to speak, and you need to know the point of divergence enough to have an idea of which &quot;timelines&quot; to look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's just exchanging one complication re: whether or not a subject can be granted additional features or possessions for another one that is even bigger while also being less consequential.<br /> <br /> I also don't really care for the restriction it would place on the casting mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T07:11:35-07:00","id":1553060,"title":"","content":"What is the relationship, if any, between The Other, Aeon of Paradox in the Astral; and The Hermit of the Black Beach in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> The thematic associations are strong: friendly, old man of indistinct ethnicity, in the shore of a large endless waterbody of dissolution (Ocean of Oroboros, Ocean of Fragments).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T07:18:05-07:00","id":1553062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553060#post1553060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship, if any, between The Other, Aeon of Paradox in the Astral; and The Hermit of the Black Beach in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> The thematic associations are strong: friendly, old man of indistinct ethnicity, in the shore of a large endless waterbody of dissolution (Ocean of Oroboros, Ocean of Fragments).</div> </div> </div> </div>None that I am aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T09:17:41-07:00","id":1553064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553060#post1553060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship, if any, between The Other, Aeon of Paradox in the Astral; and The Hermit of the Black Beach in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> The thematic associations are strong: friendly, old man of indistinct ethnicity, in the shore of a large endless waterbody of dissolution (Ocean of Oroboros, Ocean of Fragments).</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked about the Hermit in February in the Geist AaSQ thread, but no one seemed to know.<br /> <br /> I'd need to reread the section, but as I remember it, if you read the original entry in Book of the Dead, the Hermit is a lot more distinct an idea from The Other than the Geist 2e core makes it seem.<br /> <br /> Complicating things, The Other is kinda meant to be Voormas from <i>Ascension</i>. (Probably not literally, but more of an easter egg).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T09:34:18-07:00","id":1553065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553064#post1553064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked about the Hermit in February in the Geist AaSQ thread, but no one seemed to know.<br /> <br /> I'd need to reread the section, but as I remember it, if you read the original entry in Book of the Dead, the Hermit is a lot more distinct an idea from The Other than the Geist 2e core makes it seem.<br /> <br /> Complicating things, The Other is kinda meant to be Voormas from <i>Ascension</i>. (Probably not literally, but more of an easter egg).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My current headcannon is that those two are the same being, with an overmind connecting them. As to the Voormas reference, I found that recently but yes, both would actually fit the entropic concept... At the spiritual ends, perhaps that the Other ban, he can not be destroyed / harmed without actually merging it with its underworld counterpart (and would that be a challenge) or perhaps both have to be taken at the same time.<br /> <br /> Just some mussing that I got going, not even related to my Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T10:26:34-07:00","id":1553066,"title":"","content":"I don't think they are that similar, the Ocean of Fragments is made for dissolving the memories of ghosts so they can finally let go a pass on (the good ending?) - the Hermit is sitting by presumably watching things enter the ocean, then picking the shores for interesting bits and pieces and maybe going for a swim when it has too much and dissolving some bits of himself (pretty sure the 1e write-up mentions him not having any way of knowing his original sex).<br /> <br /> The Abyss is a place of unreality, only things which don't exist are there, so becoming unreal and possibly leaving your Shell of a body as a conduit for unreality has a very different feel. The Old man of the Abyss, is more of a tempter, probably promises all the things which do exist only in the Abyss, all the possibility that can't be realised in the real world. He seems humble compared to the other Aeons, those that represent all of reality, while he merely represents things unreal.<br /> <br /> The Hermit seems to just be another ghost, the Old man of the Abyss is a dangerous Aeon trying to unmake reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-11-2025, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T20:05:50-07:00","id":1553081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553066#post1553066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Old man of the Abyss, is more of a tempter, probably promises all the things which do exist only in the Abyss, all the possibility that can't be realised in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, the Old Man actively discourages people from attempting to bargain with him.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery at least affirms that he does not represent the mad-god majesty of the Abyss but the void shorn of illusions to which people turn out of desperation, ambition, or morbid curiosity. Given that, I think his character would be very much one to try and convey that attempting to draw one's idealised reality out of the Abyss is a fool's errand, and he's otherwise unsentimental about it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as to the question, I think the only connection between them is a motif that happens to be able to express itself in a couple of different places. It is not alone in that in the cosmology of the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T21:49:59-07:00","id":1553082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553064#post1553064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complicating things, The Other is kinda meant to be Voormas from <i>Ascension</i>. (Probably not literally, but more of an easter egg).</div> </div> </div> </div>He <i>looks</i> like Voormas. The Aeon of the Abyss, astral reflection of impossibilities, appears in the form of a character from the wrong gameline.<br /> <br /> Astral Realms portrays the Other as not just spooky but ambiguously malign. He is friendly and never uses force, but he invites travellers to come into his hut and rest. No one who goes in the hut ever comes out, unless they come out in service to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> He's not portrayed as engaging in salesmanship or trying to tempt visitors, but if you come to him asking for a deal, he will make one, and I haven't read anything suggesting he would dissuade you, either. The Old Man isn't a tempter. He is <i>the temptation.</i> He has a hook, but it's your decision to come and snare yourself on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T06:36:54-07:00","id":1553090,"title":"","content":"&quot;Scelesti usually worship him from afar\u2014when they do it in person, he laughs at them. He never encourages anyone to surrender to the Abyss. Occasionally, he advises desperate pilgrims to run home. But he can\u2019t reject requests to act as the Void\u2019s advocate, and in that capacity he drives a very hard bargain.&quot;<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Elder Diadem specifically, he also straight up refuses unless you're a Scelestus Master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T06:40:52-07:00","id":1553091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553090#post1553090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Scelesti usually worship him from afar\u2014when they do it in person, he laughs at them. He never encourages anyone to surrender to the Abyss. Occasionally, he advises desperate pilgrims to run home. But he can\u2019t reject requests to act as the Void\u2019s advocate, and in that capacity he drives a very hard bargain.&quot;<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Elder Diadem specifically, he also straight up refuses unless you're a Scelestus Master.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would an Aswadim get from dealing with him? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T07:28:55-07:00","id":1553092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553091#post1553091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would an Aswadim get from dealing with him?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The same things regular archmages would get from dealing with the other Aeons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T08:08:35-07:00","id":1553094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553091#post1553091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would an Aswadim get from dealing with him?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you make it to archmastery and commit to being an Aswad without having ever been any of the forms of Traveler Scelesti, those forms basically don't offer you anything that's worth the cost anymore. (Not that they're really worth the cost to Travelers either. But an archmaster isn't really going to be tempted by the Elder Diadem.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T08:12:34-07:00","id":1553095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553091#post1553091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would an Aswadim get from dealing with him?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He could retrieve knowledge and corrupted Artifacts lost to the Abyss, or locate those buried in some forgotten corner of the Tapestry. He could create a custom Abyssal being to help bring about your plans. He could, as the Aeon of the Abyss, grant you the use of an Imperial level working of the Abyss, at one level higher and requiring no Quintessence. He could do all that, but instead he sighs, shakes his head and sets a high price. He hopes to dissuade you with it, but you won't be turned away. That is fine, in time you will sink into the Abyss, it's just a matter of how much you push it's agenda before you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:34:56-07:00","id":1553107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553091#post1553091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would an Aswadim get from dealing with him?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries offers the novel idea that the Old Man can act as a guarantor of neutral ground for meetings between Aswadim and other archmages (and perhaps facilitate interaction with Travellers that are similarly not affiliated with the Abyss).<br /> <br /> Still, for the most part, I think the point about engaging as archmasters do with any Aeon is on point. The capabilities of the Aeons and their willingness to offer it up does not change. What matters is that, as a being of godlike power oneself, one has a capacity to interact with them as a peer, a more sophisticated idea of what boons from the Aeons could be applied towards, and greater ability to offer goods and services in return.<br /> <br /> For an Aswadim, I'd say that the knowledge, powers, and beings that can be drawn from the Abyss are about the same as they would be for any mage. The most significant difference is in application (since Aswadim have a very specific agenda of using the infinity of the Abyss to reshape the finite to their aspirations). Apart from that, I would suggest that the capabilities and position of respect might mean that the Old Man is more willing to take payment in a form that is external to the mage, rather than inflicting the Abyss through their pattern.<br /> <br /> I'd find it fitting if, a lot of the time, the Old Man wants things that bring complications or obstacles to fulfilling the Obsession that is the point of bargaining in the first place. This isn't done as some kind of monkey's paw thing, or out of malice; it's just an expression of paradox. A lot of the time he might actually be upfront about exactly what they're being asked to spend, the consequences it will have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T00:56:34-07:00","id":1553126,"title":"","content":"If a mage would be trying to create something that is requiring a lot of power. Then let's say he though magic or science creates something capable of creating such power but in short burst before it runs out. Could he make a mana battery out of this item and with this make sure that as long as the mana is there the power will still be there ready for the use? <br /> In a nutshell I want to create a Tony Stark mini arc reactor. But I am wondering how to do it. Having Matter 3, Death 1 and Prime 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T02:50:09-07:00","id":1553127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553126#post1553126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage would be trying to create something that is requiring a lot of power. Then let's say he though magic or science creates something capable of creating such power but in short burst before it runs out. Could he make a mana battery out of this item and with this make sure that as long as the mana is there the power will still be there ready for the use?<br /> In a nutshell I want to create a Tony Stark mini arc reactor. But I am wondering how to do it. Having Matter 3, Death 1 and Prime 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally mana have no interaction with mundane engines.<br /> As for Sign of Sorcery you could:<br /> -create an eternal electrical battery spell with force 3 (indefinite duration)<br /> -create a tank that auto refill fuel with a spell of matter 4 (indefinite duration)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T03:56:00-07:00","id":1553130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553127#post1553127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally mana have no interaction with mundane engines.<br /> As for Sign of Sorcery you could:<br /> -create an eternal electrical battery spell with force 3 (indefinite duration)<br /> -create a tank that auto refill fuel with a spell of matter 4 (indefinite duration)</div> </div> </div> </div>would it not be possible to charge the item with ether as demons do or something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T05:01:39-07:00","id":1553131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553130#post1553130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would it not be possible to charge the item with ether as demons do or something similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use Fate + Prime Ruling to move Aether or angelic Essence from vessel to vessel or Weaving with the same Arcana to convert between Essence and Aether, but given the requirements for an object to serve as a stockpile and the inability to shut it down without removing the Aether, to say nothing of the typical elementary nature of Awakened spellcasting meaning the ability to do one thing another monster can do as a template feature does not necessarily imply a neighboring ability, it's generally going to be less contentious to use the established Arcana for giving something the spell's Duration in unlimited fuel or power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T06:44:28-07:00","id":1553132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553131#post1553131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use Fate + Prime Ruling to move Aether or angelic Essence from vessel to vessel or Weaving with the same Arcana to convert between Essence and Aether, but given the requirements for an object to serve as a stockpile and the inability to shut it down without removing the Aether, to say nothing of the typical elementary nature of Awakened spellcasting meaning the ability to do one thing another monster can do as a template feature does not necessarily imply a neighboring ability, it's generally going to be less contentious to use the established Arcana for giving something the spell's Duration in unlimited fuel or power.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is not in the Core book, I default to assuming that most mages don't know that they can do this. I would allow a player to research, look at their local Mysterium records, and spend significant time in-game to figure it out (or more risky, find an Angel/demon and actively monitor them, use focused Mage sight to see what happens with Aether...).<br /> <br /> But I would never just let a player say &quot;oh it is a Fate + Prime ruling spell, and no I can weild the power of a demon&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a node with the right resonance can power an electrical device pretty much indefinitely... Which is in the Mage core, so I would be happy with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a mage would be trying to create something that is requiring a lot of power. Then let's say he though magic or science creates something capable of creating such power but in short burst before it runs out. Could he make a mana battery out of this item and with this make sure that as long as the mana is there the power will still be there ready for the use?<br /> In a nutshell I want to create a Tony Stark mini arc reactor. But I am wondering how to do it. Having Matter 3, Death 1 and Prime 2. </div> </div> </div>The issue with my node solution above is that the device needs to be stationary.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 probably isn't enough, thigh alter condictivity might help with making a super conductor or indeed a super capacitor... (Since you can mess with the condictivity of an object without relying on Forces...)<br /> <br /> Ultimately the fiction of Iron Man doesn't explain what the fuel source for the mini ar reactor is (is he doing fusion with a special type of catalyst? In which case, cool, now where does he store the fuel on his suit?).<br /> <br /> I suspect Deviant is more convienant for making something like that... But in Mage... Well do magic, maybe?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T07:04:37-07:00","id":1553133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553132#post1553132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it is not in the Core book, I default to assuming that most mages don't know that they can do this. I would allow a player to research, look at their local Mysterium records, and spend significant time in-game to figure it out (or more risky, find an Angel/demon and actively monitor them, use focused Mage sight to see what happens with Aether...).<br /> <br /> But I would never just let a player say &quot;oh it is a Fate + Prime ruling spell, and no I can weild the power of a demon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, great. Study and reasonable justification for the character believing they have the knowledge and capability to do something are kind of standard sanity-checks, particularly when dealing with an uncommon supernatural fuel type.<br /> <br /> As an answer to a plain rules question I think the bigger issue is &quot;there is nothing to suggest that making Aether stockpiles run indefinitely is an intrinsic quality of Aether rather than part of the Unchained ability to turn objects that are powered for operation into Aether stockpiles,&quot; because if the God-Machine's waste heat had perpetual motion as an incidental side-effect a decent amount of its projects probably wouldn't need as much logistical upkeep.<br /> <br /> If the intention is for the character to start with this reactor it's broadly outside the scope of the described Arcana ratings and would likely need an Artifact or an Imbued Item; simply making a battery able to retain stored energy for an indefinite period of time feels within spec for a Perfecting spell of Matter like Alter Conductivity, though investing in Forces is still going to have better returns on the &quot;having enough power for a mobile device at any given time&quot; front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T07:37:37-07:00","id":1553134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553133#post1553133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, great. Study and reasonable justification for the character believing they have the knowledge and capability to do something are kind of standard sanity-checks, particularly when dealing with an uncommon supernatural fuel type.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\udc4d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an answer to a plain rules question I think the bigger issue is &quot;there is nothing to suggest that making Aether stockpiles run indefinitely is an intrinsic quality of Aether rather than part of the Unchained ability to turn objects that are powered for operation into Aether stockpiles,&quot; because if the God-Machine's waste heat had perpetual motion as an incidental side-effect a decent amount of its projects probably wouldn't need as much logistical upkeep. </div> </div> </div>That actually raises an interesting question, though it is not a Mage one, ie if Demons have this ability and they learned how to use their abilities based on their knowledge from being Angels, then why can't the God-Machine do this too... But that is an aside. <br /> <br /> And I still think Mages have easier routes to the same destination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the intention is for the character to start with this reactor it's broadly outside the scope of the described Arcana ratings and would likely need an Artifact or an Imbued Item; simply making a battery able to retain stored energy for an indefinite period of time feels within spec for a Perfecting spell of Matter like Alter Conductivity, though investing in Forces is still going to have better returns on the &quot;having enough power for a mobile device at any given time&quot; front. </div> </div> </div>The problem with Sciening it out, is mostly &quot;this is not how magic works&quot;. <br /> <br /> In theory you could take a Super-conducting go solid and push current into it until it is storing a huge amount of energy, but A) it is not unlimited and B) releasing it on demand might be difficult... <br /> <br /> Instead of just using Matter 5 to Make and Arc reactor from nothing (or a Patterning spell to create the right properties from something you already have access to). If you want serious magic-tech, you could try some kind of portable essence source which converts the essence into electricity - a locus which is small enough to carry around...<br /> <br /> (Ignoring the fact that the Mage writers seem to think a Locus is a location, not an object).<br /> <br /> I think a sligthly cursed item which dates energy from some other sources would be interesting, like the Underworld, or mana from the Supernal, or wherever... But what makes the most narrative sense for the game in question? That requires talking to your storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T08:16:45-07:00","id":1553135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553134#post1553134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Sciening it out, is mostly &quot;this is not how magic works&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic doesn't have to work on scientific principles, but you can still use magic to affect things in a technological fashion; making a battery that doesn't lose its stored energy over time is less overall effective than simply giving unlimited power to a battery-powered object, but it's still something that can be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Ignoring the fact that the Mage writers seem to think a Locus is a location, not an object). </div> </div> </div>Because for the purposes of Mage's mechanics, a locus <i>is</i> the area of influence around the focal object or person in which the Gauntlet is thinner, compatible spirits heal faster, and Reaching can be done without the Manifestation of the same name.<br /> <br /> Werewolf itself specifies that even if the focal point of a locus is destroyed, unless the Essence it contained is quickly removed from the Resonant area it will settle into a new item in a few weeks; Lore of the Forsaken notes that the heart of a locus isn't readily discernible from the pale around it, and its section on non-standard loci, while partially outdated due to the introduction of the Waystone Wolf-Blooded Tell in 2e (which is nevertheless just a &quot;for the purposes of Reaching&quot; locus), notes that most locuses are part of the location they're in and don't move the boundaries of their area of effect with the relocation of the heart on an immediate timescale, as well as forwarding the concept of a &quot;locus of place&quot; that has no division between its core and area of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T14:11:36-07:00","id":1553522,"title":"","content":"Would the Death Arcana allow you to be able to use a Deathmask to some benefit? Maybe as an anchor or something to that effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T15:14:05-07:00","id":1553527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553522#post1553522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Death Arcana allow you to be able to use a Deathmask to some benefit? Maybe as an anchor or something to that effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to any special degree. As a Memento, you could use it as a +2 tool Yantra for spells that align with the resonance of its Key or Space spells that utilize Keys, and you could give it to a ghost to turn them into whatever Reaper corresponds with that Deathmask, but as far as benefiting spellcasting it's not mechanically different than any other Memento.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T03:19:26-07:00","id":1553535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553527#post1553527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to any special degree. As a Memento, you could use it as a +2 tool Yantra for spells that align with the resonance of its Key or Space spells that utilize Keys, and you could give it to a ghost to turn them into whatever Reaper corresponds with that Deathmask, but as far as benefiting spellcasting it's not mechanically different than any other Memento.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also use focused Mage sight to observe what happens when a ghost puts it on, and gain an arcane beat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T04:36:23-07:00","id":1553587,"title":"","content":"About Demesne and Verges as Yantras<br /> <br /> Pag 120 seems to indicate that Demesne bonuses can boost all spells that have semiotic association no matter what arcana, and that Verge bonuses can boost all spells of the associated Ruling Arcanas (if they don t use also the inferior Arcana) ignoring semiotic association.<br /> <br /> Pag 243 instead seems to indicate that both semiotic and arcana limitations are true for both places (and drops the inferior arcana limitation)<br /> <br /> What is the correct interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-02T15:14:52-07:00","id":1553595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553587#post1553587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pag 120 seems to indicate that Demesne bonuses can boost all spells that have semiotic association no matter what arcana, and that Verge bonuses can boost all spells of the associated Ruling Arcanas (if they don t use also the inferior Arcana) ignoring semiotic association.<br /> <br /> Pag 243 instead seems to indicate that both semiotic and arcana limitations are true for both places (and drops the inferior arcana limitation)<br /> <br /> What is the correct interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 243. The overriding rule of Yantras is that symbolism matters and Demesnes are functionally artificial Verges that can be more reliably engineered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T03:13:36-07:00","id":1553605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553595#post1553595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 243. The overriding rule of Yantras is that symbolism matters and Demesnes are functionally artificial Verges that can be more reliably engineered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering this, if i understand it rightly the main advantage of the Prelacy merit Temple are:<br /> -An extra free Reach if Sleepers are in the Sancta or for spell targeting outside the borders<br /> -Allied Supernal entities as &quot;guardians&quot;<br /> -As a Verge the Sancta and its Supernal guardians are immune to Dissonance<br /> Versus<br /> -one less Arcana can use the Verge as yantra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T05:21:12-07:00","id":1553606,"title":"","content":"It feels like the rules are inconsistent.<br /> <br /> Pg 120 mentions the semiotics and type of spell (not Arcanum) - based on typical order use of a Demense<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Arrow\u2019s training room helps with spells involving duels, preparation for battle, and self-mastery.<br /> A Guardian\u2019s Veiled Room helps with spells of disguise, misdirection, and uncovering truths. </div> </div> </div>While a verge is described as being useful for any type of spell so long as it uses one of the ruling arcana of the associated watchtower.<br /> <br /> But then on pg 243, the verge and Demense are described as having the same rules regarding Semiotics. With <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Stygian Verge that\u2019s filled <br /> with metal but no aspects of Death won\u2019t help a mage bind ghosts, but will help him create strange alloys. </div> </div> </div>Which is inconsistent with what was described previously, and it is unclear whether the naturally occurring supernal phenomena (in a verge but not a Demense) are sufficient to provide the environmental Yantra bonus.<br /> <br /> From the examples, it doesn't make it clear, whether a Demense made from multiple soulstones from different paths, can be used to give a bonus any of the ruling arcana of those paths, but you need to decorate them with the appropriate semiotics (where the examples seem to be order dependant not path), or if verges are more limited in Arcana but come with path aligned phenomena to balance that out... <br /> <br /> Do you need a Demense to be aligned toward Order related things? Or can you just make use a Moros Soulstone and fill the Demense with metals to invoke Matter? Rules unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T06:53:43-07:00","id":1553607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553606#post1553606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the examples, it doesn't make it clear, whether a Demense made from multiple soulstones from different paths, can be used to give a bonus any of the ruling arcana of those paths, but you need to decorate them with the appropriate semiotics (where the examples seem to be order dependant not path), or if verges are more limited in Arcana but come with path aligned phenomena to balance that out...</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from the &quot;things from 1e that aren't contradicted by things from 2e still hold&quot; heuristic, a demesne with multiple soul stones benefits the Arcana of all the included soul stones, as constrained by its semiotics as a location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you need a Demense to be aligned toward Order related things? Or can you just make use a Moros Soulstone and fill the Demense with metals to invoke Matter? Rules unclear. </div> </div> </div>The Demesne benefits spells it's symbolically outfitted to benefit, which Order mages tend to have incentives to steer toward the focuses of their Orders. Supernal Verges likewise set the semiotics of their benefits by the nature of the phenomena that the manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T10:37:03-07:00","id":1553609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553607#post1553607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going from the &quot;things from 1e that aren't contradicted by things from 2e still hold&quot; heuristic, a demesne with multiple soul stones benefits the Arcana of all the included soul stones, as constrained by its semiotics as a location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the limitations of each soul stone (ie not being able to use the inferior Arcanum).<br /> <br /> Would this mean a 5 path Demense could use all but the 5 inferior arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T14:32:08-07:00","id":1553610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553609#post1553609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the limitations of each soul stone (ie not being able to use the inferior Arcanum).<br /> <br /> Would this mean a 5 path Demense could use all but the 5 inferior arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disregard the Inferior Arcanum restriction, given it's not repeated outside of the Yantras section, pretty much every reference link points to page 243, typical demesnes in 1e had no effects relating to their Inferior Arcana, and the part about the Inferior Arcana is only in the Yantras section describing Supernal Verges to begin with. Demesnes and Verges provide their bonus to semiotically suitable spells that utilize their Ruling Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T04:24:18-07:00","id":1553621,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">orathaic</a> I think the idea is that normal demesne take on the positive aspects of a verge, whilst annulities make use of the negative ones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An annulity is a space that defines itself by its soul stones\u2019 Inferior Arcana, suppressing their effects within its borders as a sort of anti-Demesne. </div> </div> </div><i>Signs of Sorcery, pg.89</i><br /> <br /> To me that implies a demesne is defined by the Ruling Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T05:27:50-07:00","id":1553622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553610#post1553610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disregard the Inferior Arcanum restriction, given it's not repeated outside of the Yantras section, pretty much every reference link points to page 243, typical demesnes in 1e had no effects relating to their Inferior Arcana, and the part about the Inferior Arcana is only in the Yantras section describing Supernal Verges to begin with. Demesnes and Verges provide their bonus to semiotically suitable spells that utilize their Ruling Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didn't realise that it is Verge's Yantra section that mentions the inferior Arcanum, not Demense's, it is the more detailed version on 243 which says they work the same.<br /> <br /> Except there is says a Demense is limited to the Mage's Sanctum (which could be inferred as requiring a safe place over the pre-reqs for the Merit).<br /> <br /> But I tend to assume that is fluff, rather than a strict mechanical requirement.<br /> <br /> The other difference is the Yantra sections says &quot;any spell that uses [mind or space] can be used to draw upon the [Pandemonic] Verge's power&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that this versatility is why they are valuable, contrasting the Demense needing to be a &quot;Guardian's veiled room helping with spells of disguise...&quot; <br /> <br /> Whereas 243 is just like &quot;they work the same&quot;. <br /> <br /> I fear different authors wrote these different parts and semiotics got ignored.<br /> <br /> But I feel a Verge should be strictly mechanically better (with Temple to an Exarch getting some of those benefits...) which is why I suggested limiting a Demense based on the inferior Arcanum (that is clearly not RaW, my bad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-04T05:59:40-07:00","id":1553623,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna propose that a Demesne can technically be enchanted anywhere, but most places will lack the semiotic details to make that actually useful. The place you turn into a demesne typically has to be prepared to accommodate it beforehand, and the level of control one has to prepare a place as a ritual casting space is usually a sanctum by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T15:56:01-07:00","id":1553687,"title":"","content":"If someone is casting a spell sympathetically at you and you have Mage Sight up , do you have the ability to counterspell them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T17:22:39-07:00","id":1553689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553687#post1553687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone is casting a spell sympathetically at you and you have Mage Sight up , do you have the ability to counterspell them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;By the time a spell takes effect and a mage feels it in Peripheral Mage Sight, though, it's too late to counter; to use this Attainment, <b>the countering mage must see her rival</b> casting in Active Mage Sight.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that the caster is casting sympathetically while in view of you, you can use Counterspell, but otherwise the spell doesn't exist yet; there's no Awakened spellcasting equivalent to Blood Sorcery's &quot;between the sacrifice at the start and the conclusion of the extended roll, a target vampire can tell someone is using a blood sorcery ritual on them and take steps to boost their resistance.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-07T18:57:18-07:00","id":1553690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think there's something somewhere elaborating that the basis of Active Mage Sight allowing one to counterspell is that the mage can see another's Immediate Nimbus forming as they cast the spell. Sympathetic casting doesn't seem like it would have any equivalent, so there's no way to communicate the spellcasting to somebody that would want to counter it.<br /> <br /> I would observe that as far as I can tell, Second Edition removed any premise of a visible &quot;sympathetic window&quot; that was used both in First Edition as a basis to definitively tell that a sympathetic spell had been cast and allowed one to cast back through the connection even without sympathy to the mage on the other end. So that's one less element that could be used to justify countermagic there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T00:06:41-07:00","id":1553701,"title":"","content":"how do organizations in nwod in general keep from becoming global? Whats the reason preventing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 09-09-2025, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T01:39:55-07:00","id":1553702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553701#post1553701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hod do organizations in nwod in general keep from becoming global? Whats the reason preventing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing really. There are quite a lot of global organisations. Though it does depend what you mean by 'global', and that shouldn't necessarily be seen as synonymous with being powerful.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking though, there's no centralised state with a bureaucracy to act as intermediary between the monsters of the CofD. Therefore, most of the monster societies are based on personal ties which kinda only really works for a relatively small area. That's not to say those kinds of organisation don't become bigger, but they also become more brittle and liable to splinter with that expansion.<br /> <br /> The organisations that are able to maintain a global presence for long periods of time are generally either highly decentralised as the Pentacle, or are backed by some metaphysical force that keeps them inline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T02:03:57-07:00","id":1553703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553623#post1553623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna propose that a Demesne can technically be enchanted anywhere, but most places will lack the semiotic details to make that actually useful. The place you turn into a demesne typically has to be prepared to accommodate it beforehand, and the level of control one has to prepare a place as a ritual casting space is usually a sanctum by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fair, in my head a Sanctum is a personal investment and you could have a group (order or Consilium) which hosts a Demense, which isn't technically anyone's Sanctum...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T04:40:21-07:00","id":1553705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553701#post1553701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do organizations in nwod in general keep from becoming global? Whats the reason preventing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> said, nothing. If it makes sense for them to go global, they go global, and actually a lot of them did.<br /> <br /> That said, this doesn't necessarily mean a lot. As in real organizations, local branches have more to do with local occurrences than with overarching plots. Not that those don't happen, but they're not standard fare. A global organization is more likely to be able to bring resources from other places to bear if they need, but local organizations usually have a firmer grasp on local power dynamics, so it's kind of a trade-off.<br /> <br /> In the end there's little difference between a global or local organization in most places, most of the time. Global orgs will be present through local branches with mostly local resources or a limited supply of foreign resources, and local connections to help them acclimate. Local orgs are perfectly able of pulling connections if needed to act on a global stage if needed, that's not as hard as it seems. And in fact, any supernatural nature of the organization has no bearing in this aspect, save for the odd otherworldly branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T05:05:55-07:00","id":1553706,"title":"","content":"Mage in particular has been able to organise pretty globally for as long as there has been mages (mostly via the Astral, meeting and sharing knowledge without physically being in the same place, overcoming language barriers with idea, but accessible to any Mage who knows about the Temenos...)<br /> <br /> Which likely helped the proto-Seers of the Throne organise. <br /> <br /> Rapt seem unlikely to organise on any scale. Neither do Banishers (though I care very little for Banishers). The Tremere might have a global scale, but are likely busy hiding/erasing their presence...<br /> <br /> Most mages are busy with their personal Obsessions, and only interested in global events if it leads them to further their study. Sure some might be interested in Order aswell, and that can have global consequences, but usually that can make up an Obsession aswell. Fundamentally Mages are written as addicts, addicted to mysteries, and most mysteries aren't global. <br /> <br /> The God-Machine as an Obsession is liable to drive most Mages Rapt if the pursue it deeply (or killed/assimilated by Angels). Similar issues with the Judges, or trying to fix the Underworld (Reapers probably aren't the only agents working for the Chthonic Gods).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T05:26:05-07:00","id":1553707,"title":"","content":"What dice pool do additional casters roll for teamwork rituals? (It says &quot;as usual&quot;, but that means you can engineer a situation where partial supporting casters provide more help than full supportive casters...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T09:05:02-07:00","id":1553708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553707#post1553707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What dice pool do additional casters roll for teamwork rituals? (It says &quot;as usual&quot;, but that means you can engineer a situation where partial supporting casters provide more help than full supportive casters...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Teamwork rules are defined in the section on Page 214 cited in the writeup, which does not contain the words &quot;as usual.&quot; You use the same Traits in your dicepool as a secondary actor as the primary actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T11:22:21-07:00","id":1553709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553706#post1553706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage in particular has been able to organise pretty globally for as long as there has been mages (mostly via the Astral, meeting and sharing knowledge without physically being in the same place, overcoming language barriers with idea, but accessible to any Mage who knows about the Temenos...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral Realms might have their value as a forum for large scale organisation, but I think that's only the first step in actually getting people together to utilise it for such. I think that under most circumstances, it's been no more useful for that than any physical place owing to the more significant obstacles of &quot;getting people from across a wide range to be able to commit to a time and place to meet, and having a formal agenda for doing so&quot;.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, mages aren't really organised globally so much as they exist globally. It's possible for people from a variety of areas to have common cause so long as there's an underlying ideology and series of customs that they can hold together. Probably, this has historically meant that when mages venture far from home, they can encounter fellows with whom they can still identify, without anybody needing to have told them to work together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which likely helped the proto-Seers of the Throne organise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest thing that helped the numerous disparate Exarch cults coalesce into the Seers of the Throne was the fact that the Ministry of Hegemony was able to form and promote an ideology on them doing so, followed extremely closely by the factors of &quot;they have more archmasters who are more tightly bound together and supplied with a lot of infrastructure to provide centralised points of contact&quot; and &quot;they can be organised by afar through the Mystery Commands and omens of the Exarchs&quot;.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if the Seers were inclined to be introspective, they might wonder if it's more significant to have the chantry palaces of the high ministers or the distributed presence of prelates who are all taking their marching orders from the same source as a coordinating element.<br /> <br /> Either way, those are assets to make them truly function as a global system that many others lack.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T12:03:57-07:00","id":1553712,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">orathaic</a> To be clear, are you asking about yantra? Like, do secondary participants apply yantra?<br /> <br /> Personally, I <i>suspect </i>it's meant to be a pure <u>gnosis+arcana</u> for mages that could cast the spell independently, and <u>Gnosis-3</u> for those with merely the correct arcana of a lower level. Like, the spell teamwork rules on pg.119 don't mention yantra and the core mage line is IMO very conservative with bonus dice. Plus, a teamwork bonus won't contribute to the yantra limit.<br /> <br /> That said, if we take a literal reading of the text, it does seem as if secondary participants are allowed to use their own yantra. It would also make sense for low Gnosis mages who otherwise are kinda a liability.<br /> <br /> There're also some rules in <i>Signs of Sorcery pg.55</i> that modify secondary teamwork rolls depending on how co-ordinated the mages are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:03:40-07:00","id":1553716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553712#post1553712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">orathaic</a> To be clear, are you asking about yantra? Like, do secondary participants apply yantra?<br /> <br /> Personally, I <i>suspect </i>it's meant to be a pure <u>gnosis+arcana</u> for mages that could cast the spell independently, and <u>Gnosis-3</u> for those with merely the correct arcana of a lower level. Like, the spell teamwork rules on pg.119 don't mention yantra and the core mage line is IMO very conservative with bonus dice. Plus, a teamwork bonus won't contribute to the yantra limit.<br /> <br /> That said, if we take a literal reading of the text, it does seem as if secondary participants are allowed to use their own yantra. It would also make sense for low Gnosis mages who otherwise are kinda a liability.<br /> <br /> There're also some rules in <i>Signs of Sorcery pg.55</i> that modify secondary teamwork rolls depending on how co-ordinated the mages are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am asking what they roll.<br /> <br /> Here are some answers i have gotten elsewhere:<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras - spell factors<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras (but they get to set their own spell factors, so might as well leave them at 0 penalties)<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum (?+ Willpower?)<br /> <br /> I have my preference between those 3 possibilities, but I wanted a simply question, and to see what answers people give.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, I like the SoS rules, but they don't really clarify my question. The +1/+2 bonus or -2 penalty for coordination is great, and having it become dice pool +2 is a nice little addition - especially for the Initiate who is rolling Gnosis -3 (+2 for coordination?)<br /> <br /> Basically I want a step by step guide.<br /> <br /> Like<br /> Step 3. Decide your spell factors,<br /> Step 4. each ritual participant rolls the [dice pool] <br /> Step 5. Figure out if you are rolling a chance die or if the participants actually managed to get you up to rolling non-chance die...<br /> <br /> Or something similar. Ideally it would lean into the risk of failure vs power of spell factors decision which Mage's spellcasting system is at its core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  adding context to my answer. 09-09-2025, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:22:30-07:00","id":1553717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553716#post1553716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am asking what they roll.<br /> <br /> Here are some answers i have gotten elsewhere:<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras - spell factors<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum + yantras (but they get to set their own spell factors, so might as well leave them at 0 penalties)<br /> Gnosis + Arcanum (?+ Willpower?)<br /> <br /> I have my preference between those 3 possibilities, but I wanted a simply question, and to see what answers people give.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, I hadn't even considered spell factors... I mean, that maybe adds weight to what I suggested? Like, gnosis+arcana alone is probably not going to make or break a spell whilst also being simpler to run.<br /> <br /> Then again, that's pure vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:23:53-07:00","id":1553718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553708#post1553708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Teamwork rules are defined in the section on Page 214 cited in the writeup, which does not contain the words &quot;as usual.&quot; You use the same Traits in your dicepool as a secondary actor as the primary actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So per the rules on page 214, everyone rolls the same dice pool - that would be Gnosis + Arcanum + Yantras - Spell factors (more of less)? And then if one full participation gets at least a single success the leader gets a bonus for?<br /> <br /> Why, in that case, would you not just have those capable of full participation just roll their own spell, and not risk getting paradox released into any of the spells? Only 1 success needed usually suggests there is no benefit to doing ritual teamwork spellcasting at all (since everyone has to have at least -5 dice pool... You are better off with each of them casting seperately than risking a dramatic failure from a chance die...)<br /> <br /> Seperately, if the secondary casters who do not meet the Arcanum requirements are just rolling [Gnosis -3] (without spell factors or yantras, which is how I have always read that section, but maybe that is wrong) then they are also strictly better than a full participant who rolls only a chance die...which seems contrary to the spirit of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:32:45-07:00","id":1553720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553717#post1553717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOL, I hadn't even considered spell factors... I mean, that maybe adds weight to what I suggested? Like, gnosis+arcana alone is probably not going to make or break a spell whilst also being simpler to run.<br /> <br /> Then again, that's pure vibes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I have my preference, and I'm really trying to see if there is a good argument either way for this being how anyone else read the rules, or if I should just insist on it as a house rule when I am running Mage.<br /> <br /> I think adding Yantras (without subtracting spell factors) is OP and unbalanced - in the sense that yantras are there to balance out the spell factor penalties.<br /> <br /> I think Adding Yantras *and* spell factors is just pointless (most characters will then be rolling a chance die, or since you have decided the spell factors in advance, everyone is succeeding independently, and you're getting a decent spell pool bonus, but you never get to invest those dice in extra spell factors... So you might aswell not have any helpers) <br /> <br /> So I am 100% onboard having them just roll Gnosis + Arcanum (+willpower, cause most rolls let you add willpower). <br /> <br /> That makes full participants strictly better than (what I think of as the untrained pentaly of -3) secondary casters who don't meet the full Arcanum requirements.<br /> <br /> With the +1/2 for coordination from SoS as a nice addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:44:50-07:00","id":1553721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> Come to think of it, willpower probably saves it. Like, that untrained penalty <i>is</i> brutal, but it precisely matches a willpower spend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T15:08:04-07:00","id":1553722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553718#post1553718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in that case, would you not just have those capable of full participation just roll their own spell, and not risk getting paradox released into any of the spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Teamwork bonus isn't a Yantra bonus and is therefore uncapped, is the thing that immediately springs to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T16:08:13-07:00","id":1553723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553722#post1553722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teamwork bonus isn't a Yantra bonus and is therefore uncapped, is the thing that immediately springs to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That cap is only after taking spell factor penalties into account, right? (and before released paradox penalties, if any...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-09-2025, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T18:16:34-07:00","id":1553726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553723#post1553723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That cap is only after taking spell factor penalties into account, right? (and before released paradox penalties, if any...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean more in the sense that you are limited in how many Yantras you can benefit from but you are not limited in how many bonus dice from teamwork you can benefit from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T22:20:47-07:00","id":1553728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553726#post1553726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean more in the sense that you are limited in how many Yantras you can benefit from but you are not limited in how many bonus dice from teamwork you can benefit from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but let's take an example.<br /> <br /> You have a dice pool of 4, (after all of the yantras, ritual durations, willpower, whatever else is accounted for).<br /> <br /> You have one assistant who has one less gnosis and one less of the relevant Arcanum. So they have a dice pool of 2, right?<br /> <br /> Either they fail (and in two dice that is 50/50), in which case you added some paradox risk for no gain. Or they succeed, in which case they could have simply cast the spell seperately and given the full effect to the imago.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you really want to push things. So you go to -1. Your assistant is at -3.<br /> <br /> Now you get a there more assistants, and hope that all of them rolling chance die. You hope that they roll enough successes to bring you up to more than a chance die and get a real shot at successfully casting the spell - you are in the same situation as above, except now you risk them getting a dramatic failure and giving you a -4 penalty (according to the teamwork rules).<br /> <br /> Again, you are better off having everyone cast seperately and hoping one person succeeds.<br /> <br /> Alternatively (and it has been pointed out to me that this may be me misreading the rules), if you have assistants who don't have the require Arcanum dots just roll [Gnosis -3] (possobly adding willpower) - without adding yantras or subtracting spell factors - then you could have a Gnosis 5 character actually adding to your chances of having a better than chance die dice pool (when they can't simply cast it by themselves). But this makes assistants who aren't full participants better than assistants who are full secondary casters.<br /> <br /> So that is arguably not the rules as intended.<br /> <br /> So finally i conclude, you should have every secondary caster rolls [Gnosis + Arcanum/Gnosis -3] add those dice to your dice pool after deciding spell factors (or possibly before deciding spell factors) - so you are playing in to the risk of failure vs getting the most bang for your buck, but now you are risking being on a chance die and hoping the secondary casters add enough dice to get a real chance of success.<br /> <br /> And I'm happy that this house rule incentives ritual teamwork without making it either pointless or massively overpowered (which I think is that case if you let the secondary casters roll Gnosis + Arcanum + Yantras, but choose their own spell factors or not take any spell factor penalties...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T23:54:23-07:00","id":1553730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553728#post1553728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but let's take an example.<br /> <br /> You have a dice pool of 4, (after all of the yantras, ritual durations, willpower, whatever else is accounted for).<br /> <br /> You have one assistant who has one less gnosis and one less of the relevant Arcanum. So they have a dice pool of 2, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, in this hypothetical use of a system where you want the secondary actors to roll more successes, are you assuming that the point is to maximize spell factors through penalties, much less that the primary actor is working with what can rightly be called the bare minimum reasonable odds of success to cast a spell that their less-talented secondary actor is able to cast normally?<br /> <br /> Just because the spellcasting rules lean hard into the &quot;only one success is needed to succeed&quot; part of ChroD's base system doesn't mean the <i>other</i> reason you want more dice is gone, particularly when the leader still benefits from having the spell as a Praxis or Rote.<br /> <br /> The two core Merits that affect teamwork spellcasting remove the &quot;unskilled penalty&quot; for secondary actors (and increase the bonus they contribute on success by one) and grant the primary actor 8-Again, respectively. Setting aside the options that provide extra steps or Reach to the primary spell factor, an exceptional success can bypass Withstand, generate Mana, or create Conditions that grant Arcane Beats, all of which are sufficiently major for a mage to tap their fellows for assistance, particularly if they don't have the Gnosis, Yantras, or stamina necessary to build a more conventional Imago on their own in a reasonable timeframe.<br /> <br /> I am also curious why the assumption is that the casters <i>will</i> roll for and release Paradox in this situation. By definition, any teamwork casting is working with one more Reach than would be available to a mage casting in an action scene, and containing a Paradox does not penalize the spellcasting roll. The most likely situation where Paradox is an issue, outside of hypothetical wildly inadvisable constructions, is that the primary caster's Imago uses more Reach than one or more secondary casters can safely incorporate, whether because they're an Adept upscaling an Apprentice-level spell or because they're using a Rote the rest of their team haven't learned.<br /> <br /> Like, the point of teamwork casting is very much not to keep your net dicepool as low as possible and flip a coin on whether the firework explodes as planned, it is to compound the advantages of ritual casting to allow uncommon breakthroughs or cut down on the overall number of ritual intervals needed to achieve a desired result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T04:27:06-07:00","id":1553732,"title":"","content":"This is purely in the realm of homebrew, but I think that if you go with the interpretation that secondary casters don't factor in the primary actor's Yantra bonuses and spell factor penalties (which is my preferred interpretation as it would play better), then I would love to let the secondary actors use Yantras of their own, with the regular non-stacking caveat (i.e. any Yantra used by the primary actor or by another secondary actor can't be reused).<br /> That way, you can have the circle of mages each holding a tool of their own, and it actually does something.<br /> It would also mean that a cabal with high Shadow Name investment can get a <i>lot</i> of mileage out of teamworking spells that fit shared themes (as the Persona is potentially the best Yantra you could possibly have on a non-Rote spell, and it's naturally stackable since each is tied to a different identity (unless something really funky is going on)). And I think a cabal with such compatible magical identities should be incentivized to work their magic together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T04:29:03-07:00","id":1553733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553730#post1553730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, in this hypothetical use of a system where you want the secondary actors to roll more successes, are you assuming that the point is to maximize spell factors through penalties, much less that the primary actor is working with what can rightly be called the bare minimum reasonable odds of success to cast a spell that their less-talented secondary actor is able to cast normally?<br /> <br /> Just because the spellcasting rules lean hard into the &quot;only one success is needed to succeed&quot; part of ChroD's base system doesn't mean the <i>other</i> reason you want more dice is gone, particularly when the leader still benefits from having the spell as a Praxis or Rote.<br /> <br /> The two core Merits that affect teamwork spellcasting remove the &quot;unskilled penalty&quot; for secondary actors (and increase the bonus they contribute on success by one) and grant the primary actor 8-Again, respectively. Setting aside the options that provide extra steps or Reach to the primary spell factor, an exceptional success can bypass Withstand, generate Mana, or create Conditions that grant Arcane Beats, all of which are sufficiently major for a mage to tap their fellows for assistance, particularly if they don't have the Gnosis, Yantras, or stamina necessary to build a more conventional Imago on their own in a reasonable timeframe.<br /> <br /> I am also curious why the assumption is that the casters <i>will</i> roll for and release Paradox in this situation. By definition, any teamwork casting is working with one more Reach than would be available to a mage casting in an action scene, and containing a Paradox does not penalize the spellcasting roll. The most likely situation where Paradox is an issue, outside of hypothetical wildly inadvisable constructions, is that the primary caster's Imago uses more Reach than one or more secondary casters can safely incorporate, whether because they're an Adept upscaling an Apprentice-level spell or because they're using a Rote the rest of their team haven't learned.<br /> <br /> Like, the point of teamwork casting is very much not to keep your net dicepool as low as possible and flip a coin on whether the firework explodes as planned, it is to compound the advantages of ritual casting to allow uncommon breakthroughs or cut down on the overall number of ritual intervals needed to achieve a desired result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't assume anyone is going to release a paradox, I assume the more people you include in the ritual, the more likely someone who doesn't like you, or has a political agenda that wants to see you fail, gets included (never mind a secret scelesti or seer spy). And they choose to release the paradox intentionally.<br /> <br /> Getting an exceptional success does become easy, and unexceptional, but it is rarely useful.<br /> <br /> A condition and a beat? Pretty sure that are many ways to otherwise get a beat and magic can directly create conditions.<br /> <br /> Getting an extra step in the primary factor? Trust me, taking a -2 dice pool modifier is a far more effective (and reliable) way of achieving that than giving yourself a good chance of hitting 3/5 successes.<br /> <br /> Getting an extra reach in the primary factor? I guess it depends on how available mana is, but [gnosis/2] (rounded up) is enough to mitigate one extra reach.<br /> <br /> And generating mana? Again there are more reliable ways to generate mana. The only spell which actually costs enough mana that you would really want a refund is Create Truth, and if you *can* cast it, you now have a Hallow so mana shouldn't really be an issue...<br /> <br /> You seem to be questioning why the magic system is built around a risks reward mechanic where you minimise your dice pool (risking the spell failing) against maximising your outcome (additional spell factors) - ignoring the second decision of risk of paradox ba additional reach - core to the decision making of every spell is how you go about getting enough out of it and what risks you are willing to take.<br /> <br /> So unless you are planning actually push yourself, why are you bothering with a ritual at all? (Except when you need to break an unbeatable withstand, and fish for an exceptional success... Though making a system for making exceptional successes mundane and easy to achieve doesn't seem that interesting from a narrative perspective, imho).<br /> <br /> As for the Merits you mentioned, the Free Council one requires everyone to have the same focus, so less than 1 in 5 mages can help, and the Mysterium on is one is arguably the best order specific merit in the game... At least the first dot. Especially from a narrative point of view of having the Mysterium include new members in their rituals where they don't have the Arcanum requirements... It gives good vibes. <br /> <br /> But again, everyone needs it, so if the Hierarch asks for all of the Moros to get together and cast some really big Death spell, neither order merit is actually going to be usable (or all the Acanthus in the Consilium to cast a prophecy for the coming year to guide the Consilium...). <br /> <br /> You are always guaranteed that every member of a given path can participate, because they have to have at least 1 dot in their ruling arcana. So Path based rituals make some more sense... (Where Order based things feel like they are more obscure, private affairs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T04:37:18-07:00","id":1553734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553733#post1553733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting an exceptional success does become easy, and unexceptional, but it is rarely useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forget one last potential result from ES, which is potentially so good I'm pretty sure ignoring it is one of the most common house rules for 2nd edition: Ignoring Withstand<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure teamworking primarily a cabal endeavour, minimizing the risk for bad actors, and the risk of lacking the Order Merits if the cabal is single-Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-10T05:31:03-07:00","id":1553735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553733#post1553733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't assume anyone is going to release a paradox, I assume the more people you include in the ritual, the more likely someone who doesn't like you, or has a political agenda that wants to see you fail, gets included (never mind a secret scelesti or seer spy). And they choose to release the paradox intentionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, again, this is a pretty wild thing to assume reasonable increasing odds of happening in a group of people that are being deliberately asked and included.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A condition and a beat? Pretty sure that are many ways to otherwise get a beat and magic can directly create conditions. </div> </div> </div>A Condition that provides an <i>Arcane</i> Beat, which you otherwise need to seek out novelty for, deal with Paradox long-term, or get and utilize an exceptional success anyway. The most organized group of mages in the setting gets their marching orders from interpreting random events; I don't think you need an especially high threshold of persuasiveness to convince the Awakened to assist with a magical endeavor To See What Happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And generating mana? Again there are more reliable ways to generate mana. The only spell which actually costs enough mana that you would really want a refund is Create Truth, and if you *can* cast it, you now have a Hallow so mana shouldn't really be an issue... </div> </div> </div>Generating Mana <i>to render moot any Mana cost the spell might have</i>. Such as, say, spending Mana to counteract the Paradox risk of the casters putting a bunch of Reach into the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to be questioning why the magic system is built around a risks reward mechanic where you minimise your dice pool (risking the spell failing) against maximising your outcome (additional spell factors) - ignoring the second decision of risk of paradox ba additional reach - core to the decision making of every spell is how you go about getting enough out of it and what risks you are willing to take. </div> </div> </div>No, I'm questioning why you think teamwork casting, a mechanic that only applies to the mode of casting better suited to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit?p=1183441#post1183441\">the branch of play that's about preparation and being careful</a>, is supposed to be engaged with like the branch of play where you drop your active dicepool low enough to count on one hand at best and hope the coin-flip turns out in your favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Merits you mentioned, the Free Council one requires everyone to have the same focus, so less than 1 in 5 mages can help, and the Mysterium on is one is arguably the best order specific merit in the game... At least the first dot. Especially from a narrative point of view of having the Mysterium include new members in their rituals where they don't have the Arcanum requirements... It gives good vibes.<br /> <br /> But again, everyone needs it, so if the Hierarch asks for all of the Moros to get together and cast some really big Death spell, neither order merit is actually going to be usable (or all the Acanthus in the Consilium to cast a prophecy for the coming year to guide the Consilium...).<br /> <br /> You are always guaranteed that every member of a given path can participate, because they have to have at least 1 dot in their ruling arcana. So Path based rituals make some more sense... (Where Order based things feel like they are more obscure, private affairs). </div> </div> </div>Almost by definition your Order and your Legacy are the people you are narratively encouraged to petition for help outside of your cabal, because those are the most likely people counted among your mentors, apprentices, and colleagues.<br /> <br /> The existence of Space magic does not undo the fact that mages tend to live somewhere with consistent geographical access to the things they regularly need, want, or are obliged to deal with. You are <i>likely</i> to know other mages who share your Path, Order, or Arcana to some degree, and even without an institutional construct built around it like the Mysterium has, the concept of social currency and owing favors continues to exist in mage societies.<br /> <br /> Mages are not hyper-individualists to the degree that getting four Disciples of Forces together to manipulate the weather or gathering up a bunch of Time Apprentices to juice an augury is especially infeasible for a category of person who interacts with magic overall from a perspective of curiosity and self-empowerment. <i>You can absolutely happen to know a guy.</i> That's no small reason SoS's expansion of the requisitioning rules includes Availability for getting someone to cast a spell for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-11T02:44:14-07:00","id":1553748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553734#post1553734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forget one last potential result from ES, which is potentially so good I'm pretty sure ignoring it is one of the most common house rules for 2nd edition: Ignoring Withstand<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure teamworking primarily a cabal endeavour, minimizing the risk for bad actors, and the risk of lacking the Order Merits if the cabal is single-Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fine for single order cabals.<br /> <br /> I think most player character canals are not single order.<br /> <br /> I also think most single order cabals have multiple paths - because that gives the order a cabal with a lot of variety, and flexibility with what it can ask the cabal to do; but unfortunately that makes it less likely anyone else in a that cabal will be able to participate fully - at least as a secondary caster, obviously you can still have sleepwalker with Ritual related merits to help, and other cabal mates can help with this aswell.<br /> <br /> But I think for anything with more than about two full participants (and requiring more than 2 dots in the primary Arcanum ) you're usually going to have to go to a wider group - sure asking all the Mysterium Adepts of Life within your Caucus is feasible, especially with access to space magic, and higher levels of Eregore granting free Sympathetic connections to all members... My point stands, the wider a net you cast to try and find assistants, the riskier it gets - especially if there is something important enough to call in everyone, then it is probably important enough to try and sabotage (depending on who is actually there...) <br /> <br /> I think this is interesting narratively, so that is why I would place an emphasis on it. You might know even cabal in the caucus, or there might be a new cabal which isn't fully trusted... But taking the time to get each and every person may not be possible if the issue is time sensitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T06:23:52-07:00","id":1553835,"title":"","content":"What happens when a Supernal Paragon does (whether summoned or not) do they return to the Supernal (and risk being dragged into the Abyss) or do they return the the Emanation Realm which they are native to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T16:59:00-07:00","id":1553844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553835#post1553835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a Supernal Paragon does (whether summoned or not) do they return to the Supernal (and risk being dragged into the Abyss) or do they return the the Emanation Realm which they are native to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Thurae can be found in the hearts of some Supernal Verges, I think it's reasonable to say Paragons that are modeled as Supernal beings instead of living ones reform as they would in a Verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T19:15:05-07:00","id":1553846,"title":"","content":"Can a Death mage use Shadow Crafting while in the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T19:34:13-07:00","id":1553847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553846#post1553846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Death mage use Shadow Crafting while in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the Underworld prevents shadows from being cast, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T00:19:57-07:00","id":1553850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553844#post1553844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Thurae can be found in the hearts of some Supernal Verges, I think it's reasonable to say Paragons that are modeled as Supernal beings instead of living ones reform as they would in a Verge.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, i'm assuming the can reform (even the Bound Supernals do that) but my question is, do they have the same risk of being dragged into the Abyss (which regular Supernal Beings have) or are they more like Bound Supernals - where because they are bound on the Fallen world, don't have to cross the Abyss to go back to where they reform.<br /> <br /> Whatever Emanation realm they come from is on the Fallen world's side of the Abyss (at least in 2e) and they can be summoned like regular Superbal Beings. So presumably the take damage at the same rate as Supernal Beings (per the Summoning rules), unless maybe they find an appropriate Verge?<br /> <br /> The only question in my mind is whether they return to the Supernal (and then have to migrate back to their Emanation realm) or if they can avoid a dangerous trip to the Abyss....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T05:23:24-07:00","id":1553854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553850#post1553850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes, i'm assuming the can reform (even the Bound Supernals do that) but my question is, do they have the same risk of being dragged into the Abyss (which regular Supernal Beings have) or are they more like Bound Supernals - where because they are bound on the Fallen world, don't have to cross the Abyss to go back to where they reform.<br /> <br /> Whatever Emanation realm they come from is on the Fallen world's side of the Abyss (at least in 2e) and they can be summoned like regular Superbal Beings. So presumably the take damage at the same rate as Supernal Beings (per the Summoning rules), unless maybe they find an appropriate Verge?<br /> <br /> The only question in my mind is whether they return to the Supernal (and then have to migrate back to their Emanation realm) or if they can avoid a dangerous trip to the Abyss....</div> </div> </div> </div>An Emanation's mechanics include several effects that are explicitly identical to or inclusive of those of a Supernal Verge. A Paragon is not actually a Supernal being and, given the mechanics of Emanations in relation to the rest of the cosmology, cannot be summoned outside of their Emanation (presumably barring an open Thura).<br /> <br /> The circumstances that lead to the consumption of a Supernal being by the Abyss upon death involve being killed outside of the summoning circle or a Verge and an Emanation provides the benefits of a Verge. Nothing about the modifications to Corpus for Supernal beings say that they return to the Supernal like spirits get pulled into the Shadow when they enter dormancy, and in fact the Summoning section's notes on Lifespan indicates the opposite. Nonliving Paragons therefore may be read as reforming in a safe place within the Emanation when their Corpus is reduced to 0 while they have at least 1 Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T14:28:41-07:00","id":1553861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553854#post1553854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Emanation's mechanics include several effects that are explicitly identical to or inclusive of those of a Supernal Verge. A Paragon is not actually a Supernal being and, given the mechanics of Emanations in relation to the rest of the cosmology, cannot be summoned outside of their Emanation (presumably barring an open Thura).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, they aren't summonable? I was under the impression that the short amount of text on the matter was indicating that they can be summoned (just like other Supernal entities) but with a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The circumstances that lead to the consumption of a Supernal being by the Abyss upon death involve being killed outside of the summoning circle or a Verge and an Emanation provides the benefits of a Verge. Nothing about the modifications to Corpus for Supernal beings say that they return to the Supernal like spirits get pulled into the Shadow when they enter dormancy, and in fact the Summoning section's notes on Lifespan indicates the opposite. Nonliving Paragons therefore may be read as reforming in a safe place within the Emanation when their Corpus is reduced to 0 while they have at least 1 Mana. </div> </div> </div>Ok, sorry, they do reform, but near a source of mana (if destroyed in a verge/summoning circle) but usually they're not going to have time to reform in a summoning circle before getting dragged back to the Supernal... The section on Lifespan says &quot;once the being runs out of corpus it vanishes&quot; - which now that i'm reading it seem to contradict what it says in the Invisible entities section.<br /> <br /> Regardless, if a Summoned Supernal being runs out of time, it returns to the Supernal; otherwise if it just dies it isn't dragged anywhere, but needs to go to a source of mana to recover; Bound lose one mana each day, and i am presuming that they act like Supernal Beings in every way - so would also reform after destroyed if they find a source of mana...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;A Paragon is not actually a Supernal being&quot; - when it says they can usually be classified as Supernal Beings - i am assuming that (like the Bound) Supernal Paragons use the rules for Supernal Beings - apart from where it states that they don't. (and living paragons are the unusual case of things that aren't supernal beings which are nevertheless native to an emanation realm).<br /> <br /> But regardless, SoS does say that Mages can summon Supernal Paragons, and that they enjoy a +2 (so it is easier to summon them than summoning a being directly from the Supernal?) Am i misreading this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T18:18:25-07:00","id":1553864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553861#post1553861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, they aren't summonable? I was under the impression that the short amount of text on the matter was indicating that they can be summoned (just like other Supernal entities) but with a +2 bonus.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;A Paragon is not actually a Supernal being&quot; - when it says they can usually be classified as Supernal Beings - i am assuming that (like the Bound) Supernal Paragons use the rules for Supernal Beings - apart from where it states that they don't. (and living paragons are the unusual case of things that aren't supernal beings which are nevertheless native to an emanation realm).<br /> <br /> But regardless, SoS does say that Mages can summon Supernal Paragons, and that they enjoy a +2 (so it is easier to summon them than summoning a being directly from the Supernal?) Am i misreading this?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be summoned in the Emanation they come from. Emanations are so cut off from the rest of the setting that without connections specific to the Emanation an open Thura is the only route that allows Space magic to bridge the gap, and Signs contains enough non-Supernal &quot;Supernal beings&quot; that &quot;can usually be classified as Supernal beings&quot; can be clearly understood to not mean the same thing as &quot;You can summon these anywhere like normal Supernal beings.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't specify that you can't summon Ochemata or Bound, either, and those aren't being engaged with as natives to an isolated plane of existence where the living natives sicken and die when they leave and most native magical objects stop working when removed from the laws of physics that support them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, sorry, they do reform, but near a source of mana (if destroyed in a verge/summoning circle) but usually they're not going to have time to reform in a summoning circle before getting dragged back to the Supernal... The section on Lifespan says &quot;once the being runs out of corpus it vanishes&quot; - which now that i'm reading it seem to contradict what it says in the Invisible entities section.<br /> <br /> Regardless, if a Summoned Supernal being runs out of time, it returns to the Supernal; otherwise if it just dies it isn't dragged anywhere, but needs to go to a source of mana to recover; Bound lose one mana each day, and i am presuming that they act like Supernal Beings in every way - so would also reform after destroyed if they find a source of mana... </div> </div> </div>An Emanation Realm is almost certainly what the Manifestation and Possession section of the Invisible Entities rules terms as within &quot;overlapping regions of reality like a Supernal Verge&quot; and therefore makes them work like material entities. By a similar token, since Supernal Paragons are natives to their home Emanation rather than the Supernal World, it follows that they should regain their Rank in Mana per day regardless of where in the Emanation they discorporate, and they reform in a safe location as normal regardless of the presence of special Conditions.<br /> <br /> (The contradiction you are observing can be squared by the fact that the operative part of that sentence is the &quot;they are otherwise consumed by the Abyss when they run out of Corpus&quot; part \u2014 normal Supernal beings are not irrevocably destroyed if their time runs out within the bounds of a summoning circle.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T01:10:10-07:00","id":1553868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553864#post1553864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (The contradiction you are observing can be squared by the fact that the operative part of that sentence is the &quot;they are otherwise consumed by the Abyss when they run out of Corpus&quot; part \u2014 normal Supernal beings are not irrevocably destroyed if their time runs out within the bounds of a summoning circle.)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the contradiction is between A) &quot;when they run out of Corpus&quot; (their lifespan runs out, and they either return to the supernal or get dragged into the abyss)<br /> and B) when their corpus is destroyed they shatter into mana and are forced to return to a source of mana to reform.<br /> <br /> This is two different things which are supposed to happen with mechanically their last corpus box is filled with damage (or sufficiently damaging damage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't specify that you can't summon Ochemata or Bound, either, </div> </div> </div>This is a really weird comparison, it does specify that you *CAN* summon paragons, it doesn't mention summoning for Bound, or Greater Tulpas (though they are kinda summoned in a round about way...) Ochemata are not Supernal beings, are they? - no wait, they appear to be, so you could allow an Ochemata in the Supernal respond to a Summoning the same way any other Supernal Being responds (but not those that exist within the golden road or an archmaster...) I don't see why you would conclude otherwise - but that's not really relevant. It does specify that Supernal Paragons can be summoned, and your claims that they are too far away seem to pale when compared to the distance to the Supernal Realms - Emanation Realms are at least a place you can travel, the Supernal seems far further away.<br /> <br /> And <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and those aren't being engaged with as natives to an isolated plane of existence where the living natives sicken and die when they leave and most native magical objects stop working when removed from the laws of physics that support them. </div> </div> </div>It is only Living Paragons (the ones that aren't modelled after Supernal Beings) who sicken and die when removed from from their native realm. Supernal Paragons would use the same rules as other Summoned Supernals - ie life span as discussed in the Summoning section.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added responce. 09-17-2025, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T05:56:40-07:00","id":1553870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553868#post1553868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the contradiction is between A) &quot;when they run out of Corpus&quot; (their lifespan runs out, and they either return to the supernal or get dragged into the abyss)<br /> and B) when their corpus is destroyed they shatter into mana and are forced to return to a source of mana to reform.<br /> <br /> This is two different things which are supposed to happen with mechanically their last corpus box is filled with damage (or sufficiently damaging damage).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, again, the operative part of the sentence is the one that jives with the part from the Supernal Summoning section. The alternative is that you come up with your own explanation that also explains where a summoned Supernal being naturally recovers Mana while dormant.<br /> <br /> And <i>again</i>, the core of the system for invisible entities reforming is that they reform in <i>a safe place</i>. Conditions that support their regaining Essence or Mana are common additional qualities, but the base function is &quot;if they have Essence or Mana preventing them from being annihilated, they come back somewhere safe&quot; before &quot;they come back somewhere that will restore them to activity.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a really weird comparison, it does specify that you *CAN* summon paragons, it doesn't mention summoning for Bound, or Greater Tulpas (though they are kinda summoned in a round about way...) Ochemata are not Supernal beings, are they? - no wait, they appear to be, so you could allow an Ochemata in the Supernal respond to a Summoning the same way any other Supernal Being responds (but not those that exist within the golden road or an archmaster...) I don't see why you would conclude otherwise - but that's not really relevant. It does specify that Supernal Paragons can be summoned, and your claims that they are too far away seem to pale when compared to the distance to the Supernal Realms - Emanation Realms are at least a place you can travel, the Supernal seems far further away. </div> </div> </div>The Supernal is everywhere and its denizens are limited chiefly in their typical inability to emerge without circumstances that support their manifest presence. Paragons are physical natives of places that are so cut off from the rest of the cosmology by default that removing stuff from their internal laws of physics commonly makes that stuff stop functioning, whether magically or as a living creature.<br /> <br /> Mechanical classification umbrella aside, Supernal Paragons are not normal Supernal beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is only Living Paragons (the ones that aren't modelled after Supernal Beings) who sicken and die when removed from from their native realm. Supernal Paragons would use the same rules as other Summoned Supernals - ie life span as discussed in the Summoning section. </div> </div> </div>You realize I mentioned more than just the living Paragons as part of establishing a pattern of how Things From Emanations work, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T07:05:51-07:00","id":1553897,"title":"","content":"Am I wrong in reading the rules of Supernal summoning as meaning you actually have very little input on what kind of being you get at all? Like, I presume that if its second primary Arcanum can be up to the Storyteller barring spending Mana and having a 3+ Arcanum to specify, then everything else about it has the same discretion rather than beings of the same archetype having different Arcana stats.<br /> <br /> In which case, I'd think the simplest explanation for being unable to summon Paragons while not in their Emanation is because you don't have that level of control over the summoning for anything, and Paragons would be so down low on the list of things that might be fitting to answer the summons.<br /> <br /> That and how I generally interpret Supernal inhabitants as not corresponding to geography but conceptual resonance. You can call upon Metatron because Metatron exists adjacent to everywhere that certain kinds of punitive justice exist simultaneously, whereas a given Paragon has a more fixed point in space that is literally far away from you.<br /> <br /> Unless you're within the same Emanation, and even then I wouldn't see the summoning as something you can specify down to any type or individual. It's just putting out a signal into the realm that keys off of a Paragon's Supernal quality to obligate them to turn up, pose a Trial, and be at the service of the mage who passes it. It just does so with whatever Paragon is most fitting.<br /> <br /> (Likewise, you cannot summon Supernal Ochemata because you cannot specify for them and they are definitely bound to an authority that does not make them available to answer the beck and call of the Phenomenal.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T10:56:00-07:00","id":1553904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553897#post1553897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I wrong in reading the rules of Supernal summoning as meaning you actually have very little input on what kind of being you get at all? Like, I presume that if its second primary Arcanum can be up to the Storyteller barring spending Mana and having a 3+ Arcanum to specify, then everything else about it has the same discretion rather than beings of the same archetype having different Arcana stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, that had been my general read, but on the other hand, there are mechanics revolving around summoning specific Supernal beings (namely the common quality of the Aedes Tilt and the Supernal Watcher Merit).<br /> <br /> Personally I would say the more particular metaphysical/spatial relationships of Aedes, Emanations, and Supernal Watchers can be tapped into but the more general phenomenon of Supernal Summoning is a &quot;to whom it may concern,&quot; which tracks with Summoners' description of research providing trends for the Trials asked by certain types of entity rather than systematizing more particular preparation for a type of transcendent being whose manifestations are implied to vary with the summoning by the nature of their interface with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-18-2025, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T05:10:36-07:00","id":1553918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553897#post1553897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I wrong in reading the rules of Supernal summoning as meaning you actually have very little input on what kind of being you get at all? Like, I presume that if its second primary Arcanum can be up to the Storyteller barring spending Mana and having a 3+ Arcanum to specify, then everything else about it has the same discretion rather than beings of the same archetype having different Arcana stats.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are not at all wrong on this count.<br /> <br /> There a fluff about how to summon a specific Supernal Being, like particular rituals tat have worked in the past, knowing their name, basically figuring ou how to make a particular Supernal more likely to show up. But it is ultimately that Supernal Being's decision.<br /> <br /> So you could do all the research, find out the name of the specific Entity, and do loads of preparations, and it just not work (not that this would be satisfying narratively, but Mages in setting don't know this fact - they might guess at it, or becpme Obsessed with it...). <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In which case, I'd think the simplest explanation for being unable to summon Paragons while not in their Emanation is because you don't have that level of control over the summoning for anything, and Paragons would be so down low on the list of things that might be fitting to answer the summons. </div> </div> </div>To be clear RAW, it says they can be summoned. It says most paragons can be classfied as Supernal Beings, and they can be summoned(and you get a +2 when summoning them)<br /> <br /> i don't how else to interpret this other than using the Summoning supernal beings rules.<br /> <br /> Even if getting a particular Supernal Paragon is as difficur as gettinga particular Supernal Being...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T11:10:45-07:00","id":1553923,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> Personally, I tend to agree with you that on the plain reading... except for that +2 which is the same as the summoning bonus you get for being in a verge of demesne. That to me makes me really suspect that the writer thinks you're using the summoning rules inside the relevant emanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T11:37:26-07:00","id":1553924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553923#post1553923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> Personally, I tend to agree with you that on the plain reading... except for that +2 which is the same as the summoning bonus you get for being in a verge of demesne. That to me makes me really suspect that the writer thinks you're using the summoning rules inside the relevant emanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, my i interpretation was that the +2 is because it is easier to summon a paragon compared to a Supernal Being in thr Supernal - because the Paragon is already closer to thr Fallen (being manifest and not only existing in the symbolic world of the Supernal).<br /> <br /> But that implies the character is able to choose - and get the +2 - rather than the Supernal entity in question getting to decide to respond to the summons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T12:47:54-07:00","id":1553925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553924#post1553924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense, my i interpretation was that the +2 is because it is easier to summon a paragon compared to a Supernal Being in thr Supernal - because the Paragon is already closer to thr Fallen (being manifest and not only existing in the symbolic world of the Supernal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was my reading initially. However, it struck me as an odd choice for that. Like, would it not make more sense to cut the number of successes needed, as for example, the Supernal Watcher merit does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T19:02:58-07:00","id":1553947,"title":"","content":"Is there an Awakening version of Arcane (from Ascension)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T19:51:59-07:00","id":1553948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553947#post1553947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an Awakening version of Arcane (from Ascension)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get a similar effect with a combination of the Shadow Name and Occultation merits, but not the vanishing from mundane records effect higher levels of Arcane grants. A Prelacy of the Nemesis also grants a Seer the Crown of Secrecy, which makes your Nimbus very difficult to pick up on. Lastly, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1473930#post1473930\">spells </a>can be used for additional ways to hide from other mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T02:35:22-07:00","id":1553952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553947#post1553947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an Awakening version of Arcane (from Ascension)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anonymity from pg.50 of <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> is partly similar. It gives a -1 penalty per merit dot to any attempts to track your character via paperwork. (However, it's a mundane merit, so conceptually it's a bit different.)<br /> <br /> Incognito Presence on pg.160 of <i>Mage 2e</i> is a spell, but conceptually it's very similar to Arcane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T09:31:05-07:00","id":1553955,"title":"","content":"No wonder I couldn't find it; I'll look under CoD: Mage; I have the Awakening 1e, but I don't really play it as I like the Ascension more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T21:20:34-07:00","id":1553961,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you use the Fate and/or Mind Arcana to activate a Changeling token in the same way that the Word of Command spell allows?</li> <li>Can a Mage harvest / extract Glamour from themselves with the Mind Arcana? If so, can they use it to activate Changeling tokens?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T22:00:14-07:00","id":1553963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553961#post1553961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the Fate and/or Mind Arcana to activate a Changeling token in the same way that the Word of Command spell allows?</div> </div> </div> </div>By adding those Arcana to Word of Command, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Mage harvest / extract Glamour from themselves with the Mind Arcana? If so, can they use it to activate Changeling tokens? </div> </div> </div>They would need conjunctional Fate to do so since they don't have a Wyrd trait, it would likely drain a point of Willpower as with fae harvesting (the spell is Patterning, not Making), and the spell to move Glamour analogizes it to Channel Mana and describes valid targets mostly in terms of things that have a maximum Glamour capacity, with the only thing spending it does being to create a Yantra for another spell. If you want to activate a token you use its catch or use Word of Command.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T05:30:29-07:00","id":1553974,"title":"","content":"Whats the point of artefacts? what advantage do they give to a person that already can cast those spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 09-23-2025, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T06:35:41-07:00","id":1553975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553974#post1553974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the point of artefacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries to study, spells you can cast without needing to know the Arcana, potentially higher Gnosis with which to cast the spells (and thus faster ritual casting times along with the extra dice), distinctive Path Tools which might be semiotically suitable for things the normal categories or your Dedicated Tool can't manage, extra Mana storage, and any narrative effects that rely on that particular Artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what advantage do they give to a person that already can cast those spells? </div> </div> </div>Most of the above plus leverage if someone else wants to be able to use the spell but you don't want to teach it to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T06:55:43-07:00","id":1553977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553975#post1553975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mysteries to study, spells you can cast without needing to know the Arcana, potentially higher Gnosis with which to cast the spells (and thus faster ritual casting times along with the extra dice), distinctive Path Tools which might be semiotically suitable for things the normal categories or your Dedicated Tool can't manage, extra Mana storage, and any narrative effects that rely on that particular Artifact.<br /> <br /> Most of the above plus leverage if someone else wants to be able to use the spell but you don't want to teach it to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does not seem a lot for a permament willpower point<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T08:06:48-07:00","id":1553979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553977#post1553977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not seem a lot for a permament willpower point</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifacts don't cost willpower. Are you thinking of imbued items?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T17:28:59-07:00","id":1553989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1553974#post1553974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what advantage do they give to a person that already can cast those spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, their uses don't count towards spell limit... I'm pretty sure.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm on the same page that artifacts as written have a very soft distinction from Imbued Items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T08:17:21-07:00","id":1553993,"title":"","content":"They might also be the source of unique spells. The Ring of the Dethroned Queen, for example, is an Artifact that allow the subject to detect the influence of the Exarchs around them. A rote can only be codified by studying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T15:30:32-07:00","id":1554041,"title":"","content":"Multiple unconnected questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Pierce Deception. Does it find absolute truths or just what the liar knows to be false?</b><br /> Essentially, IF this finds absolute truths, this one is the strongest spell ever, because you can ask anyone any question and if it their reply is false it will ping as such (even if the person in question does not know the veracity of the question), playing a binary search until you get to the truth. This is just me being dumb of course unless Prime being connected to the realm of truth will give you all answers, <b>Words of Truth</b> at least specifies that <i>&quot;The spell only works on statements the mage knows to be true&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Will, spells and Legacy attainments.</b>\u200b<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If a spell or attainments that you generated clashes, do you get feedback from those?</li> <li>Can the subject of a spell or attainment that grants Clash of Wills willingly surrender and receive the effect that clashed? Can the caster allow it to happen?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T15:53:57-07:00","id":1554042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554041#post1554041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple unconnected questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Pierce Deception. Does it find absolute truths or just what the liar knows to be false?</b><br /> Essentially, IF this finds absolute truths, this one is the strongest spell ever, because you can ask anyone any question and if it their reply is false it will ping as such (even if the person in question does not know the veracity of the question), playing a binary search until you get to the truth. This is just me being dumb of course unless Prime being connected to the realm of truth will give you all answers, <b>Words of Truth</b> at least specifies that <i>&quot;The spell only works on statements the mage knows to be true&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Will, spells and Legacy attainments.</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If a spell or attainments that you generated clashes, do you get feedback from those?</li> <li>Can the subject of a spell or attainment that grants Clash of Wills willingly surrender and receive the effect that clashed? Can the caster allow it to happen?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>The Clasher can just choose to allow the effect, so long as the effect is still under their control. So Clashing against a relinquished spell you released is a problem to be considered.<br /> <br /> I am not sure in the case of <i>Pierce Deception</i>. I feel that lies of omission and active attempts to deceive would ping, not sure if inaccurate information would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T17:22:13-07:00","id":1554044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554041#post1554041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pierce Deception. Does it find absolute truths or just what the liar knows to be false?</b><br /> Essentially, IF this finds absolute truths, this one is the strongest spell ever, because you can ask anyone any question and if it their reply is false it will ping as such (even if the person in question does not know the veracity of the question), playing a binary search until you get to the truth. This is just me being dumb of course unless Prime being connected to the realm of truth will give you all answers, <b>Words of Truth</b> at least specifies that <i>&quot;The spell only works on statements the mage knows to be true&quot;</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can Pierce Deception. It sees illusions, phantasms, and lies for what they are. It's reading veracity of presentation. If you ask me to guess which playing card is hidden in the box, that's not a lie or a deception unless I'm genuinely trying to convince you that I <i>do</i> know that it's the Jack of Spades. You're not piercing whether it is or isn't the Jack of Spades. You're piercing whether I'm trying to mislead you.<br /> <br /> I'm drawing this conclusion primarily because, as you say, if it's testing veracity of information and whether it is or isn't the Jack of Spades, then you can play 20 questions to investigate anything with this Prime 1 spell in a way that's not interesting, fun, or genre-resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-28-2025, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T19:10:52-07:00","id":1554045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554041#post1554041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pierce Deception. Does it find absolute truths or just what the liar knows to be false?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The entire second paragraph of the spell description is quite clear that what the spell does is identify when the subject of the spell is the recipient of an active untruth or deception, providing the specific example that it can't tell that someone is committing tax fraud just by looking at them but would instead need to see the falsified tax returns.<br /> <br /> It's notable that Words of Truth has that stipulation specifically to prevent people from fishing for absolute truth by seeing which of their statements benefit from it; Pierce Deception doesn't need it because the closest thing you can get out of a lie-detector/illusion-bypassing spell to that is abstract visions of the disguised truth with the Reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T04:02:25-07:00","id":1554077,"title":"","content":"From what i undestand, Artifact effect must be activated by a mage using a specific trigger.<br /> Artifact can also self-activate using their own pool and deciding spell factors by itselfs.<br /> My question is, the self-activation happens by a second specific triggertrigby the first when there are no mages harnessing the item?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T04:42:26-07:00","id":1554078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554077#post1554077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is, the self-activation happens by a second specific triggertrigby the first when there are no mages harnessing the item?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the example triggers is &quot;the moment it's first seen by human eyes,&quot; so I would assume that yes, Artifacts in 2e don't only work when used by a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T13:07:09-07:00","id":1554169,"title":"","content":"How does <i>Pierce Deception</i> work with illusions ? Let's say you have an illusory bridge over a ravine, would the default version draw a distinction between a trapped bridge and an illusion, or would it just ping ? In the case of the Reach version, what would it do in that scenario ? What would it reveal when faced with an illusory wall, or with an illusory hazard ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T14:00:45-07:00","id":1554171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554169#post1554169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does <i>Pierce Deception</i> work with illusions ? Let's say you have an illusory bridge over a ravine, would the default version draw a distinction between a trapped bridge and an illusion, or would it just ping ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It Clashes with the illusion to tell you the bridge is an illusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the case of the Reach version, what would it do in that scenario ? </div> </div> </div>Provide symbolic indications that there is no bridge and the only thing there is a ravine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would it reveal when faced with an illusory wall, or with an illusory hazard ? </div> </div> </div>Same thing as with the bridge.<br /> <br /> Is there more to this question that I'm not understanding? Because &quot;What does a spell that sees through lies, deceptions, and illusions do when confronted with an illusion?&quot; seems self-evident from the description of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T14:05:44-07:00","id":1554172,"title":"","content":"I mean it you would see through it be default (the illusion turns transparent and see what is behind it) or if you still needed a different spell to accomplish the same objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T14:33:23-07:00","id":1554173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554172#post1554172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it you would see through it be default (the illusion turns transparent and see what is behind it) or if you still needed a different spell to accomplish the same objective.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, the spell tells you that something you are perceiving is a falsehood. You need the Reach effect or another spell or effect to see <i>through</i> the illusion in terms of determining what's behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T04:21:29-07:00","id":1554339,"title":"","content":"Whats the exact condition for needing another arcanum in a spell? when reach is not enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T05:03:59-07:00","id":1554341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554339#post1554339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the exact condition for needing another arcanum in a spell? when reach is not enough?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> A major reason is when more precision with the Arcanum is not enough. I interpret </span><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Serendipity</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, for example, as using it's Reach effect to parse through the threads of Fate to help you find one that allows you the opportunity to use the skills you want.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the case of a </span><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Golem</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, it can only be machine like by itself. You need to create or bind a fully formed mind to give it depth of thought, which is beyond the scope of Matter. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">With spells like </span><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ban</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, it allows you to recognize the kind of phenomena to permit or exclude. Lastly, additional Arcana can be used to extend the functionality of the spell beyond the Arcanum's purview, such as adding Spirit to </span><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Word of Command</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> to activate a werewolf fetish.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T15:09:06-07:00","id":1554350,"title":"","content":"The (sligthly) contraversial one is when Patterning, if you want to take something from the purview of one Arcanum and transform it entirely into the purview of another Arcanum (like Patterning a Living pillar of fire) requires both the arcana purviews (eg: Life and Forces) - explicitly according to the Creative Thaumetergy rules (only contraverysince there is a Death example Patterning for turning a person into a kind of living Shadow, and it only requires Death, but I shall endeavour too ignore that example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T17:17:36-07:00","id":1554352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554350#post1554350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The (sligthly) contraversial one is when Patterning, if you want to take something from the purview of one Arcanum and transform it entirely into the purview of another Arcanum (like Patterning a Living pillar of fire) requires both the arcana purviews (eg: Life and Forces) - explicitly according to the Creative Thaumetergy rules (only contraverysince there is a Death example Patterning for turning a person into a kind of living Shadow, and it only requires Death, but I shall endeavour too ignore that example).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I figured, it uses a being currently in decay (a mortal) as it's base and then transforms them into a being with the self awareness of a higher Ranked ghost (a mortal mind) and the form of a shadow, which might be sculpted to the shape the subject has (a 3D shadow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T04:50:30-07:00","id":1554358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554352#post1554352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I figured, it uses a being currently in decay (a mortal) as it's base and then transforms them into a being with the self awareness of a higher Ranked ghost (a mortal mind) and the form of a shadow, which might be sculpted to the shape the subject has (a 3D shadow).</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the Decay in a living pattern and turning it into Shadow (also in Death's purview) is not entirely how I would have read that section.<br /> <br /> But why worry about the Decay, since part of a person is their shadow? (One of the five-fold parts of the Soul). You are still transforming a living pattern into a deathly one, and this kind of thinking would encourage lots of rules lawyering to try and allow other Patterning spells.<br /> <br /> I prefer to compare it to Ghost Gate, it doesn't transform the subject into Ephemera, but it does push them into twilight. So pushing them into Shadow should be a similar process. Still a living being but intangible, invisible in darkness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T13:30:06-07:00","id":1554486,"title":"","content":"Does wisdom <b>only </b>measure Magic and spell usage?<br /> <br /> I am thinking bout this part in the Understanding level of wisdom sins &quot;<i>deliberate and premeditated murder and violence that leaves its victim with long-term injury</i>&quot; <br /> <br /> If Sara the mage, uses her karate and judo training to cause lasting harm or kill an enemy, will it count under Wisdom sins, or since no magic was involved, it is irrelevant for Losing Wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T13:38:21-07:00","id":1554488,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> I think it's all actions. Consider also Enlightened:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When innocent bystanders are affected by your character\u2019s spells or <b>actions</b>, she is at risk as well. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T13:42:45-07:00","id":1554491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554486#post1554486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does wisdom <b>only </b>measure Magic and spell usage?<br /> <br /> I am thinking bout this part in the Understanding level of wisdom sins &quot;<i>deliberate and premeditated murder and violence that leaves its victim with long-term injury</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If Sara the mage, uses her karate and judo training to cause lasting harm or kill an enemy, will it count under Wisdom sins, or since no magic was involved, it is irrelevant for Losing Wisdom?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will count as a wisdom sin. Since Wisdom is about power and control over things, it is usually Magic that managed have the most power (and are most likely to lose sight of things) but if you crash a car into someone and they die, then you still crashed a car into them...<br /> <br /> The power to significantly change someone's life is magic, whether that is supernal or mundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T16:37:08-07:00","id":1554500,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> thanks for your answers.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that Enlightened and Understanding mages, always suffer if they kill opponents? Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T17:26:04-07:00","id":1554501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554500#post1554500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean that Enlightened and Understanding mages, always suffer if they kill opponents? Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Killing people is consistently a big deal for the vast majority of the playable range of Integrity-alikes across the gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T19:15:52-07:00","id":1554503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554500#post1554500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean that Enlightened and Understanding mages, always suffer if they kill opponents? Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is by design.<br /> <br /> Killing don't stop being killing because of self-defense, and we must remember that the Integrity-like system doesn't measure moral or crime, but psychological impact. The idea (that is correct from a psychological standpoint IRL) is that killing always has an impact on your being.<br /> <br /> Feeling or being justified is irrelevant to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T23:57:54-07:00","id":1554511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554500#post1554500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> thanks for your answers.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that Enlightened and Understanding mages, always suffer if they kill opponents? Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the cosmic power of the universe. You can mash nouns and verbs together if you've got the Gnosis for it. If you care about having a clean, self-controlled soul, find other ways to resolve conflicts.<br /> <br /> Or you can get comfortable with taking lives and having a messy, volatile soul. That's plenty playable, and honestly, probably more genre-appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T03:37:20-07:00","id":1554515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554500#post1554500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean that Enlightened and Understanding mages, always suffer if they kill opponents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, depending on what you mean by 'suffer'. Yes, you will always suffer a degeneration roll. However the mechanic is merely an opportunity to degenerate, not a guarantee. You can even benefit from it.<br /> <br /> Additionally, mages don't exactly 'suffer' from anything. Like, Integrity loss sucks, and when enough goes you start to experience horrible psychological effects. Mages just become worse people (I mean, until they reach 0 and explode, but that's a way off).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom. </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly. Premeditated Murder is listed as a 'better' sin than doing it in a rage for example. That's the opposite of how most criminal systems would deal with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T06:45:12-07:00","id":1554522,"title":"","content":"This is one of those things where I think it's worth emphasizing how it's possible to buy Wisdom back.<br /> <br /> I think the exacting standards of Enlightened Wisdom do make it challenging to maintain for a lot of active mages. I think the typical course of the mage who is invested in that is not to never falter, but on the occasions where they do, to undertake to reflect upon themselves, make relevant investigations into the consequences of what they have done, and build themselves back up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554515#post1554515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages just become worse people</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think the impact it has on Paradox is at least supposed to be something that has player facing impact and recognition in-character.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't think mages of low Wisdom even necessarily become all that worse, just going by description of what each level is like. I'll admit that could be a consequence of how, per Dave's commentary, it's a relatively underdeveloped section, so it could well be that the intention was to have something like the roleplaying guidelines for levels of vampire Humanity.<br /> <br /> Still, personally I think it's fitting that even at Falling Wisdom, a mage is still at a point where they could effectively rationalise things to themselves and be acceptable in their society, even if they have become inured to the consequences of a lot of actions and are hovering at the point where crossing a few more lines could break their souls.<br /> <br /> Although the funny thing is that, per the mechanics, a mage in Falling Wisdom could be kind of more stable than somebody at a higher level. Becoming inured to something like pre-meditated killing of a person might not be great, but the fact that you don't roll for it as an Act of Hubris anymore means you're also not risking something like the Megalomaniacal or Rampant conditions. If you're not moved by the immorality of the action anymore, you're also not empowered by the thrill of absolute power it can give, which might technically make you somewhat safer than a mage maintaining a higher Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554500#post1554500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even those that were trying to kill them? Because as I am getting it, self-defense killing still does harm wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that raises questions of who was trying to kill them, and how effective they were at carrying that out. Magic gives you a lot of means to retreat.<br /> <br /> I'd say this plays into the depiction of how the Adamantine Arrow and Guardians of the Veil view the subject, being the Orders most likely to kill. To them, there's basically no such thing as killing in self-defence. If you kill a person, you need to make sure it's because you want them dead; that the value of them being dead has been judged as greater than them being alive. Even then, the justifications for it can be thin, both in terms of understanding and carrying the weight of a life, and recognising the potential consequence of somebody of their power becoming more okay with making that call.<br /> <br /> Their philosophies encourage them not to find justifications for that action, but to engage with those questions openly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T09:42:33-07:00","id":1554523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554522#post1554522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the impact it has on Paradox is at least supposed to be something that has player facing impact and recognition in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to see that as more just the natural result of losing Wisdom. Like, Paradox is worse because you aren't as careful, represented by your Wisdom score.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I don't think mages of low Wisdom even necessarily become all that worse, just going by description of what each level is like. </div> </div> </div>I was just referring to the two conditions you get for failure.<br /> <br /> To be fair, they do overwrite Obsessions, so I'm maybe being a bit harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T15:18:51-07:00","id":1554527,"title":"","content":"How does changing range with reach work?<br /> 1. Self/touch &gt; 1 reach &gt; ranged&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?<br /> 2. Self/touch/thrown&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T15:52:31-07:00","id":1554528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554527#post1554527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does changing range with reach work?<br /> 1. Self/touch &gt; 1 reach &gt; ranged&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?<br /> 2. Self/touch/thrown&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Aimed Spells are part of Self/Touch range, they just require the additional roll to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T16:31:10-07:00","id":1554529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554528#post1554528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter. Aimed Spells are part of Self/Touch range, they just require the additional roll to hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you<br /> Another one: what are all the ways to regain mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T16:45:39-07:00","id":1554530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554529#post1554529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one: what are all the ways to regain mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>The methods described on Page 87 of the corebook constitute the majority of the methods, though there's also choosing &quot;regain all the Mana spent on the spell plus an extra point&quot; as the benefit of an exceptionally successful spellcasting roll, or adhering to Obligations (described in Signs of Sorcery on pages 48-51).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T16:51:27-07:00","id":1554531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554527#post1554527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does changing range with reach work?<br /> 1. Self/touch &gt; 1 reach &gt; ranged&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?<br /> 2. Self/touch/thrown&gt; 1 reach &gt; autohit?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ranges are<br /> +0 Reach: self/touch/touching in combat (dex +brawl/weaponry)/thrown spell( Gnosis+ higher of athletics/firearms - subject's defence\u2020)<br /> +1 Reach: sensory/sympathetic range\u2021<br /> +2 Reach: remote viewing (must be live)<br /> <br /> \u2020subject does not get defence if you have the fast spells merit<br /> \u2021sympathetic range is an attainment, which requires Space 2, and 1 mana, and a sympathic yantra, and a sympathy connection - which is used to withstand the spell (weaker the connection the higher the withstand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T18:05:24-07:00","id":1554578,"title":"","content":"What is the Opacity of an Annulity ? Is is set by the Gnosis of the creator ? Does it vary for one made by a Rapt ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T18:45:47-07:00","id":1554581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554578#post1554578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Opacity of an Annulity ? Is is set by the Gnosis of the creator ? Does it vary for one made by a Rapt ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going from SoS's expansion of Building A Mystery, I would say an Annulity created via a soul stone is probably Opacity 2 or 3 (being functionally the same principles as creating a Demesne, which is worth three Merit dots to add to a Sanctum), one created via the Imperial Practices has Opacity equal to the Arcanum rating used to create it (7, if the sample Entities spells from IM still hold true), and either half the creator's Gnosis or the Arcanum rating linked to the creator's Fault in the case of one created via dramatic failure on a Tulpa eruption roll, all subject to the usual adjustment to taste for Building A Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T19:39:42-07:00","id":1554583,"title":"","content":"Cool, and would Prime or Time be able to preserve a Rapt's Annullity so it can be studied at leisure ? Are there any other methods to create a Prime Annulity, for example ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T08:44:36-07:00","id":1554596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554583#post1554583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, and would Prime or Time be able to preserve a Rapt's Annullity so it can be studied at leisure ? Are there any other methods to create a Prime Annulity, for example ?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Satchel's post, it seems like Archmastery can do it. In theory studying enough of them could reveal some other way to create a natural ones, subject to ST approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T05:29:24-07:00","id":1554721,"title":"","content":"Is there an equivalent of an armory in cofd? Im looking for a book filled with tables of tools and weapons and their stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T06:05:47-07:00","id":1554722,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; is a rebrand of the line's trademark name, not a new edition. There's 2e books both before and after the rebrand.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nWoD 2e/CofD 2e's closest counterpart to Armory is Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T20:24:49-07:00","id":1554754,"title":"","content":"Hello I may have totally missed where and may not be even asking this correctly but can mages with conjunctional Prime + Fate slip into the same Twilight spectrum as Demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28961-sabelforge","name":"Sabelforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28961_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T22:05:49-07:00","id":1554757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554754#post1554754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello I may have totally missed where and may not be even asking this correctly but can mages with conjunctional Prime + Fate slip into the same Twilight spectrum as Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a couple confounding factors here, chief among them being that <i>demons</i> don't typically have access to that phase of Twilight (the only thing the Unchained toolkit unambiguously provides in even the perceptual vein in that direction is that aetheric resonance pings angels who lack Cover-equivalent Infrastructure even in Twilight), with all the powers that place a demon in Twilight explicitly or conceptually accessing a different phase than the one their enemy controls. More broadly, Fate + Prime doesn't give the Awakened the ability to detect Infrastructure beyond the completion of an occult matrix, and the Machine's metaphysical inhabitation of all its works and byproducts suggests angelic Twilight is potentially closer to the kind of unelaborated-upon phenomenon described as disguising the stranger phenomena of a Supernal Verge around its periphery, which is ultimately mechanical shorthand for &quot;this phenomenon doesn't have to stick to the normal laws of physics surrounding material interaction and occupying space&quot; in a game where the primary ephemeral being regularly gets to ignore most of the systems ephemeral beings use to determine where they can go.<br /> <br /> The second issue is that not all Arcana allow interaction with all phases of Twilight equally well (Mind alone only permits little-&quot;a&quot; astral projection, Changeling and Deviant and Mage itself establish in different ways that not all forms of intangibility equate to phases of Twilight, Prime already provides &quot;you can make something solid to all phases of Twilight&quot; a full Practice below other Arcana's &quot;enter this phase of Twilight&quot; spells) and the precedent this would set for a game makes this really weird, chiefly in that even if one allows bodily entering more rarefied phases of Twilight with the inclusion of Life (and possibly Matter), that results in the really weird situation where having two Arcana that don't directly truck with invisible entities as a whole framework (Fate and Life) allows you to walk among qashmallim (completely inaccessible to ghosts, spirits, goetia, angels, etc) relatively unmolested (and neither of those two Arcana are Inferior for any standard Path).<br /> <br /> Nothing says one way or the other explicitly, but personally I feel the fact that <i>entering</i> angelic Twilight is not mentioned in either of the two places where Prime + Fate are described as the Arcana to use to interact with God-Machine metaphysics more generally is a conspicuous omission that would not be there in spite of all the other ways it allows interaction with angels if it were intended; you might swing it with access to a more particular piece of Infrastructure, but generally speaking I would treat entering &quot;angelic Twilight&quot; roughly the same as the prospect of entering Neter-Khertet and going to the akhets as someone who isn't an Arisen mummy \u2014 Twilight is mechanical shorthand for something's interface with the material world, and specific forms of it are interacted with in the ways appropriate to the games a given phase occupies, and ultimately G-M Twilight amounts to &quot;angels who aren't manifested into physical bodies are largely invisible and intangible to anything that would get in the way of their mission when they need to be, and some of the structures the Machine creates cannot be seen by anyone who isn't in the right place at the right time or sufficiently part of the Plan to have the eyes for it&quot; rather than providing an ecosystem to disappear into or a phantom wall to shelter behind.<br /> <br /> Individual table decisions may vary, of course, but as far as explicit statements, the books don't say one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T05:32:03-07:00","id":1554765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554754#post1554754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello I may have totally missed where and may not be even asking this correctly but can mages with conjunctional Prime + Fate slip into the same Twilight spectrum as Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, Angels, Demons and other creations of the GM are in a phase of Twilight attuned to both Prime and Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T07:10:17-07:00","id":1554771,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Demons, by default, can access Twilight... Angels usually come with a Twilight form, and Demons with a particular exploit can get Ephemeral cover, which would likely usually be in Death/Spirit twilight - though I see nothing in principle stopping them from harvesting the Corpus of an Angel to make such a cover... It seems unwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T12:34:30-07:00","id":1554784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554771#post1554771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Demons, by default, can access Twilight... Angels usually come with a Twilight form, and Demons with a particular exploit can get Ephemeral cover, which would likely usually be in Death/Spirit twilight - though I see nothing in principle stopping them from harvesting the Corpus of an Angel to make such a cover... It seems unwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I ask is because the source material for 2E seems to indicate you need Prime and Fate to interact with Demons/Angels/GM stuff. I don't remember seeing any source material stating the use of Death and or Spirit with the above splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28961-sabelforge","name":"Sabelforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28961_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T12:42:30-07:00","id":1554785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554757#post1554757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second issue is that not all Arcana allow interaction with all phases of Twilight equally well (Mind alone only permits little-&quot;a&quot; astral projection, Changeling and Deviant and Mage itself establish in different ways that not all forms of intangibility equate to phases of Twilight, Prime already provides &quot;you can make something solid to all phases of Twilight&quot; a full Practice below other Arcana's &quot;enter this phase of Twilight&quot; spells) and the precedent this would set for a game makes this really weird, chiefly in that even if one allows bodily entering more rarefied phases of Twilight with the inclusion of Life (and possibly Matter), that results in the really weird situation where having two Arcana that don't directly truck with invisible entities as a whole framework (Fate and Life) allows you to walk among qashmallim (completely inaccessible to ghosts, spirits, goetia, angels, etc) relatively unmolested (and neither of those two Arcana are Inferior for any standard Path).</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly agree with this, but also wonder if something like Death or Spirit spells with an optional inclusion of Prime and Fate and possibly some extra Reach would make sense as something to allow entering Twilight at that frequency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T18:37:18-07:00","id":1554804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554785#post1554785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I strongly agree with this, but also wonder if something like Death or Spirit spells with an optional inclusion of Prime and Fate and possibly some extra Reach would make sense as something to allow entering Twilight at that frequency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Matter or Forces would actually be better than Spirit or Death for interacting with G-M stuff/Twilight.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said, in the end &quot;Twilight Phase&quot; is a mechanical shorthand for different ways of becoming invisible and intangible. Thematically speaking, the God-Machine does that by using strange materials and laws of physics. It has no real connection with other Ephemera except in its capacity to use Essence as fuel, which it arguably has because it can use <i>anything</i> as fuel. At the end of the day, I don't see it as having much connection to Death or Spirit outside specific Projects.<br /> <br /> That would also make for a nice differentiation to set the mood for a Mage game involving the God Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554784#post1554784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason I ask is because the source material for 2E seems to indicate you need Prime and Fate to interact with Demons/Angels/GM stuff. I don't remember seeing any source material stating the use of Death and or Spirit with the above splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>We simply have no hard answer.<br /> <br /> In fact, a Mage would probably have to first investigate enough G-M related Mysteries to even be able to find a way to use the appropriate Arcana to interact with it in a more meaningful way, or in their own Twilight. That would be more important, thematically, than whatever specific Arcanum does the job.<br /> <br /> Having the God-Machine operate in a way familiar to any splat, even Mages, goes against its narrative role. The whole theme is that it's based on an understanding of reality beyond what anyone can grasp. If you get it out of the G-M, then there are actually better things to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T18:55:00-07:00","id":1554805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554784#post1554784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I ask is because the source material for 2E seems to indicate you need Prime and Fate to interact with Demons/Angels/GM stuff. I don't remember seeing any source material stating the use of Death and or Spirit with the above splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Prime + Fate to mess with Embeds, perceive angels in Twilight, shield against angelic Numina, or detect and mess with the output of an occult matrix at the root level; just as Forces or Matter can allow you to interfere with the products of a werewolf's Gift of the Elementals without needing to include Spirit, the relevant phenomena are still subject to the Arcana of their end use cases regardless of whether you can meddle with the framework that brings them about; the Ephemeral Cover Exploit still creates a Cover identity that occupies the relevant phase of Twilight and can be interacted with with he appropriate Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554785#post1554785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly agree with this, but also wonder if something like Death or Spirit spells with an optional inclusion of Prime and Fate and possibly some extra Reach would make sense as something to allow entering Twilight at that frequency.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like one of those things obscure and/or dangerous enough to necessitate more Reach than safely possible and/or specific Yantras to use, but also the published spells for entering Death and Spirit Twilight don't have &quot;add [Arcanum]&quot; notes like Banishment and Exorcism do to permit consolidating all possible &quot;enter Twilight&quot; variants into a single spell for Rote/Praxis purposes.<br /> <br /> Like, setting aside angelic Twilight being mostly a personal quality in practical terms, &quot;one or more mages have developed access to the phase of existence where the great engine that turns the world hides many of its secrets and routes several of its agents and assets through&quot; is kind of a localized story-hook by virtue of how the Machine operates, and is thus probably better handled as a more involved Mystery beyond the scope of simply saying You Can Do This With These Arcana Ratings; if pressed for a mechanical threshold I would probably model the necessary knowledge to do so as a Merit with potential drawbacks baked in to be developed further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T03:07:33-07:00","id":1554833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554784#post1554784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason I ask is because the source material for 2E seems to indicate you need Prime and Fate to interact with Demons/Angels/GM stuff. I don't remember seeing any source material stating the use of Death and or Spirit with the above splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons specifically have an Exploit (Ephemeral Cover, pg 164 DtD) which lets them rip a ghost/spirit's corpus apart and use it to fashion a Cover - and when in that cover enter the relevant twilight.<br /> <br /> This is more about how Demons interact with ghosts and spirits, with humans they make deals to take parts of their lives, and end up taking the entire soul (soul pact) to make Cover. Ghosts and Spirits don't have souls, but you can still use them to make Cover.<br /> <br /> I don't see any other way for them to enter twilight. Maybe at your table Demons have done a smash and grab on a piece of Angel creating Infrastructure and have built a gadget to access Angel Twilight (as a means of defence/offence against Angels in Twilight), I don't see why that would breall anything about the themes of Demon, but off Mage...<br /> <br /> I really like lots of the suggestions above, which essentially amount to, it's a Mystery.<br /> The G-M might do things differently depending on its needs. So each piece of infrastructure, each Occult Hyper-physics matrix operates on sligthly different mechanisms utilising a whole range of purviews and Arcana depending on what the G-M needs are...<br /> <br /> That said, yes, &quot;Angelic Essence&quot; and Aether are specifically called out as being Prime+Fate to channel, which is odd, because generally essence is used as Generic fuel in the purview of Spirit... So most of the time you can assume it means the same kind of energy no matter what is using it. (Eg Ghosts don't use Plasm/Ectoplasm, Goetia don't use whatever fuel stat the splatt who will not be named use, because they are generic entities and use a generic fuel source...) Angels seem to be the exception here, but that only really matters go Mages, since no ody else if going around Changeling Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T03:38:07-07:00","id":1554835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sabelforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554784#post1554784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason I ask is because the source material for 2E seems to indicate you need Prime and Fate to interact with Demons/Angels/GM stuff. I don't remember seeing any source material stating the use of Death and or Spirit with the above splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>orathaic is talking about Ephemeral Cover because that power allows demons to claim Cover identities as ghosts or spirits. So they end up in ghostly Twilight (Death) or spiritual Twilight (Spirit), not angelic Twilight. This is one of very few demon powers available that can bring them into Twilight. The only other one I can think of is Decoy, which is a form of astral projection.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, demons rarely enter Twilight and don't enter angelic Twilight at all, and have pretty limited means of even sensing angelic Twilight. It's part of the spy game Demon is playing: angels could be anywhere around you at a given time watching invisibly and you just don't know for sure.<br /> <br /> All of this is assuming God-Machine demons. There are other things called demons unrelated to Demon: the Descent and the God-Machine, like things from the Inferno or from Pandemonium. Inferno demons are pretty likely to be found in common Twilight phases (Death or Spirit, depending).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T04:29:18-07:00","id":1554837,"title":"","content":"Werent mages suposed to do anything they want provided the proper Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T06:09:24-07:00","id":1554840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554837#post1554837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werent mages suposed to do anything they want provided the proper Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and sometimes the proper Arcana are beyond the scope of use for characters who aren't operating at the level of plot devices.<br /> <br /> The highest confirmed Imperial Practice amounts to &quot;For the Duration of this spell, you can do anything relating to the Arcanum it uses within sensory range except for extending the Duration of this spell or giving another iteration of this spell to someone else.&quot; It requires a unique Yantra that is as difficult for the character to get with the resources of an archmaster capable of creating Chantries and subsoul as it was for that same character to get the Yantra that allowed them to turn themselves into an archmaster. A hypothetical higher-level version of that spell that is active all the time is one speculated route to Ascension.<br /> <br /> There are still limits before then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T07:12:22-07:00","id":1554843,"title":"","content":"When <i>Turn Momentum</i> is used to turn a projectile against the attacker, are they able to apply their defense against it, if applicable ? If so, do they try to defend against their own attack roll ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T09:14:09-07:00","id":1554852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554837#post1554837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werent mages suposed to do anything they want provided the proper Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Satchel</a> said, Mages are also supposed to have proper preparations and costs to do stuff.<br /> <br /> Contrary to <i>Ascension</i>, in <i>Awakening</i> there <b>are</b> right answers and proper ways of doing things, and a Mage has to find out what it is they need to do what they want, even when within their power.<br /> <br /> Maybe even more important, though, is that facing the God-Machine is like facing a specially powerful Archmage, just short of Ascension. You're not dealing with a static phenomenon with fixed rules and no understanding of the Supernal, you're dealing with an active entity that virtually understands every Arcanum to its fullest, at least as far as it applies to the Lie, and knew about Mages way before they knew about each other.<br /> <br /> Then again, the key is to understand the tropes involved. If the God-Machine isn't like that, there are better things to use in a game than the God-Machine. And that isn't hard even if you have the Demons of <i>Descent</i> in play, because as a strange and arbitrary entity the G-M may be absent of an area for no discernible reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T07:24:48-08:00","id":1554958,"title":"","content":"What kind of phenomenon, apart of Vampires and Revenant, could be the cause of random corpses rising as aggressive istinct driven &quot;zombies&quot; ?<br /> I need inspiration for a scene that could become a mystery to solve after some time, so i need a rule consistent explaination.<br /> The setting is on an island, somewhere on the island there are old unspecified ruins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:08:34-08:00","id":1554962,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Neos01</a> Malfunctioning God-Machine infrastructure? (There's a brief scenario involving a G-M created plague in the core).<br /> <br /> An Atlantean weapon from <i>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:19:46-08:00","id":1554964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554958#post1554958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of phenomenon, apart of Vampires and Revenant, could be the cause of random corpses rising as aggressive istinct driven &quot;zombies&quot; ?<br /> I need inspiration for a scene that could become a mystery to solve after some time, so i need a rule consistent explaination.<br /> The setting is on an island, somewhere on the island there are old unspecified ruins</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage, all kinds of things, which doesn't narrow the field much.<br /> <br /> Could be death-spirits, geists (particularly ones with an innate Key of Chance), Supernal beings, qashmallim, angels, archspells, regular long-lasting spells, Paradoxical anomaly, some sort of material echo of events in the Anima Mundi, a long-dormant curse, one of the Bound breaking out of ruins from the Time Before, some Abyssal thing washing up on the shore, overdue fae strangeness, a dormant strain of Contagion, events converging to draw a new cult to a sleeping mummy, a more isolated phenomenon of the sort that might attract a conspiracy to exploit it, and many more.<br /> <br /> Are you looking for something complex and obscure or are you intending to drip-feed the zombie encounters and related elements over the course of the story to throttle the rate at which Scrutiny can put the pieces together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:32:35-08:00","id":1554967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554964#post1554964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mage, all kinds of things, which doesn't narrow the field much.<br /> <br /> Could be death-spirits, geists (particularly ones with an innate Key of Chance), Supernal beings, qashmallim, angels, archspells, regular long-lasting spells, Paradoxical anomaly, some sort of material echo of events in the Anima Mundi, a long-dormant curse, one of the Bound breaking out of ruins from the Time Before, some Abyssal thing washing up on the shore, overdue fae strangeness, a dormant strain of Contagion, events converging to draw a new cult to a sleeping mummy, a more isolated phenomenon of the sort that might attract a conspiracy to exploit it, and many more.<br /> <br /> Are you looking for something complex and obscure or are you intending to drip-feed the zombie encounters and related elements over the course of the story to throttle the rate at which Scrutiny can put the pieces together?</div> </div> </div> </div>It s more the second option.<br /> The core is that the rising should seem spontaneous, with no visible person trafficking with the corpse.<br /> I was thinking about the coffin wood harvested from near the temple (maybe an old infrastructure) being able to put the dead alive again, but without the precise knowledge of the building methods the results are animalistic zombies.<br /> Could it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T08:46:27-08:00","id":1554969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554958#post1554958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of phenomenon, apart of Vampires and Revenant, could be the cause of random corpses rising as aggressive istinct driven &quot;zombies&quot; ?<br /> I need inspiration for a scene that could become a mystery to solve after some time, so i need a rule consistent explaination.<br /> The setting is on an island, somewhere on the island there are old unspecified ruins</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It could be an Infrastructure, see the <i>Wake The Dead</i> one on page 214 of the CofD core book. Maybe it's an Iron Seal of the Psychopomp, which makes it so those that died during the tragedyvthst created it are trapped and forced to re-experience it (like the WW1 section of <i>The Darkness</i> video game). </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T10:29:37-08:00","id":1554974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554967#post1554967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It s more the second option.<br /> The core is that the rising should seem spontaneous, with no visible person trafficking with the corpse.<br /> I was thinking about the coffin wood harvested from near the temple (maybe an old infrastructure) being able to put the dead alive again, but without the precise knowledge of the building methods the results are animalistic zombies.<br /> Could it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work. I'd note that unless you intend to link in the God-Machine in general you may be better off using a less thoroughly interlocking cause, given that the Machine tends to break down or shut down Infrastructure it's not using anymore and its failures to do so tend to have causes of their own, so either the God-Machine or something interfering with it had plans for the temple or there's a very suspicious coincidence that let to some paperwork not reaching the right Heavenly in-tray that resources for resurrection have gone dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T10:44:11-08:00","id":1554976,"title":"","content":"I think narratively it also depends on how much your players already know or that you intend to reveal to them. Like, just revealing it's the God-Machine might fall flat if your players don't really know what that is.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the idea. Reminds me of the stories you see every so often of people coming across scrap metal that turns out to be radioactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T23:33:02-08:00","id":1555001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1554958#post1554958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of phenomenon, apart of Vampires and Revenant, could be the cause of random corpses rising as aggressive istinct driven &quot;zombies&quot; ?<br /> I need inspiration for a scene that could become a mystery to solve after some time, so i need a rule consistent explaination.<br /> The setting is on an island, somewhere on the island there are old unspecified ruins</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An idigam with forge undead<br /> <br /> FORGE UNDEAD<br /> The idigam holds power over life itself. It can resurrect any corpse it can perceive, regardless of decay or the state of the body, by spending two Essence per point of Health the idigam chooses to invest in the dead flesh, up to the creature\u2019s usual maximum Health. The total invested dictates the creature\u2019s new maximum Health for the duration of the resurrection. Of course, this isn\u2019t true life, but merely an extension of the idigam\u2019s power \u2014 the revived being cannot resist his master\u2019s will, and the idigam can withdraw that life at any time. A resurrected creature has their former personalities and abilities, but cannot restore Willpower through any means except consuming human flesh; devouring the meat of a single human corpse restores all expended Willpower points.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1414367-new-shapeshifters-lyrebirds-the-orpheans#post1414367\">Or a Lyrebird</a><br /> <br /> Necromancy: By spending 3 Essence, an Orphean can reanimate a dead body as a shambling zombie for a week and a day. The walking carcass obeys the Orphean unquestioningly, and can be given relatively advanced instructions, although it has no real capacity for reasoning in and of itself. An Orphean can maintain up to her Primal Urge in zombies at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T23:49:24-08:00","id":1555004,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a Blue Book about undead, or at least with an undead chapter?<br /> <br /> The thing is, CoD being CoD, we may have any number of possible causes that aren't yet described in the books, related to any splat or none at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T05:22:09-08:00","id":1555017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555004#post1555004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a Blue Book about undead, or at least with an undead chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter One of WoD: Antagonists \u2014 some of the non-core ghost Numina in Mummy 1e (in the same section as Lucid Dead) are reprints of Numina introduced in Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T04:25:35-08:00","id":1555108,"title":"","content":"Do mages in this system increase attributes magically permamently? or is the table showing just how big they can be while using temporal busting spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T04:49:19-08:00","id":1555109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555108#post1555108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mages in this system increase attributes magically permamently? or is the table showing just how big they can be while using temporal busting spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages, like other supernaturals, have a set maximum of trait limits (skills and Attributes) that can be purchased with XP, determined by their power stat. In the case of mages, it's set by Gnosis, with Gnosis 6 being the first milestone allowing them to buy post-human traits. You can find a chart with more details on page 86.<br /> <br /> Spells can boost traits up to the subject's limit, normally through a Perfecting. It costs some Reach and a point of mana to go above trait limits.<br /> <br /> In other words, let's say you have a <i>Augment Mind</i> with no Reach options and a Potency of 5. If you have Gnosis 7 mage and a Sleeper, both with an Intelligence of 2, the spell will boost the Intelligence of the mage to 7 and Sleeper's to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T06:21:54-08:00","id":1555115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555109#post1555109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages, like other supernaturals, have a set maximum of trait limits (skills and Attributes) that can be purchased with XP, determined by their power stat. In the case of mages, it's set by Gnosis, with Gnosis 6 being the first milestone allowing them to buy post-human traits. You can find a chart with more details on page 86.<br /> <br /> Spells can boost traits up to the subject's limit, normally through a Perfecting. It costs some Reach and a point of mana to go above trait limits.<br /> <br /> In other words, let's say you have a <i>Augment Mind</i> with no Reach options and a Potency of 5. If you have Gnosis 7 mage and a Sleeper, both with an Intelligence of 2, the spell will boost the Intelligence of the mage to 7 and Sleeper's to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excelent example thank you. Could i do the same with making it indefinate duration or lasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T06:33:24-08:00","id":1555116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555115#post1555115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excelent example thank you. Could i do the same with making it indefinate duration or lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot make it Lasting and the only difference Indefinite Duration will make is that it lasts until the spell is ended or dispelled. Both targets would still have a natural Intelligence of 2 in the example; increasing the Duration just makes it last longer and stand a better chance of winning a Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T15:16:52-08:00","id":1555184,"title":"","content":"Absent have a meat suit merit, which basically locks them into their old body, and forces them to consume raw meat to keep that body in good repair; maybe something is causing low rank 1/0 ghosts to occupy their body in the same way... there are many such cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T07:16:45-08:00","id":1555238,"title":"","content":"Got a question on h<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ow spells that create &quot;charges&quot;/&quot;uses&quot;, such as Perfect Recall, interact with Advanced duration? On p. 113 it says, &quot;would logically have an immediate effect but is cast with Advanced Duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out.&quot; Would this mean the charges get reset every interval? Or do you just get a set number for the entire duration?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26144-eshangray","name":"eshangray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T07:35:08-08:00","id":1555239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eshangray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555238#post1555238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a question on how spells that create &quot;charges&quot;/&quot;uses&quot;, such as Perfect Recall, interact with Advanced duration? On p. 113 it says, &quot;would logically have an immediate effect but is cast with Advanced Duration, the effect recurs at every multiple of the character\u2019s Gnosis-based ritual casting time, until the Duration runs out.&quot; Would this mean the charges get reset every interval? Or do you just get a set number for the entire duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. Having a pool of uses that can be called upon at any time is distinct from the spell doing something right away when the spell is cast, and the description of Hexes and Boons in the Fate Arcanum provide an explicit basis for how spells with &quot;charges&quot; work in relation to their Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-08T08:32:58-08:00","id":1555241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555239#post1555239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter. Having a pool of uses that can be called upon at any time is distinct from the spell doing something right away when the spell is cast, and the description of Hexes and Boons in the Fate Arcanum provide an explicit basis for how spells with &quot;charges&quot; work in relation to their Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I figured that was the case but wanted a second opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26144-eshangray","name":"eshangray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T03:58:38-08:00","id":1555395,"title":"","content":"It is possible to put Attainment like Time in a Bottle in a imbued item?<br /> <br /> AND<br /> <br /> It is possible to add a conjunctional Mind 3 or 4 to the Web weaver spell to determine the kind of feeling associated to the modified Sympathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T07:08:15-08:00","id":1555405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555395#post1555395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible to put Attainment like Time in a Bottle in a imbued item?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Mage, the Awakening 2ed, page 195</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable of casting. Imbued items retain their magic indefinitely; a spell cast using an imbued item might run out, but the imbued item itself does not. Attainments may only be included if they modify a spell; for example, mages can imbue items with spells using Sympathetic Range, but may not imbue an item with Mage Armor or the ability to create Rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it seems like just imbuing <i>Time in a Bottle</i> by itself is not possible, but you can use it as part of the spell being imbued, which will increase it's activation mana cost. Since an imbued item has a battery of 1 mana by default and the spell would cost at least 2 (1 to activate the item + 1 for <i>Time in a Bottle</i>), you might need to spend more time imbuing to increase the capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555395#post1555395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is possible to add a conjunctional Mind 3 or 4 to the Web weaver spell to determine the kind of feeling associated to the modified Sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the primary function of <i>Web-Weaver</i> is to bolster the connection, the conjunctional Arcana is not expanding it's functionality within it's focus. So I would say you require either a conjunctional spell or a separate cast of <i>Correspondence</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T07:16:53-08:00","id":1555407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555405#post1555405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So it seems like just imbuing <i>Time in a Bottle</i> by itself is not possible, but you can use it as part of the spell being imbued, which will increase it's activation mana cost. Since an imbued item has a battery of 1 mana by default and the spell would cost at least 2 (1 to activate the item + 1 for <i>Time in a Bottle</i>), you might need to spend more time imbuing to increase the capacity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since the primary function of <i>Web-Weaver</i> is to bolster the connection, the conjunctional Arcana is not expanding it's functionality within it's focus. So I would say you require either a conjunctional spell or a separate cast of <i>Correspondence</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, whenever an Utility Attainment is added the user must always use it?<br /> Like if you add Sympathetic Range you must always cast by this mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T07:56:22-08:00","id":1555409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555407#post1555407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, whenever an Utility Attainment is added the user must always use it?<br /> Like if you add Sympathetic Range you must always cast by this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, <i>Permanence, Time in a Bottle, Everywhere</i>, always activated.<br /> <br /> I would argue the only exceptions are <i>Sympathetic Range</i> and <i>Temporal Sympathy</i>, which require sympathetic range to even be used. So you could not use them if you Imbued an item with Flexible Reach, but you would still need to pay the mana for them.<br /> <br /> So what is the benefit of that ? Since all casts of the Imbued spell only use one one spell slot in total, you can have multiple spells going, with different factors being used. The downside is that it would consume mana even faster than normal Imbued Items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-12-2025, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T23:43:36-08:00","id":1555463,"title":"","content":"Do you use reach to broaden a spell in creative taumathurgy? if so how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-14T01:40:30-08:00","id":1555467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555463#post1555463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you use reach to broaden a spell in creative taumathurgy? if so how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only 'sort of.' Spells are, by default, cast at touch Range, only effect one human or thing, with Potency 1, and last 1 turn.<br /> <br /> Potency, Scale, Range, and Duration are the spell factors. They can go up by just taking a penalty during the casting. So, a spell that lasts one turn can take a -4 hit to the roll to successfully cast the spell to last three turns instead of one..<br /> <br /> You use Reach to shift them from regular casting limits. Like the spell mentioned above, the Default is One turn, but the Advanced Default (Advanced is achieved by using reach) is one scene. If used with the other example, where you use Reach but still take a -4, if cast correctly, the spell now has a Duration of one week.<br /> <br /> The charts for the different spell factors are around page 113. Here's the chart for Duration:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/aKyBu2n\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/aKyBu2n\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/aKyBu2n\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/a/aKyBu2n </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-15T16:58:07-08:00","id":1555494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555463#post1555463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you use reach to broaden a spell in creative taumathurgy? if so how?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by broaden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-16T09:12:50-08:00","id":1555499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555494#post1555494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you mean by broaden.</div> </div> </div> </div>For example the spell from the main book Deepen Shadows with 1 reach allows to make full darkness and that is beyond the power of a 1 lvl arkanum. So that is what i mean by broaden, extend the power above what the arcanum dot should be able to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T00:21:27-08:00","id":1555519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555499#post1555499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example the spell from the main book Deepen Shadows with 1 reach allows to make full darkness and that is beyond the power of a 1 lvl arkanum. So that is what i mean by broaden, extend the power above what the arcanum dot should be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so for your particular example... that spell isn't creating darkness out of nothing, it's affecting the distribution of ambient shadows. The Reach effect doesn't change that, it just modifies the extent of the penalty it imposes. They're both Compelling effects in so far as they pull and direct existing darkness, just one is more... precise.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe you disagree with the logic or mechanical expression of that, but it would probably match the intent of the writers. Reach effects are not intended to grow beyond the capabilities of the Practice, they just apply the effect of the spell with more precision or severity.<br /> <br /> So as far as creative thaumaturgy goes, I see two points of relevance. One is that a person can certainly have the point that their custom spells can have such Reach effects, and indeed probably ought to (which I would approach from the angle of &quot;consider the strongest applications of the spell effect and whether they ought to be put behind a Reach cost&quot;. The other is whether creative thaumaturgy can devise additional Reach effects for written spells. I would say yes if it sounds like it makes sense, but would caution against the impulse to make too many additional things rest on single spells. Indeed, I would imagine that a lot of things a person might think of as a Reach at first would actually be fine just being there own spells, with the proposed effect as the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T16:14:22-08:00","id":1555560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555519#post1555519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so for your particular example... that spell isn't creating darkness out of nothing, it's affecting the distribution of ambient shadows. The Reach effect doesn't change that, it just modifies the extent of the penalty it imposes. They're both Compelling effects in so far as they pull and direct existing darkness, just one is more... precise.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe you disagree with the logic or mechanical expression of that, but it would probably match the intent of the writers. Reach effects are not intended to grow beyond the capabilities of the Practice, they just apply the effect of the spell with more precision or severity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure i can agree here<br /> Lets compare this to Influence heat (forces 1) and control heat (forces 2). <br /> Influencing heat does not allow for it to be hoter only to move it from the source to the target. Meanwhile controling does allow to increase heat. The same logic should apply to darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T14:04:47-08:00","id":1555606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555560#post1555560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure i can agree here<br /> Lets compare this to Influence heat (forces 1) and control heat (forces 2).<br /> Influencing heat does not allow for it to be hoter only to move it from the source to the target. Meanwhile controling does allow to increase heat. The same logic should apply to darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The consequences of making things hotter and making an area darker are very different. For the latter, it's basically incidental.<br /> <br /> Even so, you're actively interpreting the idea of the Reach effect fulfilling a different way of applying a penalty for difficulty seeing in terms of &quot;increase darkness&quot; as opposed to &quot;make shifting shadows around have a more pronounced effect&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, considering what the Blind Tilt <i>is</i>, the Reach is basically achieving an effect of &quot;wrap those shadows directly around a person's face&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now maybe that's interpretive, but it's interpretive from a position of &quot;make the rules as internally consistent as possible rather than look for ways to complain about them being at fault and try to apply the implications of that elsewhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, on review, I think even your contrary example has a fault. Influence Heat doesn't &quot;increase&quot; heat by itself, but the premise of drawing ambient heat from numerous environmental sources in order to remain warm in extreme conditions pretty much implies that gathering lots of minor heat into one space provides an effective increase in temperature. Its Reach effects are also going on the same premise of greater efficiency in the application of relocating it; where else is it getting the means to keep you from receiving damage while doing something like walking exposed in the Antarctic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-18-2025, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T14:16:24-08:00","id":1555607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555606#post1555606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The consequences of making things hotter and making an area darker are very different. For the latter, it's basically incidental.<br /> <br /> Even so, you're actively interpreting the idea of the Reach effect fulfilling a different way of applying a penalty for difficulty seeing in terms of &quot;increase darkness&quot; as opposed to &quot;make shifting shadows around have a more pronounced effect&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, considering what the Blind Tilt <i>is</i>, the Reach is basically achieving an effect of &quot;wrap those shadows directly around a person's face&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now maybe that's interpretive, but it's interpretive from a position of &quot;make the rules as internally consistent as possible rather than look for ways to complain about them being at fault and try to apply the implications of that elsewhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, on review, I think even your contrary example has a fault. Influence Heat doesn't &quot;increase&quot; heat by itself, but the premise of drawing ambient heat from numerous environmental sources in order to remain warm in extreme conditions pretty much implies that gathering lots of minor heat into one space provides an effective increase in temperature. Its Reach effects are also going on the same premise of greater efficiency in the application of relocating it; where else is it getting the means to keep you from receiving damage while doing something like walking exposed in the Antarctic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood<br /> I consider &quot;wraping shadows around someone to blind them&quot; as a clearly supernatural effect that should be at least weaving as shadows do not stand in front of light sources naturaly. At the moment im starting to be convinced that deepen shadows should be a ruling rote.<br /> As for my example it clearly does increase the heat as it gathers them in one source. Energy transferal is something heat naturaly does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 11-18-2025, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T17:09:54-08:00","id":1555615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555607#post1555607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my example it clearly does increase the heat as it gathers them in one source. Energy transferal is something heat naturaly does.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Moving&quot; heat from several places to a single location in order to increase temperature is literally how it works in thermodynamics. So increasing the temperature of something by stealing Heat (the unity of thermal energy) from other places is a thing and does means heat isn't being increased, even if temperature is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T00:23:21-08:00","id":1555626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555615#post1555615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Moving&quot; heat from several places to a single location in order to increase temperature is literally how it works in thermodynamics. So increasing the temperature of something by stealing Heat (the unity of thermal energy) from other places is a thing and does means heat isn't being increased, even if temperature is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, thats what i said. i have no problmes with influence or increase heat spells, im placing them as a staple of how this should work on those lvls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T02:29:04-08:00","id":1555627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555607#post1555607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...as shadows do not stand in front of light sources naturaly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? I don't think 2e brings it up, but I think the Death Arcanum still follows the logic of 1e. That's to say, shadows aren't just an absence of light, they're an actual presence in the world.<br /> <br /> To compare, the Weaving practice allows you to mess with the properties of things without transforming them... and <i>Shadow Crafting</i> on pg. 132 gives shadows a physical form?<br /> <br /> Death has a bunch of implied metaphysical entities in both editions that are never really elaborated on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the moment im starting to be convinced that deepen shadows should be a ruling rote. </div> </div> </div>I mean, I wouldn't treat the 2e core as gospel. From what I gather multiple people wrote the different Arcana with their own ideas about how the setting should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T13:38:10-08:00","id":1555736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555607#post1555607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider &quot;wraping shadows around someone to blind them&quot; as a clearly supernatural effect that should be at least weaving as shadows do not stand in front of light sources naturaly. At the moment im starting to be convinced that deepen shadows should be a ruling rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think like a Compelling spell to make objects roll towards a specified source would be a nice indicator of how far it can pull them and what it can make them defy.<br /> <br /> If Deepening Shadows is too much for Compelling, what is not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my example it clearly does increase the heat as it gathers them in one source. Energy transferal is something heat naturaly does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that fine, but different levels of Reach to determine the extent of darkness for pulling shadows together is not?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T14:11:47-08:00","id":1555741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555736#post1555736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think like a Compelling spell to make objects roll towards a specified source would be a nice indicator of how far it can pull them and what it can make them defy.<br /> <br /> If Deepening Shadows is too much for Compelling, what is not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why is that fine, but different levels of Reach to determine the extent of darkness for pulling shadows together is not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple, shadows do not move naturaly without the movement to avoid a light source. Heat does naturally move as energy exchange rules.<br /> Even if we asume shadows are a thing (not just absence of light) then compeling does not work. In the examples of compeling practice we cant force a spirit to interact with its ban, the same shadows acting in open light should not be possible,<br /> As for what is not too much for compeling? Making the phenomena act how it naturaly could on its own but maybe a bit faster (increasing the intensity of the phenomena does not count here as it is clearly a ruling thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T14:55:46-08:00","id":1555743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555741#post1555741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we asume shadows are a thing (not just absence of light) then compeling does not work. In the examples of compeling practice we cant force a spirit to interact with its ban, the same shadows acting in open light should not be possible,</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, how do you know that?<br /> <br /> Like, there's a logic to what you're suggesting, but at same time, we have very little to go on. Maybe the shadows just choose not to go outside of the areas they should be in? Maybe shadows do it all the time and it's just that no one notices? (That latter would fit with lots of weirdness reported by people, like shadow people etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T15:11:10-08:00","id":1555744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555743#post1555743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, how do you know that?<br /> <br /> Like, there's a logic to what you're suggesting, but at same time, we have very little to go on. Maybe the shadows just choose not to go outside of the areas they should be in? Maybe shadows do it all the time and it's just that no one notices? (That latter would fit with lots of weirdness reported by people, like shadow people etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Its very hard to prove something does not exist. It is possible that shadows work differently here but without any data on that i refer to our real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T17:44:08-08:00","id":1555776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555744#post1555744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its very hard to prove something does not exist. It is possible that shadows work differently here but without any data on that i refer to our real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows have always worked differently in 2e, The fact that one can turn themselves + possessions into animated shadow without needing life or matter 4 is a prime example of shadows/death being different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T04:23:26-08:00","id":1555793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555776#post1555776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadows have always worked differently in 2e, The fact that one can turn themselves + possessions into animated shadow without needing life or matter 4 is a prime example of shadows/death being different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You also dont need life to turn into a living flame. Thats a feature of the system coming away from arkanum combos and not of shadows themselves. Making shadows material is also not an argument as from third dot we can do things defying nature. In this discusion we should focus on the true nature of aspects of reality and that is contained in the 1 dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 11-23-2025, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T07:14:38-08:00","id":1555796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555793#post1555793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. You also dont need life to turn into a living flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Transforming into a living pillar of fire&quot; using Life and Forces is literally the example the corebook uses for Patterning spells requiring two Arcana in the same section you're referencing for the capabilities of Compelling spells \u2014 see page 124.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this discusion we should focus on the true nature of aspects of reality and that is contained in the 1 dot. </div> </div> </div>In which case I can point to the multiple times I've seen weird shadows from lensing and other refractive effects through nominally clear air or water in real life and thus have no especial difficulty believing basic Death magic can occlude the light enough in an area that the standard penalty for a difficult-but-not-too-difficult task applies to visual Perception rolls and ranged combat, rising to the level of effects associated with pitch darkness with extra Reach equivalent to upscaling it to a Ruling spell.<br /> <br /> The spell is called Deepen Shadows. It makes shadows deeper. An argument that it's too extreme an effect for a Compelling spell because it doesn't technically say you can't use it in ways that are blatantly unnatural is both forgetting how Paradox and Dissonance work and ignoring that without Reaching or taking penalties for extra spell factors the spell has a Duration measured in turns and affects an area the breadth of a human wingspan.<br /> <br /> Forget comparisons to Forces for a moment: the two sample Matter Compelling spells allow a character to not get wet in a rainstorm and make mechanical switches flip themselves, and the Space spell for messing with a subject's Speed in a way that is visually alarming is also Compelling, as is the Time spell to make <i>every possible delay</i> occur for a subject trying to get somewhere. &quot;Compelling spells can't create obviously unnatural effects&quot; is self-evidently false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T08:36:01-08:00","id":1555800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555796#post1555796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Transforming into a living pillar of fire&quot; using Life and Forces is literally the example the corebook uses for Patterning spells requiring two Arcana in the same section you're referencing for the capabilities of Compelling spells \u2014 see page 124.<br /> <br /> In which case I can point to the multiple times I've seen weird shadows from lensing and other refractive effects through nominally clear air or water in real life and thus have no especial difficulty believing basic Death magic can occlude the light enough in an area that the standard penalty for a difficult-but-not-too-difficult task applies to visual Perception rolls and ranged combat, rising to the level of effects associated with pitch darkness with extra Reach equivalent to upscaling it to a Ruling spell.<br /> <br /> The spell is called Deepen Shadows. It makes shadows deeper. An argument that it's too extreme an effect for a Compelling spell because it doesn't technically say you can't use it in ways that are blatantly unnatural is both forgetting how Paradox and Dissonance work and ignoring that without Reaching or taking penalties for extra spell factors the spell has a Duration measured in turns and affects an area the breadth of a human wingspan.<br /> <br /> Forget comparisons to Forces for a moment: the two sample Matter Compelling spells allow a character to not get wet in a rainstorm and make mechanical switches flip themselves, and the Space spell for messing with a subject's Speed in a way that is visually alarming is also Compelling, as is the Time spell to make <i>every possible delay</i> occur for a subject trying to get somewhere. &quot;Compelling spells can't create obviously unnatural effects&quot; is self-evidently false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then tell me the exact range of compeling not with examples but the general exact range of posibilities given any part of reality if as you claim its not reserved to the laws of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T08:50:38-08:00","id":1555801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555800#post1555800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then tell me the exact range of compeling not with examples but the general exact range of posibilities given any part of reality if as you claim its not reserved to the laws of nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not logistically possible to do so conclusively in a collaborative storytelling game and I don't particularly feel like doing so if you're going to wave off <i>four other examples</i> from <i>three other Arcana</i> as supporting evidence.<br /> <br /> Compelling spells are spells. They are subject to Paradox and Dissonance and their general tendency to be subtle does not undo the fact that they are the least durable to Dissonance. If you can buy someone using them to stay dry in a torrential downpour you ought be able to buy their enhancing shadows to be as hard to see in as a nightclub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T09:21:27-08:00","id":1555802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555801#post1555801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not logistically possible to do so conclusively in a collaborative storytelling game and I don't particularly feel like doing so if you're going to wave off <i>four other examples</i> from <i>three other Arcana</i> as supporting evidence.<br /> <br /> Compelling spells are spells. They are subject to Paradox and Dissonance and their general tendency to be subtle does not undo the fact that they are the least durable to Dissonance. If you can buy someone using them to stay dry in a torrential downpour you ought be able to buy their enhancing shadows to be as hard to see in as a nightclub.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see any waterproof spell in the main book.<br /> <br /> Discernig practices exact limits should be possible, Thats one of the main selling points from ascension to awakening: more strict and predictable spell rules. Operating solely on vibes seems problematic. The compeling spell says: &quot;spells nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for your previous examples with switches and time. As you mentioned by yourself evry posible delay is every POSSIBLE delay. The greenlight/redlight spell should be more of a fate thing anyway. If we were to get any consistent thing from it is that compeling can speed up existing phenemena so speeding up time i guess would make sense.<br /> <br /> As for fliping swithes i find this one harder to refufe. On one hand its perfectly natural that mechanical partes ment to move can move on the other making them move on their own seems problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T10:05:44-08:00","id":1555803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555802#post1555802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see any waterproof spell in the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Lodestone. The spell literally gives keeping dry in a rainstorm as one of the things its repelling effect can accomplish, and its attracting effect can still turn any imparted movement into a direction that's not fighting gravity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discernig practices exact limits should be possible, Thats one of the main selling points from ascension to awakening: more strict and predictable spell rules. Operating solely on vibes seems problematic. The compeling spell says: &quot;spells nudge a preferred but possible outcome into reality.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And 2e accomplishes that compared to 1e by putting the basic effects of a spell at the level appropriate to the Practice they describe instead of arbitrarily increasing their dot rating to suit a power level or class of phenomena \u2014 it's why now you only strictly need to be an Adept to deal aggravated damage and why Matter and Life no longer set spells' Practices by solid/liquid/gas or base/median/advanced life.<br /> <br /> Shadows are extremely imprecise and ephemeral as mundane phenomena go in the first place \u2014 the other pre-Disciple shadow-affecting spell lets you completely control the shapes of existing shadows, and even without narratively treating a shadow as an independent thing the existence of a material atmosphere is all that one needs to direct the light whose absence shapes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T13:52:03-08:00","id":1555806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555803#post1555803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And 2e accomplishes that compared to 1e by putting the basic effects of a spell at the level appropriate to the Practice they describe instead of arbitrarily increasing their dot rating to suit a power level or class of phenomena \u2014 it's why now you only strictly need to be an Adept to deal aggravated damage and why Matter and Life no longer set spells' Practices by solid/liquid/gas or base/median/advanced life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the best changes they made between 1e and 2e.<br /> <br /> Reach as a soft limit while practices define what is possible with each dot level - in 1e you would need an extra dot to get aggravated damage, in 2e you need an extra reach (and an extra dot gives you an extra safe reach - but you choose whether to overreach). <br /> <br /> So it is no longer Bashing at 3 dots, Lethal at 4 dots, and Aggravated at 5 dots. Instead what you can do follows from your practices. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadows are extremely imprecise and ephemeral as mundane phenomena go in the first place \u2014 the other pre-Disciple shadow-affecting spell lets you completely control the shapes of existing shadows, and even without narratively treating a shadow as an independent thing the existence of a material atmosphere is all that one needs to direct the light whose absence shapes it. </div> </div> </div>This is my thinking. Not only is the Shadow a part of the 5-fold soul, and metaphysically a thing which 1/5 vampires have to deal with, but shadows seem to move on their own in the real world, often unpredictably, they almost feel alive; so in Mage this is taken to be true where Shadows have an objective existence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T13:59:53-08:00","id":1555809,"title":"","content":"If we were to asume that then what are the properties of those objective existence shadows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T14:56:42-08:00","id":1555811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555809#post1555809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were to asume that then what are the properties of those objective existence shadows?</div> </div> </div> </div>He just said. In Chronicles, most explicitly in Mummy but also in Mage and Vampire and Changeling, your shadow is the part of your soul that corresponds to your reflection, echo, and other likenesses and lingering forms, which is the thematic reason why the Arcanum that deals with ghosts \u2014 the persisting image of the deceased \u2014 also deals with shadows, and why the Gross counterpart to that Subtle manifestation is Matter (of which statues, paintings, etc are typically composed).<br /> <br /> A changeling's shadow reveals their true nature to other fae even when they've strengthened the Mask that disguises them as a mundane person to extend to the senses of other fae; a Hollow Mekhet casts no shadow and leaves no sign of themselves in recorded or transmitted media and the hungry ghost that took those things when it separated from them can <i>only</i> manifest in reflections, phone calls, etc; the Sheut Pillar stands alongside metaphysical phenomena like a person's essential nature, heart, or identity, and the powers it enables mostly deal with darkness, ghosts, the state of Twilight, and the living dead.<br /> <br /> Again, the spell's effect is that a targeted area gets dark enough to create a Tilt that Deviant has apply for smoke grenades, thick fog, or a Magnitude 1 effect from the Pyrokinesis Variation. &quot;The shadows intensify to the level of being in a cloud&quot; is not beyond the realm of possibility when Matter 1 lets you prevent tear gas from reaching your location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T04:39:42-08:00","id":1555823,"title":"","content":"We also have two other creatures which are 'of shadow' - a Shade, in mummy, which is a different type of ghost but which feeds on vice amd spilled blood, has no anchor but is affected by bright lights. And of course everyone's favourite Shadow Owls, the Strix (though they may be more likely the spirits humans never had... and thus not a shadow).<br /> <br /> For a mage perspective, looking at what the various practices can do with Shadows is informative. You've got shadow equipment at ruling; so you can get a 2 dot lock pick, or sword/shield... (compared to the real material platonic forms which Prime has access to, or the immaterial cast-offs which Death can drag from twilight into the physical for different magically created objects); up to Shadow Form, with Patterning, where the subject is transformed into their Shadow - similar to pushing someone into twilight, their body is still their body, it is just in a different state of matter now, and the Shadow state is more like a custom thing, rather than a fully detailed ruleset for twilight entities...<br /> <br /> There is no example Making spell, but you should be able to Make a Shadow retainer (like how Eidolon uses the retainer merit, despite being a Making spell, which seems like it should be way beyond adding a few merit dots). And Unmaking should allow removal of people's shadows - with all the implications mentioned above: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a Hollow Mekhet casts no shadow and leaves no sign of themselves in recorded or transmitted media </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T06:14:31-08:00","id":1555974,"title":"","content":"Are the Sorcerers from mage any different than those from mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T06:31:10-08:00","id":1555975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555974#post1555974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Sorcerers from mage any different than those from mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage: the Awakening does not have &quot;sorcerers&quot; as a named discrete concept. The sorcerers of Mage: the Ascension are roughly similar, but given that Mummy's sorcerers exist in the context of Mummy there's a little more specificity for them than &quot;any unAwakened magic used by mortals.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T11:23:08-08:00","id":1555985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555974#post1555974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Sorcerers from mage any different than those from mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean like linear magic from Ascension, then unfortunately there are not. However, the use of the Occult skill for non-template dependent magic is expanded upon in <i>Hurt Locker</i>. If you want a character with minor mage abilities, there are the Proximi, people who inherited magic through their bloodline, as well as a curse. They are covered in page 307 of the mage 2ed core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T13:27:56-08:00","id":1555992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555974#post1555974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Sorcerers from mage any different than those from mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, depends mostly on you.<br /> <br /> Nothing specifically states how they differ from a conceptual level. Mummy Sorcerers have somewhat specific rules, so they're not exactly how &quot;sorcerer&quot; in any other book, but it may be just the rules of a given book.<br /> <br /> Mage doesn't really have Sorcerers, but there is magic that common humans can use. Geist and some other books also have means for humans to use magic without a minor template (and some books have Merits that serve as Minor Templates). The relationship between all those non-splat &quot;sorcerers&quot;, though, is completely up to you.<br /> <br /> It's like Mummy having Immortals that are extremely similar to the ones found in the book <i>Immortals</i>, and the rules are completely compatible. Are they the same thing? The game won't tell you that at all.<br /> <br /> But as far as it goes, I'd say Mummy's rules for sorcerers are simple and good enough for broad use, so you can do worse than using them with whatever splat you want, up to and including Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1555985#post1555985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean like linear magic from Ascension, then unfortunately there are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not it.<br /> <br /> Mummy uses a system more similar to the one in <i>Hurt Locker</i>, with a few twists to use the splat-specific resource and give Sorcerers reason to seek out Mummies.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T04:02:19-08:00","id":1556122,"title":"","content":"Does a weapon with appropriate form (a simple bow for Acanthus) or appropriate material (a silver mace for acanthus) qualify as a Weapon yantra or it needs both of the qualities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T06:39:15-08:00","id":1556124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556122#post1556122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a weapon with appropriate form (a simple bow for Acanthus) or appropriate material (a silver mace for acanthus) qualify as a Weapon yantra or it needs both of the qualities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what I can see in page 121, it would need to have either form or material to be a Path Tool. So an Obrimos could use a steel mace or one adorned with gold filigree, a Thyrsus could use a copper or stone mace, a Mastigos an iron or brass mace, and a Moros any mace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T08:01:37-08:00","id":1556125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556122#post1556122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a weapon with appropriate form (a simple bow for Acanthus) or appropriate material (a silver mace for acanthus) qualify as a Weapon yantra or it needs both of the qualities?</div> </div> </div> </div>The expanded charts on pages 47 and 48 of Signs of Sorcery make it pretty clear that weapons and vehicles aren't subject to the material restrictions that apply to the simpler tool types of cups, coins, rods and mirrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T13:00:32-08:00","id":1556131,"title":"","content":"Ok then, for example, if an Acanthus have a silver mace can he use it as a Weapon path tool or is he limited in using it as another kind of path tool, like a Mirror?<br /> Also, then each kind of knife counts as a weapon tool for any path no matter how they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T13:26:31-08:00","id":1556132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556131#post1556131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok then, for example, if an Acanthus have a silver mace can he use it as a Weapon path tool or is he limited in using it as another kind of path tool, like a Mirror?<br /> Also, then each kind of knife counts as a weapon tool for any path no matter how they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>The weapon is the weapon. Knives notwithstanding, weapon Path tools need to be the type of weapons that correspond to that Path; a mace is not a precise weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T13:31:30-08:00","id":1556133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556122#post1556122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a weapon with appropriate form (a simple bow for Acanthus) or appropriate material (a silver mace for acanthus) qualify as a Weapon yantra or it needs both of the qualities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intention is either a knife made of the appropriate material OR an appropriate form of weapon. So the silver mace probably doesn't qualify for an Acanthus as it's not a knife or a 'precision weapon'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-03T14:43:00-08:00","id":1556137,"title":"","content":"I can't even think of an example of a precision weapon that I would accept as such and isn't a knife.<br /> <br /> Even knifes when used for precision are more tools than weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T03:10:05-08:00","id":1556140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556137#post1556137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't even think of an example of a precision weapon that I would accept as such and isn't a knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with rapiers and bows?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even knifes when used for precision are more tools than weapons. </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends how much you choose to carry over the descriptions from <i>Tome of the Mysteries</i>, but daggers designed for precision strikes between armour is a not uncommon idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T09:17:42-08:00","id":1556146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556140#post1556140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with rapiers and bows?<br /> <br /> I suppose it depends how much you choose to carry over the descriptions from <i>Tome of the Mysteries</i>, but daggers designed for precision strikes between armour is a not uncommon idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has a lot to do with too much learning about actual weapon fight IRL.<br /> <br /> Rapiers... I can see the case, although not really. There's no such a thing as a precision strike with the tip of a meter long metal stick. But sure, as a fantasy trope people tend to conflate pierce with precision, I guess.<br /> <br /> Precision strikes between armor is basically using a tool, even with a specialized weapon it's a very particular technique with limited opportunities for use. At leas as far as it goes in a real battle.<br /> <br /> Bows? Not even close, that's just ridiculous. Target practicing isn't combat, you can do that with anything, it doesn't make a weapon precise. Bows are less precise than a shotgun, and I wouldn't call that a precise weapon, or any gun for that matter. Precision requires control, and you can't really control were a projectile lands after you let it go.<br /> <br /> Again, though, that may be both a severe take on the meaning of &quot;precision&quot; and demanding too much &quot;realism&quot;, so I'm open to arguments on lowering this bar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T10:02:05-08:00","id":1556148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556146#post1556146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, though, that may be both a severe take on the meaning of &quot;precision&quot; and demanding too much &quot;realism&quot;, so I'm open to arguments on lowering this bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the &quot;argument&quot; is that this is about the weapons' utility as symbolic aids for spellcasting, so &quot;realism&quot; doesn't enter into it unless a character is using that realism to recognize additional symbolic latitude (or contrariwise, experiencing a mental block on recognizing applicable semiotics because of it).<br /> <br /> &quot;Precise&quot; weapons in that context are mostly going to be lighter-looking piercing weapons, just like how a whip is a &quot;cruel&quot; weapon and a double-edged sword is a &quot;noble&quot; weapon. The symbolism of the weapon is &quot;this hits a small area and can thus be used to strike precisely,&quot; which isn't communicated with crushing weapons like maces or hammers or with weapons designed to make big cuts \u2014 the Ars Nova uses blackjacks as an example Acanthus weapon because they're used mainly for blows to the head (often as part of a surprise attack), which is harder to hit than the body in general. The weapons of the Acanthus are the tools of meticulous planners and quick-witted opportunists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T11:54:16-08:00","id":1556149,"title":"","content":"I think that raises a question of how much the symbolism of a weapon, or of anything, should be defined by contemporary pop culture understanding of it.<br /> <br /> Is there a long-standing tradition of seeing a bow as a precision weapon? Or even a meticulous planning/quick-witted opportunist weapon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T12:07:02-08:00","id":1556150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556149#post1556149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that raises a question of how much the symbolism of a weapon, or of anything, should be defined by contemporary pop culture understanding of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have the qualifications for Environment Yantras right there in the corebook along with the explicit statement that the mage has to recognize the symbolism of a tool to use it as one.<br /> <br /> Masterminds seldom have an obvious weapon associated with them, but the go-to feats for a bow are striking targets that are very small or far away. Similarly, while most anyone can use anything as a weapon in theory, characters who think on their feet but keep a consistent weapon on them tend to go for things that are easy to wield and able to decide a conflict swiftly, because big swings of oversized weapons have larger spreads of physical and tactical failure points in the absence of the kind of overwhelming strength that doesn't <i>need</i> precision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T14:38:37-08:00","id":1556153,"title":"","content":"I think the symbolism is a good enough argument, but a few other avenues arise:<br /> <br /> Has symbolism to be widely recognized, or just by the character, or yet something that &quot;exists&quot; in the Supernal regardless of recognition by denizens of the Lie? The character having to recognize the symbolism does not mean <i>any</i> symbolism they recognize flies.<br /> <br /> Because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>'s question is pertinent, not only in if modern pop culture is a valid reference, but what is or isn't. And that brings the more pertinent question if symbolism should be defined by the ST alone, or how much the player has input through the character. That question comes even before the ST needs any reference on how to make the decision.<br /> <br /> As for bows, I personally understand &quot;precision weapon&quot; and &quot;accurate shot&quot; as distinct symbolic classes, they don't hit the same tropes/archetypes/conceptual points for me at all, even before considerations if they would historically have this associations or not. Even because that brings another question: if bows are precision weapons, is this classification for ranged weapons even that relevant? Which ones are <b>not</b> precision weapons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-04T15:14:35-08:00","id":1556156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556153#post1556153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has symbolism to be widely recognized, or just by the character, or yet something that &quot;exists&quot; in the Supernal regardless of recognition by denizens of the Lie? The character having to recognize the symbolism does not mean <i>any</i> symbolism they recognize flies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The symbolism for Path Tools adds qualifiers like materials and weapon types to narrow them down <i>as a function of those Paths</i>, which is why I bring up meticulous planners and quick-witted opportunists \u2014 because those are the archetypes of the Acanthus Path as a collection of symbols focused on Time, Fate, Choice, and Consequence. The things you can do with it are still broadly defined by what Weapons can benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>'s question is pertinent, not only in if modern pop culture is a valid reference, but what is or isn't. And that brings the more pertinent question if symbolism should be defined by the ST alone, or how much the player has input through the character. That question comes even before the ST needs any reference on how to make the decision. </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of archetype, for which personal idiosyncracy usually has little relevance. Changeling 2e approaches Regalia in a similar manner \u2014 giving advice for coming up with new Regalia starting with the theme or with the symbol \u2014 and Signs of Sorcery gives Prelates and entire five alternate forms of Path Tool with their own symbolic applications in the Profane Forms.<br /> <br /> These are bog-standard +1 Yantras that technically have their benefits duplicated as part of basic Dedication \u2014 the point of them is to contribute to the aesthetics of the Paths moreso than to restrict their use in spellcasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for bows, I personally understand &quot;precision weapon&quot; and &quot;accurate shot&quot; as distinct symbolic classes, they don't hit the same tropes/archetypes/conceptual points for me at all, even before considerations if they would historically have this associations or not. Even because that brings another question: if bows are precision weapons, is this classification for ranged weapons even that relevant? Which ones are <b>not</b> precision weapons? </div> </div> </div>Because the Ars Nova being a distinct school of thought significantly narrows the range of ranged weapons present among the classical archetypes \u2014 most things that pre-date the crossbow are either bows or throwing weapons, and as a weapon that propels its projectiles through stored energy in the weapon itself rather than the arc of the character's arm accuracy is more readily associated with the wielder's ability to see (and foresee) their target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T02:11:40-08:00","id":1556164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556153#post1556153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even because that brings another question: if bows are precision weapons, is this classification for ranged weapons even that relevant? Which ones are <b>not</b> precision weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the only clarification we ever get is <i>Tome of the Mysteries</i>, where yeah, it does actually list other ranged weapons.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I think there's an unspoken assumption that 2e carries over from 1e that firearms don't count:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it stands (and what Mage assumes), Path weapons can only comprise hand weapons and simple human-powered machines such as bows, slings and atlatls. Any firearms, explosives or electricity-based weapons can only be turned into tools by the Adamantine Arrow and Free Council. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T05:08:25-08:00","id":1556165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556164#post1556164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the only clarification we ever get is <i>Tome of the Mysteries</i>, where yeah, it does actually list other ranged weapons.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I think there's an unspoken assumption that 2e carries over from 1e that firearms don't count:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall Yantras really being a thing in 1e! What part are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T05:18:26-08:00","id":1556166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556165#post1556165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall Yantras really being a thing in 1e! What part are you referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have said: Page 99.<br /> <br /> Yantra weren't a thing, but magical tools were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T13:22:26-08:00","id":1556188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556156#post1556156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of archetype, for which personal idiosyncracy usually has little relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I wanted to know, because that means while <i>the player may argue</i> if something fits, the character has limited weight on it.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing in favor of being too rigid, but just want to understand how the ST should adjudicate such things when going by the spirit of the rule instead of by a list of pre-aproved examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556164#post1556164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only clarification we ever get is <i>Tome of the Mysteries</i>, where yeah, it does actually list other ranged weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm less interested in a list than in the reasoning behind them.<br /> <br /> My gut feeling for this is that ranged weapons need their own classifications, I really don't see bows being more linked to precision than most any ranged weapon.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's a lot of characters and media that depict archers as defined by their precision. But so do most any other ranged character. Throw dagger, sling, pistol, rifle, crossbow, bumerangue, any character that masters ranged combat is almost always depicted as extremely precise. Even when they have something else as a key trait, it's on top of accuracy or an explanation for it. Ranged weapons that don't have this archetype are either explosive or massive enough to work as artillery, or being wielded by characters for whom they're secondary (and even then).<br /> <br /> Heck, Captain's America shield is a major &quot;precision&quot; weapon, not only used for precise hits, but precise enough to bounce around in the way the character predicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:34:40-08:00","id":1556198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556188#post1556188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I wanted to know, because that means while <i>the player may argue</i> if something fits, the character has limited weight on it.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing in favor of being too rigid, but just want to understand how the ST should adjudicate such things when going by the spirit of the rule instead of by a list of pre-aproved examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the case of Path Tools in particular the position I'm taking is that the aesthetics, symbolism, and themes painted by the lists are the primary guideline for whether something is appropriate to that Path. Helicopters and black sedans are in the Obrimos's Ars Nova examples for vehicles because they're a thing that communicates Power; the same section of the chart for the Thyrsus lists ATVs and Land Rovers because as off-road vehicles they have a relation to Boundaries, while the Mastigos have sports cars and motorcycles because of that Path's thematic ties to Transgression and Confrontation.<br /> <br /> The spirit of the rule is &quot;does this tool fit the Path as-presented?&quot; and the core ideas of the Paths are pretty consistently communicated for the purposes of detailed correspondence. (Some of the more esoteric categories may require a reference book or Internet search, but the vibes still largely match up.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My gut feeling for this is that ranged weapons need their own classifications, I really don't see bows being more linked to precision than most any ranged weapon. </div> </div> </div>Most ranged weapons that have an archetype built up around them are either throwing weapons that don't visually communicate range or precision (axes, knives, etc) or, setting aside the question of how viable firearms are as symbols outside the context of the Adamantine Arrow's broader bailiwick, can be used practically from near range and/or have sights or other aiding mechanisms. Trick-shots are impressive for gunslingers because historically pistols were sufficiently inaccurate that you could have duels with them with the fact that you were prepared to risk the chance that a shot would hit you being enough to make your statement without it being guaranteed that you would die, and an arrow is one of the faster projectiles in common awareness before the spread of firearms.<br /> <br /> If you see a character wielding a bow, you know they fight at a distance, can safely assume they aim solely with their senses, and can see from the way the weapon works that they are not relying on rifling or scopes to ensure their shot goes straight and hits the place they wanted to hit. This is an appropriate weapon for the Path of Witches and Enchanters to use to make &quot;direct, decisive action upon the world (or a person)&quot; with magic.<br /> <br /> Also, to make a weaker argument for the sake of addressing another part of the symbolism, you don't get boomerangs, slings or rifles used to illustrate Zeno's paradoxes because the bow and arrow has archetypal weight and ease of use for that particular meditation on time.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, the thing for ranged weapons in general is that firearms are implicitly not applicable as Path Tools and that the ability to serve as a spellcasting aid in the capacity as <i>a weapon</i> is the greater concern for its utility than whether you're using a ranged or non-ranged weapon for casting a spell whose range that distinction is irrelevant to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T21:58:57-08:00","id":1556222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556198#post1556198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trick-shots are impressive for gunslingers because historically pistols were sufficiently inaccurate that you could have duels with them with the fact that you were prepared to risk the chance that a shot would hit you being enough to make your statement without it being guaranteed that you would die, and an arrow is one of the faster projectiles in common awareness before the spread of firearms.<br /> <br /> If you see a character wielding a bow, you know they fight at a distance, can safely assume they aim solely with their senses, and can see from the way the weapon works that they are not relying on rifling or scopes to ensure their shot goes straight and hits the place they wanted to hit. This is an appropriate weapon for the Path of Witches and Enchanters to use to make &quot;direct, decisive action upon the world (or a person)&quot; with magic.<br /> <br /> Also, to make a weaker argument for the sake of addressing another part of the symbolism, you don't get boomerangs, slings or rifles used to illustrate Zeno's paradoxes because the bow and arrow has archetypal weight and ease of use for that particular meditation on time.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, the thing for ranged weapons in general is that firearms are implicitly not applicable as Path Tools and that the ability to serve as a spellcasting aid in the capacity as <i>a weapon</i> is the greater concern for its utility than whether you're using a ranged or non-ranged weapon for casting a spell whose range that distinction is irrelevant to.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all I want to say that I agree with most of what you say, I'm picking the parts I have comments on, but I'm not ignoring the rest.<br /> <br /> Historically bows have been used in combat for volleys, not for precise shots. Just as trick-shots are impressive because pistols are actually inaccurate, so are bows. Both weapons are known for accuracy because of tricks and practices that impressed precisely because they're actually hard to do. And I repeat, this is the archetype tied to any and every ranged weapon that isn't artillery-like. Certainly not all weapons will be promptly recognized as ranged, but whenever they are, the archetype of precision applies even though it's realistically false.<br /> <br /> I also don't see why the use of scopes or something would detract from the concept. For me it actually enhances it, especially if we talk about &quot;direct, decisive action upon the world (or a person)&quot;, as far as the Symbol pertains to the weapon, not to the user. Upon seeing a ranged weapon, I picture as a trope accurate shots, regardless if because the user has the skill or the weapon has the tools to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Bows have a strong archetypal weight on Zeno's Paradox because arrows have a perceivable-yet-straight-ish motion. This has nothing to do with precision, although I do think it's actually a better reason to associate them to the Path than the notion of &quot;precision weapons&quot;. They really work as a meditation on time and fate better than other ranged weapons.<br /> <br /> And for the last part, I fail to see why firearms can't be Path Tools, how exactly this proscription helps the game, and I'm really unconvinced about the &quot;precision&quot; archetype applied to bows and not other ranged weapons. I'm not really worried that this or that category should apply as I'm aware that at the end of the day this is just, <i><b>as far as balance goes</b></i>, about aesthetics and procurement. In the end what matters is that preparing those tools take some thought, but not straining effort, and enhance the symbolism both as a factor in the fiction and a theme in the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T06:33:08-08:00","id":1556234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556188#post1556188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see bows being more linked to precision than most any ranged weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say they are. It's just an example. From the extra material, yeah, basically any ranged weapon that isn't a firearm can count for the Acanthus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, Captain's America shield is a major &quot;precision&quot; weapon, not only used for precise hits, but precise enough to bounce around in the way the character predicted. </div> </div> </div>Okay. I mean, if you put Captain America in your game and your players steal his shield... Sure, why not? Think I'd be tempted to give them a +2 for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T06:34:46-08:00","id":1556235,"title":"","content":"My take about the precision thing is that it s less related to &quot;i can get a bullseye from one hundred meter&quot; an more related to &quot;the hit point is so small that i can hit a glass without hurting the hand holding it&quot;.<br /> Expecially about rapiers over other melee weapons, in my experience it s way easier to hit with a spear over a sword.<br /> The thing is i think, a blade that cut suggest less control in relation to a tip over which part i can willfully hit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T11:03:32-08:00","id":1556254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556235#post1556235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take about the precision thing is that it s less related to &quot;i can get a bullseye from one hundred meter&quot; an more related to &quot;the hit point is so small that i can hit a glass without hurting the hand holding it&quot;.<br /> Expecially about rapiers over other melee weapons, in my experience it s way easier to hit with a spear over a sword.<br /> The thing is i think, a blade that cut suggest less control in relation to a tip over which part i can willfully hit</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get that, but then again it becomes too broad an archetype because most ranged weapons, obvious or not, are like that in fiction. Even when you have a bladed or blunt object, upon being used as a ranged weapon it all comes to hitting the right spot, often with little room for error for some reason. Even characters that throw handaxes, when it really matters instead of just being part of a larger melee scene, they're doing stuff like cutting ropes from a large distance and other actions I would definitely describe as &quot;precision&quot; if we get it like that.<br /> <br /> And a concept that's too broad may become a problem, not because it's unbalanced, but because it ends up detracting from this aspect of the narrative. It stops being about the character carefully preparing their tools and becomes them justifying any BS to not have to worry. It also makes the Symbol harder to notice or to link characters using the same Symbol.<br /> <br /> Bows as a meditation on time and fate really is an approach I liked more. It's sufficiently specific, very interesting and quite fitting for the Acanthus, maybe even more than daggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T11:12:28-08:00","id":1556256,"title":"","content":"How would one close a Verge? Would it be some powerful Unmaking Practice, related to the Verge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:09:04-08:00","id":1556259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556256#post1556256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one close a Verge? Would it be some powerful Unmaking Practice, related to the Verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest way I can think of is to use a <i>Quarantine</i> spell over the physical area where you find the Verge's entrance, with indefinite duration and permanent relinquishment, maybe with the extra Reach to add a Key, so it can be selectively accessed if necessary.<br /> <br /> Depending on whether Sleepers knew the area well, additional spellwork might be necessary to keep Disbelief from eroding the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T13:42:29-08:00","id":1556265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556256#post1556256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one close a Verge? Would it be some powerful Unmaking Practice, related to the Verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to depend almost entirely on what &quot;opened&quot; the Verge and what's keeping it open \u2014 this isn't like with a locus, where the phenomenon follows consistent causes and has circumstances that allow it to reform itself. Short of going through a series of Scrutiny rolls to get the necessary information to sort it out, your main other options are to section it off with Space magic as Afini describes above or hope it sorts itself out with time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T06:00:32-08:00","id":1556288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556259#post1556259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simplest way I can think of is to use a <i>Quarantine</i> spell over the physical area where you find the Verge's entrance, with indefinite duration and permanent relinquishment, maybe with the extra Reach to add a Key, so it can be selectively accessed if necessary.<br /> <br /> Depending on whether Sleepers knew the area well, additional spellwork might be necessary to keep Disbelief from eroding the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, is disbelief an issue of you can add the optional Mind 4 or Time 5 effects?<br /> <br /> Actually maybe Time 5 is a bad option since it alters the timeline, the Mind 4 optional effect directly alters the memories off anyone who &quot;knew the area well&quot;...<br /> <br /> That said, mundanely closing it seems more sustainable. Perhaps disbelief is not enough to erode the effects, and to be honest I've only really thought about opening a Verge... I think Satchel is correct. You have to study it, maybe Prime and Fate/Time to help understand how it came to be, but some Verges seem to be permanent. I think it would be an interesting mystery in itself. Definitely something to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T09:21:08-08:00","id":1556300,"title":"","content":"Paradox, from at least what I've read, <i>does</i> slowly erode Supernal things in the Fallen World. If enough Sleepers encounter something Supernal, their disbelief <i>eventually</i> causes it to collapse and disappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T10:46:57-08:00","id":1556304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556300#post1556300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox, from at least what I've read, <i>does</i> slowly erode Supernal things in the Fallen World. If enough Sleepers encounter something Supernal, their disbelief <i>eventually</i> causes it to collapse and disappear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally yes, but Verges may be the one exception. Notably, spells cast in a natural verge are not subject to dissonance (Emanation realms are also immune to dissonance). <br /> <br /> And the edges of a verge naturally cloak supernal phenomena so that sleepers outside tend to not be able to see the effects from without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T13:26:57-08:00","id":1556308,"title":"","content":"Ok, question concerning Verges:<br /> A Verge is blatantly supernatural, with giant onyx towers shaped like clawed habds, salty barriws full of ghosts who answer questions if fed blood, and so on, but theae efects are often hidden in Twilight.<br /> <br /> What does 'hidden in Twilight' <i>mean</i>, exactly?<br /> \u25cf Sleepers can't peeceive them, obviously.<br /> \u25a0 Can Sleepwalkers/Proximi perceive them?<br /> <br /> \u25cf Do mages interact with Verges without the need for magic?<br /> \u25a0 Do they need Active Mage Sight up to do so?<br /> \u25a0 Need a mage enter some sort of Twilight frequency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T13:54:09-08:00","id":1556310,"title":"","content":"So Tremere lose their Path abilities, and on NH-NA p. 132-133 it mentions them having a &quot;soul sight&quot; which acts as active death sight and the soul marks spell in one. This is at first seems a replacement to mage sight, but it's not in actuality... it's just taking one aspect of an Arcanum's specific seen things and a spell-like ability attached to it, not the general use mage sight with all its other quirks.<br /> <br /> Mage sight is one of the single most defining things of what a mage can do and how their &quot;binding&quot; to a Watchtower manifests, each one tending to see certain things in each path (though still personalized), so what would a Tremere's mage sight actually be/look like? Considering their increased Obsessions, it wouldn't make sense if they lacked the ability to unravel Mysteries with their sight, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T13:58:10-08:00","id":1556312,"title":"","content":"The Tremere are corrupted echoes of mages. They bartered away their souls for mere extended life. They see <i>everything</i> in a narrower light. They're parasites. Should it surprise you their Mage Sight has shrunken accordingly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T15:05:48-08:00","id":1556315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556310#post1556310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Tremere lose their Path abilities, and on NH-NA p. 132-133 it mentions them having a &quot;soul sight&quot; which acts as active death sight and the soul marks spell in one. This is at first seems a replacement to mage sight, but it's not in actuality... it's just taking one aspect of an Arcanum's specific seen things and a spell-like ability attached to it, not the general use mage sight with all its other quirks.<br /> <br /> Mage sight is one of the single most defining things of what a mage can do and how their &quot;binding&quot; to a Watchtower manifests, each one tending to see certain things in each path (though still personalized), so what would a Tremere's mage sight actually be/look like? Considering their increased Obsessions, it wouldn't make sense if they lacked the ability to unravel Mysteries with their sight, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hollow works as Gnosis except where noted. Soul Sight is saying that, without having to engage Active Mage Sight or cast a spell (or have any mastery of the Death Arcanum), the Tremere can detect if a person has a soul and discern whether they're a supernatural being or similar soul-based information.<br /> <br /> They still have Mage Sight, and in fact it would make no sense if they didn't because Mage Sight is how mages parse High Speech, which the Tremere as an Order were historically proficient with. For simplicity's sake, I would follow the note in &quot;Bound to the Final Watchtower&quot; and treat their Sight as that of whatever Path has their highest-rated Subtle Arcanum as Ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T15:25:40-08:00","id":1556316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556308#post1556308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, question concerning Verges:<br /> A Verge is blatantly supernatural, with giant onyx towers shaped like clawed habds, salty barriws full of ghosts who answer questions if fed blood, and so on, but theae efects are often hidden in Twilight.<br /> <br /> What does 'hidden in Twilight' <i>mean</i>, exactly?<br /> \u25cf Sleepers can't peeceive them, obviously.<br /> \u25a0 Can Sleepwalkers/Proximi perceive them?<br /> <br /> \u25cf Do mages interact with Verges without the need for magic?<br /> \u25a0 Do they need Active Mage Sight up to do so?<br /> \u25a0 Need a mage enter some sort of Twilight frequency?</div> </div> </div> </div>See the relevant section in Signs of Sorcery:<br /> &quot;These paralocations can only be seen from inside of the Verge; from the other side they\u2019re conveniently obscured by fog, look and act like ordinary places, or vanish. The Lie conceals them through the most plausible, expedient means. If the Verge is destroyed or a paralocation somehow strays from its bounds, it degrades into ordinary phenomena. Sky castles fall to earth as Gothic follies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the lack of \u200belaboration on the bit from the corebook that you're referencing, &quot;disguised by Twilight&quot; can be taken to be being used in a similar fashion to how Demon sometimes uses it: &quot;This location/these phenomena exist in a way that mostly disregards the surrounding material world except where necessary.&quot; A Verge might only be able to be entered from certain points and outside of the heart of it \u2014 where a Thura might exist \u2014 any particularly obvious manifestations of the Supernal World are on a parallel track to what any surrounding mortals can see and/or are naturally veiled from recorded observation. If you've entered the Verge and haven't left it the you can see and interact with anything that's not separately invisible or intangible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T15:44:39-08:00","id":1556318,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T16:29:25-08:00","id":1556319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556315#post1556315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hollow works as Gnosis except where noted. Soul Sight is saying that, without having to engage Active Mage Sight or cast a spell (or have any mastery of the Death Arcanum), the Tremere can detect if a person has a soul and discern whether they're a supernatural being or similar soul-based information.<br /> <br /> They still have Mage Sight, and in fact it would make no sense if they didn't because Mage Sight is how mages parse High Speech, which the Tremere as an Order were historically proficient with. For simplicity's sake, I would follow the note in &quot;Bound to the Final Watchtower&quot; and treat their Sight as that of whatever Path has their highest-rated Subtle Arcanum as Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it should be special since their whole thing is separating from the paths... the ruling arcana at least makes sense through the lens of being able to carry over that affinity and then eventually build up the others but I feel like keeping the same path-bound mage sight would aggravate them to hell and back (aren't ruling arcana free to add too, and thus higher gnosis ones would have impossibly expansive sight compared to normal path + legacy mages?). Guess it's something I could always brew for my own game though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T17:30:59-08:00","id":1556488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1536079#post1536079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does <i>Gain Skill </i>work on a target who unknowingly had that ability? Lets say its cast on a Sleepwalker to give them the expression skill, but they already had two dots, would it still boost the ones that were there by the spell's Potency ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have the same doubt, would <i>Gain Skill</i> include the effects of <i>Enhance Skill</i> if you already have the skill?<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack has Intimidation 3, someone casts <i>Gain Skill</i> on him, with potence 1 for Intimidation. Would Jack have Intimidation 4 or 3 after the spell is cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T13:24:12-08:00","id":1556537,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> I'd probably allow it. <br /> <br /> Could always require a +1 reach for <i>Gain Skill</i> to act like <i>Enhance Skill?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T09:23:04-08:00","id":1556558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p. 61</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When used as a Magical Tool for the appropriate Path, the mage gains the 9-again quality on her spellcasting</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it mean that a non Path tool would not benefit (9-again on spellcasting) from being perfected? Something like Kassiterum mask for a Guardian of the Veil, or a Brontium ring for a Silver Ladder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T10:06:58-08:00","id":1556560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556558#post1556558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean that a non Path tool would not benefit (9-again on spellcasting) from being perfected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Like, the material is only relevant for Path tools, so having perfected materials is probably only relevant for Path tools.<br /> <br /> Also, on pg. 63 with regards to perfected non-metals:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they also give the 9-again quality to spellcasting when used as a Path Tool. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T15:47:40-08:00","id":1556574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556560#post1556560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. Like, the material is only relevant for Path tools, so having perfected materials is probably only relevant for Path tools.<br /> <br /> Also, on pg. 63 with regards to perfected non-metals:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, based on the Path Tools in the core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2ed Core p. 121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coins or <b>other symbols of material wealth</b></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would a signet ring count as a coin in this case?</li> <li>Which perfected metal would it serve it best? I am of the opinion that Orichalcum or Lunargent are the only valuable enough materials to count (and also their Amalgamated versions).</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T02:17:23-08:00","id":1556600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556574#post1556574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a signet ring count as a coin in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think so. I mean, jewellery in general has a lot of associations with material wealth (I mean, in many cases it literally <i>is</i> material wealth).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which perfected metal would it serve it best? I am of the opinion that Orichalcum or Lunargent are the only valuable enough materials to count (and also their Amalgamated versions). </div> </div> </div>I think the perfected metal to use is the one associated with your path. So for example, an Acanthus is going to want a Lunargent ring, whilst a Mastigos will want a siderite one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T10:20:09-08:00","id":1556614,"title":"","content":"The <i>Familiar </i>spell, shouldnt it have a Lasting Reach option? Otherwise every familiar (goetia, ghost, or spirit) is one dispellation away from breaking the bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T10:45:23-08:00","id":1556615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556614#post1556614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Familiar </i>spell, shouldnt it have a Lasting Reach option? Otherwise every familiar (goetia, ghost, or spirit) is one dispellation away from breaking the bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's the point.<br /> <br /> The spell is already a Duration-primary Adept-level effect that only works on mutually-willing parties, meaning anyone who can create a Familiar bond can make it last for a year with basic Advanced Duration and only needs one extra Reach, a -2 penalty, and a point of Mana to make it Indefinite if they aren't a Master or using a Rote.<br /> <br /> Remember also that dispellation spells default to suppressing the targeted spell for their Duration, that Familiar definitionally has at least two Subjects and needs at least Potency 5 to overcome its Withstand rating, and that without dedicating extra factors or Reach to Duration the dispellation will last a single turn before the spell reasserts itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T15:33:49-08:00","id":1556626,"title":"","content":"Whats the point of unveiling practice? Lets say we have a spell to scan a living organism based on the knowing practice. If the user encounters a veiling effect on the subject it would still be a clash of wills to determine with effect is stronger would it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T16:19:44-08:00","id":1556628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556626#post1556626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the point of unveiling practice? Lets say we have a spell to scan a living organism based on the knowing practice. If the user encounters a veiling effect on the subject it would still be a clash of wills to determine with effect is stronger would it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unveiling is about extending your sensory perception, while Knowing is about receiving information about a phenomenon directly. So, for example, an Unveiling will let you see ley lines you would not normally perceive, but a Knowing will tell you about what Resonance one has. An Unveiling will let you follow the ley lines to an interception, a Knowing will let you know the strength of the Hallow, if it's tass is volatile or plentiful, etc. An Unveiling will let you know something is tass, a Knowing will let you know if it has any unusual properties. <br /> <br /> Both Clash against a Veiling, but what you find out from winning the Clash will be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T07:16:46-08:00","id":1556645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556615#post1556615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's the point.<br /> <br /> The spell is already a Duration-primary Adept-level effect that only works on mutually-willing parties, meaning anyone who can create a Familiar bond can make it last for a year with basic Advanced Duration and only needs one extra Reach, a -2 penalty, and a point of Mana to make it Indefinite if they aren't a Master or using a Rote.<br /> <br /> Remember also that dispellation spells default to suppressing the targeted spell for their Duration, that Familiar definitionally has at least two Subjects and needs at least Potency 5 to overcome its Withstand rating, and that without dedicating extra factors or Reach to Duration the dispellation will last a single turn before the spell reasserts itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it commonly assumed that you need scale to include all subjects to suppress a spell?<br /> <br /> And comparatively if you can to disspell a spell with has one subject but a large area (like a Space spell which affect an area of space, rather than an AoE spell, but either will do) do you need to cover the same scale as the spell/AoE?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-15-2025, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T07:31:18-08:00","id":1556646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556645#post1556645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it comkonly assumed that you need scale to include all subjects to suppress a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need conjunctive Fate to suppress the target spell selectively for a limited number of subjects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And comparatively if you can to disspell a spell with has one subject but a large area (like a Space spell which affect an area of space, rather than an AoE spell, but either will do) do you need to cover the same scale as the spell/AoE? </div> </div> </div>I think the thing that makes intuitive sense, since Dispel Magic is not part of the Shielding Practice and both its effects and those of Supernal Dispellation are framed in terms of manipulating the spell's capacity to end, is that you need to cast Dispel Magic with a Scale factor that can encompass that of the target spell unless you have the ability to use Fate to selectively apply the effect.<br /> <br /> If a werewolf becoming Size 7 is enough to negate the effects of a spell cast for their human Size, targeting a spell should definitely have to account for the &quot;size&quot; of the spell in question, and at least in the case of Familiar and similar spells there is a distinct difference between the prospects of dispelling the bond and simply blocking one end of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T07:34:15-08:00","id":1556647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556626#post1556626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats the point of unveiling practice? Lets say we have a spell to scan a living organism based on the knowing practice. If the user encounters a veiling effect on the subject it would still be a clash of wills to determine with effect is stronger would it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Unveiling affects your own senses (or subject's senses) it allows you see things where ever you apply those senses (rather than just knowing something within a given spell area).<br /> <br /> So a knowing spell might be withstood by the subject you want to know about (Know Spirit is withstood by Rank, though Know Nature, the Mind equivalent, is not withstood, and nor are an other examples Knowing spells). But an Unveiling spell is cast on yourself - or another subject whose senses you want to enhance... So Unveiling spells would usually not be withstood (though Mental Scan is, telling me something is wrong, and that it is not actually an Unveiling spell... Likewise for the Death Spell Soul Marks)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the subject matters, you leave a signature Nimbus on your subject and a weak sympathetic connection between caster and subject. So Unveiling leaves less trace if you cast the unveiling spell on yourself.<br /> <br /> Lastly, with the Forces example spells, we have Tune-in (Knowing) and Reciever (Unveiling). Both let you gain information about signals (radio and infrasound signals respectively) but the knowing effect tell you what the signal means, so you don't need to translate, decrypt or use Mind's purview of communication; whereas the Unveiling effect just let's you hear whatever is there... So you might know there is a Whalesong, but not what the Whale is singing about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  grammar 12-15-2025, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T07:41:12-08:00","id":1556648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556646#post1556646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need conjunctive Fate to suppress the target spell selectively for a limited number of subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so my question is not can your partially suppress the spell, but do you need to take all the subjects into account (making it harder to dispell a spell with more subjects....) - there doesn't seem to be a RAW answer, but the example spell in question, when you do add fate - uses Scale for the number of subjects the spell is selectively suppressed for - which at least suggests to me that the author didn't consider Scale to already be needed (or less likely that adding Fate allows you to useless scale for partial dispellation)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I think the thing that makes intuitive sense, since Dispel Magic is not part of the Shielding Practice and both its effects and those of Supernal Dispellation are framed in terms of manipulating the spell's capacity to end, is that you need to cast Dispel Magic with a Scale factor that can encompass that of the target spell unless you have the ability to use Fate to selectively apply the effect.<br /> <br /> If a werewolf becoming Size 7 is enough to negate the effects of a spell cast for their human Size, targeting a spell should definitely have to account for the &quot;size&quot; of the spell in question, and at least in the case of Familiar and similar spells there is a distinct difference between the prospects of dispelling the bond and simply blocking one end of it. </div> </div> </div>I would tend to agree with this, but I don't know that it is the common interpretation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T08:04:37-08:00","id":1556651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556648#post1556648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so my question is not can your partially suppress the spell, but do you need to take all the subjects into account (making it harder to dispell a spell with more subjects....)</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, if you need a specific other Arcanum in order to selectively suppress a spell for some subjects and not others, you cannot do that otherwise, which means you normally need to take all the subjects into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T10:37:59-08:00","id":1556658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556651#post1556651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition, if you need a specific other Arcanum in order to selectively suppress a spell for some subjects and not others, you cannot do that otherwise, which means you normally need to take all the subjects into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm not talking about selective suppression. I am imagining you target the spell (default scale, size 0, 1 subject) rather than targeting all of the subjects of the spell (who you may not even be able to find).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T12:57:23-08:00","id":1556661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556658#post1556658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not talking about selective suppression. I am imagining you target the spell (default scale, size 0, 1 subject) rather than targeting all of the subjects of the spell (who you may not even be able to find).</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell is on the area or subjects it affects. You cannot target the spell without targeting those, dispellation suppresses the spell unless you use Reach and Mana to make it Lasting, and the need to use Fate for selective dispellation implies targeting some but not all of the spell's subjects is not possible with the base effect alone.<br /> <br /> Spells aren't Size 0. They're at least the Size of whatever they're affecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T14:17:04-08:00","id":1556664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556661#post1556661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell is on the area or subjects it affects. You cannot target the spell without targeting those, dispellation suppresses the spell unless you use Reach and Mana to make it Lasting, and the need to use Fate for selective dispellation implies targeting some but not all of the spell's subjects is not possible with the base effect alone.<br /> <br /> Spells aren't Size 0. They're at least the Size of whatever they're affecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the logical extension of this is: I can prevent my spell from being dispelled by including one extra target (a rock I found) and sinking it too the bottom of the ocean (or other equally difficult to find place?) and unless they have sufficient space magic to trace down that rock (assuming i don't seperately destroy any Sympathetic connections to it).<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding your interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T15:01:12-08:00","id":1556669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556664#post1556664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the logical extension of this is: I can prevent my spell from being dispelled by including one extra target (a rock I found) and sinking it too the bottom of the ocean (or other equally difficult to find place?) and unless they have sufficient space magic to trace down that rock (assuming i don't seperately destroy any Sympathetic connections to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if they, y'know, have the lowest nonzero amount of practice in the Fate Arcanum possible, something that literally any mage can develop without special training even if they belonged to a hypothetical Path with Fate as its Inferior Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Basic dispellation targets <i>the spell</i> and lasts for a matter of seconds unless you dedicate Reach or factors to Duration that the spell is turned off. You need Fate to turn the spell off only part of the way directly (as opposed to, say, using Wards and Signs to make a subject more resistant to the spell). The way Dispel Magic works already incentivizes you to develop basic competence in as many Arcana as you can even if Fate wasn't one of the more broadly useful Arcana to have.<br /> <br /> Adding Scale to spells that don't need it takes Reach or penalties (or Mana, if you're an Adept of Space) and presumably if you're dedicating the time needed to hide away or near-permanently non-destructively dispose of an object whose only purpose is to preserve a spell against casual dispellation it's something that's supposed to be durable anyway, so setting aside the silly framing I'm not sure why you're presenting this hypothetical as though it defeats the interpretation \u2014 Focused Mage Sight can hypothetically steer a scrutinizing mage in the direction of the connected Mystery of &quot;this rock has a spell on it that doesn't do anything to it&quot; even if &quot;this spell has more than one target it's affecting&quot; wasn't revealed by the spell factors, with or without any tampering with sympathetic connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T16:36:08-08:00","id":1556677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556669#post1556669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if they, y'know, have the lowest nonzero amount of practice in the Fate Arcanum possible, something that literally any mage can develop without special training even if they belonged to a hypothetical Path with Fate as its Inferior Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Basic dispellation targets <i>the spell</i> and lasts for a matter of seconds unless you dedicate Reach or factors to Duration that the spell is turned off. You need Fate to turn the spell off only part of the way directly (as opposed to, say, using Wards and Signs to make a subject more resistant to the spell). The way Dispel Magic works already incentivizes you to develop basic competence in as many Arcana as you can even if Fate wasn't one of the more broadly useful Arcana to have.<br /> <br /> Adding Scale to spells that don't need it takes Reach or penalties (or Mana, if you're an Adept of Space) and presumably if you're dedicating the time needed to hide away or near-permanently non-destructively dispose of an object whose only purpose is to preserve a spell against casual dispellation it's something that's supposed to be durable anyway, so setting aside the silly framing I'm not sure why you're presenting this hypothetical as though it defeats the interpretation \u2014 Focused Mage Sight can hypothetically steer a scrutinizing mage in the direction of the connected Mystery of &quot;this rock has a spell on it that doesn't do anything to it&quot; even if &quot;this spell has more than one target it's affecting&quot; wasn't revealed by the spell factors, with or without any tampering with sympathetic connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why I'm disagreeing, when I think spells should account for the scale, sometimes... It does seem contrary to the game's design goals to require Fate 1, since the attempted to bring Conjunctional Arcana to a minimum (even dropping that phrase in 2e from what I can see); but it effectively adds a way to make spells harder to dispell. Like Pocket Dimension being dispelled is a fairly big weakness, but if your Dispell needs to have the same scale as the whole Pocket, then a -10 dice pool is rather daunting to pull off on the fly (after you overcome whatever potency/withstand is required...) <br /> <br /> But I think I would rather not have &quot;random hidden rock&quot; as a way to defend a spell, like by default, Dispel Magic is cast at touch range, but just touching one subject should allow you to affect the entire spell (rather than needing to touch every subject) in the same way touching the edge of a building allows you to cast a building sized AoE spell on an entire building.<br /> <br /> Being forced to account for the number of subjects, without actually touching each one seems enough to me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T18:56:09-08:00","id":1556688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556677#post1556677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why I'm disagreeing, when I think spells should account for the scale, sometimes... It does seem contrary to the game's design goals to require Fate 1, since the attempted to bring Conjunctional Arcana to a minimum (even dropping that phrase in 2e from what I can see); but it effectively adds a way to make spells harder to dispell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much every increased spell factor makes a spell harder to counteract in some way and Scale is the least durable factor of the ones that exist beyond the moment of casting; Scale is the least durable of those three spell factors and the portion of the game's design goals you're talking about were to reduce the expected amount of interdisciplinary expertise just to affect a given type of monster (e.g. being clear that you don't need both Life and Spirit to affect a werewolf the way you would anything else with a body made of flesh).<br /> <br /> Dispel Magic's default effect in 1e is a Reach effect in 2e and it contends with a much flatter defensive trait. The need to be a magical generalist to most safely erase any spell you come across is not a new feature and doing surgery on a spell to pare down who it's affecting is in line with other things Fate does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I think I would rather not have &quot;random hidden rock&quot; as a way to defend a spell, like by default, Dispel Magic is cast at touch range, but just touching one subject should allow you to affect the entire spell (rather than needing to touch every subject) in the same way touching the edge of a building allows you to cast a building sized AoE spell on an entire building. </div> </div> </div>I have been humoring you on the &quot;random hidden rock&quot; scenario because the concept of keeping an essential vulnerability out of the way is a well-established trope for supernatural framework, but the notion of targeting a Subject-Scale spell to something that the spell will specifically not have an actual effect on just to make it harder to dispel is the kind of thing basically any ST is either going to say no to or remind you is also a valid tactic for NPCs to employ if you abuse it.<br /> <br /> The default for <i>every</i> spell is that it affects one subject at touch range. The default is also that spells last less than thirty seconds and can't affect an unwilling target with peak human [Resistance Trait], but those latter two get freebies that scope or headcount don't, and the obvious primary use-case of Dispel Magic is for getting rid of a discrete magical effect that you can look at in its entirety. The conjunctional Fate effect exists for roughly the same reason Warding Gesture is an explicit flexible exemption clause for your AoE effects in contrast to, say, shaping the set boundaries of your AoE spells to avoid the immediate location of things you don't want it to affect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being forced to account for the number of subjects, without actually touching each one seems enough to me. </div> </div> </div>This gets into the other end of the problem, where you can shut down a master's long-standing defenses because they happened to cast them on all of their apprentices at the same time for efficiency's sake but you still need Fate to <i>only</i> strip the warding off of one of them. A spell cast on a platoon of soldiers should not be able to be removed just by getting into contact with one of those soldiers.<br /> <br /> Analogy to Imperial Practices is a nightmare because propagative effects like those in Dynamics and Entities ultimately don't seem like they engage with Scale and Seekers' spells are exempt from most methods of elimination, but there's a reason Quintessence makes a qualitative distinction between what you need to do to cure one person's vampirism and what you need to do to wipe out a whole bloodline of vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T19:51:28-08:00","id":1556694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556688#post1556688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell cast on a platoon of soldiers should not be able to be removed just by getting into contact with one of those soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just not sure I agree. That is the downside of casting a single spell on all the soldiers instead off casting seperate spells in each one. <br /> <br /> It is a choice, and with Mind magic to regain the willpower, you can easily cast 100 individual spells in ~ 10 minutes, assuming you unsafely relinquish them all (which is fine so long as you don't make them last long enough to deteriorate and be left going wild...) <br /> <br /> Having the more powerful spell be harder to dispell is ok as an upside. <br /> <br /> Advanced Potency does give a bonus to dispellation increased potency doesn't do anything, and how does Duration? Apart from the dispellation having a duration, making it a lasting effect isn't affect by the target spell's duration, and you can optionally dispell for an arbitrary amount of time.<br /> <br /> In this case, only Scale let's you directly alter the difficult of dispellation... In my interpretation, varying the difficulty based on the scale, in yours making some spells rely on<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . the concept of keeping an essential vulnerability out of the way is a well-established trope for supernatural framework </div> </div> </div>Which, I like as a trope and could be worked into Mage, but it is too much for too little cost, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T20:35:52-08:00","id":1556699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556694#post1556694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a choice, and with Mind magic to regain the willpower, you can easily cast 100 individual spells in ~ 10 minutes, assuming you unsafely relinquish them all (which is fine so long as you don't make them last long enough to deteriorate and be left going wild...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell that doesn't last long enough for unsafe relinquishment to be an issue is almost definitionally one for which you are starkly limited in where anchoring extra subjects can be squirreled away and/or safeguarded within that time. A hypothetical Mastigos doing all this casting is statistically likely to fail at least some of those spellcasting rolls and the ST would be justified in using the penalties for Successive Attempts in such a case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Advanced Potency does give a bonus to dispellation increased potency doesn't do anything, and how does Duration? Apart from the dispellation having a duration, making it a lasting effect isn't affect by the target spell's duration, and you can optionally dispell for an arbitrary amount of time. </div> </div> </div>Longer-lasting supernatural effects gain bonus dice to Clashes of Wills, which are the main way antimagic effects that aren't Awakened spells work, including the Counterspell Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T09:45:10-08:00","id":1556834,"title":"","content":"Does a scrying window or live security camera feed count as material sympathy ? Let's say you don't have the spare Reach for remote viewing, but you do have the mana for sympathetic range, would you be able to use them to cast ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T12:51:02-08:00","id":1556841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556834#post1556834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a scrying window or live security camera feed count as material sympathy ? Let's say you don't have the spare Reach for remote viewing, but you do have the mana for sympathetic range, would you be able to use them to cast ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You could make a record of the feed to <i>get</i> a material sympathy Yantra, but just being able to see your target live does not count as a sympathy Yantra whether you're looking at them from across the room or across the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T10:32:11-08:00","id":1556858,"title":"","content":"Yantras<br /> Lets say i use yantras to a total of +7 in a spell<br /> in that spell i also use 4 dice to increase potency by 2<br /> having 2 gnosis and 3 highest spell arcanum do i roll 8 dice or 6 given the 5+ yantra limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 12-20-2025, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T11:03:17-08:00","id":1556859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556858#post1556858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yantras<br /> Lets say i use yantras to a total of +7 in a spell<br /> in that spell i also use 4 dice to increase potency by 2<br /> having 2 gnosis and 3 highest spell arcanum do i roll 8 dice or 6 given the 5+ yantra limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>8 dice, you apply the +5 cap after adding all modifiers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T15:34:51-08:00","id":1556863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556859#post1556859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 8 dice, you apply the +5 cap after adding all modifiers</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way you should roll less is you cause a paradox and don't attempt to contain it. Then the successes on the paradox dice applies a negative modified *after* the +5 cap. (Which honestly, since I have never seen a player with uncontained paradox, I would be tempted to make it a bonus to the dice pool, as an incentive...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T17:20:29-08:00","id":1556865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556863#post1556863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way you should roll less is you cause a paradox and don't attempt to contain it. Then the successes on the paradox dice applies a negative modified *after* the +5 cap. (Which honestly, since I have never seen a player with uncontained paradox, I would be tempted to make it a bonus to the dice pool, as an incentive...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The negative modifier is an incentive to contain the Paradox despite failure to completely do so resulting in a Paradox Condition. If you want an incentive to release the Paradox, you either emphasize the fact that the anomalies aren't inherently bad for the character or you start dangling antinomian magic in front of their noses. The vast majority of non-egregious Paradoxes amount to the subject of the spell getting a Condition or a spell factor being greater or lesser than intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T09:43:02-08:00","id":1556875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556865#post1556865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The negative modifier is an incentive to contain the Paradox despite failure to completely do so resulting in a Paradox Condition. If you want an incentive to release the Paradox, you either emphasize the fact that the anomalies aren't inherently bad for the character or you start dangling antinomian magic in front of their noses. The vast majority of non-egregious Paradoxes amount to the subject of the spell getting a Condition or a spell factor being greater or lesser than intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing the subject of the spell, seems pretty dramatic of an anomoly... Getting a condition may or may not be drastic, depending on how broad the conditions are.<br /> <br /> But the upside of containing is you can get an arcane beat for resolving a paradox condition before it lapses (if my reading is right... Lower wisdom, harder to get the best, or at least you have less time).<br /> <br /> You can invoke and contain a paradox just because you want to earn the beat. Meanwhile uncontained paradox risks your spell not hitting who you targeted, and usually that is a pretty important part.<br /> <br /> The negative dice pool modifier is, I think, the biggest risk (your spell entirely failing is bad... Especially if you have spent resources on it). Dying from contained paradox damage is obviously worse, but I have never seen that happen (and would need to be a pretty dramatic situation, ideally one where the character is intentionally sacrificing themself)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T12:23:24-08:00","id":1556877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556875#post1556875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the subject of the spell, seems pretty dramatic of an anomoly... Getting a condition may or may not be drastic, depending on how broad the conditions are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing the target entirely takes 2 Paradox Reach where increasing or decreasing the Scale takes 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the upside of containing is you can get an arcane beat for resolving a paradox condition before it lapses (if my reading is right... Lower wisdom, harder to get the best, or at least you have less time). </div> </div> </div>The intention of the text seems to be that the Condition can't be removed by Scouring until it lapses and lapsing is how it gives an Arcane Beat instead of a regular Beat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can invoke and contain a paradox just because you want to earn the beat. Meanwhile uncontained paradox risks your spell not hitting who you targeted, and usually that is a pretty important part.<br /> <br /> The negative dice pool modifier is, I think, the biggest risk (your spell entirely failing is bad... Especially if you have spent resources on it). Dying from contained paradox damage is obviously worse, but I have never seen that happen (and would need to be a pretty dramatic situation, ideally one where the character is intentionally sacrificing themself) </div> </div> </div>You are limited in how many Beats you can get from a given category and the line has never put forward death as a real direct risk from invoking Paradox.<br /> <br /> The idea is that you <i>don't</i> spend resources on spells for which you intend to risk substantial Paradox, which is typically spells that you can try to cast repeatedly if they fail.<br /> <br /> The usual dichotomy with the above is that if you don't want a spell to fail, you dedicate the time and preparation to make it work. Releasing Paradox goes best with the part of the game where the character is looking for immediate results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T16:01:52-08:00","id":1556881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556877#post1556877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the target entirely takes 2 Paradox Reach where increasing or decreasing the Scale takes 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the second smallest amount of paradox reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The intention of the text seems to be that the Condition can't be removed by Scouring until it lapses and lapsing is how it gives an Arcane Beat instead of a regular Beat. </div> </div> </div>The actual text is rather unclear. Pg 83 of the core rules say<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any time you resolve a Condition resulting from spellcasting, Paradox, or a magical effect, take an Arcane Beat </div> </div> </div>The Wisdom vs time to lapse seems to read as a punishment for lower wisdom characters (anomolies created by lower wisdom mages seems to work the opposite).<br /> <br /> Given that the line tends to reward doing risky things (surrendering in combat, taking dramatic failure, etc.) it makes sense that there would be a rewarded for doing stuff.<br /> <br /> Resolving a paradox condition and generating a normal beat seems counter intuitive in itself. And rewarding a low Wisdom character (who will on average lose less health to paradox containment), with faster arcane beats (less time to lapse), seems entirely backwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are limited in how many Beats you can get from a given category and the line has never put forward death as a real direct risk from invoking Paradox. </div> </div> </div>In combat, you may be stretched to your limits, and therefore carrying lords of damage and risking more paradox than you would usually be comfortable with. It is only in these circumstances where a few too many bashing may push you over and kill you. This being a dramatic moment, I think it could be a player choice, and valid in some moments (and maybe some time travel can undo it is the player was unhappy they got unlucky?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea is that you <i>don't</i> spend resources on spells for which you intend to risk substantial Paradox, which is typically spells that you can try to cast repeatedly if they fail.<br /> <br /> The usual dichotomy with the above is that if you don't want a spell to fail, you dedicate the time and preparation to make it work. Releasing Paradox goes best with the part of the game where the character is looking for immediate results. </div> </div> </div>You don't always have the luxury of time and prep. That is a resource which can not be guaranteed. Aside from interference in a carefully laid out ritual casting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T19:17:46-08:00","id":1556888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556881#post1556881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the second smallest amount of paradox reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, were you confused when I said &quot;the vast majority of non-egregious Paradoxes&quot; and &quot;emphasize the fact that the anomalies aren't inherently bad for the character,&quot; or does the difference between the average success count for three Paradox risk dice and six Paradox risk dice without dice tricks not make itself immediately plain?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that the line tends to reward doing risky things (surrendering in combat, taking dramatic failure, etc.) it makes sense that there would be a rewarded for doing stuff. </div> </div> </div>Surrendering in combat is the opposite of a risky thing \u2014 you're gating any further interaction in either direction behind a Willpower surcharge and you can't do it in conflicts where the opposition's goal is specifically to do violence to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resolving a paradox condition and generating a normal beat seems counter intuitive in itself. And rewarding a low Wisdom character (who will on average lose less health to paradox containment), with faster arcane beats (less time to lapse), seems entirely backwards. </div> </div> </div>It is not a reward to put a character on track for being stuck with constant Paradox risk faster and I think the line is pretty clear that risking lower Wisdom is <i>routinely</i> rewarded with Arcane Beats, since that's also one of the mechanical incentives to engage in Acts of Hubris. The antinomian counterpart to the roll to containing Paradox uses Gnosis in place of Wisdom and mages with the shortest duration of Paradox Conditions in the game are the ones that constantly leak Quiescence and whose 1e material had Abyssal Manifestations summoned by their magic not know who summoned them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In combat, you may be stretched to your limits, and therefore carrying lords of damage and risking more paradox than you would usually be comfortable with. It is only in these circumstances where a few too many bashing may push you over and kill you. </div> </div> </div>Unless you are using spells or Death Armor to negate it, the consequence of bashing damage alone is not going to kill you. Unless you are already badly injured (and here note that Mage is not one of the gamelines that rewards you with Beats for having enough Health boxes marked to suffer wound penalties), dying from containing a Paradox requires the extraordinary circumstances of you rolling at least six success on a Paradox roll <i>and then rolling at least that many successes on an unmodified Wisdom roll</i>. Damage from Paradox has literally never been designed as something that can kill you outright.<br /> <br /> Needing to Scour yourself to get Abyssal taint out of your Pattern, meanwhile, serves as a pacing mechanism not unlike Kindred vampires not being able to take enough Vitae from a single person to keep waking up each night without eventually killing that person; characters with Falling Wisdom who take their chances with releasing Paradox add an extra margin for error to their spellcasting, fail more often, and/or court the chance of dramatically failing and getting a Paradox Condition anyway on a less frequent basis, which means capping your effective Health for a couple days the same as if you were trying to get Mana without reducing your Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't always have the luxury of time and prep. That is a resource which can not be guaranteed. Aside from interference in a carefully laid out ritual casting... </div> </div> </div>Yes. The incentives to release Paradox instead of containing it are specifically not geared toward mages with the luxury of time and prep. Accepting Paradox risk is a gamble, and the whole point of Reach as a system is to add another layer to spellcasting that makes it so that casting a spell without taking at least several minutes is something you can do at the cost of making bigger swings more likely to go bad and adding &quot;you can safely cast these even if you're a couple spells over your limit&quot; to the benefits of Rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T01:46:19-08:00","id":1556957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556888#post1556888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you are using spells or Death Armor to negate it, the consequence of bashing damage alone is not going to kill you. Unless you are already badly injured (and here note that Mage is not one of the gamelines that rewards you with Beats for having enough Health boxes marked to suffer wound penalties), dying from containing a Paradox requires the extraordinary circumstances of you rolling at least six success on a Paradox roll <i>and then rolling at least that many successes on an unmodified Wisdom roll</i>. Damage from Paradox has literally never been designed as something that can kill you outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear. It takes precisely 1 bashing damage to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T05:51:54-08:00","id":1556963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556957#post1556957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear. It takes precisely 1 bashing damage to kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the extraordinary circumstance that you only have one Health box that is not marked with lethal or aggravated damage and that one Health box is marked with bashing or lethal damage and you have somehow gotten to this point without falling unconscious, yes, deliberately doing something that will hurt you when getting hurt anymore will kill you will, in fact, kill you.<br /> <br /> This does not change the fact that reaching that threshold without negating the human frailty of passing out once your Health track is full of either of the damage levels reserved for the nearly dead is an extraordinary circumstance that most mages will not be casting in and that the Paradox mechanics are obviously not written to make a primary concern. You take resistant bashing damage when containing Paradoxes because that pushes you closer to effectively turning off for the scene, not because saving your casting roll from a penalty as low as one die is expected to end your life.<br /> <br /> Resistant <i>lethal</i> damage runs a more direct risk of killing you because bleeding out can't be solved by just getting lucky on Stamina rolls, but that's the domain of Scouring, which is directly limited in how frequently you can do it and gives you a method of doing so that doesn't deal Health damage if you're doing it to regain Mana instead of clearing out Abyssal taint from your Pattern \u2014 as deliberate actions either of those is incentivized to be done in circumstances where you are not likely to be taking more damage, because, as mentioned before, mages don't get Beats from taking wound penalty-level damage the way most other splats do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T09:00:47-08:00","id":1556965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556963#post1556963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does not change the fact that reaching that threshold without negating the human frailty of passing out once your Health track is full of either of the damage levels reserved for the nearly dead is an extraordinary circumstance that ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said they would not negate the human frailty? I think, apart from Death Armour, Life or Mind should be able to ignore wound penalties, Fate is able to gives bonus to mundane rolls, leaving only one path which I think would struggle with only their ruling arcana to avoid them.<br /> <br /> And the point remains, if you continue to push your luck, dying is the outcome. I don't see how dying from a source of damage seems so extraordinary to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T09:49:54-08:00","id":1556966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1556965#post1556965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said they would not negate the human frailty? I think, apart from Death Armour, Life or Mind should be able to ignore wound penalties, Fate is able to gives bonus to mundane rolls, leaving only one path which I think would struggle with only their ruling arcana to avoid them.<br /> <br /> And the point remains, if you continue to push your luck, dying is the outcome. I don't see how dying from a source of damage seems so extraordinary to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because <i>you need to go out of your way to negate the frailty.</i> Mages are not immune to unconsciousness by default and their powerset and advancement mechanics do not incentivize them to hang out in situations where they are taking heavy damage.<br /> <br /> Bashing damage being what it is, even with your Health track effectively shortened with lethal or aggravated damage, every roll to contain Paradox and deal damage to yourself is a deliberate decision by the character and each open Health box increases the number of Paradox successes you need to negate before you <i>accidentally</i> kill yourself from containing them. Even in the circumstances where the character is not already fighting to stay conscious, self-preservation usually takes priority over avoiding Paradox anomalies or failed spells, <i>because Paradox anomalies are not automatically bad for the caster themselves </i>and if you're desperate enough to cast without prep in those circumstances you're usually desperate enough to try again or cut your losses and run.<br /> <br /> This mechanic has literally never been primarily about casting magic safely being a good way to kill yourself. The characters who are in a position to do so have to go rather deep into dangerous circumstances for that to be probable and the type of characters who do so are mechanically incentivized not to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T14:50:22-08:00","id":1556968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you need to go out of your way to negate the frailty </div> </div> </div>And that is somehow unusual for a mage who is getting into a fight, or perhaps expecting to get into a fight, to have prepared for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you're desperate enough to cast without prep in those circumstances you're usually desperate enough to try again or cut your losses and run. </div> </div> </div>If you are desperate enough to stick around, then you *by definition* don't want - what may be the last spell you can manage - to end up failing due to uncontained paradox. <br /> <br /> Imagine that saving your own skin isn't going to stop the big plan...<br /> <br /> But aside from that, how resistant damage works, you end up with resistant lethal and Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Say you take 3 bashing from the first contained paradox, great, it will heal fairly soon, but next you take 2 lethal from some other source. This pushes the bashing over and now you have 2 resistant lethal in your first 2 boxes, and 1 resistant bashing.<br /> <br /> Suddenly you are not healing that at all for several days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"extra reply) 12-24-2025, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T14:53:30-08:00","id":1556969,"title":"","content":"I don't know why this is an extended argument given it started from &quot;I've never seen death as a result of contained Paradox happen and I think it would only really happen if a mage was dramatically sacrificing himself or something.&quot;<br /> <br /> Either way, I think a back and forth like this merits a thread of its own to continue rather than being a Simple Question and Simple Answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T14:53:49-08:00","id":1557106,"title":"","content":"Do &quot;Rotting Flesh&quot; or &quot;Withering&quot; work on ephemeral entities? If so, it is conditional on being on the same wavelength of Twilight for example? Or imagine a Moros trapped in the Shadow, would any of those spells affect spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:00:53-08:00","id":1557107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557106#post1557106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do &quot;Rotting Flesh&quot; or &quot;Withering&quot; work on ephemeral entities? If so, it is conditional on being on the same wavelength of Twilight for example? Or imagine a Moros trapped in the Shadow, would any of those spells affect spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotting Flesh works on subjects that have flesh to rot, which ephemera isn't, so no. Ditto for Withering. An Unraveling equivalent of Damage Ghost could deal lethal or aggravated damage to a ghost or other being made of Death-ephemera, but that's a different spell doing a different thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:36:26-08:00","id":1557111,"title":"","content":"I'm re-reading Signs of Sorcery, a sidebar mentions two sets of powerful artifacts, the regaila of the dethroned queen, and the ring and scepter of Ahriman. I'm familar with the former, but this is the first I've heard of the latter. The only artifact of Ahriman in mage I have heard of is the eye in 1e. Is there any stat block or other mention of what that set of artifacts does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","user":"Snailslayer","date":". 12-29-2025, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T16:05:30-08:00","id":1557113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557111#post1557111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm re-reading Signs of Sorcery, a sidebar mentions two sets of powerful artifacts, the regaila of the dethroned queen, and the ring and scepter of Ahriman. I'm familar with the former, but this is the first I've heard of the latter. The only artifact of Ahriman in mage I have heard of is the eye in 1e. Is there any stat block or other mention of what that set of artifacts does?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Eye of Ahriman</i> is a 12 dot found on page 208 of the Mysterium book. It replaces your real eye, but refuses to bond with anyone with less than Destiny 5. It grants several powers, including the ability to be under permanent <i>Nightvision</i>, use <i>Scrying</i> freely, permanent Death Mage Armor, the ability to summon shadows and the ability to make minions from shadows, both these end if exposed to sunlight. So if you ever played one of <i>The Darkness</i> games, it has those vibes.<br /> <br /> It was discovered in an Atlantean ruins and they only figured out how to use it when a Scelestus came for it with the sister Artifact. So <i>Signs of Sorcery </i>now clarifying it was a scepter and a ring, which were never detailed anywhere AFAIK, and adds to the confusion of where the eye falls in the set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-29-2025, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T18:06:43-08:00","id":1557123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557113#post1557113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was discovered in an Atlantean ruins and they only figured out how to use it when a Scelestus came for it with the sister Artifact. So <i>Signs of Sorcery </i>now clarifying it was a scepter and a ring, which were never detailed anywhere AFAIK, and adds to the confusion of where the eye falls in the set.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very definitely not clarifying that it was a scepter and a ring, because the Eye of Ahriman was an amulet and the sidebar wouldn't be talking about characters uniting those two Artifacts speculatively if that was definitely how it was discovered that the Eye of Ahriman was activated. For all we know the sister Artifact \u2014 and it was <i>a</i> sister Artifact, not <i>the</i> sister Artifact \u2014 could have just been a different Eye of Ahriman.<br /> <br /> More probably, given the book this sidebar is in, it's using Ahriman as a mythological reference in the same way that Dahhak claims to be the son of the Adversary of Zoroastrianism as an example of the sort of being to whom Artifacts of the Profane Forms on the same page might belong \u2014 the Dethroned Queen's regalia from Reign of the Exarchs are definitely known, but possessions of the Enemy of Truth with powers of the types accorded to Rings and Scepters paint a certain sort of picture of what an ambitious Seer might expect to get a set bonus from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of shadow powers, though: what Practice would it be to create a solid animate shadow a la Retainer spells like Golem or Eidolon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T18:29:21-08:00","id":1557126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557123#post1557123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very definitely not clarifying that it was a scepter and a ring, because the Eye of Ahriman was an amulet and the sidebar wouldn't be talking about characters uniting those two Artifacts speculatively if that was definitely how it was discovered that the Eye of Ahriman was activated. For all we know the sister Artifact \u2014 and it was <i>a</i> sister Artifact, not <i>the</i> sister Artifact \u2014 could have just been a different Eye of Ahriman.<br /> <br /> More probably, given the book this sidebar is in, it's using Ahriman as a mythological reference in the same way that Dahhak claims to be the son of the Adversary of Zoroastrianism as an example of the sort of being to whom Artifacts of the Profane Forms on the same page might belong \u2014 the Dethroned Queen's regalia from Reign of the Exarchs are definitely known, but possessions of the Enemy of Truth with powers of the types accorded to Rings and Scepters paint a certain sort of picture of what an ambitious Seer might expect to get a set bonus from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of shadow powers, though: what Practice would it be to create a solid animate shadow a la Retainer spells like Golem or Eidolon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it would require Death 3 (solid shadows) and Spirit 3. You would be taking motes of ephemera, Weaving them with a simple task or purpose, them make them animate the solid shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T19:21:07-08:00","id":1557127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557113#post1557113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <i>Eye of Ahriman</i> is a 12 dot found on page 208 of the Mysterium book. It replaces your real eye, but refuses to bond with anyone with less than Destiny 5. It grants several powers, including the ability to be under permanent <i>Nightvision</i>, use <i>Scrying</i> freely, permanent Death Mage Armor, the ability to summon shadows and the ability to make minions from shadows, both these end if exposed to sunlight. So if you ever played one of <i>The Darkness</i> games, it has those vibes.<br /> <br /> It was discovered in an Atlantean ruins and they only figured out how to use it when a Scelestus came for it with the sister Artifact. So <i>Signs of Sorcery </i>now clarifying it was a scepter and a ring, which were never detailed anywhere AFAIK, and adds to the confusion of where the eye falls in the set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... that's confusing lol. But thank you, that's helpful. <br /> <br /> Speaking of oddities, the Naga, they seem to have been a big deal for the Indian pre-Alexander orders, are they a thing or Bygone or something like the Rmoahals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T19:50:56-08:00","id":1557129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557127#post1557127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of oddities, the Naga, they seem to have been a big deal for the Indian pre-Alexander orders, are they a thing or Bygone or something like the Rmoahals?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're that Great Cult's take on/contribution to the Atlantis mythology \u2014 note that the Naga people worshipped serpentine gods who gave them the Paths much as the Tremere's take on Atlantis in the Suspire claims the Dragons/Watchtowers were around to petition for inquiry on the nature of the soul despite modern thought treating the Paths as a post-Fall creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T03:10:44-08:00","id":1557135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557123#post1557123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very definitely not clarifying that it was a scepter and a ring, because the Eye of Ahriman was an amulet and the sidebar wouldn't be talking about characters uniting those two Artifacts speculatively if that was definitely how it was discovered that the Eye of Ahriman was activated. For all we know the sister Artifact \u2014 and it was <i>a</i> sister Artifact, not <i>the</i> sister Artifact \u2014 could have just been a different Eye of Ahriman.<br /> <br /> Speaking of shadow powers, though: what Practice would it be to create a solid animate shadow a la Retainer spells like Golem or Eidolon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I m not sure, what are your considerations about the shadows controlled by the death Arcanum?<br /> If they are &quot;soul stuff&quot; like in Mummy shades probabli Patterning is ok.<br /> If they are the more conceptual &quot;absence of something&quot; probably Making is necessary<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T03:35:48-08:00","id":1557138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557123#post1557123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very definitely not clarifying that it was a scepter and a ring, because the Eye of Ahriman was an amulet and the sidebar wouldn't be talking about characters uniting those two Artifacts speculatively if that was definitely how it was discovered that the Eye of Ahriman was activated. For all we know the sister Artifact \u2014 and it was <i>a</i> sister Artifact, not <i>the</i> sister Artifact \u2014 could have just been a different Eye of Ahriman.<br /> <br /> More probably, given the book this sidebar is in, it's using Ahriman as a mythological reference in the same way that Dahhak claims to be the son of the Adversary of Zoroastrianism as an example of the sort of being to whom Artifacts of the Profane Forms on the same page might belong \u2014 the Dethroned Queen's regalia from Reign of the Exarchs are definitely known, but possessions of the Enemy of Truth with powers of the types accorded to Rings and Scepters paint a certain sort of picture of what an ambitious Seer might expect to get a set bonus from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of shadow powers, though: what Practice would it be to create a solid animate shadow a la Retainer spells like Golem or Eidolon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it would require Death 3 (solid shadows) and Spirit 3. You would be taking motes of ephemera, Weaving them with a simple task or purpose, them make them animate the solid shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-30T05:24:59-08:00","id":1557144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557138#post1557138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking it would require Death 3 (solid shadows) and Spirit 3. You would be taking motes of ephemera, Weaving them with a simple task or purpose, them make them animate the solid shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only issue is the Shadows don't typically have a solid form - compared to Tass which naturally congeals from mana, and Prime still requires Prime 5 for an Eidolon (but 3 for Platonic forms).<br /> <br /> But given that Shadow Crafting requires only Death 3 and creates solid objects, I don't see any requirement for including Spirit.<br /> <br /> Death 5 to create a minion from nothing. probably Death 4 to create a retainers from an existing ghost/ectoplasm/absence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T08:10:11-08:00","id":1557231,"title":"","content":"Ghost Shield states:<br /> <br /> The caster creates a shield that protects her subject from ghost-<br /> ly Numina, Influences, Manifestations, Death spells, and<b> any<br /> death-related powers of other supernatural creatures</b>. Any power<br /> attempting to pierce the shield provokes a Clash of Wills roll.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that this shield should work against Geist powers (Death Shielding protects against any Haunt as per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle), and Kerberoi, etc.<br /> <br /> What would count to the bolded part? Would vampire Dominate / Majesty count? Theban Sorcery? Cruac? Any example of death-related powers from the other gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, etc) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T09:03:11-08:00","id":1557233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557231#post1557231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would count to the bolded part? Would vampire Dominate / Majesty count? Theban Sorcery? Cruac? Any example of death-related powers from the other gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the PGCC, Disciplines are defended against using the appropriate Arcana for their effects, which remains a viable means of defending against Haunts as well. It's the same deal as Ephemeral Shield working against Gifts and Rites \u2014 unless the root of the power comes from a specific Arcana (even if it manipulates other phenomena), Ghost Shield is only going to defend against powers that leverage ghosts, shadows, ectoplasm, the energies of death, and so on in their outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T12:16:51-08:00","id":1557238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557231#post1557231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Shield states:<br /> <br /> The caster creates a shield that protects her subject from ghost-<br /> ly Numina, Influences, Manifestations, Death spells, and<b> any<br /> death-related powers of other supernatural creatures</b>. Any power<br /> attempting to pierce the shield provokes a Clash of Wills roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that this shield should work against Geist powers (Death Shielding protects against any Haunt as per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle), and Kerberoi, etc.<br /> <br /> What would count to the bolded part? Would vampire Dominate / Majesty count? Theban Sorcery? Cruac? Any example of death-related powers from the other gamelines (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, etc)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would be very rare for any Werewolf to become so transformed that they derive their power from the Underworld. <br /> <br /> Changelings might be more likely, but they too usually derive their powers from Arcadia/Glamour. Maybe some contract with Death/the Underworld would be defended, but those are few and far between afaik.<br /> <br /> Vampires derive their powers from the blood (or Vitae) which is think is the life force stolen from humans... Kinda PGCC describes it as Death and Life.<br /> <br /> Deviants are probably more varied that Changelings and the same caveats apply. Could you have a necromantic conspiracy using the power of the Underworld to make Deviants? Probably...<br /> <br /> Mummy would depend on the pillar used I think... But it is unclear since PGCC didn't bother to give any info and the material referenced only really deals with Mind and Time/Fate spells interacting with Mummys...<br /> <br /> Promethean do have a death attuned lineage but they still ultimately derive their main powers from Alchemy.<br /> <br /> And Demon manipulate reality in a cheating the game kinda way, which is usually outside of the rules...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T12:58:34-08:00","id":1557240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Core 2ed p. 99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effects of making a soul stone don\u2019t wear off unless the<br /> object is destroyed, in which case the creator is immediately<br /> aware of the change and the lost potential Gnosis is restored.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p. 73 Reaping Relinquishment</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage destroys a soul to relinquish a spell safely.<br /> ...<br /> Add Prime \u2022\u2022: <b>The caster can destroy a soul stone instead<br /> for the same effect.\u200b</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Is the destruction crippling permanently (never gain that Gnosis dot again) or does it count as regular destruction as per the Mage core p 99?<br /> <br /> <br /> Similar question whether Tremere consuming a Soul Stone causes permanent loss of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T13:51:19-08:00","id":1557243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557240#post1557240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the destruction crippling permanently (never gain that Gnosis dot again) or does it count as regular destruction as per the Mage core p 99?<br /> <br /> Similar question whether Tremere consuming a Soul Stone causes permanent loss of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the corebook. The Willpower dot cost of creating a soul stone means the conjunctional effect functionally makes Reaping Relinquishment into &quot;you can offload the Experience cost of safe relinquishment to another mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the mechanic doesn't say destroying a soul stone works different, it works as normal. Tremere already don't derive any particular sustenance from soul stones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-03-2026, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T13:59:02-08:00","id":1557244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557243#post1557243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the corebook. The Willpower dot cost of creating a soul stone means the conjunctional effect functionally makes Reaping Relinquishment into &quot;you can offload the Experience cost of safe relinquishment to another mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the mechanic doesn't say destroying a soul stone works different, it works as normal. Tremere already don't derive any particular sustenance from soul stones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I believe I have not understood the answer. <br /> <br /> Any of those examples I listed, will NOT cause issues with regaining the Gnosis potential and work as regularly destroying the item. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T14:31:32-08:00","id":1557246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557244#post1557244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I believe I have not understood the answer.<br /> <br /> Any of those examples I listed, will NOT cause issues with regaining the Gnosis potential and work as regularly destroying the item. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Destroying the item works as described in the corebook unless a mechanic says differently, yes. There is nothing anywhere that says Reaping Relinquishment or consumption by the Tremere works differently to normal destruction, so it works as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T01:33:45-08:00","id":1557254,"title":"","content":"Following on from that question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creating a soul stone is an Act of Hubris against Enlightened and Understanding Wisdom. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so how many dice do you roll?<br /> <br /> Afaik, an AoH against Enlightened wisdom is 5 dice base pool, while and AoH against Understanding is 3 dice. (IE if you have wisdom 8 but do something which would qualify as an AoH even for a Wisdom 5 character, then you roll the smaller dice pool). Wording seems weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T03:15:06-08:00","id":1557255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557254#post1557254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so how many dice do you roll? Afaik, an AoH against Enlightened wisdom is 5 dice base pool, while and AoH against Understanding is 3 dice. (IE if you have wisdom 8 but do something which would qualify as an AoH even for a Wisdom 5 character, then you roll the smaller dice pool). Wording seems weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not strictly wrong, but the wording is a little odd. Wonder if it's from an earlier version of Wisdom?<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's 3 dice. It's listed as an sin against Understanding on page 88.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T09:26:13-08:00","id":1557260,"title":"","content":"Do Rote Specialties count as Skill dots for the purposes of using knowledge of a Rote Mudra as a +1 Yantra for an improvised spell of the same Arcanum and Practice (SoS p52)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T10:52:23-08:00","id":1557264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557260#post1557260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Rote Specialties count as Skill dots for the purposes of using knowledge of a Rote Mudra as a +1 Yantra for an improvised spell of the same Arcanum and Practice (SoS p52)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. To me the language looks relatively unambiguous.<br /> <br /> That said, personally I'd allow it. It's kinda cool whilst also being a real edge case. Would also allow Orders to use the yantra for 5-dot spells which I don't think they can otherwise.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T10:56:58-08:00","id":1557265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557260#post1557260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Rote Specialties count as Skill dots for the purposes of using knowledge of a Rote Mudra as a +1 Yantra for an improvised spell of the same Arcanum and Practice (SoS p52)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mudras. Signs of Sorcery p52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effect: A mage may attempt to use a mudra on an improvised<br /> spell, if she knows a rote of the same Arcanum and Practice.<br /> If she has <b>more dots in that rote\u2019s Skill </b>than in the required<br /> Arcana dots, she adds one die to her roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mudras. Mage Core 2ed p121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effect: Using a Rote\u2019s mudra <b>adds the user\u2019s rating</b> in the Rote\u2019s<br /> encoded Skill <b>to her dice pool up to +5</b>. If the <b>Skill is one of her<br /> Order\u2019s specialized Rote Skills, she adds an extra die</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the extra dice is never part of the skill dot amount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:00:05-08:00","id":1557267,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Which effects (besides destroying a soul as a Yantra) can be achieved on souls with Fate, Prime and Spirit? Death protects, removes, captures, sees, detect; Mind can interact with the Oneiros part of you that is the soul content... But how do the other 3 Subtle Arcana interact with souls?</li> <li>Do animals have any soul like equivalent? If so, which Arcana can affect it?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:02:17-08:00","id":1557270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557264#post1557264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. To me the language looks relatively unambiguous.<br /> <br /> That said, personally I'd allow it. It's kinda cool whilst also being a real edge case. Would also allow Orders to use the yantra for 5-dot spells which I don't think they can otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by 'they can't otherwise use these Yantra for a 5 dot spell? Gnosis 6 characters can get 6 in a skill, right? (Without resorting to magic and spending mana)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:04:04-08:00","id":1557271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557270#post1557270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by 'they can't otherwise use these Yantra for a 5 dot spell? Gnosis 6 characters can get 6 in a skill, right? (Without resorting to magic and spending mana)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I was getting myself confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:10:05-08:00","id":1557273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557271#post1557271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, I was getting myself confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seperately, a gnosis 5 character can only have mastery in 1 Arcanum, so they would indeed be limited until they reach gnosis 6... And at that, they would also need to encode a rote (or learn one) which requires 5 dots.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how useful/common it is to have Making/Unmaking rotes, since everyone who can use them can also make rotes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:28:57-08:00","id":1557274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557267#post1557267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which effects (besides destroying a soul as a Yantra) can be achieved on souls with Fate, Prime and Spirit? Death protects, removes, captures, sees, detect; Mind can interact with the Oneiros part of you that is the soul content... But how do the other 3 Subtle Arcana interact with souls?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned in the corebook's section on Reapers, while Death is where most of the stuff interacting with souls as systems objects is found, the soul narratively serves as the vector of access to other aspects of its owner like their good fortune, intellect, or other things relating to their Subtle Arcana.<br /> <br /> Spirit is tricky in this regard mainly because its most direct applications are toward expressly nonhuman phenomena, but at bare minimum having a person's soul should logically allow you to duplicate whatever Resonances they have and draw the attention of any spirits they're tagged for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do animals have any soul like equivalent? If so, which Arcana can affect it? </div> </div> </div>Animals do not have individual souls in the sense that humans do outside the context of unusual circumstances like Uplift deviants or more particular Mysteries. The closest other phenomena are the individual spirits born from individual animals and the Goetia from the Anima Mundi corresponding to that species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T12:07:16-08:00","id":1557275,"title":"","content":"Two questions;<br /> <br /> What kind of reputation or acknowledgment will a mage who has become a master of an arcana in their consilium? Is there any or a rank or a attaboy?<br /> <br /> second, 2e mentions that a cabal that has each member create a legacy would be considered legendary. What about just one mage making a legacy itself? Does it come with perks or rank or acknowledgment of any type?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T12:22:00-08:00","id":1557276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557275#post1557275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of reputation or acknowledgment will a mage who has become a master of an arcana in their consilium? Is there any or a rank or a attaboy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Chapter Two of the corebook, any mage attending a Convocation who can prove Mastery of an Arcanum can join the committee of Magisters running the joint and being able to codify Rotes is a social currency all its own. What you do with the accomplishment is going to be the greater determinant of how you're received for it, but it's a solid basis for at least middling Status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> second, 2e mentions that a cabal that has each member create a legacy would be considered legendary. What about just one mage making a legacy itself? Does it come with perks or rank or acknowledgment of any type? </div> </div> </div>It's rare for a mage to not have a Legacy by the time they've become an Adept and creating a Legacy requires substantial legwork and puts you in a nominal position of power over anyone inducted into it. Anything else is going to depend on particulars, as with Mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T12:34:03-08:00","id":1557277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557274#post1557274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned in the corebook's section on Reapers, while Death is where most of the stuff interacting with souls as systems objects is found, the soul narratively serves as the vector of access to other aspects of its owner like their good fortune, intellect, or other things relating to their Subtle Arcana.<br /> <br /> Spirit is tricky in this regard mainly because its most direct applications are toward expressly nonhuman phenomena, but at bare minimum having a person's soul should logically allow you to duplicate whatever Resonances they have and draw the attention of any spirits they're tagged for.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait, Fate is fine if we ascribe things like a destiny (not necessarily there Destiny) as an aspect of the soul. That works for me.<br /> <br /> Spirit is difficult as you discuss. <br /> <br /> Mind works ok with the Onerios bring apart of the soul - you can manipulate memories, vice/virtue, aspiration... That will all he reflected in the Onerios<br /> <br /> But what about Prime?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T12:59:51-08:00","id":1557279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557277#post1557277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana and the Nimbus are the most obvious and least contentious Prime-based aspects of the self to co-opt, but Shadow Names are also contextually suitable and a case could be made for limited appropriation of Gnosis or Arcana ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T13:08:12-08:00","id":1557280,"title":"","content":"Page 192 of Mage corebook mentions that players or Storytellers may devise more Lesser Utility Attainments than the ones listed in the book \u2014 how would this work? Would these new base-Arcana Attainments be devised by specific mages and need to be learned like Legacy Attainments are (with the same XP cost)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T17:25:14-08:00","id":1557285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557279#post1557279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana and the Nimbus are the most obvious and least contentious Prime-based aspects of the self to co-opt, but Shadow Names are also contextually suitable and a case could be made for limited appropriation of Gnosis or Arcana ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these only apply to Mages. AFAIK there is no example of Mana, Nimbuses or Shadow Names from Sleepers, but they have souls nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T18:08:07-08:00","id":1557289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557285#post1557285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these only apply to Mages. AFAIK there is no example of Mana, Nimbuses or Shadow Names from Sleepers, but they have souls nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though if you are developing magic to borrow the aspects of the soul that correspond to specifically magic it is not a huge concern that nonmagical people do not have magic to borrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T19:11:25-08:00","id":1557290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557289#post1557289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though if you are developing magic to borrow the aspects of the soul that correspond to specifically magic it is not a huge concern that nonmagical people do not have magic to borrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do, there is the capacity to do hedge magics powered by the soul - like the Blue Book Abjuration that I haven't read..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T02:22:47-08:00","id":1557299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557275#post1557275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions;<br /> <br /> What kind of reputation or acknowledgment will a mage who has become a master of an arcana in their consilium? Is there any or a rank or a attaboy?<br /> <br /> second, 2e mentions that a cabal that has each member create a legacy would be considered legendary. What about just one mage making a legacy itself? Does it come with perks or rank or acknowledgment of any type?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, pg.86, has public acknowledgements of arcana rank and legacy being made during the Day of Scrolls of a convocation.<br /> <br /> <i>Silver Ladder</i> pg.53 indicates that magisteria(?) quite often give out prizes to encourage mages to contribute to the proceedings.<br /> <br /> Run the two together and there's plenty of room for public acknowledgment and reputation building. That said, mages tend to challenge each other on points of magical theory, so if you declare a new legacy, I'd expect to be challenged on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T06:28:48-08:00","id":1557305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557275#post1557275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions;<br /> <br /> What kind of reputation or acknowledgment will a mage who has become a master of an arcana in their consilium? Is there any or a rank or a attaboy?<br /> <br /> second, 2e mentions that a cabal that has each member create a legacy would be considered legendary. What about just one mage making a legacy itself? Does it come with perks or rank or acknowledgment of any type?</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is just my interpretation of it. Founding a Legacy first requires you to delve deeply into an aspect of your connection with magic that holds personal significance. Then you must distill and refine whatever deep insights you obtained into what is simultaneously an occult methodology and a philosophy, which lets you embody that aspect of Supernal Truth. The entire process requires time, diligence and is personally, spiritually and mentally challenging. Not many mages have the mettle to see the work through. So a cabal where every member was able to see the journey through would be seen as legendary not only because of this, but also since each cabalmate created a personal inheritance of their own connection to magic for future generations of the Awakened.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T08:38:28-08:00","id":1557309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557305#post1557305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So this is just my interpretation of it. Founding a Legacy first requires you to delve deeply into an aspect of your connection with magic that holds personal significance. Then you must distill and refine whatever deep insights you obtained into what is simultaneously an occult methodology and a philosophy, which lets you embody that aspect of Supernal Truth. The entire process requires time, diligence and is personally, spiritually and mentally challenging. Not many mages have the mettle to see the work through. So a cabal where every member was able to see the journey through would be seen as legendary not only because of this, but also since each cabalmate created a personal inheritance of their own connection to magic for future generations of the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just spitballing so correct me if I'm wrong, but it also feels like it could be slightly concerning for more paranoid Diamond members who think these guys could start their own very powerful nameless order, while others might be overjoyed and see them as experts and want to study them as a Mystery on how their views of magic affected one another and their legacies?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T09:40:40-08:00","id":1557310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557309#post1557309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but it also feels like it could be slightly concerning for more paranoid Diamond members who think these guys could start their own very powerful nameless order...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's unlikely. There are legacies that already have their own internal structures which resemble nameless orders. But really, as long as you're not doing anything wildly illegal (or at least keep it mostly secret), the Orders are quite accommodating.<br /> <br /> What's more worrying is that your new legacy is totally untested. With established legacies, you have some certainty that their teachings aren't inherently tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T09:50:27-08:00","id":1557311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557310#post1557310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's unlikely. There are legacies that already have their own internal structures which resemble nameless orders. But really, as long as you're not doing anything wildly illegal (or at least keep it mostly secret), the Orders are quite accommodating.<br /> <br /> What's more worrying is that your new legacy is totally untested. With established legacies, you have some certainty that their teachings aren't inherently tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if they are uncomfortable while not being philosophically illegal, like how the <i>Eleventh Question</i> are dedicated to uncovering the truth when the Guardians are all about veils of obfuscation. Or if you are doing something so wildly useful that the founder's Order wants to keep control of it, like the Guardians with the <i>Bearers of the Eternal Voice or </i>the status the<i> Stewards of the Celestial Orrery </i>brought to the Silver<i> Ladder </i>before the Great Refusal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-05-2026, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T10:13:02-08:00","id":1557312,"title":"","content":"Why would a legacy become more like a nameless order rather than being part of the founding member's order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T06:09:03-08:00","id":1557415,"title":"","content":"Multiple related questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would <i>Ephemeral Shield</i> offer protection against Geryo, Hosts and Idigam?</li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Spirit and like?</li> <li>Would <i>Ghost Shield</i> offer protection against Kerberoi, Ferrymen, and Geists?</li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Ghosts and like?</li> <li>Would <i>Mental Shield</i> offer protection against Horrors?</li> <li>\u200bWould it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Goetia and like?</li> <li>Which Arcana, if any, would offer protection against Pangaeans the same way that the \u200b\u200b<i>Ephemera</i>l <i>/ Ghost /\u200b Mental Shield</i> family of spells?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T07:07:07-08:00","id":1557416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557415#post1557415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple related questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would <i>Ephemeral Shield</i> offer protection against Geryo, Hosts and Idigam?</li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Spirit and like?</li> <li>Would <i>Ghost Shield</i> offer protection against Kerberoi, Ferrymen, and Geists?</li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Ghosts and like?</li> <li>Would <i>Mental Shield</i> offer protection against Horrors?</li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Goetia and like?</li> <li>Which Arcana, if any, would offer protection against Pangaeans the same way that the \u200b\u200b<i>Ephemera</i>l <i>/ Ghost /\u200b Mental Shield</i> family of spells?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>As with the &quot;What's the Deal with Prime?&quot; sidebar in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, supernatural effects and physical damage that is entirely supernatural in nature (with the Reach effect for relevant physical attacks) are fair game for the relevant ephemeral beings or their supernatural effects. Anything else is not.<br /> <br /> So possessed creatures' attacks aren't going to ping the Shield spells any more than werewolf claws are subject to Prime Armor, but Ghost Shield is notionally fair game against the subtypes of ghost found or sourced to the Underworld; if a Host or Pangaean uses supernatural powers based on their spiritual nature instead of their bodies or their Arcana those have to contend with Ephemeral Shield, but anything above Rank 5 wins a Clash of Wills with anything below that supernatural weight class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T08:39:17-08:00","id":1557418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557415#post1557415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple related questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would <i>Ephemeral Shield</i> offer protection against Geryo, Hosts and Idigam?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Geryo - no, in the same way it usually doesn't protect against werewolves.<br /> Idigam - yes, they are basically spirits, right?<br /> Hosts - when possessing something, no, when in their natural form, probably also no. Pangeans are not really spirits, and Hosts aren't even Pangeans anymore - so I suspect it would depend on your table. But I don't think they typically use spirit Numina, so I'm leaning towards no.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div></li> <li>Would it count against a creature possessed by an entity of the relevant type i.e. Spirit and like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T18:48:44-08:00","id":1557432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557312#post1557312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a legacy become more like a nameless order rather than being part of the founding member's order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be disagreements or wanting to exist outside of the order? Or could be like the keepers of Vedet before their destruction and were planning on applying for full order status.<br /> <br /> <br /> Question, could an ochemata or proxy be unaware they are one? Like, someone has a seemingly normal life but were created by an archmaster as a tool or experiment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T18:56:16-08:00","id":1557434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557432#post1557432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, could an ochemata or proxy be unaware they are one? Like, someone has a seemingly normal life but were created by an archmaster as a tool or experiment?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Powerful supernatural being forgot what they were and/or incarnated as a superficially mortal entity&quot; is a whole story hook that shows up in varying degrees throughout the franchise, yes. SoS's section on Ochemata outright says some Ochemata separated from their creator have forgotten what they were.<br /> <br /> Being an aspect of a god (or the vessel therefor) doesn't require self-knowledge of that type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-09-2026, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T19:39:24-08:00","id":1557435,"title":"","content":"<b>Ghost Gate</b> is duration primary and has a Reach effect:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +1 Reach: The mage is able to transform her subject into the<br /> Twilight state without the use of the gate. All of her clothes<br /> and personal possessions turn into ephemera as she makes<br /> the transition. </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Essentially, what happens when the duration expires? Does the subject goes back to the material? Are they stuck on the Twilight?<br /> 2. If someone is on the Twilight side, casting Ghost Gate with this Reach, sends them back to the material? Seems obvious but it is not stated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding <b>Empty Presence</b>:<br /> <br /> 3. This spells ends all conditions on you, what happens with things like Aponoia, Embarrassing Secret, Enervated, Madness, Mystery Commands, etc? Will the Embarrassisng Secret be made public or somehow dissapears from the limelight? Does the Exarch leave your soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-09-2026, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T19:57:21-08:00","id":1557436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557435#post1557435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Essentially, what happens when the duration expires? Does the subject goes back to the material? Are they stuck on the Twilight?<br /> 2. If someone is on the Twilight side, casting Ghost Gate with this Reach, sends them back to the material? Seems obvious but it is not stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;side&quot; \u2014 casting the spell with the Reach effect directly converts its subject into a Twilight state for the Duration, after which they return to the material frequency of reality. The plane created by the base effect works the same way except it destroys the material forms of items that pass through it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding <b>Empty Presence</b>:<br /> 3. This spells ends all conditions on you, what happens with things like Aponoia? </div> </div> </div>Aponoia doesn't have a resolution criterion in the first place; I would treat it the same as Paradox Conditions as far as &quot;this spell does not affect this Condition.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T05:01:54-08:00","id":1557445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557436#post1557436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Aponoia doesn't have a resolution criterion in the first place; I would treat it the same as Paradox Conditions as far as &quot;this spell does not affect this Condition.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for replying, what about things like Embarrassing Secret, Enervated, Madness, Mystery Commands, etc? Will the Embarrassisng Secret be made public or somehow dissapears from the limelight? Does the Exarch leave your soul as per the normal resolution? etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T06:04:49-08:00","id":1557446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557435#post1557435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding <b>Empty Presence</b>:<br /> <br /> 3. This spells ends all conditions on you, what happens with things like Aponoia, Embarrassing Secret, Enervated, Madness, Mystery Commands, etc? Will the Embarrassisng Secret be made public or somehow dissapears from the limelight? Does the Exarch leave your soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an example of the mini-rule system (conditions) not meshing with a spell's fluff.<br /> <br /> RAW, yes the spell causes the conditions to end. At my table i would look at the individual conditions. Enervated makes very little sense to end because your presence in the world has dissapeared.<br /> <br /> Mystery Commands might end since the Exarchs can't see you, but on the other hand any clash of wills with an Exarch will automatically be won by the Exarch... So it depends on if they try to see the character.<br /> <br /> All other conditions I would determine on a case by case basis (like no, this doesn't heal the Blind condition, unless the Blindness is somehow caused by something ongoing...)<br /> <br /> A Death 5 spell to end conditions which have a normal resolution does kinda make sense given the Death Purview of Endings... So your milage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-10-2026, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T07:02:29-08:00","id":1557449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557445#post1557445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for replying, what about things like Embarrassing Secret, Enervated, Madness, Mystery Commands, etc? Will the Embarrassisng Secret be made public or somehow dissapears from the limelight? Does the Exarch leave your soul as per the normal resolution? etc</div> </div> </div> </div>The intention of Empty Presence is very clearly not that a Master of Death can fully bypass parts of the metaphysics that exist outside the Phenomenal World or cure soullessness. The spell is in some ways poorly worded, but the description of its narrative effect is roughly akin to those of the fifth dot of the Curse Haunt in Geist \u2014 it's a way to <i>It's a Wonderful Life</i> somebody or otherwise pull their presence out of the world for a limited time.<br /> <br /> Conditions internal to the character should logically not be affected by the spell, nor should Conditions that bypass the material and social reality being messed with. A clearer way to read the text would be &quot;if the character has applied a Condition to someone or something else, or someone or something else has a Condition that references the character, that Condition is gone.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your rival was Inspired to take action against you? That Inspired Condition resolves flatly. You made that sweetheart at the bar Swooned for you? Not anymore. Your Embarrassing Secret got out and now you've got Notoriety with the locals? No you don't. Your apprentice feels Guilty about getting into trouble that you had to suffer a severe Paradox to resolve? They've forgotten all about it. You're Connected with City Hall? Might as well have burned those bridges. You Bonded with a dog you were training? You are a stranger to it now.<br /> <br /> The subject of Empty Presence is invisible to the naked eye and has their impact on the world erased from the present state of things until the spell ends, whether by natural Duration or violent action. It does not fix anything that isn't reliant on other living beings knowing you exist or physical evidence of your presence. Think of it like if you used Time to erase yourself from the timeline except with a smaller scope of alteration to the rest of the world \u2014 it's not going to un-build the construction project that exists because you saved a politician's life, nor will it retroactively kill that politician, but as far as the world is concerned there's no evidence of your involvement and people will either not think of those things or attribute them to other causes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T08:40:34-08:00","id":1557452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557434#post1557434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Powerful supernatural being forgot what they were and/or incarnated as a superficially mortal entity&quot; is a whole story hook that shows up in varying degrees throughout the franchise, yes. SoS's section on Ochemata outright says some Ochemata separated from their creator have forgotten what they were.<br /> <br /> Being an aspect of a god (or the vessel therefor) doesn't require self-knowledge of that type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Speaking of Archmages, is there a limit to how big a chantry can be or what laws of physics or arcana are present, and is there any way to shield something from the threat of imperial spells accidentally erasing them or changing them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","user":"Snailslayer","date":". 01-10-2026, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T09:38:08-08:00","id":1557453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557452#post1557452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Archmages, is there a limit to how big a chantry can be</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct conversion is tricky because 1e and 2e use different metrics for area scale (notably also having Advanced Area Scale be a direct continuation of Standard Area Scale in 2e), but Imperial Spell Factors increased Area/Volume by a factor of 8 per rank (up from a factor of 4 per rank with Advanced or a factor of 2 per rank normally) such that going to Imperial Scale 6 could easily encompass a notable portion of a city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or what laws of physics or arcana are present, </div> </div> </div>Assuming the basics haven't changed between editions, a Chantry is initially created based on an existing location of great personal significance to the archmaster with the effective size of the area being based on the spell factors, and then further modified by whatever else its creator does with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and is there any way to shield something from the threat of imperial spells accidentally erasing them or changing them? </div> </div> </div>They're the products of spells and therefore subject to a Clash of Wills for anything that would somehow target them, but they're inside an archmaster's soul in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T12:31:18-08:00","id":1557454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557453#post1557453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're the products of spells and therefore subject to a Clash of Wills for anything that would somehow target them, but they're inside an archmaster's soul in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah thanks for the size. Do you mean the Imperial spells or like, could an archmaster stick their loved ones in a chantry to protect them by having them within the archmasters soul?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-10T12:51:40-08:00","id":1557455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557454#post1557454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah thanks for the size. Do you mean the Imperial spells or like, could an archmaster stick their loved ones in a chantry to protect them by having them within the archmasters soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting into a Chantry requires sympathy, uses the caster's sympathy to the archmaster, and only works if the spell is able to target from or into the location the Chantry's basis is from (e.g. if the formative Iris into the Chantry is in the Shadow, you need Spirit to cast into that Chantry). Not for nothing does 2e compare them to Emanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T07:58:17-08:00","id":1557802,"title":"","content":"Does a piece of Tass with a Resonance (happy) harvested from a &quot;Noded&quot; Hallow also have a Resonant Manifestation condition or the two things are not linked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:09:31-08:00","id":1557803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557802#post1557802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a piece of Tass with a Resonance (happy) harvested from a &quot;Noded&quot; Hallow also have a Resonant Manifestation condition or the two things are not linked?</div> </div> </div> </div>The breadth of the Resonant Condition means that anything that matches the description of one of a spirit or goetia's Influences has that Condition tagged to that ephemeral being, so yes, Happy tass is Resonant with spirits and ideoforms related to happiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:18:25-08:00","id":1557805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557803#post1557803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The breadth of the Resonant Condition means that anything that matches the description of one of a spirit or goetia's Influences has that Condition tagged to that ephemeral being, so yes, Happy tass is Resonant with spirits and ideoforms related to happiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or ghosts who... Died happy? No wait, that doesn't work... (Plus ghosts and anchors work differently, and I don't know how Geists actually work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:22:05-08:00","id":1557806,"title":"","content":"So, it s safe to assume that the whole Node would have the Resonant Condition as a place or probably only some fixed items, produced tass and inhabitants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T08:40:48-08:00","id":1557808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557806#post1557806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it s safe to assume that the whole Node would have the Resonant Condition as a place or probably only some fixed items, produced tass and inhabitants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the contributing ley line and any of the tass that has that Resonance, since tass from a Node only has one of its Resonances. You might be able to use a Compelling spell to expand the effect a la Invoke Bane, but generally speaking the Resonant Condition is very common to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T04:14:03-08:00","id":1557892,"title":"","content":"Do you think that a Knowing Prime spell Withstanded by Opacity is enough to &quot;identify&quot; an awakened spell?<br /> Or do i need conjunctional other Arcana used in the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T07:56:36-08:00","id":1557895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557892#post1557892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that a Knowing Prime spell Withstanded by Opacity is enough to &quot;identify&quot; an awakened spell?<br /> Or do i need conjunctional other Arcana used in the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the only published spell Withstood by Opacity is Path to Jerusalem, which does the opposite of this, as well as the way the Opacity mechanics work and the fact that spells can be lent to other characters through Imbuing them, I don't think you can use spells to bypass the normal Revelation and Scrutiny mechanics in this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T08:26:19-08:00","id":1557897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557895#post1557895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the only published spell Withstood by Opacity is Path to Jerusalem, which does the opposite of this, as well as the way the Opacity mechanics work and the fact that spells can be lent to other characters through Imbuing them, I don't think you can use spells to bypass the normal Revelation and Scrutiny mechanics in this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the reasons of the answer, but considering that Prime has &quot;magic&quot; under its purview, i find equally strange the absence of a Knowing spell ONLY for this Arcana.<br /> If each level of potency gives an information on the subject spell i don t think that a similar spell would be game breaking, so i wonder if this omission is a conscious game choice or not.<br /> I mean, i can dispel a spell but not know it, why so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 01-25-2026, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T08:57:12-08:00","id":1557900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557897#post1557897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the reasons of the answer, but considering that Prime has &quot;magic&quot; under its purview, i find equally strange the absence of a Knowing spell ONLY for this Arcana.<br /> If each level of potency gives an information on the subject spell i don t think that a similar spell would be game breaking, so i wonder if this omission is a conscious game choice or not.<br /> I mean, i can dispel a spell but not know it, why so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Surface Information only gives the Practice and Arcana of the spell and that it's an Awakened spell, while Deep Information provides things like how the Arcana relate to the Mystery in question, what its spell factors are, and so on.<br /> <br /> A Knowing spell almost by definition is going to be a Potency-primary spell, and since the number of successes needed to fully Scrutinize a Mystery is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triangular_number\" target=\"_blank\">triangular number</a> based on its Opacity that makes the spell disproportionately more useful than the primary tool mages use for scrutinizing spells.<br /> <br /> Prime also has the Supernal World under its purviews, but a Master of Prime can't create or destroy the Aether just because Making and Unmaking spells in that Arcanum exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T15:14:49-08:00","id":1557904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557900#post1557900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Surface Information only gives the Practice and Arcana of the spell and that it's an Awakened spell, while Deep Information provides things like how the Arcana relate to the Mystery in question, what its spell factors are, and so on.<br /> <br /> A Knowing spell almost by definition is going to be a Potency-primary spell, and since the number of successes needed to fully Scrutinize a Mystery is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triangular_number\" target=\"_blank\">triangular number</a> based on its Opacity that makes the spell disproportionately more useful than the primary tool mages use for scrutinizing spells.<br /> <br /> Prime also has the Supernal World under its purviews, but a Master of Prime can't create or destroy the Aether just because Making and Unmaking spells in that Arcanum exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see.<br /> Instead, does the existence of Path to jerusalem imply the possibility of an opposed spell that decrease Opacity?<br /> What practice would it be?<br /> Would it be necessary to add one Mana cost to make it more fair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T16:56:59-08:00","id":1557906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557904#post1557904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, does the existence of Path to jerusalem imply the possibility of an opposed spell that decrease Opacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same issues I described above are the basis for my opinion that it does not. A single Potency would be enough to cut off a significant fraction of the required total successes needed for Scrutiny because, again, every extra level of Opacity adds more to that number than the last \u2014 for spells, you need to be dealing with Master-level conjunctive effects or the products of archmastery for a one-Opacity reduction to not take off at least a third of the required Scrutiny successes.<br /> <br /> Combined with the fact that Scrutiny allows you to spend Mana to get extra successes on its rolls, a one-Mana cost for a spell to reduce the Opacity of a Mystery flatly is not a fair exchange, especially since the equivalent of an opposed spell to Path to Jerusalem, which is a Veiling spell, would be an Unveiling spell \u2014 and the Unveiling spell that lets a target contend with the Opacity of a Mystery is Shared Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T04:29:08-08:00","id":1557910,"title":"","content":"When a mage uses Focused mage sight on an Artifact, is the trigger included in the deep information or it s necessary to research or divine it with prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T07:54:31-08:00","id":1557912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557910#post1557910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a mage uses Focused mage sight on an Artifact, is the trigger included in the deep information or it s necessary to research or divine it with prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per SoS, Deep Information represents total understanding of a Mystery, with one of the examples including how to open the Mystery Door, so in all probability fully Scrutinizing and Revealing an Artifact would include the trigger.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that you can find the trigger of an Artifact through a regular extended research action, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T09:18:24-08:00","id":1557913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1557906#post1557906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same issues I described above are the basis for my opinion that it does not. A single Potency would be enough to cut off a significant fraction of the required total successes needed for Scrutiny because, again, every extra level of Opacity adds more to that number than the last \u2014 for spells, you need to be dealing with Master-level conjunctive effects or the products of archmastery for a one-Opacity reduction to not take off at least a third of the required Scrutiny successes.<br /> <br /> Combined with the fact that Scrutiny allows you to spend Mana to get extra successes on its rolls, a one-Mana cost for a spell to reduce the Opacity of a Mystery flatly is not a fair exchange, especially since the equivalent of an opposed spell to Path to Jerusalem, which is a Veiling spell, would be an Unveiling spell \u2014 and the Unveiling spell that lets a target contend with the Opacity of a Mystery is Shared Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just add, a lot of people don't actually like the scrutiny rules, because they are not fun to play. So while the above is a fair RAW, I think it is worthwhile discussing what a valid alternative would be...<br /> <br /> Replacing a system which all mages can use with a better/faster one which only Prime mages can use seems like it would be a bad design choice.<br /> <br /> On the meta-physics side (or more Watsonian way of addressing the question). Scrutiny/revelation is different from Knowing, in the sense that Knowing usually extracts some knowledge/supernal symbols from the underlying world. on the other hand, Scrutiny is about looking at many different supernal symbols at the same time and collectively examining them in more depth (even to the point of spending mana to see how those symbols work as mana flows through them), and this implies a deeper kind of understanding being extracted than a simple Knowing spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T05:15:56-08:00","id":1558064,"title":"","content":"How would you create an invisible force sword with forces that acts a bit like powerswords in wh40 (it tears anything that dares to touch it)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T05:24:56-08:00","id":1558065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558064#post1558064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you create an invisible force sword with forces that acts a bit like powerswords in wh40 (it tears anything that dares to touch it)?</div> </div> </div> </div>To literally tear up anything, and only the Forces Arcanum, I would want an item which projects an AoE Unmaking effect, to remove the force binding anything together.<br /> <br /> The sharp edge of the blade (once activated) slicing through any physical object held together by forces.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the limitations of imbued items would leave you rather limited by the withstand/potency of any sword made using an imbued effect. And it may be more reasonable to use a Eeaving or Patterning effect which dealt damage rather than simply Unmaking things directly (or failing to unmake things where it lacked the potency... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-02-2026, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T05:54:21-08:00","id":1558066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558065#post1558065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To literally tear up anything, and only the Forces Arcanum, I would want an item which projects an AoE Unmaking effect, to remove the force binding anything together.<br /> <br /> The sharp edge of the blade (once activated) slicing through any physical object held together by forces.<br /> <br /> However, I suspect the limitations of imbued items would leave you rather limited by the withstand/potency of any sword made using an imbued effect. And it may be more reasonable to use a Eeaving or Patterning effect which dealt damage rather than simply Unmaking things directly (or failing to unmake things where it lacked the potency...</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont want it to be a imbuned item, i would prefer it be a spell that makes a invisibble sword made of pure force in the characters hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T06:31:08-08:00","id":1558068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558066#post1558066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont want it to be a imbuned item, i would prefer it be a spell that makes a invisibble sword made of pure force in the characters hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure Power Swords in 40K can be switched off, and are still Swords (unlike, say light sabres).<br /> <br /> But even just using a spell, to localise the effect onto the edge of a blade (this making it easier to handle like a sword) would work fine as a AoE spell - with the area defined by the edge of the blade.<br /> <br /> There is some question of whether an AoE spell can move around. But for an invisible blade like effect, it does need to be an AoE, because the effect is dissolving the bonds between any subject which enters the area. Otherwise you have to define the subjects when the spell is cast.<br /> <br /> Imbued items have the advantage that they can define the subjects as whoever is welding the item...but that doesn't really work for a sword.<br /> <br /> In theory you don't need the physical sword to define a sword shaped AoE, but it is more intuitive to me... Like having a hilt which projects an AoE spell might work too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T06:34:36-08:00","id":1558069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558066#post1558066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont want it to be a imbuned item, i would prefer it be a spell that makes a invisibble sword made of pure force in the characters hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there still a Death spell to pull together tools and such out of shadows? I think that might be a decent starting place to model a similar spell elsewhere. <br /> <br /> I do think the level of specificity you're suggesting out of it might be beyond the granularity of the overall game system and the level of complexity that typically exists in the subjects of a single spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T10:20:03-08:00","id":1558079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558069#post1558069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there still a Death spell to pull together tools and such out of shadows? I think that might be a decent starting place to model a similar spell elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I do think the level of specificity you're suggesting out of it might be beyond the granularity of the overall game system and the level of complexity that typically exists in the subjects of a single spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a death spell, comparable to platonic form (prime) making tools out of solidified mana.<br /> <br /> But for some reason Shadow Crafting limits you to 2 (durability/weapon rating/armour rating/equipment bonus). While Platonic forms have 1 + potency divided among the (durability/weapon rating/armour rating/equipment bonus) - I'm not sure if they should be using the same rules as each other... (Death also has Shape Ephemera, which lets you turn a ghost/Castoff into a object with durability 2 using the same mechanics as Shadow Crafting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T06:50:32-08:00","id":1558090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558066#post1558066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont want it to be a imbuned item, i would prefer it be a spell that makes a invisibble sword made of pure force in the characters hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a Potency primary Unraveling of Matter. When the weapon hits, each point of bonus allows the user to reduce either a dot of armor or durability from the target as the blade tears the material apart. Then just add a combined cast of <i>Hidden Hoard </i>and people will not notice the blade. I think that would be the closest thing to a discrete power sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T13:08:29-08:00","id":1558098,"title":"","content":"Not mechanically but in terms of what a mage actually perceives, what exactly is the difference between Active and Focused Mage Sight? Like if an Acanthus were studying some Thorns wrapped around a Mystery, how would their view change in switching between Active and Focused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28277-nebulous_bat","name":"Nebulous_Bat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T13:50:26-08:00","id":1558099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558098#post1558098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not mechanically but in terms of what a mage actually perceives, what exactly is the difference between Active and Focused Mage Sight? Like if an Acanthus were studying some Thorns wrapped around a Mystery, how would their view change in switching between Active and Focused?</div> </div> </div> </div>Active sight is like turning on an UI in all your senses, letting you see every symbol related to that Arcanum at once, like detective mode in an Arkham game. Focused Sight is when you block out all distractions, trying to understand whatever you are focusing on above everything else, going so deep down the rabbit hole that you peer directly into the Supernal, parsing all the symbolism associated to that Mystery into hallucinated insight, giving you understanding you might not have otherwise had available or even considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-03T17:16:25-08:00","id":1558102,"title":"","content":"Can you break Sympathetic Connections with Fate? A more advanced version of<i> Sever Oaths</i> perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T03:15:01-08:00","id":1558112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nebulous_Bat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558098#post1558098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not mechanically but in terms of what a mage actually perceives, what exactly is the difference between Active and Focused Mage Sight? Like if an Acanthus were studying some Thorns wrapped around a Mystery, how would their view change in switching between Active and Focused?</div> </div> </div> </div>With Active Mage Sight, you see symbols of your Path concerning the Arcana that you've incorporated it overlaying the world as a whole. This gives you a general sense of the interplay of things as they relate to the Path. Arcadia has a perspective of things unfolding with a sense of narrative, with a particular sense of some things having portentous significance or highly variable future, so you'll recognise the interplay of circumstances corresponding to that; primarily, <i>that</i> something progressing in a manner with a narrative format is occurring, but not any of the finer details. A Mystery whose nature corresponds to any Arcana included in your Sight will be highlighted strongly; you'll know it has greater significance than the things surrounding it, that the narrative effect it is drawing has supernatural potency.<br /> <br /> Focused Mage Sight contracts your vision to the point of a single subject, a single Pattern. You go from a general overlay upon the world into seeing the subject of scrutiny entirely in terms of your Path symbols, often with the aid of mana released to form more coherent patterns of it. Successful dice rolls represent the process of the meaning of these symbols being understood by you, allowing you to discern the driving nature of them. For a Mystery, that means acquiring information about its features. For a mundane subject, that means seeing what its experience of reality through the lens of your Path is. When you Focus your Sight on a person you noticed is caught up in something that stands out in Arcadia, you can get an impression of what their role in events is, what has brought them to this point, and the possibilities in their future.<br /> <br /> If Active Sight is where you see the Thorns and Mists gather around a person in a way that indicates that they have stuff going on, Focused Sight is where those symbols coalesce into a rose in their breast pocket, a rapier at their side, and tears streaming down their face to give the understanding that theirs is the story of a torrid romance (although I'd say it helps to include the Mind Arcanum to have a clearer sense of the emotional context).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T03:28:30-08:00","id":1558113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558102#post1558102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you break Sympathetic Connections with Fate? A more advanced version of<i> Sever Oaths</i> perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily phrase it in terms of a stronger version of an unrelated spell, but yeah, between what Fate covers in general and it having been established to have some coverage of sympathy, that seems to make sense. I feel as though it would be an Unmaking spell that removes whatever common path its subjects have together in a manner that includes the loss of their sympathetic connection but is not necessarily even limited to it. It's like, whatever their story was, it's gone now, and with it goes most circumstance or personal motive to continue interacting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T09:01:00-08:00","id":1558115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558113#post1558113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't necessarily phrase it in terms of a stronger version of an unrelated spell, but yeah, between what Fate covers in general and it having been established to have some coverage of sympathy, that seems to make sense. I feel as though it would be an Unmaking spell that removes whatever common path its subjects have together in a manner that includes the loss of their sympathetic connection but is not necessarily even limited to it. It's like, whatever their story was, it's gone now, and with it goes most circumstance or personal motive to continue interacting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I disagree. When you read about sympathetic links, you can imagine a person loving their partner who has grown apart still having a strong connection one way while the other direction it is medium or weak.<br /> <br /> Those emotional aspects of sympathy are almosst entirely Mind. <br /> <br /> Fate could indeed set up a path where two people (or a person and the murder weapon which killed their father) are no longer destined to kill each other (for example) and that the sympathy will necessarily weaken, but I don't think they can get rid of the emotional impact.<br /> <br /> Sure, a person might forget their partner over time. Their feelings might diminish, but that just happens naturally. <br /> <br /> You could rewrite Romeo and Juliette to no longer he star crossed lovers, but they will still have some romantic attraction to each other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-04T11:14:07-08:00","id":1558116,"title":"","content":"Fine. Adjust the precise wording of the thing that I said so that it captures the same sentiment while remaining consistent with this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sever a man\u2019s link to his husband and the relationship cools and grows distant. Create a bond between a woman and a gun, and she\u2019ll find herself thinking about it, dreaming about it \u2014 and left to their own devices odds are good woman and gun will cross paths. This isn\u2019t precisely mind control, or even an expression of Fate magic: all Space can do is manipulate the connections, not control reactions or guarantee outcomes. Maybe the chilled couple seeks counseling and repairs their relationship. Maybe the woman tells herself she\u2019s being crazy and deliberately ignores thoughts of firearms. The point is that playing with people\u2019s sympathetic links has a real, tangible effect on their lives. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T07:02:54-08:00","id":1558379,"title":"","content":"I m working on a Mystery.<br /> Do you think it s possible that a powerful Sekhem Relic shattering in a Time related Node (with or without Hallow) could cause a semi-permanent area of &quot;time freeze&quot; effect or it s a bit implausible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T09:55:58-08:00","id":1558381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558379#post1558379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m working on a Mystery.<br /> Do you think it s possible that a powerful Sekhem Relic shattering in a Time related Node (with or without Hallow) could cause a semi-permanent area of &quot;time freeze&quot; effect or it s a bit implausible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not versed enough in Mummy to say for sure, but wouldn't part of the issue be that, if you don't figure it out before entering, you are frozen permanently until someone teleports you asay or uses a Making of Time on you ? Maybe have conditions to be cauht by the freeze, have a grace period or have them exposed to some kind of energy that lets them function inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T11:09:20-08:00","id":1558383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558381#post1558381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not versed enough in Mummy to say for sure, but wouldn't part of the issue be that, if you don't figure it out before entering, you are frozen permanently until someone teleports you asay or uses a Making of Time on you ? Maybe have conditions to be cauht by the freeze, have a grace period or have them exposed to some kind of energy that lets them function inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a shielding spell before entering the area could protect a subject.<br /> My problem is not how the player would manage it, i m not experienced in designing Mysteries and i don t know what phenomenon has the potential to cause weird and unusual things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T12:14:51-08:00","id":1558385,"title":"","content":"Mysteries don't have to be some mechanical thing which is explained by other rules. The universe is just weird sometimes! (Like sometimes a ghost is created with rank 3-5, and sometimes Demon Exploits are just bugs in the universe).<br /> <br /> I don't think any of the big signature mysteries in the book have explanations. The magical dead zones in Tokyo, the magical portal to another world in Salamanca? They just are that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T12:21:42-08:00","id":1558386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558379#post1558379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m working on a Mystery.<br /> Do you think it s possible that a powerful Sekhem Relic shattering in a Time related Node (with or without Hallow) could cause a semi-permanent area of &quot;time freeze&quot; effect or it s a bit implausible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just about anything is possible in the right circumstances, though in a case like this it would almost definitely have to be either a very powerful relic or a Node with a lot more going on in or around it.<br /> <br /> Freezing time is within the scope of both Awakened magic and Arisen Utterances at high levels, albeit the latter's published effects are limited to a handful of turns and require Sekhem 5 or higher to use as well as a total of four Pillar points, so something like applying the Frozen Time Environmental Tilt to an area with an extended duration is probably going to require a fairly potent and/or complex setup to produce and/or maintain, but a Shielding spell to Clash with the effect is intuitive enough (though of course beware the duration-based boost to Clash rolls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T00:51:33-08:00","id":1558389,"title":"","content":"I think the book &quot;Night Horrors: The Unbidden&quot; is instructive here. It's a First Edition book, but I think it's consistent with a lot of the presentation in Second Edition, and indeed is arguably prototypical.<br /> <br /> It depicts a lot of weird beings and phenomena that are a result of Awakened magic, but aren't strictly consistent with the kind of magic that the rules enable one to cast. They run more on a narrative premise of &quot;unconsidered consequences and magic left to decay can turn freakish and disturbing&quot;.<br /> <br /> So when it comes to something like a magical item breaking in a magical location as the background for a strange phenomenon, you're not really bound by the limits of how this stuff works for the sake of being applied by players. At best, investigation might determine that a confluence of particulars led to that outcome, and were specific enough as to not be easily replicated.<br /> <br /> It's like all the oddities Star Trek gets up to with transporters. You get somebody improvising a beam through a unique atmospheric phenomenon under constrained circumstances, and bam, two Rikers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T07:34:20-08:00","id":1558409,"title":"","content":"In sign of sorcery it says:<br /> &quot;An Acanthus peers through a hag stone to study the Mysteries. A Moros sees the Supernal through the distortions of a cracked crystal ball.&quot;<br /> And states that those items are used as path tools.<br /> Does they conunt as Mirrors or are another form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T08:05:03-08:00","id":1558410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558409#post1558409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does they conunt as Mirrors or are another form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've wondered that.<br /> <br /> I think the crystal ball makes sense as a mirror, though I'm not sure why it's cracked. Could also be a coin.<br /> <br /> The hag stone could fit most of the categories, though none of them very well. Honestly, the closest I think is the coin. Hag stones aren't valuable in a traditional sense, but they are somewhat rare. Also, the ones people tend to pick up tend to be small and comparable in size to a large coin.<br /> <br /> The alternative is perhaps that although the book seems fairly restrictive in what counts as a path tool, those are actually more like examples, and at least some of the writers were fine with anything suitably evocative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T09:12:05-08:00","id":1558411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558410#post1558410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is perhaps that although the book seems fairly restrictive in what counts as a path tool, those are actually more like examples, and at least some of the writers were fine with anything suitably evocative.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's this; these are drawback-free +1 Yantras that make the spellcasting (or Mage Sight) more symbolically appropriate and the limited bus space for Yantras per usage means their comparatively low effectiveness incentivizes using more potent symbolism if you can swing it.<br /> <br /> Dedicated tools count as Path or Order tools, soul stones count as Dedicated tools when used by their creators, and soul stones have no restrictions on what they can be except for Size. Dark Eras presents historical Path tools that are notably different from the core five categories, and Signs of Sorcery itself notes that there are other categories like vehicles and places.<br /> <br /> My overall interpretation is that soul stones and other forms of Dedication gradually shape the symbolism of the Paths and give rise to Order Tools over time; in general a Tool offers its symbolism as appropriate to its form and the Path limits what a mage can make use of in those categories without Dedication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T10:47:29-08:00","id":1558414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558411#post1558411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dedicated tools count as Path or Order tools,</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I've never noticed that line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My overall interpretation is that soul stones and other forms of Dedication gradually shape the symbolism of the Paths and give rise to Order Tools over time; in general a Tool offers its symbolism as appropriate to its form and the Path limits what a mage can make use of in those categories without Dedication. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think you've got this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T11:08:06-08:00","id":1558415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558411#post1558411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">soul stones count as Dedicated tools when used by their creators, and soul stones have no restrictions on what they can be except for Size. </div> </div> </div> </div>There is no restrictions on what you can imprint your nimbus, or make into a soulstone (apart from size) but there is a restriction on when it can be used as a tool Yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When used by another mage as a tool Yantra, soul stones offer a +2 die bonus, or +3 if the creator\u2019s Gnosis is higher than the user\u2019s. <b>The stone\u2019s form must still be useable for the spell.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not the same for used by the creator (except it is automatically a dedicated tool - so presuming the dedicated tool rules apply, it can be a +0 tool Yantra with a bonus paradox mitigation?)<br /> <br /> At least that was my understanding...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T11:27:32-08:00","id":1558416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558415#post1558415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no restrictions on what you can imprint your nimbus, or make into a soulstone (apart from size) but there is a restriction on when it can be used as a tool Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same limitation as exists for using any Yantra. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/893054-question-about-the-dedicated-tool?p=893116#post893116\">You do still get the Paradox mitigation</a>, presumably because that aspect is to do with having a focus for your Nimbus rather than constructing the Imago itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T11:28:01-08:00","id":1558417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558415#post1558415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not the same for used by the creator (except it is automatically a dedicated tool - so presuming the dedicated tool rules apply, it can be a +0 tool Yantra with a bonus paradox mitigation?)<br /> <br /> At least that was my understanding...</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that as it requiring a semiotic link to the spell rather than it having to conform to a path or order tool. Given that soul stones are already limited to being tools it seems a slightly odd way to phrase it. Wouldn't you just say that explicitly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T11:57:41-08:00","id":1558418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558417#post1558417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read that as it requiring a semiotic link to the spell rather than it having to conform to a path or order tool. Given that soul stones are already limited to being tools it seems a slightly odd way to phrase it. Wouldn't you just say that explicitly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say anything about being limited to bring tools, it says they must be an object of size 2 or less.<br /> <br /> If they are also a Path tool, then where used as a tool Yantra by someone else they offer a +2/+3 bonus. <br /> <br /> But I spent ages assuming it was any object* and could be used with any spell. As opposed to &quot;if it is a tool appropriate to the spell&quot;, which is far more restrictive (and perhaps reasonable).<br /> <br /> The Nimbus/dedicated tool part is explained upon in SoS (dedicating other people's soul stones, for example). But how it works as a tool is not elaborated upon.<br /> <br /> *Probably because as written you <i>can</i> make any object into a soulstone...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T12:09:18-08:00","id":1558420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558418#post1558418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't say anything about being limited to bring tools, it says they must be an object of size 2 or less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read your quote again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When used by another mage as a <b>tool Yantra</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T12:24:06-08:00","id":1558421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558420#post1558420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read your quote again.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, so if the object you happen to impose your nimbus in happens to be an appropriate tool, that is &quot;The stone\u2019s form must still be useable for the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> Then it offers a +2/+3 bonus. Otherwise it can not be used as a Yantra for someone else. <br /> <br /> That seems to be the implication ar least.<br /> <br /> Look at the creation rules, it says &quot;an object&quot; multiple times, nothing like the limits in making a dedicated magical tool.<br /> <br /> But also, when used by the creator, it doesn't say it needs to be usable for the spell. So it could be A) appropriate to use with the spell and offer the usual +1 tool Yantra bonus. Or B) inappropriate and only offer the Paradox mitigation - just like a DMT (the soul stone merit in SoS is rather focused on other things, so adds no illumination to this conversation).<br /> <br /> Maybe you create a soulstone which intentionally has no obvious use as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Maybe you make one from a perfected metal to get the +2 bonus for using it as appropriate for that metal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T18:00:29-07:00","id":1558779,"title":"","content":"Faction question: Do members of a cross-Order faction whose Order's Rote Skills include both of the options for the additional Rote Skill double the bonus of one of their existing three, pick an appropriate alternative, or only gain the extra effective Status from the Faction Member Merit's third dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T08:24:30-07:00","id":1558793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558779#post1558779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faction question: Do members of a cross-Order faction whose Order's Rote Skills include both of the options for the additional Rote Skill double the bonus of one of their existing three, pick an appropriate alternative, or only gain the extra effective Status from the Faction Member Merit's third dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking an appropriate alternative would be my go to answer, that way you have an equivalent of the extra yantra flexibility you would normally associate with Faction membership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T10:53:33-07:00","id":1558796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558421#post1558421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, so if the object you happen to impose your nimbus in happens to be an appropriate tool, that is &quot;The stone\u2019s form must still be useable for the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> Then it offers a +2/+3 bonus. Otherwise it can not be used as a Yantra for someone else.<br /> <br /> That seems to be the implication ar least.<br /> <br /> Look at the creation rules, it says &quot;an object&quot; multiple times, nothing like the limits in making a dedicated magical tool.<br /> <br /> But also, when used by the creator, it doesn't say it needs to be usable for the spell. So it could be A) appropriate to use with the spell and offer the usual +1 tool Yantra bonus. Or B) inappropriate and only offer the Paradox mitigation - just like a DMT (the soul stone merit in SoS is rather focused on other things, so adds no illumination to this conversation).<br /> <br /> Maybe you create a soulstone which intentionally has no obvious use as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> Maybe you make one from a perfected metal to get the +2 bonus for using it as appropriate for that metal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The limit on the bonuses you can HAVE from a single tool is set by materials plus the available semiotic associations, the limit on what you can USE is the maximum number of Yantras your Gnosis allows (plus being Dedicated, that is always a free rider as DaveB mentioned already).<br /> <br /> For example, a Silver Ladder Acanthus, who dedicates a Lunargent signet ring that is also their Soulstone. They would get all the bonuses when applicable: made of Lunargent, a Silver Ladder tool (as a symbol of authority), a coin (as a symbol of material wealth), being a Soulstone, and being Dedicated.<br /> <br /> But it is a single point of failure if stolen or lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-11-2026, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T11:01:03-07:00","id":1558797,"title":"","content":"If I am understanding correctly your Oneiros is a representation of your personal soul.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you lose you soul, do you lose the capability to have Astral Experiences? Do you lose the Oneiros? If you get someone else's soul as a replacement, what happens with your Oneiros?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-11-2026, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T12:36:41-07:00","id":1558799,"title":"","content":"A soulless mage cannot enter the Astral Realms. Presumably their Oneiros does not exist while soulless, or if it can somehow be accessed by other characters, would be a riven and treacherous place. What happens with the Oneiros of a mage whose soul has been replaced with another is a question for the Storyteller beyond simple answers for the simple questions thread. It's probably not entirely unlike the mage's old Oneiros. It's probably not exactly identical to it, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T12:41:09-07:00","id":1558800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558797#post1558797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am understanding correctly your Oneiros is a representation of your personal soul.<br /> <br /> If you lose you soul, do you lose the capability to have Astral Experiences? Do you lose the Oneiros? If you get someone else's soul as a replacement, what happens with your Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per &quot;Matters of the Soul&quot; (corebook, p98), soulless mages cannot attempt to contain Paradoxes or enter the Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T02:41:47-07:00","id":1558815,"title":"","content":"There is a pretty good argument that the Oneiros is not the same thing as the Soul. The Mummy perspective would place them both as parts of the Five-fold soul, so from what we know in Mage.<br /> <br /> 1) replacing a Mage's soul with a sleeper's soul doesn't stop them doing magic or change their personality.<br /> <br /> 2) removing the soul doesn't instantly remove their path/gnosis, so they are still connected to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> There remains a question about what would happen to anyone inside their Oneiros when the soul is removed.<br /> <br /> To me the most intuitive answer is that the Oneiros begins to shut down, its power source is gone, the driving force, but the personality doesn't change.<br /> <br /> Any native Goetia will stop gaining essence and slowly lose energy and eventually enter hibernation, unless a soul is restored - in a similar manner to the willpower/gnosis/wisdom draining away slowly.<br /> <br /> Any visitors to the Oneiros will be unharmed until it eventually collapses on itself, and they are either ejected, or soul-shocked as if their astral form had been destroyed (particularly in the case where the soul is removed and the character instantly gain the thrall condition, skipping the slow degredation - for example if the extra reach effects of Sever soul are used).<br /> <br /> The alternative is that the Oneiros just vanishes, but that doesn't seem as satisfying to roleplay.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  aau 03-12-2026, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T13:39:45-07:00","id":1558829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558815#post1558815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There remains a question about what would happen to anyone inside their Oneiros when the soul is removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other traumatic incidents involving being in an Oneiros when something goes wrong lead to the Soul Shocked Condition (which doesn't seem to actually require a soul). So it seems like a good start.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T05:31:22-07:00","id":1558832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558815#post1558815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a pretty good argument that the Oneiros is not the same thing as the Soul. The Mummy perspective would place them both as parts of the Five-fold soul, so from what we know in Mage.<br /> <br /> 1) replacing a Mage's soul with a sleeper's soul doesn't stop them doing magic or change their personality.<br /> <br /> 2) removing the soul doesn't instantly remove their path/gnosis, so they are still connected to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> There remains a question about what would happen to anyone inside their Oneiros when the soul is removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the ability to use magic is related to the subject of the Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T09:10:12-07:00","id":1558836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558832#post1558832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how the ability to use magic is related to the subject of the Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that mages tends to see their path as a connection through the Astral to the Supernal, Archmages forge their own Golden Road, which is sort of determined to be within their soul? <br /> <br /> So since doing magic involves drawing the supernal - down their path - across the Abyss and then coming from something akin to their soul. It begs the question whether that path is still open (if only temporarily, as the Enervated condition slowly reduced her gnosis aswell).<br /> <br /> The reason it is worth mentioning is that, we as players don't have a solid answer, so if you want to homebrew something for your table you might aswell take what clues you can from the metaphysics we do know about. <br /> <br /> Ultimately I think, &quot;do whatever is fun&quot; is a fine guideline for figuring out what to do. But to me it makes sense that just as willpower/gnosis and wisdom slowly degrade, so should the Oneiros. And since plugging in a new soul reversed those changes without affecting the actual personality, that should also be reflect in the Oneiros. <br /> <br /> And having Goetia which represent your Inner most drives slowly lose essence seems to be the most coherent mechanically (with the usual Ephemeral entities rules for running out of essence and going into hibernation being right there).<br /> <br /> The alternative is to model it after a Wending. But they tend to be a bit more elaborate than an Oneiros, and without much of a detailed set of rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T13:46:51-07:00","id":1558840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558836#post1558836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point is that mages tends to see their path as a connection through the Astral to the Supernal, Archmages forge their own Golden Road, which is sort of determined to be within their soul?<br /> <br /> So since doing magic involves drawing the supernal - down their path - across the Abyss and then coming from something akin to their soul. It begs the question whether that path is still open (if only temporarily, as the Enervated condition slowly reduced her gnosis aswell).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question it begs (as opposed to raising) is whether it's accurate to view magic in such literal or materialistic terms. I think such a thing overlooks other parts of the metaphysics, such as the notion of patterns, the capabilities mages gain by virtue of what they've become apart from spell casting, the nimbus and effects of Shadow Names, and indeed descriptions of the imago as a component of spell casting in the first place.<br /> <br /> Heck, even things like &quot;Awakening is impossible to foresee before it happens, but if you travel back in time to before one it becomes an almost certainty&quot;, and what they say for the wider metaphysics. Or stuff like Metamorphic Awakenings.<br /> <br /> I think the key component of Awakening is the establishment of a symbol of one's identity in the Supernal, whether that be a &quot;name&quot; on a Watchtower or the Cintamannus of an archmaster. I think once that is there, it becomes a fact of reality that one is Awakened, attuned with the Supernal in a manner that can realign primal forms to produce phenomenal results. A soul is a necessary component of that, whether it be because it takes a complete pattern to be so attuned, or its specific qualities are required to properly form and will imagos, or it's something like a lens to see through. But it is not, in and of itself, the sum total of one's Awakened being, such that its absence immediately prevents spellcasting, nor can its transfer carry Awakening, nor is it irreplaceable.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I think the soul <i>does</i> encompass the sum total of the Oneiros, such that the absence of it gives nothing to actually project into.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T13:59:56-07:00","id":1558841,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit to the number of Vices a character can have? I am thinking for a Prelate of the Hegemony benefits (extra vice, extra mana from fulling them)<br /> <br /> Normally you have 1, just by being a person; you can get another with the Vice-Ridden merit; another &quot;Selfish&quot; Vice with the <i>Megalomaniacal </i>condition; a Prelate of the Hegemony grants another, and from all 4 you can get Willpower and Mana.<br /> <br /> Is that analysis right?<br /> <br /> There are also Mummy Emanations (the Sacrifice) that add extra Vice. Would all stack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T14:09:39-07:00","id":1558842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558841#post1558841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would all stack?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no defined limit on having extra Vices from multiple sources, but the Vice-Ridden Merit is explicit about only providing additional options to satisfy rather than increasing the frequency with which you can gain Willpower and neither Mage nor Mummy's copy of the mechanics, nor the ChroD corebook's instance, say anything like &quot;for each Vice&quot; or &quot;per Vice.&quot; The extras broaden the definition of &quot;your Vice&quot; rather than staple an extra container for guilty fulfillment onto the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T01:08:32-07:00","id":1558847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558840#post1558840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the question it begs (as opposed to raising) is whether it's accurate to view magic in such literal or materialistic terms. I think such a thing overlooks other parts of the metaphysics, such as the notion of patterns, the capabilities mages gain by virtue of what they've become apart from spell casting, the nimbus and effects of Shadow Names, and indeed descriptions of the imago as a component of spell casting in the first place.<br /> <br /> Heck, even things like &quot;Awakening is impossible to foresee before it happens, but if you travel back in time to before one it becomes an almost certainty&quot;, and what they say for the wider metaphysics. Or stuff like Metamorphic Awakenings.<br /> <br /> I think the key component of Awakening is the establishment of a symbol of one's identity in the Supernal, whether that be a &quot;name&quot; on a Watchtower or the Cintamannus of an archmaster. I think once that is there, it becomes a fact of reality that one is Awakened, attuned with the Supernal in a manner that can realign primal forms to produce phenomenal results. A soul is a necessary component of that, whether it be because it takes a complete pattern to be so attuned, or its specific qualities are required to properly form and will imagos, or it's something like a lens to see through. But it is not, in and of itself, the sum total of one's Awakened being, such that its absence immediately prevents spellcasting, nor can its transfer carry Awakening, nor is it irreplaceable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking this through, the soul clearly has some affect, given that soulless character can no longer contain paradoxes, but if the formation of an imago requires some sort of force of will (imposing your will upon the world) that suggests this ability to care slowly degrades as the soulless conditions worsen and your gnosis drops...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, I think the soul <i>does</i> encompass the sum total of the Oneiros, such that the absence of it gives nothing to actually project into. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure there is anything to back this. Give what I said previously about losing their soul and replacing it with someone else's*not* changing their personality - and this the content of their Oneiros.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it is worth mentioning, but specific soul shaping (making/joining a legacy) is also pretty damned cool - you soul becomes a source of mana, and a source of supernatural (but not supernal) powers. <br /> <br /> And again, swapping souls doesn't change your legacy, even if you took the soul of someone from a different legacy (I think Tremere eating the souls of the last remanants of a Legacy and turning them into a House may be an exception to this, but they don't have souls in the normal sense...) So you are shaping something else with the 'soul' just acting as a fungible power source?<br /> <br /> Does it seems right that you can still use legacy attainments and Oblations while soulless? Afaik there is no specific rule here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T03:20:23-07:00","id":1558850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558847#post1558847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, swapping souls doesn't change your legacy, even if you took the soul of someone from a different legacy</div> </div> </div> </div>Although your soul does carry a lingering trace of your legacy, allowing another mage to join it using the soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you are shaping something else with the 'soul' just acting as a fungible power source? </div> </div> </div>That's correct. Page 197 of the 2e core restates it as the shaping of the mages <i>gnosis</i> as opposed to the soul itself. With the 1e language of 'soulcraft' etc. being recontextualised as mages speaking colloquially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T07:25:03-07:00","id":1558852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558847#post1558847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it seems right that you can still use legacy attainments and Oblations while soulless? Afaik there is no specific rule here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblations generating Mana is limited by mastery of the Legacy's Ruling Arcanum, and Mana capacity is limited by Gnosis, which goes down as an intermediate consequence of soul loss; in a strict sense there's nothing stopping Legacy Oblations from working while soulless.<br /> <br /> Legacy Attainments count as natural phenomena to such a significant degree that there are multiple published Legacies whose Attainments permanently alter their bodies, but also the direct implication of regaining access to your Legacy Attainments when your Gnosis has recovered is that you lose access to them if your Gnosis drops below the prerequisite level and not before those points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T17:22:36-07:00","id":1558859,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=orathaic;n1558847]<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there is anything to back this.[/uote]<br /> <br /> I back this up with the consistent language used to describe what the Oneiros is.<br /> <br /> [quote=orathaic]<br /> Give what I said previously about losing their soul and replacing it with someone else's*not* changing their personality - and this the content of their Oneiros.<br /> [/quote[<br /> <br /> I find this begs the question of why assume the soul is the basis of the personality.<br /> <br /> Why not the personality be the basis of the soul?<br /> <br /> Your Oneiros wouldn't change based on a different soul because the Oneiros is the soul personifying the traits of a person it resides within before the eyes of a projected traveller. The Oneiros itself does not create those traits, beyond some of the impacts based on the actions of conscious wills encroaching on it.<br /> <br /> But this is not Inside Out, and you do not have a bunch of Goetia running around within you causing your decisions and traits based on their actions and interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, swapping souls doesn't change your legacy, even if you took the soul of someone from a different legacy (I think Tremere eating the souls of the last remanants of a Legacy and turning them into a House may be an exception to this, but they don't have souls in the normal sense...) So you are shaping something else with the 'soul' just acting as a fungible power source?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's consistent with the language used to describe Legacies in this Edition. <br /> <br /> Indeed, I'm not certain what impact the whole &quot;soul shaping&quot; thing is supposed to have besides the fact that it makes Legacies visible in disembodied souls.<br /> <br /> As for the Tremere, I think some of the presence of Legacy in souls has some impact on it, but I suspect that's kind of minimal considering the far more onerous requirements of &quot;only other Reapers can be made into Houses&quot; and &quot;a House only forms when every last member of the Reaper Legacy has been consumed&quot;. I think the basis of that resides a lot more in anything powering their particular magical symbolism of consumption and that they do not share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T10:58:59-07:00","id":1558872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558859#post1558859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, I'm not certain what impact the whole &quot;soul shaping&quot; thing is supposed to have besides the fact that it makes Legacies visible in disembodied souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an apt comparison can be made most clearly with Deviants and Changelings (and maybe vampires). Afaik, Deviants souls become shattered (though they are so varied this may be a simplification) and Changelings becomes twisted in a way which also alters their souls.<br /> <br /> In both cases, the resulting out come is a former human with powers.<br /> <br /> Mages forming legacies alter their souls with a lot more subtelty and gain powers. it is rarely conaidered damage. I suppose this depends on perspective.<br /> <br /> Like if the alteration to the person (to make them a changeling/Deviant) *only* has altering their soul as a side effect of a process then maybe they could gain powers without such damage to the soul. But for Mages is seems clear that altering the shape gives them their supernatural legacy abilities.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could really push things and have a mage alter their legacy, but that would twist the soul so much if would create a Deviant. Or maybe some worse outcome, like twisting it into a contradiction which is somehow Abyssal in nature... <br /> <br /> But afaik, legacy formation is the only form of soul shaping which doesn't break the soul, so it being limited in his car you can push things is interesting... While this comparison may be more appropriate to Deviants (though they are rather varied) and perhaps Changelings just have their soul alterations as a side effect of their durancs... I think the general &quot;human souls do this&quot; but what if we tore them to shreds and put them back together... &quot;Now they do something different&quot; seems like a general principle which works across lines to me (not sure this really applies to Vampire, Promethean might provide a different insight/perspective... )<br /> <br /> Can you do some kind of soul shaping in a sleeper and make them something else? Form a line of proximi perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T14:16:08-07:00","id":1558877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558872#post1558872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an apt comparison can be made most clearly with Deviants and Changelings (and maybe vampires). Afaik, Deviants souls become shattered (though they are so varied this may be a simplification) and Changelings becomes twisted in a way which also alters their souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shallow Graves describes breaking points as damaging and puncturing the metaphysical container for the human soul (putting holes in it that provide ways in for possessing entities and reduces the &quot;pressure&quot; that a soul can muster to drive out such beings through abjuration) in its subsection on Integrity in the larger section on souls in general; deviants lack the part of their spiritual anatomy that would correspond to a soul-container with Integrity in a way that likens trying to steal a transformed soul with grabbing a live wire. All deviants have at least a passable substitute for a soul, whose volatility is the reason they have a Stability track.<br /> <br /> Changelings lose bits of their souls in the transition into and out of Arcadian servitude (crossing through a realm that exists on the boundary between conscious and unconscious experience) in a way that takes some of their memories with it in solidified metaphors and leaves them prone to evoking sudden bursts of emotion in those who perceive them, stitching those missing pieces back into their souls by taking them out of the Hedge. The Lost liches known as the Empty do not remove their souls \u2014 quite the opposite \u2014 but instead remove their hearts for safekeeping as part of their immortality, and Contracts (and the Wyrd more generally) work on sympathetic principles that heavily involve names and identity and reciprocity.<br /> <br /> Mages develop Legacies by altering their Gnosis and magical identity, which in turn shapes the soul attached to it. Their Awakening already causes them to attract consistent magical phenomena to them and the things related to them (even if constrained to &quot;just&quot; things connected to their Shadow Name), and their magical identity affects the development of their Nimbus. Legacy Attainments are strictly metered in what they are capable of as non-Supernal manifestations of Supernal study. &quot;This character tried to get more Legacy Attainments and it went sideways&quot; is a category of Rapture because messing with the soul is tricky business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you do some kind of soul shaping in a sleeper and make them something else? Form a line of proximi perhaps? </div> </div> </div>Depending on the specific instances, this could be the source of some Supernatural Merits, but broadly speaking Integrity is not quite as durable as Gnosis in this fashion \u2014 any given Sleeper of the right mindset might experience a lucky breaking point, fail the Watchtower's trials, and come out of the experience as a Sleepwalker, and some Proximus lineages are almost certainly the result of spontaneous phenomena rather than deliberate action by archmasters or Supernal beings, but things beyond the scope of the published material on the Subtle Arcana are deep lore about the soul that would be developed specifically for a given table's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T03:19:20-07:00","id":1558882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558877#post1558877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shallow Graves describes breaking points as damaging and puncturing the metaphysical container for the human soul (putting holes in it that provide ways in for possessing entities and reduces the &quot;pressure&quot; that a soul can muster to drive out such beings through abjuration) in its subsection on Integrity in the larger section on souls in general; deviants lack the part of their spiritual anatomy that would correspond to a soul-container with Integrity in a way that likens trying to steal a transformed soul with grabbing a live wire. All deviants have at least a passable substitute for a soul, whose volatility is the reason they have a Stability track.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings lose bits of their souls in the transition into and out of Arcadian servitude (crossing through a realm that exists on the boundary between conscious and unconscious experience) in a way that takes some of their memories with it in solidified metaphors and leaves them prone to evoking sudden bursts of emotion in those who perceive them, stitching those missing pieces back into their souls by taking them out of the Hedge. The Lost liches known as the Empty do not remove their souls \u2014 quite the opposite \u2014 but instead remove their hearts for safekeeping as part of their immortality, and Contracts (and the Wyrd more generally) work on sympathetic principles that heavily involve names and identity and reciprocity. </div> </div> </div>Does Sympathy and name not fit into the Mummy/Egyptian concept of the Five-fold soul? (Ren?). Like that Changeling has a different part of their five fold soul messed with - and not necessarily the part that Mages call a soul...<br /> <br /> Which I think could work, though I've often associated Ren with ghosts, how memory and identity is fundamental to ghosts and the Underworld (and giving up your identity/losing anchors/entering the Ocean of Fragments as the ultimate end goal for ghosts to pass on)... Messing with Den/identity while still alive could be a fine place to leave Changelings... But maybe Sympathy is a different thing (to Mages Mind/Space is the sublte/gross Arcanum pairing which links sympathy and memories... But I don't know that that necessarily corresponds neatly with Ren as presented in Mummy). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages develop Legacies by altering their Gnosis and magical identity, which in turn shapes the soul attached to it. Their Awakening already causes them to attract consistent magical phenomena to them and the things related to them (even if constrained to &quot;just&quot; things connected to their Shadow Name), and their magical identity affects the development of their Nimbus. Legacy Attainments are strictly metered in what they are capable of as non-Supernal manifestations of Supernal study. &quot;This character tried to get more Legacy Attainments and it went sideways&quot; is a category of Rapture because messing with the soul is tricky business. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Rapture for mages, or if you try too hard on a sleeper, Deviantation (or maybe something unique, but I think Deviant is flexible enough to model most optio s...) basically you break a person by messing too much with their soul - and crafting a soul is really messy and dangerous cf: Promethean/Alchemicy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on the specific instances, this could be the source of some Supernatural Merits, but broadly speaking Integrity is not quite as durable as Gnosis in this fashion \u2014 any given Sleeper of the right mindset might experience a lucky breaking point, fail the Watchtower's trials, and come out of the experience as a Sleepwalker, and some Proximus lineages are almost certainly the result of spontaneous phenomena rather than deliberate action by archmasters or Supernal beings, but things beyond the scope of the published material on the Subtle Arcana are deep lore about the soul that would be developed specifically for a given table's game. </div> </div> </div>Soul explorers, that's going to be my next game i think...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T06:08:50-07:00","id":1558886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558882#post1558882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Sympathy and name not fit into the Mummy/Egyptian concept of the Five-fold soul? (Ren?). Like that Changeling has a different part of their five fold soul messed with - and not necessarily the part that Mages call a soul...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The part that mages call a soul&quot; <i>is</i> the fivefold soul \u2014 the Weret-Hekau got a not-insignificant amount of research out of being the Great Cult of the lands near where Irem never-was, and the Tremere's postulated Sixth Watchtower exists to fill the gap between &quot;the soul is made of all five Subtle Arcana&quot; and &quot;the five Subtle Arcana alone are not sufficient to create a brand new soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which I think could work, though I've often associated Ren with ghosts, how memory and identity is fundamental to ghosts and the Underworld (and giving up your identity/losing anchors/entering the Ocean of Fragments as the ultimate end goal for ghosts to pass on)... Messing with Den/identity while still alive could be a fine place to leave Changelings... But maybe Sympathy is a different thing (to Mages Mind/Space is the sublte/gross Arcanum pairing which links sympathy and memories... But I don't know that that necessarily corresponds neatly with Ren as presented in Mummy). </div> </div> </div>While Space is the Arcanum mages use for messing with sympathy, one of the standard Fate Unveiling spells reveals sympathetic connections between its targets. Changelings use powers derived from other beings via mimicry of those other beings by virtue of the Wyrd being a force of reciprocity, which is part of the same bit of metaphysics that makes oaths and other magically enforced agreements the purview of Fate. The Lost have the ability to alter themselves through Contracts and pledgecraft because the Gentry defined them as party to their agreements as servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T07:08:49-07:00","id":1558889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558886#post1558886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The part that mages call a soul&quot; <i>is</i> the fivefold soul \u2014 the Weret-Hekau got a not-insignificant amount of research out of being the Great Cult of the lands near where Irem never-was, and the Tremere's postulated Sixth Watchtower exists to fill the gap between &quot;the soul is made of all five Subtle Arcana&quot; and &quot;the five Subtle Arcana alone are not sufficient to create a brand new soul.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I was tending towards a metaphysics where the soul is more, like Fate has Destiny which is part of a person and linked to them in some way, but not something Mages 'call' the soul.<br /> <br /> But I would have assumed it is part of the person which corresponds to part of the Five-fold soul... (Which brings us back to the Oneiros being the part associated with Mind, and the power source maybe fitting more with Prime, but being associated with Death via endings and ghosts...) All of which is made more messy if you assume the ghost is a part of that soul... And not having anything to associate with Spirit (or arguable Prime... )<br /> <br /> The link between Ghosts and Ren (name/identity) seems the most obvious, with the remembering of a ghost (or the person they were) giving them essence, with the soul passing on but the identity left behind... And Mages explicitly saying ghosts aren't souls.<br /> <br /> But maybe they don't need to be. Like most non-humans have spirits, but souls create an impression on the fabric of the world which leaves behind an echo... Maybe ghosts (along with castoffs, dopplegangers, and barghest) are entirely seperate effects of the soul - though the reincarnation and passing on seems less important if you take that view.<br /> <br /> And Shades add a whole other level of complexity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Space is the Arcanum mages use for messing with sympathy, one of the standard Fate Unveiling spells reveals sympathetic connections between its targets. Changelings use powers derived from other beings via mimicry of those other beings by virtue of the Wyrd being a force of reciprocity, which is part of the same bit of metaphysics that makes oaths and other magically enforced agreements the purview of Fate. The Lost have the ability to alter themselves through Contracts and pledgecraft because the Gentry defined them as party to their agreements as servants. </div> </div> </div>Mimicry of other beings? I had not heard that.<br /> <br /> Do you mean like an Elemental used by their keeper as a torch to light the ballroom is mimicing a really torch, and thus powers derived from this are like borrowing from the kind of thing a real torch could do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added responce. 03-16-2026, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T12:06:47-07:00","id":1558898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558889#post1558889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I was tending towards a metaphysics where the soul is more, like Fate has Destiny which is part of a person and linked to them in some way, but not something Mages 'call' the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Subtle Arcana correspond to the Pillars \u2014 particular interactions mean the Venn diagram between the two is not a perfect circle, but a character's Ren is part of their Fate Pattern, just as their Ka is part of their Prime Pattern and their Ba is part of their Mind Pattern. There's a reason Sheut-based Affinities and Utterance tiers have so much truck with ghosts, after all.<br /> <br /> There's more to the soul than the Pillars \u2014 Sekhem binds them together in addition to being the thing they're derived from, and direct comparisons to either model result in seeming inconsistencies when taken as gospel, like the Life Arcanum being derived from the Pillar of the Heart despite the Essence being the thing that differentiates a living body from a dead one \u2014 but the general principles hold fairly firm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mimicry of other beings? I had not heard that.<br /> <br /> Do you mean like an Elemental used by their keeper as a torch to light the ballroom is mimicing a really torch, and thus powers derived from this are like borrowing from the kind of thing a real torch could do? </div> </div> </div>I mean that the form of sympathetic magic changelings call dramaturgy is most commonly encountered in the form of Contract Loopholes, which effectively bypass the need for Glamour by masquerading as the patron whose identity the ability is derived from through props and actions \u2014 see the relevant section of Kith and Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T02:19:42-07:00","id":1558907,"title":"","content":"The spell Shared sight (in Signs of sorcery) gives an extra Arcana sight, but could the subject use it for focused mage sight?<br /> if yes how many dots are given?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T02:42:38-07:00","id":1558908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558907#post1558907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell Shared sight (in Signs of sorcery) gives an extra Arcana sight, but could the subject use it for focused mage sight?<br /> if yes how many dots are given?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question. So shared sight is like the reach option for Apocalypse, but allows you grant someone else your Mage sight.<br /> <br /> It think it should just work like Apocalypse, which mentions that Awakened subjects can push the Mage sight into the perihpery. It does not mention being able to use focused mage sight, but since focused mage sight just requires focusing, I would assume yes. You can (if we're talking about an Awakened subject, or indeed a sleeper/sleeper Walker who has done this enough times that they bought a homebrew merit to let them control Mage sight) simply focus.<br /> <br /> Which leads to your second question. And honestly, I think the number of dots that the caster has makes most sense.<br /> <br /> They pay mana for the privilege...<br /> <br /> The bigger question is, are you actually using the scrutiny/Revelation rules, as opposed to just not ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T07:34:26-07:00","id":1558911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558872#post1558872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like if the alteration to the person (to make them a changeling/Deviant) *only* has altering their soul as a side effect of a process then maybe they could gain powers without such damage to the soul. But for Mages is seems clear that altering the shape gives them their supernatural legacy abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say again; with the corebook having given the explicit, unambiguous statement that Legacy formation consists of reshaping Gnosis, the only effect of substance upon the soul is the fact that the Legacy becomes visible within it when detached.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you do some kind of soul shaping in a sleeper and make them something else? Form a line of proximi perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave Brookshaw has said that, if Deviant was a game that existed or was conceived of at the time, they're basically what the Servitor races of the Seers of the Throne would be.<br /> <br /> Like, they need a bit of help in most cases to warp the souls, and something that standardises the results, but the essential principle is the same.<br /> <br /> The warping of the Myrmidons probably isn't what makes them Proximi, but what makes them slaves to a language bestowed by the General.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T07:33:44-07:00","id":1558922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558908#post1558908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting question. So shared sight is like the reach option for Apocalypse, but allows you grant someone else your Mage sight.<br /> <br /> It think it should just work like Apocalypse, which mentions that Awakened subjects can push the Mage sight into the perihpery. It does not mention being able to use focused mage sight, but since focused mage sight just requires focusing, I would assume yes. You can (if we're talking about an Awakened subject, or indeed a sleeper/sleeper Walker who has done this enough times that they bought a homebrew merit to let them control Mage sight) simply focus.<br /> <br /> Which leads to your second question. And honestly, I think the number of dots that the caster has makes most sense.<br /> <br /> They pay mana for the privilege...<br /> <br /> The bigger question is, are you actually using the scrutiny/Revelation rules, as opposed to just not ...</div> </div> </div> </div>About the second question, i tnink that the possible answers are:<br /> -zero dots (you use only gnosis on rolls)<br /> -one dot<br /> -your answer (but i m worried about game balance)<br /> <br /> About the bigger question... yes, after two chronicles i think it s a good way to give the &quot;you are a supernatural detective&quot; vibes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T08:06:23-07:00","id":1558923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558922#post1558922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the second question, i tnink that the possible answers are:<br /> -zero dots (you use only gnosis on rolls)<br /> -one dot<br /> -your answer (but i m worried about game balance)<br /> <br /> About the bigger question... yes, after two chronicles i think it s a good way to give the &quot;you are a supernatural detective&quot; vibes</div> </div> </div> </div>For game balance, I'm not sure. Again, I know many people who dislike the mechanics of that system entirely (too much repitative dice rolling) so there is no argument to be made to remove it and focus instead on building mysteries with Locked opacity/Linked Opacity, clues as mysteries/mysteries as clues... To remove it from the dicce rolling, and have the built in mana cost as the game balance for a more narrative system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T12:16:58-07:00","id":1558926,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to assume from the lack of any guidance on Revelation or Scrutiny and the inherent necessity of dice rolls for those two that Shared Sight and Apocalypse only allow you to treat your Active Sight as though it contained the added Arcana; I would use the spell's Clash pool for any attempts to overcome relevant concealment but not otherwise allow a spell whose function is to share awareness of facets of the Supernal World to grant wholesale insight into the Mysteries of a given Arcanum \u2014 a mage subject might use the Permutation described in the corebook to supplement the roll with their own Arcana at risk of faster contamination, but four dots in Prime (much less one) isn't enough to let the uninitiated probe deeply enough into the Supernal to allow things to poke back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558923#post1558923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For game balance, I'm not sure. Again, I know many people who dislike the mechanics of that system entirely (too much repitative dice rolling) so there is no argument to be made to remove it and focus instead on building mysteries with Locked opacity/Linked Opacity, clues as mysteries/mysteries as clues... To remove it from the dicce rolling, and have the built in mana cost as the game balance for a more narrative system.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've repeatedly made your opinion on the Focused Mage Sight systems clear and all, but this is increasingly irrelevant to the function of this thread. Speaking of which\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> Do/Can Shared Sight and Apocalypse with the appropriate Arcana carry over applicable Attainments or Merits like Eyes of the Dead or Mana Sensitivity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T14:46:29-07:00","id":1558927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558922#post1558922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the second question, i tnink that the possible answers are:<br /> -zero dots (you use only gnosis on rolls)<br /> -one dot<br /> -your answer (but i m worried about game balance)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd use Gnosis - 3 for being untrained in the arcana, following the untrained penalty for spell teamwork.<br /> <br /> For non-mages, they're rolling a chance die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do/Can Shared Sight and Apocalypse with the appropriate Arcana carry over applicable Attainments or Merits like Eyes of the Dead or Mana Sensitivity? </div> </div> </div>Given that Shared Sight refers to Prime mage Sight (or the other active Sights) specifically, I doubt Mana Sensitivity would do anything. Though I'm not sure what to make of Prime Sight not including mana in it's purview.<br /> <br /> I'd probably allow the active sight altering attainments to work. I don't see anything indicating either way, so I'd tend to go for the more interesting option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T04:20:56-07:00","id":1558936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558927#post1558927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'd use Gnosis - 3 for being untrained in the arcana, following the untrained penalty for spell teamwork.<br /> <br /> For non-mages, they're rolling a chance die.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be reasonable, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> noted the mage could simply use the Permutation rule to gain a roll far higher with a little sacrifice so i will probably use this solution, it keeps the whole thing more simple.<br /> <br /> About non mages... Apocalypse description specify that they are locked in active mage sight, so i m inclined to think that they cannot use the focused one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T07:41:29-07:00","id":1558939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558927#post1558927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'd use Gnosis - 3 for being untrained in the arcana, following the untrained penalty for spell teamwork.<br /> <br /> For non-mages, they're rolling a chance die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that non-mages are explicitly not able to push their Mage sight into the perihpery, I would assume they also can't use Focused Mage sight at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T14:11:33-07:00","id":1558943,"title":"","content":"I agree with orathaic on non-Awakened recipients receiving the Mage Sight in a similar form to the Apocalypse spell: locked into Active Mage Sight, no focus or periphery.<br /> <br /> My default, I think, is that Awakened subjects of Shared Sight would be able to use Focused Sight with their own Arcanum rating, with no untrained penalty, by default. Perhaps a Reach effect and/or a Perfecting variant of the spell could lend an Awakened subject use of the caster's Arcanum ratings for the purposes of Focused Mage Sight, up to a maximum of the spell's Potency (or 5. Lending archmastery ain't that simple).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-19-2026, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T15:12:27-07:00","id":1558944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558936#post1558936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About non mages... Apocalypse description specify that they are locked in active mage sight, so i m inclined to think that they cannot use the focused one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's right. I was confusing Apocalypse with Stealing Fire and didn't check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T07:52:55-07:00","id":1558959,"title":"","content":"If a mage transform a human in a cat and then shows it to a sleeper what are the necessary conditions to trigger Dissonance?<br /> Telling him and being believed is enough?<br /> Showing a recorded video of what happened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T12:38:55-07:00","id":1558962,"title":"","content":"Obvious magic being witnessed. It would vary from person to person. Since a baby might not realise that isn't how the world work... While a scientist might be very skeptical of even the most subtle change. A skeptic used to debunking might decide that the video was clearly a fraud (and thus not magic)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T13:10:14-07:00","id":1558963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558959#post1558959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage transform a human in a cat and then shows it to a sleeper what are the necessary conditions to trigger Dissonance?<br /> Telling him and being believed is enough?<br /> Showing a recorded video of what happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the cat behaving in a way that is distinctly uncat-like? Like, you find the cat has scratched the words, &quot;help me, a wizard turned me into a cat!&quot; into the floor.<br /> <br /> Simply believing that magic's been done isn't enough. Mages are frequently surrounded by sleepers who believe them that they can do magic. <i>The Sundered World</i> Dark Era has mages as the central figures of an entire culture. It doesn't really help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T14:13:36-07:00","id":1558964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558959#post1558959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage transform a human in a cat and then shows it to a sleeper what are the necessary conditions to trigger Dissonance?<br /> Telling him and being believed is enough?<br /> Showing a recorded video of what happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Obvious magic&quot; sidebar on Page 298 of the corebook is pretty plain about the threshold \u2014 &quot;clearly, openly supernatural&quot; and &quot;conscious and cognizant of the magic's impossibility&quot; is going to take some doing for any sort of recording that the Sleeper doesn't have any reason to believe has been altered unless they're extremely credulous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T07:24:01-07:00","id":1558973,"title":"","content":"When i use yantras for a total of +8 is the limit of +5 only twoards the end? So if i give the spell +2 potency reducing the dice i get by 4 do i get +5 from the yantras or +8?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T09:01:27-07:00","id":1558975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558973#post1558973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When i use yantras for a total of +8 is the limit of +5 only twoards the end? So if i give the spell +2 potency reducing the dice i get by 4 do i get +5 from the yantras or +8?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. look at the quick reference, pg 357, step 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maximum bonus is +5 after offsetting spell factor penaltiea </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T02:45:18-07:00","id":1558980,"title":"","content":"A question about potency.<br /> Lets say i want someone to combust in fire. I get a total of 6 potency. The targets resist trait is 5. Does the flame hit with the power of potency 6 or 1?<br /> <br /> Bonus question it says in VTR that frenzy ads blood potency to resistance traits. Does that mean that a frenzied vampire with 5 blood potency is that much harder to affect by magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-24-2026, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T02:58:47-07:00","id":1558981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558980#post1558980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about potency.<br /> Lets say i want someone to combust in fire. I get a total of 6 potency. The targets resist trait is 5. Does the flame hit with the power of potency 6 or 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell is withstood then it would be potency 1.<br /> <br /> For direct damage, spells are not usually withstood (stamina is taken into account via health levels which need to be overcome in lieu of a withstand). <br /> <br /> If you are trying to transform them into fire, or turn the energy of their kinetic energy into heat, then that spell may be withstood. Whereas, if you are taking a candle and pushing it to be a fireball (with 6 potency) the subject of the spell is not the target you are hoping to damage, so it is again not withstood by their resist trait...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T03:27:26-07:00","id":1558982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558980#post1558980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about potency.Bonus question it says in VTR that frenzy ads blood potency to resistance traits. Does that mean that a frenzied vampire with 5 blood potency is that much harder to affect by magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's meant to be rolls or resistances using Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina rather than all resistances.<br /> <br /> In any case, the answer is probably no. Frenzy doesn't add points to your attributes, it adds them to rolls or resistances made with those attributes. Withstand isn't either of those.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a potentially interesting idea. A frenzied vampire probably should be hard to control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T03:31:55-07:00","id":1558983,"title":"","content":"How about i use fate to inflict a poisined condition on the target. Does potency affect its toxicity? or is it more of &quot;anything thats actually probable so ST decides&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T03:35:33-07:00","id":1558984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558982#post1558982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's meant to be rolls or resistances using Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina rather than all resistances.<br /> <br /> In any case, the answer is probably no. Frenzy doesn't add points to your attributes, it adds them to rolls or resistances made with those attributes. Withstand isn't either of those.<br /> <br /> That said, it's a potentially interesting idea. A frenzied vampire probably should be hard to control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im refering to this<br /> <img title=\"obraz.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_2085_1774348518090_847\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"obraz.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T05:00:07-07:00","id":1558986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558983#post1558983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about i use fate to inflict a poisined condition on the target. Does potency affect its toxicity? or is it more of &quot;anything thats actually probable so ST decides&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poison is not directly in the purview of Fate, so Potency is *probably* affecting how many times the subject gets unlucky, or how unlikely they are to be poisoned by this particular rare thing... (More potency meaning you can reach more unlikely things happening...) Which would then indirectly affect the toxicity, I guess.<br /> <br /> It is comparable to using a fire which is already burning to harm someone. You use the normal fire rules for damage rather than the direct damage for spells. So a poison's toxicity would depend on the poison in question and standard rules for such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T05:06:01-07:00","id":1558987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558984#post1558984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im refering to this<br /> <img title=\"obraz.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_2085_1774348518090_847\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2085&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"obraz.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Frenzy would not add, but Resilience does","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T17:08:06-07:00","id":1559002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1558986#post1558986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Poison is not directly in the purview of Fate, so Potency is *probably* affecting how many times the subject gets unlucky, or how unlikely they are to be poisoned by this particular rare thing... (More potency meaning you can reach more unlikely things happening...) Which would then indirectly affect the toxicity, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Poisoned Tilt is one of several effects suggested on page 134 to model the effects of hexes such as those from the Exceptional Luck spell, with one Tilt applying per point of Potency.<br /> <br /> I would assume the Poisoned Tilt to apply at moderate severity, and am honestly not sure off the top of my head whether I would allow a second point of Potency to be spent on upgrading it to grave toxicity, or just keep hexes stuck at moderate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T13:50:22-07:00","id":1559018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559002#post1559002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Poisoned Tilt is one of several effects suggested on page 134 to model the effects of hexes such as those from the Exceptional Luck spell, with one Tilt applying per point of Potency.<br /> <br /> I would assume the Poisoned Tilt to apply at moderate severity, and am honestly not sure off the top of my head whether I would allow a second point of Potency to be spent on upgrading it to grave toxicity, or just keep hexes stuck at moderate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that two points of Potency would not be <i>too</i> cheap to impose an effect that can apply 1 lethal per turn to somebody who has failed a Stamina roll.<br /> <br /> As for the question, I'm inclined to think that Toxicity doesn't enter into it. That the target has not been literally poisoned, just that they can experience a hex in the form that emulates the effect within the boundaries of a fight. Just for the idea that hexes in the form of Tilts might be for the sake of depicting bad luck that specifically undermines and inhabits in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-26T01:20:23-07:00","id":1559027,"title":"","content":"Is the Exorcist eye spell (+reach) enough to talk to a spirit across the gauntlet?<br /> The reach mention only perceptions but i can t fcad any other ways to do it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-27T21:10:34-07:00","id":1559048,"title":"","content":"Im confused about the combat of mage in relation to the Adamantine Arrow. <br /> <br /> With how people describe mages in combat, why would they have an order so focused on being fit even mundanely and utilizing spells that may give one claws or increased musculature for combat? Why would the adamantine arrow exist if any mage could just stop a threat my crushing it with Space or turning it into a cockroach and stepping on it? Nameless and accursed has advice abkut this, so it seems to be a real problem in games. <br /> <br /> Im not complaining about combat, only confused on how the martial Arrow could exist when combat seems so trivial/who throws a spell first. And i dont see a point of buffing yourself via spells in combat when you could just make someone drown or choke to death with a spell. Is it just a case of people exaggerating how easy it would be to form these imagos mid combat? Like yeah you could kill everyone instantly with a co-location spell, but that would take too much time to form an imagos before the dude who made his hands into claws slashes your neck open","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T05:08:27-07:00","id":1559053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559048#post1559048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im confused about the combat of mage in relation to the Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> With how people describe mages in combat, why would they have an order so focused on being fit even mundanely and utilizing spells that may give one claws or increased musculature for combat? Why would the adamantine arrow exist if any mage could just stop a threat my crushing it with Space or turning it into a cockroach and stepping on it? Nameless and accursed has advice abkut this, so it seems to be a real problem in games.<br /> <br /> Im not complaining about combat, only confused on how the martial Arrow could exist when combat seems so trivial/who throws a spell first. And i dont see a point of buffing yourself via spells in combat when you could just make someone drown or choke to death with a spell. Is it just a case of people exaggerating how easy it would be to form these imagos mid combat? Like yeah you could kill everyone instantly with a co-location spell, but that would take too much time to form an imagos before the dude who made his hands into claws slashes your neck open</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I will say, which may not be reflected in how people talk about Mage, is that a single Mage can be killed by an unsuspecting bullet to the head.<br /> <br /> So actually being trained for mundane combat and knowing what to do (in terms of basic first aid, situational awareness, and tactical things) is always useful. Mages tend to have a blind spot for doing thing with magic which they could do mundanely - which is often also the Wiser option (and I think that should be used as a weakness for various NPC antagonists). And in particular, when you attack a mage, the very worst time to pick is when they are out in public - in these cases mundane responces can be idealer...<br /> <br /> There are entities which have very high withstands where attacking them with an Unmaking spell (for example) may be next to impossible, and slowly wearing down their health levels may be necessary. Higher rank ephemeral entities for example (including Abyssal entities) and I think they would fall under the Arrow purview to deal with... In longer term conflicts, you have to consider resources. In a single fight you might spend 1 mana per Spell (to deal aggravated damage) or cast one spell to give yourself the ability to deal aggravated damage by hand (maybe making your weapons the entities bane with Prime). Then you can save a considerable amount of mana by being able to hit things real good.<br /> <br /> Not sure this is a complete answer, as it really doesn't imagine the Arrow complexly, it doesn't delve into their history of philosophy (nor at the darker mirror that is the Seer Ministry of the Praetorians).<br /> <br /> But it does touch on three things which combat conversations often ignore, is Wisdom, Withstand, and Mana costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T07:10:57-07:00","id":1559056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559048#post1559048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im confused about the combat of mage in relation to the Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> With how people describe mages in combat, why would they have an order so focused on being fit even mundanely and utilizing spells that may give one claws or increased musculature for combat? Why would the adamantine arrow exist if any mage could just stop a threat my crushing it with Space or turning it into a cockroach and stepping on it? Nameless and accursed has advice abkut this, so it seems to be a real problem in games.<br /> <br /> Im not complaining about combat, only confused on how the martial Arrow could exist when combat seems so trivial/who throws a spell first. And i dont see a point of buffing yourself via spells in combat when you could just make someone drown or choke to death with a spell. Is it just a case of people exaggerating how easy it would be to form these imagos mid combat? Like yeah you could kill everyone instantly with a co-location spell, but that would take too much time to form an imagos before the dude who made his hands into claws slashes your neck open</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that Arrows starts fights with other mages frequently, even in public.<br /> A bullet cannot be counterspelled and don t cause paradox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T07:25:55-07:00","id":1559057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559048#post1559048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And i dont see a point of buffing yourself via spells in combat when you could just make someone drown or choke to death with a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you think that's their primary strategy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T07:54:47-07:00","id":1559058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559048#post1559048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the adamantine arrow exist if any mage could just stop a threat my crushing it with Space or turning it into a cockroach and stepping on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two reasons I see.<br /> <br /> One is that mages have an actual cultural and philosophical background that gives them deeper perspectives on the use of magic and cultivation of their own characters than just blunt pragmatism. For the Adamantine Arrow in particular, they emphasize the development of additional skills because of the precept that values adaptability; their perspective of a warrior mage does not suit for one's offensive capabilities to be shut down by a Shielding of Prime or being in a scenario where using magic would be imprudent or anything.<br /> <br /> The other is that, no, any mage cannot do those things. Those things require a person to have four dots in respective Arcana, and possibly other complications aside (such as being Withstood or what they mean for Paradox and Dissonance). What is your newly Awakened Arrow supposed to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T07:54:55-07:00","id":1559059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559057#post1559057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you think that's their primary strategy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think thats their primary strategy. Im saying it IS something they do (and other mages, whether from an order or not). I just struggle to see the point in utilizing spells that focus on self enhancement or have a philosophy of combat like that.<br /> <br /> I understand tyat Arrows are NOT going to charge in for direct combat. They are mages. They arent foolish. They, like any military force, make strategies for any opponent they face. What i struggle with is how ANY conflict they deal with isnt done via subtle magic. Why use Matter to enhance your armor, or mind to multitask tactics, when you could just use mind to make someone kill themselves?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> that makes sense, but what about in regards to seers ane banishers? I apologize, i should have been more specific that this area is where i struggle with most in terms of not understansing why not just focusing on magic to neutralize the threat in subtle or brutal (by magic) ways. Wouldnt the best strategy always be &quot;isolate them from sleepers&quot; and then go crazy with reach?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24346_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24346\" data-vbnamecard=\"24346\">Neos01</a> lol that is true. but arent they odten trying not to do so in public?<br /> <br /> for the record, im reading the Adamantine arrow book right now (and all other supplements for mage) becuase its the series i most struggle with due to my impressions of how it is discussed and my own misunderstandings<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> wouldnt that make maxxing out your magic be most important to the poijt its better not to train your other qualities (to a degree?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-28-2026, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T09:05:49-07:00","id":1559061,"title":"","content":"To some limited degree, arcane XP can only be used for certain arcane skills, and you have other XP to spend on mundane skills, but it does not really encourage both ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T10:51:42-07:00","id":1559064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559048#post1559048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not complaining about combat, only confused on how the martial Arrow could exist when combat seems so trivial/who throws a spell first.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arrow's magical praxis is &quot;Challenge is Magical&quot; and the full breadth of possibility is not the actual scope of most conflict \u2014 see also Werewolf, where Acrozatarim <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful?p=464503#post464503\">shared a playtest example</a> of a pack of werewolves ganging up and killing their Pure opposition's Gauru specialist and getting their Irraka killed in turn in what was ultimately intended as a much lower-stakes conflict. The Duel Arcane exists as a practice because chucking lethal spells at your opposition to make a point is a good way to escalate a conflict beyond repair. You fight in a way that isn't guaranteed to annihilate the other guy so that they match that energy or are at least open to negotiations (or underestimating you enough to mess around).<br /> <br /> Also, more to the point, there is a clear and obvious reason why wizards whose magic can go sideways or damage their ability to manage consequences would want to have well-honed options at their disposal that do not go away the minute countermeasures against specific or general forms of magic come into play.<br /> <br /> Assuming most mages in the world are running on the typical Supernatural Tolerance range of 3-5 and approaching spellcasting with an eye toward the pressures of safe Reach, Mana costs, Arcana limits, and Wisdom (plus the need to actively develop or learn Rotes, Praxes, Merits, etc), and spreading their dots around at least a little bit to have more options available to them, unless they are actively specializing their magical persona toward being able to murder people they are going to be rather limited in the harm they can do without personal cost or consequence, especially in conflicts that they did not prepare for. Most mages cannot become more than an Adept in their non-Ruling Arcana without being tutored by a Master in those Arcana and need to spend regular Experiences in greater quantities and without the crutch of Arcane Experiences; without Rotes they are therefore limited in the free Reach available to them, which makes casting safely more difficult.<br /> <br /> Turning people into lizards is bad for your Wisdom unless you're already very unWise, and the same goes for killing them on short notice. Inuring spells for murder is an opportunity cost that also requires you to lose Wisdom casting that spell in the first place. Rotes don't exist in a vacuum and developing Praxes from non-Ruling Arcana still requires you to put resources toward raising those ratings that could be spent on other things. Without a good argument to make about why you did it, other mages are likely to have opinions on your character actually putting into practice theoretically heinous applications of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> The advice in Nameless and Accursed exists because the full breadth of reality-warping cosmic power nominally enables conflicts to be trivialized and it is therefore important to ground those possibilities in the world they would be dropped into. The Arrow engages in conflicts whose scope can extend below that of torture, murder, and dehumanization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T11:12:42-07:00","id":1559066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559059#post1559059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> wouldnt that make maxxing out your magic be most important to the poijt its better not to train your other qualities (to a degree?)</div> </div> </div> </div>How are you going to max out magic if you never pursue Obsessions related to a mystical philosophy of pursuing challenges, self-imposed or otherwise, and developing adaptable capabilities?<br /> <br /> See also the tenet of &quot;the Supernal is the Self&quot;, where in the individual is regarded as a microcosm of the universe, such that effective understanding of the cosmos requires personal self-development.<br /> <br /> Like, keep in mind that they're still mages, and not people using magic for conflict resolution for the sake of safe-guarding the mystical development and exploration of others. They're people on their own mystical journey, and are taking that through the very common path of conflict.<br /> <br /> (There's also a matter of how direct damage spells are somewhat limited in efficiency, given that the most direct way to do them requires taking on a decent amount of penalty for spell factor and Reach, and that's a lot of complications to juggle for an end result that is probably not more effective than just shooting somebody a couple of times. Like, you can say &quot;oh, why don't they just make people choke&quot;, but you can't bypass how the spellcasting system works for that.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559059#post1559059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why use Matter to enhance your armor, or mind to multitask tactics, when you could just use mind to make someone kill themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a matter of how, for the Awakened, the ethics of what they do aren't just abstract philosophical points, but things that can have real substantive effects on their behaviour.<br /> <br /> Mind controlling somebody into killing themselves (once one gets past the high amount of Reach that requires and other spellcasting considerations) is kind of messed up on the face of it. Now consider what mages might think about how a person who does such a thing might cop an attitude of that level of authority over another person makes them a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-28-2026, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T11:30:58-07:00","id":1559068,"title":"","content":"Totally different question -<br /> <br /> Can someone summarize the differences between 1st and 2nd edition mage sight rules? I'm slightly used to 2nd edition but have reason to want to know about 1e. Is the difference mostly that since it is a spell in 1e a mage has no magical sense of any kind unless they are running the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T12:42:15-07:00","id":1559069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559068#post1559068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone summarize the differences between 1st and 2nd edition mage sight rules? I'm slightly used to 2nd edition but have reason to want to know about 1e. Is the difference mostly that since it is a spell in 1e a mage has no magical sense of any kind unless they are running the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>In both editions, Awakening provides enough knowledge of the Arcana to activate Mage Sight for at least your Ruling Arcana; 1e just makes the equivalent of Active Mage Sight and Focused Mage Sight a spell instead of a pseudo-Attainment with Arcana prerequisites.<br /> <br /> 1e uses Intelligence + Occult instead of Gnosis + Arcanum for rolls to scrutinize resonance while a Mage Sight spell is active, gives a minor dice modifier based on the physical/metaphysical density of the subject, and treats it as a conventional extended action roll with gleaning information on various qualities adding to the required total instead of having some or all information gated behind different levels of Opacity.<br /> <br /> Peripheral Mage Sight is modeled in 1e as the equivalent of having the Unseen Sense Merit for every type of supernatural phenomenon, which functions as a cue to cast an Unveiling spell just as the Periphery it does for turning on Active Mage Sight in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T13:52:38-07:00","id":1559071,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> thanks for the further explanation. I understand the lore makes it clear (from the stories ive read at least) that magic isnt easy to do on the fly. Its just thats how a lot of people seem to describe their games going when a mage player enters combat. Levi, doing a spell that requires touching someone to make them choke costs a lot of reach? I thought that would be very little?<br /> <br /> My final question is within gameplay (ignoring lore that confirms this seems to be the case), is going into combat with a strategy focusing on self enhancement magic rather than directly damaging the enemy mage with damaging magic more practical in some scenarios, whether sleepers are present or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T14:51:50-07:00","id":1559073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559071#post1559071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and [USER=&quot;158&quot;]<br /> My final question is within gameplay (ignoring lore that confirms this seems to be the case), is going into combat with a strategy focusing on self enhancement magic rather than directly damaging the enemy mage with damaging magic more practical in some scenarios, whether sleepers are present or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sellf-enhancement can be defensive, allowing you survive a fight longer (increasing Wits and Dexterity improves Defence, Time can allow using defence against fiearms, Life to provide an Armour rating etc.) <br /> <br /> Magically defences could be Thaunium item filled with mana, or Prime Shielding effect, which would cover all forms of magical attacks. Though also defence can be not fighting, Time or Space can end combat without killing as you exit. Spirit mages may be able to escape into the Shadow to exit a fight, Death mages may transport themselves to Deathly twilight... Leaving only Obrimos without a method of escape.<br /> <br /> Also Fate magic might have been employed before a fight even begins to avoid whatever circumstances lead to the fight to begin with. A form of proactive defence where your car happens to break down so you are late for the meeting where others are attacked... Or whatever circumstances narratively make sense. <br /> <br /> Ultimately it is not a white room. Mages are people and have their own approaches and philosophicies, reasons for getting into a conflict, which can often be resolved without resorting to murdering the opponent (with the possible exception of dealing with Harrowed Banishers?) Seers and even Scelesti might be negotiated with... The local Lex Magica might also be more restrictive depending on circumstances... Again, like an actual character, the specific a of the setting will vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T15:06:28-07:00","id":1559074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559071#post1559071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Levi, doing a spell that requires touching someone to make them choke costs a lot of reach? I thought that would be very little?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touching someone requires a Dexterity + Brawl roll that is resisted by Defense and choking someone is either a modification of an attack spell (requiring at least Disciple-level competence in the Arcanum), requires a timescale long enough that in immediate terms the target might readily take actions against you, or is an area effect with its own complications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My final question is within gameplay (ignoring lore that confirms this seems to be the case), is going into combat with a strategy focusing on self enhancement magic rather than directly damaging the enemy mage with damaging magic more practical in some scenarios, whether sleepers are present or not? </div> </div> </div>Internal qualities of the caster themselves are both consistently use less Reach for range and have more ability to control for witnesses, as well as not typically needing perception of an external target to prepare in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T16:51:42-07:00","id":1559076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559069#post1559069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peripheral Mage Sight is modeled in 1e as the equivalent of having the Unseen Sense Merit for every type of supernatural phenomenon, which functions as a cue to cast an Unveiling spell just as the Periphery it does for turning on Active Mage Sight in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Somewhere along the way I had missed this bit and was wondering why a 1e mage wasn't always running Mage Sight. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T17:14:24-07:00","id":1559077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559076#post1559076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Somewhere along the way I had missed this bit and was wondering why a 1e mage wasn't always running Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is notably a bit in Legacies: the Sublime's section on Legacy design that notes that you usually can't go wrong with including always-on Mage Sight and Armor as part of the first Attainment; in an edition where Mage Armor is an Arcanum Attainment even newly-Awakened mages qualify for and Active Mage Sight is an innate ability with drawbacks to its use, this advice is largely redundant or irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T07:47:35-07:00","id":1559092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559071#post1559071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Levi, doing a spell that requires touching someone to make them choke costs a lot of reach? I thought that would be very little?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming based on your assumption of triviality that the person was casting the spell as a sensory effect.<br /> <br /> If not, then sure, it's a fair bit easier to cast that instant-or-very-quick death spell if you walk up to and lay hands on a person.<br /> <br /> While in a fight with them.<br /> <br /> Hopefully in the time it takes to get up to them, they don't shoot you.<br /> <br /> It would help to have something like a self-enhancement there to let you apply Defence against firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T16:38:19-07:00","id":1559106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559092#post1559092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was assuming based on your assumption of triviality that the person was casting the spell as a sensory effect.<br /> <br /> If not, then sure, it's a fair bit easier to cast that instant-or-very-quick death spell if you walk up to and lay hands on a person.<br /> <br /> While in a fight with them.<br /> <br /> Hopefully in the time it takes to get up to them, they don't shoot you.<br /> <br /> It would help to have something like a self-enhancement there to let you apply Defence against firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok. That makes sense. I struggle so much due to impressions and assumptions. I really need to get a hang of the rules because i always read these as being as simple as &quot;cast spell, next turn throw it&quot; <br /> <br /> it is assumed that once a spell is cast its ready to go right? Or would it be &quot;if you get hit, the spell dissipates as you lose focus needed to maintain it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T17:12:26-07:00","id":1559108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559106#post1559106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh ok. That makes sense. I struggle so much due to impressions and assumptions. I really need to get a hang of the rules because i always read these as being as simple as &quot;cast spell, next turn throw it&quot;<br /> <br /> it is assumed that once a spell is cast its ready to go right? Or would it be &quot;if you get hit, the spell dissipates as you lose focus needed to maintain it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A default spell is<br /> duration 1 (~3 seconds),<br /> range: touch,<br /> casting time: ritual duration(up to 3 hours),<br /> potency 1 (eg 1 damage/healing for a typical attack or healing spell),<br /> scale: 1 subject up to size 5 (a normal person, so a Werewolf shifted into a larger form may be immune)<br /> ---<br /> You can take a reach to increase (most of) these. Casting time -&gt; instant is 1 reach, and entirely necessary in combat.<br /> <br /> Range -&gt; sensory -&gt; remote viewing (probably only need the one reach for combat, unless you are casting from behind a CCTV, or through live web feed (from a mobile phone) or a scrying window...)<br /> <br /> Duration -&gt; 1 scene (most buffs or similar will need this to be useful in combat scenes).<br /> <br /> So since you only usually have 1 safe reach (with the most powerful spells you can cast), you are talking about over-reach is you go Instant casting *and* sensory range (which avoids the subject's Defence). You are immediately risking paradox when you cast something, and each paradox risked in a scene adds another die to the next paradox roll. So in a combat scene you do really want to keep track of things... One big spells which ends the fight is ideal, but risks failing if they have some magical defences... But throwing spells (if you have the athletics/firearms) or using touch range (if you can beat their Defence*) can save on that reach...<br /> --<br /> <br /> To your question, you can spend multiple turns using yantras/spending mana to prep a spell, but then you need to cast it immediately on the turn you roll it, Including either touching the opponent or throwing the spell... concentration only matters if you used the concentration Yantra, or if you are using the rules from SoS for being interrupted durings ritual casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T18:07:34-07:00","id":1559110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559106#post1559106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh ok. That makes sense. I struggle so much due to impressions and assumptions. I really need to get a hang of the rules because i always read these as being as simple as &quot;cast spell, next turn throw it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Throwing&quot; a spell is a reflexive action that happens on the same turn as the instant action of casting it. It's also a straight roll of Gnosis + ranged attack Skill penalized by Defense unless you have Fast Spells, surprise, or other workarounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it is assumed that once a spell is cast its ready to go right? Or would it be &quot;if you get hit, the spell dissipates as you lose focus needed to maintain it&quot; </div> </div> </div>Without Adamant Hand or other Merits or mechanics to allow you to use appropriate (instant) combat actions as reflexive Yantras, spellcasting takes up your turn in combat, and every Yantra you use after the first in instant casting requires an instant action to use otherwise. You can still benefit from your Defense, but Dodging deprives you of your normal action for the turn.<br /> <br /> So the issue is more that, unless you are a practitioner of the martial techniques of the struggle-exalting Order or have some other trick up your sleeve in a similar vein, casting a spell during combat directly trades number of Yantras for frequency of casting, and even the biggest conventional Yantra bonus only gets you two full extra spell factors before you start reducing your base dicepool.<br /> <br /> Rotes are worth their weight in gold for this and other reasons (see again &quot;mages cannot master most Arcana without learning from Masters&quot; re: free Reach), but if you misjudge your target's Withstand score or rely on roll-based means of getting the spell to affect them you run the risk of having wasted a turn even without using multiple Yantras; you can try and make up the shortfall in preparation-based resources by overReaching instead, but then you have decisions to make about how to handle the risk of Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T20:36:51-07:00","id":1559111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559110#post1559110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Throwing&quot; a spell is a reflexive action that happens on the same turn as the instant action of casting it. It's also a straight roll of Gnosis + ranged attack Skill penalized by Defense unless you have Fast Spells, surprise, or other workarounds.<br /> <br /> Without Adamant Hand or other Merits or mechanics to allow you to use appropriate (instant) combat actions as reflexive Yantras, spellcasting takes up your turn in combat, and every Yantra you use after the first in instant casting requires an instant action to use otherwise. You can still benefit from your Defense, but Dodging deprives you of your normal action for the turn.<br /> <br /> So the issue is more that, unless you are a practitioner of the martial techniques of the struggle-exalting Order or have some other trick up your sleeve in a similar vein, casting a spell during combat directly trades number of Yantras for frequency of casting, and even the biggest conventional Yantra bonus only gets you two full extra spell factors before you start reducing your base dicepool.<br /> <br /> Rotes are worth their weight in gold for this and other reasons (see again &quot;mages cannot master most Arcana without learning from Masters&quot; re: free Reach), but if you misjudge your target's Withstand score or rely on roll-based means of getting the spell to affect them you run the risk of having wasted a turn even without using multiple Yantras; you can try and make up the shortfall in preparation-based resources by overReaching instead, but then you have decisions to make about how to handle the risk of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok. Im starting to understand. It does seem suicidal now to just go in with a spell now.<br /> <br /> Last question. If its a spellcasting roll that cost your turn, wouldnt you be unable to throw it till next? Or is throwing it simply the roll being done, and NEXT turn its assumed you threw it? Either way, i understand why the Adamant Hand is so treasured.<br /> <br /> Oh, and to be clear. So if i cast a spell, and get take some bashing or lethal damage, i still retain the spell since once cast there is no imago needed to maintain anymore? Meaning that mundane methods can only hope to prevent spellcasting rather than erase it like Counterspell would?<br /> <br /> The last question is just so i understand whether the Arrow can utilize mundane strategies to stop a spell ready to throw out, or if they have to do shock tactics so the spell isnt made in the first place<br /> <br /> EDIT: also no idea why you got a thumbs down <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> i didnt mean to miss your post. That breakdown was a HUGE help. Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-29-2026, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T23:33:26-07:00","id":1559113,"title":"","content":"Other considerations for using a Touch range spell as aimed in order to literally throw it is that the spell takes the form of a visible bolt (which may be an issue if discretion is desired), and needs to be used as Area scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T23:41:41-07:00","id":1559114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559111#post1559111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last question. If its a spellcasting roll that cost your turn, wouldnt you be unable to throw it till next? Or is throwing it simply the roll being done, and NEXT turn its assumed you threw it? Either way, i understand why the Adamant Hand is so treasured.</div> </div> </div> </div>The roll to hit with an Aimed spell is reflexive and happens on the same turn you make the casting roll, after the rolls for casting and Paradox. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and to be clear. So if i cast a spell, and get take some bashing or lethal damage, i still retain the spell since once cast there is no imago needed to maintain anymore? Meaning that mundane methods can only hope to prevent spellcasting rather than erase it like Counterspell would? </div> </div> </div>Unless you have used the Concentration Yantra on a spell with a Duration long enough to qualify for its bonus, a Conditional Duration that can be triggered by such things, and/or some other means of causing a spell to end early, getting hurt doesn't cause a spell that has been cast to end it before its Duration runs its course. All of a mage's spells still under their control when they die are unsafely relinquished, which may result in Paradox-like warping of spells that would last beyond the start of the next chapter.<br /> <br /> Yantras that have already been incorporated into an instant casting don't go away, though Situation Yantras (described in Signs of Sorcery) have their own complications if they end early and ritual casting takes long enough that you can't &quot;lock in&quot; an individual Yantra before the casting roll (to sat nothing of the mechanics for interruption in Signs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The last question is just so i understand whether the Arrow can utilize mundane strategies to stop a spell ready to throw out, or if they have to do shock tactics so the spell isnt made in the first place </div> </div> </div>They use Counterspell and Counterspell Prime and the fact that even without the need to roll to make contact a mage needs to be able to perceive you to target you with spells without sympathy. Shock tactics are counterproductive in stopping someone from throwing out very dubious smokescreens in desperation, particularly for an Order whose praxis lives in the space surrounding self-imposed challenges, friendly competition, and having champions fight on behalf of something greater.<br /> <br /> Counterspell needing Active Mage Sight running is incidentally another reason for the Arrow to strengthen their mundane competencies \u2014 it's easier to work through a -2 penalty to all actions that don't relate to using or perceiving magic if you're good enough at those actions, and the Arrow isn't institutionally built to encourage members to not be also doing something else if the situatipn demands it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T02:44:39-07:00","id":1559115,"title":"","content":"Question: I was presuming that touching someone in combat to affect them with a spell allowed defence (like aimed spell) but the rules don't mention it.<br /> <br /> So my quick reference reads like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the ranges are<br /> +0 Reach: self/touch/touching in combat (dex +brawl/weaponry)/thrown spell( Gnosis+ higher of athletics/firearms - subject's defence\u2020)<br /> +1 Reach: sensory/sympathetic range\u2021<br /> +2 Reach: remote viewing (must be live)<br /> <br /> \u2020subject does not get defence if you have the fast spells merit<br /> \u2021sympathetic range is an attainment, which requires Space 2, and 1 mana, and a sympathic yantra, and a sympathy connection - which is used to withstand the spell (weaker the connection the higher the withstand). </div> </div> </div>Should touching in combat range be minus the subject's Defence. Since the Defence rules speecifc applying defence when the subject is aware, or is it not an attack?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> <br /> Spells can be cast in one turn with a reflexive Yantra, and either ar the +0 reach self/touch/thrown ranges or the +1 reach sensory range. (Extra yantras take extra turns pre-casting, so this means acting really fast in combat limits the size of your dice pool, and hence the number of spell factors you can add). But when people say &quot;throwing&quot; a spell above they are talking about this +0 reach thrown spell range. In case you meant something else (like releasing the spell).<br /> <br /> Counter spelling uses up your action and can be done out of initiative order so long as you have an Active Mage sight up (to see the imago) and the right Arcanum/Prime attainment to pull that Imago apart. But you risk failing the Clash of Wills and wasting your action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added the question and some context 03-30-2026, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T04:33:17-07:00","id":1559117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559115#post1559115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should touching in combat range be minus the subject's Defence. Since the Defence rules speecifc applying defence when the subject is aware, or is it not an attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's not an attack. Like, it's listed separately in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T04:51:53-07:00","id":1559118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559115#post1559115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should touching in combat range be minus the subject's Defence. Since the Defence rules speecifc applying defence when the subject is aware, or is it not an attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little confusing:<br /> <br /> The version of the mechanics presented in Changeling and onward specifies that Touching An Opponent is a simple action (neither contested nor resisted) in the same way as a ranged attack and furthermore is a type of attack action.<br /> <br /> Deviant's primary attack power Lash has four options for adjusting the roll the attack uses, for which the &quot;Defense does not apply at all&quot; option is exclusively for ranged attacks and the melee-exclusive &quot;the Brawl/Weaponry attack uses Dexterity instead of Strength&quot; option still subtracts Defense regardless of whether the attack is a type that does damage (and attacks that don't deal damage apply their effects on a target with any number of successes regardless of Armor).<br /> <br /> The Combat Summary Chart in the Rules Appendix included in Demon, which is also included in Beast and Promethean, specifies that while armor may or may not apply to attempts at Touching A Target, Defense does apply.<br /> <br /> The 1e mechanics specify that Defense always applies to the Dexterity + Brawl/Weaponry dicepool used to touch a resisting opponent, as does Armor against touch effects for which it would make sense (though in 1e Armor worked different mechanically).<br /> <br /> For sanity's sake it's likely prudent to subtract Defense from attempts to touch a resisting opponent as before, since Defense and Dodging are the only way to make that harder and &quot;Defense is a measure of your character's ability to mitigate harm to themselves&quot; doesn't really scan as an argument against using it when grappling counts as an unarmed attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T05:31:51-07:00","id":1559119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559118#post1559118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little confusing:</div> </div> </div> </div>That is comprehensive, but confusing...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The version of the mechanics presented in Changeling and onward specifies that Touching An Opponent is a simple action (neither contested nor resisted) in the same way as a ranged attack and furthermore is a type of attack action. </div> </div> </div>So as an attack action, I am assuming by the Changeling rules, you usually get a Defence against being touched (unless you choose not to avoid it - or infact, do cabal mates who know what you're doing not require you to even roll?); barring the circumstances such as being surprised, or otherwise bring unaware that they are trying to touch you (such as being touched through a co-locate which they cannot see, of from twilight?) or perhaps from being too fast to defend against (though the Acceleration example spell doesn't seem to include this as an effect so maybe not?)<br /> <br /> And in that case, I would assume going prone grants the touched a +2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T13:18:31-07:00","id":1559123,"title":"","content":"Re-reading pg. 219, I think it might be noteworthy that the other example with touch-range spell is planting a bug on someone.<br /> <br /> Like, you wouldn't use defence for whether you can attach a bug to someone would you? The whole point of a bug is that the target doesn't know it's there.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the idea is that the paragraph gives you the basic dicepool, and then you resist it with whatever the circumstances call for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T14:27:39-07:00","id":1559125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559123#post1559123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of a bug is that the target doesn't know it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of picking pockets is that you take something off of somebody without their knowing. Is that also a basis for meaning it should just work without a chance to impede or notice?<br /> <br /> After all, the dice roll is there to represent the challenge of accomplishing a goal under duress, with penalties to represent the difficulties in doing that. Laying hands upon a person without their knowing or responding seems like a difficulty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T14:59:34-07:00","id":1559126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559123#post1559123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading pg. 219, I think it might be noteworthy that the other example with touch-range spell is planting a bug on someone.<br /> <br /> Like, you wouldn't use defence for whether you can attach a bug to someone would you? The whole point of a bug is that the target doesn't know it's there.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the idea is that the paragraph gives you the basic dicepool, and then you resist it with whatever the circumstances call for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it depends on whether it is in combat and they are actively trying to avoid being touched by you, or if it is a social situation and they are relaxed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T05:13:26-07:00","id":1559138,"title":"","content":"I have doubts about the Primal transfer spell from Signs of sorcery.<br /> If i understand it rightly in the reach option you must imbue it as a Persistent spell, then when another mage uses the item all of the spells (included primal transfer) passes under the user control?<br /> Does it work on both Persistent and Activation spells?<br /> Does the Item occupy one slot even if it has multiple spells imbued?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T11:18:59-07:00","id":1559144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559138#post1559138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i understand it rightly in the reach option you must imbue it as a Persistent spell, then when another mage uses the item all of the spells (included primal transfer) passes under the user control?</div> </div> </div> </div>It says &quot;those spells&quot; are transferred to the user's spell control when activated, and this comes after the part of the sentence referring to &quot;any <i>other</i> spells included in the item,&quot; so presumably Primal Transfer remains under the creator's control.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it work on both Persistent and Activation spells? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though Persistent items only need to be activated if dispelled.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Item occupy one slot even if it has multiple spells imbued? </div> </div> </div>Each spell in an imbued item takes up a spell control slot, regardless of how many instances of that spell are currently active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T13:42:20-07:00","id":1559395,"title":"","content":"Clash of wills,<br /> Can you redo the same action making clashes again and again until you win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T14:09:41-07:00","id":1559397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559395#post1559395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clash of wills,<br /> Can you redo the same action making clashes again and again until you win?</div> </div> </div> </div>In which circumstances? <br /> <br /> You can repeat an action, in stressful situations (like combat) isn't there a -1 for trying to repeat a failed action?<br /> <br /> Or is the stress and waste action considered enough of a risk, like if you shoot someone with a gun and miss, you don't take a pentalty to shoot them again, so maybe it is only in stress-free situations...<br /> <br /> But then again, a Clash of Wills doesn't mean you failed the action, right? So it is a third thing....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T14:43:10-07:00","id":1559399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559395#post1559395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clash of wills,<br /> Can you redo the same action making clashes again and again until you win?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;action&quot; involved in a Clash of Wills that is not simply bringing the powers into conflict. If you Clash with a supernatural effect, the winner of the two contradictory effects takes precedence. Within the scope of a scene, the only way to roll the Clash again is with another instance of the power, whether a different effect or re-casting the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T16:09:12-07:00","id":1559400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559399#post1559399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no &quot;action&quot; involved in a Clash of Wills that is not simply bringing the powers into conflict. If you Clash with a supernatural effect, the winner of the two contradictory effects takes precedence. Within the scope of a scene, the only way to roll the Clash again is with another instance of the power, whether a different effect or re-casting the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what i mean say X is veiling and Y is trying to scry him. Whats stoping Y from rolling again and again until he lucks up in a Clash of Wills roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T17:27:55-07:00","id":1559403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559400#post1559400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats what i mean say X is veiling and Y is trying to scry him. Whats stoping Y from rolling again and again until he lucks up in a Clash of Wills roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Time, Withstand, resources, and the fact that any given bit of spellcasting requires a roll before you get to the Clash roll. Most defensive spells that trigger a Clash are Duration-primary and therefore have easy access to extra dice.<br /> <br /> Scrying in particular requires the use of Borrow Threads to leverage Sympathetic Range on anything you don't already have ties to and needs spell factors or Reach dedicated to adding Potency to overcome the Withstand rating of the connection, and the number of elements of spellcasting that add surcharges or limiting factors to those without Path-based affinity for a spell's Arcanum mean it's entirely probable that a character who doesn't have Space as a Ruling Arcanum either risks Paradox casting rapidly, takes hours recasting slightly more safely, or has gone out of their way to train in scrying in a way that makes lucky breaks more likely or borrows the expertise of a Master to better prepare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T18:12:34-07:00","id":1559406,"title":"","content":"Attempting failed rolls over accumulates penalties, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T18:20:20-07:00","id":1559408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559406#post1559406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attempting failed rolls over accumulates penalties, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When time is short and the situation is tense, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T04:02:51-07:00","id":1559427,"title":"","content":"On which kind of powers does the Fate Atonement spell work?<br /> The description says &quot;supernatural effect enforced by the dictates of destiny, including Awakened spells&quot; which is not clear to me (all spells counts? Only Fate spells? All effect described in the Unbound fate Attainment?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T05:53:57-07:00","id":1559429,"title":"","content":"Creating a loophole to end the effect of any supernal spell sounds like adding a conditional duration to a spell.<br /> <br /> But as much fun as that might be, I don't think that is intended.<br /> <br /> Take a look at Sworn Oaths, it explicitly states &quot;Fate itself enforces the subject's adherence to her how&quot; - I think that is a kind of spell which would qualify under the &quot;enforced by the dictates of destiny&quot;... But not all Fate spells...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T06:23:38-07:00","id":1559430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559427#post1559427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On which kind of powers does the Fate Atonement spell work?<br /> The description says &quot;supernatural effect enforced by the dictates of destiny, including Awakened spells&quot; which is not clear to me (all spells counts? Only Fate spells? All effect described in the Unbound fate Attainment?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect is caused by something that doesn't have a discrete actor at the wheel (such as &quot;a vampire is controlling my mind&quot; or &quot;a fire-spirit is using its Influence to meddle with my car engine&quot;), but is instead the product of an ongoing subtle influence brought into effect through a magical agreement, pronouncement, document, etc. (i.e. the cause is essentially &quot;It Is Written&quot; rather than something directly caused by the being whose power is having an escape clause built into it).<br /> <br /> There are some edge cases in this interpretation \u2014 the type of pledge called a curse puts deleterious effects on its target as long as the changeling who cursed them maintains a routine or adheres to a forbiddance, but being burned by the sound of church bells for as long as the Hunterheart who cursed you abstains from eating meat isn't <i>caused</i> by that Grim's diet except in the sense that the force of destiny known as the Wyrd has a while-loop in place that connects those two things; meanwhile, the Haunt called the Curse puts a mark on its target that allows the Sin-Eater who cursed them to bring negative circumstances into play or worsen existing ones until the charges are used up or the mark is removed, but despite the mechanical framing of its effects being player-triggered it's still very definitely a case of &quot;the world is going wrong for you in a way that is distinct from something exerting direct control over the material vectors of that misfortune.&quot;<br /> <br /> A quick shorthand would be to check if the effect is ongoing and autonomous rather than requiring specific actions or oversight from the source to trigger it \u2014 being haunted by ghosts because a Shade made you a universal Anchor doesn't require that death-god to give instructions to the dead shoplifters to get you in trouble at the mall, and the cunning-man who wiped ectoplasm on your shirt three days ago doesn't need to diegetically know your current situation or available sources of trouble to spend a charge to make you sprain your ankle or be unable to light a fire for an hour. Anything described as a &quot;curse&quot; in the text is usually fair game, as is anything that isn't a direct injury or manipulation of a specific phenomenon, i.e. the power is ongoing but does not have the source of the power doing more than putting you in a circumstance where reality is predisposed toward the effects of the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T15:35:05-07:00","id":1559436,"title":"","content":"Warlocks and Necromancers using their magic for world conquest is such a cliche trope at this point.<br /> <br /> Subvert expectations!<br /> <br /> Defy conventional norms!<br /> <br /> Make mankind resent its creators!<br /> <br /> <b>PLAY AN EVIL THEURGE!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Mwahahahahahahahaha!!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T04:59:50-07:00","id":1559449,"title":"","content":"About the Correspondence spell (space 1)<br /> If i choose the &quot;follow&quot; reach option, how many subjects does the spell requires?<br /> Is the original subject the only one or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T05:25:28-07:00","id":1559450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559449#post1559449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Correspondence spell (space 1)<br /> If i choose the &quot;follow&quot; reach option, how many subjects does the spell requires?<br /> Is the original subject the only one or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most intuitive read to me is that the Scale for number of subjects caps the extent of the spell's &quot;range&quot; for that Reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T05:46:13-07:00","id":1559451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559450#post1559450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most intuitive read to me is that the Scale for number of subjects caps the extent of the spell's &quot;range&quot; for that Reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is strange because this would imply that the spell could cast to subjects out of the sensory range without the Sympathetic range attainment<br /> So if a mage is one of the secondary subject would the spell activete the Pheriperal sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T06:08:58-07:00","id":1559452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559451#post1559451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is strange because this would imply that the spell could cast to subjects out of the sensory range without the Sympathetic range attainment</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing the spell does is identify sympathetic connections and the location of their other half within sensory range, after all, and Potency still limits the number of connections you can determine in one casting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if a mage is one of the secondary subject would the spell activete the Pheriperal sight? </div> </div> </div>They would be in the area of the spell, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T05:57:39-07:00","id":1559557,"title":"","content":"Two questions this time.<br /> 1. Lets say a mage wants to propel a stone from his hand with great speed at a target using forces 3 or 4. Would you allow him to use advanced range to autohit the target? Why?<br /> <br /> 2. Lets say Mage 1 has a antiscrying veiling spell on himself. Meanwhile Mage 2 has a hair of Mage 1. Can Mage 2 cast a curse on Mage 1 throught a sympatetic connection (hair) without it starting a clash of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T06:11:35-07:00","id":1559558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559557#post1559557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions this time.<br /> 1. Lets say a mage wants to propel a stone from his hand with great speed at a target using forces 3 or 4. Would you allow him to use advanced range to autohit the target? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the kind of thing that First Edition would have used spell-based range rules for, in a way that confused their whole application and that Second Edition specifically worked to drum out.<br /> <br /> Spell range is for the limits of the subject of the spell. If a person casts a spell on something they're holding, they shouldn't play into using it afterwards. I would think a premise like that is being able to treat something like a thrown attack as a firearms attack in terms of interaction with Defence and cover rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Lets say Mage 1 has a antiscrying veiling spell on himself. Meanwhile Mage 2 has a hair of Mage 1. Can Mage 2 cast a curse on Mage 1 throught a sympatetic connection (hair) without it starting a clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, strictly speaking a mage can't cast a spell through a sympathetic connection possessed by something else. They need to use magic to transfer that connection to themselves, while at the same time the hair is valid as the sympathetic yantra necessary to cast. <br /> <br /> But otherwise, if a person has for whatever reason cast a spell to specifically protect them from scrying rather than more broadly being protected from any sympathetic casting, a sympathetic spell that is not scrying would not be clashed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T07:06:39-07:00","id":1559560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559557#post1559557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions this time.<br /> 1. Lets say a mage wants to propel a stone from his hand with great speed at a target using forces 3 or 4. Would you allow him to use advanced range to autohit the target? Why?<br /> <br /> 2. Lets say Mage 1 has a antiscrying veiling spell on himself. Meanwhile Mage 2 has a hair of Mage 1. Can Mage 2 cast a curse on Mage 1 throught a sympatetic connection (hair) without it starting a clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> said, plus reading the description of <br /> Veil Sympathy spell (veiling) it states: <br /> &quot;Any attempt to uncover or USE the link provokes a Clash of Wills.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T12:32:37-07:00","id":1559570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559557#post1559557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions this time.<br /> 1. Lets say a mage wants to propel a stone from his hand with great speed at a target using forces 3 or 4. Would you allow him to use advanced range to autohit the target? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw a similar question on Reddit recently, I think you cast ar touch range on the stone. That's it.<br /> <br /> Look at something like telekenisis, which (while an odd spell in itself) requires them Mage to simply concentrate and use an instant action each turn.<br /> <br /> For simplicity using it as a reflexive spell on a stone you have already thrown would let you cast while the stone is in the air (say) velocity control, which would add 1point of damage to projectile attacks (without the ability to cast reflecively, I've no idea how you would affect a projectile... Or should I say when...).<br /> <br /> But the 1 point of damage is rather lacklustre. Especially compared to &quot;damage based on collision&quot; - which effectively let's you force a car out of control and potentially killing all occupants...<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what Istar said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 04-22-2026, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T01:02:14-07:00","id":1559593,"title":"","content":"About ghost mages, i ve read somewhere that Dave Brookshaw mentioned the possibility of becoming one using a 5 dot death spell.<br /> Does someone has the link?<br /> If i m right, would it be correct to assume that dispelling the original spell would destroy the mage or make it a regular ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T01:57:02-07:00","id":1559595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559593#post1559593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About ghost mages, i ve read somewhere that Dave Brookshaw mentioned the possibility of becoming one using a 5 dot death spell.<br /> Does someone has the link?<br /> If i m right, would it be correct to assume that dispelling the original spell would destroy the mage or make it a regular ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the spell, if you wasn't it to be permanent, a legacy attainment is usually recommended. <br /> <br /> If you are just altering a pre-existing thing, 4 dots is usually enough, so a mage already being there and maybe dying can be patterned into something else (like a ghost mage). Which, allows an extra reach for any capstone attainment (probably necessary to go indefinite)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T13:33:26-07:00","id":1559622,"title":"","content":"What stops a mage from having 10 indefinate buffs on himself all the time and paying willpower to release control?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T14:43:45-07:00","id":1559624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559622#post1559622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stops a mage from having 10 indefinate buffs on himself all the time and paying willpower to release control?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of unsafe relinquishment, degradation per chapter as described in the mechanic. In the case of safe relinquishment, functional Experience costs.<br /> <br /> In both cases, indefinite Duration is a big swing even for Duration-primary spells cast by a Master, having spells visible to appropriate Active Mage Sight on you is a peripheral giveaway to your being a mage when you're pretending not to be while going out in public, and removing spells from your spell control could result in problems of not necessarily always wanting some effects to be active (if they bring you too far from the domain of typical human capabilities it's possible they may affect your Wisdom, per the sidebar in Nameless and Accursed about spending excessive time in a bestial or posthuman mindset potentially leading to Rapture).<br /> <br /> In short, the fact that magic is a thing you need to keep under control and significant elements of the reality you inhabit are out to get you make it unwise to walk around with raw mythic power manifested onto you without an off-switch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T17:22:06-07:00","id":1559627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559622#post1559622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What stops a mage from having 10 indefinate buffs on himself all the time and paying willpower to release control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal Dispellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T00:44:04-07:00","id":1559631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559627#post1559627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Supernal Dispellation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, spending XP (usually) on spells which are not lasting and can be destroyed by a simple Prime effect, is generally risky.<br /> <br /> I suppose you could do some other stuff to relinquish safely, but those are usually acts of hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T05:13:55-07:00","id":1559633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559631#post1559631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is, spending XP (usually) on spells which are not lasting and can be destroyed by a simple Prime effect, is generally risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mostly meant it as a bit of a cheeky comment of the most literal way to answer that question.<br /> <br /> You encounter a person with ten indefinite spells on them. Somebody casts that one spell with appropriate target factors. Person doesn't have ten indefinite spells on them anymore.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there is a key point of while that might create an incentive against going around with ten indefinite and relinquished spells, there is a straightforward counter even if somebody does opt for that.<br /> <br /> Still, I think the major way that should inform gameplay is to understand that there's no one neat trick that functions as a killer app, so mages in general need to be more flexible and strategically discerning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T05:53:38-07:00","id":1559636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559633#post1559633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mostly meant it as a bit of a cheeky comment of the most literal way to answer that question.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, I was actually thinking that sanctity of merits (or other sanctities of things that cost XP) does not apply to spells you have relinquished...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T10:28:46-07:00","id":1559646,"title":"","content":"Multiple questions about status, orders, and a random one:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As merits can be lost, what happens to you if losing the Order status merit but not move to any other order? Can you still use the Order tool and rote skills?</li> <li>If you switch orders, what happens with your rote skills? Do you keep the old? New only? Both?</li> <li>If you are part of an order, and buy the Nameless order status as described in character creation, can you get up to 6 rote skills?</li> <li>Is there anywhere stated the Crown Prelacy benefit of the Psychopomp? AFAIK it is the only Exarch who has not been officially given a Crown.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T11:14:09-07:00","id":1559647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559646#post1559646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple questions about status, orders, and a random one:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As merits can be lost, what happens to you if losing the Order status merit but not move to any other order? Can you still use the Order tool and rote skills?</li> <li>If you switch orders, what happens with your rote skills? Do you keep the old? New only? Both?</li> <li>If you are part of an order, and buy the Nameless order status as described in character creation, can you get up to 6 rote skills?<br /> </li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I think these are like the Shadow Name merit. There is an argument that you must be aligned with the symbolic philosophy of the order (or nameless order) to use the rote skills. So new ones if you join a new order, old ones if you are technically kicked from the Order by still align with their goals?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div></li> <li>Is there anywhere stated the Crown Prelacy benefit of the Psychopomp? AFAIK it is the only Exarch who has not been officially given a Crown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T12:39:29-07:00","id":1559694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. With the exception of unusual mechanics like the systems for using other splats' fuel or rituals as Yantras as described in the Contagion Chronicle PG, individual Yantras generally top out at +3 unless they're rote Mudras or a fully-invested Shadow Name with a Cabal Theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not expecting to get more than a +3.<br /> <br /> I am now re-reading the section on page 98<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage2eCore</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When used by another mage as a tool Yantra, soul stones offer a +2 die bonus...</div> </div> </div> </div>So my question isn't can you get more than +2/+3 from a single use of the Yantra, it is if the single item happens to be symbolic of the spell on two different ways (so you use it as a tool Yantra twice for one spell) can it give +2/+3 each time (taking up two Yantra slots and an extra turn of spellcasting for the second Yantra use)?<br /> <br /> Which is inline with Sacraments, Investments, and Lex Magica yantras (which I think all allow a +3 Yantra bonus if you put in sufficient effort roleplaying...) <br /> <br /> The alternative reading (which I'm now thinking is a misunderstanding) is that soulstones gain an extra use for resonant spells... Which doesn't seem to align with the quote above from pg 98.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T13:29:31-07:00","id":1559695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559694#post1559694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my question isn't can you get more than +2/+3 from a single use of the Yantra, it is if the single item happens to be symbolic of the spell on two different ways (so you use it as a tool Yantra twice for one spell) can it give +2/+3 each time (taking up two Yantra slots and an extra turn of spellcasting for the second Yantra use)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The general situation would be that, per the &quot;Effect&quot; note at the start of the section, tool Yantras provide a +1 bonus unless a different bonus supersedes it as described in the individual Yantra.<br /> <br /> You would need to be leveraging <i>different symbolism</i> to use a single tool as multiple different types of Tool Yantra, so you couldn't double up on either of Path Tools or Order Tools with the same tool, but if you're an Arrow and you have a Path Tool that's a weapon you can use it as both of those things in their different interpretations of What Weapons Mean.<br /> <br /> Soul stones count as Dedicated Tools for their creators, and part of that is that they double as Path or Order Tools, which normally provide a +1 bonus. A sanity-check interpretation (unless you want soul stones to be even more especially useful as magical aids if aligned with overlapping symbolism) is to interpret the &quot;or&quot; as exclusive and thus only allow the benefit of casting with someone else's soul stone to apply to the first use of it as a tool, with any additional applications using the more typical bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T01:40:00-07:00","id":1559697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559695#post1559695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would need to be leveraging <i>different symbolism</i> to use a single tool as multiple different types of Tool Yantra, so you couldn't double up on either of Path Tools or Order Tools with the same tool, but if you're an Arrow and you have a Path Tool that's a weapon you can use it as both of those things in their different interpretations of What Weapons Mean.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have another simple question on this topic. What the hell does &quot;symbols of conflict&quot; mean? Like sure, Arrows have a philosophy around combat, and using order tools to give a +1 for symbols of conflict (ie the tool is a symbol of conflict) makes sense.<br /> <br /> But what spells are symbolically resonant with those tools?<br /> <br /> Like for path tools it seems clear: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> any spell that takes direct, decisive action <br /> on the world (or a person) can benefit from a weapon. </div> </div> </div>It lists what counts as a knife for each path, and it lists what spells count for benefiting from that symbol.<br /> <br /> But for order tools, it seems we only get half of that (the what counts as an order tool). Is the Liberties &quot;complex mechanisms and systems&quot; applicable to any spell which is inline with Libertine philosophy? Is it like Shadow names where you define the limits and you vibe check whether or not this is inline with the character of the order? Or do Order factions what their own supernal resonance so you can use the same tools for sa different set of spells?<br /> <br /> Seers display a word or sigil to use as a tool, is that only got spells where they are imposing a particular type of Tyranny or generally for expressing authority?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T06:47:15-07:00","id":1559698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559697#post1559697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another simple question on this topic. What the hell does &quot;symbols of conflict&quot; mean? Like sure, Arrows have a philosophy around combat, and using order tools to give a +1 for symbols of conflict (ie the tool is a symbol of conflict) makes sense.<br /> <br /> But what spells are symbolically resonant with those tools?<br /> <br /> Like for path tools it seems clear:<br /> <br /> It lists what counts as a knife for each path, and it lists what spells count for benefiting from that symbol.<br /> <br /> But for order tools, it seems we only get half of that (the what counts as an order tool). Is the Liberties &quot;complex mechanisms and systems&quot; applicable to any spell which is inline with Libertine philosophy? Is it like Shadow names where you define the limits and you vibe check whether or not this is inline with the character of the order? Or do Order factions what their own supernal resonance so you can use the same tools for sa different set of spells?<br /> <br /> Seers display a word or sigil to use as a tool, is that only got spells where they are imposing a particular type of Tyranny or generally for expressing authority?</div> </div> </div> </div>Order Tools are functionally mechanically identical to Path Tools in almost every way, i.e. they provide a +1 bonus for each different tool used to make the casting appropriate to the archetype the group represents.<br /> <br /> The Arrow exalts challenge and martial prowess, so the things that their magic incorporates include means of inflicting harm on others and means of protecting someone from harm and their Order Merit allows them to treat actions related to Fighting as Order Tools.<br /> <br /> The Free Council puts particular stock in the idea that human culture shapes the Supernal, so the common ground between the objects their magic may incorporate is that they're complex systems and their Order Merit allows them to treat less material examples of such systems in action as Order Tools and double up on doing so with Sleepers engaging in it.<br /> <br /> The Seers believe magic is a reward from the rulers of the Supernal for their servitude, so their Order Tools are designed to invoke the Exarch they serve, with lay members doing so through their Ministry connection and Prelates gaining the ability to further invoke them as more direct Patrons.<br /> <br /> Faction members further expand the material definition of what counts as an Order Tool based on their philosophy just as they add to the list of Skills they are encouraged to practice to benefit their Rote casting.<br /> <br /> Magic is sufficiently open-ended that an exhaustive definition of what spells can and cannot benefit from the less-personal-than-Persona-Yantras Flavor Tools would be prohibitively verbose to no real benefit. It's a vibe check.<br /> <br /> <br /> Related but tangential: Do the Yantras provided by a Legacy count as any specific other type of Tool for mechanics that make a distinction, or is &quot;Legacy Tools&quot; a mechanical category that has relevance to any published rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T11:40:06-07:00","id":1559702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559698#post1559698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Related but tangential: Do the Yantras provided by a Legacy count as any specific other type of Tool for mechanics that make a distinction, or is &quot;Legacy Tools&quot; a mechanical category that has relevance to any published rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Legacy Tools mostly differ from Path/Order/Patron Tools in that they often include +2 tool bonuses, something akin to the +2 tool bonus from Perfected metal tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T01:16:00-07:00","id":1559712,"title":"","content":"Can you explain legacy attainments to me? The wording in the book is confusing and i cant get why they get less duration than potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T07:02:52-07:00","id":1559718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559712#post1559712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain legacy attainments to me? The wording in the book is confusing and i cant get why they get less duration than potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically or metaphysically?<br /> <br /> They get primary factor steps equal to the arcana rating (so a 4th dot attainment would be potency 4 or 4 duration), right? <br /> <br /> And they can add to secondary factors a number of steps depending on how big the dice pool would be (each step costing two dice, for 4th/5th attainments get 2 steps, 2nd/3rd get 1 step, and 1st attainments get 0 steps). <br /> <br /> Sorry, looking at the book, it seems to be based on the Mage's current Arcanum rating, not the level of the attainment. But otherwise what I said above is the minimums for what a new member without extra dots in the Arcanum has just gotten access to the attainment.<br /> <br /> Whether duration or potency gets more steps depends entirely on whether it is a duration or potency primary effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T07:14:43-07:00","id":1559719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559712#post1559712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain legacy attainments to me? The wording in the book is confusing and i cant get why they get less duration than potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. They get free ranks equal to its highest prerequisite Arcanum minus one in Potency or Duration as determined by the primary factor of the spell the Attainment is based on, plus additional spell factors that would penalize casting the Attainment as a spell based on its lowest Arcanum.<br /> <br /> For example, a Fourth Attainment based on Stealing Fire used by a practitioner with Prime 4 can make a Sleeper into a Sleepwalker for up to five turns (or a month, if one of the Attainment's two fixed Reach are put toward Advanced Duration) because that's three free steps up the Duration chart for a Duration-primary spell cast by someone with four dots in the Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Without assigning Reach or other factors, it takes a scene to use and they can only affect a single willing target, because Potency starts at 1, Withstand reduces effective Potency, and Resolve doesn't go below 1 in normal circumstances, but since the Legacy member definitionally has enough Prime dots to offset four dice worth of spell factor penalties they could assign two spell factors between increasing Potency on a one-for-one basis (allowing them to affect subjects who haven't consciously allowed it with Resolve ratings up to 1 and 2, respectively) or doubling the number of subjects they can affect in one sitting (first two, then four).<br /> <br /> In this case, assigning one Reach to Advanced Duration is easily the highest priority from that budget, since Stealing Fire is not terribly useful in extremely short-term situations, but the remaining Reach can be assigned to either making the Attainment usable as an instant action with no prep time, changing the primary factor from Duration to Potency (making the effect only last a scene without assigning other factors but allowing it to affect targets up to Resolve 3 without their conscious allowance), multiplying the number of subjects it can be used on in one sitting by five (up to five subjects with no Scale factors assigned, up to ten with one assigned, or up to twenty with two assigned), or (with 1 Mana and both additional factors assigned to Duration) making the Attainment's effects last indefinitely. It's technically also possible to spend the Reach on giving it Advanced Potency, but since Legacy Attainments can't be dispelled there's not much point to that.<br /> <br /> Between the fixed Reach assignment and the limited ability to increase other spell factors, Legacy Attainments are less flexible than the spells they're based on, but they have consistent and reliable effects that can't be dispelled, and their power and flexibility still increase with knowledge of the Arcanum they're based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T09:18:48-07:00","id":1559757,"title":"","content":"COuld you give a practical example? its still feels confusing if i have to pick the reaches and factors before i get the ataiment or can i change them every time i cast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T11:44:57-07:00","id":1559763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559757#post1559757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">COuld you give a practical example? its still feels confusing if i have to pick the reaches and factors before i get the ataiment or can i change them every time i cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Reaches and primary factors are set, though you can use less than the full primary factors. The &quot;secondary&quot; factors are more flexible, but there's much less of them.<br /> <br /> The tradeoff here is because you aren't actually casting a spell despite using the spellcasting mechanics to build the effect \u2014 a Legacy Attainment is a natural facet of the mage's presence that doesn't have to cross the Abyss to become real.<br /> <br /> The spellcasting system being as broad as it is, could you give an example of what you want to put into practice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T04:53:16-07:00","id":1559784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559763#post1559763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spellcasting system being as broad as it is, could you give an example of what you want to put into practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not include legacies at first in my games. Now i want to include a Knight templar legacy about protecting the timeline from anomalies and abusers.<br /> The first attainment i want to include is for it to work like Serendipity form Fate 1. Where the patron gods guide the user to the closest anomaly with a optional time effect of the next step on the road to get rid of it having extra dice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T07:01:15-07:00","id":1559788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559784#post1559784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not include legacies at first in my games. Now i want to include a Knight templar legacy about protecting the timeline from anomalies and abusers.<br /> The first attainment i want to include is for it to work like Serendipity form Fate 1. Where the patron gods guide the user to the closest anomaly with a optional time effect of the next step on the road to get rid of it having extra dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so as a First Attainment it gives you one Reach to work with regardless of how high your Fate dots later become; unless you have something else you intend to use that Reach for, you'll want to use it on instant &quot;casting&quot; (otherwise using it will take a scene); it'll have effective Potency equal to your Fate dots and about half as many other ranks in spell factors (rounded down). The optional Time effect works the same way except it uses your Time dots instead of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T09:22:08-07:00","id":1559820,"title":"","content":"Max bonus we can get for most things is 5, but does it stack if its a different bonus. Lets say i wana bust my fighting abilities will it stack if i increase my str by 5, my melee by 5 and to that gain an additional dice bonus of 5 to a total of 15 extra dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T10:10:01-07:00","id":1559821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559820#post1559820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Max bonus we can get for most things is 5, but does it stack if its a different bonus. Lets say i wana bust my fighting abilities will it stack if i increase my str by 5, my melee by 5 and to that gain an additional dice bonus of 5 to a total of 15 extra dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think yes because you are boosting 3 different &quot;things&quot;, considering the generally high defence score of mages and the fact that it uses 3 arcana at minimum level 3 it s not too unbalanced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T11:26:00-07:00","id":1559822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559820#post1559820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Max bonus we can get for most things is 5, but does it stack if its a different bonus. Lets say i wana bust my fighting abilities will it stack if i increase my str by 5, my melee by 5 and to that gain an additional dice bonus of 5 to a total of 15 extra dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you can get your Strength to 10, just costs some reach and mana (and may be obviously magical) actually with enough potency, reach or mana, it seems neither the Mind spell nor the Life spell have any limits.<br /> <br /> +5 seems to be the limit of Monkey's Paw (Gate), but I don't see a limit for Matter...<br /> <br /> So I think a Str 5, Weaponry 5, +5 weapon wouldn't be obviously magical...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-07T18:42:00-07:00","id":1559829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559822#post1559822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+5 seems to be the limit of Monkey's Paw (Gate), but I don't see a limit for Matter...</div> </div> </div> </div>Monkey's Paw has the same caveat as Honing the Form and Augment the Mind, i.e. it's a +1 Reach effect with a Mana cost; it's just worded differently because Equipment Bonus doesn't have a variable maximum like Attribute or Skill ratings. Matter instead runs afoul of the fact that there are no published Matter spells that simply directly adjust the equipment bonus of an existing item, but it's a fairly simple Perfecting effect and the Bonuses/Penalties subsection of the &quot;Determine Effect and Cost&quot; part of the CThaum guidelines is explicit that any spell that grants or increases equipment bonuses (and any spell that simply increases a dice pool) counts as a Trait bonus and going above +5 on an equipment bonus requires a point of Mana.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, does the +2 Equipment Bonus from Astral Grimoire count as a Yantra, or is it a separate bonus like the cumulative bonus from adding ritual casting time intervals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T00:35:58-07:00","id":1559832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559829#post1559829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monkey's Paw has the same caveat as Honing the Form and Augment the Mind, i.e. it's a +1 Reach effect with a Mana cost; it's just worded differently because Equipment Bonus doesn't have a variable maximum like Attribute or Skill ratings. Matter instead runs afoul of the fact that there are no published Matter spells that simply directly adjust the equipment bonus of an existing item, but it's a fairly simple Perfecting effect and the Bonuses/Penalties subsection of the &quot;Determine Effect and Cost&quot; part of the CThaum guidelines is explicit that any spell that grants or increases equipment bonuses (and any spell that simply increases a dice pool) counts as a Trait bonus and going above +5 on an equipment bonus requires a point of Mana.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, does the +2 Equipment Bonus from Astral Grimoire count as a Yantra, or is it a separate bonus like the cumulative bonus from adding ritual casting time intervals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is like the bonus die gived if a Grimoire has an appropriate form related to the inscribed spell (SoS).<br /> Maybe i m wrong but i think that there is a reason if it is described as Equipment bonus without the yantra word","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T01:16:36-07:00","id":1559833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559829#post1559829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of which, does the +2 Equipment Bonus from Astral Grimoire count as a Yantra, or is it a separate bonus like the cumulative bonus from adding ritual casting time intervals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a seperate equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> Looking at the wording, it is different from any Yantra, it seems like it would be inconsistent to use it as a Yantra. Though it is the only equipment bonus I've seen for spell casting. And it seems like it only applies when the Grimoire is within the caster's soul.<br /> <br /> That said, casting from a Grimoire means gaining to rote quality and doubled ritual duration, right? You can't memorize or use the rote mundra as a Yantra while casting from a Grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T01:50:21-07:00","id":1559834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559829#post1559829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, does the +2 Equipment Bonus from Astral Grimoire count as a Yantra, or is it a separate bonus like the cumulative bonus from adding ritual casting time intervals?</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinct is to say it's a mistake. I don't think there are other examples of the yantra system working this way, and it's not noted as being special.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not going to destroy the game, and I think it's an interesting idea to have purely additive yantra, even if it wasn't intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T02:32:07-07:00","id":1559835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559834#post1559834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My instinct is to say it's a mistake. I don't think there are other examples of the yantra system working this way, and it's not noted as being special.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not going to destroy the game, and I think it's an interesting idea to have purely additive yantra, even if it wasn't intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>The unique thing is that this Grimoire is part of your soul... Like memorizing a rote gives certain advantages and a praxis shaping your soul different advantages... This is a weird mix of the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 05-08-2026, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T04:53:23-07:00","id":1559836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559835#post1559835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unique thing is that this Grimoire is part of your soul... Like memorizing a rote gives certain advantages and a praxis shaping your soul different advantages... This is a weird mix of the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning 'special' in the sense of writing style not special in terms of the setting. Like, 2e always uses 'yantra' to refer to bonuses to spellcasting, even though hypothetically you could use 'equipment bonus' and it'd still be understandable if not as precise.<br /> <br /> That said, and having given it more thought, I think I lean towards it being intentional.<br /> <br /> Aside from the bonus from Astral Grimoires, there's also the line on pg.83 of <i>SoS</i> that grimoires of appropriate symbolism give a bonus die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T11:48:04-07:00","id":1559838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559836#post1559836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was meaning 'special' in the sense of writing style not special in terms of the setting. Like, 2e always uses 'yantra' to refer to bonuses to spellcasting, even though hypothetically you could use 'equipment bonus' and it'd still be understandable if not as precise.<br /> <br /> That said, and having given it more thought, I think I lean towards it being intentional.<br /> <br /> Aside from the bonus from Astral Grimoires, there's also the line on pg.83 of <i>SoS</i> that grimoires of appropriate symbolism give a bonus die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not see that; Very interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T21:13:30-07:00","id":1559849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559833#post1559833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, casting from a Grimoire means gaining to rote quality and doubled ritual duration, right? You can't memorize or use the rote mundra as a Yantra while casting from a Grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the first time you have said this and you have still not presented more persuasive evidence than a particular reading of the initial Rotes section, but for the sake of further progressing that discussion it is worth noting that The Sundered World Dark Era has, as part of its mechanics for Neolithic Wise characters, that such characters in a pre-Order world cannot use Rote Mudras to cast Rotes they didn't create themselves <i>without</i> a Grimoire, which at bare minimum suggests you aren't prevented from using Mudras while casting from a Grimoire.<br /> <br /> Slightly less concretely, Signs of Sorcery's section on Rotecraft makes it pretty clear that memorizing a Rote is a matter of arcane muscle memory moreso than anything that would be obviated by casting from a Grimoire, with the Sects' teaching methods being more efficient than less established traditions meaning that learning Rotes the more esoteric way prevents you from fast-casting them; as I've said previously, there's little in the way of intuitive sense in saying that you can benefit from your Survival rating from remembering your training of experiencing through precise patterns of heat and cold over the course of three hours to cast Body Control but you can't do so if you take six hours reading a manual describing that same training you underwent.<br /> <br /> The Grimoire Merit's mechanical description from the corebook likewise only describes the difference between its two uses as &quot;learn the Rote&quot; or &quot;gain the rote quality on casting.&quot; The text is not explicit that you can't gain the Mudra bonus while casting from a Grimoire, only that casting from a Grimoire is the only innate way for a spell to gain the rote quality unless it's a Rote you made yourself (and thus know well enough to be the source of any Grimoires made transcribing it). It is still not clear to me why you insist on this reading that treats adding a character's Skill dots to rolls to cast singular individual spells as mutually exclusive with taking lots of time to cast it with a book or a tablet in front of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T05:09:56-07:00","id":1559852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559849#post1559849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my question, which I think you got side-tracked from, is can you only get the +2 equipment bonus when casting from an Astral Grimoire, thus if you are casting from memory, it doesn't give you the bonus.<br /> <br /> And the downside of casting from a Grimoire (double ritual duration) is still a thing (regardless of what other limits I think the book says there are)<br /> <br /> Ie no instant casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T07:52:46-07:00","id":1559854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559852#post1559852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, my question, which I think you got side-tracked from, is can you only get the +2 equipment bonus when casting from an Astral Grimoire, thus if you are casting from memory, it doesn't give you the bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got sidetracked from the question about the equipment bonus, which is not a Mudra regardless of whether it counts as a Yantra, because you opted to throw in a previously contested interpretation of Mudras in conversation with a person who previously contested that interpretation.<br /> <br /> The Temenos Reach effect describing how it doesn't provide an equipment bonus seems to suggest that yes, the bonus is only when casting from the Grimoire rather than a more general bonus for having it present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the downside of casting from a Grimoire (double ritual duration) is still a thing (regardless of what other limits I think the book says there are)<br /> <br /> Ie no instant casting? </div> </div> </div>Yes, regardless of which variant mechanics are in play it is consistent that casting from a Grimoire requires ritual casting (though there are exemptions to the doubling of the casting time, such as for Grimoires penned in Perfected blood or scribed on Perfected flesh or Grimoires created by a mage with the Cognoscente Merit).<br /> <br /> Thinking on this more\u2026<br /> <br /> The Astral Grimoire equipment bonus only exists for the Awakened subject of the spell who is hosting the Grimoire in their own Oneiros, and specifically is not provided to characters who travel to its Astral representation or summon its Goetia if it is scribed into the Temenos instead. I suppose the case to be made for it being an equipment bonus instead of a Yantra is that, like the &quot;appropriate form&quot; bonus Neos pointed out, Astral Grimoire benefits (at minimum) all the rotes from the Grimoire just from the subject having it in hand, i.e. a secondary effect of becoming the host of an Astral Grimoire is that you in particular can get extra benefits from &quot;physically&quot; having the Grimoire when you cast its spells, which is a benefit of the Astral Grimoire spell rather than Astral Grimoires more generally.<br /> <br /> There might also be a case to be made that since Living Grimoire does not have a similar benefit for Awakened subjects even if the Grimoire is visible, the Astral Grimoire bonus is a Yantra because it's using the symbolism of manifestly possessing a text whose contents you can otherwise reference by virtue of its presence inside your soul, i.e. it's a symbolic boost that you have to go out of your way to benefit from (particularly since summoning the Goetia of the Grimoire from your Oneiros means you lose that part of yourself while it's out), but the mechanics for a Grimoire's form giving a bonus to appropriate spells uses a specific example that directly overlaps with conventional Path and Order Tools (only otherwise differentiated by the lack of restriction to symbolism appropriate to one's Path or Order) and the only symbolism shared between the spells in an Astral Grimoire is that they're in the same single-soul Astral Grimoire.<br /> <br /> Considering the conventional suggested means of repairing the Hitch Condition from creating or modifying a warped Rote (which is only gained by the character for Rotes they've learned) is to enter the character's Oneiros and fixing circumstances with the Goetia of the internalized Rote, there might be something interesting to be gotten out of a mix of Astral Grimoire and the separate Astral representations of Rotes the character has learned from that and other Grimoires.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going diagonal of this subject: am I forgetting any interactions specifically between soul stones and Imbuement or Grimoire creation, or does the published material only have whatever theoretical overlap exists between peripheral phenomena (like using the Goetic Evocation Reach effect and Haunted Grimoire to use an Astral representation of a soul stone's creator to empower a Grimoire)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T03:46:02-07:00","id":1559898,"title":"","content":"A question about Veiling spells.<br /> Let s take Shield of Cronos as an example.<br /> The core spells states that any spell trying to penetrate it must win a Clash of will.<br /> Does the Time active sight detect the spell presence automatically or it requires the clash?<br /> The reach option adds false info and require a clash to pierce the illusion.<br /> Does it changes the conditions to see the spell?<br /> And what effect could trigger the clash? (Active time sight? Focused? A time spell like postcognition? The Prime arcana?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T19:01:16-07:00","id":1559973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559898#post1559898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about Veiling spells.<br /> Let s take Shield of Cronos as an example.<br /> The core spells states that any spell trying to penetrate it must win a Clash of will.<br /> Does the Time active sight detect the spell presence automatically or it requires the clash?</div> </div> </div> </div>Active Time Sight would highlight Shield of Chronos as an ongoing supernatural effect relating to Time. It may require a Clash to use its supplementary effect of detecting when someone is about to act for the purposes of being able to preempt it, depending on how stringently the ST reads Shield of Chronos's ability to prevent &quot;predicting the subject's future,&quot; (since Time Sight doesn't tell you what they're about to do) but the core effect of Shield of Chronos does not do anything except stop its subject from being perceived at any time other than the present and the basic function of Active Time Sight is simply to highlight Time-related phenomena.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reach option adds false info and require a clash to pierce the illusion.<br /> Does it changes the conditions to see the spell?<br /> And what effect could trigger the clash? (Active time sight? Focused? A time spell like postcognition? The Prime arcana?) </div> </div> </div>Active Time Sight is not going to pierce the illusion for the reasons just described \u2014 the very particular overlap Active Mage Sights normally Clash for is if the phenomenon would obfuscate senses the character is using <i>and</i> the Active Sight(s) overlaid on those senses correspond to the principles the phenomenon runs on, and the only information Active Time Sight can give about a Time spell is that it's a temporal effect (barring more particular examples like temporal warping, time travel, and keeping track of Initiative and when people are about to act). By the same token, the Reach effect is not going to stop Active Time Sight from registering that Shield of Chronos is an active Time-related supernatural effect on a subject.<br /> <br /> Focused Mage Sight could, with Scrutiny, glean an understanding of what a given instance of Shield of Chronos is doing, but it runs on the same principles as Active Sight re: whether it triggers a Clash, and the way Focused Sight works means this is functionally a fairly expensive way to go around the need to discern the illusion by simply spending Willpower to go through the process of figuring out what the spell does in its entirety.<br /> <br /> Postcognition does not discern illusions as part of its normal functioning and thus does not trigger a Clash.<br /> <br /> Prime is the most probable culprit for piercing the veil of an advanced Shield of Chronos, via combining spells like Pierce Deception with whatever Time spells are being used to examine a subject's past or future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-15-2026, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T00:39:45-07:00","id":1559984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559973#post1559973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By the same token, the Reach effect is not going to stop Active Time Sight from registering that Shield of Chronos is an active Time-related supernatural effect on a subject.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>About this, we know by Signs of Sorcery that Active sight can recognize previously scrutinized spells.<br /> Considering that Advanced Shield of Chronos use is to fool a Time user, it is strange to me if it is supposed to be visible as such before piercing it with a clash.<br /> <br /> Unless... the narrator keeps the results of clashes hidden, and the function of Advanced Shield of Chronos is to fool a clasher to have pierced it.<br /> Do you think is that so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-15-2026, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T00:59:51-07:00","id":1559985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559973#post1559973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Postcognition does not discern illusions as part of its normal functioning and thus does not trigger a Clash.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>My supposition is that as Postcognition would clash with the basic version of Shield of chronos it would clash with the advanced too.<br /> If it wins it would reveal the true events, but i don t know if it would perceive the concealment attempt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T15:23:35-07:00","id":1559995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559984#post1559984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About this, we know by Signs of Sorcery that Active sight can recognize previously scrutinized spells.<br /> Considering that Advanced Shield of Chronos use is to fool a Time user, it is strange to me if it is supposed to be visible as such before piercing it with a clash.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between recognizing that the past/future of a subject is being falsified and revealing the true events, and the costs and limitations of Active Sight mean a mage may not recognize that there is a need to examine a subject for temporal meddling before examining their past or future \u2014 remember that Peripheral Mage Sight mostly only detects supernatural effects as they become active, not the presence of ongoing supernatural effects more generally, and unlike with spellcasting the only way to bypass the Mana surcharge for including an Arcanum from outside your Path in your Sight is to gain it as an extra Ruling Arcanum, so most non-Acanthus have to think about whether they want to spend Mana to check for Time-related tampering in this way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless... the narrator keeps the results of clashes hidden, and the function of Advanced Shield of Chronos is to fool a clasher to have pierced it.<br /> Do you think is that so? </div> </div> </div>While there's some ambiguity in the phrasing of the Reach effect, it's worth remembering that Shield of Chronos in both usages is not affecting a casual mode of perception \u2014 a case can be made that the advanced version of the spell is forgoing the normal Clash to falsify the subject's timeline, which offloads the point of contradiction with other powers to &quot;a false vision is being presented.&quot;<br /> <br /> My supposition is mainly that &quot;the spell now has two separate chances to Clash as a way of faking out inquisitive postcognitives&quot; is a <i>more complicated</i> effect than simply changing the main application of the spell's Practice in a related way separate from the root spell, which is not even an especially uncommon category of Reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T16:13:11-07:00","id":1559997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1559995#post1559995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between recognizing that the past/future of a subject is being falsified and revealing the true events, and the costs and limitations of Active Sight mean a mage may not recognize that there is a need to examine a subject for temporal meddling before examining their past or future \u2014 remember that Peripheral Mage Sight mostly only detects supernatural effects as they become active, not the presence of ongoing supernatural effects more generally, and unlike with spellcasting the only way to bypass the Mana surcharge for including an Arcanum from outside your Path in your Sight is to gain it as an extra Ruling Arcanum, so most non-Acanthus have to think about whether they want to spend Mana to check for Time-related tampering in this way.<br /> <br /> While there's some ambiguity in the phrasing of the Reach effect, it's worth remembering that Shield of Chronos in both usages is not affecting a casual mode of perception \u2014 a case can be made that the advanced version of the spell is forgoing the normal Clash to falsify the subject's timeline, which offloads the point of contradiction with other powers to &quot;a false vision is being presented.&quot;<br /> <br /> My supposition is mainly that &quot;the spell now has two separate chances to Clash as a way of faking out inquisitive postcognitives&quot; is a <i>more complicated</i> effect than simply changing the main application of the spell's Practice in a related way separate from the root spell, which is not even an especially uncommon category of Reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, i phrased it badly.<br /> I agree with the spell only giving one type of clash at a time.<br /> What i m saying is that even if the Postcognition caster can recognize Shield of chronos by Active sight, if he doesn t know the result of the clash he will never know for sure if what he sees is true.<br /> <br /> So Advanced Shield of chronos, even if visible, is still a useful tool to instill doubt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-26T03:55:52-07:00","id":1560226,"title":"","content":"Beast plater guide states:<br /> &quot;Beasts who explore Kinship with other supernatural beings quickly learn that the Begotten experience of the Primordial Dream is not universal. Mages (perhaps the most likely kin found exploring the dreamscape) navigate almost as though using a Burrow no matter where they go, appearing and disappearing as they hop from scene to scene along thematic or symbolic lines.&quot;<br /> <br /> This passage confounds me<br /> Does that means that Mages traveling alone can only visit Chambers and not the Primordial landscape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-26T04:00:55-07:00","id":1560227,"title":"","content":"Also, is the cliff with the entrance of the Cave simply the &quot;rear&quot; of the Omphalos stone from the Beast perspective?<br /> Or it is another similar place without the Swath or Spire layers to access Anima mundi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-26T18:00:28-07:00","id":1560229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560226#post1560226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast plater guide states:<br /> &quot;Beasts who explore Kinship with other supernatural beings quickly learn that the Begotten experience of the Primordial Dream is not universal. Mages (perhaps the most likely kin found exploring the dreamscape) navigate almost as though using a Burrow no matter where they go, appearing and disappearing as they hop from scene to scene along thematic or symbolic lines.&quot;<br /> <br /> This passage confounds me<br /> Does that means that Mages traveling alone can only visit Chambers and not the Primordial landscape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chambers represent the most likely place a mage will transition through on their way between Temenos realms of a less prosaic sort, but any dream-logic shift along the axis of a material geographic location could see one of the Awakened come across one of the Begotten in the dreamscape along the way.<br /> <br /> The passage is essentially saying that the way mages navigate the Astral doesn't normally have any engagement with the contiguous landscape of the Dark Dream, much like Beasts who only leave their Chambers through Burrows and Primordial Pathways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560227#post1560227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is the cliff with the entrance of the Cave simply the &quot;rear&quot; of the Omphalos stone from the Beast perspective?<br /> Or it is another similar place without the Swath or Spire layers to access Anima mundi?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mists and the Cave are the Begotten perspective of the Omphalos, which is itself just the Awakened(/human occultist) perspective on the interface between the soul of humanity and the soul of the world.<br /> <br /> The Anthropic Redoubts exist in Mage's view of the Astral as places for mysteries about past attempts to claim the power of the gods, modern consequences of mankind's acts of blindness upon the world, etc. A view of the Astral in which you begin to approach the soul of the world by navigating toward places where humanity's impact is reduced doesn't have any place in that layer of the soul for a refuge for humanity and its mark upon the world beyond the Cave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-27T07:18:35-07:00","id":1560232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560229#post1560229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chambers represent the most likely place a mage will transition through on their way between Temenos realms of a less prosaic sort, but any dream-logic shift along the axis of a material geographic location could see one of the Awakened come across one of the Begotten in the dreamscape along the way.<br /> <br /> The passage is essentially saying that the way mages navigate the Astral doesn't normally have any engagement with the contiguous landscape of the Dark Dream, much like Beasts who only leave their Chambers through Burrows and Primordial Pathways.<br /> <br /> The Mists and the Cave are the Begotten perspective of the Omphalos, which is itself just the Awakened(/human occultist) perspective on the interface between the soul of humanity and the soul of the world.<br /> <br /> The Anthropic Redoubts exist in Mage's view of the Astral as places for mysteries about past attempts to claim the power of the gods, modern consequences of mankind's acts of blindness upon the world, etc. A view of the Astral in which you begin to approach the soul of the world by navigating toward places where humanity's impact is reduced doesn't have any place in that layer of the soul for a refuge for humanity and its mark upon the world beyond the Cave.</div> </div> </div> </div>But on the other hand, if i understand it rightly, Beasts experience the Bright dream the same way as mages (using symbolical connection to travel between realms), right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 05-27-2026, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-27T07:25:10-07:00","id":1560233,"title":"","content":"Also in player guide it states &quot;Once kin enter a Lair, though, they\u2019re forced to use the Burrows like everyone else or leave.&quot;<br /> Does that mean that mages can exit Lairs chamber simply walking away (those without the Sealed exit trait at least)?<br /> Because Beasts core seems to imply that intruders cannot do it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-27T12:10:06-07:00","id":1560234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560232#post1560232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the other hand, if i understand it rightly, Beasts experience the Bright dream the same way as mages (using symbolical connection to travel between realms), right?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that once you've crossed through the Day (or used a Primordial Pathway to move directly to the Temenos) you use the same Wits + Investigation roll with relation-based penalties that Astral Realms describes mages using to navigate the Temenos, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560233#post1560233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in player guide it states &quot;Once kin enter a Lair, though, they\u2019re forced to use the Burrows like everyone else or leave.&quot;<br /> Does that mean that mages can exit Lairs chamber simply walking away (those without the Sealed exit trait at least)?<br /> Because Beasts core seems to imply that intruders cannot do it</div> </div> </div> </div>It's saying that inside of a Lair mages cannot travel to other realms like they could in the Bright Dream. Beast Core says that people in the external location of a Chamber with an open Primordial Pathway go further into the Lair if they try to leave; attempt to exit a Chamber that is not currently being overlapped with the outside world go to the appropriate point in the dreamscape instead, at which point mages may use normal Bright navigation methods.<br /> <br /> Burrows may be thought of as the Begotten's human heritage influencing the plasticity of their Lairs, particularly when contrasted with the lockout on Temenos-style navigation in a Lair rhyming with the inability to use shortcuts in the Mother's Land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T14:03:56-07:00","id":1560292,"title":"","content":"I keep getting the same problem again and again. Can someone describe me the clear difference between compeling, ruling and weaving practices? I constantly find that the examples in the game clash with the practices descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T14:20:03-07:00","id":1560293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560292#post1560292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep getting the same problem again and again. Can someone describe me the clear difference between compeling, ruling and weaving practices? I constantly find that the examples in the game clash with the practices descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The baseline effects of Compelling spells tend to be relatively subtle nudges to existing phenomena, making things that could have happened normally happen with certainty. Ruling spells are generally more overt but still within the realm of normal possibility. Weaving gets into the sphere of the vastly unlikely to impossible and encompasses more effects than just manipulating the environment.<br /> <br /> Tome of the Mysteries from 1e goes over the Practices in some detail in its first chapter, if you want more discussion of them than the abbreviated blurbs 2e could fit into the corebook, but a decent shorthand that doesn't require referencing the previous edition may be to look at it in terms of Legacy Attainment construction: it's easier to make reliable outward qualities out of subtler effects with lower Reach, and Compelling spells serve as the lower bound for subtlety in Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> Another metric that may be useful is to remember that Proximus Blessings are limited to three-dot spells at most, or that Influence switches descriptive focus entirely at the fourth dot \u2014 you can break Compelling, Ruling, and Weaving down into Minor, Moderate, and Major Manipulations of [Phenomenon], with the first dot being particularly biased toward tipping the scales for an event that might or might not happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T14:32:30-07:00","id":1560294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560293#post1560293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The baseline effects of Compelling spells tend to be relatively subtle nudges to existing phenomena, making things that could have happened normally happen with certainty. Ruling spells are generally more overt but still within the realm of normal possibility. Weaving gets into the sphere of the vastly unlikely to impossible and encompasses more effects than just manipulating the environment.<br /> <br /> Tome of the Mysteries from 1e goes over the Practices in some detail in its first chapter, if you want more discussion of them than the abbreviated blurbs 2e could fit into the corebook, but a decent shorthand that doesn't require referencing the previous edition may be to look at it in terms of Legacy Attainment construction: it's easier to make reliable outward qualities out of subtler effects with lower Reach, and Compelling spells serve as the lower bound for subtlety in Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> Another metric that may be useful is to remember that Proximus Blessings are limited to three-dot spells at most, or that Influence switches descriptive focus entirely at the fourth dot \u2014 you can break Compelling, Ruling, and Weaving down into Minor, Moderate, and Major Manipulations of [Phenomenon], with the first dot being particularly biased toward tipping the scales for an event that might or might not happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is contradictory to for example making things go magnetic with firs dot of matter or making darkness with first dot of death. Thats not something that normaly could have happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-01T00:55:50-07:00","id":1560301,"title":"","content":"Weaving is very different, I think.<br /> <br /> Weaving and Patterning share a lot. Where Patterning let's you transform a thing completely, weaving let's you alter it's pattern in a more limited way. <br /> <br /> So I think Weaving would let you give fire the features of any type of fire. Patterning let's you transform fire entirely into sound or kinetic force. Ruling is making things do stuff without altering them.<br /> <br /> So fire can be ruled to spread or extinguish - but those are things that fire does under the right circumstances anyway. You just rule them to happen. It doesn't have the right circumstances, but it is still fire being fire.<br /> <br /> The more difficult ones go figure out are like &quot;what is normal for mana or essence to do&quot; and &quot;what is weaving a new feature into these things...&quot; <br /> <br /> Makes me wonder actually, Why is Eidolon not Patterning? If you safe taking mana and giving it a pattern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T07:51:54-07:00","id":1560308,"title":"","content":"1. What is in this case considered sublte and pissble for space time and prime?<br /> 2. Is there a consensus how the bonus for spellcasting for exceptional luck should work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T10:40:34-07:00","id":1560312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560308#post1560308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What is in this case considered sublte and pissble for space time and prime?<br /> 2. Is there a consensus how the bonus for spellcasting for exceptional luck should work?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Do you mean examples of Compelling spells? <br /> <br /> <br /> 2. I don't know, but I believe the books allowing 9-again/8-again should be allowed (as per page 134) to apply to spell casting, while the other boons should not.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T14:30:17-07:00","id":1560315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560312#post1560312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Do you mean examples of Compelling spells?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>and ruling. Not examples, more like whats normal for this sphere of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-02T19:49:56-07:00","id":1560317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560315#post1560315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and ruling. Not examples, more like whats normal for this sphere of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason there were no core Compelling spells for Time and Space in 1e, but again, the example spells we have in 2e paint a certain picture when examined in their basic state rather than with Reach effects or other significant upscaling. Ground-Eater lasts for a turn and adds 1-5 to a Trait that the average person has rated at 9-10. Green Light/Red Light wiggles microdelays around to produce an effect that is largely just narrative and within the realm of possibility. Isolation makes someone <i>feel</i> more distant from the people around them. Tiny adjustments to the real or perceived passage of time or arrangement of space can be managed with Compelling, which is why the example tilt toward convenient timing and psychological tampering.<br /> <br /> Compare the likes of Borrow Threads or Scrying or Break Boundary, which mess with spatial connections and the ability to move in more obvious ways which nevertheless are not changing things about the space or connection that they're bypassing or reorienting, or Choose the Thread and Tipping the Hourglass, which extend foresight to the level of doubling the subject's chances of success or failure and alter a character's place in time enough to change their Initiative order without making them actually move faster or travel back in time, respectively. Ruling spells can meddle with the frame of reality in more overt ways, but most of the effects you can pull off with the Practice are still perceptual or situational rather than enduring aberrations in the world, because they're working through much more ephemeral mediums than rocks or bugs or fire.<br /> <br /> The core effects of Ruling spells can be overt in ways that Compelling spells aren't while still being less drastic than those of the Disciple-level practices, which are where the likes of Shifting Sands and Co-Location and Ban and Temporal Summoning live. Weaving spells occupy the same tier of Practice as the Fraying/Perfecting duality by escalating from &quot;manipulation&quot; to &quot;alteration&quot; \u2014 it's the difference between making a fish swim towards a lure, making it jump out of the water, and making it sprout wings and fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T10:24:08-07:00","id":1560550,"title":"","content":"I m devising the fifth attainment of a lagacy.<br /> The core theme is that the mage creates artificial Qi lines in an area, affecting items, places and creatures.<br /> My doubt is, would it be too much an Optional Matter 5 - Life 5 effect that boosts Healing and growth, Crafting and mitigates Environmental tilts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T14:19:16-07:00","id":1560559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560550#post1560550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m devising the fifth attainment of a lagacy.<br /> The core theme is that the mage creates artificial Qi lines in an area, affecting items, places and creatures.<br /> My doubt is, would it be too much an Optional Matter 5 - Life 5 effect that boosts Healing and growth, Crafting and mitigates Environmental tilts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be loading the plate a bit much. What does the primary effect do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T22:37:58-07:00","id":1560570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560559#post1560559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be loading the plate a bit much. What does the primary effect do?</div> </div> </div> </div>A life 5 that boosts attributes (honing the form)<br /> I was thinking, there are examples of Legacy Attainments composed of different spells, so maybe it would be more balanced if only one of the 3 effect can be applied per casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 06-12-2026, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T02:27:53-07:00","id":1560576,"title":"","content":"I think legacies tend to be fairly limited, but the option to have heresies - ie different legacy members develop different capstone attainments.<br /> <br /> I feel like the soul shaping/philosophy behind a legacy require a clear choice. And it would be one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T02:35:16-07:00","id":1560577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560576#post1560576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think legacies tend to be fairly limited, but the option to have heresies - ie different legacy members develop different capstone attainments.<br /> <br /> I feel like the soul shaping/philosophy behind a legacy require a clear choice. And it would be one or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but the Eleventh question fifth optional attainment allows to use both \u201cEx Nihilo\u201d or \u201cAnnihilate Matter\u201d, that s what i meant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T04:29:45-07:00","id":1560578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560550#post1560550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m devising the fifth attainment of a lagacy.<br /> The core theme is that the mage creates artificial Qi lines in an area, affecting items, places and creatures.<br /> My doubt is, would it be too much an Optional Matter 5 - Life 5 effect that boosts Healing and growth, Crafting and mitigates Environmental tilts?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use a Perfecting of Prime to increase the benefits of a Node described on page 242. The befits extend to the radius of the spell, they add [Potency] to any rolls or bonuses related to harnessing its Resonance (such as the Life, Space or Time effects) and they half the time of related effects for each level of Potency (such as the Matter effect). Highly specific to a Node's area, but captures the spirit of what you want. <br /> <br /> So now you just need to give someone <i>Sacred Geometry</i> and they can benefit from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T04:44:58-07:00","id":1560579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560578#post1560578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could use a Perfecting of Prime to increase the benefits of a Node described on page 242. The befits extend to the radius of the spell, they add [Potency] to any rolls or bonuses related to harnessing its Resonance (such as the Life, Space or Time effects) and they half the time of related effects for each level of Potency (such as the Matter effect). Highly specific to a Node's area, but captures the spirit of what you want.<br /> <br /> So now you just need to give someone <i>Sacred Geometry</i> and they can benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would work, but the legacy is based on primary life and optional matter.<br /> Maybe it s possible to create something similar, like a reverse of Salt the earth with a conjunctional matter to add something relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T05:17:06-07:00","id":1560580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560579#post1560579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would work, but the legacy is based on primary life and optional matter.<br /> Maybe it s possible to create something similar, like a reverse of Salt the earth with a conjunctional matter to add something relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a version of <i>Contagion </i>or <i>Create Life</i>? Make a bioorganic construct, which costs a mana to create, that repairs [Potency] health to any living beings and inorganic matter every Gnosis based intervals and grants a bonus of [Potency] to any Medicine rolls on an infected subject. Think of them like the canoptek scarabs from 40k, but not deadly. You could add <i>Permanence </i>for advanced duration, and then you could just have them stay in the area or organism they were deployed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T05:29:32-07:00","id":1560581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560580#post1560580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe a version of <i>Contagion </i>or <i>Create Life</i>? Make a bioorganic construct, which costs a mana to create, that repairs [Potency] health to any living beings and inorganic matter every Gnosis based intervals and grants a bonus of [Potency] to any Medicine rolls on an infected subject. Think of them like the canoptek scarabs from 40k, but not deadly. You could add <i>Permanence </i>for advanced duration, and then you could just have them stay in the area or organism they were deployed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is good, but i was more inclined to create some sort of blessing in the area, like better crops and tools.<br /> The apex of the legacy aims to bring prosperity like the way in theory feng shui is supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T00:26:00-07:00","id":1560669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560581#post1560581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is good, but i was more inclined to create some sort of blessing in the area, like better crops and tools.<br /> The apex of the legacy aims to bring prosperity like the way in theory feng shui is supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ve tought about this, do you think it would be ok a life 5 matter 5 spell that boosts the Resources merit of everyone in an area by creating a &quot;living&quot; territory that empowers the results of their labor (better crops, better crafting, natural resource renews faster and extraction is easier, ecc) ?<br /> Or is it not enough for a spell so complex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T06:35:28-07:00","id":1560674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560669#post1560669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ve tought about this, do you think it would be ok a life 5 matter 5 spell that boosts the Resources merit of everyone in an area by creating a &quot;living&quot; territory that empowers the results of their labor (better crops, better crafting, natural resource renews faster and extraction is easier, ecc) ?<br /> Or is it not enough for a spell so complex?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to substantially depend on other things, like &quot;what Practice is this Attainment emulating [and therefore what base Arcanum rating]?&quot; and &quot;what Reach effects are being applied [mainly Area and Duration]?&quot;<br /> <br /> You could certainly do worse than side-porting the temporary Merit effect of Shifting the Odds and/or making use of Crucible for flatly raising the Availability of things to represent heightened monetary value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T06:38:44-07:00","id":1560675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560669#post1560669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ve tought about this, do you think it would be ok a life 5 matter 5 spell that boosts the Resources merit of everyone in an area by creating a &quot;living&quot; territory that empowers the results of their labor (better crops, better crafting, natural resource renews faster and extraction is easier, ecc) ?<br /> Or is it not enough for a spell so complex?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably expand on the <i>Crucible</i> spell. Reach is assigned to instant use, advanced scale, increasing Availability by Potency and granting rechargeable rote quality. A single point of mana pays for <i>Permanence</i> and rechargeable rote quality, per Legacy rules. With conjunctional Life 3, it can also affect organic substances (food, poisons, etc), which you would need to figure out what it means rules wise. <br /> <br /> So now everything works better, is higher quality and more valuable within. Conduct the ritual once in a while, spend the mana and the land will yield a greater bounty. If you do your job right, people will use it to catapult the area to unprecedented prosperity. If you do your job wrong, they grow complacent and dependent on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T09:02:14-07:00","id":1560678,"title":"","content":"The crucible approach is interesting.<br /> I ll probably use Permanence and the 3 reach on switching to duration primary, scale, and one of the two spell special reach option.<br /> About the added life effect... maybe everyone who eats the subjected food gains Potency level of the Hardy level?<br /> This, plus the bonus on the drug tools of a physician could boost the general health and growth level.<br /> Or maybe plant and animals (and people) could gain a boost in fertility and &quot;production&quot; (more fruits, more milk, ecc..)<br /> Or, simply adding the effect of Honing the form would be too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T10:34:58-07:00","id":1560680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560678#post1560678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The crucible approach is interesting.<br /> I ll probably use Permanence and the 3 reach on switching to duration primary, scale, and one of the two spell special reach option.<br /> About the added life effect... maybe everyone who eats the subjected food gains Potency level of the Hardy level?<br /> This, plus the bonus on the drug tools of a physician could boost the general health and growth level.<br /> Or maybe plant and animals (and people) could gain a boost in fertility and &quot;production&quot; (more fruits, more milk, ecc..)<br /> Or, simply adding the effect of Honing the form would be too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without seeing the rest of the Legacy I worry that this might be trying to do too much for an Attainment, particularly given that I don't entirely believe Afini's reading of Reach-saving Utility Attainments being applicable to Legacy Attainments is intended (particularly given that Permanence has its limitations for a clear reason.<br /> <br /> Since this is kind of getting out of the scope of &quot;simple questions,&quot; it may be helpful to create a thread for the Legacy to lay out the goals and existing structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T11:36:08-07:00","id":1560681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560680#post1560680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without seeing the rest of the Legacy I worry that this might be trying to do too much for an Attainment, particularly given that I don't entirely believe Afini's reading of Reach-saving Utility Attainments being applicable to Legacy Attainments is intended (particularly given that Permanence has its limitations for a clear reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying you think Permanace should only be usable with spells? Or that all Arcanum attainments (like conditional duration) should be assumed to not apply to legacy attainments? I'm confused by the &quot;has its limitations for as clear reason&quot; part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T12:12:15-07:00","id":1560682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560681#post1560681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying you think Permanace should only be usable with spells? Or that all Arcanum attainments (like conditional duration) should be assumed to not apply to legacy attainments? I'm confused by the &quot;has its limitations for as clear reason&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanence only applies to spells that have Matter as their highest Arcanum because it's meant to make spells dealing with inanimate objects easier to have last longer, which is of dubious applicability with spells like, say, Life-variant Wonderful Machine cast on animals, much less something more esoteric like the described &quot;artificial qi lines&quot; whose entire deal is very clearly not casting a spell on an object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T04:08:14-07:00","id":1560777,"title":"","content":"The current Archigenitor Exarchs are associated with the numbers 1 through 4. Are the other Exarchs associated with other specific numbers?<br /> Obviously the Chancellor is the Queen of Numbers but I couldn't name one in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T07:56:04-07:00","id":1560783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560777#post1560777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current Archigenitor Exarchs are associated with the numbers 1 through 4. Are the other Exarchs associated with other specific numbers? Obviously the Chancellor is the Queen of Numbers but I couldn't name one in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess it depends who you are. Standard Seer doctrine is that the Archigenitors are eternal (untrue as that is); therefore to assign the Chancellor a number outside the four would perhaps be to admit that they're not one of them.<br /> <br /> Then again, the numbers aren't obviously related to position in a hierarchy as much as ideology.<br /> <br /> If the Chancellor is the 'Queen of Numbers', then maybe '10' would be appropriate given that's the number of numerals there are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T08:44:01-07:00","id":1560784,"title":"","content":"I would find it odd and kind of inconsistent with what numerology even is if the Archigenitors were the only Exarchs with associated numbers. I think the fact that the current set has one through four can easily just be read as coincidence.<br /> <br /> I would agree that 10 seems like a fitting one to associate with the Chancellor, having connotations of having the whole pot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T09:44:19-07:00","id":1560785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560784#post1560784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the fact that the current set has one through four can easily just be read as coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it feels odd to just have 4 slots, but once you start putting things down to coincidence you start undermining the entire enterprise of numerology. Also, it's so neat numerically, that it'd be odd to ignore it.<br /> <br /> I could see the book as maybe describing a standardised numerology, (quite possibly originating with Hegemony hence partly why they get number 1 spot) where the individual ministries develop their own private numerologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T18:09:31-07:00","id":1560798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560785#post1560785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree it feels odd to just have 4 slots</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a thing that I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">quite possibly originating with Hegemony hence partly why they get number 1 spot)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the number one necessarily has much value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">where the individual ministries develop their own private numerologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would regard that as a premise that gets overcomplicated and rather silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T22:52:10-07:00","id":1560806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560777#post1560777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current Archigenitor Exarchs are associated with the numbers 1 through 4. Are the other Exarchs associated with other specific numbers?<br /> Obviously the Chancellor is the Queen of Numbers but I couldn't name one in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The number of the Archigenitors seem consistent with Hermetic numerology:<br /> <br /> 1 - The Monad, the everything, the Unity<br /> 2 - Antagonism, separation, the General<br /> 3 - The trinity, building on the symbolism of the Father<br /> 4- Visible nature, the four corners of the world, aka Space, the Eye<br /> <br /> Perhaps the other numbers could be deduced based on it.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T09:01:56-07:00","id":1560817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1560806#post1560806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of the Archigenitors seem consistent with Hermetic numerology:<br /> <br /> 1 - The Monad, the everything, the Unity<br /> 2 - Antagonism, separation, the General<br /> 3 - The trinity, building on the symbolism of the Father<br /> 4- Visible nature, the four corners of the world, aka Space, the Eye<br /> <br /> Perhaps the other numbers could be deduced based on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big trouble there is that, from the admittedly limited resources I looked at, even 5-7 alone seem to have focal connotations that are in some ways opposite to the Exarchs, and the Prophet and the Ruin specifically have the odd syzygy of focusing on methods of control that seem more appropriate to each other's Arcanum. Still, offhand\u2026<br /> <br /> 5 - Change, unpredictability, the journey through the senses, the Raptor<br /> 6 - Equilibrium, the bridge between the microcosm and the macrocosm, the Nemesis<br /> 7 - Cycles of the universe, aka Fate, the Ruin<br /> 8 - Infinity and cause and effect, aka Time, the Prophet<br /> 9 - Foundation, completion, the cusp of a new beginning, the Psychopomp<br /> 10 - End state, new baseline, the physical kingdom in the Tree of Life, the Chancellor<br /> <br /> Some of these are just derived from what the m.o. of the Exarch in question corrupts, and I won't pretend there isn't also a simplistic reason for assigning all of them except 5 (which is in some ways given to the Raptor by process of elimination).<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that the Seers' standpoint on who the Archigenitors are is part of the larger fact that the contents of the Supernal as we encounter it from the perspective of non-transcendent beings are only ever eternal at any given moment and the Exarchs in particular are fairly unstable magical identities when it comes to existing on their own \u2014 they don't do what the other Sects have done and shore up the Primal symbolism of the Ministries that serve them, they basically consume their Ministers, and regardless of how effective it is, their servants' primary means of discerning their will without direct orders is to use nonmagical fortunetelling and other methods indistinguishable from superstition, and those same servants take it as an article of selfish faith that their service will be rewarded by Ascension to the ranks of lesser Exarchs.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say that the numerology of the Archigenitors and the Iron Seals exists for the Seers, who are mages who can leverage any symbolism they can recognize, and whose Order-Tools-cum-Patron-Tools just need to invoke the Exarch in question, which is likely going to be a little more overt than e.g. putting an eye on a square to scry on somebody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T15:24:02-07:00","id":1560834,"title":"","content":"Thank you, very helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T11:23:30-07:00","id":1561081,"title":"","content":"Exceptional luck.... again<br /> In the general hex section on the imposing dice penalty it says that for 2 reach it can work for spellcasting rolls and other suppernatural effects. Is this a mistake or correct? Im contiinuing my former question on the topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T12:55:39-07:00","id":1561083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561081#post1561081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional luck.... again<br /> In the general hex section on the imposing dice penalty it says that for 2 reach it can work for spellcasting rolls and other suppernatural effects. Is this a mistake or correct? Im contiinuing my former question on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is consistent on this, yes. Regardless of any ambiguity on the breadth of applicable boon or hex effects for supernatural powers, it is unambiguous that penalties and 9-Again/8-Again can be applied to spellcasting rolls with extra Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T14:04:34-07:00","id":1561090,"title":"","content":"I see. How strict o you make rotes? lets say there is a rote to increase an attribute, Do you require the rote should specify the attribute or can it be used to increase/ descrease anny possible attribute (with the sphere)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T15:33:47-07:00","id":1561092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561090#post1561090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. How strict o you make rotes? lets say there is a rote to increase an attribute, Do you require the rote should specify the attribute or can it be used to increase/ descrease anny possible attribute (with the sphere)</div> </div> </div> </div>As listed, the example spells are assumed to be things you can use as rotes (with the recommended rote mundras) so a Mind spell to increase either a mental or social attribute, or a Life spell to increase any physical attribute is one spell to learn as a rote (either of them would be a single rote...).<br /> <br /> It is a bit of a vague thing for Creative Thaumaturgy, but if you're players are making their own rotes, lest them do whatever you would let them do with a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T16:43:27-07:00","id":1561093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561090#post1561090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. How strict o you make rotes? lets say there is a rote to increase an attribute, Do you require the rote should specify the attribute or can it be used to increase/ descrease anny possible attribute (with the sphere)</div> </div> </div> </div>As orathaic says above. Unless you are running a specific case of a Master only encoding enough of the rote's symbolism to accomplish a specific effect more limited than a published spell that effect would fall under, a normal rote works like the spell it's codifying with the extra advantages of being a rote. There's precedent for rotes having unusual limitations or extra effects, but by default the spell is the spell and knowing a rote of it only adds to your ability to use it effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T07:43:49-07:00","id":1561136,"title":"","content":"The strictest idea I have about rotes is that some Abilities for the yantra are a bit more obscure than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T15:12:26-07:00","id":1561204,"title":"","content":"<i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> says Briareus was the first to invent Masques in the Foundation Age. However, King Solomon was a Guardian wearing the Masque of the Adamant Judge in the Scholastic Age. Does that mean that Masques existed before Briareus as niche or informal knowledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T16:13:13-07:00","id":1561207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561204#post1561204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> says Briareus was the first to invent Masques in the Foundation Age. However, King Solomon was a Guardian wearing the Masque of the Adamant Judge in the Scholastic Age. Does that mean that Masques existed before Briareus as niche or informal knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That same section is pretty clear that the bit about Solomon is future characters claiming a historical figure as a precedent, because in the same sentence it says the Silver Ladder does the same thing. This is derived from the Guardians' Order book identifying him as a legendary example of that Masque, and Masques are archetypal personas.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be outside of possibility for the Guardians' signature technique to have historical precedents, but that's pretty definitely not what the timeline is concretely saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T01:22:38-07:00","id":1561219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561204#post1561204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> says Briareus was the first to invent Masques in the Foundation Age. However, King Solomon was a Guardian wearing the Masque of the Adamant Judge in the Scholastic Age. Does that mean that Masques existed before Briareus as niche or informal knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the sentence doesn't make sense without that implication. Though, i think it's a carryover from the original released version which was explicit about Solomon being a Guardian of the Veil, hence his using the Adamant Judge Masque. The writers edited the direct reference out, but left the indirect reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T06:53:38-07:00","id":1561381,"title":"","content":"Question about the Forces Arcanum.<br /> Why is it that each type of Force is its own spell, but Matter has basically a &quot;free for all matter&quot; spell? Example: If you want to manipulate water, air, sand, clay, chlorine gas, you have the Shaping spell. If you want to do the same to fire, electricity, heat, radiation, each has its own different spell... Could it not be all combined in an Influence Energy/Control Energy/Bolster Energy/Transform Energy/Create Energy spell (yes, I know the last two already exist, my point precisely)?<br /> This because creating a Legacy around the elements becomes very trying, since Matter can shape all but fire (well, you can alter the flow of fuel and comburant, but you get my drift) and then you're forced to stick to Command Fire and leave behind the also fun Command Heat and Command Electricity spells, because they're not in one simple spell.<br /> And I could've been persuaded to accept it because fire, electricity, heat, etc. are all different purviews for Forces, but solids, liquids and gases are also different purviews for Matter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T10:56:04-07:00","id":1561387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561381#post1561381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Forces Arcanum.<br /> Why is it that each type of Force is its own spell, but Matter has basically a &quot;free for all matter&quot; spell? Example: If you want to manipulate water, air, sand, clay, chlorine gas, you have the Shaping spell. If you want to do the same to fire, electricity, heat, radiation, each has its own different spell... Could it not be all combined in an Influence Energy/Control Energy/Bolster Energy/Transform Energy/Create Energy spell (yes, I know the last two already exist, my point precisely)?<br /> This because creating a Legacy around the elements becomes very trying, since Matter can shape all but fire (well, you can alter the flow of fuel and comburant, but you get my drift) and then you're forced to stick to Command Fire and leave behind the also fun Command Heat and Command Electricity spells, because they're not in one simple spell.<br /> And I could've been persuaded to accept it because fire, electricity, heat, etc. are all different purviews for Forces, but solids, liquids and gases are also different purviews for Matter...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think mostly because the rules for how those forces work and how they are interacted with are fairly different from one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T09:48:18-07:00","id":1561420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561387#post1561387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think mostly because the rules for how those forces work and how they are interacted with are fairly different from one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the complexity of writing rules when electrocution and being set on fire have different mechanics for when you use them in combat.<br /> <br /> That said, you can CT a legacy attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T11:19:05-07:00","id":1561422,"title":"","content":"Where the Ministry of Mammon rote skills are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T13:42:44-07:00","id":1561431,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> I don't think we're ever told. Dave Brookshaw might have said on here what he intended them to have at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T09:00:42-07:00","id":1561470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561422#post1561422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the Ministry of Mammon rote skills are?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\">I would imagine they would be:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><b>Persuasion</b>- Marketing sows the seeds for a harvest of wealth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><b>Politics</b> - When greed becomes law, transactions becomes worship.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><b>Subterfuge</b> - Sell them what they want, price it as what they need.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T07:42:40-07:00","id":1561767,"title":"","content":"When casting a knowing spell, do i need to consider a minimum of two subjects (the one scanned and the one receiving the informations)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T09:15:20-07:00","id":1561768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1561767#post1561767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When casting a knowing spell, do i need to consider a minimum of two subjects (the one scanned and the one receiving the informations)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intention is that if you're not giving the information to someone other than the caster, the spell only needs to account for the subject whose information is being gleaned. Lesser Tulpas replicating Knowing effects specifically change the way they work, and the parenthetical &quot;or to another target&quot; in the corebook's description of the Practices doesn't suggest the mage needs to be a target of a spell for getting information on something else to get that information. (More to the point, it would be really weird for a spell that any mage can cast with the lowest possible Gnosis and Arcanum ratings to need Reach or penalties to use its most basic application.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T14:50:59-07:00","id":1562059,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a mage to create an undead werewolf in garou form from a werewolfs body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T15:16:38-07:00","id":1562060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562059#post1562059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a mage to create an undead werewolf in garou form from a werewolfs body?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have a corpse in that shape then they can animate that corpse. The corpse is not going to have regeneration or any other supernatural qualities without plot-device-level magic, whether that's archspells or more particular Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T07:50:21-07:00","id":1562082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562060#post1562060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have a corpse in that shape then they can animate that corpse. The corpse is not going to have regeneration or any other supernatural qualities without plot-device-level magic, whether that's archspells or more particular Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do werewolves typically retain their shape after death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T07:55:26-07:00","id":1562083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562082#post1562082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do werewolves typically retain their shape after death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalypse had a &quot;natural form&quot; in which werewolves reverted while unconscious/dead but Forsaken didn t mention anything similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T10:40:25-07:00","id":1562089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562082#post1562082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves typically retain their shape after death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken 1e had an explicit note that werewolves knocked unconscious or killed revert to Hishu (human) form, and while 2e doesn't have that note it does specify that after a werewolf's time in <i>Basu-Im</i> (hard Rage, forced into Gauru/full wolfman form) is over they collapse into Hishu form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T12:20:32-07:00","id":1562092,"title":"","content":"I propose that it would make sense in Second Edition for whether a werewolf reverts to a different form (and which one) or not depends on their Harmony, although even then I'd think the transient nature of Gauru makes that highly uncommon at best to stay in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T00:07:13-07:00","id":1562106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562082#post1562082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do werewolves typically retain their shape after death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the kind of lifestyle they live, retaining their shape would be a gargantuan risk for the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Think about how often they die in the midst of battle. Chances are they weren't in human form when that happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T02:55:32-07:00","id":1562116,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>. It fits with how Harmony works, as well as reinforcing that Uratha aren't just humans who turn into werewolves, they're shapeshifters whose forms are all equally natural to them...<br /> <br /> That said, I also agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> that it's a problem from a world-building perspective, and that returning to human form would so very easily fix it...<br /> <br /> CofD has a much looser approach to Masquerades, but wolf-men turning up at the morgue on the regular seems pushing it a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T12:59:30-07:00","id":1562131,"title":"","content":"Considering that you probably don't want to be leaving human corpses around where the authorities will notice them and try to follow up anyway, I think one can comfortably assume that the Uratha generally clean up after themselves.<br /> <br /> Still, at the same time, Second Edition leans more on an idea that the masquerade is preserved by wilful ignorance as much as by anything else. Just in case it's a situation where a whole pack is wiped out.<br /> <br /> Although on the other hand, packs are also bigger than the werewolves now, so that might also be a thing where the last action of the human and Wolf-blooded support staff is going to reclaim the bodies before others can. <br /> <br /> Even then, I assume these things are typically motivated by the desire for respectful funeral rites more than secrecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T03:17:06-07:00","id":1562176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562131#post1562131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, at the same time, Second Edition leans more on an idea that the masquerade is preserved by wilful ignorance as much as by anything else. Just in case it's a situation where a whole pack is wiped out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that a tad hard to believe, with how large and widespread the Cryptid, UFO and Ghost Hunter communities have shown to be. They hold national conventions for this kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T06:51:40-07:00","id":1562184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562176#post1562176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that a tad hard to believe, with how large and widespread the Cryptid, UFO and Ghost Hunter communities have shown to be. They hold national conventions for this kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those communities are broadly considered to be harmless eccentrics at best, because learning the things they believe in are actually factually real tends to shake the worldview and self-concept of most people brought up in the setting.<br /> <br /> Second Edition's switch from Morality to Integrity as the root human &quot;code&quot; means even nonviolent, nonvisceral expressions of the supernatural risk degrading one's confidence in who they are and what they've learned all their life, which combines with the way Awakening works and the Awakened being the metaphysical 1% to explain where certain elements of mainstream mage society keep their contempt for other people's spiritual integrity in an edition where that's no longer described purely in terms of what crimes they can commit without internal consequence.<br /> <br /> I will add that the lack of explicit &quot;you assume Hishu form when you die&quot; note is supplemented by the fact that this edition also makes Gauru the most expedient way for a werewolf to avoid dying and the most consistent way to enter Hard Rage (locking you into Gauru for what is likely to be at least an appreciable fraction of an hour) is to spend too long in Gauru (like, say, relying on its accelerated regeneration to stave off death in a protracted violent encounter with something that can't be frightened off by the powerful Lunacy pouring off of it). I personally wouldn't assume a werewolf killed in Gauru form stays in Gauru form when their Death Rage is cut short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-26T08:13:47-07:00","id":1562186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562176#post1562176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find that a tad hard to believe, with how large and widespread the Cryptid, UFO and Ghost Hunter communities have shown to be. They hold national conventions for this kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> And in the context of the Chronicles of Darkness, if the majority of them actually encountered that stuff, they would freak the fuck out and have some reaction that would probably alienate them from their communities of harmless weirdos, whether that be wanting to retreat from anything that would remind them of it (keeping in mind that Integrity Breaking Points include things vaguely similar to personal supernatural traumas) or becoming the one person who is way too intense about it in a way that makes everybody else uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> You ever see Buffy the Vampire Slayer? That one episode with the group of vampire wannabes and what happens when they actually meet a vampire? It's like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T04:39:00-07:00","id":1562221,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you need Matter 3 (Hone the Perfected Form) and Life 3 to perfect living materials? Or does Matter on its own suffice?</li> <li>Can perfecting living materials be under the Life Arcana scope on its own?</li> </ol>I ask the first question because the write-up of <i>Hone the Perfected Form </i>makes just for the Matter arcana not needing Life (unless the Storyteller requires it so), and the second question because being under the purview and being special, it might be feasible by using a Life arcana equivalent of <i>Hone the Perfected Form</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p. 62</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">+2 Reach: The spell may Perfect another substance, such<br /> as glass or gemstones (see p. 63.) If the spell also includes<br /> Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, it may Perfect fire.<b> Other, stranger substances<br /> may be Perfected with additional Arcana at the Storyteller\u2019s<br /> discretion.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p. 64</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Organics have a tie to the Supernal giving them a potent<br /> quality on their own, but they can also be Perfected much like<br /> other materials. The problem lies in the fact that the substance<br /> cannot be separated from a person for more than a few minutes<br /> before they become dead, symbolically speaking, and the Per\u00ad<br /> fecting spell results in Perfected bone, leather, or wood. <b>Other</b><br /> <b>substances such as hair and <u>blood</u> don\u2019t have a Perfected form<br /> at all once dead; at least, not one known outside specialist<br /> Legacies. The only way to get <u>Perfected blood</u> or flesh is to cast<br /> Hone the Perfected Form at the exact time of separation of<br /> these substances from a living host</b>, which is an act of hubris<br /> against Falling Wisdom.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-27-2026, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T07:17:54-07:00","id":1562224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562221#post1562221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do you need Matter 3 (Hone the Perfected Form) and Life 3 to perfect living materials? Or does Matter on its own suffice?</li> <li>Can perfecting living materials be under the Life Arcana scope on its own?</li> </ol>I ask the first question because the write-up of <i>Hone the Perfected Form </i>makes just for the Matter arcana not needing Life (unless the Storyteller requires it so), and the second question because being under the purview and being special, it might be feasible by using a Life arcana equivalent of <i>Hone the Perfected Form</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If we disregard the exceptions, like blood or hair, you might be able to do it by casting a Shielding of Life on a transplant organ so it stays in that key moment when it can be perfected, then subject it to the standard process of passes through Twilight while the spell is up. Its slow, its disturbing, but it might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T14:59:44-07:00","id":1562238,"title":"","content":"Lets say a mage is in the spirit realm he is atempting to cast a spell using a sympathetic connection to 4 different people (mages) on the material plane that are not awere he will cast the spell.<br /> So we have a sympatetic potency requirement, the target resistance attribute and the fact the spell is cast between realms. Does the potency requirement add up or should i pick the higest resistance that needs to be beaten with potency?<br /> Also should there be any penalty for casting a spell with sympathetic range on 4 different targets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T16:04:02-07:00","id":1562240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562238#post1562238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage is in the spirit realm he is atempting to cast a spell using a sympathetic connection to 4 different people (mages) on the material plane that are not awere he will cast the spell.<br /> So we have a sympatetic potency requirement, the target resistance attribute and the fact the spell is cast between realms. Does the potency requirement add up or should i pick the higest resistance that needs to be beaten with potency?<br /> Also should there be any penalty for casting a spell with sympathetic range on 4 different targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every extra source of Withstand between you and a target adds +1 to the highest Withstand rating in the way, reducing spell Potency accordingly for that target <br /> <br /> The penalty for casting sympathetically on multiple targets is that you need a sympathy Yantra for all the targets, it doesn't provide a dice bonus when used for the Attainment in that way, and unless you have some unifying factor connecting the targets that means you're limited in how much you can juice the spell with penalties instead of Reach, especially since Advanced Potency doesn't help overcome Withstand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T23:43:36-07:00","id":1562287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562240#post1562240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every extra source of Withstand between you and a target adds +1 to the highest Withstand rating in the way, reducing spell Potency accordingly for that target<br /> <br /> The penalty for casting sympathetically on multiple targets is that you need a sympathy Yantra for all the targets, it doesn't provide a dice bonus when used for the Attainment in that way, and unless you have some unifying factor connecting the targets that means you're limited in how much you can juice the spell with penalties instead of Reach, especially since Advanced Potency doesn't help overcome Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are targeting a group (like all members of a cabal) and they have a clear identity (like a strong Cabal theme) do you need a name or can you target them without know their Sympathetic names? (Regardless of the issue with Yantras)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T05:47:36-07:00","id":1562298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562287#post1562287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are targeting a group (like all members of a cabal) and they have a clear identity (like a strong Cabal theme) do you need a name or can you target them without know their Sympathetic names? (Regardless of the issue with Yantras)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to know who you're targeting regardless of whether they get the extra Withstand from you not knowing their sympathetic name. Magic addressed &quot;to whom it may concern&quot; doesn't go through personal sympathetic channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T07:34:09-07:00","id":1562303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562298#post1562298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to know who you're targeting regardless of whether they get the extra Withstand from you not knowing their sympathetic name. Magic addressed &quot;to whom it may concern&quot; doesn't go through personal sympathetic channels.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can target a Building, or other Area (like your Sanctum) if you have a Sympathetic connection. <br /> <br /> I guess you would have a Sympathetic connection to each member of a Cabal, not the Cabal as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T15:24:37-07:00","id":1562323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562224#post1562224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we disregard the exceptions, like blood or hair, you might be able to do it by casting a Shielding of Life on a transplant organ so it stays in that key moment when it can be perfected, then subject it to the standard process of passes through Twilight while the spell is up. Its slow, its disturbing, but it might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply.<br /> <br /> Based on your idea, what do you think it would happen if you return the body part to the person or animal?<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, you Perfect all the blood from someone, and put it back in the body, will it change the rest of the organs? Will it get degraded?<br /> <br /> If you do the thing you mention, what would happen if you perfect individual organs (liver, kidneys, lungs, spleen, heart, individual bones?, brain?) and reconnect them to the body? Would it make the person/animal immortal?<br /> <br /> Because a fully Perfected body sounds like Archmastery stuff: a very powerful Yantra, if not a Quintessence for Imperial spells.<br /> <br /> I have read the quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p.64</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the best efforts of many<br /> liches, whole life forms (including mages) cannot be turned into<br /> Perfected flesh, only parts carefully excised.</div> </div> </div> </div>But with your idea, nothing makes impossible to go organ by organ, and reattach/rejoin, specially if it is the original organ of the person/animal. There should not be a rejections due being a foreign body, only if being Perfected makes it less usable. And if you go by the blood (and red bone marrow), you get a constant exchange of the Perfected substance with the rest of the body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-29-2026, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T03:45:38-07:00","id":1562339,"title":"","content":"The Spiritual tool spell (SoS) ends with:<br /> If the object is carried into either other realm, it retains its material form when the object returns to the material realm while under the effects of this spell.<br /> <br /> This seems to imply a destruction effect similar to the Ghost gate spell, am i right?<br /> Or i m reading it wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T10:41:44-07:00","id":1562370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562339#post1562339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spiritual tool spell (SoS) ends with:<br /> If the object is carried into either other realm, it retains its material form when the object returns to the material realm while under the effects of this spell.<br /> <br /> This seems to imply a destruction effect similar to the Ghost gate spell, am i right?<br /> Or i m reading it wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes ? But it makes no sense for Spirit, it does not make sense for it to be destroyed. I think it could mean an item that exists only in those realms could me made solid in the material. Think of it as a better version of <i>Touch of the Grave</i>, that applies to different Ephemeral frequencies and preserves the full durability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T10:48:43-07:00","id":1562371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562323#post1562323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the reply.<br /> <br /> Based on your idea, what do you think it would happen if you return the body part to the person or animal?<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, you Perfect all the blood from someone, and put it back in the body, will it change the rest of the organs? Will it get degraded?<br /> <br /> If you do the thing you mention, what would happen if you perfect individual organs (liver, kidneys, lungs, spleen, heart, individual bones?, brain?) and reconnect them to the body? Would it make the person/animal immortal?<br /> <br /> Because a fully Perfected body sounds like Archmastery stuff: a very powerful Yantra, if not a Quintessence for Imperial spells.<br /> <br /> I have read the quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But with your idea, nothing makes impossible to go organ by organ, and reattach/rejoin, specially if it is the original organ of the person/animal. There should not be a rejections due being a foreign body, only if being Perfected makes it less usable. And if you go by the blood (and red bone marrow), you get a constant exchange of the Perfected substance with the rest of the body</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that probably leads to the kind of research that created the Patchwork People immortals, Frankenstein Prometheans and some variations of Renegades. I could also see a Sleepwalker using the notes to jury rig a lesser version of it, becoming a Blood Bather so they can hopefully gain enough time for the Watchtowers to Awaken them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T16:48:12-07:00","id":1562594,"title":"","content":"<i>Acceleration</i> can halve extended action time per level of Potency. <i>Body Control </i>can half or quarter healing times. <i>Good Time Management</i> could arguably be granted with a Ruling of Mind. So could you make a Ruling of Mind to half the time of mental and social extended research actions for each level of Potency ? Essentially making you very efficient at parsing data.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-03-2026, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T12:08:00-07:00","id":1562783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562594#post1562594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Acceleration</i> can halve extended action time per level of Potency. <i>Body Control </i>can half or quarter healing times. <i>Good Time Management</i> could arguably be granted with a Ruling of Mind. So could you make a Ruling of Mind to half the time of mental and social extended research actions for each level of Potency ? Essentially making you very efficient at parsing data.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very similar to what the 1e Time 2 spell Library of Time did; it allowed you to roll a number of extended research rolls equal to successes at half the usual time per roll. You can easily port it over to 2e as a Time 2 or Mind 2 spell, though I'd limit Potency to affecting the number of rolls whose time is halved like the 1e version instead of affecting the factor by which all such rolls are divided, as that is already a +1 Reach effect of 2e Acceleration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T18:12:51-07:00","id":1562909,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to cast a chain sympathetic connection spell? for example A mage has a relic x that belonged to a mumy. Could it be used to cast a sympathetic spell to detect all of the mumies cultists in proximity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T19:56:37-07:00","id":1562916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562909#post1562909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to cast a chain sympathetic connection spell? for example A mage has a relic x that belonged to a mumy. Could it be used to cast a sympathetic spell to detect all of the mumies cultists in proximity?</div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot use Sympathetic Range without having a sympathy Yantra for the target(s) and a sympathetic connection to the target, which for most possible subjects means the mage will need to use Borrow Threads to steal or copy the sympathetic connection to the target from someone or something else.<br /> <br /> Even if you allowed the relic as a sympathy Yantra for the cult as a whole you wouldn't have the necessary connection to every cultist, and using Borrow Threads sympathetically would also be spell-intensive, potentially runs afoul of the spell-stacking rules, strains the validity of using the relic as a Yantra representing individual cultists, and doesn't bypass the extra insulation of not knowing all the sympathetic names involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T03:37:10-07:00","id":1562936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562909#post1562909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to cast a chain sympathetic connection spell? for example A mage has a relic x that belonged to a mumy. Could it be used to cast a sympathetic spell to detect all of the mumies cultists in proximity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to what was said, if you know the mummy is connected to all the cultists, you can use the relic as a yantra to target the mummy sympathetically and get all you need. Ideally you first cast <i>Read the Depths</i> sympathetically to know all cultist's names and how many there are. You could them cast <i>Borrow Threads</i> sympathetically at the mummy to borrow those connections, with scale to account for it. You would then have all the information and sympathetic connections needed to target them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T05:41:19-07:00","id":1562947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1562909#post1562909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to cast a chain sympathetic connection spell? for example A mage has a relic x that belonged to a mumy. Could it be used to cast a sympathetic spell to detect all of the mumies cultists in proximity?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need sympathetic spells to cast zone of detection spells, and indeed that's a premise that seems to truncate how targeting for spells works in any event.<br /> <br /> If there's a quality of being a member of a mummy's cult that can be perceived by magic, you can set up an area of effect to perceived that quality's presence. You can also cast a spell on a Relic to perceived the flow of its sympathetic connections and follow those to anybody who has had meaningful connection to it.<br /> <br /> But you can't cast a spell with undefined targets that fall into a certain category and have it rove about or identify otherwise untargeted people, nor bounce a spell through one target to affect several more.<br /> <br /> That does sound like a thing with complexity and self-guided variance to qualify for the lowest levels of archmastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T07:03:14-07:00","id":1563006,"title":"","content":"Interesting. A bit of a metaquestion why are there limits on combined spells? For me it looks like the developers did not want us to combine arcana for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T08:05:01-07:00","id":1563007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563006#post1563006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. A bit of a metaquestion why are there limits on combined spells? For me it looks like the developers did not want us to combine arcana for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combining arcana is not combining spells.<br /> The first one is using more than one arcana in one single effect, the second is casting more than one spell in a single casting/spell control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T10:03:32-07:00","id":1563010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563006#post1563006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. A bit of a metaquestion why are there limits on combined spells? For me it looks like the developers did not want us to combine arcana for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting a combined spell is for doing things like simultaneously increasing someone's Mental Attributes and decreasing their Physical Attributes, or turning an object into gold and making it cursed. A spell can have a singular effect that requires multiple Arcana (such as turning a living creature into stone) without being a combined spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T15:07:40-07:00","id":1563021,"title":"","content":"Combined spells reduce the needed spell control. Spell control is realistically a limited resources, and should be treated as such. <br /> <br /> Conjunctional spells (which are the other thing), are about as common as you want. The example spells try to go hard on avoiding them. With several examples from each Arcanum where you can just do the magic bit. Like Golemn giving you an animate object which can follow simple instructions - not requiring any Mind at all... This is just magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T10:47:26-07:00","id":1563031,"title":"","content":"If someone would use fate to find money the effect would depend on uses and duration and then the money would in some way dissapear.<br /> What about scrying or going back in time to know the lotery numbers? Would that be lasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:26:33-07:00","id":1563036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563031#post1563031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone would use fate to find money the effect would depend on uses and duration and then the money would in some way dissapear.<br /> What about scrying or going back in time to know the lotery numbers? Would that be lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you just keep the information, same as if you used the <i>Divination </i>with a Reach effect to predict the numbers (target a TV broadcast, a newspaper or website screen that divulges the winning numbers). The main issue is getting the prize. Is the winner publicly disclosed ? Is there someone who keeps an eye on the winners for supernatural ones, since its a very elemental temptation to any divination and luck based powers ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:28:55-07:00","id":1563037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563031#post1563031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone would use fate to find money the effect would depend on uses and duration and then the money would in some way dissapear.<br /> What about scrying or going back in time to know the lotery numbers? Would that be lasting?</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefits of using Fate spells like Shifting the Odds don't &quot;disappear,&quot; they're inherently temporary effects brought about situationally. As with Shifting the Odds, if you spend Experiences to permanently gain the benefits of a Social Merit it's a part of your character sheet that you happen to have justified by using a spell to get the opportunity.<br /> <br /> This is the case regardless of which Arcana you use to produce this opportunity \u2014 the money/connections/authority isn't intrinsically magical just because you used magic to reach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:50:01-07:00","id":1563039,"title":"","content":"i dont think i get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:58:28-07:00","id":1563041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563039#post1563039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i dont think i get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The money isn't magical. The luck is.<br /> <br /> But the game also has rules. If the money isn't a Merit you bought with XP, it's not guaranteed to stay because the Merit exists for this.<br /> <br /> How the money will go away is entirely on the ST hands, but overall it's seen as a dick move towards those who buy Resources with dots to let a player get away with indefinite wealth for a large period of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T14:02:46-07:00","id":1563042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563039#post1563039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i dont think i get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell's effects are Lasting if it makes sense for them to persist after the spell stops sustaining an effect \u2014 a fireball whose Duration is only a couple seconds doesn't un-burn the things it burned when the spell ends, increasing your Social Skills for a week doesn't make the friends you made suddenly forget you met (though later interactions might not go as well with your lower Skill ratings), a chair built using tools created with Matter doesn't fall apart when the tools cease to exist, and so on. Benefits you gained from using information that you used a spell to get don't vanish when the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T14:38:10-07:00","id":1563044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563036#post1563036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you just keep the information, same as if you used the <i>Divination </i>with a Reach effect to predict the numbers (target a TV broadcast, a newspaper or website screen that divulges the winning numbers). The main issue is getting the prize. Is the winner publicly disclosed ? Is there someone who keeps an eye on the winners for supernatural ones, since its a very elemental temptation to any divination and luck based powers ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, given the way that Time magic is supposed to establish the universe as not being deterministic and Divination is supposed to provide information on &quot;likely&quot; futures, I'm of a mind to say that it's actually basically useless at providing foresight of truly randomised outcomes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563041#post1563041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The money isn't magical. The luck is.<br /> <br /> But the game also has rules. If the money isn't a Merit you bought with XP, it's not guaranteed to stay because the Merit exists for this.<br /> <br /> How the money will go away is entirely on the ST hands, but overall it's seen as a dick move towards those who buy Resources with dots to let a player get away with indefinite wealth for a large period of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to approach it in terms of the typical difference between having a lot of money because you have a sustainable income stream and having it because of some one-off circumstance.<br /> <br /> People who suddenly receive several million dollars have a tendency to blow through it very quickly, because in the best case scenario there's something of high value that they're willing to indulge in without concern for the money in the long term, and in the worst (and most typical) they don't really have a good perspective on how far that money can go and suddenly escalate their spending in a manner that soaks it up at speed.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you're trying to spend it sustainably over a lifetime, and like... spending a few million at a rate where it will last the rest of your life will maintain a comfortable middle class lifestyle (for the people who don't have a few million because they're being compensated for damages that entail costly medical care).<br /> <br /> It's different sure if a player proposes that their character is using illicit means to rip off several million a month, but buying the Merit is probably how you represent them undergoing the process of making that money look legit, rather than being something that brings intense scrutiny on them even if it isn't judged to be illegal.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's like a lot of illegal enterprises; sometimes you end up with a lot of money that just sits around on pallets waiting to be laundered or spent. Pablo Escobar lost about 10% of his money a year to rats, mould, and water damage.<br /> <br /> (A person might do something like use their magic to bullshit their way into being a professional gambler who always wins at high stakes and is maybe able to distribute those winnings through multiple identities so that nobody refuses to deal them in or starts becoming suspicious that they cheat, but that in itself entails so much extra effort that even if that isn't folded into it being the Merit, it probably just isn't practical as something for most mages to care to deal with, and certainly more than should take up the time of a PC.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T00:28:07-07:00","id":1563049,"title":"","content":"Spending dots in merits and then losing all the money/status/whatever through roleplaying isn't as significant imo, since sanctity of merits means they effectively get a refund.<br /> <br /> So why then bother with buying the merit at all? Why not cast a spell whenever you need money (probably because the Seers may track you down and spank you), then spending the money means you can't lose it when the spell ends (or otherwise).<br /> <br /> Fate magic changing how you approach life then leads to meeting the low-wisdom/Rapt Acanthus who takes that perspective too far and your players have to decide what to do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T04:46:47-07:00","id":1563053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563049#post1563049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (probably because the Seers may track you down and spank you)</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll have to get to you before the Guardians do, and the Guardians are probably closer.<br /> <br /> Still, I plain think that most mages, as people, aren't well-suited for the lifestyle of going from hustle to hustle, and that for some others who might, it's just a lot of hassle when there's Mysteries to solve.<br /> <br /> The Seers of the Throne are able to sustain a basis of having greater base wealth overall, and being able to furnish that even to low ranked members, because their command hierarchy is able to put some soldiers on the task of constantly acquiring money, regardless of their personal wants, which gets funnelled up the pyramid. And even then, I'd say that's more often in the form of cultivating sustainable revenue streams rather than just robbing stuff or manipulating gambling odds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T06:40:37-07:00","id":1563056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563053#post1563053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seers of the Throne are able to sustain a basis of having greater base wealth overall, and being able to furnish that even to low ranked members, because their command hierarchy is able to put some soldiers on the task of constantly acquiring money, regardless of their personal wants, which gets funnelled up the pyramid. And even then, I'd say that's more often in the form of cultivating sustainable revenue streams rather than just robbing stuff or manipulating gambling odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, not to put too fine a point on it, but it was a point of presentation in 2e that the Sects are more than their mages. The Seers don't need to fully dedicate lower-rung Awakened members to the process of making money \u2014 they have normal people for that just like the Ladder has Cryptopolies and the Guardians have their Labyrinths, in addition to the occasional windfall sent their way by Exarchal Miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T06:48:49-07:00","id":1563057,"title":"","content":"In terms of engagement with the Availability system, I think it's also simple enough to jury rig having money without Resources. It would just be something like having no option to buy anything above a certain rating, certain one-off purchases will essentially wipe out your spending power (you might have actual money left over, but it can be assumed to be dedicated towards more regular needs), and low rating purchases still ultimately have a limit on them.<br /> <br /> None of this need be broken down to specific numbers, since some of it is probably assuming that money is still also being spent on some basic regularities. It's more about capturing the idea that it's only a certain amount of money that can only ever go down, and doesn't come with backing financial stability. Resources gives you recourse to buy things beyond your character's expected means by virtue of credit, debt, and equity, a bit of money you pulled out of a one-off action does not.<br /> <br /> This being something that engages with the fact that the Availability system already doesn't limit itself to Resources, right down to the fact that Signs of Sorcery gives a reference point for assuming that characters can acquire things in exchange for magical services.<br /> <br /> That in itself can be something that can play off of characters not really having much money, but not strictly needing it and being able to live somewhat above your means. There's stuff where Order Status can be leveraged for items, such that a mage can get what they want or need without being diverted from doing their mage stuff, because their mage stuff is what they exchange for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T06:52:44-07:00","id":1563058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563056#post1563056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not to put too fine a point on it, but it was a point of presentation in 2e that the Sects are more than their mages. The Seers don't need to fully dedicate lower-rung Awakened members to the process of making money \u2014 they have normal people for that just like the Ladder has Cryptopolies and the Guardians have their Labyrinths, in addition to the occasional windfall sent their way by Exarchal Miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a lot like organised crime; the soldiers will be evaluated by their bosses in terms of being &quot;earners&quot;, but for the most part they're not actually doing the work that makes the money, they're just recruiting, pushing, and collecting from the people outside the hierarchy who do.<br /> <br /> A low-ranking Seer with this assignment is Christopher Soprano sitting at the front of an office bored out of his mind while other people make the calls for pumping and dumping, just where he's casting the odd spell to keep it going (and maybe scrutinising the workers to make sure they're not skimming).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T11:14:21-07:00","id":1563065,"title":"","content":"I think one important distinction to make here is that one off vs consistent earnings (big win vs having Resources) is not a distinction of legality.<br /> <br /> A Mafia Boss, or a Seer running embezzlement schemes, are not one-offing their way to riches, they effectively have Resources.<br /> <br /> The point isn't just having a salary, but having a system in place, whomever put it there, making the flow of money somewhat reliable. That's what organized crime do, what companies do, etc.<br /> <br /> But such systems also have costs, which is why the one-off rarely is sustainable. This is something most players gloss over.<br /> <br /> Let's say you got your big win and now want to use it to open a storefront, so you make it into stable funds. You go to NYC to open a grocery store, mid-tier nothing too fancy, where you can also discreetly hide some magical works.<br /> <br /> Going for Lower Manhattan or SoHo, staying the hell away of Fifth Avenue, your opening cost alone can hit US $ 400.000 between rent, utilities, renovations, staff, etc, take 9 months to open and still this covers the first 6 months only. You'll need extra capital for emergencies and to stay open during the build up of traffic, which means more rent (100k to 200k every 6 months), maintenance, wages, taxes, utilities, insurance... And it can take a couple years for a successful business to start to really sustain itself and generate revenue. Be prepared for 2 solid years feeling that you're the poorest member of staff.<br /> <br /> That'll easily lock away 1 Million dollars even if some of this money remains at the &quot;end&quot; of the process, and even then things can go wrong in several ways that you can't control. Wanna just live off interest, instead? Contrary to movies, a well maintained investment won't reliably give you more than 10% a year above inflation. Any bigger wins are due to volatility, not acumen, and are offset by equally uncontrollable risks of loss.<br /> <br /> Want to personally control things to guarantee success in game? Then be prepared to spend a lot of time in-character making money rather than engaging the actual game.<br /> <br /> In the end, the point is that having things for an extended period of time is a completely 'nother beast than buying something once. A house or vehicle will have maintenance, stable revenue is a long-term, high investment process, and if you can't delegate this it'll also take your time.<br /> <br /> You know, as in there's a reason why the great real financial professionals in the market work for wages and fees, not from investments. The ones who do were rich to begin with.<br /> <br /> A character that one-off a big sum isn't fated to loose it only because they don't know how to make it last. They'll loose it because making it last is complex and rarely within their interests. It takes time and requires you to give up the big sum right away just to start reaping benefits sometime in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T16:53:10-07:00","id":1563074,"title":"","content":"So whats the point of investing in resourcess again? A spell once or twice a sesion and you have all the resourcess you need.<br /> Also if its lasting why does shifting the odds have a primary factor of duration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T17:42:13-07:00","id":1563075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563074#post1563074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So whats the point of investing in resourcess again? A spell once or twice a sesion and you have all the resourcess you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to cast the spell, you have consistent access to the benefits of that Merit, and you know where the money is coming from. Shifting the Odds being Duration-primary means you have to take penalties to the casting roll to get more than one use of the Merit at a rating of more than one dot.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also if its lasting why does shifting the odds have a primary factor of duration? </div> </div> </div>It isn't. Shifting the Odds can give you temporary access to Social Merits, which go away after you've used them [Potency] times <i>unless you spend Experiences to purchase the Merit.</i><br /> <br /> Also, it has Duration as its primary factor because the base effect (which doesn't scale off of Potency at all) brings you to what you're looking for within 24 hours <i>as long as the spell is active</i>, which requires it to last for more than one scene in most contexts. That doesn't mean the corrupt cop you find by Shifting the Odds doesn't remember you when you next meet them after the spell's Duration ends, because the Lasting effects of Shifting the Odds are that you met the person from the category you were trying to meet or made use of the Social Merit you had temporary access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T20:39:42-07:00","id":1563080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563074#post1563074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So whats the point of investing in resourcess again? A spell once or twice a sesion and you have all the resourcess you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there something about the preceding seven or eight posts addressing that subject which is unclear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T23:29:26-07:00","id":1563083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563080#post1563080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there something about the preceding seven or eight posts addressing that subject which is unclear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. Why spend character points when every time you need something you can just cast a spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T03:51:47-07:00","id":1563085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563083#post1563083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it is. Why spend character points when every time you need something you can just cast a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because:<br /> <br /> 1. That takes time,<br /> <br /> 2. It can fail,<br /> <br /> 3. Others may mess with your shit,<br /> <br /> 4. Will attract undesirable attention,<br /> <br /> 5. Has added steps.<br /> <br /> You don't have to think it's worth it, no one here is saying you're required to. But the reasons are pretty clear and suffice for most players. If you have an actual doubt feel free to ask, but if you're just trying to force others into agreeing with your opinion, this is not the thread for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T04:15:19-07:00","id":1563087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563085#post1563085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because:<br /> <br /> 1. That takes time,<br /> <br /> 2. It can fail,<br /> <br /> 3. Others may mess with your shit,<br /> <br /> 4. Will attract undesirable attention,<br /> <br /> 5. Has added steps.<br /> <br /> You don't have to think it's worth it, no one here is saying you're required to. But the reasons are pretty clear and suffice for most players. If you have an actual doubt feel free to ask, but if you're just trying to force others into agreeing with your opinion, this is not the thread for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also 6. Not all characters have access to the Fate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Like the underlying merit system exists for sleepers. The fact that Mages have spells which CT literally says can grant merits does infact make it less necessary to spend XP on things.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can cast a spell to gain Occultation or grant you the Astral Adept merit. But learning things the mundane way means you have more spell control and flexibility availarthe rest of the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T04:29:22-07:00","id":1563088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563085#post1563085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because:<br /> <br /> 1. That takes time,<br /> <br /> 2. It can fail,<br /> <br /> 3. Others may mess with your shit,<br /> <br /> 4. Will attract undesirable attention,<br /> <br /> 5. Has added steps.<br /> <br /> You don't have to think it's worth it, no one here is saying you're required to. But the reasons are pretty clear and suffice for most players. If you have an actual doubt feel free to ask, but if you're just trying to force others into agreeing with your opinion, this is not the thread for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>All im doing is asking so i dont know what youre trying to build with that insinuation. Im looking at it from player perspective to avoid rules abuse as a ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T08:57:04-07:00","id":1563093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563088#post1563088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All im doing is asking so i dont know what youre trying to build with that insinuation. Im looking at it from player perspective to avoid rules abuse as a ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked the same question twice in a row despite being given the answer multiple times, using phrasing that sounds like you're challenging straightforward answers for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's the point of buying Attributes if you can just cast Honing the Form or Augment the Mind whenever you need to roll better?&quot; is in the same vein of question. You have already been told multiple times by multiple people that consistency and lack of the issues specific to spellcasting are the main point of not using spells for everything.<br /> <br /> Every time you cast a spell to accomplish something there is at least some chance that something will go wrong in a way that doesn't come up from simply having mundane traits and resources to achieve your goal \u2014 this is also why Legacy Attainments are desirable even though they're more limited than the spells they emulate.<br /> <br /> If your player is using spells to bypass the need to network then you have the whole set of complications the system enables for interfering with or establishing consequences for spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T08:57:23-07:00","id":1563094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563083#post1563083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it is. Why spend character points when every time you need something you can just cast a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's not really answering my question, because it's not actually engaging with any of the things that have already been described, in detail.<br /> <br /> If you find those details unconvincing then maybe argue to that effect. Don't act as though they aren't there and haven't been addressed.<br /> <br /> Still, to offer some kind of additional point, the thing to take away from this is not that Resources is a pointless Merit. It's that magic offers recourse to engage with the Availability system that a character might not otherwise have based on what's on their sheet. Magic actually does that for a lot of things; a mage only needs three dots in an Arcanum to be capable of inflicting significant harm on other people while lacking any skills for fighting, for instance.<br /> <br /> But magic can come with complications based on the opportunity cost of using it or the possible scrutiny of peers or enemies, or other matters of practicality. The benefit of having something like a Merit is that it puts all of that stuff off into the background, and allows the player to focus on using it for the end result.<br /> <br /> Like, a Storyteller should absolutely shut down any attempt to say that a person has used magic to acquire money off-stage; in the absence of mechanical backing or sanctity of Merits, it needs to be something that takes place in a scene. Apart from any other possibility of inviting complications from how one goes about it, I would have to imagine that gets unbelievably tedious after a while.<br /> <br /> But again, that's just one point among many. The answer to your question is found in several preceding posts. One of my preferred ones is &quot;Resources gives one a capacity to acquire things higher on the Availability rating than one's Merit dots, because finance is more than the number in your savings account, and bespoke acquisition of certain quantities of money won't substitute for that (and no you aren't casually pulling together hundreds of thousands at least on a whim)&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T08:58:13-07:00","id":1563095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563088#post1563088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All im doing is asking so i dont know what youre trying to build with that insinuation. Im looking at it from player perspective to avoid rules abuse as a ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just that the answers were given. At this point it's hard to say something more.<br /> <br /> Social Merits aren't meant to gatekeep benefits like money, they're meant to be reliable and run as a background process. You pay XP for three things: easy and predictable access, not have to worry with it actively in game and making a statement about the character.<br /> <br /> A clever player can find many ways to achieve the same results without them, but it will take active effort and be subject to circumstances and rolls. Supernatural powers intensify this.<br /> <br /> This is not a loophole, it's the system working as intended. If a player decides to magic their way to money every session, let them try and roll with it, as long as it is an active part of the game and everyone has fun with it, it's ok.<br /> <br /> You should only avoid letting it become dull or push it to the background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T09:01:05-07:00","id":1563096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563093#post1563093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You have already been told multiple times by multiple people that consistency and lack of the issues specific to spellcasting are the main point of not using spells for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the less considered ones might be leaving traces of your nimbus in a lot of places where that might be visible, trackable, and indicative of patterns and priorities in a way that might be hazardous. I would find it reasonable to infer from the general tone of the game that one reason mages are trained with a bit of discernment in use of their magic is that it's a good idea to not leave that kind of information behind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T09:22:18-07:00","id":1563097,"title":"","content":"As i was asked whats was unclear in the former responses, i answered.<br /> The unclear part was: how do i avoid abusing this and having players dump resources all the time. Perhaps i framed it as the repeating of my question but i did not feel nor reason my former question was answered. Sure narative consequences can apply, they always can but in this case they seemed inssuficient. Failing isnt a big issue since you can do it again.<br /> I realy was expecting something like wisdom checks or some personal method to deal with the problem. Not for a moment did i anticipate its not a problem. <br /> In short i apriciate the answers even if i found them at first unclear. No need to assume malice or to be rude about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T09:28:16-07:00","id":1563098,"title":"","content":"Also does that mean you can find a mage mentor using magic? Since the effect of the merit fades do you have to use a different mentor each time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T09:48:17-07:00","id":1563099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563098#post1563098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also does that mean you can find a mage mentor using magic? Since the effect of the merit fades do you have to use a different mentor each time?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell guides you to arbitrary objects or people who fit the criteria, requires time to work that can vary based on plausibility, and cannot guarantee you will encounter specific people.<br /> <br /> There's a comparable power in Deviant (higher-level Superhuman Manipulation) that specifies the people it brings you to are ordinary humans, and while the Mentor Merit includes people who are in a teaching position for you the mechanical representation being leveraged is &quot;someone who wants something from your character can be asked for a favor commensurate to their rating once per session, which automatically succeeds but likely demands a favor of equivalent scope in return,&quot; which stands in contrast with Allies, Contacts, and Retainer, which all require rolls to use but are less strictly metered in their usability.<br /> <br /> That is to say, you can't use Shifting the Odds to guarantee a long-term magical teacher, though the people the spell leads you do could happen to be mages with the skills or resources to trade favors for greater guarantee of success in accomplishing what you need from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T10:06:33-07:00","id":1563100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563097#post1563097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for a moment did i anticipate its not a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom checks wouldn't exactly be a restraint on it even if it was some horrible game-breaker, considering that Wisdom primarily functions as a way to track character development than be some kind of punishment mechanism.<br /> <br /> Even within the boundaries of &quot;it doesn't render a whole Merit redundant if mages can occasionally use magic to secure what they need&quot;, I would regard the statements of &quot;Guardians of the Veil or Seers of the Throne might target you for it&quot; to be a by far more restrictive consideration than &quot;you might get the Megalomania Condition for a session or two and some of the numbers related to Paradox calculations will tick down&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T14:25:16-07:00","id":1563108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563098#post1563098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also does that mean you can find a mage mentor using magic? Since the effect of the merit fades do you have to use a different mentor each time?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is, rtfm. <br /> <br /> To quote the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Increasing a Merit is typically a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell. Attributes and Skills can be increased by a Perfecting (\u2022\u2022\u2022) spell. Gaining a Skill that has no dots is a Patterning (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) spell.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> Trait dots granted by magic last only as long as the spell\u2019s Duration, and are not subject to the Sanctity of Merits rule. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can increase a Merit with Ruling. <br /> <br /> You can grant a Mentor, per the rules. Whether that is a Creative Thaumaturgy spell or and Example Spell.<br /> <br /> Which Arcanum is appropriate depends on the circumstances, the ST should be asking &quot;how do you gain a mentor&quot; and this will then answer the next question.<br /> <br /> Maybe they decide to summon a ghost mage to act as their mentor, and it burns out for some reason unable to teach more after some innate limit (of being a ghost). Let the players go wild, create their own solutions. There is an explicit spell for creating ghosts of dead Mages by using their Soulstone, and you can have them tutor you in joining their legacy (for example). It is all good, so long as it drives the narative forward. <br /> <br /> Being able to use magic is a big part of the game. So let the players do it. The interesting part isn't can they do X, but should they.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T04:48:38-07:00","id":1563121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563108#post1563108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The short answer is, rtfm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See im asking about things that in my opinon could be problematic. I know more or less whats writen ruleswise generaly in the book. Im asking about specific instances and how would they work in practice. In this example i found it strange that you could potentialy get a magic teacher with a spell. Also was unsure how the limited use thing would work in this instance. Exploits are a thing and the developers did not think about everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T06:11:18-07:00","id":1563123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563121#post1563121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this example i found it strange that you could potentialy get a magic teacher with a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mystically inclined teachers and students being brought together by destiny happens all the time in fiction. This would just be an instance where destiny is mandated a bit by one or the other of them.<br /> <br /> Besides that, people in general seek out teachers, so why should mages be any different? Needing to use spells to do so is somewhere between &quot;maintaining the bit&quot; and &quot;they're not exactly going to be listed at the local learning annex&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still, the spell might not exactly give you the precision between a nurturing, encouraging, patient mentor and one who attacks at random while demanding you dodge, so not necessarily a simple fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T07:38:41-07:00","id":1563124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563121#post1563121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See im asking about things that in my opinon could be problematic. I know more or less whats writen ruleswise generaly in the book. Im asking about specific instances and how would they work in practice. In this example i found it strange that you could potentialy get a magic teacher with a spell. Also was unsure how the limited use thing would work in this instance. Exploits are a thing and the developers did not think about everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to look at it is that the spell brings you a mentor quickly and conveniently for a few favors. After it expires, its up to you. Cast it again and you get the most likely one, which might not be the same person or have a similar dynamic. <br /> <br /> If you clicked with that mentor, you can cut a deal or do something personally significant to gain a temporary Mentor merit, proportional to how meaningful your actions were. It has the caveat of requiring more maintenance than the normal merit and having no Sanctity of Merits. Essentially, the player is paying in active attentiveness to the mentor rather than XP.<br /> <br /> So yeah, hopping from one teacher to the next by destined mentorship is just as viable as finding the mentor and then choosing to invest in the bond (via more involved roleplay or XP)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T10:51:13-07:00","id":1563126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563124#post1563124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to look at it is that the spell brings you a mentor quickly and conveniently for a few favors. After it expires, its up to you. Cast it again and you get the most likely one, which might not be the same person or have a similar dynamic.<br /> <br /> If you clicked with that mentor, you can cut a deal or do something personally significant to gain a temporary Mentor merit, proportional to how meaningful your actions were. It has the caveat of requiring more maintenance than the normal merit and having no Sanctity of Merits. Essentially, the player is paying in active attentiveness to the mentor rather than XP.<br /> <br /> So yeah, hopping from one teacher to the next by destined mentorship is just as viable as finding the mentor and then choosing to invest in the bond (via more involved roleplay or XP)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the bit where, while the Merit makes doing a favor in return technically optional, the fleeting relationships the spell is likely to bring you into are almost definitely going to require something in exchange \u2014 Signs of Sorcery's note that sometimes the cost in service for getting a rote from your order or mentor is just meeting expectations for business as usual, and that doesn't necessarily follow for a mentor you're brought into confluence with by tweaking the force of destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T15:38:05-07:00","id":1563129,"title":"","content":"In the end it all boils down to consistency, maintenance and active effort.<br /> <br /> This is not really a Mage thing. Any character can leverage circumstances and traits to get this kind of effect. A blue book detective can cheat in a gamble or steal money, seek hints of someone who can teach a skill or weirder ability and so on.<br /> <br /> Without a Merit all those things still work, but it requires focus in game and can come with all kinds of problems and unpredictable results. A supernatural power amplifies the good and the bad, but otherwise the dynamic is the same, and mundane methods can be pretty effective.<br /> <br /> Merits give you convenience. Not only that it is always there without hassle, but also that you know exactly what to expect out of it, which is crucial to be able to take maximum benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T00:20:40-07:00","id":1563161,"title":"","content":"Worrying about being able to abuse gaining resources or a mentor, when mages can be immune to bullets whilst invisibly running through walls is quite amusing..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T01:56:26-07:00","id":1563167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563161#post1563161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worrying about being able to abuse gaining resources or a mentor, when mages can be immune to bullets whilst invisibly running through walls is quite amusing..</div> </div> </div> </div>Worrying about a trait players pay with dots/XP for is perfectly legit in any RPG. There's a reason we explained why it's not a problem rather than making a useless oneliner trying to humiliate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png",