xpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T13:01:09-07:00","id":1563190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563173#post1563173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wonder this forum has turned to shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, truly the reason for reduced activity in the forum isn't a combination of &quot;Onyx Path has a vastly reduced output&quot; and &quot;Discord absorbs most of this kind of conversation&quot;. It's all about some people having little tolerance for folks who don't lose their taste for drive-by contemptuous one-liners once they get out of their twenties, who are certainly the majority of people on the internet and definitely worth having around anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T13:16:45-07:00","id":1563191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563190#post1563190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, truly the reason for reduced activity in the forum isn't a combination of &quot;Onyx Path has a vastly reduced output&quot; and &quot;Discord absorbs most of this kind of conversation&quot;. It's all about some people having little tolerance for folks who don't lose their taste for drive-by contemptuous one-liners once they get out of their twenties, who are certainly the majority of people on the internet and definitely worth having around anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, we really should get rid of these people with low tolerances. As somebody who has been told by mods here that i dont need to read peoples posts and reply to them, and then gotten infractions because of a reply asking &quot;wtf the OP was going on about.&quot; Monte certainly didnt need to reply to my comment, or make it out to be something it wasnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T15:41:15-07:00","id":1563200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563187#post1563187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If making useless (one line) comments was banned here, there would be a lot less posters. But accusing me of trying to humiliate the OP is out of order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. It was unnecessarily disrespectful, but &quot;humiliate&quot; I concede that may be more in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> Even then I'm not sure if responding in favor of the questioning poster was out of order, but I've been quite rambunctious lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T21:04:05-07:00","id":1563356,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">SImmer down folks, no need to get upset or be rude. Let's refocus and be a little gentler, please</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T04:57:54-07:00","id":1563363,"title":"","content":"In Awakening mind, prime and death have their own spiritual realms with their own summoned spiritual creatures. What makes Spirit stand out as an Arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T07:13:03-07:00","id":1563366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563363#post1563363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Awakening mind, prime and death have their own spiritual realms with their own summoned spiritual creatures. What makes Spirit stand out as an Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime does not have its own spiritual realm in the standard model, but what makes Spirit notable is that the Shadow is the most accessible realm and its denizens are notionally the most durable and sustainable, which makes it the most useful one for getting low-investment familiars or traveling unseen without sticking to Twilight.<br /> <br /> The Underworld can largely only be physically accessed through Avernian Gates, which are limited by/affect local Resonance, and while training can allow characters to overcome the geographical requirements for meditating into the Astral its contents don't normally have any sort of predictable interface with the world outside of dreams. While Shadowed Gates are uncommon, technically any spirit can cross the Gauntlet from anywhere it can feed from and loci are just particularly easy places to cross.<br /> <br /> Ghosts need specific and limited phenomena to gain Essence and, while Goetia are the only common invisible entities to which the &quot;regain their Rank in Essence every day in their home realm&quot; mechanic actually applies and they theoretically have no greater difficulty finding Essence than a spirit of the same concepts, they're severely limited in their ability to affect the material world between lack of native Manifestations and inconsistent ability to leave the Astral. Spirits feed on the energies of the same things that created them and have a survivorship bias toward representing concrete phenomena, and their ecology is such that despite their limited free Essence they can replenish themselves from the stores of similar beings.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Regularly making use of ghosts and Goetia requires extra preparation and support that spirits don't typically need, and the Shadow hews relatively close to Earthly geography and doesn't have a hard limit on where you can enter and exit from overall. The Spiritual frame has the most &quot;natural&quot; interface with the material world and its denizens don't require special treatment to be effective tools and allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T11:46:29-07:00","id":1563369,"title":"","content":"Put another way, Spirit retains most of its purview. It isn't the Universal Otherworld Sphere as it is in Ascension, but what the others got are more niche things than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T14:26:24-07:00","id":1563376,"title":"","content":"Spirit stands out as an Arcanum because the animism premise gives it a few things to engage with that might not otherwise be expected, because the ecological and social fabric of the Shadow is a bit more sophisticated to be able to engage with (ghosts and Goetia are kind of self-contained to their own particular subrealms), and because it's always right next to you.<br /> <br /> I think there are things with gameplay approach and creative thaumaturgy that can be pursued in that last one, particularly through the kind of lens where the Exarch called the Nemesis resides; that the Shadow retains the imprint of unacknowledged consequences. The imprint of dramatic or traumatic events lingers in the Shadow close at hand to where they occurred, compared to the more distant reach of the Underworld or the deeper layers of the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T16:23:03-07:00","id":1563382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563366#post1563366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Goetia are the only common invisible entities to which the &quot;regain their Rank in Essence every day in their home realm&quot; mechanic actually applies</b> and they theoretically have no greater difficulty finding Essence than a spirit of the same concepts</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your whole text, but I got confused by the bolded part, could you clarify it for me please? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T16:36:58-07:00","id":1563384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563382#post1563382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with your whole text, but I got confused by the bolded part, could you clarify it for me please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite early indications to the contrary (see page 254), Geist's more detailed presentation of the Underworld makes it clear that, like spirits in the Shadow, ghosts are not sustained by the Great Below, and while in theory Supernal beings still regain their Rank in Mana per day while in the Supernal, the only context in which that's relevant \u2014 the one in which a playable character watches a Supernal being from scene to contiguous scene \u2014 is unlikely to be relevant (between the Willpower cost for mages and the long-term effects of casting Apocalypse on unAwakened targets).<br /> <br /> In practice, the only sense in which the mechanic is both true and relevant is for Goetia in the Astral. (Chthonians regain their Rank in Essence each day in the Underworld, rising to each hour in the Rivers or the Ocean, but they're unusual specimens.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T03:57:02-07:00","id":1563399,"title":"","content":"In fact, if you look closely, both the Bluebook and Mage (2e) have Gateway conditions for Avernian Gates, which state that ghosts gain 1 essence per scene (I think). Whereas Geist seaps that to loses 1 essence per scene.<br /> <br /> Geist is much more about ghostly life sucking ass, and only mlbeing made a little bit better by Sin-eaters helping them out. Whereas the other gamelines present a possibility that ghosts can gain large amount of essence and thus become powerful antagonists - not the role ghosts play in Geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563363#post1563363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Awakening mind, prime and death have their own spiritual realms with their own summoned spiritual creatures. What makes Spirit stand out as an Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit is the Arcanum of Animism, it is a symbiotic realm of natural resonance and direct interactions with the material world.<br /> <br /> The Shadow (so named, at least in part because it looks like a shadow of the material world) reinforces the aspects of the world that it mirrors making Resonances stronger while also competing with itself over resonance. So it has a measurable effect on basically the entire world 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> The Astral is much more disconnected, and does't have the same symbiotic interaction.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is completely different, reflecting the world only as it was. Has very different politics and narrative/direction. <br /> <br /> Spirit is everything (apart from humans) Death is only the dead things (particularly ones that affected humans)... The Astral is both humans and non-humans...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-24-2026, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T05:04:05-07:00","id":1563406,"title":"","content":"More important is the mere fact that the Shadow interact with the Material reciprocally and directly all the time, while the others are their own things.<br /> <br /> If you master and apply all the lore and rules about the Shadow, that'll be rich material for all your CoD games in every single line regardless of chronicle, because it's relevant for everyone all the time and interacts with everything, even if not noticed/recognized.<br /> <br /> The Underworld, Astral and Supernal are kinda niche even in their own lines. You can go long stretches of time with minimal interaction, and when you go there it's basically another place, it's like going to the next town rather than a superimposed Reality over your regular turf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T06:15:09-07:00","id":1563409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563406#post1563406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More important is the mere fact that the Shadow interact with the Material reciprocally and directly all the time, while the others are their own things.<br /> <br /> If you master and apply all the lore and rules about the Shadow, that'll be rich material for all your CoD games in every single line regardless of chronicle, because it's relevant for everyone all the time and interacts with everything, even if not noticed/recognized.<br /> <br /> The Underworld, Astral and Supernal are kinda niche even in their own lines. You can go long stretches of time with minimal interaction, and when you go there it's basically another place, it's like going to the next town rather than a superimposed Reality over your regular turf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant you just summon any of the 3 to interact and it will be the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T06:56:10-07:00","id":1563410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563409#post1563409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cant you just summon any of the 3 to interact and it will be the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you remove the entire framework of needing to be in the presence of an open Iris to the Underworld for ghosts or a place where you could meditate into the Astral for Goetia (in contrast with an Iris simply making spirit summoning easier) and disregard the differences in their Influences and supporting Conditions and their ability to Manifest, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T07:45:33-07:00","id":1563412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563409#post1563409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cant you just summon any of the 3 to interact and it will be the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the only way one engages with these as characters is in terms of their stat blocks, and one lines up a few that happen to have the same Influences and Numina, then sure.<br /> <br /> If one reads into what makes them tick as entities, what drives them, what motivates them, the likely terms in which they will apply their stats to accomplish goals negotiated or imposed on them by mages, then no.<br /> <br /> Never mind the caveat that summoning with precision requires a bit of exploration of the realm one would propose to summon them from in order to get some identities to target, so the experience of a mage exploring the Shadow will differ from the Astral and the Underworld in the course of getting their staple of what to summon.<br /> <br /> Actually, scratch that point about identical stat blocks; I forgot about the fact that's also where Bans and Banes are, and those will also be things that tend to have some of the guidelines for their character drawing on the broader principles of what kind of entity they are. A Goetia from the Temenos with a Fire Influence and a Ban of &quot;can't pass by a mounted fire extinguisher&quot; might have different parameters for being summoned than a spirit from the Shadow with a Ban of &quot;must ignite a copse of trees every time it passes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:19:55-07:00","id":1563414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563409#post1563409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cant you just summon any of the 3 to interact and it will be the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Adding to what others said and also a maybe simpler explanation:<br /> <br /> 1. They won't have the same stats, variety and ease to summon. Spirits will be by far easier to find and summon within almost any parameter you may want.<br /> <br /> 2. Won't be the same. Interaction is different, bargaining for services will be different and opposing them if needed will be different. And again Spirits will offer you way more versatility in every aspect.<br /> <br /> 3. Even within the same Rank and Influence they have distinct perspectives and means of interaction that affect what they can do in practice. Goetia, ghosts and supernal beings in this regard have highly specialized strengths, while spirits have vastly broader applications.<br /> <br /> So you can summon any of the four, but what it takes, what you can do with them and what they can do for you isn't equal, and spirits far outweigh the others three in overall ease and usefulness. And that's only talking about you summoning them, which is the smallest use case for all four Arcana.<br /> <br /> More important is all the rest. You need the respective Arcana to interfere magically with the respective realms, their phenomena, their interactions with the Material, any denizen that comes your way and the materials and energy that comprise them.<br /> <br /> It then becomes extremely relevant the fact that the Shadow is way bigger, meaner and closer than the other three realms, by orders of magnitude. Between the three, the Underworld is by far the closest to the Material and still the points of contact are few. Only in the premises of an Avernian Gate do you have interactions between realms, and those gates are maybe a few dozen in a metropolis.<br /> <br /> Only one point of contact exists between the Material and the Shadow, though. It is called <i>the whole fucking universe</i>. The realm is so close to the Material that areas where they're not in direct contact with each other are scary anomalies rarer and more dangerous than a gate to the Supernal (and you don't come back from one of those if you fall in).<br /> <br /> Loci aren't just maybe 10 times more common and easier to make than Avernian Gates, they are not just contact surfaces, they're damned holes in the fabric of reality with a thin layer of inconvenience separating them. Get away from one and everywhere you'll still be close enough to the Shadow to influence of directly, be influenced by it directly, be at reach for a lot of spirits, be surrounded by spirits in the Shadow and so on. It's so overwhelmingly everywhere that ghosts in Twilight interact with things from the Shadow more frequently than with anything coming from the Underworld.<br /> <br /> You also have greater variety of environments, phenomena and materials in the Shadow, with means everything said about the differences in summoning denizens applies to pretty much each and every imaginable use of contact with another dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T13:10:56-07:00","id":1563427,"title":"","content":"I would argue for the Astral actually being bigger than than the Shadow, or at least more vast... Like you can visit the Astral representation of distant stars (regardless of whether that will drive you mad), or parts of the Astral/World-soul which relate to actual places (even if they are less interesting), but even if that is smaller, every human (and potentially other supernaturals) has their own personal astral realm, which is going to include potentially every memory of their's represented as a Goetia... <br /> <br /> But that is not to take away from the point that the Astral is seperated rather differently.<br /> <br /> Of course if you're including Prime (which doesn't seem comparable) then the Aeons are in that space where Astral and Supernal entities start to blur (but that is rather at the god-like level of it doesn't matter) arguably the Aeons are Supernal Gods in the Astral, and the Supernal is an extension of the Astral... So they should only be considered one realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T16:44:24-07:00","id":1563436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563427#post1563427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue for the Astral actually being bigger than than the Shadow, or at least more vast...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is a measurable infinity: the whole material universe exist there, plus areas that only exist there. That also mean it has at least every possible environment that exists in the universe, plus several impossible variations of those environments, plus who knows how wild it can get with completely unique environments and, on top of that, it is both expanded by human thought and imagination, but not limited to it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean it's necessarily bigger in literal and absolute sense, but we can more readily grasp a notion of it being super fucking huge in a manner that's also easier to come up with uses in game that bring this hugeness to bear.<br /> <br /> But the Astral is certainly the next contender. It has potentially every conceivable place and environment, which may or may not be more than what we get out of the Shadow. At least the Shadow is theoretically limited by having to make some sense, which the Astral bypasses. It has also something I wouldn't call more vast, but certainly more applicable vastness in that you're not bound to regular space there. There is no reason to think the Shadow doesn't have distant stars, but in the Astral you can get there without the inconvenience of journeying across several parsecs. At least without magic.<br /> <br /> Supernal reality and the Underworld are small in the narrative sense, which is what matter here. Even if you could travel for real to the Supernal Realms they'd be homogeneous in any comparison with the Material. Even by their definition, since they only have the perfected form of concepts, while the Lie has the infinite imperfect variations, the Supernal can't hold more diverse experiences. But you can't really go there or anything close to it, not without you ceasing utterly to exist in any known sense of the it, so it's basically whatever you summon plus brief weird phenomena and the eventual Reality Thrash Can opening so you can dump stuff that won't ever come back.<br /> <br /> With a pretty samey description of an endless cave with trickling streams, a shore with some cities, rivers of stuff, geographically limited island Dominions and the Ocean of Memories as a very well known practical end, Underworld is the most limited known realm as it has a non trivial chance of being spatially smallish. Like, add to it all that the others exist beyond human life and experience, but the Underworld is only for human created ghosts, and it has a pretty decent chance of not being larger than Europe if it isn't spatially mapped over the Material the way the Shadow is.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just a fun exercise. Their size isn't literally measurable or comparable, their application in game is, and then that's it: Astral and Shadow more or less tie in regards to how varied is the shit you can pull out of them, but the Shadow has too much more immediately applicable relevance by being a superimposed mirror reality in constant interaction with the Material everywhere and that is effectively an integral part of the Material's composition and regular physics. Hence having its own Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T08:37:53-07:00","id":1563463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563427#post1563427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue for the Astral actually being bigger than than the Shadow, or at least more vast... Like you can visit the Astral representation of distant stars (regardless of whether that will drive you mad),</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thrice-Great do that.<br /> <br /> Luna doesn't like them for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T09:20:56-07:00","id":1563464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563463#post1563463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thrice-Great do that.<br /> <br /> Luna doesn't like them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Shadow of the sky. The Whorl is in the Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T15:49:03-07:00","id":1563513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563464#post1563464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the Shadow of the sky. The Whorl is in the Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that the Astral Realms does not have some monopoly on being as big as the sky.<br /> <br /> The statement of &quot;the Astral is bigger than the Shadow because it goes out to distant stars&quot; falters in the face of the fact that the distant stars are where the Idigam come from. Like, the Werewolf antagonist so iconic that the Chronicle was going to be named after them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T15:56:22-07:00","id":1563514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563513#post1563513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is that the Astral Realms does not have some monopoly on being as big as the sky.<br /> <br /> The statement of &quot;the Astral is bigger than the Shadow because it goes out to distant stars&quot; falters in the face of the fact that the distant stars are where the Idigam come from. Like, the Werewolf antagonist so iconic that the Chronicle was going to be named after them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point, but I'm not aware of Mages actually travelling there... And what is accessible to Mages within the Astral is not the same. I mean it isn't a fair comparison between the two when travelling in the Astral is such a different experience compared to the more mundane journeys through actual Shadow Environments. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to realistically or fairly compare the two. <br /> <br /> That said, are Idigam not from the moon? I thought that was another type of entity which came from beyond the stars... void spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T16:32:45-07:00","id":1563515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563514#post1563514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fair point, but I'm not aware of Mages actually travelling there... And what is accessible to Mages within the Astral is not the same. I mean it isn't a fair comparison between the two when travelling in the Astral is such a different experience compared to the more mundane journeys through actual Shadow Environments.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to realistically or fairly compare the two.<br /> <br /> That said, are Idigam not from the moon? I thought that was another type of entity which came from beyond the stars... void spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Idigam were imprisoned in the Moon, they didn't originate there.<br /> <br /> I don't think using &quot;Mages travel there&quot; as reference is anything close to an adequate measure of vastness. Even because I can just as easily say the Shadow is vaster because the spaces are so vast you can't just get wherever, and the Astral is actually a quaint model that fits small versions of everything in an easy to access experience.<br /> <br /> Not being relatable is the point. They clan only be compared within particular contexts, not as an absolute fact. And the context that started was &quot;more relevant to have an entire Arcanum just to deal with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other than that it's asking if an infinite space of iterations of material reality is bigger than an infinite space of mental constructs by every single mind to have ever existed, including the one expanding it in the process of exploring it.<br /> <br /> What's bigger, the entire universe and possible configurations it can have, or the collective of consciousness and unconscious of everything to have ever thought?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T17:28:40-07:00","id":1563517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563513#post1563513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distant stars are where the Idigam come from. Like, the Werewolf antagonist so iconic that the Chronicle was going to be named after them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries about their ultimate origin notwithstanding, for all practical purposes, the idigam come from Earth or the Moon, as evident from &quot;idigam&quot; being the First Tongue rendering of their epithet of &quot;Moon-Banished&quot; and the other category being &quot;Earth-Bound.&quot; If they came from distant stars the distinction between them and the more conventional void-spirits getting past Luna's orbit would be entirely arbitrary and their resurgence following the Moon landings would be a drop in the bucket.<br /> <br /> The Shadow of outer space is largely as empty as its material counterpart and that shows itself in the types of spirits that come from outer space being hungry and desperate and ill-suited to what-passes-for-life on the Shadow of the Earth when they aren't particularly spiteful reflections of Helios's baleful radiance in the form of planetary angels. Idigam with the right Dread Power can call void spirits down from beyond the lunar sphere, but the root quality of their initial Formlessness and ability to Coalesce speaks more to some sort of primordial process of the Shadow than anything to do with the likes of Alpha Centauri and such.<br /> <br /> The Whorl allows you to travel astronomic distances in the part of the cosmology that corresponds to the interiority of the universe separate from human culture and individual human minds, which themselves are each theoretically several times the scope of the material world that forms the basis for their creators' perspectives. Even accounting for entropic processes like the loss of a Temenos realm's connections winnowing the actual accessible space, that's dramatically bigger in practice than any realistic amount of spatial distortion the Shadow brings into play because <i>the Shadow is a singular reflection of the world</i>, no matter how distorted it sometimes gets \u2014 it's shaped by the perspectives of the living world on the other side of the Gauntlet, the less human activity in a location to thicken the Gauntlet the <i>less</i> distorted the Shadow tends to be on average, and the fact that everything's perspectives are feeding into the same space means there's only so much &quot;this space feels bigger because it's inhabited by fingernail-sized bugs&quot; can skew the scale of anywhere that hasn't been carved out by a god or subject to a similar level of plot device.<br /> <br /> It's a different branch of the metaphysics, but the material on the limits of Supernal Verges is salient here as a storytelling tool: the Shadow is defined primarily by reflecting the world as it is, with things like entire horrible alternate-universe cities or phantom mountains where the Firstborn dwell being legendary outlier locations. Even with the assumption of frugal set-dressing in Oneiric memory-realms, a popular tree in a national park is reflected in the Astral on three different layers, one of those layers has copies of it for every individual person who remembers it, and another layer may have multiple thematically distinct archetypes of it for different categories of people who know about it.<br /> <br /> All of this is setting aside that I don't think &quot;the Astral is as big as the sky&quot; was the point of the line being quoted and that all of the above makes it plain that at bare minimum the Shadow needs to lean heavily into outliers to approach the scales that the Astral easily surpasses due to not being confined to connections to real geography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T18:52:44-07:00","id":1563519,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say to which degree any mind is really able to create a representation of everything they experience, much less to give such representations adequate proportions.<br /> <br /> Both the Earth and the universe at large are too good at doing things in unimaginable scales in the literal sense: not just big, but big enough that while we can mathematically comprehend their size, we have no parameter to picture it without heavily simplifying distortions.<br /> <br /> So... Is any Astral representation proportional to the actual phenomena or places? I highly doubt. Very few people are capable of forming a proportional mental picture of their city, and the actual populated area is so small that even if you sum the &quot;mental world&quot; of everyone it will not necessarily cover an area comparable to their proportional share of uninhabited area on Earth. And that's talking about surface, only.<br /> <br /> As a reality that sums up mental experiences and representations, the Astral is unbound by spatial limits, true. But as a reality that sums up the reflections and interpretations of all space and matter in the universe, the Shadow is unbound by limits on what can be or has been experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T19:39:06-07:00","id":1563520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563519#post1563519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to say to which degree any mind is really able to create a representation of everything they experience, much less to give such representations adequate proportions.</div> </div> </div> </div>An individual human soul is capable of reproducing events with sufficient fidelity that going through the Oneiros to reexamine memories is one way to get a better picture of what actually happened without the distortions of conscious recollection, and the Temenos gets away with generating scenarios live and incorporating them into the zeitgeist because it's created by multiple human souls. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So... Is any Astral representation proportional to the actual phenomena or places? I highly doubt. Very few people are capable of forming a proportional mental picture of their city, and the actual populated area is so small that even if you sum the &quot;mental world&quot; of everyone it will not necessarily cover an area comparable to their proportional share of uninhabited area on Earth. And that's talking about surface, only. </div> </div> </div>Going back to the Temenos again, the Metropolis is both the archetypal Realm of cities and the Astral representation of every city in human conception. It is populated by the Astral reflections of people's public personas and whole swathes of personlike individuals who only exist as everything from living set-dressing to collectively-imagined figures, and the collective human unconscious is sophisticated enough that, where the actors spawned by a single soul will tend to ignore intruders or address them as though they were the viewpoint character/dreamer, the contents of the Temenos can roll visitors into a thematically appropriate narrative and more consistently pass for reality, being the midpoint on the Astral continuum that continues to the Anima Mundi feeling more real than material reality (whether due to proximity to the Supernal shores or the emotional rawness of things like the Ecstatic Wind).<br /> <br /> At the bare minimum Temenos realms are living worlds of their own beyond the limits of poking around in someone's memories or examining metaphorical representations of their hangups, their most prominent figures explicitly come in multiple versions by audience, and even within the limits of resonant ideas &quot;a substantial amount of the collective unconscious is made from works of fiction&quot; means Goetia live in places that bear only basic resemblance to material reality and those places are real enough to support spells cast in line with their themes and aesthetics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a reality that sums up mental experiences and representations, the Astral is unbound by spatial limits, true. But as a reality that sums up the reflections and interpretations of all space and matter in the universe, the Shadow is unbound by limits on what can be or has been experienced. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that this is very explicitly not how the Shadow works as a place where spirits are born, in practical terms the Shadow outside of the Earth is vastly irrelevant to the Chronicles setting as-presented except when bits of it are brought where they aren't supposed to be and cause problems due to poor interfacing. Most of the problems that the Shadow causes for werewolves and other concerned parties stem from conceptual borders and human involvement.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is important because it's close to material reality and has broad concrete influence over its phenomena. It can do that without trying to equivocate on whether its spatial dimensions can outpace the entirety of significant subjective experience in the realm of souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T23:22:22-07:00","id":1563524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563520#post1563520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow is important because it's close to material reality and has broad concrete influence over its phenomena. It can do that without trying to equivocate on whether its spatial dimensions can outpace the entirety of significant subjective experience in the realm of souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>And likewise the Astral is important because it interfaces with human minds and can bring to the table the full realm of culture, meaning and abstraction, and can do that without trying to equivocate on whether its spatial dimensions can outpace the entirety of a mostly unknown universe beyond human references.<br /> <br /> Being relevant or not is mostly immaterial to this tangent, even because any aspect of any Realm must first be conceptually defined before becoming relevant. And I don't think anyone here questions how easy it is to make anything about the Astral relevant to a game, while exploring space in the Shadow would be a rather particular kind of game.<br /> <br /> Your descriptions also fully ignore the point I made: however big you think the entirety of significant subjective experience in the realm of souls is, the comparison is with the entirety of objective reality outside the need for souls or subjective experience, which is <i>by definition</i> an unknowable quantity. As is anything we say about the Shadow beyond the Moon since we only know it through spirits already within our influence sphere and as such compromise as data: we don't know if entering the area change them to what we see.<br /> <br /> I fully understand the underlying philosophical concept you're starting from, the capacity of subjective reality to multiply instantiations of the world and of impossible worlds would be inherently &quot;bigger&quot; than reality as it encompasses and then expands.<br /> <br /> What I'm doing is reject this as fact. Because it is philosophically objectionable. It assumes a lot about both human experience and reality beyond this experience. Objectively it faces a lot of real challenges as several experiments can demonstrate the innate limitations of what subjective experience can really encompass, giving us insight on where it fails.<br /> <br /> Not that it proves the opposite, but those other perspectives demonstrate the assumption is fragile, a possibility open to debate at best. It has no bearing on the fictional setting, either, but the setting accepts and benefits from the lack of a definitive answer. The Astral improves upon conscious experience, making it factually bigger than objective experience by orders of magnitude. The Shadow also improves upon physical reality, though, and this reality is itself bigger in a fiction where untold supernatural phenomena may exist beyond our knowledge and perception.<br /> <br /> The only true answer for those questions in the game if taken that seriously is that all those realms are incomprehensibly large and of isn't possible to meaningfully measure them. What we can do at best is make some educated guesses and be honest about assumptions and their limitations when doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T02:11:42-07:00","id":1563527,"title":"","content":"I'm actually agreeing with Satchel. There's a relevant distinction between the Sidereal Wastes and the hypothetical Shadow of deep space on at least the grounds of the fact that the former has a more innate mechanism for exploring its more distant and ambiguous reaches, and there's at least a premise that what mages might discover there is more immediately or broadly useful (if largely in a form of being an effective source of Arcane Beats).<br /> <br /> I also feel as though the reference to limits of effective means to mentally model things might constitute some wires being crossed. I think it bears noting that the Anima Mundi is not the human conception of the Earth and wider universe; it is the world beyond humanity's apparent conception of itself. Animal Avatars aren't big because of their sense of proportion to humans, they're big because you're in the Astral reflection of the ecosystem, where those things possess greater conceptual significance.<br /> <br /> The presentation of the limits of human comprehension in this equation are not of the Anima Mundi being only a vague approximation of reality, they're in the fact that a human mind trying to project into that Astral layer needs a protective shell to not be overwhelmed and Soul Shocked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T02:57:21-07:00","id":1563528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563514#post1563514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair point, but I'm not aware of Mages actually travelling there...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe other people remember better than me, but I'm sure Bill Bridges, the original developer of <i>Awakening</i> stated in a Q&amp;A that supernal magic was only meant to work as far as the moon (no idea if that included the moon itself or not).<br /> <br /> At the very least, that seems like it might have been the working assumption for the first half decade or so of Awakening. The Thrice-Great are written in a manner that suggests they don't have much direct contact with space, whilst the Bellerophon Society in <i>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</i> apparently needed a space ship to go to Mars (or at least other mages thought that was what they were up to).<br /> <br /> However, <i>Astral Realms</i> specifically mentions on page 160 that you absolutely can teleport to Mars if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, any mage interested in doing this must first ask herself why she is interested in visiting a lifeless and hostile world. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T06:22:09-07:00","id":1563532,"title":"","content":"This feels to me like it's not a Simple Question or a Simple Answer anymore, and could warrant its own thread to continue discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T18:48:38-07:00","id":1563552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563528#post1563528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Maybe other people remember better than me, but I'm sure Bill Bridges, the original developer of <i>Awakening</i> stated in a Q&amp;A that supernal magic was only meant to work as far as the moon (no idea if that included the moon itself or not).</b><br /> <br /> At the very least, that seems like it might have been the working assumption for the first half decade or so of Awakening. The Thrice-Great are written in a manner that suggests they don't have much direct contact with space, whilst the Bellerophon Society in <i>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</i> apparently needed a space ship to go to Mars (or at least other mages thought that was what they were up to).<br /> <br /> However, <i>Astral Realms</i> specifically mentions on page 160 that you absolutely can teleport to Mars if you want.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that stated? I might be misremembering, but I think it was about finding the right sympatethic connections, not that magic did not work. As a poster in anothr forum said, <i>&quot;you CAN teleport someone to the black hole in the center of the galaxy, but how are you getting a piece of it in the first place to establish the connection and not dying in the process?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That opens the question, is sunlight tangible/significant (for lack of a better term) and connected enough to allow you to shunt someone into the corona? After all it was there 8 minutes ago (the approximate time it takes light to reach Earth from the Sun), it was literally part of the sun not that long ago and one of its biggest symbolic associations is with the sun itself.<br /> <br /> What about neutrinos if you somehow get hold of one? How much mass/size/relation does a connection need? Which type of connections get valid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T19:24:33-07:00","id":1563553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563552#post1563552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That opens the question, is sunlight tangible/significant (for lack of a better term) and connected enough to allow you to shunt someone into the corona? After all it was there 8 minutes ago (the approximate time it takes light to reach Earth from the Sun), it was literally part of the sun not that long ago and one of its biggest symbolic associations is with the sun itself.<br /> <br /> What about neutrinos if you somehow get hold of one? How much mass/size/relation does a connection need? Which type of connections get valid?</div> </div> </div> </div>No on both counts for the same reason that starlight isn't sufficient to teleport you to Sirius, with a side of &quot;this is another angle on 'being able to see someone does not constitute a sympathetic connection to them.'&quot; Unless you are operating in a vastly different worldstate from the one the game is built for, practically anything subatomic lacks the concrete narrative presence needed to serve as a symbolic referent for anything else.<br /> <br /> If a metaphysical reason is needed, extraterrestrial light has undergone several substantial changes from its origin point in even that very short time, such that at the bare minimum a sunbeam has traversed an AU, crossed the orbit of the Earth, and entered the atmosphere, to say nothing of any particular reflection or refraction it's undergone closer to the surface \u2014 you might as well be trying to use a lock of your hair to divine the childhood pastimes of your great-grandmother with how far the starting point has gotten from your destination.<br /> <br /> Get to a part of the cosmology where you can get bottled sunlight that <i>is</i> a piece of the sun with the attendant mystical connections and this is less of an issue, but the closest thing the games have established to that is the Hedge, where the locals seldom leave the borderland and everything has a commensurate price, and that's without getting into the usual issue that third-party teleportation is a spell-intensive process that you absolutely have better alternatives to as an Adept if all you want to do is put them in a situation they are unlikely to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T22:09:08-07:00","id":1563557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563553#post1563553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No on both counts for the same reason that starlight isn't sufficient to teleport you to Sirius, with a side of &quot;this is another angle on 'being able to see someone does not constitute a sympathetic connection to them.'&quot; Unless you are operating in a vastly different worldstate from the one the game is built for, practically anything subatomic lacks the concrete narrative presence needed to serve as a symbolic referent for anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that stated or inferred somewhere? Because I got more of a &quot;the game is silent about this so the ST decides&quot; than a straight &quot;stop using physics to work outside the bounded setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> My take is more that the books avoid talking on the matter of extraterrestrial adventures than it is a big no for the setting.<br /> <br /> Light reflected is a very different thing from light generated, and it's not subatomic: you can get a pretty big amount of light without much effort. A connection with the sun in particular is sound, as light is the means through which it delivers both the clarity of day and life-giving warmth that defines it.<br /> <br /> What's more likely is that few Mages care to use light as a sympathetic connection to a star, including the sun, because that's... Not really useful for much. There's a ton of simpler ways to disintegrate someone and not much else to do with a star.<br /> <br /> But if a Mage decided to explore stars as either a Mystery or whatever else they think of... Why not? Astronomy is the oldest science, even for a human centered game it isn't antithetical to it to have a character that fixates on stars.<br /> <br /> Now, I do remember Forsaken 1st edition had a limit a little above the Moon for exploring the Shadow. Not sure it's still there, but I wouldn't find it strange for this limit to actually exist in Mage, I only find it unnecessary, maybe even harmful to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T03:36:06-07:00","id":1563559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563552#post1563552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. It's <i>not</i>.<br /> <br /> Bill Bridges, the original developer mentioned it in a Q&amp;A which was posted (or possibly reposted) to an older iteration of this forum. I believe it was already posted when I joined that forum in 2007.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I might be misremembering, but I think it was about finding the right sympatethic connections, not that magic did not work. </div> </div> </div>It was more specific than that. Like, someone asked if magic worked in space, and Bridges answered that it did, but only as far as the Moon.<br /> <br /> It reads as very arbitrary unless you know that it's an idea from <i>Ars Magica</i>, the grandparent of <i>Awakening</i>, which in turn borrowed it from Aristotelian physics which is the basis for much of the magic that Awakening riffs on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a poster in anothr forum said, <i>&quot;you CAN teleport someone to the black hole in the center of the galaxy, but how are you getting a piece of it in the first place to establish the connection and not dying in the process?&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Again, <i>Astral Realms</i> more or less literally says that. My reason for bringing it up is that it explains why early Awakening doesn't really address space (as well as why when it does, it's kinda odd).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T05:51:57-07:00","id":1563563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563559#post1563559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing. It's <i>not</i>.<br /> <br /> Bill Bridges, the original developer mentioned it in a Q&amp;A which was posted (or possibly reposted) to an older iteration of this forum. I believe it was already posted when I joined that forum in 2007.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was more specific than that. Like, someone asked if magic worked in space, and Bridges answered that it did, but only as far as the Moon.<br /> <br /> It reads as very arbitrary unless you know that it's an idea from <i>Ars Magica</i>, the grandparent of <i>Awakening</i>, which in turn borrowed it from Aristotelian physics which is the basis for much of the magic that Awakening riffs on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, <i>Astral Realms</i> more or less literally says that. My reason for bringing it up is that it explains why early Awakening doesn't really address space (as well as why when it does, it's kinda odd).</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of what Bridges may have answered. I don't think it is relevant today 20 years and 1 edition later.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense, the moon does have significance in terms of Werewolf and Luna as a Rank 8 entity. But having her power affect Supernal magic is silly.<br /> <br /> There is also an Emanation Realm on Mars. And I think we've got space rocks from Mars, which would probably allow a Sympathetic connection.<br /> <br /> (Using star light is odd since that is sensory range nit Sympathetic... But that is an aside).<br /> <br /> And finally, we have a booking with potential space travel (is it a shard?) and a quote from DaveB about the Exarchs literally rewriting the rules of reality, which is justification for Archmasters being able to do the same in Imperial Mysteries. *If* Supernal magic didn't work beyond the moon, you would damn well think that Imperial Mysteries would have mentioned it.<br /> <br /> Of course if that works at your table, more power to you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T06:08:18-07:00","id":1563564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563563#post1563563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It makes no sense, the moon does have significance in terms of Werewolf and Luna as a Rank 8 entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that relationship goes the other way around, or it at least more reciprocal. That Luna is a powerful Shadow spirit because the moon is significant.<br /> <br /> Certainly, there are more references to empowering engagement with the Moon through magic across the games than invoking its spirit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But having her power affect Supernal magic is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ruins of Troy affect Supernal magic. The western reaches of the Atlantic Ocean affected Supernal magic in the Golden Age of Piracy. The aura of celebrity in Los Angeles affects Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all Mysteries attached to specific regions in the setting chapter of the core book and Tome of the Pentacle amounts to &quot;this is how local idiosyncrasies affect Supernal magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> A statement of &quot;casting magic on things out in further space is Withstood to a degree that makes it nigh impossible&quot; is perfectly in line with other Mysteries as a way to establish certain boundaries.<br /> <br /> Never mind things like how the whole Supernal thesis of the Free Council sect is that Supernal magic is affected by human community and culture.<br /> <br /> And then there's this one line from the core that I never seem to see other people bring up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even though the Awakened believe the Supernal casts the light of reality as pure symbols, mages debate whether the fundamentals of Creation are eternal, or are generated elsewhere \u2014 perhaps even in the Fallen World \u2014 and through some incomprehensible process, exalted on high and sent below again. Mages know the legends of Ascension, where mortals become Supernal Forms. What else might rise up from the Lie, insinuating itself within ultimate truth? What slithers between the poles of Creation, contradicting the Supernal/ Fallen divide? </div> </div> </div>So it's at least ambiguous to people in character whether things that do not originate as Supernal might have power to affect it, or even fundamentally alter it. You could have a Thyrsus who is Obsessed with the question of whether the Moon having a godlike spirit is the kind of thing that fed back into the Supernal to be the thing that actually created power for Moon symbolism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T06:17:41-07:00","id":1563565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563557#post1563557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that stated or inferred somewhere? Because I got more of a &quot;the game is silent about this so the ST decides&quot; than a straight &quot;stop using physics to work outside the bounded setting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage needs to be able to recognize the symbolism of a Yantra to be able to leverage that symbolism, sympathy is sufficiently particular that temporal sympathy requires a correspondence to the time that you're trying to view/evoke/travel to, and spatial sympathy's descending order of metaphysical closeness is easy to compare to the notion that you can't use the fact that someone was born in or lives in a country to teleport to that country while they're outside of it or scry on its president. &quot;Starlight comes from stars&quot; does not outpace the fact that most starlight is barely a material piece of a specific star at all in the same way that a random passerby on the street about whom you know nothing at all is not even close enough to be considered a Weak connection to you even if they happen to live on that street.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic connections are significant enough that the spell for turning the faint semblance of one from physical contact into a mechanically definite one requires that contact to last for at least the system's smallest unit of narrative time (still loosely measured in seconds) and 2e lacks 1e's mechanical categories of sympathetic connection below casual acquaintance. Tome of the Pentacle has a whole section dedicated to explaining why would-be archaeomancers typically visit the locations they're investigating instead of relying on secondhand connections for reasons that can be summarized as &quot;sympathy is particular,&quot; itself further refining on the corebook's stipulation that a material sympathy Yantra represents the subject as it is now.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic specifically doesn't occupy the framework where ground-level PCs can play with abstractions as though they were concrete phenomena like some powers available to monsters do \u2014 see the whole observed deal with the Mask of Eyes not working on the known principles of sympathy, or Darklings from Changeling being able to merge with immaterial phenomena like smoke and sunlight to become temporarily intangible, or Unchained demons being able to do things like conceptually redirect or move injuries. 2e defines the Supernal World mages see as where the concrete and the abstract mix, and explicitly states that without archmastery it's impossible to Veil something against abstract concepts or forces.<br /> <br /> On the other end of comparison, Mage shares a setting with Promethean, where the repeatable means of making one of the Created involve recombination of discernible parts of a human body (which tears itself apart if it fails) and the main successful peripheral methods of using Azoth to create life from parts of other life are all forms of cloning or mutating an existing specimen \u2014 an Extempore can get away with being a human form spun together from desert sands or an archetypal idea because their whole struggle is being practically non-repeatable phenomena even by Created standards and needing to figure out how to reproduce their condition to end it, but most Prometheans whose creation rituals work regularly are ones made from human parts big enough that the likes of the Residual Memory Merit make sense in the same vein as urban legends about organ transplants changing people's personalities.<br /> <br /> The inference, in short, is that nothing about the game <i>does</i> support using extremely small, very fast, functionally interchangeable particles as &quot;pieces of&quot; an extremely distant subject, but the game <i>does</i> take pains to emphasize the limits of sympathy in multiple places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T10:02:42-07:00","id":1563572,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> Please, just read what you're quoting before replying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless of what Bridges may have answered. I don't think it is relevant today 20 years and 1 edition later. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>My reason for bringing it up is that it explains why early Awakening doesn't really address space (as well as why when it does, it's kinda odd</b>). </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes no sense, the moon does have significance in terms of Werewolf and Luna as a Rank 8 entity. But having her power affect Supernal magic is silly. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>It reads as very arbitrary unless you know that it's an idea from <i>Ars Magica</i>, the grandparent of <i>Awakening</i>, which in turn borrowed it from Aristotelian physics which is the basis for much of the magic that Awakening riffs on.</b>\u200b </div> </div> </div>Additionally, it would presumably have been more developed if it wasn't dumped as an idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is also an Emanation Realm on Mars. And I think we've got space rocks from Mars, which would probably allow a Sympathetic connection. </div> </div> </div>I know. I gave you the page number that literally says that works. <i>Astral Realms</i> page 160.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T23:47:49-07:00","id":1563588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563564#post1563564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much all Mysteries attached to specific regions in the setting chapter of the core book and Tome of the Pentacle amounts to &quot;this is how local idiosyncrasies affect Supernal magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> A statement of &quot;casting magic on things out in further space is Withstood to a degree that makes it nigh impossible&quot; is perfectly in line with other Mysteries as a way to establish certain boundaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think those are in the same line of saying &quot;Supernal Magic doesn't work beyond the Moon&quot;. One thing is to say Mysteries affect Magic, and as such there may be a Mystery in the Moon's orbit that interferes with Magic. But it's other to say that Magic as we understand it doesn't exist outside this area and exploring it is not a valid part of the game.<br /> <br /> Which is of little relevance as it is an old idea, never formalized in the books and evidently dropped long ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563565#post1563565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inference, in short, is that nothing about the game <i>does</i> support using extremely small, very fast, functionally interchangeable particles as &quot;pieces of&quot; an extremely distant subject, but the game <i>does</i> take pains to emphasize the limits of sympathy in multiple places.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is how much you extrapolate from that and assumes such extrapolations as fact.<br /> <br /> First of all stop talking about light as inherently limited to subatomic particles in this exercise. Macroscopic objects are also agglomerations of interchangeable subatomic particles. We're talking about using a sizeable amount of light, enough to be semantically understood as a thing in its own.<br /> <br /> Second, I was very clear that in this context I'm talking about stars being light generators, not merely places where it was. It's absurd to the point of being disingenuous to compare it with using a person as a sympathetic connection to another because they live in the same street. It was more like using the lava of a volcano as the connection to the volcano, or you as the connection to your mother.<br /> <br /> You are arbitrarily using and discarding the fact the main unit of relevance is symbolism, which is an abstract construction, not a physical fact. If you can't see a symbolic link between light in large amounts and the phenomenon that make it in such amounts to the point that this light is both how we know about it and what establish its presence in our lives and all its effects, that is more you disagreeing with the symbolism than it being weak or non existent objectively.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it would be particularly strong as a connection, either. Only that the possibility is there and I don't find it convincing that the actual game doesn't admit any way to use this connection, even if through exceptional work. The Mage may be required to gather enough light in some fashion, or find any other solution to focus the sympathetic connection. It may still be weak and hard to use.<br /> <br /> But &quot;light doesn't count because light doesn't count&quot;, unless you have a better argument for it I don't see as really what the game defines as a hard limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T01:11:26-07:00","id":1563590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563588#post1563588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all stop talking about light as inherently limited to subatomic particles in this exercise. Macroscopic objects are also agglomerations of interchangeable subatomic particles. We're talking about using a sizeable amount of light, enough to be semantically understood as a thing in its own.<br /> <br /> Second, I was very clear that in this context I'm talking about stars being light generators, not merely places where it was. It's absurd to the point of being disingenuous to compare it with using a person as a sympathetic connection to another because they live in the same street. It was more like using the lava of a volcano as the connection to the volcano, or you as the connection to your mother.<br /> <br /> You are arbitrarily using and discarding the fact the main unit of relevance is symbolism, which is an abstract construction, not a physical fact. If you can't see a symbolic link between light in large amounts and the phenomenon that make it in such amounts to the point that this light is both how we know about it and what establish its presence in our lives and all its effects, that is more you disagreeing with the symbolism than it being weak or non existent objectively.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it would be particularly strong as a connection, either. Only that the possibility is there and I don't find it convincing that the actual game doesn't admit any way to use this connection, even if through exceptional work. The Mage may be required to gather enough light in some fashion, or find any other solution to focus the sympathetic connection. It may still be weak and hard to use.<br /> <br /> But &quot;light doesn't count because light doesn't count&quot;, unless you have a better argument for it I don't see as really what the game defines as a hard limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot stop talking about light as a material phenomenon in the discussion of its use as a required component of a type of casting that requires a material component, specifically compared with subatomic particles by the immediate following inquiry about neutrinos.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the fact that you are talking about stars as light generators is immaterial to the fact that the question that prompted this discussion was &quot;can you use sunlight to teleport someone to the corona of the sun?&quot;<br /> <br /> The unit of relevance being symbolism is a limiting factor on what a mage can use as a Yantra because spellcasting is an act of will and imagination. The light of a lamp is not a symbolic referent to the lamp for the purposes of surpassing vast distances either \u2014 you can't use a distant spotlight to sympathetically teleport over the horizon, either, because while you could teleport to the location within range of your senses that corresponds to the part of the beam you can see and even use Forces and Space to bend your perceptions to better see an endpoint that doesn't require you to emerge in midair, the light does not have material sympathy with the lamp any more than you have sympathy with the air you exhaled five minutes ago. Material sympathy Yantras use concrete objects of macroscopic scale for a reason and they are the foundation of this conversation.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness are a setting where multiple frames of reality are actively deceiving the people that inhabit them. The Chronicles of Darkness are a place where matter routinely goes missing without explanation and causality allows for things like the Key to an Avernian Gate always reappearing in the same abandoned house or a mummy emerging from its tomb minutes after it was destroyed. Physics exists and mostly works as we know it to in the real world, but magic does not consistently adhere to physical laws and there is only so far &quot;characters with moderate to major knowledge of the Space Arcanum don't teleport subjects to outer space using sunlight/moonlight/starlight because they don't think it's worth it&quot; can explain why the topic has never come up despite the established curiosity and knowledge bases of the Awakened in the twenty years the line has existed in published form.<br /> <br /> Awakened sympathetic magic requires a Sympathy Yantra, which is a type of Tool Yantra, which the system defines as an item in the absence of mechanics allowing other things to be treated as Tool Yantras. Light is not an item and any attempts to treat it as such require engagement with the fact that the typical Awakened toolkit does not have means of turning light into an item with sympathies that the mage can borrow for Space magic \u2014 air is a similarly insubstantial vector for connection to a subject, and that's much closer to being material. By direct comparison, a lacuna prevents Time magic from being used to examine the history of a rubber tree that was used to make a rubber item being scrutinized; a change in fundamental form has consequences on an object's magical utility even if it's made of the same material, and ubiquitous or diffuse phenomena are not objects.<br /> <br /> I could see a case to be made for splitting hairs over how small a quantity of sand from a beach or desert could serve as a connection to that location, but phenomena that are almost entirely sensory experiences like light or smells are insubstantial enough that while they might serve as vectors for targeting spells via Sensory range or function as Environmental Yantras, they do not have the weight of concrete presence to serve as Tools for sympathetic magic, else you open the door to weird questions like &quot;why do mages need to take solid or liquid samples from things they want to use sympathy on when they could just use little jars full of air or magically preserve the heat from exposure/contact?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T05:53:48-07:00","id":1563593,"title":"","content":"I may have a silly questions this time:<br /> Can a mage autokill someone with a making death or unmaking life spell if it has potency above the victims resistance trait? Not do damage, just kill. Its not in the rote examples and should be a really obvious use of those arcana but im unsure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T06:29:48-07:00","id":1563594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563593#post1563593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have a silly questions this time:<br /> Can a mage autokill someone with a making death or unmaking life spell if it has potency above the victims resistance trait? Not do damage, just kill. Its not in the rote examples and should be a really obvious use of those arcana but im unsure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's one of the specific examples given of an Unmaking spell \u2014 &quot;Life can be snuffed out like a candle&quot; (corebook p125) \u2014 and it's also mentioned in the sidebar two pages afterward about the ability to incapacitate with magic (&quot;I Turn Him Into a Frog!&quot; corebook p127). Instakill spells are Unmaking effects as the step above applying Mana and Reach to Unraveling spells to deal aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T06:31:23-07:00","id":1563595,"title":"","content":"The \u201cI Turn Him Into a Frog!\u201d sidebar says that unmaking spells can do that, but i see no wrong in an equivalent Making spell for Death","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T00:29:44-07:00","id":1563624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563595#post1563595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u201cI Turn Him Into a Frog!\u201d sidebar says that unmaking spells can do that, but i see no wrong in an equivalent Making spell for Death</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unmaking Death example spell brings people back from the dead. I don't think anyone would argue that you can't also kill things using the Death Arcanum...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T05:13:52-07:00","id":1563758,"title":"","content":"A Making of Death or an Unmaking of Life are to me the most straightforward way to make a &quot;Withstand or die&quot; spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativ