-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563816#post1563816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything Nasnasi is an immediate &quot;stop everything, we annihilate them <b>NOW</b>&quot; kind of escalation. Call the Hierarch and Counsilors, the Sentinel, the Adamant Sage if you have one. Nasnasi are attuned to the Abyss and rewarded by destroying reality and the Supernal, they are one of those threats that even the Seers will work with the Pentacle to nuke. Plus the fact the cavaleer abuse of Sleepers will cause indignation. So an extreme reaction if they can confirm it, or have others confirm it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, what do you think that the ordinary mages of the Adamantine Arrow should do face the warning? If you want to answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25364-brunomoonchangeling","name":"BrunoMoonChangeling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T14:45:37-07:00","id":1563839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrunoMoonChangeling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563838#post1563838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, what do you think that the ordinary mages of the Adamantine Arrow should do face the warning? If you want to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they would call the higher ups to lead and coordinate with the other Orders, start organizing to keep people safe, try to get more details on the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T05:01:37-07:00","id":1563852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrunoMoonChangeling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1563838#post1563838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, what do you think that the ordinary mages of the Adamantine Arrow should do face the warning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you've constructed your setting.<br /> <br /> For example, is the Scelesti information from <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> common knowledge? There's heavy implication that that information is kept relatively secret within the Pentacle. Given that at least as the books present it, the character is <i>never</i> going to be trusted after their earlier behaviour, and now, they're telling a group of ordinary mages about the Nasnasi. That's incredibly suspicious behaviour, even if it makes sense from the character's point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T18:59:43-07:00","id":1564061,"title":"","content":"Souls, can they be affected and destroyed, how?<br /> <br /> The mage core<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Souls are insubstantial constructs, wholly invisible except to<br /> Death Sight when properly integrated into a person, and visible as<br /> vague humanoid auras in the Mage Sight of the five subtle Arcana<br /> when removed from a host. They are clearest when viewed under<br /> magic that reveals subjects in Twilight resonating with Death<br /> (such as the Death 2 Attainment), but are not made of ephemera,<br /> so remain insubstantial to ephemeral beings unless they have<br /> Numina or Influences allowing them to manipulate souls. All<br /> Supernal beings may spend one Mana to physically interact with<br /> unattached souls. Mages must use spells to manipulate them.<br /> The origin and destination of souls remains a Mystery even<br /> to the Awakened \u2014 they appear at birth and vanish completely<br /> at the moment of death.<br /> Souls, however, have value, and a number of uses;<br /> \u2022 Destroying a soul is a universally-applicable sacrament<br /> Yantra for a Death, Fate, Mind, Prime, or Spirit spell. </div> </div> </div>Is it a spell? or just a mage ability? if so, which arcana is needed to do it? Can you do it only with the 5 subtle arcana? Do you always need Death to interact with the soul before destruction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T19:28:53-07:00","id":1564062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564061#post1564061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a spell? or just a mage ability? if so, which arcana is needed to do it? Can you do it only with the 5 subtle arcana? Do you always need Death to interact with the soul before destruction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never fully explained, but for simplicity's sake it's feasible to have it require a spell from a Subtle Arcanum from one of the destructive Practices. Reaper Legacies from Left-Hand Path and elsewhere (to say nothing of the Tremere) indicate Death isn't strictly required to interact with souls (particularly not disembodied ones), though Death has the easiest time of doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T01:27:09-07:00","id":1564073,"title":"","content":"Talking about souls, AFAIK they have no proper personality or agency. Has that changed, or are they still just an immaterial fungible battery for Willpower (or maybe better described as engine for the generator)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T05:59:00-07:00","id":1564076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564073#post1564073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about souls, AFAIK they have no proper personality or agency. Has that changed, or are they still just an immaterial fungible battery for Willpower (or maybe better described as engine for the generator)?</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, it has not changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T06:07:32-07:00","id":1564077,"title":"","content":"Familiar questions.<br /> <br /> How do they catch up with you if you are in a fast moving vehicle? <br /> <br /> To clarify, you have a Familiar of any type (Ghost, Goetia, Spirit), you enter a plane and start moving in the sky at high speed. The ephemeral creatures can only interact with other ephemeral things in the same frequency of Twilight, so your Familiar gets stuck on your departure city, as there is no Twilight representation of the plane (except some rare cases) to transport them.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something about their capabilities as Familiars? Can they get draged along with you if you wish it? Or can use Mana/Essence to teleport to you? Because it would mean only mages with the Space arcanum can move around fast and keep their familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T06:23:51-07:00","id":1564078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564077#post1564077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiar questions.<br /> <br /> How do they catch up with you if you are in a fast moving vehicle?<br /> <br /> To clarify, you have a Familiar of any type (Ghost, Goetia, Spirit), you enter a plane and start moving in the sky at high speed. The ephemeral creatures can only interact with other ephemeral things in the same frequency of Twilight, so your Familiar gets stuck on your departure city, as there is no Twilight representation of the plane (except some rare cases) to transport them.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something about their capabilities as Familiars? Can they get draged along with you if you wish it? Or can use Mana/Essence to teleport to you? Because it would mean only mages with the Space arcanum can move around fast and keep their familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use the matching level 2 attainment to make the familiar sit un your lap or hold its hand (1/2 mana for the entire trip)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T07:04:11-07:00","id":1564080,"title":"","content":"First things first, are you sure it was intended by the rules that things in Twilight don't &quot;stay&quot; within vehicles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T09:32:31-07:00","id":1564084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564080#post1564080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First things first, are you sure it was intended by the rules that things in Twilight don't &quot;stay&quot; within vehicles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the description of Twilight says not everything has an equivalent, so there is no vehicle to stay inside of.<br /> <br /> As per the description, bolded parts mine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without Manifestations or magic, ephemeral entities in the<br /> material world exist in the state of Twilight. To beings in Twilight,<br /> physical objects appear pale and semi-translucent; light sources are<br /> dimmed, and sounds are distorted. They can only touch and inter\u00ad<br /> act with Twilight objects, phenomena, and creatures comprised of<br /> the same kind of ephemera. Attacks pass through a Twilight being,<br /> and <b>even solid concrete in the material world is no more hindrance<br /> than fog.</b> <b><u><i>Sometimes</i></u> structures and objects can enter the state of<br /> Twilight, such as the ghostly reflections of destroyed buildings or<br /> items, as well as those made immaterial through magic \u2014 these are<br /> entirely solid to Twilight entities of the same type of ephemera.</b><br /> Movement through Twilight roughly corresponds to that<br /> of the material world, even though there is no gravity, wind,<br /> or pressure. </div> </div> </div>So that would say that there is no vehicle to stay in Twilight AND that the real world vehicle is not even solid to them. How are they to stay inside something like that then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T09:33:54-07:00","id":1564085,"title":"","content":"The description of ghosts that they 'hug the material terrain' rather than being subject to gravity suggests to me that they can probably stay attached to the floor of a moving vehicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T10:45:24-07:00","id":1564088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564084#post1564084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they to stay inside something like that then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same way they aren't left in space behind the planet, as the floor isn't solid to them either. It's a referential for position, whatever the physics behind it may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T15:14:39-07:00","id":1564097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564073#post1564073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about souls, AFAIK they have no proper personality or agency. Has that changed, or are they still just an immaterial fungible battery for Willpower (or maybe better described as engine for the generator)?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of specific Mysteries relating to them, a disembodied soul remains where it is if separated from its owner for the duration of a soul-stealing spell or subsequent attachment/storage, after which it returns to them if they're still alive or moves on to wherever souls go after death if they're dead. Spells and other effects to manipulate souls may leverage aspects of their owners deliberately or as side-effects, but that falls firmly within the realm of specific Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The typical business of souls in the world is to be in bodies; if a soul is outside of a body, something Weird is going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T18:28:47-07:00","id":1564107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564062#post1564062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never fully explained, but for simplicity's sake it's feasible to have it require a spell from a Subtle Arcanum from one of the destructive Practices. Reaper Legacies from Left-Hand Path and elsewhere (to say nothing of the Tremere) indicate Death isn't strictly required to interact with souls (particularly not disembodied ones), though Death has the easiest time of doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reaping Relinquishment (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) allows destroying a soul for relinquishing a spell safely, so either at third level or lower with Death you could do it. And the spells says that the soul has to be either in the caster power through a different Death spell or contained in a Soul Jar, so that puts some boundaries on how it is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-16-2026, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T11:03:45-07:00","id":1564124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564077#post1564077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiar questions.<br /> <br /> How do they catch up with you if you are in a fast moving vehicle?<br /> <br /> To clarify, you have a Familiar of any type (Ghost, Goetia, Spirit), you enter a plane and start moving in the sky at high speed. The ephemeral creatures can only interact with other ephemeral things in the same frequency of Twilight, so your Familiar gets stuck on your departure city, as there is no Twilight representation of the plane (except some rare cases) to transport them.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something about their capabilities as Familiars? Can they get draged along with you if you wish it? Or can use Mana/Essence to teleport to you? Because it would mean only mages with the Space arcanum can move around fast and keep their familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually disagree with the others and agree with yourself that a fairly straight reading of the description of Twilight means that planes or any other form of vehicle are not particularly privileged for interactions within it. Things adhere to the logic of the terrain, but otherwise everything else is experienced as intangible beyond relevant magic to make it otherwise.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Familiars are not afforded any kind of intimacy that privileges them remaining in the presence of the mages to whom they are bonded. It's not some deep loss or transgression if they're greatly separated physically.<br /> <br /> So yes, if a mage gets on a plane and flies far away, they're leaving their familiar behind in the same way that they're leaving their house or their cabalmates behind. If mage or familiar wants them to go together, they make arrangements to that effect, same as they would for anything else.<br /> <br /> So, assuming a familiar that is not itself capable of flight and moving at fairly high speeds, either it Materializes and gets on the plane as well, or the mage arranges for some form of magic to allow it to keep adhering to something on the plane. Cast a Weaving of Prime on your suitcase and let them hitch along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T12:02:20-07:00","id":1564126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564124#post1564124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, Familiars are not afforded any kind of intimacy that privileges them remaining in the presence of the mages to whom they are bonded. It's not some deep loss or transgression if they're greatly separated physically.</div> </div> </div> </div>They treat their bonded mage's Signature Nimbus as a relevant condition/location for the purposes of reforming after discorporation.<br /> <br /> I feel the fact that the book does not see fit to expressly state that invisible entities occupying a large-scale frame of reference that happens to be a mobile structure move with it owes more to the general assumption of the game that action is going to be taking place on solid ground than any deeper metaphysical implication about the ability of planes, trains, camper vans, and boats to deny a mage access to their disembodied familiars. Phantom hitchhikers are an entire acknowledged category of ghost in this franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T15:00:30-07:00","id":1564130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564126#post1564126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They treat their bonded mage's Signature Nimbus as a relevant condition/location for the purposes of reforming after discorporation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I guess having an atypical Condition to reform at does barely count as a privilege of proximity. So all a Familiar has to do to take advantage of that is painfully self-destruct and possibly spend a period of several days in hibernation and Essence regain until they can move around again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the fact that the book does not see fit to expressly state that invisible entities occupying a large-scale frame of reference that happens to be a mobile structure move with it owes more to the general assumption of the game that action is going to be taking place on solid ground than any deeper metaphysical implication about the ability of planes, trains, camper vans, and boats to deny a mage access to their disembodied familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>A person can project whatever they want into what a book doesn't say, but I think that when a book does say &quot;things are intangible unless there's something weird going on&quot;, it's a shorter path to things like vehicles not having a useful presence as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phantom hitchhikers are an entire acknowledged category of ghost in this franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that refer to phantoms who incidentally hitchhike, or phantoms where being hitchhikers is their gimmick?<br /> <br /> If the latter, does that imply that cars are tangible for any ghost who wants to use them, or that some ghosts can treat cars as anchors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T15:18:47-07:00","id":1564131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564130#post1564130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person can project whatever they want into what a book doesn't say, but I think that when a book does say &quot;things are intangible unless there's something weird going on&quot;, it's a shorter path to things like vehicles not having a useful presence as a matter of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think it's a shorter path to get to &quot;You can have ghosts on moving boats&quot; than &quot;any ephemeral being that isn't specifically attached to a vehicle or its passengers cannot stay on it&quot; in a game that is not premised around the occult having bizarre interactions with the physical world.<br /> <br /> Ghosts being able to walk through walls that weren't there before they died or spirits being able to ignore unwarded closed doors is a statement about relative terrain that exists to make those entities more threatening, unsettling, or mysterious. The same cannot be said for treating multi-person vehicles large enough to stand in as Not A Place for the purpose of a narrative in which any actors need the ability to stand on the floor unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does that refer to phantoms who incidentally hitchhike, or phantoms where being hitchhikers is their gimmick?<br /> <br /> If the latter, does that imply that cars are tangible for any ghost who wants to use them, or that some ghosts can treat cars as anchors? </div> </div> </div>The specific example I am thinking of is Anchored to an entire stretch of road, but thank you for bringing up the other way that the reading you're supporting doesn't make sense, which is that the Anchor Condition having a distance limit in no way physically forces a ghost to remain within its range.<br /> <br /> If an ephemeral being needs a Condition that specifically pulls it around (and none of them do this, not even the Fettered Condition) then exorcism is a simple matter of putting an Anchor or Fettered subject in the back of a van and driving down the highway for an hour. Since that's ridiculous on its face as a default state of affairs, we assume a moving location is still a location for the purposes of stories that aren't relying on that location being familiar-proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T23:39:47-07:00","id":1564136,"title":"","content":"Even outside considerations about Familiars, but simply going by spirits and other Twilight denizens, I think it very weird to have this hard rule that vehicles are intangible for them.<br /> <br /> Bringing strange entities with you is an entire trope and common folklore motif. The idea is not particularly tied to the entity being capable at attaching to things or something, and isn't even tied to a particular kind of entity.<br /> <br /> Particularly in this case I don't think it fair to call this interpretation a &quot;projection&quot;. The idea is intuitive. A lot of people would naturally have this understanding. The way it's written may be technically clear, but it's easily something that they could have missed for thinking it obvious rather than intended like that.<br /> <br /> This should have received more attention since actual games will face all sorts of liminal cases. If the God-Machine, or just a really big machine, moves a mountain, do the spirits stay or are they moved? Where's the litmus test of what's a vehicle and what's ground for the entity?<br /> <br /> In the specific case, I don't see a benefit for the game, either. If a Familiar can't get into a car, the Mage will have to be on foot whenever they want to keep the Familiar they paid for? How is the fiction benefitted by having to left your Familiar behind when traveling abroad? It isn't even in tune with the narrative of a Familiar, as yes, those entities are totally expected to be close by to their masters, always.<br /> <br /> Sure, the book is written the way it's is and the methods to solve this are there, particularly fetter, so whatever floats your boat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T01:37:51-07:00","id":1564211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564061#post1564061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souls, can they be affected and destroyed, how?<br /> <br /> The mage core<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is it a spell? or just a mage ability? if so, which arcana is needed to do it? Can you do it only with the 5 subtle arcana? Do you always need Death to interact with the soul before destruction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as sa universal sacrament Yantra that could be +1-+3 bonus. Since sacraments have that range. Would it default to +3 given the severity of severing a soul or otherwise finding one in a soul jar, or would it be limited to +2 since you don't typically go to an Otherworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T02:43:22-07:00","id":1564212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564211#post1564211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as sa universal sacrament Yantra that could be +1-+3 bonus. Since sacraments have that range. Would it default to +3 given the severity of severing a soul or otherwise finding one in a soul jar, or would it be limited to +2 since you don't typically go to an Otherworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally go for +3, but it's hard to say what was intended. The text reads rather disjointedly to me, as if there was a revision at some point and the text and effect drifted apart. Like, the text implies that it's the magical nature of the item that makes it +3, not simply the fact it's not from the material... But then that's not how the effect is written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T03:11:25-07:00","id":1564267,"title":"","content":"How do you describe that the spell did not manage to overcome a resistance trait &quot; you cast the spell and nothing happens&quot;? &quot;your will was pushed away&quot;? &quot;The power was not strong enough and nothing happened&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T14:28:45-07:00","id":1564279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564267#post1564267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you describe that the spell did not manage to overcome a resistance trait &quot; you cast the spell and nothing happens&quot;? &quot;your will was pushed away&quot;? &quot;The power was not strong enough and nothing happened&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell has visible effects, it doesn't produce them. Otherwise the character will have to use appropriate mystical senses to check the actual Potency of the spell in execution and/or the relevant Withstand ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T15:40:00-07:00","id":1564314,"title":"","content":"Is <i>Lure &amp; Repel</i> a good rote to take ? What kind of ways have you seen it used ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-25T00:28:05-07:00","id":1564330,"title":"","content":"Got a question around how magic and the dream form work. On p.248 it mentions that magic affects things as normal when in the Astral and your magic pretty much works the same (you can use matter to affect a chair, same as the real world) but how would this apply to affecting your dream form stats? Could you just use a Life Perfecting to increase your stats as normal or would that not apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26144-eshangray","name":"eshangray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-25T01:34:38-07:00","id":1564331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eshangray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564330#post1564330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you just use a Life Perfecting to increase your stats as normal or would that not apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <i>Astral Realms</i> page 16 uses this as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T04:37:08-07:00","id":1564350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564314#post1564314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is <i>Lure &amp; Repel</i> a good rote to take ? What kind of ways have you seen it used ?</div> </div> </div> </div>How often will the character use it? Like I'm sure some characters spend a majority of their time in places like the Amazon jungle, in which case, great. You have a powerful utility spell. Most characters don't.<br /> <br /> The other side is, how often will you get use of 4 reach? Instant Cast, Advanced Duration, and Advanced Scale, along with one of the spell specific reaches seems fairly reasonable.<br /> <br /> Using it on humans means varying resolve scores, which give them Yantra bonus (and maybe spending a reach to swap primary factor to potency) leaves you fairly easily hitting potency 5/6, so pretty good? may be less likely to be a Act of Hubris than the equivalent Mind spell.<br /> <br /> Again, how often do you think it will come in handy for that character?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-26T18:21:29-07:00","id":1564375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564350#post1564350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How often will the character use it? Like I'm sure some characters spend a majority of their time in places like the Amazon jungle, in which case, great. You have a powerful utility spell. Most characters don't.<br /> <br /> The other side is, how often will you get use of 4 reach? Instant Cast, Advanced Duration, and Advanced Scale, along with one of the spell specific reaches seems fairly reasonable.<br /> <br /> Using it on humans means varying resolve scores, which give them Yantra bonus (and maybe spending a reach to swap primary factor to potency) leaves you fairly easily hitting potency 5/6, so pretty good? may be less likely to be a Act of Hubris than the equivalent Mind spell.<br /> <br /> Again, how often do you think it will come in handy for that character?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the uses I see are keeping Sleepers away from a dangerous area, making an opponent attract all the Sleeper attention to deeply inconvenience them, driving opponents out of their Sanctums or equivalent base, break up a fight by repelling people from an area, repelling pathogens and dangerous animals and attracting aid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T19:49:12-07:00","id":1564403,"title":"","content":"In the Free Council, can someone hold Strategos and Syndic positions at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-28T21:12:33-07:00","id":1564404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564403#post1564403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Free Council, can someone hold Strategos and Syndic positions at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since &quot;In some regions, where Free Council mages are few, every mage is given the title of strategos over some area of experience (if not expertise), to prevent one strategos from wielding too much power over the three or four other mages who make up the Consilium.&quot; it seems like it would have to be possible. But the Free Council books warns against the undue influence both strategoi and syndics can hold and would probably be aware that it might be tempting to cling to that power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T01:27:57-07:00","id":1564411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564403#post1564403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Free Council, can someone hold Strategos and Syndic positions at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no indication that they can't as a general rule.<br /> <br /> Also, there's some indication that what a Syndic actually is, varies in formality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T18:05:39-07:00","id":1564439,"title":"","content":"In the most common scenarios, how many masters has an order in a city? and how common is a 3rd degree master?<br /> <br /> <br /> (I am aware that chronicle specific situations might make this &quot;whatever the Storyteller says&quot; but I am asking as part of the known or speculated world building for second edition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T19:36:55-07:00","id":1564441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564439#post1564439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the most common scenarios, how many masters has an order in a city? and how common is a 3rd degree master?<br /> <br /> (I am aware that chronicle specific situations might make this &quot;whatever the Storyteller says&quot; but I am asking as part of the known or speculated world building for second edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside chronicle specific situations, the population of mages in a city at all is variable, the size of the Orders is not uniform globally nor locally, and the Orders divide their Caucuses into culturally similar regional groups rather than singular cities like a Consilium is made to manage.<br /> <br /> And while 2e has made the chart less granular a mage still needs to be at least Gnosis 6 to have any kind of multiple Mastery. This is to say nothing of the fact that the easiest way to master three Arcana is to have a Legacy that grants a third Ruling Arcanum, which not all of them do, with the alternative being tutelage in the dots above your natural limit by an existing Master, which comes with its own power dynamics and social circumstances. Every dot of Gnosis a mage gains comes with a breakthrough significant enough to potentially change the character's Anchors in line with their Obsessions and Aspirations, and this narrative requirement for a breakthrough is the main limiting factor against mages generating Arcane Experiences casually ratcheting up their Gnosis from grinding their teeth against singular Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Convocations, which are more events than political bodies, are run by committees of Magisters who can be any Pentacle mage that can prove mastery of an Arcanum, but while the Silver Ladder tries to have Convocations regularly in areas that overlap the territories of all five Orders, that doesn't indicate anything about the population of Masters of any degree in a specific city operating locally.<br /> <br /> It can probably safely be assumed that any city with enough of an established Awakened presence to have a Consilium there are likely to be at least enough Masters living or formerly active to maintain a healthy currency of rotecraft either directly or through grimoires and to act as mentors to at least one newer generation of mages. The tendency of the Pentacle Orders to all be meritocratic to some degree means Masters are likely to occupy positions of importance in a political structure if they are present.<br /> <br /> Masters are rare enough to be notable figures, but not so extraordinary that it's not weirder to have a good-sized Consilium without Masters than for there to be one with any at all, and every mage not laboring under unusual circumstances has the capacity for second-degree Mastery without special training. Fifth-degree Masters of the sort who could verify that it takes more than a conjunctional Making spell of all the Subtle Arcana are described with terms like &quot;vanishingly rare&quot; and &quot;luminaries,&quot; so third- and fourth-degree Masters presumably fit into the middle ground between those two extremes, with the note that mages seldom pour all their advancement resources into just mastering singular Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T22:11:37-07:00","id":1564444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564439#post1564439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the most common scenarios, how many masters has an order in a city? and how common is a 3rd degree master?<br /> <br /> <br /> (I am aware that chronicle specific situations might make this &quot;whatever the Storyteller says&quot; but I am asking as part of the known or speculated world building for second edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplest answer is: there's no Normal distribution for this. It's less that the ST can do whatever and more that statistical variance is way too large.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume that Awakenings follow an even statistical spread, once it happens the result is an unusually resourceful, and as such mobile, individual. Both the social dynamics of Order and Concilia and the nature of Mysteries add good reason for this mobile individual to move, to relocate to where their interests are.<br /> <br /> You should expect most Mages in a city to not be from there at all, and the overall population to depend from what the area offers to those Mages rather than be a reflection of population size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T00:29:42-07:00","id":1564448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is to say nothing of the fact that the easiest way to master three Arcana is to have a Legacy that grants a third Ruling Arcanum, which not all of them do, with the alternative being tutelage in the dots above your natural limit by an existing Master, which comes with its own power dynamics and social circumstances. </div> </div> </div>How is it harder to get a master to teach your one dot of their ruling arcana (which ~1 in 5 mages will have) compared to joining a legacy (which is likely to be far rarer and comes with all kinds of permanent social connections and expectations)?<br /> <br /> Mages exchanging knowledge for some specific payment seems like it is perfectly reasonable.<br /> <br /> Approach any master of the Arcanum you want to learn, ask them what it will cost. No longer term commitment like a legacy, simple interaction. It could be as simple as casting and safely relinquishing a spell for them. Finding or giving them an imbued item/Artifact. Or hundreds of other tasks they are too busy to do (what with being a Master with their own Obsessions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T04:44:34-07:00","id":1564451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564439#post1564439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and how common is a 3rd degree master?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find any in the books outside of full-on Archmasters. Even NPCs referred to as particularly powerful are mere double-masters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I am aware that chronicle specific situations might make this &quot;whatever the Storyteller says&quot; but I am asking as part of the known or speculated world building for second edition). </div> </div> </div>It's a fair question, but not really one that the books answer directly. The only conclusion I can really make is that it tends to be quite conservative. A lot of NPCs that maybe read as Masters, tend to be Adepts or even Disciples. Same for the Masters; many that read as having been around forever, are still only single-masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T08:54:29-07:00","id":1564454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564448#post1564448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it harder to get a master to teach your one dot of their ruling arcana (which ~1 in 5 mages will have) compared to joining a legacy (which is likely to be far rarer and comes with all kinds of permanent social connections and expectations)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly rare for a mage to become an Adept or Master before joining a Legacy unless they have a reason for not doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages exchanging knowledge for some specific payment seems like it is perfectly reasonable.<br /> <br /> Approach any master of the Arcanum you want to learn, ask them what it will cost. No longer term commitment like a legacy, simple interaction. It could be as simple as casting and safely relinquishing a spell for them. Finding or giving them an imbued item/Artifact. Or hundreds of other tasks they are too busy to do (what with being a Master with their own Obsessions) </div> </div> </div>The knowledge in question is being able to create and destroy the phenomena of an Arcanum at will, with a bonus of the ability to create rotes, which most mages are willing to trade favors for as isolated effects. Even setting aside those cases where a Master is jealously guarding their niche, both of the Orders that maintain stores of knowledge that aren't an individual person require compensation.<br /> <br /> There's already mild social gates implied around teaching certain rotes and ratings of the Mastigos Arcana and it's not hard to imagine it could take some convincing for someone to believe teaching you the Lore of Disintegrating People and the methods to create and propagate methods of making any spell you have the ability to cast more effective is not going to come back to bite them, especially since the most expedient way for them to have attained Mastery was from hard-earned Arcane Experiences.<br /> <br /> Joining a Legacy gives your mentor direct leverage and an incentive to get along and generally provides less inherently dangerous knowledge than the Practice of Unmaking. Getting a Master to teach you involves approaching someone of a different Path with its own perspective, or a Legacy whose knowledge of that Arcanum may come from Mysteries that they want to keep stewardship of, and the only thing they have over you as insurance or assurance that the knowledge won't be misused is whatever they get out of it.<br /> <br /> Lest we forget, mages in Awakening are not assumed to be altruists and there are many reasons they keep secrets, including the root powerset whose modern name literally means &quot;secret.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T10:43:51-07:00","id":1564455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564448#post1564448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it harder to get a master to teach your one dot of their ruling arcana (which ~1 in 5 mages will have) compared to joining a legacy (which is likely to be far rarer and comes with all kinds of permanent social connections and expectations)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's harder to learn up to mastery in a non-Ruling Arcanum than it is to get a third Ruling Arcanum because the latter requires fewer steps and is likely to be part of a mage's general experience.<br /> <br /> Also, it costs more Experience and they can't be Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> Like, step one; have an approachable Master around. Not necessarily a given in the first place.<br /> <br /> I don't think the book quite elaborates just how in depth the teaching needs to be, but I think it's not unreasonable to assume that it's at least as much of an imposition on the time of a Master as any of the things they don't have time for that might theoretically be sufficient payment to be provided with such teaching.<br /> <br /> One might also look at how Signs of Sorcery gives a framework for using the Availability system as a way to model mages requisitioning resources from one another. In which case, finding somebody who would agree to teach you to develop mastery of an Arcanum is probably a difficult proposition if you have the highest possible status in an Order or Consilium, and only goes up from there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T13:27:34-07:00","id":1564457,"title":"","content":"It's honestly not something I'd given much thought to, but I really like the idea of a third mastery being a real prize that requires a great deal of work to get.<br /> <br /> Like, if you're a Master in Boston, do you want the Nemean to become a 3rd degree master? You'd be allowing him to outrank even other double-masters, an already small group. At that point you can forget about Khumeia and the Magisters removing him from office. He'll be glued to that Hierarch's seat till he dies or Ascends.<br /> <br /> Hell, were they in such a position, would you want any of the other masters to become 3rd degree masters? I'd strongly suspect no.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, all the masters have extensive resources, so a trade is not out of the question. Maybe the Nemean can have his training, but you get to have a good long read of the Secret Concord. Or maybe your pick gets to have the open Councillor seat. Or maybe you simply get some undefined huge favour at some future date. Or maybe it's all three. Either way, it needs to be big enough to justify handing even more authority to him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T17:17:30-07:00","id":1564461,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you be both member of an Order and (by using the Mystery Cult Initiation) a Nameless Order? Do you get the same status restrictions as when using Order Status?</li> <li>How many people you need for a Mystery Cult Initiation? I was seeing the one in Night Horros, and it seems to be at least 4 people (Tanris, Pictas, Rowan, Sylvene) minimum for formation.</li> <li>Can you have an Awakened only Mystery Cult that offers Awakened only merits, WITHOUT being a Nameless Order?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T20:16:31-07:00","id":1564463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564461#post1564461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be both member of an Order and (by using the Mystery Cult Initiation) a Nameless Order? Do you get the same status restrictions as when using Order Status?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mystery Cult Initiation Merit explicitly reifies the &quot;Nameless&quot; sidebar's statement that being Nameless is mutually exclusive with belonging to one of the six major Orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many people you need for a Mystery Cult Initiation? I was seeing the one in Night Horros, and it seems to be at least 4 people (Tanris, Pictas, Rowan, Sylvene) minimum for formation. </div> </div> </div>The characters named in the Hand of Destiny's description are the inner circle of the Mystery Cult in addition to being a cabal of mages, and the same paragraph states that &quot;Most Hand of Destiny mages outside of the inner circle&quot; don't know about the hope-eating gulmoth Tamris is running a pyramid scheme to feed. There are way more than four people in the Hand by design.<br /> <br /> There are no hard numbers given for the threshold for what constitutes a Mystery Cult with an Initiation Merit, but the type of thing they are means it's definitionally unlikely for anything that you wouldn't describe as at least a secret society to qualify.<br /> <br /> Nameless Orders can be as small in scope as the local level and potentially being just a few cabals who joined forces, with the section immediately after that description in the corebook defining the cabal a mage might join having between two and thirty of their peers (i.e. around three to thirty-one mages per cabal), so you may reasonably assume the membership numbers for a given cabal to be in the same range as you would get for the total number of monsters of a given type in a given faction in a given city, which I've generally shorthanded to &quot;enough to fill a typical high school class&quot; \u2014 anywhere between fifteen and forty, depending on the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you have an Awakened only Mystery Cult that offers Awakened only merits, WITHOUT being a Nameless Order? </div> </div> </div>The definition of a Nameless Order is a small organization of mages. They're Nameless because they don't have the huge metaphysical backing of the Sects. It's purely a matter of nomenclature and at best you'd get characters who'd have words to say about being called Nameless \u2014 if you have a mage-based Mystery Cult and you're not a Nameless Order, you're a subgroup within the Orders and don't get to use the Merit to get Rote Specialties like a Nameless Order gets to do as a workaround for not getting them from basic Order Status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Forgot to finish the last sentence. 10-02-2026, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T01:57:06-07:00","id":1564469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564461#post1564461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people you need for a Mystery Cult Initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a game mechanic, so what it actually represents is quite open as long as it makes sense narratively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you have an Awakened only Mystery Cult that offers Awakened only merits, WITHOUT being a Nameless Order? </div> </div> </div>I could see some of the more organised legacies having a mystery cult merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-03T13:23:13-07:00","id":1564512,"title":"","content":"Tilts and conditions:<br /> Lets say were operating at 2 dot arkana<br /> 1. Can i do damage manifesting a limb wrack condition? From fate someone probably would fell and dislocate/breka an arm<br /> 2. Can i implement the poisoned tilt? That deals damage. Additionaly poisons deal long term damage based on toxicity <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-03T13:59:50-07:00","id":1564514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564512#post1564512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tilts and conditions:<br /> Lets say were operating at 2 dot arkana<br /> 1. Can i do damage manifesting a limb wrack condition? From fate someone probably would fell and dislocate/breka an arm<br /> 2. Can i implement the poisoned tilt? That deals damage. Additionaly poisons deal long term damage based on toxicity</div> </div> </div> </div>For Fate, any of the published spells that can apply a hex can apply Tilts, which includes the Apprentice-level spell Exceptional Luck. The list of non-custom Tilts a hex can apply includes Poisoned, which is not included on the list of Tilts that can be applied more than once with a hex to get the more severe version.<br /> <br /> More generally, the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines note that applying a Tilt is usually a Reach effect on an attack spell but may also be done from whole cloth with a 3- or 4-dot spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T04:39:29-07:00","id":1564527,"title":"","content":"in the legacy attainments section its mentioned that:<br /> &quot;For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.<br /> If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two<br /> ratings.<br /> Unless specified otherwise, activating an Attainment is an instant action. Attainments cannot be enhanced by longer casting times.&quot;<br /> So is tihis a typo or do the legacy spells count potency differently? also it mentions that the attainments are an instant action but somewhere else its said they need to use a reach for that. Which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T05:19:09-07:00","id":1564528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564527#post1564527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the legacy attainments section its mentioned that:<br /> &quot;For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.<br /> If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two<br /> ratings.<br /> Unless specified otherwise, activating an Attainment is an instant action. Attainments cannot be enhanced by longer casting times.&quot;<br /> So is tihis a typo or do the legacy spells count potency differently? also it mentions that the attainments are an instant action but somewhere else its said they need to use a reach for that. Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its worded poorly, here is a more concise explanation :<br /> <br /> * Calculate primary factor normally, no yantras apply and no roll is required.<br /> * You can spend pseudo-dice in spell factors equal to your Arcanum rating.<br /> * If you Attainment uses two Arcana, use the mage's lowest dot rating in the calculation. So if it uses Forces and Time, for example, and the user has Time 3 and Forces 4, you use a rating of 3.<br /> * Ritual casting time is an hour/scene, but &quot;we are assuming most will be designed to be cast instantly&quot; (hence the confusion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-05-2026, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T04:45:17-07:00","id":1564583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564527#post1564527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the legacy attainments section its mentioned that:<br /> &quot;For example, if a member of a fire-summoning Legacy who possesses Forces 5 activates her Forces-based Legacy Attainment.<br /> Its primary factor is Potency. The Attainment scores 5 Potency automatically. If Duration is required, it lasts for three turns (as per Duration rating with \u20134 dice penalty). It scores 5 successes.<br /> If the Attainment also harnessed Spirit and the mage possessed three dots in that Arcanum, the Duration would decrease to two turns, since the secondary factor uses the lower of the two<br /> ratings.<br /> Unless specified otherwise, activating an Attainment is an instant action. Attainments cannot be enhanced by longer casting times.&quot;<br /> So is tihis a typo or do the legacy spells count potency differently? also it mentions that the attainments are an instant action but somewhere else its said they need to use a reach for that. Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer to your questions was vanished for a bit, its back now and on the post above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T17:45:56-07:00","id":1564597,"title":"","content":"If you are part of a Legacy and you learn a novel attainment, is every attainment onwards considered novel, even if you learn the traditional ones?<br /> <br /> For example, you learn the first attainment from a legacy teacher.<br /> Then you invent your own second attainment.<br /> Third attainment you want the original legacy third attainment and go back to the teacher, do you have to learn it as a novel attainment (Gnosis 5 instead of Gnosis 4)? Can the teacher even share it? Same for fourth and fifth attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T23:17:49-07:00","id":1564600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564597#post1564597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are part of a Legacy and you learn a novel attainment, is every attainment onwards considered novel, even if you learn the traditional ones?<br /> <br /> For example, you learn the first attainment from a legacy teacher.<br /> Then you invent your own second attainment.<br /> Third attainment you want the original legacy third attainment and go back to the teacher, do you have to learn it as a novel attainment (Gnosis 5 instead of Gnosis 4)? Can the teacher even share it? Same for fourth and fifth attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacy attainments have to be learned in order and you've locked yourself out of being able to learn the orthodox attainments in order. You're on your own track now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:13:17-07:00","id":1564613,"title":"","content":"Space intro states that Sympathetic casting is withstood by Space itself.<br /> Does that mean that a conscious subject cannot decide to not withstand the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:35:45-07:00","id":1564616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564613#post1564613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space intro states that Sympathetic casting is withstood by Space itself.<br /> Does that mean that a conscious subject cannot decide to not withstand the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't get rid of their sympathetic Withstand rating voluntarily like they can with their Resistance Trait, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:41:42-07:00","id":1564617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564613#post1564613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space intro states that Sympathetic casting is withstood by Space itself.<br /> Does that mean that a conscious subject cannot decide to not withstand the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> The withstand rating is that of the Sympathetic connection. So two connected this (eg: a mage and her soulstone, a pregnant person and fetus inside them, etc) will have a withstand of 0. Weak sympathy have a withstand of 5.<br /> <br /> Then other withstands are added to that (and the subject can resist or not as usual) per the usual rules for multiple withstands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T03:29:08-07:00","id":1564633,"title":"","content":"I m confused about the first reach option of the One mind two toughts spell:<br /> &quot;The subject may perform two separate Mental instant tasks at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> -what kind of actions could be considered Mental istant?<br /> -why it requires a reach? All of the spell examples are things that could normally be defined as a series of instant actions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T05:05:00-07:00","id":1564636,"title":"","content":"Also, would it be balanced (for a level 5 mind legacy attainment) to give the option to enter physicalli into the astral realms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T07:08:43-07:00","id":1564638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564633#post1564633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m confused about the first reach option of the One mind two toughts spell:<br /> &quot;The subject may perform two separate Mental instant tasks at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> -what kind of actions could be considered Mental istant?<br /> -why it requires a reach? All of the spell examples are things that could normally be defined as a series of instant actions</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the description of Attributes on Page 207, any time an action is described as a &quot;[Mental/Physical/Social] action,&quot; it means that it's a mundane action that uses an Attribute from that category in its dicepool. Meditation is a Mental action, as is Perception, as is memorizing something.<br /> <br /> &quot;Carrying on a conversation&quot; is the closest thing in the spell's set of examples to something that is not the type of thing that is modeled using the extended action mechanics to represent an ongoing project that can suffer setbacks or be left alone and resumed later. It requires a Reach because it allows you to multitask your thoughts at the timescale of an action scene instead of just in the looser timekeeping of scenes that aren't tracking Initiative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564636#post1564636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would it be balanced (for a level 5 mind legacy attainment) to give the option to enter physicalli into the astral realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>With an appropriate supporting Arcanum and theory behind it, sure, but not from Mind alone. Spirit or Death would be the most straightforward basis, with their ability to turn a body into ephemera on their own, or Fate might be able to manage the more particular feat of leveraging the Gate of Horn from Changeling, and unless the plan is to rely on Synesi I'd probably include the Astral Adept Merit as a prerequisite as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T08:08:50-07:00","id":1564640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564636#post1564636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would it be balanced (for a level 5 mind legacy attainment) to give the option to enter physicalli into the astral realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just use <i>Create Avernian Gate</i> as a baseline, but for the Astral. You can also use a Ruling to grant Astral Adept for widely accessible, but not instant, Astral travel. You can also use Arcana combinations, for example, I use a Ruling of Mind and Space to make a mental variation of <i>Break Boundary</i> for the second optional Attainment of he <i>Parliament of the Needle</i> update.<br /> <br /> However, an important caveat is that your body will still be in a deep meditative state in the Material, as with normal Astral travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-09-2026, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T14:15:09-07:00","id":1564653,"title":"","content":"Astral adept is included, the most important part is to don t leave a body behind.<br /> The idea of mixing other Ephemeral Arcana is not bad, i m wondering if it would be possible to use also Fate (for his link to the Hedge Ghosts parricular form of twilight) or Prime (for his ability to interact with all of the twilights).<br /> In each of the case it would be a level 2 or 3 of the added Arcana?<br /> Also would it be ok for a level 1 or 2 attainment (mind) to give automatic Exeptional success on the Astral projection roll (to make it always instant)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T15:07:41-07:00","id":1564655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564653#post1564653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of mixing other Ephemeral Arcana is not bad, i m wondering if it would be possible to use also Fate (for his link to the Hedge Ghosts parricular form of twilight) or Prime (for his ability to interact with all of the twilights).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge Ghosts quite crucially don't occupy an actual phase of Twilight and Prime is generally about the exact opposite of de-phasing a material body. Short of swapping between the three orthodox phases of Twilight anything else is going to be pretty firmly in the realm of Atypical Attainments to be determined as appropriate to the individual game this is for, which means the particular Mystery/theory is going to be important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In each of the case it would be a level 2 or 3 of the added Arcana? </div> </div> </div>Whole-body transformation between states, teleportation, or interdimensional transportation without leveraging an Iris is typically Patterning or else using Reach on a lower Practice that would need at least four dots to be safe to use (and thus a valid construction for an Attainment).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also would it be ok for a level 1 or 2 attainment (mind) to give automatic Exeptional success on the Astral projection roll (to make it always instant)? </div> </div> </div>The game generally does not do full no-roll automatic success, though I could see an Apprentice effect to allow the character to gain or grant the Informed Condition relating to meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T09:29:34-07:00","id":1564721,"title":"","content":"Does Legacy attainment take spell control slots?<br /> I m thinking on a Legacy that could have Hung spell as an attainment and i m wondering if it could suspend the other Legacy Attainments","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T09:42:50-07:00","id":1564722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564721#post1564721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Legacy attainment take spell control slots?<br /> I m thinking on a Legacy that could have Hung spell as an attainment and i m wondering if it could suspend the other Legacy Attainments</div> </div> </div> </div>No as far as I am aware. Hung Spell suspends well, spells. There is nothing there in the interaction with Legacy attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T09:47:35-07:00","id":1564723,"title":"","content":"The Faction Member merit and regular Order Status , how is it counted when in another caucus?<br /> <br /> <br /> Normal status works like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Consilium/Order Status Mage 2ed Core p.100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Orders are both global organizations and locally compart\u00ad<br /> mentalized. <b>If a character uses Order Status in a Caucus other than<br /> her home one, reduce her effective rating in this Merit by \u20131 if the<br /> Caucus is a member of the same Consilium or Assembly, \u20132 if it<br /> is a member of the same Convocation, and \u20133 if it is unrelated.\u200b</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faction Member Tome of the Pentacle p.90</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>When dealing with other members of her<br /> faction outside of her Caucus, the character\u2019s dots in this Merit<br /> count as Status dots with them</b>, even if they\u2019re not members of<br /> the same Order (for cross-Order factions).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> So I am Order Status 5, I go to an unrelated Convocation, my status is -3; therefore there for my order I am at Status 2. So far clear.<br /> <br /> But when dealing with members of my Faction there, is my Status 2 + Faction Member rank, or just Faction Member rank?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T14:27:00-07:00","id":1564730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564721#post1564721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Legacy attainment take spell control slots?<br /> I m thinking on a Legacy that could have Hung spell as an attainment and i m wondering if it could suspend the other Legacy Attainments</div> </div> </div> </div>Specificity of Hung Spell notwithstanding, there's also the fact that Legacy Attainments are only built like spells for the purposes of producing effects; an Attainment is metaphysically the same as an equivalent phenomenon not produced by magic. To borrow language from Deviant, Legacy Attainments are like Natural Variations apart from their ability to be passively improved with increased Arcanum mastery.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564723#post1564723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Faction Member merit and regular Order Status , how is it counted when in another caucus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Faction Member dots raise your effective Order Status within your Order and double as Status with cross-Order faction members who don't share your Order, the latter of which would not apply at all if you were not in the same faction.<br /> <br /> Faction Member has a prerequisite of Order Status 2 and raises your effective Order Status within your Caucus by 1 when dealing with your Faction. It also gives you effective Status dots equal to your dots in the Merit outside of your Caucus, even with faction members who don't share your Order; interpreting the shared-Order/unshared-Caucus mechanic as additive means any Faction Member effectively reduces the Caucus penalties by at least one step among their faction.<br /> <br /> If you're dealing with faction members in your Order your effective Status is Faction Member + 2; for faction members from other Orders it's just your Faction Member dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T20:05:19-07:00","id":1564738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564730#post1564730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faction Member dots raise your effective Order Status within your Order and double as Status with cross-Order faction members who don't share your Order, the latter of which would not apply at all if you were not in the same faction.<br /> <br /> Faction Member has a prerequisite of Order Status 2 and raises your effective Order Status within your Caucus by 1 when dealing with your Faction. It also gives you effective Status dots equal to your dots in the Merit outside of your Caucus, even with faction members who don't share your Order; interpreting the shared-Order/unshared-Caucus mechanic as additive means any Faction Member effectively reduces the Caucus penalties by at least one step among their faction.<br /> <br /> If you're dealing with faction members in your Order your effective Status is Faction Member + 2; for faction members from other Orders it's just your Faction Member dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but this reading means that your Status is higher outside your Caucus than inside?<br /> <br /> Same example:<br /> <br /> <br /> Order Status 5. and Faction Member 3.<br /> <br /> In my Caucus: Order Status +1; therefore <b>Order Status (among faction members) 6</b><br /> <br /> In another Caucus that is a member of the same Consilium: Order Status -1 + Faction Member 3; therefore <b>Order Status (among faction members) <u>7??</u></b><br /> <br /> In another Caucus that is a member of the same Convocation: Order Status -2 + Faction Member 3; therefore <b>Order Status (among faction members) 6</b>. Same as in home Caucus<br /> <br /> In another Caucus that is unrelated: Order Status -3 + Faction Member 3; therefore <b>Order Status (among faction members) 5</b>. Less than home Caucus<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T21:50:39-07:00","id":1564739,"title":"","content":"I understand, but does it mean that after casting a mage loses all control on an Attainment?<br /> Because the Hung spell as an Attainment could still be useful to suspend regular spells, but only IF the mage retains control to cancel it whenever the need arises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T22:57:18-07:00","id":1564740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564738#post1564738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but this reading means that your Status is higher outside your Caucus than inside?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to go out on a limb here and suppose that the explicit note about the effects of membership in a Heretical faction mean that in non-Heretical factions the bonus Status cannot bring you above five dots or else that line would be part of the first paragraph of the effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564739#post1564739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, but does it mean that after casting a mage loses all control on an Attainment?Because the Hung spell as an Attainment could still be useful to suspend regular spells, but only IF the mage retains control to cancel it whenever the need arises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hung Spell was originally a Utility Attainment in an earlier iteration of the 2e mechanics and as a spell it balances its benefits with the fact that each different released set of spells requires its own instance of Hung Spell, which eats into your spell control and potentially affects your available free Reach even if you're not spending Mana to cast your own spells into the storage.<br /> <br /> It would be excessively useful mechanically and of questionable theoretical grounding narratively to remove the main limiting factor on Hung Spell's usage by making it a Legacy Attainment. Regardless of how broadly you might interpret &quot;control&quot; of a spell, I think it can safely be said that dynamically reducing spell factors to let a bottled spell slip containment is beyond the scope of Legacy Attainments' reduced flexibility to manage unless your game is making a point of including a version of the Hung Spell effect that does not stem from Awakened magic and which this hypothetical Legacy is emulating with a compelling theory for what causes this to work. The same goes for any of the Limited Use Item spells from Signs of Sorcery \u2014 most Legacies have more narratively interesting things to dedicate their time to than trying to make a more efficient means to stocking spell effects.<br /> <br /> This looks more like chicanery based on the idea that it would be useful than the sort of thing that would be an actually compelling part of a Legacy's philosophy, aesthetic, or Mystery. If you want to mess with the various ways to produce bargain-bin Imbuement on a subject, you can do so with a Merit or other open-ended mechanic, but Legacy Attainments have fairly clear limitations and function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T02:04:29-07:00","id":1564742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564740#post1564740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go out on a limb here and suppose that the explicit note about the effects of membership in a Heretical faction mean that in non-Heretical factions the bonus Status cannot bring you above five dots or else that line would be part of the first paragraph of the effect.<br /> <br /> Hung Spell was originally a Utility Attainment in an earlier iteration of the 2e mechanics and as a spell it balances its benefits with the fact that each different released set of spells requires its own instance of Hung Spell, which eats into your spell control and potentially affects your available free Reach even if you're not spending Mana to cast your own spells into the storage.<br /> <br /> It would be excessively useful mechanically and of questionable theoretical grounding narratively to remove the main limiting factor on Hung Spell's usage by making it a Legacy Attainment. Regardless of how broadly you might interpret &quot;control&quot; of a spell, I think it can safely be said that dynamically reducing spell factors to let a bottled spell slip containment is beyond the scope of Legacy Attainments' reduced flexibility to manage unless your game is making a point of including a version of the Hung Spell effect that does not stem from Awakened magic and which this hypothetical Legacy is emulating with a compelling theory for what causes this to work. The same goes for any of the Limited Use Item spells from Signs of Sorcery \u2014 most Legacies have more narratively interesting things to dedicate their time to than trying to make a more efficient means to stocking spell effects.<br /> <br /> This looks more like chicanery based on the idea that it would be useful than the sort of thing that would be an actually compelling part of a Legacy's philosophy, aesthetic, or Mystery. If you want to mess with the various ways to produce bargain-bin Imbuement on a subject, you can do so with a Merit or other open-ended mechanic, but Legacy Attainments have fairly clear limitations and function.</div> </div> </div> </div>First thing i must thank you because i had not realized that reducing Potency on a regular Hung spell to activate singular spells on the set was an option (i usually cancelled the whole spell and activate the whole set).<br /> <br /> The question arises mostly because Attainments are... weird.<br /> Having no control (on factors and cancelling) on a thing that springs on your soul seems wrong, but having to dedicate a spell control slot on something that is not a spell seems equally wrong.<br /> So how do you manage those things?<br /> <br /> Secondly, yes i m having an hard time trying to fit an optional level 2-3 time effect on a Legacy based on amplifying the mental faculties, so Hung spell is a little wild shot, but that said don t you think that some Legacies based on crafting would make a good use of Limited Use Item?<br /> For example i can totally see an alchemy based legacy with a spell potion Attainment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T02:48:52-07:00","id":1564743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564742#post1564742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First thing i must thank you because i had not realized that reducing Potency on a regular Hung spell to activate singular spells on the set was an option (i usually cancelled the whole spell and activate the whole set).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This begs the question, which spell is released? Is that a case of designing the Imago of the Hung spell, so you can have it be first in, first out. Or would last in, first out make more sense?<br /> <br /> That is, if you have only two spells hung, and you reduce the potency, which spell gets cast? And if this isn't a choice of the spell controller, how is it determined? (Not really an issue of all the spells bring hung are identical... like if you're using it to store Healing effects and you want to be able to release them one at a time, on demand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T03:05:05-07:00","id":1564744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564743#post1564743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This begs the question, which spell is released? Is that a case of designing the Imago of the Hung spell, so you can have it be first in, first out. Or would last in, first out make more sense?<br /> <br /> That is, if you have only two spells hung, and you reduce the potency, which spell gets cast? And if this isn't a choice of the spell controller, how is it determined? (Not really an issue of all the spells bring hung are identical... like if you're using it to store Healing effects and you want to be able to release them one at a time, on demand).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, spell control rules makes the example of reducing chosen targets by reducing Scale factor, so i think that the caster decides which spell is activated by reducing potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T10:25:46-07:00","id":1564748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564742#post1564742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no control (on factors and cancelling) on a thing that springs on your soul seems wrong, but having to dedicate a spell control slot on something that is not a spell seems equally wrong.<br /> So how do you manage those things?<br /> <br /> Secondly, yes i m having an hard time trying to fit an optional level 2-3 time effect on a Legacy based on amplifying the mental faculties, so Hung spell is a little wild shot, but that said don t you think that some Legacies based on crafting would make a good use of Limited Use Item?<br /> For example i can totally see an alchemy based legacy with a spell potion Attainment</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, it's important to note that while Legacy Attainments come from your soul and scale off of Arcana, they're mostly just reliably &quot;things you can do&quot; without all the metaphysical baggage of spells \u2014 they're unrolled like how you don't usually need to roll Athletics to do a cartwheel without dramatic stakes involved, and the limits of their Potency and Duration are part of why most Attainments are buffs or unopposed actions rather than interpersonal effects. Most of them haven't been updated to 2e, but there's a reason there were multiple published Legacies in 1e that bodily altered their practitioners.<br /> <br /> On the other end of things, it's important to remember that not everything a Legacy does has to be managed through its Attainments \u2014 an alchemy-based Legacy can almost certainly teach its members the rote for Spell Potion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-15-2026, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T18:53:34-07:00","id":1564773,"title":"","content":"If you use Hermium and any Kassiterum to form an Amalgam, the item would be able to be used as a Magical tool by all Paths (gaining 9-again) except the Obrimos. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> Essentially, Hermium + any Perfected metal would keep both properties of the materials and it means it always grants 9-again to Acanthus and Mastigos, +2 tool Yantra for shapeshifting and transformation spells, PLUS whatever the other Perfected metal grants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T03:13:47-07:00","id":1564785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564773#post1564773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use Hermium and any Kassiterum to form an Amalgam, the item would be able to be used as a Magical tool by all Paths (gaining 9-again) except the Obrimos. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> Essentially, Hermium + any Perfected metal would keep both properties of the materials and it means it always grants 9-again to Acanthus and Mastigos, +2 tool Yantra for shapeshifting and transformation spells, PLUS whatever the other Perfected metal grants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems the plain meaning of the text.<br /> <br /> What makes you think that might not be a correct reading?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T05:06:02-07:00","id":1564786,"title":"","content":"Another interpretation could be that Hermium can melt two other metal and join all the 3 togheter.<br /> The artificial Alloyed spells seems to suggest that (they all use 2 metals + Hermium)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T12:28:52-07:00","id":1564790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564785#post1564785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that seems the plain meaning of the text.<br /> <br /> What makes you think that might not be a correct reading?</div> </div> </div> </div>The material validity to create a path tool.<br /> <br /> This was my original concept:I wanted a signet ring (as a &quot;Coin, or other symbols of material wealth&quot; and as &quot;signs of authority to as Tools of status and persuasion&quot;) for my Silver Ladder Acanthus, the material should be silver (or its perfected version, Lunargent).<br /> <br /> BUUUUUT with Hermium and Brontium, I can have a ring that is symbolically a coin plus the Brontium benefits. The Hermium makes it a valid Acanthus path tool, independent of the Brontium component.<br /> <br /> Now I have a tool that I can use as both as an Order tool and a Path tool, while still keeping the symbolic association and the benefits of the perfected metals (mainly 9-again, but also the Brontium active and passive bonuses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T13:08:54-07:00","id":1564791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564790#post1564790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The material validity to create a path tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but your question implies that you're not sure if you've understood the rules, and to my eye, the rules are pretty clear, (indeed, you've understood them correctly as far as I can see).<br /> <br /> My worry is that I've missed some text that would make you doubt your reading of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T18:28:16-07:00","id":1564811,"title":"","content":"Has anyone stated up the Keepers of Vedet as a legacy? They seem so cool as witcher-esque mages and it sucks the Tremere killed all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T03:37:34-07:00","id":1564885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564811#post1564811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone stated up the Keepers of Vedet as a legacy? They seem so cool as witcher-esque mages and it sucks the Tremere killed all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not afaik, they are Space primary and Death or Spirit optional, with a focus on manipulating the soul (so they qualify to become a House), so it would be interesting to see what their original form was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T07:14:22-07:00","id":1564953,"title":"","content":"The Sleepwalker merits p. 305 of the Core are valid for all minor templates? (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls, humans with supernatural merits, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T10:34:50-07:00","id":1564956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564953#post1564953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker merits p. 305 of the Core are valid for all minor templates? (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls, humans with supernatural merits, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. 'All Shapes and Sizes' on page 303 of the core more or less states directly that Wolf-Blooded and Ghouls are sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T10:56:43-07:00","id":1564957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564953#post1564953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker merits p. 305 of the Core are valid for all minor templates? (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls, humans with supernatural merits, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Minor splats are already sleepwalkers without the merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T13:18:25-07:00","id":1564961,"title":"","content":"Does<b> Meditative Mind </b>help you to meditate into the Astral?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 1 says you do not suffer environmental penalties to mediation rolls but normal meditation rolls are Composure + Wits. Will this affect the Astral Meditation roll? (Resolve + Composure) Very useful if so.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 2 grants a +3 on Resolve + Composure rolls, like the Astral Meditation rolls, this one is directly applicable as it is.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 4, would it allow to enter the Astral with a single success? This one seems not applicable as it just means the meditation bonus you can get faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-25-2026, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T13:54:27-07:00","id":1564964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564961#post1564961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does<b> Meditative Mind </b>helps you to meditate into the Astral?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 1, says you do not suffer environmental penalties to mediation rolls but normal meditation rolls are Composure + Wits. Will this affect the Astral Meditation roll? (Resolve + Composure) Very useful if so.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 2 grants a +3 on Resolve + Composure rolls, like the Astral Meditation rolls, this one is directly applicable, no rules interpretation.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 4, would it allow to enter the Astral with a single success? This one seems not applicable as it just means the meditation bonus you can get faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would, you are paying merit dots for it, and its a great way to give it some extra value for the Awakened. If paired with <i>Astral Adept</i>, I would allow them to build on each other, so long as you flavored your ritual as a type of meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T17:28:50-07:00","id":1564966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564961#post1564961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meditative Mind 4, would it allow to enter the Astral with a single success? This one seems not applicable as it just means the meditation bonus you can get faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be completely irrelevant to the roll to meditate into (or deeper into) the Astral, which is an instant action that takes time to resolve rather than an extended action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T23:53:33-07:00","id":1564974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564961#post1564961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does<b> Meditative Mind </b>help you to meditate into the Astral?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 1 says you do not suffer environmental penalties to mediation rolls but normal meditation rolls are Composure + Wits. Will this affect the Astral Meditation roll? (Resolve + Composure) Very useful if so.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 2 grants a +3 on Resolve + Composure rolls, like the Astral Meditation rolls, this one is directly applicable as it is.<br /> <br /> Meditative Mind 4, would it allow to enter the Astral with a single success? This one seems not applicable as it just means the meditation bonus you can get faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the last one i would simply rule that for Astral travel it reduces to 3 the successes needed for instant travel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T01:54:07-07:00","id":1564975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1564953#post1564953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleepwalker merits p. 305 of the Core are valid for all minor templates? (Wolf-Blooded, Ghouls, humans with supernatural merits, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there supernatural merit needs to represent an inherent trait. So from Geist, memento collectors would probably not be sleepwalkers (for just that merit). While Eaters of the Dead probably do count (much the same as wolf-blooded&amp;ghouls) - and again human members of a Krewe may gain power from that, regalia benefits, learning new Ceremonies, while that not being inherent to them. And thus not qualify as a sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T03:04:27-07:00","id":1565017,"title":"","content":"During the Dream reaching spell (with or without the special Reach) does the caster dream too or is aware of her body?<br /> If the first is true, does the spell One mind two toughts without the Reach options allow to retain consciousness while dreaming (but limiting the caster to extended mental actions only)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T12:44:29-07:00","id":1565022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565017#post1565017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the Dream reaching spell (with or without the special Reach) does the caster dream too or is aware of her body?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Enter and share&quot; seems fairly unambiguously the former.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the first is true, does the spell One mind two toughts without the Reach options allow to retain consciousness while dreaming (but limiting the caster to extended mental actions only)? </div> </div> </div>In the case of dreams I'm moderately certain the &quot;while going to sleep&quot; part is not superceded by the ability to manage two trains of thought at once \u2014 the Reach option for Astral activity on OMTT doesn't split your attention between dreams and reality so much as broaden the scope of viable activities while in a frame of reference where the mind and &quot;body&quot; are more aligned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T01:47:21-07:00","id":1565031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565022#post1565022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Enter and share&quot; seems fairly unambiguously the former.<br /> In the case of dreams I'm moderately certain the &quot;while going to sleep&quot; part is not superceded by the ability to manage two trains of thought at once \u2014 the Reach option for Astral activity on OMTT doesn't split your attention between dreams and reality so much as broaden the scope of viable activities while in a frame of reference where the mind and &quot;body&quot; are more aligned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding Space &quot;Co-location&quot; would make it possible?<br /> Because i m planning to use Dreamspeaker in 2ed and i will need to replicate Astral Dreamwalking wich has similar problematics.<br /> I understand that the spell dividing thoughts maybe is not enough to divide the consciousness, but maybe one of higher level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 10-29-2026, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T04:50:10-07:00","id":1565033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565022#post1565022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Reach option for Astral activity on OMTT doesn't split your attention between dreams and reality so much as broaden the scope of viable activities while in a frame of reference where the mind and &quot;body&quot; are more aligned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure they are canon, but didn't Soul Cage have a legacy based around doing this exact thing? <br /> <br /> That is, using an attainment based in One Mind, Two Thoughts, which lets them be active in Astral and in the physical world at the same time? I assumed that 2e adopted this until the spell. But you're right, it doesn't read that way to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T05:22:42-07:00","id":1565034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565033#post1565033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure they are canon, but didn't Soul Cage have a legacy based around doing this exact thing?<br /> <br /> That is, using an attainment based in One Mind, Two Thoughts, which lets them be active in Astral and in the physical world at the same time? I assumed that 2e adopted this until the spell. But you're right, it doesn't read that way to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, the <i>Parliament of the Needle</i>, I even updated it to 2ed. Essentially what I did was split it in two. One Attainment was <i>One Mind, Two Thoughts</i> with advanced duration and the Reach for instant actions. The other was a Mind specialized variation of <i>Break Boundary</i>, allowing you to pass through mental barriers, instantly entering your dreams, Oneiros or the shared Legacy realm. Since the Dreamwalkers have no Astral Threshold due to their initiation, I would say they can instantly enter their dreams, Oneiros or Temenos with it instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T02:38:49-08:00","id":1565078,"title":"","content":"I need some ideas about temporal sympathy yantras.<br /> let s say for example, there is a Hallow in the woods with a node on top of it.<br /> The caster knows that roughly 200 years before a volcanic eruption in a distant location changed the direction of a ley line that previously connected to that node.<br /> if the caster needs to use Postcognition to watch the moment the ley line changed direction, what yantra could he use?<br /> <br /> A piece of the rock created by the eruption?<br /> A drawing representing the positions of stars at the eruption moment?<br /> A piece of paper with the precise date of the eruption written upon?<br /> <br /> No tass prior to the event survived and the Hallow itself changed only mystically after the event, so i ve little ideas about material sympathy candidates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-08T06:16:02-08:00","id":1565178,"title":"","content":"Do ilusion based mages make any sense or ar ilusions possible to detect by simple mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-08T06:46:59-08:00","id":1565179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565178#post1565178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ilusion based mages make any sense or ar ilusions possible to detect by simple mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition any sort of concealing spell does not ping Peripheral Mage Sight (which also typically only registers magical effects as they are activated), and Active Mage Sight only sees through an illusion that works on the same principles as its Arcana and still requires a Clash of Wills to do so. The Pierce Deception spell allows the subject to identify illusions as illusions (gaining a sense of what the disguised truth is with the Reach effect) on a successful Clash, but that's a spell rather than simple Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-08T14:26:31-08:00","id":1565187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1565178#post1565178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ilusion based mages make any sense or ar ilusions possible to detect by simple mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but you might use the Piercing Glance merit (Signs of Sorcery p. 26) to get a clash of wills when using peripheral mage sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}